sable to check local regulations before bringing your pet.','2025-03-27 22:25:57','2025-03-27 22:25:57'),(9585,'trails',54,'What are the geographical coordinates of the trail?','The trail is located at approximately 37.784 latitude and -112.332 longitude.','2025-03-27 22:25:57','2025-03-27 22:25:57'),(9586,'trails',55,'What is the overall difficulty of the trail?','The trail is considered to be difficult due to its steep incline and challenging terrain.','2025-03-27 22:26:08','2025-03-27 22:26:08'),(9587,'trails',55,'What ecosystems will I experience along the trail?','Hikers will encounter a striking contrast between a dusty reddish desert with desert foliage and ephemeral streams, transitioning into a lush pine forest adorned with wildflowers and, in summer, remnants of snow.','2025-03-27 22:26:08','2025-03-27 22:26:08'),(9588,'trails',55,'How long is the trail?','The total length of the trail is 3.3 miles, making it a manageable distance for a day hike.','2025-03-27 22:26:08','2025-03-27 22:26:08'),(9589,'trails',55,'What is the elevation gain on the trail?','Hikers will experience an elevation gain of 3,318 feet as they ascend the trail.','2025-03-27 22:26:08','2025-03-27 22:26:08'),(9590,'trails',55,'What is the highest elevation reached on the trail?','The highest point on the trail reaches an elevation of 6,549 feet.','2025-03-27 22:26:08','2025-03-27 22:26:08'),(9591,'trails',55,'Is the trail well maintained?','Yes, the trail features well-maintained switchbacks that are easy to follow, making it easier for hikers to navigate the steep terrain.','2025-03-27 22:26:08','2025-03-27 22:26:08'),(9592,'trails',55,'What kind of views can I expect while hiking?','As you hike, you will be rewarded with stunning views that include the Colorado Plateau, the red rock formations in the distance, and panoramic sights down into St. George and Snow Canyon State Park.','2025-03-27 22:26:08','2025-03-27 22:26:08'),(9593,'trails',55,'What notable features might I find along the trail?','You\'ll encounter impressive granite cliffs and massive boulders that have tumbled from them, adding to the scenic beauty of the trail.','2025-03-27 22:26:08','2025-03-27 22:26:08'),(9594,'trails',55,'Can I bring my dog on this trail?','It is currently unknown if dogs are allowed on this trail, so it\'s recommended to verify any regulations before your hike.','2025-03-27 22:26:08','2025-03-27 22:26:08'),(9595,'trails',55,'What type of trail is this?','This is a point-to-point trail, leading from the desert environment into the heart of the Pine Valley mountains.','2025-03-27 22:26:08','2025-03-27 22:26:08'),(9596,'trails',55,'What is the average and maximum grade of the trail?','The average grade is about 0.20%, with sections reaching a maximum grade of 0.51%, contributing to its difficult rating.','2025-03-27 22:26:08','2025-03-27 22:26:08'),(9597,'trails',55,'What is the latitude and longitude of the trail?','The trail is located at approximately 37.3169° latitude and -113.453° longitude.','2025-03-27 22:26:08','2025-03-27 22:26:08'),(9598,'trails',59,'What is the starting point of the trail?','The trail begins at a parking area and then winds south through ancient bristlecone pines on a large limestone cliff.','2025-03-27 22:26:14','2025-03-27 22:26:14'),(9599,'trails',59,'What can I expect in terms of views?','Expect stunning views throughout the trail, especially at the end where you\'ll reach Powell Point, one of the best viewpoints in Southern Utah.','2025-03-27 22:26:14','2025-03-27 22:26:14'),(9600,'trails',59,'What is the difficulty level of the trail?','The trail is classified as easy, making it suitable for hikers of all experience levels.','2025-03-27 22:26:14','2025-03-27 22:26:14'),(9601,'trails',59,'What are the elevation details of the trail?','The trail maintains a consistent elevation of 10,138 feet, with a slight incline of 83 feet and a decline of 129 feet.','2025-03-27 22:26:14','2025-03-27 22:26:14'),(9602,'trails',59,'How long is the trail?','The total length of the trail is 0.7 miles, making it a short but rewarding hike.','2025-03-27 22:26:14','2025-03-27 22:26:14'),(9603,'trails',59,'What type of trail is it?','This is a point-to-point trail, meaning you will return to your starting point after reaching the end.','2025-03-27 22:26:14','2025-03-27 22:26:14'),(9604,'trails',59,'What is the average and maximum grade of the trail?','The average incline is a gentle 0.06%, peaking at a maximum of 0.09%.','2025-03-27 22:26:14','2025-03-27 22:26:14'),(9605,'trails',59,'What features does the trail offer?','The trail is known for its breathtaking views, particularly from Powell Point at its conclusion.','2025-03-27 22:26:14','2025-03-27 22:26:14'),(9606,'trails',59,'Are dogs allowed on this trail?','It\'s currently unclear whether dogs are allowed on the trail.','2025-03-27 22:26:14','2025-03-27 22:26:14'),(9607,'trails',59,'What are the GPS coordinates for the trail?','The trail is located at a latitude of 37.6936 and a longitude of -111.898.','2025-03-27 22:26:14','2025-03-27 22:26:14'),(9608,'trails',60,'What is the overview of the Grand View Trail?','The Grand View Trail is a winding singletrack that meanders through beautiful aspen stands, black timber, and meadows, making for a picturesque hike.','2025-03-27 22:26:27','2025-03-27 22:26:27'),(9609,'trails',60,'How do I access the start of the trail?','To reach the trailhead, drive to the end of Forest Service Road 601. From there, the trail begins approximately 200 yards to the west.','2025-03-27 22:26:27','2025-03-27 22:26:27'),(9610,'trails',60,'What should I expect in the initial section of the hike?','The initial stretch from FS601 leading up to Proctor Canyon offers a thrilling downhill experience.','2025-03-27 22:26:27','2025-03-27 22:26:27'),(9611,'trails',60,'Are there any notable landmarks along the trail?','Yes, just a couple of miles in, you\'ll find a pond on the east side of the trail and three old metal beds nestled in the trees, known locally as the \'three bears camp.\'','2025-03-27 22:26:27','2025-03-27 22:26:27'),(9612,'trails',60,'What unique natural features can be seen along the trail?','Further along, you\'ll encounter a spring that appears to flow from the base of a tree, along with a small creek from another natural spring that you\'ll need to cross using a log.','2025-03-27 22:26:27','2025-03-27 22:26:27'),(9613,'trails',60,'What can I expect midway through the hike?','About five miles in, you\'ll cross the Proctor Canyon FS road and tackle a steep stretch that leads you up toward Johnson Canyon.','2025-03-27 22:26:27','2025-03-27 22:26:27'),(9614,'trails',60,'Is there a tough section on this trail?','The steepest areas of the trail are found between Proctor Canyon and Johnson Canyon, requiring a good level of fitness.','2025-03-27 22:26:27','2025-03-27 22:26:27'),(9615,'trails',60,'Are there any directional cues I should be aware of?','Prior to reaching the Johnson Canyon Junction, you\'ll spot an old pole fence and trough. Make sure to stay on the trail to the west and avoid heading over the fence to the north, which leads off the correct path.','2025-03-27 22:26:27','2025-03-27 22:26:27'),(9616,'trails',60,'What is the condition of the trail at the Hillsdale Canyon?','At Hillsdale Canyon, you\'ll cross FS642, where the trail becomes the hottest and driest, with exposed red shale, but remains mostly flat aside from a few areas that may require walking your bike.','2025-03-27 22:26:27','2025-03-27 22:26:27'),(9617,'trails',60,'How does the trail change after Thunder Mountain Trail #33098?','After you join Thunder Mountain Trail #33098, the route features a gentle downhill slope through scenic Ponderosa trees.','2025-03-27 22:26:27','2025-03-27 22:26:27'),(9618,'trails',60,'What is the overall trail etiquette I should follow?','As this is a local favorite, please adhere to \'Leave No Trace\' principles by taking out everything you bring in.','2025-03-27 22:26:27','2025-03-27 22:26:27'),(9619,'trails',60,'What are some characteristics of the trail?','The Grand View Trail is considered intermediate to difficult, spans 13.9 miles, and boasts stunning views, wildflowers, and wildlife encounters.','2025-03-27 22:26:27','2025-03-27 22:26:27'),(9620,'trails',60,'What elevations can I expect on this trail?','The trail reaches a highest elevation of 7,080 feet and a lowest elevation that is also 7,080 feet, with a total incline of 1,279 feet and a decline of 2,821 feet.','2025-03-27 22:26:27','2025-03-27 22:26:27'),(9621,'trails',60,'Is the trail suitable for dogs?','Yes, dogs are welcome on this trail and can be off-leash.','2025-03-27 22:26:27','2025-03-27 22:26:27'),(9622,'trails',60,'What are the geographical coordinates of the trail?','The Grand View Trail is located at a latitude of 37.5911 and a longitude of -112.359.','2025-03-27 22:26:27','2025-03-27 22:26:27'),(9623,'trails',45,'What is the purpose of this trail?','This trail serves as a stunning alternative to a section of the Golden Wall Trail, offering hikers an up-close view of remarkable geological formations.','2025-03-27 22:26:43','2025-03-27 22:26:43'),(9624,'trails',45,'What is the difficulty level of the trail?','The trail is rated as intermediate to difficult, making it suitable for those with some hiking experience.','2025-03-27 22:26:43','2025-03-27 22:26:43'),(9625,'trails',45,'What is the highest elevation of the trail?','The highest point on the trail reaches an elevation of 7,375 feet.','2025-03-27 22:26:43','2025-03-27 22:26:43'),(9626,'trails',45,'What is the lowest elevation of the trail?','The lowest elevation along the trail is also 7,375 feet.','2025-03-27 22:26:43','2025-03-27 22:26:43'),(9627,'trails',45,'What is the length of the trail?','The trail spans a distance of 0.6 miles.','2025-03-27 22:26:43','2025-03-27 22:26:43'),(9628,'trails',45,'What type of trail is this?','This is a point-to-point trail, meaning you will start and end at different points.','2025-03