','2025-03-27 22:28:16'),(9731,'trails',6,'What is the highest elevation on the trail?','The highest point on the trail reaches 7,596 feet.','2025-03-27 22:28:16','2025-03-27 22:28:16'),(9732,'trails',6,'Are dogs allowed on the trail?','Yes, dogs are permitted on the trail and can be off-leash.','2025-03-27 22:28:16','2025-03-27 22:28:16'),(9733,'trails',6,'What type of terrain can hikers expect on the Blowhard Mountain Trail?','Hikers will experience steep, rocky ascents, narrow canyons, and sections along cliff edges, transitioning into pine forests with gentle undulating terrain.','2025-03-27 22:28:16','2025-03-27 22:28:16'),(9734,'trails',6,'What notable features does this trail offer?','The trail offers stunning cliffside views and opportunities to observe local wildlife, such as grazing sheep in the pasture area.','2025-03-27 22:28:16','2025-03-27 22:28:16'),(9735,'trails',6,'What should I be cautious about when hiking with a dog?','Keep an eye on your dog, especially around the sheep grazing in the pasture, and ensure you secure the gate after passing through it.','2025-03-27 22:28:16','2025-03-27 22:28:16'),(9736,'trails',6,'How does the trail progress after the first mile?','After the initial steep climb, the trail flattens slightly as it heads into a pine forest, allowing for a more gentle hike for the next couple of miles.','2025-03-27 22:28:16','2025-03-27 22:28:16'),(9737,'trails',6,'What is the elevation gain on the trail?','The trail features a significant elevation gain of 3,285 feet.','2025-03-27 22:28:16','2025-03-27 22:28:16'),(9738,'trails',6,'Is the Blowhard Mountain Trail point-to-point or a loop?','This trail is a point-to-point route, leading hikers up to the upper trailhead near the Doppler radar station.','2025-03-27 22:28:16','2025-03-27 22:28:16'),(9739,'trails',6,'What notable landmarks should hikers look for along the trail?','Key landmarks include a steep rocky hill known as the \'breaks\', a transmission line crossing, and the Doppler radar station at the trail\'s upper end.','2025-03-27 22:28:16','2025-03-27 22:28:16'),(9740,'trails',6,'Are there any intersections with other trails?','Yes, the Blowhard Mountain Trail intersects with the Potato Hollow Trail around mile 3.9, where you can continue straight through a meadow.','2025-03-27 22:28:16','2025-03-27 22:28:16'),(9741,'trails',6,'What can hikers expect at the start of the trail?','The trail begins with a steep singletrack ascent through a narrow canyon, providing a challenging start to the hike.','2025-03-27 22:28:16','2025-03-27 22:28:16'),(9742,'trails',6,'Are there any significant switchbacks on the trail?','Yes, there are a series of steep switchbacks around mile 5.3 as the trail navigates around the ridge.','2025-03-27 22:28:16','2025-03-27 22:28:16'),(9743,'trails',6,'What references are available for map coordinates?','The geographical coordinates for the trail are approximately 37.616 latitude and -112.932 longitude.','2025-03-27 22:28:16','2025-03-27 22:28:16'),(9744,'trails',7,'What is the general experience like on Dark Hollow Trail?','The Dark Hollow Trail offers an adventurous hike with steep, rugged descents and sharp, rocky switchbacks. It\'s an exhilarating journey that concludes with breathtaking mountain vistas and stunning red rock cliffs.','2025-03-27 22:28:24','2025-03-27 22:28:24'),(9745,'trails',7,'What is the difficulty level of Dark Hollow Trail?','This trail is rated as difficult, making it suitable for experienced hikers looking for a challenging trek.','2025-03-27 22:28:24','2025-03-27 22:28:24'),(9746,'trails',7,'What are the elevation stats for Dark Hollow Trail?','The trail\'s highest and lowest elevation is 8,695 feet, providing a unique high-altitude hiking experience.','2025-03-27 22:28:24','2025-03-27 22:28:24'),(9747,'trails',7,'How long is Dark Hollow Trail?','The total length of Dark Hollow Trail is 4.6 miles, making it a manageable yet challenging hike.','2025-03-27 22:28:24','2025-03-27 22:28:24'),(9