g cliffs and impressive rock formations, making it a visual treat for hikers.','2025-03-27 22:34:00','2025-03-27 22:34:00'),(10089,'trails',42,'What is the difficulty level of the Boulder Dash trail?','This trail is classified as very difficult, so it\'s best suited for experienced hikers seeking a challenging adventure.','2025-03-27 22:34:00','2025-03-27 22:34:00'),(10090,'trails',42,'What is the highest elevation along the Boulder Dash trail?','The trail reaches an elevation of 6,516 feet, providing a high vantage point and rewarding views.','2025-03-27 22:34:00','2025-03-27 22:34:00'),(10091,'trails',42,'What is the lowest elevation on the Boulder Dash trail?','The lowest elevation on this trail is also 6,516 feet, indicating that the trail does not descend significantly.','2025-03-27 22:34:00','2025-03-27 22:34:00'),(10092,'trails',42,'How long is the Boulder Dash trail?','The Boulder Dash trail is 0.7 miles long, making it a short yet challenging hike.','2025-03-27 22:34:00','2025-03-27 22:34:00'),(10093,'trails',42,'What type of trail is the Boulder Dash?','Boulder Dash is a point-to-point trail, meaning it starts and ends at different locations.','2025-03-27 22:34:00','2025-03-27 22:34:00'),(10094,'trails',42,'What is the incline and decline of the Boulder Dash trail?','The trail features an incline of 55 feet and a decline of 282 feet, contributing to its challenging nature.','2025-03-27 22:34:00','2025-03-27 22:34:00'),(10095,'trails',42,'What are the average and maximum grades of the Boulder Dash trail?','The average grade of the trail is approximately 0.10%, while the maximum grade reaches up to 0.23%, making for varied hiking conditions.','2025-03-27 22:34:00','2025-03-27 22:34:00'),(10096,'trails',42,'Can you provide the geographical coordinates for the Boulder Dash trail?','Certainly! The geographical coordinates for the trail are approximately 37.6355° latitude and -113.075° longitude.','2025-03-27 22:34:00','2025-03-27 22:34:00'),(10097,'trails',43,'What are the views like on Thunder Mountain Trail?','Hikers can expect stunning views of Thunder Mountain, offering breathtaking sights throughout the trail, complemented by sweeping hills and valleys ideal for photography.','2025-03-27 22:34:08','2025-03-27 22:34:08'),(10098,'trails',43,'How is the trail terrain described?','The majority of the Thunder Mountain Trail features smooth hard-packed surfaces, though there are short segments that include steep, loose switchbacks that add a bit of challenge.','2025-03-27 22:34:08','2025-03-27 22:34:08'),(10099,'trails',43,'What is the overall difficulty of the Thunder Mountain Trail?','This trail is classified as intermediate, making it a manageable hike for those with some experience and fitness.','2025-03-27 22:34:08','2025-03-27 22:34:08'),(10100,'trails',43,'What is the elevation range on this trail?','The highest point along the trail reaches 7,085 feet, while the lowest point also stands at 7,085 feet, although it features a varying incline of 1,706 feet and a decline of 711 feet.','2025-03-27 22:34:08','2025-03-27 22:34:08'),(10101,'trails',43,'What is the length and type of the trail?','Thunder Mountain Trail spans 8 miles and is a point-to-point trail that can be navigated in either direction.','2025-03-27 22:34:08','2025-03-27 22:34:08'),(10102,'trails',43,'What should I know about camping near the trail?','Just east of the Red Canyon Visitor Center, there is a fantastic Federal campground with amenities like flush toilets, paid hot showers, and BBQ grills nestled among trees. Online reservations are available, but it\'s often possible to find great spots on a walk-in basis, especially if you arrive early.','2025-03-27 22:34:08','2025-03-27 22:34:08'),(10103,'trails',43,'Are there alternative camping options available?','Yes, in addition to the Federal campground, there are several free campsites managed by the Bureau of Land Management (BLM) in the nearby area.','2025-03-27 22:34:08','2025-03-27 22:34:08'),(10104,'trails',43,'What unique features can hikers expect on this trail?','The trail offers unique features resembling those found in Sedona, paired with harboring remarkable views that echo the beauty of Bryce Canyon.','2025-03-27 22:34:08','2025-03-27 22:34:08'),(10105,'trails',43,'Can I bring my dog on this trail?','The policy regarding dogs on Thunder Mountain Trail is currently unknown.','2025-03-27 22:34:08','2025-03-27 22:34:08'),(10106,'trails',43,'What is the average and maximum grade of the trail?','The average grade of the trail is approximately 0.06%, with a maximum grade reaching 0.31%, indicating a relatively gentle ascent and descent overall.','2025-03-27 22:34:08','2025-03-27 22:34:08'),(10107,'trails',44,'What is the Golden Wall Trail #33095?','The Golden Wall Trail #33095 is a picturesque hike that takes you through beautiful ponderosa pine forests, showcasing stunning golden and red rock formations.','2025-03-27 22:34:17','2025-03-27 22:34:17'),(10108,'trails',44,'How accessible is the Golden Wall Trail?','This trail is easily reachable from the road and is located close to the visitor center, making it a convenient option for families and casual hikers.','2025-03-27 22:34:17','2025-03-27 22:34:17'),(10109,'trails',44,'What is the trail length of the Golden Wall Trail?','The Golden Wall Trail stretches for approximately 2.9 miles and can be enjoyed as a short out-and-back hike or as part of a longer loop.','2025-03-27 22:34:17','2025-03-27 22:34:17'),(10110,'trails',44,'What is the difficulty level of the trail?','The Golden Wall Trail is classified as intermediate to difficult, offering a moderate challenge for experienced hikers.','2025-03-27 22:34:17','2025-03-27 22:34:17'),(10111,'trails',44,'What are the elevation details for the Golden Wall Trail?','The trail reaches a maximum elevation of 7,157 feet, with a total incline of 925 feet and a decline of 442 feet.','2025-03-27 22:34:17','2025-03-27 22:34:17'),(10112,'trails',44,'What types of views can hikers expect on this trail?','Hikers can enjoy beautiful scenic views of the golden and red rock walls that give the trail its name, along with the tranquil surroundings of ponderosa pines.','2025-03-27 22:34:17','2025-03-27 22:34:17'),(10113,'trails',44,'Are dogs allowed on the Golden Wall Trail?','Yes, dogs are permitted on the trail and are allowed to roam off-leash, making it a great outing for pet owners.','2025-03-27 22:34:17','2025-03-27 22:34:17'),(10114,'trails',44,'What is the maximum grade of the Golden Wall Trail?','The trail features a maximum grade of 0.26%, making it a relatively gentle hike overall.','2025-03-27 22:34:17','2025-03-27 22:34:17'),(10115,'trails',44,'What are the coordinates for the Golden Wall Trail?','The trail is located at a latitude of 37.7466 and a longitude of -112.322.','2025-03-27 22:34:17','2025-03-27 22:34:17'),(10116,'trails',46,'Where does the Buckhorn Trail #33037 start?','The Buckhorn Trail begins at the Red Canyon Campground.','2025-03-27 22:34:27','2025-03-27 22:34:27'),(10117,'trails',46,'What kind of terrain can I expect on the Buckhorn Trail?','Hikers will encounter stunning red rock terrain as they ascend the trail.','2025-03-27 22:34:27','2025-03-27 22:34:27'),(10118,'trails',46,'What is the vantage point on this trail?','The trail leads to a beautiful overlook of Red Canyon, providing breathtaking views.','2025-03-27 22:34:27','2025-03-27 22:34:27'),(10119,'trails',46,'Is there a junction on the Buckhorn Trail within the first mile?','Yes, about 0.75 miles into the hike, there\'s a junction with the Golden Wall Trail #33095.','2025-03-27 22:34:27','2025-03-27 22:34:27'),(10120,'trails',46,'How do I continue on the Buckhorn Trail at the junction?','To stay on the Buckhorn Trail, keep to the right at the junction.','2025-03-27 22:34:27','2025-03-27 22:34:27'),(10121,'trails',46,'What is the trail length of Buckhorn Trail?','The Buckhorn Trail is approximately 0.9 miles long.','2025-03-27 22:34:27','2025-03-27 