'What are the elevation levels of the Pink Ledges Trail?','The trail maintains a consistent elevation at 7,189 feet, with a slight incline of 139 feet and a decrease of 131 feet.','2025-03-27 22:34:37','2025-03-27 22:34:37'),(10133,'trails',47,'What type of trail is the Pink Ledges Trail?','This is a point-to-point trail, allowing you to explore its features in both directions.','2025-03-27 22:34:37','2025-03-27 22:34:37'),(10134,'trails',47,'Are dogs allowed on the Pink Ledges Trail?','Yes, dogs are permitted on the trail, but they must be kept on a leash.','2025-03-27 22:34:37','2025-03-27 22:34:37'),(10135,'trails',47,'What unique features can I expect to see on the Pink Ledges Trail?','Hikers on the Pink Ledges Trail can enjoy stunning views and observe unique geological formations including hoodoos and alcoves that characterize the landscape.','2025-03-27 22:34:37','2025-03-27 22:34:37'),(10136,'trails',47,'Is the Pink Ledges Trail family-friendly?','Absolutely! The trail is designed to be family-friendly, making it a great option for visitors of all ages.','2025-03-27 22:34:37','2025-03-27 22:34:37'),(10137,'trails',47,'What is the average grade of the Pink Ledges Trail?','The average grade of the trail is a gentle 0.09%, ensuring a relatively easy hike.','2025-03-27 22:34:37','2025-03-27 22:34:37'),(10138,'trails',47,'What is the maximum grade encountered on the Pink Ledges Trail?','The trail features a maximum grade of 0.23%, providing an enjoyable hike without strenuous climbs.','2025-03-27 22:34:37','2025-03-27 22:34:37'),(10139,'trails',47,'What are the geographical coordinates of the Pink Ledges Trail?','The geographical coordinates for the Pink Ledges Trail are approximately 37.7452° latitude and -112.318° longitude.','2025-03-27 22:34:37','2025-03-27 22:34:37'),(10140,'trails',48,'What is the Birdseye Trail #33097?','The Birdseye Trail #33097 is a short, family-friendly hike that takes you through stunning rock formations near the highway, providing an accessible experience for all ages.','2025-03-27 22:34:44','2025-03-27 22:34:44'),(10141,'trails',48,'How long is the Birdseye Trail?','The total length of the Birdseye Trail is 0.8 miles, making it a manageable option for families and those with shorter attention spans.','2025-03-27 22:34:44','2025-03-27 22:34:44'),(10142,'trails',48,'What is the difficulty level of the Birdseye Trail?','The trail is rated as intermediate, which means it may present some challenges, but it is still suitable for families and casual hikers.','2025-03-27 22:34:44','2025-03-27 22:34:44'),(10143,'trails',48,'What is the elevation range on the Birdseye Trail?','The trail maintains a steady elevation at 7,127 feet, with an incline of 89 feet and a decline of 124 feet.','2025-03-27 22:34:44','2025-03-27 22:34:44'),(10144,'trails',48,'Is the Birdseye Trail a loop or point to point?','Birdseye Trail is a point-to-point trail, offering unique views along its length.','2025-03-27 22:34:44','2025-03-27 22:34:44'),(10145,'trails',48,'What features can hikers expect to see along the trail?','Hikers will enjoy breathtaking views of unique and beautiful red-rock formations, especially near the Visitor Center.','2025-03-27 22:34:44','2025-03-27 22:34:44'),(10146,'trails',48,'Are dogs allowed on the Birdseye Trail?','It\'s unclear whether dogs are permitted on the Birdseye Trail, so it\'s advisable to check local regulations before bringing your pet.','2025-03-27 22:34:44','2025-03-27 22:34:44'),(10147,'trails',48,'What are the geographical coordinates of the Birdseye Trail?','The Birdseye Trail is located at a latitude of 37.7472 and a longitude of -112.321.','2025-03-27 22:34:44','2025-03-27 22:34:44'),(10148,'trails',48,'What is the average and maximum grade of the trail?','The trail has an average grade of 0.05%, with a maximum grade of 0.22%, indicating that it is relatively gentle overall.','2025-03-27 22:34:45','2025-03-27 22:34:45'),(10149,'trails',50,'Is the Hoodoo Trail suitable for families?','Absolutely! The Hoodoo Trail is designed to be family-friendly, making it perfect for visitors of all ages.','2025-03-27 22:34:51','2025-03-27 22:34:51'),(10150,'trails',50,'How long is the Hoodoo Trail?','The Hoodoo Trail stretches for just 0.1 miles, making it a brief and enjoyable hike.','2025-03-27 22:34:51','2025-03-27 22:34:51'),(10151,'trails',50,'What is the difficulty level of the Hoodoo Trail?','This trail is rated as easy to intermediate, which means it\'s accessible for most hikers.','2025-03-27 22:34:51','2025-03-27 22:34:51'),(10152,'trails',50,'What are the starting and ending elevations of the Hoodoo Trail?','The trail maintains a consistent elevation of 7156 feet throughout its length.','2025-03-27 22:34:51','2025-03-27 22:34:51'),(10153,'trails',50,'What kind of terrain can I expect on the Hoodoo Trail?','The Hoodoo Trail is predominantly flat, with an incline of only 38 feet, ensuring an easy walk.','2025-03-27 22:34:51','2025-03-27 22:34:51'),(10154,'trails',50,'Are dogs allowed on the Hoodoo Trail?','Yes, leashed dogs are welcome to join you on the Hoodoo Trail.','2025-03-27 22:34:51','2025-03-27 22:34:51'),(10155,'trails',50,'What features can I see along the Hoodoo Trail?','While hiking, you\'ll be treated to stunning views of the towering red hoodoos, which are a highlight of the area.','2025-03-27 22:34:51','2025-03-27 22:34:51'),(10156,'trails',50,'What is the latitude and longitude of the Hoodoo Trail?','The Hoodoo Trail is located at a latitude of 37.747 and a longitude of -112.321.','2025-03-27 22:34:51','2025-03-27 22:34:51'),(10157,'trails',50,'What type of trail is the Hoodoo Trail?','The Hoodoo Trail is a point-to-point trail, making it easy to navigate.','2025-03-27 22:34:51','2025-03-27 22:34:51'),(10158,'trails',50,'What is the average and maximum grade of the Hoodoo Trail?','The average grade of the trail is 0.07%, with a maximum grade of 0.09%, which contributes to its easy accessibility.','2025-03-27 22:34:51','2025-03-27 22:34:51'),(10159,'trails',51,'What is the Arches Trail #33075 like for families?','The Arches Trail #33075 is a fantastic option for families, especially those with small children. The trail features fascinating rock formations such as hoodoos, arches, and turrets that spark the imagination and provide opportunities for exploration.','2025-03-27 22:35:02','2025-03-27 22:35:02'),(10160,'trails',51,'How difficult is the Arches Trail?','The trail has an intermediate level of difficulty. It\'s manageable for those who have some hiking experience, particularly because it’s relatively short.','2025-03-27 22:35:02','2025-03-27 22:35:02'),(10161,'trails',51,'What are the elevation details of the trail?','The Arches Trail reaches a maximum elevation of 7,127 feet, with a starting point at the same elevation, making it a noteworthy addition to your hiking experience.','2025-03-27 22:35:02','2025-03-27 22:35:02'),(10162,'trails',51,'How long is the Arches Trail?','The Arches Trail is half a mile in length, making it a quick hike that can easily fit into your day.','2025-03-27 22:35:02','2025-03-27 22:35:02'),(10163,'trails',51,'What kind of terrain can I expect on the trail?','This is a point-to-point trail, and hikers will encounter a short but steep incline of 178 feet. It also features a decline of 108 feet as you navigate the landscape.','2025-03-27 22:35:02','2025-03-27 22:35:02'),(10164,'trails',51,'What is the average and maximum grade of the trail?','The trail has an average grade of approximately 0.11% and a maximum grade of 0.39%, which provides a steady climb without extreme challenges.','2025-03-27 22:35:02','2025-03-27 22:35:02'),(10165,'trails',51,'What natural features can I expect along the trail?','Hikers on the Arches Trail will be treated to breathtaking views and may spot a variety of wildflowers, enhancing the overall hiking experience.','2025-03-27 22:35:02','2025-03-27 22:35:02'),(10166,'trails',51,'Are dogs allowed on the Arches Trail?','Yes, dogs are permitted on the trail and can enjoy the adventure off-leash, making it a fun outing for both pets and their owners.','2025-03-27 22:35:02','2025-03-27 22:35:02'),(10167,'trails',51,'What are the geographical coordinates of the Arches Trail?','The trail is located at a latitude of 37.7697 and a longitude of -112.334, so you can easily find it on a map or GPS.','2025-03-27 22:35:02','2025-03-27 22:35:02'),(10168,'trails',52,'What can I expect to see along the Cassidy Trail #33093?','Hikers will be treated to breathtaking rock formations, expansive views of the desert landscape, and the natural beauty that characterizes southern Utah and northern Arizona.','2025-03-27 22:35:14','2025-03-27 22:35:14'),(10169,'trails',52,'How difficult is the Cassidy Trail?','The trail is classified as easy to intermediate, making it accessible for a wide range of hikers.','2025-03-27 22:35:14','2025-03-27 22:35:14'),(10170,'trails',52,'What is the highest elevation on the Cassidy Trail?','The highest point along the Cassidy Trail reaches an elevation of 7,337 feet.','2025-03-27 22:35:14','2025-03-27 22:35:14'),(10171,'trails',52,'What is the lowest elevation on the Cassidy Trail?','The lowest elevation along the trail is also 7,337 feet, indicating a generally flat hike.','2025-03-27 22:35:14','2025-03-27 22:35:14'),(10172,'trails',52,'How long is the Cassidy Trail?','The total length of the Cassidy Trail is approximately 8.7 miles, making it a perfect option for a half-day hike.','2025-03-27 22:35:14','2025-03-27 22:35:14'),(10173,'trails',52,'What is the trail type of Cassidy Trail?','The Cassidy Trail is a point-to-point trail, meaning you will start at one point and end at another.','2025-03-27 22:35:14','2025-03-27 22:35:14'),(10174,'trails',52,'What is the elevation gain on this trail?','Hikers will experience an incline of 1,203 feet along the Cassidy Trail.','2025-03-27 22:35:14','2025-03-27 22:35:14'),(10175,'trails',52,'What is the elevation decline while hiking this trail?','During the hike, you will encounter a decline of 800 feet.','2025-03-27 22:35:14','2025-03-27 22:35:14'),(10176,'trails',52,'What is the average grade of Cassidy Trail?','The average grade of the trail is about 0.04%, making it relatively gentle.','2025-03-27 22:35:14','2025-03-27 22:35:14'),(10177,'trails',52,'What is the maximum grade on this trail?','The maximum grade experienced on the Cassidy Trail can reach up to 0.20%, indicating a mild steepness in some sections.','2025-03-27 22:35:14','2025-03-27 22:35:14'),(10178,'trails',52,'What are the geographic coordinates of the Cassidy Trail?','The trail is located at a latitude of 37.7451 and a longitude of -112.302.','2025-03-27 22:35:14','2025-03-27 22:35:14'),(10179,'trails',53,'What is the Rich Trail #33092 known for?','Rich Trail #33092 is celebrated for its breathtaking landscapes, featuring rugged canyons, impressive rock formations, and sweeping views of the surrounding desert.','2025-03-27 22:35:23','2025-03-27 22:35:23'),(10180,'trails',53,'What is the difficulty level of Rich Trail #33092?','The trail presents a challenge that ranges from easy to intermediate, making it accessible for a variety of hikers.','2025-03-27 22:35:23','2025-03-27 22:35:23'),(10181,'trails',53,'What are the highest and lowest elevations on Rich Trail #33092?','The trail reaches its highest point at 7,537 feet, and it maintains this elevation throughout, providing a consistent experience.','2025-03-27 22:35:23','2025-03-27 22:35:23'),(10182,'trails',53,'How long is the Rich Trail #33092?','Rich Trail #33092 stretches for 2.3 miles, making it a manageable hike suitable for those looking for a short adventure.','2025-03-27 22:35:23','2025-03-27 22:35:23'),(10183,'trails',53,'What type of trail is Rich Trail #33092?','This is a point-to-point trail, meaning hikers will begin and end at different locations.','2025-03-27 22:35:23','2025-03-27 22:35:23'),(10184,'trails',53,'What is the total incline and decline on Rich Trail #33092?','Hikers can expect a total incline of 469 feet and a decline of 151 feet while traversing the trail.','2025-03-27 22:35:23','2025-03-27 22:35:23'),(10185,'trails',53,'What is the average and maximum grade of Rich Trail #33092?','The trail has an average grade of 0.05%, with a maximum grade reaching up to 0.20%, indicating a relatively gentle slope.','2025-03-27 22:35:23','2025-03-27 22:35:23'),(10186,'trails',53,'What are the geographic coordinates of Rich Trail #33092?','Rich Trail #33092 is located at approximately 37.7553° latitude and -112.298° longitude.','2025-03-27 22:35:23','2025-03-27 22:35:23'),(10187,'trails',54,'What is the difficulty level of the Casto Canyon Trail?','The Casto Canyon Trail is rated as easy, making it accessible for hikers of all skill levels.','2025-03-27 22:35:32','2025-03-27 22:35:32'),(10188,'trails',54,'What is the total distance of the Casto Canyon Trail?','The trail spans approximately 5.6 miles, providing a nice route for a leisurely hike.','2025-03-27 22:35:32','2025-03-27 22:35:32'),(10189,'trails',54,'What is the elevation range of the Casto Canyon Trail?','The trail reaches a highest elevation of 7079 feet and maintains that elevation throughout, making it quite flat.','2025-03-27 22:35:32','2025-03-27 22:35:32'),(10190,'trails',54,'Is the Casto Canyon Trail a loop or point-to-point trail?','The Casto Canyon Trail is a point-to-point trail, meaning you will have to return the same way you came or arrange for transportation at one end.','2025-03-27 22:35:32','2025-03-27 22:35:32'),(10191,'trails',54,'What type of scenery can I expect along the Casto Canyon Trail?','Hikers can enjoy breathtaking views of stunning red rock formations as the trail winds along a sandy wash.','2025-03-27 22:35:32','2025-03-27 22:35:32'),(10192,'trails',54,'Are there any connecting trails from the Casto Canyon Trail?','Yes, the Casto Canyon Trail offers connections to the Fremont Trail and the Cassidy Trail for those looking to extend their hiking journey.','2025-03-27 22:35:32','2025-03-27 22:35:32'),(10193,'trails',54,'What are the incline and grade characteristics of the trail?','The trail features a modest incline of 779 feet, with an average grade of just 0.03% and a maximum grade of 0.06%, ensuring a comfortable hiking experience.','2025-03-27 22:35:32','2025-03-27 22:35:32'),(10194,'trails',54,'Are dogs allowed on the Casto Canyon Trail?','It is currently unclear whether dogs are allowed on the Casto Canyon Trail, so it\'s advisable to check local regulations before bringing your pet.','2025-03-27 22:35:32','2025-03-27 22:35:32'),(10195,'trails',54,'What are the latitude and longitude coordinates of the Casto Canyon Trail?','The trail is located at approximately 37.784° latitude and -112.332° longitude, which can help with navigation and mapping your hike.','2025-03-27 22:35:32','2025-03-27 22:35:32'),(10196,'trails',55,'What is the Oak Grove Trail like?','The Oak Grove Trail offers a steep ascent that transitions from a dusty desert landscape to a vibrant pine forest, showcasing stunning views of the Colorado Plateau and impressive granite cliffs along the way.','2025-03-27 22:35:42','2025-03-27 22:35:42'),(10197,'trails',55,'What kind of scenery can I expect on this trail?','Hikers will experience breathtaking vistas that include distant red rock formations, deep canyons, and unique granite boulders, particularly as the trail winds through the Pine Valley Mountains.','2025-03-27 22:35:42','2025-03-27 22:35:42'),(10198,'trails',55,'How challenging is the Oak Grove Trail?','This trail is considered difficult due to its steep nature and significant elevation gain, making it more suitable for experienced hikers.','2025-03-27 22:35:42','2025-03-27 22:35:42'),(10199,'trails',55,'What is the length and elevation change of the trail?','The Oak Grove Trail is 3.3 miles long, featuring an incline of 3,318 feet and a decline of 117 feet, culminating at a peak elevation of 6,549 feet.','2025-03-27 22:35:42','2025-03-27 22:35:42'),(10200,'trails',55,'What are the ecosystems I will pass through on the trail?','Hikers will traverse two main ecosystems—starting in a dusty desert and gradually moving into a lush pine forest filled with wildflowers and potential snow remnants during summer.','2025-03-27 22:35:42','2025-03-27 22:35:42'),(10201,'trails',55,'Are dogs allowed on the Oak Grove Trail?','It is currently unclear whether dogs are allowed on this trail, so it’s advised to check local regulations before bringing your pet.','2025-03-27 22:35:42','2025-03-27 22:35:42'),(10202,'trails',55,'What kind of trail is it?','The Oak Grove Trail is a point-to-point trail, allowing hikers to journey from one endpoint to another, specifically designed to navigate the steep terrain.','2025-03-27 22:35:42','2025-03-27 22:35:42'),(10203,'trails',55,'What should I keep in mind regarding the trail\'s condition?','Despite being constructed a long time ago, the trails and switchbacks are maintained well, making it generally easy to follow for hikers.','2025-03-27 22:35:42','2025-03-27 22:35:42'),(10204,'trails',55,'Will there be shaded areas along the trail?','Yes, as you ascend and reach the evergreen forest at the trail\'s end, you\'ll find plenty of shaded areas that provide relief from the sun.','2025-03-27 22:35:42','2025-03-27 22:35:42'),(10205,'trails',55,'What kind of views can I expect as I hike?','The trail offers increasingly magnificent views of the surrounding landscapes, including sights of St. George and the red rocks of Snow Canyon State Park, especially as you gain elevation.','2025-03-27 22:35:42','2025-03-27 22:35:42'),(10206,'trails',60,'What is the Grand View Trail #601 like?','The Grand View Trail #601 offers a scenic journey through aspen groves, black timber, and meadows, featuring a pond, an old sheep camp, a spring/bog, and a creek, along with stunning views of pink cliffs and the valley floor.','2025-03-27 22:35:53','2025-03-27 22:35:53'),(10207,'trails',60,'How do I access the Grand View Trail #601?','Access the trail by heading to the end of FS601, where the trail begins approximately 200 yards west.','2025-03-27 22:35:53','2025-03-27 22:35:53'),(10208,'trails',60,'What should I expect at the beginning of the trail?','The initial section of the trail from FS601 descends quickly, allowing for a thrilling downhill experience early in your hike.','2025-03-27 22:35:53','2025-03-27 22:35:53'),(10209,'trails',60,'Are there any notable sights along the trail?','Yes, just a couple of miles into the hike, you\'ll encounter a pond on the east side, further along you\'ll find three old metal beds from an old sheep camp known locally as the \'three bears camp.\'','2025-03-27 22:35:53','2025-03-27 22:35:53'),(10210,'trails',60,'Is there water available on the trail?','Yes, after the sheep camp, there is a spring/bog and a creek from a natural spring, which you\'ll cross using a log.','2025-03-27 22:35:53','2025-03-27 22:35:53'),(10211,'trails',60,'What is the most challenging part of the trail?','The steepest sections are found between Proctor and Johnson Canyon, so be prepared for some rigorous climbs and descents.','2025-03-27 22:35:53','2025-03-27 22:35:53'),(10212,'trails',60,'Are there any trail markers or signs?','Yes, look out for FS signs at the Johnson Canyon Junction to guide you; be sure to stay right towards the trail to Red Canyon.','2025-03-27 22:35:53','2025-03-27 22:35:53'),(10213,'trails',60,'What should I know about the Hillsdale Canyon crossing?','At Hillsdale Canyon, you’ll cross FS642, which is the warmest and driest part of the trail, offering exposed red shale sections.','2025-03-27 22:35:53','2025-03-27 22:35:53'),(10214,'trails',60,'What can I expect after the Thunder Mountain Trail #33098?','From there, the trail gradually descends through the Ponderosas, providing a gentle downhill trek with beautiful surrounding scenery.','2025-03-27 22:35:53','2025-03-27 22:35:53'),(10215,'trails',60,'What is the overall difficulty of the Grand View Trail?','The trail is classified as intermediate to difficult, making it suitable for experienced hikers.','2025-03-27 22:35:53','2025-03-27 22:35:53'),(10216,'trails',60,'What are the elevation details of the trail?','The trail reaches a maximum elevation of 7080 feet and features an incline of 1279 feet and a decline of 2821 feet.','2025-03-27 22:35:53','2025-03-27 22:35:53'),(10217,'trails',60,'What is the total length of the trail?','The Grand View Trail spans 13.9 miles and is established as a point-to-point trail.','2025-03-27 22:35:53','2025-03-27 22:35:53'),(10218,'trails',60,'Are pets allowed on the trail?','Yes, dogs are allowed off-leash along the trail.','2025-03-27 22:35:53','2025-03-27 22:35:53'),(10219,'trails',60,'What should I remember when hiking this trail?','As this is a local running trail, please remember to pack out whatever you bring with you to help keep it clean.','2025-03-27 22:35:53','2025-03-27 22:35:53'),(10220,'trails',61,'What is the starting point of the hike?','The hike begins across the road from the Pine Valley Equestrian campground, heading north into the beautiful pine forests of Gardner Peak.','2025-03-27 22:36:00','2025-03-27 22:36:00'),(10221,'trails',61,'What can I expect in terms of terrain and elevation during the hike?','The trail features an ascent for approximately 1 1/2 miles before turning east for the remainder of the distance. Hikers will experience a total elevation gain of 1867 feet, reaching a peak elevation of 6647 feet.','2025-03-27 22:36:00','2025-03-27 22:36:00'),(10222,'trails',61,'How long is the trail?','The total distance of the trail is 3.4 miles, making it a manageable hike for those seeking a rewarding viewpoint.','2025-03-27 22:36:00','2025-03-27 22:36:00'),(10223,'trails',61,'What is the difficulty level of this hike?','This hike is considered intermediate to difficult, catering to those with some hiking experience.','2025-03-27 22:36:00','2025-03-27 22:36:00'),(10224,'trails',61,'Are there any notable features along the hike?','Yes, hikers can enjoy breathtaking views from the overlook at the end of the trail, which enhances the overall experience.','2025-03-27 22:36:00','2025-03-27 22:36:00'),(10225,'trails',61,'Is the trail a loop or point-to-point?','The trail is a point-to-point route, requiring hikers to plan for their return from the viewpoint.','2025-03-27 22:36:00','2025-03-27 22:36:00'),(10226,'trails',61,'What are the incline and decline stats for this hike?','The trail has a total incline of 1867 feet and a minor decline of 29 feet, indicating a primarily uphill journey.','2025-03-27 22:36:00','2025-03-27 22:36:00'),(10227,'trails',61,'What is the average grade of the trail?','The average grade of the trail is about 0.11%, which can vary in slope along different sections of the hike.','2025-03-27 22:36:00','2025-03-27 22:36:00'),(10228,'trails',61,'What is the maximum grade on this trail?','The trail features a maximum grade of 0.25%, which may pose a challenge in certain areas.','2025-03-27 22:36:00','2025-03-27 22:36:00'),(10229,'trails',61,'Are dogs allowed on this trail?','Information about dog permission on this trail is currently unknown, so it\'s advisable to check local regulations before visiting.','2025-03-27 22:36:00','2025-03-27 22:36:00'),(10230,'trails',61,'What are the geographical coordinates of the trail?','The geographical coordinates of the trail are approximately 37.3842° latitude and -113.483° longitude.','2025-03-27 22:36:00','2025-03-27 22:36:00'),(10231,'trails',62,'What type of terrain can I expect on the Race Course Loop?','Hikers will encounter a diverse range of terrains on the Race Course Loop, including sandy stretches, challenging climbs, downhill portions, and rugged sections, all offering stunning views.','2025-03-27 22:36:07','2025-03-27 22:36:07'),(10232,'trails',62,'What is the difficulty level of the Race Course Loop?','The trail is rated as intermediate, making it suitable for those with