at the end.','2025-03-27 22:43:06','2025-03-27 22:43:06'),(10497,'trails',85,'Are dogs allowed on the Hurricane Wash trail?','Unfortunately, dogs are not permitted on this trail, ensuring a quieter experience for all hikers.','2025-03-27 22:43:06','2025-03-27 22:43:06'),(10498,'trails',85,'What are the exact coordinates of the trail?','The trail is located at latitude 37.3855 and longitude -111.132, making it easy to find on a map.','2025-03-27 22:43:06','2025-03-27 22:43:06'),(10499,'trails',88,'What is the Wahweep Hoodoos trail like?','The Wahweep Hoodoos trail is a family-friendly hike featuring stunning geological formations that spark the imagination, including toadstools, hoodoos, and unique floatstone-like structures.','2025-03-27 22:43:17','2025-03-27 22:43:17'),(10500,'trails',88,'Is the Wahweep Hoodoos trail suitable for families?','Absolutely! This trail is designed to be family-friendly, making it a great choice for hikers of all ages, including young children.','2025-03-27 22:43:17','2025-03-27 22:43:17'),(10501,'trails',88,'What is the difficulty level of the Wahweep Hoodoos trail?','The trail is classified as intermediate, making it a moderate challenge for most hikers.','2025-03-27 22:43:17','2025-03-27 22:43:17'),(10502,'trails',88,'What are the elevation details for the Wahweep Hoodoos trail?','The trail has an elevation range with a highest point of 4,041 feet and a lowest point also at 4,041 feet.','2025-03-27 22:43:18','2025-03-27 22:43:18'),(10503,'trails',88,'How long is the Wahweep Hoodoos trail?','The total length of the Wahweep Hoodoos trail is 4.4 miles, making it a manageable hike for families.','2025-03-27 22:43:18','2025-03-27 22:43:18'),(10504,'trails',88,'What type of trail is Wahweep Hoodoos?','Wahweep Hoodoos is a point-to-point trail, meaning you will hike to a destination and then return by the same route.','2025-03-27 22:43:18','2025-03-27 22:43:18'),(10505,'trails',88,'What is the elevation change while hiking the Wahweep Hoodoos trail?','The trail features a slight incline of 237 feet and a minimal decline of just 1 foot.','2025-03-27 22:43:18','2025-03-27 22:43:18'),(10506,'trails',88,'What scenic features can I expect on the Wahweep Hoodoos trail?','Hikers will enjoy beautiful views, wildflowers in bloom, and the possibility of spotting wildlife along the route.','2025-03-27 22:43:18','2025-03-27 22:43:18'),(10507,'trails',88,'Are dogs allowed on the Wahweep Hoodoos trail?','Yes, dogs are allowed on the trail and can be enjoyed off-leash.','2025-03-27 22:43:18','2025-03-27 22:43:18'),(10508,'trails',88,'What are the coordinates of the Wahweep Hoodoos trail?','The trail is located at latitude 37.1122 and longitude -111.689.','2025-03-27 22:43:18','2025-03-27 22:43:18'),(10509,'trails',89,'What is the difficulty level of the Yellow Rock Trail?','The Yellow Rock Trail is classified as difficult, so hikers should be prepared for a challenging experience.','2025-03-27 22:43:28','2025-03-27 22:43:28'),(10510,'trails',89,'Where does the hike start?','The hike begins at an unmarked parking area on Cottonwood Canyon Road, located approximately 14 miles north of US 89.','2025-03-27 22:43:28','2025-03-27 22:43:28'),(10511,'trails',89,'How can I find the starting point of the trail?','Since Yellow Rock isn\'t visible from the road, the easiest way to locate the starting point is to go to the nearby Hackberry Canyon parking area, which is marked, and then backtrack 0.2 miles south past a dirt road heading east.','2025-03-27 22:43:28','2025-03-27 22:43:28'),(10512,'trails',89,'What obstacles will I encounter when crossing the creek?','To begin the hike, you\'ll need to traverse Cottonwood Creek. Depending on the season, be prepared to wade through a shallow stream or find a dry crossing during the summer months.','2025-03-27 22:43:28','2025-03-27 22:43:28'),(10513,'trails',89,'What should I expect after I start the hike?','Shortly after beginning your ascent in the canyon, you\'ll notice an eroded trail heading steeply up the ravine to your right, which is relatively easy to navigate.','2025-03-27 22:43:28','2025-03-27 22:43:28'),(10514,'trails',89,'How can I ensure I find my way back down?','Pay attention to your ascent, noting key landmarks, as it\'s easy to lose your way on the descent. Make mental notes of your route.','2025-03-27 22:43:28','2025-03-27 22:43:28'),(10515,'trails',89,'What can I find at the summit?','The summit offers a broad, flat area with stunning 360-degree views. Explore various colorful rock formations, including a notable castle-like rock to the southwest.','2025-03-27 22:43:28','2025-03-27 22:43:28'),(10516,'trails',89,'What kind of scenery can I expect on this hike?','Expect to see a magnificent dome of yellow sandstone adorned with streaks of red, pink, and white. The summit is rich in diverse colors and textures.','2025-03-27 22:43:28','2025-03-27 22:43:28'),(10517,'trails',89,'What are the trail specifications?','The Yellow Rock Trail is a point-to-point route, approximately 1 mile long, with the highest elevation reaching 4,753 feet and a total incline of 667 feet.','2025-03-27 22:43:28','2025-03-27 22:43:28'),(10518,'trails',89,'Are dogs allowed on the trail?','Yes, dogs are permitted off-leash on the Yellow Rock Trail, making it a great hike for animal companions.','2025-03-27 22:43:28','2025-03-27 22:43:28'),(10519,'trails',89,'What is the average and maximum grade of the trail?','The average grade of the trail is about 0.13%, with the maximum grade reaching up to 0.30%.','2025-03-27 22:43:28','2025-03-27 22:43:28'),(10520,'trails',96,'What is the overall difficulty of the Bull Valley Gorge Route?','The Bull Valley Gorge Route is categorized as difficult, making it suitable for experienced hikers looking for a challenging adventure.','2025-03-27 22:43:35','2025-03-27 22:43:35'),(10521,'trails',96,'What is the highest elevation along the Bull Valley Gorge Route?','The highest point on the trail reaches an elevation of 5,404 feet, offering spectacular views of the surrounding landscape.','2025-03-27 22:43:35','2025-03-27 22:43:35'),(10522,'trails',96,'What is the lowest elevation along the Bull Valley Gorge Route?','The lowest elevation on this hike also stands at 5,404 feet, indicating that the trail maintains a relatively high altitude throughout.','2025-03-27 22:43:35','2025-03-27 22:43:35'),(10523,'trails',96,'How long is the Bull Valley Gorge Route?','This trail stretches 6.1 miles, making it a substantial hike that requires proper preparation and stamina.','2025-03-27 22:43:35','2025-03-27 22:43:35'),(10524,'trails',96,'What type of trail is the Bull Valley Gorge Route?','The trail is a point-to-point route, which means you will need to plan for a return trip or arrange for transportation at the end.','2025-03-27 22:43:35','2025-03-27 22:43:35'),(10525,'trails',96,'What is the elevation gain and loss on the Bull Valley Gorge Route?','Hikers can expect an elevation gain of 194 feet along with a descent of 834 feet, making for a diverse hiking experience.','2025-03-27 22:43:35','2025-03-27 22:43:35'),(10526,'trails',96,'What is the average grade of the Bull Valley Gorge Route?','The average grade of the trail is a gentle 0.03%, which makes some sections more manageable, although the overall terrain can still be tough.','2025-03-27 22:43:35','2025-03-27 22:43:35'),(10527,'trails',96,'What is the maximum grade encountered on the Bull Valley Gorge Route?','The trail has a maximum grade of 0.09%, presenting some challenging spots that can test your hiking skills.','2025-03-27 22:43:35','2025-03-27 22:43:35'),(10528,'trails',96,'What are the coordinates for the Bull Valley Gorge Route?','The geographical coordinates for this trail are approximately 37.4732° latitude and -112.116° longitude, easy to use for navigation.','2025-03-27 22:43:35','2025-03-27 22:43:35'),(10529,'trails',97,'What is the experience like on the South Rim Trail?','The South Rim Trail is characterized by its technical features, with ups and downs over large sandstone mounds, twists through narrow rock canyons, and areas that run along edges, all providing stunning views throughout the hike.','2025-03-27 22:43:47','2025-03-27 22:43:47'),(10530,'trails',97,'What is the elevation of the Gooseberry Mesa trail network?','The Gooseberry Mesa trail network is located at an elevation of 5200 feet on a slickrock mesa.','2025-03-27 22:43:47','2025-03-27 22:43:47'),(10531,'trails',97,'How is the trail marked?','The trail is indicated by white paint dots on the slickrock and features informative signs at trail junctions to help guide you along.','2025-03-27 22:43:47','2025-03-27 22:43:47'),(10532,'trails',97,'Is the trail easy to navigate?','While the trail system can feel somewhat like a maze, it is generally easy to follow for most hikers.','2025-03-27 22:43:47','2025-03-27 22:43:47'),(10533,'trails',97,'What should first-time hikers consider?','First-time visitors might want to start with the Practice Trail to gain some experience before tackling the South Rim Trail.','2025-03-27 22:43:47','2025-03-27 22:43:47'),(10534,'trails',97,'What amenities are available for hikers?','Hikers should bring plenty of water, as there are no drinking water sources available on the mesa.','2025-03-27 22:43:47','2025-03-27 22:43:47'),(10535,'trails',97,'Is camping allowed in the area?','Yes, primitive camping is permitted in the vicinity for those looking to extend their adventure.','2025-03-27 22:43:47','2025-03-27 22:43:47'),(10536,'trails',97,'What is the route of the South Rim Trail?','The trail begins at the White Trailhead and heads south, terminating at a viewpoint on the western edge of the mesa.','2025-03-27 22:43:47','2025-03-27 22:43:47'),(10537,'trails',97,'How difficult is the South Rim Trail?','The South Rim Trail is rated as difficult, featuring more substantial climbs and descents compared to other trails in the area.','2025-03-27 22:43:47','2025-03-27 22:43:47'),(10538,'trails',97,'What is the total length and type of the South Rim Trail?','The South Rim Trail is a point-to-point trail that spans 5.6 miles.','2025-03-27 22:43:47','2025-03-27 22:43:47'),(10539,'trails',97,'What is the elevation change on the trail?','The trail features an incline of 382 feet and a decline of 184 feet throughout its course.','2025-03-27 22:43:47','2025-03-27 22:43:47'),(10540,'trails',97,'What kind of views can hikers expect?','Hikers will enjoy picturesque vistas along the trail, especially since it traverses higher and more exposed areas.','2025-03-27 22:43:47','2025-03-27 22:43:47'),(10541,'trails',97,'Can I bring my dog on the South Rim Trail?','It is currently unknown if dogs are allowed on the South Rim Trail, so it\'s best to check local regulations before your visit.','2025-03-27 22:43:47','2025-03-27 22:43:47'),(10542,'trails',97,'What are the geographical coordinates of the trail?','The South Rim Trail is located at latitude 37.1419 and longitude -113.172.','2025-03-27 22:43:47','2025-03-27 22:43:47'),(10543,'trails',98,'What is the North Rim Trail like?','The North Rim Trail offers a technical and challenging hiking experience, navigating through tight rock canyons and featuring house-sized sandstone mounds that provide stunning views.','2025-03-27 22:43:55','2025-03-27 22:43:55'),(10544,'trails',98,'Where is the Gooseberry Mesa trail network located?','The Gooseberry Mesa trail network is situated at an elevation of 5200 feet on a slickrock mesa, offering a variety of trail options.','2025-03-27 22:43:55','2025-03-27 22:43:55'),(10545,'trails',98,'How is the North Rim Trail marked?','The trail is marked with white paint dots on the slickrock and includes signs at junctions, making it relatively straightforward to follow despite its maze-like nature.','2025-03-27 22:43:55','2025-03-27 22:43:55'),(10546,'trails',98,'What is the recommended beginner trail for newcomers?','If it\'s your first time hiking in this area, consider trying the Practice Trail first to get accustomed to the terrain of Gooseberry.','2025-03-27 22:43:55','2025-03-27 22:43:55'),(10547,'trails',98,'What should I bring for the hike?','Make sure to bring plenty of water, as there are no drinking water sources available on the mesa.','2025-03-27 22:43:55','2025-03-27 22:43:55'),(10548,'trails',98,'Is camping allowed near the trail?','Yes, there is primitive camping available in the vicinity for those who wish to extend their adventure.','2025-03-27 22:43:55','2025-03-27 22:43:55'),(10549,'trails',98,'What is the starting and ending point of the North Rim Trail?','The North Rim Trail begins at a junction with the Practice Trail and concludes just north of the viewpoint near the junction with the South Rim Trail.','2025-03-27 22:43:55','2025-03-27 22:43:55'),(10550,'trails',98,'Can I access other trails from the North Rim Trail?','Yes, hikers can branch off onto the Windmill Trail near the beginning, which offers a different, yet still challenging, experience compared to the South Rim Trail.','2025-03-27 22:43:55','2025-03-27 22:43:55'),(10551,'trails',98,'What is the overall difficulty of the North Rim Trail?','The trail is categorized as difficult, making it suitable for experienced hikers.','2025-03-27 22:43:55','2025-03-27 22:43:55'),(10552,'trails',98,'What is the length of the North Rim Trail?','The trail stretches for 1.8 miles and is a point-to-point hike.','2025-03-27 22:43:55','2025-03-27 22:43:55'),(10553,'trails',98,'What are the elevation details of the North Rim Trail?','The trail has a highest elevation of 5208 feet and a lowest elevation of 5208 feet, with a slight incline of 150 feet.','2025-03-27 22:43:55','2025-03-27 22:43:55'),(10554,'trails',98,'Are dogs allowed on the North Rim Trail?','It is unclear whether dogs are allowed on this trail.','2025-03-27 22:43:55','2025-03-27 22:43:55'),(10555,'trails',98,'What are the geographical coordinates of the North Rim Trail?','The trail is located at latitude 37.1417 and longitude -113.185.','2025-03-27 22:43:55','2025-03-27 22:43:55'),(10556,'trails',98,'What types of features can I expect on the North Rim Trail?','Hikers can expect spectacular views along the trail, making for a rewarding hiking experience.','2025-03-27 22:43:55','2025-03-27 22:43:55'),(10557,'trails',99,'What kind of trail is the White Trail?','The White Trail is a flat doubletrack that offers access through the scenic Gooseberry Mesa, featuring a mix of hard packed dirt, sand, and unique slickrock surfaces.','2025-03-27 22:44:01','2025-03-27 22:44:01'),(10558,'trails',99,'What is the difficulty level of the White Trail?','The White Trail is classified as intermediate in difficulty, making it suitable for those with some hiking or biking experience.','2025-03-27 22:44:01','2025-03-27 22:44:01'),(10559,'trails',99,'What are the elevation statistics of the White Trail?','The trail maintains a consistent elevation of 5164 feet throughout, with a total incline of 273 feet and a decline of 81 feet.','2025-03-27 22:44:01','2025-03-27 22:44:01'),(10560,'trails',99,'How long is the White Trail?','The White Trail stretches for 3.2 miles, providing plenty of distance for exploration.','2025-03-27 22:44:01','2025-03-27 22:44:01'),(10561,'trails',99,'Is the White Trail a loop or point-to-point?','The White Trail is a point-to-point trail, which makes it a great connector for creating loops with other trails in the Gooseberry network.','2025-03-27 22:44:01','2025-03-27 22:44:01'),(10562,'trails',99,'What kind of terrain can I expect on the White Trail?','Hikers will encounter a varied terrain along the White Trail, including sections of hard packed dirt, sandy spots, and areas of slickrock, offering a diverse hiking experience.','2025-03-27 22:44:01','2025-03-27 22:44:01'),(10563,'trails',99,'What are some features of the White Trail?','One of the highlights of the White Trail is the stunning views it provides, allowing hikers to enjoy the natural beauty of the surrounding landscape.','2025-03-27 22:44:01','2025-03-27 22:44:01'),(10564,'trails',99,'Are dogs allowed on the White Trail?','It is currently unknown whether dogs are allowed on the White Trail, so it\'s best to check local regulations before bringing your furry friend.','2025-03-27 22:44:01','2025-03-27 22:44:01'),(10565,'trails',99,'What is the latitude and longitude of the White Trail?','The White Trail is located at a latitude of 37.1415 and a longitude of -113.173, making it easy to find on a map.','2025-03-27 22:44:01','2025-03-27 22:44:01'),(10566,'trails',100,'What is the route for the Bowls and Ledges trail?','The Bowls and Ledges trail begins by branching off the North Rim Train and leads to the junction with the Practice Trail. Hikers can also opt to connect with the Windmill Trail along the way.','2025-03-27 22:44:10','2025-03-27 22:44:10'),(10567,'trails',100,'What makes the Bowls and Ledges trail special?','This trail is like a natural roller coaster, featuring many bowls and ledges that provide unique hiking experiences. It\'s a delightful connector trail that allows you to enjoy the landscape while serving as a warm-up for other trails.','2025-03-27 22:44:10','2025-03-27 22:44:10'),(10568,'trails',100,'Can you hike Bowls and Ledges in both directions?','Yes, hikers can tackle the Bowls and Ledges trail in either direction, depending on which loop they wish to complete.','2025-03-27 22:44:10','2025-03-27 22:44:10'),(10569,'trails',100,'What is the difficulty level of the Bowls and Ledges trail?','The trail is categorized as difficult, making it a suitable choice for experienced hikers looking for a challenge.','2025-03-27 22:44:10','2025-03-27 22:44:10'),(10570,'trails',100,'What are the elevation details for this trail?','The Bowls and Ledges trail reaches a maximum elevation of 5163 feet, with a consistent elevation throughout, meaning there is minimal incline and decline.','2025-03-27 22:44:10','2025-03-27 22:44:10'),(10571,'trails',100,'How long is the Bowls and Ledges trail?','The trail spans 1.0 mile, making it a relatively short trek that can be completed fairly quickly.','2025-03-27 22:44:10','2025-03-27 22:44:10'),(10572,'trails',100,'What type of trail is Bowls and Ledges?','It is a point-to-point trail, which means it has a distinct start and endpoint.','2025-03-27 22:44:10','2025-03-27 22:44:10'),(10573,'trails',100,'What are the incline and decline statistics for the trail?','Hikers will experience a slight incline of 13 feet and a decline of 66 feet along the trail.','2025-03-27 22:44:10','2025-03-27 22:44:10'),(10574,'trails',100,'Are dogs allowed on the Bowls and Ledges trail?','The policy on dogs is currently unknown, so it’s best to check local regulations before bringing your pet.','2025-03-27 22:44:10','2025-03-27 22:44:10'),(10575,'trails',100,'What kind of views can hikers expect along the trail?','The trail offers scenic views, enhancing the experience as you navigate the natural features of the area.','2025-03-27 22:44:10','2025-03-27 22:44:10'),(10576,'trails',100,'What are the latitude and longitude coordinates for Bowls and Ledges?','The trail is located at approximately 37.1425° latitude and -113.187° longitude.','2025-03-27 22:44:10','2025-03-27 22:44:10'),(10577,'trails',101,'What is the Practice Trail at Gooseberry Mesa like?','The Practice Trail offers a challenging yet enjoyable warm-up, featuring undulating sandstone mounds and twisting rock canyons, perfect for a technical hike.','2025-03-27 22:44:19','2025-03-27 22:44:19'),(10578,'trails',101,'What is the elevation of Gooseberry Mesa?','Gooseberry Mesa is situated at an elevation of 5200 feet, providing stunning views as you hike.','2025-03-27 22:44:19','2025-03-27 22:44:19'),(10579,'trails',101,'How is the trail marked for navigation?','The trails are marked with white paint dots on the slickrock and have signs at junctions, making it relatively easy to navigate despite the maze-like nature.','2025-03-27 22:44:19','2025-03-27 22:44:19'),(10580,'trails',101,'Is the Practice Trail suitable for beginners?','While it serves as a great warm-up, the Practice Trail can be quite challenging for newcomers to slickrock hiking; experienced hikers also find it enjoyable.','2025-03-27 22:44:19','2025-03-27 22:44:19'),(10581,'trails',101,'How can I customize my hiking experience on the trails?','You have the flexibility to connect various trails to adjust your hike, making it longer or shorter, easier or harder based on your preference.','2025-03-27 22:44:19','2025-03-27 22:44:19'),(10582,'trails',101,'What should I bring with me when hiking the trails?','Be sure to bring plenty of water, as there is no drinking water available on the mesa.','2025-03-27 22:44:19','2025-03-27 22:44:19'),(10583,'trails',101,'Is camping allowed near the Gooseberry Mesa trails?','Yes, primitive camping is available in the area for those looking to extend their outdoor adventure.','2025-03-27 22:44:19','2025-03-27 22:44:19'),(10584,'trails',101,'What is the length and type of the Practice Trail?','The Practice Trail is 1.3 miles long and is classified as a point-to-point trail.','2025-03-27 22:44:19','2025-03-27 22:44:19'),(10585,'trails',101,'What kind of terrain can I expect on the Practice Trail?','Prepare for a terrain that undulates over house-sized sandstone mounds and navigates through tight rock canyons.','2025-03-27 22:44:19','2025-03-27 22:44:19'),(10586,'trails',101,'What are the elevation statistics for the Practice Trail?','The trail has both a highest and lowest elevation of about 5138 feet, with a total incline of 81 feet and a decline of 49 feet.','2025-03-27 22:44:19','2025-03-27 22:44:19'),(10587,'trails',101,'Are dogs allowed on the Gooseberry Mesa trails?','It\'s currently unclear whether dogs are permitted on the trails.','2025-03-27 22:44:19','2025-03-27 22:44:19'),(10588,'trails',101,'What is the average and maximum grade of the Practice Trail?','The average grade of the trail is only 0.02%, with a maximum grade reaching up to 0.06%.','2025-03-27 22:44:19','2025-03-27 22:44:19'),(10589,'trails',102,'What is the Windmill Trail like?','The Windmill Trail is a traditional singletrack that provides a refreshing change from the rugged slickrock terrain, allowing hikers to enjoy beautiful views after a day spent exploring the other trails in the Gooseberry area.','2025-03-27 22:44:24','2025-03-27 22:44:24'),(10590,'trails',102,'What is the difficulty level of the Windmill Trail?','The trail is classified as intermediate, making it suitable for those with some hiking experience.','2025-03-27 22:44:25','2025-03-27 22:44:25'),(10591,'trails',102,'What are the elevation details of the Windmill Trail?','The Windmill Trail has a highest elevation of 5,067 feet and a lowest elevation of 5,067 feet, indicating a relatively level hike throughout.','2025-03-27 22:44:25','2025-03-27 22:44:25'),(10592,'trails',102,'How long is the Windmill Trail?','The trail stretches 1.3 miles in length.','2025-03-27 22:44:25','2025-03-27 22:44:25'),(10593,'trails',102,'What type of trail is the Windmill Trail?','It is a point-to-point trail, which means hikers will start and end at different locations.','2025-03-27 22:44:25','2025-03-27 22:44:25'),(10594,'trails',102,'What is the decline on the Windmill Trail?','The trail has a decline of 115 feet.','2025-03-27 22:44:25','2025-03-27 22:44:25'),(10595,'trails',102,'What is the average grade of the Windmill Trail?','The average grade of the trail is about 0.02%, making it relatively flat.','2025-03-27 22:44:25','2025-03-27 22:44:25'),(10596,'trails',102,'What is the maximum grade of the Windmill Trail?','The maximum grade reaches up to 0.03%, which is not steep at all.','2025-03-27 22:44:25','2025-03-27 22:44:25'),(10597,'trails',102,'What are the geographical coordinates of the Windmill Trail?','The trail is located at a latitude of 37.1468 and a longitude of -113.184.','2025-03-27 22:44:25','2025-03-27 22:44:25'),(10598,'trails',103,'What is the overall experience like on the JEM Trail?','The JEM Trail offers an exhilarating ride with its smooth and fast flow, complemented by stunning views of the surrounding landscapes.','2025-03-27 22:44:31','2025-03-27 22:44:31'),(10599,'trails',103,'What is the difficulty level of the JEM Trail?','The JEM Trail is classified as intermediate, making it suitable for those with some prior hiking or biking experience.','2025-03-27 22:44:31','2025-03-27 22:44:31'),(10600,'trails',103,'What is the highest elevation point on the JEM Trail?','The trail reaches a highest elevation of 3,455 feet.','2025-03-27 22:44:31','2025-03-27 22:44:31'),(10601,'trails',103,'What is the lowest elevation point on the JEM Trail?','The lowest elevation also stands at 3,455 feet, indicating a relatively flat profile throughout the hike.','2025-03-27 22:44:31','2025-03-27 22:44:31'),(10602,'trails',103,'What is the total length of the JEM Trail?','The JEM Trail stretches for 6.9 miles.','2025-03-27 22:44:31','2025-03-27 22:44:31'),(10603,'trails',103,'What type of trail is the JEM Trail?','The JEM Trail is a point-to-point trail, meaning you\'ll start at one location and finish at another.','2025-03-27 22:44:31','2025-03-27 22:44:31'),(10604,'trails',103,'What is the incline of the JEM Trail?','The trail features an incline of 916 feet, providing a moderate challenge.','2025-03-27 22:44:31','2025-03-27 22:44:31'),(10605,'trails',103,'How much decline is there on the JEM Trail?','There is a decline of 64 feet along the route.','2025-03-27 22:44:31','2025-03-27 22:44:31'),(10606,'trails',103,'What is the average grade of the JEM Trail?','The average grade of the trail is a gentle 0.03%, making it accessible for many hikers.','2025-03-27 22:44:31','2025-03-27 22:44:31'),(10607,'trails',103,'What is the maximum grade found on the JEM Trail?','The JEM Trail has a maximum grade of 0.17%, which keeps the trail mostly easy to navigate.','2025-03-27 22:44:31','2025-03-27 22:44:31'),(10608,'trails',103,'Can you provide the geographic coordinates of the JEM Trail?','Yes, the JEM Trail is located at approximately latitude 37.2 and longitude -113.218.','2025-03-27 22:44:31','2025-03-27 22:44:31'),(10609,'trails',104,'What is the Dead Ringer trail?','The Dead Ringer trail is located within the Hurricane Cliffs Trail network and was completed in 2015 through a collaboration between the Dixie Mountain Bike Trails Association and the BLM. It offers a scenic hiking experience with both climbing and descending sections.','2025-03-27 22:44:38','2025-03-27 22:44:38'),(10610,'trails',104,'How did Dead Ringer get its name?','The trail is named after the remains of a long-gone cow discovered during the trail scouting process, which had a cowbell still attached to its neck.','2025-03-27 22:44:38','2025-03-27 22:44:38'),(10611,'trails',104,'What is the trail\'s elevation profile?','The Dead Ringer trail reaches a highest elevation of 3,777 feet and has a relatively flat average grade, making it suitable for a wide range of hikers.','2025-03-27 22:44:38','2025-03-27 22:44:38'),(10612,'trails',104,'How long is the Dead Ringer trail?','The overall length of the Dead Ringer trail is approximately 5.2 miles, making it a pleasant hike for those looking for a manageable distance.','2025-03-27 22:44:38','2025-03-27 22:44:38'),(10613,'trails',104,'What are the difficulty levels of Dead Ringer?','The trail is rated as easy to intermediate, which makes it accessible for hikers with varying experience levels.','2025-03-27 22:44:38','2025-03-27 22:44:38'),(10614,'trails',104,'Can the Dead Ringer trail be combined with other trails?','Yes, hikers can combine Dead Ringer with the JEM Trail or Goulds Rim trail to create longer loops of over 20 miles.','2025-03-27 22:44:38','2025-03-27 22:44:38'),(10615,'trails',104,'Are there any notable features on the trail?','One of the key highlights of the Dead Ringer trail is its stunning views, as well as its gradual incline of 578 feet and a fun downhill section.','2025-03-27 22:44:38','2025-03-27 22:44:38'),(10616,'trails',104,'What precautions should hikers take on the Dead Ringer trail?','Hikers should be cautious of two-way traffic and a few blind corners along the narrow bench section, where passing space is limited.','2025-03-27 22:44:38','2025-03-27 22:44:38'),(10617,'trails',104,'Are dogs allowed on the Dead Ringer trail?','Yes, dogs are permitted to be off-leash along the Dead Ringer trail, making it a great option for pet owners.','2025-03-27 22:44:38','2025-03-27 22:44:38'),(10618,'trails',104,'What is the general terrain like on the Dead Ringer trail?','The Dead Ringer trail features a smooth and well-maintained surface with a long bench cut into the steep mesa, making for both an enjoyable climb and descent.','2025-03-27 22:44:38','2025-03-27 22:44:38'),(10619,'trails',107,'What is the Cryptobionic Family Friendly trail like?','The Cryptobionic Family Friendly trail offers a fun, smooth, and easy-to-navigate pathway, making it ideal for families and those looking for a leisurely hike. It features beautiful views and a pleasant environment.','2025-03-27 22:44:44','2025-03-27 22:44:44'),(10620,'trails',107,'What is the difficulty level of the trail?','This trail is rated as intermediate in difficulty, making it suitable for a wide range of hikers.','2025-03-27 22:44:44','2025-03-27 22:44:44'),(10621,'trails',107,'What are the highest and lowest elevations on the trail?','The trail reaches a maximum elevation of 3,667 feet, while the lowest point is also at 3,667 feet.','2025-03-27 22:44:44','2025-03-27 22:44:44'),(10622,'trails',107,'How long is the Cryptobionic Family Friendly trail?','The total length of the trail is 3.3 miles.','2025-03-27 22:44:44','2025-03-27 22:44:44'),(10623,'trails',107,'What type of trail is this?','The trail is a point-to-point type, allowing hikers to enjoy a continuous journey from start to finish.','2025-03-27 22:44:44','2025-03-27 22:44:44'),(10624,'trails',107,'What is the elevation change along the trail?','Hikers will experience a total incline of 279 feet and a decline of 26 feet throughout the trail.','2025-03-27 22:44:44','2025-03-27 22:44:44'),(10625,'trails',107,'What is the average and maximum grade of the trail?','The average grade of the trail is quite gentle at 0.02%, with a maximum steepness of 0.09%.','2025-03-27 22:44:44','2025-03-27 22:44:44'),(10626,'trails',107,'Are there any notable features along the trail?','Hikers can expect stunning views throughout the trail, making it a scenic hike.','2025-03-27 22:44:44','2025-03-27 22:44:44'),(10627,'trails',107,'Are dogs allowed on the Cryptobionic Family Friendly trail?','It is currently unclear whether dogs are permitted on this trail.','2025-03-27 22:44:44','2025-03-27 22:44:44'),(10628,'trails',107,'What are the geographical coordinates of the trail?','The trail is located at latitude 37.1961 and longitude -113.235.','2025-03-27 22:44:44','2025-03-27 22:44:44'),(10629,'trails',108,'What can I expect to see while hiking the Secret Trail?','Prepare to be amazed by breathtaking views along the mesa\'s edge, showcasing the area\'s natural beauty as you traverse a charming mix of slick rock and dirt trails.','2025-03-27 22:44:50','2025-03-27 22:44:50'),(10630,'trails',108,'What is the difficulty level of the Secret Trail?','The Secret Trail is considered difficult, making it suitable for experienced hikers looking for a challenge.','2025-03-27 22:44:50','2025-03-27 22:44:50'),(10631,'trails',108,'What is the total length of the Secret Trail?','The trail stretches for an impressive 6.6 miles, offering ample opportunity to immerse yourself in the stunning surroundings.','2025-03-27 22:44:50','2025-03-27 22:44:50'),(10632,'trails',108,'Is the Secret Trail point-to-point or a loop?','This trail is a point-to-point route, meaning you\'ll start at one endpoint and finish at another, so plan your logistics accordingly.','2025-03-27 22:44:50','2025-03-27 22:44:50'),(10633,'trails',108,'What are the elevation details for the Secret Trail?','You will experience a consistent elevation throughout the hike, with both the highest and lowest points sitting at 5,090 feet.','2025-03-27 22:44:50','2025-03-27 22:44:50'),(10634,'trails',108,'What is the overall elevation change on the Secret Trail?','Hikers will face an incline of 786 feet and a decline of 907 feet during the hike, adding to the cardio challenge.','2025-03-27 22:44:50','2025-03-27 22:44:50'),(10635,'trails',108,'How steep is the Secret Trail?','The average grade is quite manageable at 0.05%, with a maximum steepness reaching up to 0.30%, ensuring a terrain that is mostly gentle.','2025-03-27 22:44:50','2025-03-27 22:44:50'),(10636,'trails',108,'What are the geographical coordinates of the Secret Trail?','If you need to find it on a map, the trail is located at approximately 37.1293° latitude and -113.198° longitude.','2025-03-27 22:44:50','2025-03-27 22:44:50'),(10637,'trails',109,'What is the North Point Loop trail like?','The North Point Loop offers a diverse hiking experience with a mix of singletrack paths and some rougher terrain. The hike features stunning views of Gooseberry Mesa, making it an enjoyable adventure.','2025-03-27 22:44:58','2025-03-27 22:44:58'),(10638,'trails',109,'How challenging is the North Point Loop?','The trail is classified as difficult, with some more challenging sections. While most of it has a moderate grade, you will encounter a few steeper areas.','2025-03-27 22:44:58','2025-03-27 22:44:58'),(10639,'trails',109,'What is the total length of the North Point Loop?','The North Point Loop stretches for about 4.1 miles.','2025-03-27 22:44:58','2025-03-27 22:44:58'),(10640,'trails',109,'What are the elevation details of the North Point Loop?','The trail has a highest and lowest elevation of 5,369 feet, with a total incline of 484 feet and a decline of 491 feet.','2025-03-27 22:44:58','2025-03-27 22:44:58'),(10641,'trails',109,'What type of trail is the North Point Loop?','The North Point Loop is a point-to-point trail, offering varied surfaces from loose rocks to solid sandstone slick rock.','2025-03-27 22:44:58','2025-03-27 22:44:58'),(10642,'trails',109,'Are dogs allowed on the North Point Loop?','Yes, dogs are permitted on the North Point Loop and can be off-leash.','2025-03-27 22:44:58','2025-03-27 22:44:58'),(10643,'trails',109,'What should I be aware of while hiking the North Point Loop?','Be mindful of other trail users, especially mountain bikers who frequent the area. Respecting everyone on the trail ensures a pleasant experience for all.','2025-03-27 22:44:58','2025-03-27 22:44:58'),(10644,'trails',109,'What is the average and maximum grade of the North Point Loop?','The trail has an average grade of 0.04%, and a maximum grade that reaches up to 0.34%.','2025-03-27 22:44:58','2025-03-27 22:44:58'),(10645,'trails',109,'What can I expect in terms of scenic views?','Hikers will be treated to breathtaking views, particularly of Gooseberry Mesa, which enhances the beauty of the trek.','2025-03-27 22:44:58','2025-03-27 22:44:58'),(10646,'trails',110,'What is the experience like on the Goosebump trail?','The Goosebump trail offers an exhilarating experience as it meanders along the scenic contours of the mesa, providing stunning views throughout. It\'s an exhilarating \'roller coaster\' route that consists of frequent short climbs and descents.','2025-03-27 22:45:07','2025-03-27 22:45:07'),(10647,'trails',110,'What is the difficulty level of the Goosebump trail?','This trail is classified as intermediate in difficulty, making it suitable for those with some hiking experience.','2025-03-27 22:45:07','2025-03-27 22:45:07'),(10648,'trails',110,'What is the total length of the Goosebump trail?','The Goosebump trail stretches for 3.6 miles, taking you on an enjoyable journey through diverse terrain.','2025-03-27 22:45:07','2025-03-27 22:45:07'),(10649,'trails',110,'What elevations can be found on the Goosebump trail?','The trail maintains a steady elevation, with both the highest and lowest points reaching 3924 feet.','2025-03-27 22:45:08','2025-03-27 22:45:08'),(10650,'trails',110,'What should I expect in terms of incline and decline on the Goosebump trail?','Hikers can anticipate an incline of 219 feet and a decline of 272 feet along the trail, which contributes to its rolling nature.','2025-03-27 22:45:08','2025-03-27 22:45:08'),(10651,'trails',110,'Are there different trail sections on Goosebump?','Yes, several parts of the trail split into Blue and Green sections. The Blue sections can be somewhat rugged, while the Green sections offer fun, smooth up-and-down terrain.','2025-03-27 22:45:08','2025-03-27 22:45:08'),(10652,'trails',110,'Where does the Goosebump trail end?','The trail concludes at a junction with various jeep and ATV trails, marking the end of this thrilling hiking experience.','2025-03-27 22:45:08','2025-03-27 22:45:08'),(10653,'trails',110,'What views can I expect from the Goosebump trail?','Hikers will be treated to excellent vistas as the trail follows the mesa\'s contours, enhancing the outdoor experience.','2025-03-27 22:45:08','2025-03-27 22:45:08'),(10654,'trails',110,'Are dogs permitted on the Goosebump trail?','The policy regarding dogs on this trail is currently unknown, so it\'s advisable to check local regulations before bringing your pet.','2025-03-27 22:45:08','2025-03-27 22:45:08'),(10655,'trails',110,'What are the geographical coordinates for the Goosebump trail?','The trail is located at approximately 37.1519° latitude and -113.252° longitude.','2025-03-27 22:45:08','2025-03-27 22:45:08'),(10656,'trails',111,'What is the More Cowbell trail like?','The More Cowbell trail is an enjoyable beginner loop that connects to the JEM Trail and Dead Ringer trail, featuring smooth and wide paths along with stunning views in all directions.','2025-03-27 22:45:16','2025-03-27 22:45:16'),(10657,'trails',111,'Is the More Cowbell trail suitable for beginners?','Yes, it\'s an excellent choice for beginners or families, offering a fun and rewarding hiking experience with a few challenges along the way.','2025-03-27 22:45:16','2025-03-27 22:45:16'),(10658,'trails',111,'What are the trail conditions on the More Cowbell trail?','The trail consists mainly of bench trails that are wide, typically over 3 feet, and relatively smooth, making it accessible for most hikers.','2025-03-27 22:45:16','2025-03-27 22:45:16'),(10659,'trails',111,'Can I combine the More Cowbell trail with other trails?','Absolutely! The More Cowbell trail connects with the JEM and Dead Ringer trails, allowing for the possibility of a longer hike by merging routes.','2025-03-27 22:45:16','2025-03-27 22:45:16'),(10660,'trails',111,'What is the difficulty level of the More Cowbell trail?','The trail is classified as intermediate, making it suitable for those with some hiking experience.','2025-03-27 22:45:16','2025-03-27 22:45:16'),(10661,'trails',111,'What are the elevation details for the More Cowbell trail?','The trail reaches a maximum elevation of 4207 feet and maintains that altitude throughout, with a total elevation gain of 176 feet and a decline of 221 feet.','2025-03-27 22:45:16','2025-03-27 22:45:16'),(10662,'trails',111,'How long is the More Cowbell trail?','The trail stretches for 2.7 miles, providing a pleasant hike for those looking to enjoy the scenery.','2025-03-27 22:45:16','2025-03-27 22:45:16'),(10663,'trails',111,'What type of trail is the More Cowbell trail?','The More Cowbell trail is a point-to-point trail, allowing you to start and finish at different locations.','2025-03-27 22:45:16','2025-03-27 22:45:16'),(10664,'trails',111,'What is the average grade of the More Cowbell trail?','The trail has an average grade of 0.03%, which makes for a relatively flat hiking experience.','2025-03-27 22:45:16','2025-03-27 22:45:16'),(10665,'trails',111,'What is the maximum grade of the More Cowbell trail?','The maximum grade on the trail is 0.11%, indicating minimal steep sections, ideal for beginners.','2025-03-27 22:45:16','2025-03-27 22:45:16'),(10666,'trails',111,'What features can I expect on the More Cowbell trail?','This trail is known for its spectacular views, providing hikers with beautiful landscapes to enjoy.','2025-03-27 22:45:16','2025-03-27 22:45:16'),(10667,'trails',111,'Are dogs allowed on the More Cowbell trail?','Yes, dogs are welcome on the trail and can be off-leash, making it a great outing for pet owners.','2025-03-27 22:45:16','2025-03-27 22:45:16'),(10668,'trails',111,'What are the geographical coordinates of the More Cowbell trail?','The More Cowbell trail is located at a latitude of 37.1414 and a longitude of -113.244.','2025-03-27 22:45:16','2025-03-27 22:45:16'),(10669,'trails',112,'What is the Goosebump Connector trail?','The Goosebump Connector is a simple trail that links the Goosebump Trail to the Jems Trail, allowing hikers to experience beautiful views of the Utah and Arizona landscapes.','2025-03-27 22:45:22','2025-03-27 22:45:22'),(10670,'trails',112,'What is the difficulty level of the Goosebump Connector?','This trail is rated as intermediate, making it suitable for hikers with some experience.','2025-03-27 22:45:22','2025-03-27 22:45:22'),(10671,'trails',112,'What is the elevation range of the Goosebump Connector?','The trail has a consistent elevation of 3,758 feet, providing a stable hiking experience without significant elevation changes.','2025-03-27 22:45:22','2025-03-27 22:45:22'),(10672,'trails',112,'How long is the Goosebump Connector trail?','The total length of the Goosebump Connector is approximately 1.7 miles.','2025-03-27 22:45:22','2025-03-27 22:45:22'),(10673,'trails',112,'What type of trail is the Goosebump Connector?','The Goosebump Connector is a point-to-point trail, meaning it connects two distinct trailheads.','2025-03-27 22:45:22','2025-03-27 22:45:22'),(10674,'trails',112,'What is the decline in elevation along the Goosebump Connector?','Hikers can expect a slight decline of about 196 feet along the trail.','2025-03-27 22:45:22','2025-03-27 22:45:22'),(10675,'trails',112,'What is the average grade of the Goosebump Connector?','The trail has a very gentle average grade of just 0.02%, making it relatively easy to navigate.','2025-03-27 22:45:22','2025-03-27 22:45:22'),(10676,'trails',112,'What is the maximum grade on the Goosebump Connector?','The maximum grade encountered on this trail reaches up to 0.05%, which is quite mild.','2025-03-27 22:45:22','2025-03-27 22:45:22'),(10677,'trails',112,'What are the geographical coordinates of the Goosebump Connector?','The coordinates for the Goosebump Connector are approximately 37.1624° latitude and -113.227° longitude.','2025-03-27 22:45:22','2025-03-27 22:45:22'),(10678,'trails',113,'What should I expect to see along the Holy Guacamole trail?','Hikers can enjoy breathtaking sights of the iridescent green mesa, glowing sagebrush, and vibrant wildflowers during certain seasons. You\'ll also encounter juniper, mesquite, and rabbit brush, complemented by stunning views of Eagle Crags and the valley.','2025-03-27 22:45:30','2025-03-27 22:45:30'),(10679,'trails',113,'What is the trail surface like?','The Holy Guacamole trail features a mix of slickrock and singletrack paths with sections of dirt and small loose stones. While there are some challenging spots, they are generally brief.','2025-03-27 22:45:31','2025-03-27 22:45:31'),(10680,'trails',113,'What makes hiking along the rim special?','The experience is awe-inspiring as you hike near the rim next to Zion National Park. The combination of the landscape and flora, particularly after rainfall when the mesa shines in vibrant colors, adds to the adventure.','2025-03-27 22:45:31','2025-03-27 22:45:31'),(10681,'trails',113,'Are there specific types of plants I might encounter?','Yes, you\'ll find a variety of native plants including sagebrush and rabbit brush, especially in the areas where the moisture brings out their colors.','2025-03-27 22:45:31','2025-03-27 22:45:31'),(10682,'trails',113,'Are there any recommended spots for a break or picnic?','Absolutely! There are several scenic lunch spots along the rim providing excellent views of Eagle Crags and the surrounding valley where you enter.','2025-03-27 22:45:31','2025-03-27 22:45:31'),(10683,'trails',113,'What is the difficulty level of the Holy Guacamole trail?','The trail is classified as difficult, making it suitable for experienced hikers who are prepared for its challenges.','2025-03-27 22:45:31','2025-03-27 22:45:31'),(10684,'trails',113,'What are the elevation details of the trail?','The trail reaches a height of 4,452 feet at its highest point and remains at that elevation throughout, with a slight incline of 208 feet and a decline of 186 feet.','2025-03-27 22:45:31','2025-03-27 22:45:31'),(10685,'trails',113,'How long is the Holy Guacamole trail?','The total length of the trail is 3.3 miles and it is a point-to-point type.','2025-03-27 22:45:31','2025-03-27 22:45:31'),(10686,'trails',113,'What are the trail grades like?','The average grade of the trail is a very gentle 0.02%, with a maximum steepness of 0.14% at certain points.','2025-03-27 22:45:31','2025-03-27 22:45:31'),(10687,'trails',113,'Can I bring my dog on the trail?','Yes, dogs are allowed off-leash on the Holy Guacamole trail, making it a great outing for pet owners.','2025-03-27 22:45:31','2025-03-27 22:45:31'),(10688,'trails',113,'What are the geographical coordinates of the trail?','The Holy Guacamole trail is located at a latitude of 37.1998 and a longitude of -113.11.','2025-03-27 22:45:31','2025-03-27 22:45:31'),(10689,'trails',114,'What can I expect to see on the Lime Trail?','Hikers will be treated to stunning views of West Temple and Mount Kinesava along the trail, and you may even spot a California Condor soaring above.','2025-03-27 22:45:38','2025-03-27 22:45:38'),(10690,'trails',114,'What type of terrain is the Lime Trail?','The Lime Trail features an exciting mix of slickrock and rugged sections, making it a fun and challenging hike.','2025-03-27 22:45:38','2025-03-27 22:45:38'),(10691,'trails',114,'What is the difficulty level of the Lime Trail?','This trail is classified as difficult, suitable for those looking for a challenge.','2025-03-27 22:45:38','2025-03-27 22:45:38'),(10692,'trails',114,'What is the length of the Lime Trail?','The hike covers a distance of 0.9 miles, making it a relatively short trek.','2025-03-27 22:45:38','2025-03-27 22:45:38'),(10693,'trails',114,'What is the elevation range of the Lime Trail?','The Lime Trail reaches an elevation of 4517 feet at its highest point, with minimal elevation change throughout the hike.','2025-03-27 22:45:38','2025-03-27 22:45:38'),(10694,'trails',114,'What type of trail is Lime Trail?','The Lime Trail is a point-to-point trail, allowing hikers to experience a complete loop by connecting with other nearby trails.','2025-03-27 22:45:38','2025-03-27 22:45:38'),(10695,'trails',114,'Are dogs allowed on the Lime Trail?','Yes, dogs are permitted on this trail and can enjoy the freedom of being off-leash.','2025-03-27 22:45:38','2025-03-27 22:45:38'),(10696,'trails',114,'What should I be cautious of while hiking the Lime Trail?','While hiking, be sure to pay attention to the rock cairns that mark the path, as they guide you through the more rugged sections.','2025-03-27 22:45:38','2025-03-27 22:45:38'),(10697,'trails',114,'What is the latitude and longitude of the Lime Trail?','The Lime Trail is located at a latitude of 37.203 and a longitude of -113.111.','2025-03-27 22:45:38','2025-03-27 22:45:38'),(10698,'trails',114,'What is the incline and decline on the Lime Trail?','Hikers can expect an incline of 56 feet and a moderate decline of 14 feet during their trek.','2025-03-27 22:45:38','2025-03-27 22:45:38'),(10699,'trails',114,'What features make the Lime Trail special?','The trail is notable for its breathtaking views, especially of the majestic surrounding landscapes.','2025-03-27 22:45:38','2025-03-27 22:45:38'),(10700,'trails',115,'What is the Three Falls Trail known for?','The Three Falls Trail is renowned for its challenging scrambles through a river gorge and breathtaking views of towering canyon walls and three dry, slick rock waterfalls.','2025-03-27 22:45:46','2025-03-27 22:45:46'),(10701,'trails',115,'What is the difficulty level of the Three Falls Trail?','This trail is classified as very difficult, making it suitable for experienced hikers.','2025-03-27 22:45:46','2025-03-27 22:45:46'),(10702,'trails',115,'What are the highest and lowest elevations on the trail?','The trail reaches a highest elevation of 3,285 feet and also has a lowest elevation of 3,285 feet, indicating a relatively flat terrain despite its difficulty.','2025-03-27 22:45:46','2025-03-27 22:45:46'),(10703,'trails',115,'How long is the Three Falls Trail?','The trail stretches for a total of 1.0 mile, offering a short but intense hiking experience.','2025-03-27 22:45:46','2025-03-27 22:45:46'),(10704,'trails',115,'What type of trail is the Three Falls Trail?','The Three Falls Trail is a point-to-point trail, meaning hikers will start and finish at different locations.','2025-03-27 22:45:46','2025-03-27 22:45:46'),(10705,'trails',115,'What is the elevation change on the trail?','Hikers will experience an elevation gain of 326 feet and a decline of 112 feet along the course of the trail.','2025-03-27 22:45:46','2025-03-27 22:45:46'),(10706,'trails',115,'What is the average grade of the trail?','The average grade of the Three Falls Trail is 0.08%, providing a generally level hiking experience.','2025-03-27 22:45:46','2025-03-27 22:45:46'),(10707,'trails',115,'What is the maximum grade on the trail?','The trail\'s maximum grade reaches up to 0.39%, which may present some steep sections during the scramble.','2025-03-27 22:45:46','2025-03-27 22:45:46'),(10708,'trails',115,'What are the geographic coordinates of the Three Falls Trail?','The trail is located at approximately 37.1642° latitude and -113.287° longitude.','2025-03-27 22:45:46','2025-03-27 22:45:46'),(10709,'trails',116,'What kind of terrain can I expect on the Wire Mesa Loop?','The Wire Mesa Loop features a diverse range of terrains, providing a richer experience compared to other mesa trails. Hikers can look forward to stunning panoramic views of southern Utah and northern Arizona.','2025-03-27 22:45:51','2025-03-27 22:45:51'),(10710,'trails',116,'What is the difficulty level of the Wire Mesa Loop hike?','This trail is rated as intermediate, making it suitable for those with some hiking experience.','2025-03-27 22:45:51','2025-03-27 22:45:51'),(10711,'trails',116,'What are the highest and lowest elevations on the Wire Mesa Loop?','Both the highest and lowest elevations on the trail are at 4,326 feet, making the trail relatively flat despite its variety.','2025-03-27 22:45:51','2025-03-27 22:45:51'),(10712,'trails',116,'How long is the Wire Mesa Loop trail?','The total length of the trail is 7.4 miles, providing a nice hike that can be enjoyed in a single outing.','2025-03-27 22:45:51','2025-03-27 22:45:51'),(10713,'trails',116,'Is the Wire Mesa Loop a loop trail or an out-and-back?','The Wire Mesa Loop is a loop trail, allowing you to start and finish at the same point without retracing your steps.','2025-03-27 22:45:51','2025-03-27 22:45:51'),(10714,'trails',116,'What is the total incline and decline on the Wire Mesa Loop?','During the hike, you\'ll encounter a total incline of 428 feet and a decline of 415 feet, which adds a bit of elevation challenge.','2025-03-27 22:45:51','2025-03-27 22:45:51'),(10715,'trails',116,'What is the average and maximum grade of the Wire Mesa Loop?','The trail has an average grade of 0.02%, with a maximum grade reaching 0.12%, making it relatively gentle overall.','2025-03-27 22:45:51','2025-03-27 22:45:51'),(10716,'trails',116,'What are the geographical coordinates of the Wire Mesa Loop?','The trail is located at approximately 37.1328° latitude and -113.071° longitude.','2025-03-27 22:45:51','2025-03-27 22:45:51'),(10717,'trails',117,'What is the starting point of the Margarita Trail?','The Margarita Trail begins on a mesa located just above Dalton Wash.','2025-03-27 22:45:59','2025-03-27 22:45:59'),(10718,'trails',117,'What kind of terrain can I expect on the Margarita Trail?','Hikers will navigate through slickrock primarily marked by cairns and rock-filled baskets, providing clear guidance along the route.','2025-03-27 22:45:59','2025-03-27 22:45:59'),(10719,'trails',117,'How often are the trail markers placed?','The cairns and rock markers are frequently spaced, making it relatively easy to follow the trail. In areas where visibility is low, mountain bike tracks often provide additional guidance.','2025-03-27 22:45:59','2025-03-27 22:45:59'),(10720,'trails',117,'Are there any scenic views along the trail?','Absolutely! After about 1 mile, the trail approaches the edge of the mesa, offering stunning views into the lush Dalton Wash, especially vibrant in the spring.','2025-03-27 22:45:59','2025-03-27 22:45:59'),(10721,'trails',117,'What type of vegetation can be found on the trail?','The trail starts in a sparse forest composed of low shrubs and trees, later transitioning to open areas with breathtaking vistas of Cougar Mountain and nearby peaks.','2025-03-27 22:45:59','2025-03-27 22:45:59'),(10722,'trails',117,'What should I be aware of regarding weather conditions while hiking?','As the trail is largely exposed, it can become quite hot during the summer months, so proper hydration and sun protection are advisable.','2025-03-27 22:45:59','2025-03-27 22:45:59'),(10723,'trails',117,'What is the total distance of the Margarita Trail?','The trail length is approximately 2.1 miles, following a point-to-point route.','2025-03-27 22:45:59','2025-03-27 22:45:59'),(10724,'trails',117,'What is the elevation change along the trail?','The highest elevation on the trail reaches 4,462 feet, with a slight incline of 167 feet and a modest decline of 23 feet.','2025-03-27 22:45:59','2025-03-27 22:45:59'),(10725,'trails',117,'How difficult is the Margarita Trail?','The trail is classified as intermediate, making it suitable for hikers with a moderate level of experience.','2025-03-27 22:45:59','2025-03-27 22:45:59'),(10726,'trails',117,'Are dogs allowed on the Margarita Trail?','It is currently unknown whether dogs are permitted on the trail.','2025-03-27 22:45:59','2025-03-27 22:45:59'),(10727,'trails',117,'What can I expect when the Margarita Trail connects with the Guacamole Trail?','The junction with the Guacamole Trail offers a thrilling continuation over more slickrock terrain, boasting more fantastic views and exciting hiking experiences.','2025-03-27 22:45:59','2025-03-27 22:45:59'),(10728,'trails',117,'What are the coordinates of the Margarita Trail?','The trail is located at latitude 37.2262 and longitude -113.114.','2025-03-27 22:45:59','2025-03-27 22:45:59'),(10729,'trails',120,'What is the Tom\'s Canyon Trail like?','Tom\'s Canyon Trail is an intermediate singletrack path featuring minimal technical challenges, characterized by quick ups and downs. Although it includes a few short steep climbs, the trail is generally accessible for hikers.','2025-03-27 22:46:08','2025-03-27 22:46:08'),(10730,'trails',120,'Where can I park to access Tom\'s Canyon Trail?','You can park on Ladera Lane, and the trailhead starts right at the bend in the road.','2025-03-27 22:46:08','2025-03-27 22:46:08'),(10731,'trails',120,'Is the trail shared with any other trails?','Yes, the Tom\'s Canyon Trail shares its trailhead with the \'K Hill\' trail, which is currently off-limits to mountain biking.','2025-03-27 22:46:08','2025-03-27 22:46:08'),(10732,'trails',120,'How long is the Tom\'s Canyon Trail?','The trail stretches for 1.2 miles and is currently designed as an out-and-back route.','2025-03-27 22:46:08','2025-03-27 22:46:08'),(10733,'trails',120,'What is the highest elevation on the trail?','The highest elevation reached along the trail is 5,027 feet.','2025-03-27 22:46:08','2025-03-27 22:46:08'),(10734,'trails',120,'What kind of views can I expect on the trail?','Hikers will be treated to stunning views of the canyon and the La Estancia housing development, particularly from a scenic viewpoint marked \'Bench\' which features a stone bench for resting.','2025-03-27 22:46:08','2025-03-27 22:46:08'),(10735,'trails',120,'What are the incline and decline statistics for the trail?','The trail has a total incline of 168 feet and a decline of 64 feet.','2025-03-27 22:46:08','2025-03-27 22:46:08'),(10736,'trails',120,'Are dogs allowed on the trail?','Yes, dogs are permitted on the trail, but they must be kept on a leash.','2025-03-27 22:46:08','2025-03-27 22:46:08'),(10737,'trails',120,'What is the difficulty level of Tom\'s Canyon Trail?','The trail is classified as intermediate, making it suitable for hikers with some experience.','2025-03-27 22:46:08','2025-03-27 22:46:08'),(10738,'trails',120,'When was this trail renovated, and why?','Tom\'s Canyon Trail is currently undergoing renovations aimed at making it more mountain bike friendly, enhancing the overall experience for both hikers and cyclists.','2025-03-27 22:46:08','2025-03-27 22:46:08'),(10739,'trails',121,'What is the main highlight of the Cottonwood Canyon Trail #22?','The Cottonwood Canyon Trail #22 offers a beautiful hike through juniper trees and presents stunning views of the red cliffs that frame the path.','2025-03-27 22:46:14','2025-03-27 22:46:14'),(10740,'trails',121,'What is the difficulty level of the hike?','This trail is categorized as intermediate, making it suitable for those with some hiking experience.','2025-03-27 22:46:14','2025-03-27 22:46:14'),(10741,'trails',121,'What are the highest and lowest elevations on the trail?','The trail has a consistent elevation of 5049 feet, so there are no significant elevation changes throughout the hike.','2025-03-27 22:46:14','2025-03-27 22:46:14'),(10742,'trails',121,'How long is the Cottonwood Canyon Trail #22?','The trail stretches for 4.5 miles, providing a satisfying hike amidst scenic landscapes.','2025-03-27 22:46:14','2025-03-27 22:46:14'),(10743,'trails',121,'What type of trail is Cottonwood Canyon Trail #22?','Cottonwood Canyon Trail #22 is a point-to-point trail, which means you\'ll start at one point and end at another.','2025-03-27 22:46:14','2025-03-27 22:46:14'),(10744,'trails',121,'What is the total incline and decline of the trail?','Hikers can expect an incline of 510 feet and a decline of 582 feet along the route, which adds to the overall experience.','2025-03-27 22:46:14','2025-03-27 22:46:14'),(10745,'trails',121,'What is the average and maximum grade of the Cottonwood Canyon Trail?','The trail has an average grade of 0.05%, with a maximum grade reaching up to 0.19%.','2025-03-27 22:46:14','2025-03-27 22:46:14'),(10746,'trails',121,'What are the geographical coordinates of the trail?','The trail is located at a latitude of 37.0214 and a longitude of -112.566.','2025-03-27 22:46:14','2025-03-27 22:46:14'),(10747,'trails',122,'What is the starting point for the Sherry Belle Trail?','You can begin your hike on the Sherry Belle Trail at the Sherryville trailhead located off Terrel Avenue.','2025-03-27 22:46:26','2025-03-27 22:46:26'),(10748,'trails',122,'What direction does the Sherry Belle Trail head towards?','The trail descends southward towards the reservoir.','2025-03-27 22:46:26','2025-03-27 22:46:26'),(10749,'trails',122,'How long is the Sherry Belle Trail?','The total length of the Sherry Belle Trail is approximately 4.4 miles.','2025-03-27 22:46:26','2025-03-27 22:46:26'),(10750,'trails',122,'What is the difficulty level of the Sherry Belle Trail?','This trail is considered easy, making it suitable for hikers of all experience levels.','2025-03-27 22:46:26','2025-03-27 22:46:26'),(10751,'trails',122,'What are the elevation details for the trail?','The highest elevation along the trail reaches 4,881 feet, while the lowest elevation is also 4,881 feet, providing a mostly flat terrain.','2025-03-27 22:46:26','2025-03-27 22:46:26'),(10752,'trails',122,'What features can be found along the Sherry Belle Trail?','Hikers can enjoy birding, fishing, swimming, scenic views, and wildlife sightings along the trail.','2025-03-27 22:46:26','2025-03-27 22:46:26'),(10753,'trails',122,'Are there any recreational facilities available on the trail?','Yes, the trail leads to a park equipped with crossfit workout stations, a beach volleyball court, and artificial bouldering rocks.','2025-03-27 22:46:26','2025-03-27 22:46:26'),(10754,'trails',122,'Does the Sherry Belle Trail have any steep sections?','The trail features a gentle incline of 110 feet and a decline of 172 feet, with an average and maximum grade of just 0.01% and 0.09% respectively.','2025-03-27 22:46:26','2025-03-27 22:46:26'),(10755,'trails',122,'Can I bring my dog on the Sherry Belle Trail?','Dogs are welcome on this trail, but they must be kept on a leash.','2025-03-27 22:46:26','2025-03-27 22:46:26'),(10756,'trails',122,'What notable landmarks does the trail connect to?','The trail crosses over a dam and links back to a paved path that circles Kanab and Jackson Flat Reservoir.','2025-03-27 22:46:26','2025-03-27 22:46:26'),(10757,'trails',122,'What are the geographic coordinates of the Sherry Belle Trail?','The trail is located at a latitude of 37.032 and a longitude of -112.506.','2025-03-27 22:46:26','2025-03-27 22:46:26'),(10758,'trails',123,'Where does the K-Hill Trail begin?','The K-Hill Trail starts on the east side, accessible from a charming parking area located at the end of a paved residential road.','2025-03-27 22:46:35','2025-03-27 22:46:35'),(10759,'trails',123,'What can hikers expect to see along the K-Hill Trail?','Hikers will be treated to stunning views as they traverse along the cliffs of Kanab, with magnificent vistas throughout the trail.','2025-03-27 22:46:35','2025-03-27 22:46:35'),(10760,'trails',123,'What is the trail length of the K-Hill Trail?','The K-Hill Trail is approximately 1.8 miles long.','2025-03-27 22:46:35','2025-03-27 22:46:35'),(10761,'trails',123,'What is the difficulty level of the K-Hill Trail?','The trail is categorized as easy to intermediate, making it suitable for a range of hikers.','2025-03-27 22:46:35','2025-03-27 22:46:35'),(10762,'trails',123,'What are the highest and lowest elevations on the trail?','The K-Hill Trail reaches a highest elevation of 5053 feet and has the same lowest elevation of 5053 feet.','2025-03-27 22:46:35','2025-03-27 22:46:35'),(10763,'trails',123,'What type of trail is the K-Hill Trail?','The K-Hill Trail is a point-to-point trail.','2025-03-27 22:46:35','2025-03-27 22:46:35'),(10764,'trails',123,'What is the incline and decline of the K-Hill Trail?','The trail features an incline of 204 feet and a decline of 196 feet.','2025-03-27 22:46:35','2025-03-27 22:46:35'),(10765,'trails',123,'What is the average and maximum grade of the trail?','The average grade of the K-Hill Trail is about 0.04%, with a maximum grade reaching up to 0.13%.','2025-03-27 22:46:35','2025-03-27 22:46:35'),(10766,'trails',123,'Are there any special features along the K-Hill Trail?','Yes, hikers can enjoy birding opportunities, geological significance, beautiful views, and wildlife sightings along the trail.','2025-03-27 22:46:35','2025-03-27 22:46:35'),(10767,'trails',123,'Are dogs allowed on the K-Hill Trail?','Yes, dogs are permitted on the trail, but they must be leashed.','2025-03-27 22:46:35','2025-03-27 22:46:35'),(10768,'trails',123,'Can the K-Hill Trail be combined with other trails?','Absolutely! The K-Hill Trail connects with Tom\'s Canyon Trail and can be paired with several nearby trails for longer hiking experiences.','2025-03-27 22:46:35','2025-03-27 22:46:35'),(10769,'trails',123,'What are the GPS coordinates for the K-Hill Trail?','The trail is located at approximately 37.0464° latitude and -112.501° longitude.','2025-03-27 22:46:35','2025-03-27 22:46:35'),(10770,'trails',124,'Where does the Pugh Canyon trail begin?','The Pugh Canyon trail starts at the end of a paved residential road.','2025-03-27 22:46:41','2025-03-27 22:46:41'),(10771,'trails',124,'What can hikers expect to see along the Pugh Canyon trail?','As you hike along the trail, you\'ll be surrounded by striking red cliffs and a creekbed, with increasingly rich vegetation as you move deeper into the canyon.','2025-03-27 22:46:41','2025-03-27 22:46:41'),(10772,'trails',124,'How difficult is the Pugh Canyon trail?','The trail is classified as easy to intermediate in difficulty, making it accessible for a wide range of hikers.','2025-03-27 22:46:41','2025-03-27 22:46:41'),(10773,'trails',124,'What is the total length of the Pugh Canyon trail?','The Pugh Canyon trail spans approximately 1.7 miles, following a point-to-point route.','2025-03-27 22:46:41','2025-03-27 22:46:41'),(10774,'trails',124,'What elevation changes can hikers expect on this trail?','The highest elevation on the trail reaches 5,052 feet, while the lowest point is also at 5,052 feet, resulting in a minimal incline and decline.','2025-03-27 22:46:41','2025-03-27 22:46:41'),(10775,'trails',124,'Are there any noteworthy features along the Pugh Canyon trail?','Yes, hikers can enjoy opportunities for bird watching, scenic views, encounters with wildlife, vibrant wildflowers, and the highlight: a beautiful 35-foot waterfall at the trail\'s end.','2025-03-27 22:46:41','2025-03-27 22:46:41'),(10776,'trails',124,'Are dogs allowed on the Pugh Canyon trail?','Yes, dogs are welcome on the trail as long as they are leashed.','2025-03-27 22:46:41','2025-03-27 22:46:41'),(10777,'trails',124,'What is the terrain like near the end of the trail?','Towards the end of the trail, the canyon narrows, which can make the path a bit challenging to follow. But sticking close to the creek will guide you to the waterfall.','2025-03-27 22:46:41','2025-03-27 22:46:41'),(10778,'trails',124,'What is the waterfall like at the end of the Pugh Canyon trail?','At the conclusion of the hike, hikers will be rewarded by the sight of a stunning 35-foot waterfall, which features a gentle flow, creating a picturesque scene.','2025-03-27 22:46:41','2025-03-27 22:46:41'),(10779,'trails',124,'What type of trail is the Pugh Canyon trail?','The Pugh Canyon trail is a point-to-point trail, allowing hikers to enjoy a linear journey through the beautiful canyon.','2025-03-27 22:46:41','2025-03-27 22:46:41'),(10780,'trails',125,'What is the length of the Squaw Trail?','The Squaw Trail is approximately 3 miles for a round trip journey.','2025-03-27 22:46:49','2025-03-27 22:46:49'),(10781,'trails',125,'When is the best time to hike the Squaw Trail?','This trail can be enjoyed throughout the year, making it a versatile option for hikers.','2025-03-27 22:46:49','2025-03-27 22:46:49'),(10782,'trails',125,'What is the difficulty level of the Squaw Trail?','The trail is rated as moderate, featuring a steep section with an elevation gain of 780 feet.','2025-03-27 22:46:49','2025-03-27 22:46:49'),(10783,'trails',125,'What are the elevation levels along the Squaw Trail?','Hikers will experience elevations ranging from 5,040 to 5,802 feet.','2025-03-27 22:46:49','2025-03-27 22:46:49'),(10784,'trails',125,'Is the Squaw Trail accessible for all hikers?','Unfortunately, this trail is not wheelchair accessible.','2025-03-27 22:46:49','2025-03-27 22:46:49'),(10785,'trails',125,'Are pets allowed on the Squaw Trail?','Yes, pets are welcome on the trail, but must be kept on a leash.','2025-03-27 22:46:49','2025-03-27 22:46:49'),(10786,'trails',125,'Is a reservation required to hike the Squaw Trail?','No, you do not need a reservation to hike this trail.','2025-03-27 22:46:49','2025-03-27 22:46:49'),(10787,'trails',125,'How long on average does it take to hike the Squaw Trail?','Expect to spend around 2 to 3 hours completing the hike.','2025-03-27 22:46:49','2025-03-27 22:46:49'),(10788,'trails',125,'What type of vehicle is recommended for getting to the Squaw Trail trailhead?','You can reach the trailhead using any type of vehicle.','2025-03-27 22:46:49','2025-03-27 22:46:49'),(10789,'trails',125,'What are the directions to get to the Squaw Trail trailhead?','To find the trailhead, turn at the stoplight of Cemer and Ivain onto Main Street, then take another right on 300 North. After one block, turn left on 100 E, drive past Jacob Hamblin Park, and continue to the Squaw Trail sign.','2025-03-27 22:46:49','2025-03-27 22:46:49'),(10790,'trails',125,'Can you describe the Squaw Trail?','The Squaw Trail is a beloved hiking route in Kanab, easily accessible from the town. It offers a moderately challenging hike with incredible views of the surrounding areas and unique rock formations. At the summit, hikers can connect to other trails as well.','2025-03-27 22:46:49','2025-03-27 22:46:49'),(10791,'trails',125,'Where can I find additional information or maps for the Squaw Trail?','For extra maps and resources, check out the Kane County Visitor Center, or you can download the Kanab Trails App.','2025-03-27 22:46:49','2025-03-27 22:46:49'),(10792,'trails',126,'What is the total length of the Kanarra Creek Trail?','The Kanarra Creek Trail has a round trip length of 4.2 miles.','2025-03-27 22:46:59','2025-03-27 22:46:59'),(10793,'trails',126,'Is Kanarra Creek Trail suitable for families?','Yes, this trail is family-friendly, making it a great option for hiking with children.','2025-03-27 22:46:59','2025-03-27 22:46:59'),(10794,'trails',126,'What is the difficulty level of the Kanarra Creek Trail?','The trail is classified as intermediate to difficult, so some hiking experience may be beneficial.','2025-03-27 22:46:59','2025-03-27 22:46:59'),(10795,'trails',126,'What is the highest elevation on the Kanarra Creek Trail?','The highest point on the trail reaches an elevation of 5,648 feet.','2025-03-27 22:46:59','2025-03-27 22:46:59'),(10796,'trails',126,'What is the lowest elevation on the Kanarra Creek Trail?','The lowest elevation on the trail is also 5,648 feet.','2025-03-27 22:46:59','2025-03-27 22:46:59'),(10797,'trails',126,'Can you describe the trail type for Kanarra Creek?','The Kanarra Creek Trail is a point-to-point trail.','2025-03-27 22:46:59','2025-03-27 22:46:59'),(10798,'trails',126,'What is the elevation change on the Kanarra Creek Trail?','The trail has an elevation gain of 809 feet and a decline of 110 feet.','2025-03-27 22:46:59','2025-03-27 22:46:59'),(10799,'trails',126,'What is the average grade and maximum grade of the Kanarra Creek Trail?','The trail has an average grade of 0.08% and a maximum grade of 0.31%.','2025-03-27 22:46:59','2025-03-27 22:46:59'),(10800,'trails',126,'Where is Kanarra Creek Trail located (latitude and longitude)?','The trail is located at a latitude of 37.5372 and a longitude of -113.176.','2025-03-27 22:46:59','2025-03-27 22:46:59'),(10801,'trails',126,'What can hikers expect to see at the end of the Kanarra Creek Trail?','At the end of the trail, hikers can enjoy a beautiful waterfall and a refreshing pool, perfect for relaxing.','2025-03-27 22:46:59','2025-03-27 22:46:59'),(10802,'trails',127,'What is the Spring Creek Route like?','The Spring Creek Route offers a picturesque experience with a spring and a flowing wash along the first mile, providing a refreshing start to your hike.','2025-03-27 22:47:06','2025-03-27 22:47:06'),(10803,'trails',127,'How difficult is the Spring Creek Route?','This trail is classified as intermediate to difficult, so it\'s perfect for those looking for a challenging outdoor adventure.','2025-03-27 22:47:06','2025-03-27 22:47:06'),(10804,'trails',127,'What are the elevation details of the Spring Creek Route?','The trail reaches a highest elevation of 5617 feet, maintaining the same lowest elevation, making it a consistent trek without drastic elevation changes.','2025-03-27 22:47:06','2025-03-27 22:47:06'),(10805,'trails',127,'What is the length of the Spring Creek Route?','The entire trail spans 3.2 miles, providing ample distance for a rewarding hike.','2025-03-27 22:47:06','2025-03-27 22:47:06'),(10806,'trails',127,'Is the Spring Creek Route a loop or point to point?','The Spring Creek Route is a point-to-point trail, allowing for a straightforward hiking experience.','2025-03-27 22:47:06','2025-03-27 22:47:06'),(10807,'trails',127,'What is the incline and decline of the Spring Creek Route?','Hikers can expect an incline of 912 feet along the route, with a minimal decline of only 9 feet.','2025-03-27 22:47:06','2025-03-27 22:47:06'),(10808,'trails',127,'What is the average grade of the trail?','The trail has an average grade of 0.05%, ensuring a relatively gentle ascent throughout the hike.','2025-03-27 22:47:06','2025-03-27 22:47:06'),(10809,'trails',127,'What is the maximum grade encountered on the trail?','At its steepest point, the maximum grade is 0.37%, making the trail manageable for most intermediate hikers.','2025-03-27 22:47:06','2025-03-27 22:47:06'),(10810,'trails',127,'What are the geographic coordinates of the Spring Creek Route?','The trail is located at a latitude of 37.5215 and a longitude of -113.184, making it easy to find on a map.','2025-03-27 22:47:06','2025-03-27 22:47:06'),(10811,'trails',132,'What is the Cobra Arch Trail?','The Cobra Arch Trail is a scenic hike managed by the BLM Utah - Kanab Field Office, which offers breathtaking views along the Paria Canyon rim before descending to reveal a magnificent standalone sandstone arch.','2025-03-27 22:47:13','2025-03-27 22:47:13'),(10812,'trails',132,'What is the difficulty level of the trail?','The trail is classified as intermediate, making it suitable for those with some hiking experience.','2025-03-27 22:47:13','2025-03-27 22:47:13'),(10813,'trails',132,'What are the elevation details of the trail?','The highest point of the trail reaches 4,654 feet, while the lowest elevation is the same, creating a relatively flat hiking experience despite the 229 feet of incline and 544 feet of decline.','2025-03-27 22:47:13','2025-03-27 22:47:13'),(10814,'trails',132,'How long is the Cobra Arch Trail?','The total length of the trail is 3.5 miles, offering a manageable hiking distance for most adventurers.','2025-03-27 22:47:13','2025-03-27 22:47:13'),(10815,'trails',132,'What type of trail is it?','The Cobra Arch Trail is a point-to-point trail, meaning hikers will start at one point and return to the same location after exploring.','2025-03-27 22:47:13','2025-03-27 22:47:13'),(10816,'trails',132,'What is the average grade of the trail?','The average grade of the trail is quite gentle at 0.04%, with a maximum incline reaching up to 0.21%.','2025-03-27 22:47:13','2025-03-27 22:47:13'),(10817,'trails',132,'What are some highlights of the trail?','Hikers can enjoy stunning views throughout the hike, especially when descending to witness the captivating sandstone arch.','2025-03-27 22:47:13','2025-03-27 22:47:13'),(10818,'trails',132,'Are dogs allowed on the trail?','It is currently unknown if dogs are permitted on the Cobra Arch Trail, so it\'s best to check in with the BLM or local regulations before bringing a pet.','2025-03-27 22:47:13','2025-03-27 22:47:13'),(10819,'trails',132,'What are the geographical coordinates of the trail?','The trail is located at latitude 37.0443 and longitude -111.92.','2025-03-27 22:47:13','2025-03-27 22:47:13'),(10820,'trails',133,'What is the name of the trail?','The trail is called Lottery Location.','2025-03-27 22:47:28','2025-03-27 22:47:28'),(10821,'trails',133,'What is the total distance of the trail?','The trail stretches 2.9 miles.','2025-03-27 22:47:28','2025-03-27 22:47:28'),(10822,'trails',133,'What is the best season to hike this trail?','The ideal season for hiking is not specified, but timing your visit for mild weather is recommended.','2025-03-27 22:47:28','2025-03-27 22:47:28'),(10823,'trails',133,'How difficult is the trail?','The trail is considered to be of intermediate to difficult level.','2025-03-27 22:47:28','2025-03-27 22:47:28'),(10824,'trails',133,'What are the elevation details for the trail?','The highest and lowest points of the trail are both at 4822 feet.','2025-03-27 22:47:28','2025-03-27 22:47:28'),(10825,'trails',133,'What are the latitude and longitude coordinates for the trail?','The trail is located at a latitude of 37.0191 and a longitude of -112.025.','2025-03-27 22:47:28','2025-03-27 22:47:28'),(10826,'trails',133,'Is the trail accessible year-round?','Accessibility details are not provided; please check local conditions before planning your hike.','2025-03-27 22:47:28','2025-03-27 22:47:28'),(10827,'trails',133,'Are pets allowed on this trail?','Pet policies are not specified; check local regulations if you plan to bring your pet.','2025-03-27 22:47:28','2025-03-27 22:47:28'),(10828,'trails',133,'Do I need a reservation to hike this trail?','Yes, a permit is required to hike North and South Coyote Buttes, which can be obtained through an online lottery.','2025-03-27 22:47:28','2025-03-27 22:47:28'),(10829,'trails',133,'How many hours should I expect to spend hiking?','The average time to complete the hike is not mentioned, but plan according to your hiking pace and the trail\'s conditions.','2025-03-27 22:47:28','2025-03-27 22:47:28'),(10830,'trails',133,'What type of vehicle is suitable for getting to the trail?','The trail location suggests accessibility by standard vehicles, but check specific road conditions before your visit.','2025-03-27 22:47:28','2025-03-27 22:47:28'),(10831,'trails',133,'How do I get to the trailhead?','To access the trail, permits must be picked up at the Kane County Office of Tourism in Kanab, where you can also get a safety briefing.','2025-03-27 22:47:28','2025-03-27 22:47:28'),(10832,'trails',133,'Can you provide a brief description of the trail?','Lottery Location is notable for being the only legal lottery in Utah and offers access to the stunning North and South Coyote Buttes regions.','2025-03-27 22:47:28','2025-03-27 22:47:28'),(10833,'trails',133,'What additional information should I know before hiking this trail?','Due to the delicate nature of the area, strict permit requirements apply. A lottery system is in place for permit acquisition to manage visitor impacts.','2025-03-27 22:47:28','2025-03-27 22:47:28'),(10834,'trails',134,'What is the main highlight of this trail?','The trail offers an incredible experience through a stunning slot canyon, which narrows at various points, leading to the remarkable Buckskin Gulch.','2025-03-27 22:47:35','2025-03-27 22:47:35'),(10835,'trails',134,'What is the difficulty level of the trail?','The hike is classified as intermediate, making it suitable for those with some prior hiking experience.','2025-03-27 22:47:35','2025-03-27 22:47:35'),(10836,'trails',134,'What are the highest and lowest elevations along the trail?','The trail maintains a constant elevation of 4722 feet, with no significant change in height.','2025-03-27 22:47:35','2025-03-27 22:47:35'),(10837,'trails',134,'How long is the trail?','The total length of the trail is 1.8 miles, making it a manageable hike for most outdoor enthusiasts.','2025-03-27 22:47:35','2025-03-27 22:47:35'),(10838,'trails',134,'What type of trail is this?','It is a point-to-point trail, meaning you\'ll start at one point and finish at another, providing a unique hiking experience.','2025-03-27 22:47:35','2025-03-27 22:47:35'),(10839,'trails',134,'What are the elevation changes during the hike?','There is a minor incline of 59 feet and a decline of 183 feet along the trail, offering a gentle yet pleasant trek.','2025-03-27 22:47:35','2025-03-27 22:47:35'),(10840,'trails',134,'What is the average grade of the trail?','The average grade is approximately 0.03%, indicating a mostly flat surface throughout the hike.','2025-03-27 22:47:35','2025-03-27 22:47:35'),(10841,'trails',134,'What is the maximum grade encountered on the trail?','The steepest section of the trail reaches a maximum grade of 0.12%, making it quite manageable.','2025-03-27 22:47:35','2025-03-27 22:47:35'),(10842,'trails',134,'What are the geographical coordinates of the trail?','The trail is located at a latitude of 37.0191 and a longitude of -112.025.','2025-03-27 22:47:35','2025-03-27 22:47:35'),(10843,'trails',135,'What is the total distance of the Wire Pass/Buckskin Gulch trail?','The Wire Pass/Buckskin Gulch trail spans approximately 8.4 miles.','2025-03-27 22:47:52','2025-03-27 22:47:52'),(10844,'trails',135,'When is the best time to hike the Wire Pass/Buckskin Gulch trail?','The ideal seasons to hike this trail are Spring, Summer, and Fall.','2025-03-27 22:47:52','2025-03-27 22:47:52'),(10845,'trails',135,'What is the difficulty level of the Wire Pass/Buckskin Gulch trail?','This trail is rated as Difficult, providing a challenging experience for hikers.','2025-03-27 22:47:52','2025-03-27 22:47:52'),(10846,'trails',135,'What is the elevation of the Wire Pass/Buckskin Gulch trail?','The trail reaches an elevation of 4860 feet.','2025-03-27 22:47:52','2025-03-27 22:47:52'),(10847,'trails',135,'Is the Wire Pass/Buckskin Gulch trail accessible for everyone?','Yes, this trail is accessible to hikers.','2025-03-27 22:47:52','2025-03-27 22:47:52'),(10848,'trails',135,'Are pets allowed on the Wire Pass/Buckskin Gulch trail?','Absolutely, pets are welcome on the trail.','2025-03-27 22:47:52','2025-03-27 22:47:52'),(10849,'trails',135,'Do I need reservations to hike the Wire Pass/Buckskin Gulch trail?','No reservations are required for this trail.','2025-03-27 22:47:52','2025-03-27 22:47:52'),(10850,'trails',135,'How long does it typically take to hike the Wire Pass/Buckskin Gulch trail?','Hikers can expect to spend between 12 hours and 2 days on this trail.','2025-03-27 22:47:52','2025-03-27 22:47:52'),(10851,'trails',135,'What type of vehicle is recommended for getting to the Wire Pass/Buckskin Gulch trailhead?','A 4x4 vehicle is recommended for the best access to the trailhead.','2025-03-27 22:47:52','2025-03-27 22:47:52'),(10852,'trails',135,'How do I get to the Wire Pass/Buckskin Gulch trailhead?','To reach the trailhead, drive 38.6 miles east from Kanab on Hwy 89. After passing mile post 26, turn right onto House Rock Valley Road and travel 4 miles to the Wire Pass Trailhead parking area, located on your right.','2025-03-27 22:47:52','2025-03-27 22:47:52'),(10853,'trails',135,'Can you describe the Wire Pass/Buckskin Gulch hiking experience?','The Wire Pass/Buckskin Gulch trail offers a captivating adventure through stunning slot canyons starting from the Wire Pass Trailhead. You\'ll hike through a wash before entering the narrow canyon sections, which may present challenges like boulder jams and deep water pools, surrounded by breathtaking rock formations.','2025-03-27 22:47:52','2025-03-27 22:47:52'),(10854,'trails',135,'What additional precautions should hikers take before embarking on this trail?','Before heading into the canyon, check the weather and potential flash flood risks. It\'s essential to bring ample water, as there are no water sources available inside Buckskin Gulch. Additionally, bringing a rope can be helpful for lowering gear and for safety. Always respect private property and adhere to leave-no-trace principles.','2025-03-27 22:47:52','2025-03-27 22:47:52'),(10855,'trails',135,'Can I use a GPS while hiking the Wire Pass/Buckskin Gulch trail?','It\'s important to note that GPS may not function well in the canyon due to minimal sky visibility.','2025-03-27 22:47:52','2025-03-27 22:47:52'),(10856,'trails',135,'What kind of features can I expect along the Wire Pass/Buckskin Gulch trail?','Hikers will encounter a variety of features including fascinating caves, the nearby river or creek, and stunning views throughout the hike.','2025-03-27 22:47:52','2025-03-27 22:47:52'),(10857,'trails',135,'What precautions should I take regarding my dog while hiking the Wire Pass/Buckskin Gulch?','If you bring your dog, make sure it is leashed during the hike.','2025-03-27 22:47:52','2025-03-27 22:47:52'),(10858,'trails',135,'What can I expect in terms of elevation change on this trail?','Throughout the hike, expect a vertical incline of approximately 660 feet and a decline of about 1007 feet.','2025-03-27 22:47:52','2025-03-27 22:47:52'),(10859,'trails',136,'What is the White House Trail like?','The White House Trail offers an engaging hike and wade experience along an alkaline river, immersing you in a rich ecosystem where you can spot various bird species and lizards.','2025-03-27 22:48:00','2025-03-27 22:48:00'),(10860,'trails',136,'How long is the White House Trail?','The trail stretches about 7.5 miles, providing a good amount of hiking and wading adventure.','2025-03-27 22:48:00','2025-03-27 22:48:00'),(10861,'trails',136,'What is the difficulty level of the White House Trail?','This trail is considered to be of intermediate difficulty, making it suitable for those with some hiking experience.','2025-03-27 22:48:01','2025-03-27 22:48:01'),(10862,'trails',136,'What is the elevation range of the White House Trail?','The trail maintains a steady elevation of 4182 feet, with a slight incline and decline during your hike.','2025-03-27 22:48:01','2025-03-27 22:48:01'),(10863,'trails',136,'What kind of terrain can I expect on the trail?','Hikers will encounter both hiking and wading segments along the alkaline river, and should be mindful of quicksand areas.','2025-03-27 22:48:01','2025-03-27 22:48:01'),(10864,'trails',136,'Is the White House Trail a loop or point-to-point?','The White House Trail is a point-to-point trail, meaning you\'ll need to plan for transportation back to your starting point.','2025-03-27 22:48:01','2025-03-27 22:48:01'),(10865,'trails',136,'What is the total incline and decline on the trail?','Throughout the trail, expect an incline of around 388 feet and a decline of about 450 feet.','2025-03-27 22:48:01','2025-03-27 22:48:01'),(10866,'trails',136,'What is the maximum grade of the White House Trail?','The maximum grade on this trail is 0.26%, making it fairly gentle overall.','2025-03-27 22:48:01','2025-03-27 22:48:01'),(10867,'trails',136,'What types of wildlife might I see on this trail?','While hiking, keep an eye out for a variety of birds and lizards that inhabit the area around the alkaline river.','2025-03-27 22:48:01','2025-03-27 22:48:01'),(10868,'trails',136,'What are the GPS coordinates for the White House Trail?','The trail is located at latitude 37.0015 and longitude -111.866.','2025-03-27 22:48:01','2025-03-27 22:48:01'),(10869,'trails',137,'What makes Whiterocks trail unique?','Whiterocks trail offers a refreshing escape from the typical red rock scenery, showcasing striking natural formations and a variety of plant life throughout the hike.','2025-03-27 22:48:09','2025-03-27 22:48:09'),(10870,'trails',137,'What is the difficulty level of the Whiterocks trail?','The difficulty of the Whiterocks trail is classified as intermediate, making it suitable for hikers with some experience.','2025-03-27 22:48:09','2025-03-27 22:48:09'),(10871,'trails',137,'What is the highest elevation along the Whiterocks trail?','The highest point on the Whiterocks trail reaches an elevation of 3754 feet.','2025-03-27 22:48:09','2025-03-27 22:48:09'),(10872,'trails',137,'What is the lowest elevation on the Whiterocks trail?','Interestingly, the lowest elevation on the Whiterocks trail is also 3754 feet, indicating a relatively flat hike.','2025-03-27 22:48:09','2025-03-27 22:48:09'),(10873,'trails',137,'How long is the Whiterocks trail?','The total length of the Whiterocks trail is 1.6 miles, making it a manageable distance for most hikers.','2025-03-27 22:48:09','2025-03-27 22:48:09'),(10874,'trails',137,'What type of trail is Whiterocks?','Whiterocks is a point-to-point trail, meaning hikers will start at one point and finish at another, requiring transportation for the return trip.','2025-03-27 22:48:09','2025-03-27 22:48:09'),(10875,'trails',137,'What is the elevation decline on the Whiterocks trail?','During the hike, you will experience an elevation decline of 463 feet, providing a gradual descent as you progress.','2025-03-27 22:48:09','2025-03-27 22:48:09'),(10876,'trails',137,'What is the average and maximum grade of the Whiterocks trail?','The trail has an average grade of 0.05%, and peaks at a maximum grade of 0.16%, indicating a relatively gentle terrain.','2025-03-27 22:48:09','2025-03-27 22:48:09'),(10877,'trails',137,'What are the geographical coordinates of the Whiterocks trail?','The Whiterocks trail is located at a latitude of 37.2376 and a longitude of -113.637.','2025-03-27 22:48:09','2025-03-27 22:48:09'),(10878,'trails',138,'What kind of terrain can I expect on the Lava Flow Trail?','The Lava Flow Trail features a unique landscape with a surprisingly lush vegetated lava field, providing a fascinating contrast to the volcanic rock.','2025-03-27 22:48:14','2025-03-27 22:48:14'),(10879,'trails',138,'What is the difficulty level of the Lava Flow Trail?','This trail is categorized as intermediate, making it suitable for hikers with some experience.','2025-03-27 22:48:14','2025-03-27 22:48:14'),(10880,'trails',138,'What are the highest and lowest elevations on the trail?','Both the highest and lowest points of the trail are at an elevation of 3405 feet.','2025-03-27 22:48:14','2025-03-27 22:48:14'),(10881,'trails',138,'How long is the Lava Flow Trail?','The trail stretches for 1.3 miles, offering a manageable hike.','2025-03-27 22:48:14','2025-03-27 22:48:14'),(10882,'trails',138,'What type of trail is the Lava Flow Trail?','The Lava Flow Trail is a point-to-point trail, requiring hikers to plan transportation for both ends.','2025-03-27 22:48:14','2025-03-27 22:48:14'),(10883,'trails',138,'What is the elevation change on the Lava Flow Trail?','The trail features a minor incline of 19 feet and a decline of 389 feet.','202