93,'trails',139,'What is the maximum grade on the Butterfly Trail?','The steepest section of the Butterfly Trail has a maximum grade of 0.12%, which is relatively mild.','2025-03-27 22:48:19','2025-03-27 22:48:19'),(10894,'trails',139,'What are the GPS coordinates for the Butterfly Trail?','The Butterfly Trail is located at approximately 37.2157° latitude and -113.644° longitude.','2025-03-27 22:48:19','2025-03-27 22:48:19'),(10895,'trails',140,'What kind of experience can I expect at Whiterocks Amphitheater?','Whiterocks Amphitheater offers a fantastic hiking experience, highlighted by its breathtaking sandstone pothole, making it an exciting destination for nature lovers.','2025-03-27 22:48:25','2025-03-27 22:48:25'),(10896,'trails',140,'What is the difficulty level of the hike?','The hike is classified as intermediate to difficult, so it\'s recommended for those with some hiking experience.','2025-03-27 22:48:25','2025-03-27 22:48:25'),(10897,'trails',140,'What is the highest elevation on the trail?','The trail reaches a maximum elevation of 4,192 feet.','2025-03-27 22:48:25','2025-03-27 22:48:25'),(10898,'trails',140,'What is the lowest elevation on the trail?','The lowest elevation along the trail is also 4,192 feet, indicating a fairly flat terrain.','2025-03-27 22:48:25','2025-03-27 22:48:25'),(10899,'trails',140,'How long is the trail?','The total length of the trail is 0.2 miles, making it a short hike.','2025-03-27 22:48:25','2025-03-27 22:48:25'),(10900,'trails',140,'What type of trail is this?','The trail is a point-to-point hike.','2025-03-27 22:48:25','2025-03-27 22:48:25'),(10901,'trails',140,'What is the total incline for the hike?','The hike features a total incline of 87 feet.','2025-03-27 22:48:25','2025-03-27 22:48:25'),(10902,'trails',140,'What is the total decline on the trail?','Participants will experience a decline of 12 feet while hiking.','2025-03-27 22:48:25','2025-03-27 22:48:25'),(10903,'trails',140,'What is the average grade of the trail?','The trail has an average grade of 0.08%, making it relatively gentle overall.','2025-03-27 22:48:25','2025-03-27 22:48:25'),(10904,'trails',140,'What is the maximum grade found on the trail?','The maximum gradient encountered on this trail is 0.27%.','2025-03-27 22:48:25','2025-03-27 22:48:25'),(10905,'trails',140,'What are the geographical coordinates of Whiterocks Amphitheater?','The geographic coordinates for Whiterocks Amphitheater are approximately 37.2368° latitude and -113.64° longitude.','2025-03-27 22:48:25','2025-03-27 22:48:25'),(10906,'trails',141,'What is the Padre Canyon Trail like?','The Padre Canyon Trail is a challenging hike that takes you through stunning landscapes, including a wash marked by several cairns as you make your way to a picturesque saddle with impressive views of the White Cliffs section of the park.','2025-03-27 22:48:34','2025-03-27 22:48:34'),(10907,'trails',141,'How difficult is the Padre Canyon Trail?','This trail is rated as difficult, making it best suited for experienced hikers who are comfortable with challenging terrain.','2025-03-27 22:48:34','2025-03-27 22:48:34'),(10908,'trails',141,'What are the elevations on the Padre Canyon Trail?','The trail has a consistent highest and lowest elevation of 3,144 feet, providing a steady environment as you complete the hike.','2025-03-27 22:48:34','2025-03-27 22:48:34'),(10909,'trails',141,'What is the total length of the Padre Canyon Trail?','The Padre Canyon Trail spans 3.1 miles, taking you through scenic routes and rewarding views.','2025-03-27 22:48:34','2025-03-27 22:48:34'),(10910,'trails',141,'What type of trail is Padre Canyon?','This is a point-to-point trail, meaning you will start and finish at different locations.','2025-03-27 22:48:34','2025-03-27 22:48:34'),(10911,'trails',141,'What is the incline and decline on the trail?','During the hike, you will face an incline of 537 feet and a decline of 279 feet, adding to the overall challenging experience.','2025-03-27 22:48:34','2025-03-27 22:48:34'),(10912,'trails',141,'What is the average and maximum grade of the Padre Canyon Trail?','The average grade of the trail is a gentle 0.05%, while the maximum steepness reaches up to 0.22%, indicating some points of increased challenge.','2025-03-27 22:48:34','2025-03-27 22:48:34'),(10913,'trails',141,'What features can I expect on the trail?','Hikers can look forward to stunning views along the trail, particularly from the saddle where you can see the mesmerizing White Cliffs.','2025-03-27 22:48:34','2025-03-27 22:48:34'),(10914,'trails',141,'Are dogs allowed on the Padre Canyon Trail?','It is currently unclear whether dogs are permitted on this trail, so it would be best to check local regulations before your hike.','2025-03-27 22:48:34','2025-03-27 22:48:34'),(10915,'trails',141,'What are the GPS coordinates for the Padre Canyon Trail?','The trail is located at a latitude of 37.178 and a longitude of -113.646, which you can use for navigation.','2025-03-27 22:48:34','2025-03-27 22:48:34'),(10916,'trails',142,'What is the Red Sands Trail like?','The Red Sands Trail offers a unique experience as it navigates through both deep sand and varied desert landscapes. Expect to encounter a significant amount of deep sand along the path, making your journey both challenging and rewarding.','2025-03-27 22:48:43','2025-03-27 22:48:43'),(10917,'trails',142,'How long is the Red Sands Trail?','The Red Sands Trail spans 1.7 miles, making it a manageable yet engaging hike.','2025-03-27 22:48:43','2025-03-27 22:48:43'),(10918,'trails',142,'What is the difficulty level of the Red Sands Trail?','This trail is rated as difficult, so be prepared for the challenges it presents, especially the deep sand and varied terrain.','2025-03-27 22:48:43','2025-03-27 22:48:43'),(10919,'trails',142,'What are the elevation details for the Red Sands Trail?','The trail reaches a highest elevation of 3,332 feet and starts at the same elevation, maintaining a stable altitude over the hike.','2025-03-27 22:48:43','2025-03-27 22:48:43'),(10920,'trails',142,'What should I prepare for when hiking the Red Sands Trail?','Make sure to allocate enough time for your hike, as navigating through deep sand can be time-consuming. It\'s essential to bring plenty of water to stay hydrated throughout your adventure.','2025-03-27 22:48:43','2025-03-27 22:48:43'),(10921,'trails',142,'What is the incline and decline of the Red Sands Trail?','The trail features a total incline of 138 feet and a decline of 57 feet, which adds to the overall challenge of the hike.','2025-03-27 22:48:43','2025-03-27 22:48:43'),(10922,'trails',142,'What type of hiking trail is the Red Sands Trail?','The Red Sands Trail is a point-to-point trail, providing a unique route to explore the area\'s landscapes.','2025-03-27 22:48:43','2025-03-27 22:48:43'),(10923,'trails',142,'Are dogs allowed on the Red Sands Trail?','The current policy regarding dogs on the Red Sands Trail is unclear. It’s advisable to check local regulations or guidelines before bringing your dog.','2025-03-27 22:48:43','2025-03-27 22:48:43'),(10924,'trails',142,'What kind of views can I expect from the Red Sands Trail?','Hikers on the Red Sands Trail will be treated to stunning views of the surrounding desert landscape, enhancing the overall hiking experience.','2025-03-27 22:48:43','2025-03-27 22:48:43'),(10925,'trails',142,'What are the geographical coordinates of the Red Sands Trail?','The Red Sands Trail is located at a latitude of 37.2022 and a longitude of -113.643.','2025-03-27 22:48:43','2025-03-27 22:48:43'),(10926,'trails',143,'What is the general experience of hiking the Whiptail Trail?','The Whiptail Trail offers an enjoyable experience alongside Snow Canyon Drive, featuring a well-maintained paved path that is ideal for both cyclists and pedestrians. It creates a convenient route to return to your vehicle after enjoying the scenic Padre Canyon Trail.','2025-03-27 22:48:51','2025-03-27 22:48:51'),(10