y surrounding the path.','2025-03-27 22:48:51','2025-03-27 22:48:51'),(10935,'trails',143,'What is the general geographical information for the Whiptail Trail?','The Whiptail Trail is located at a latitude of 37.2135 and a longitude of -113.642, positioning it beautifully within Snow Canyon State Park.','2025-03-27 22:48:51','2025-03-27 22:48:51'),(10936,'trails',144,'What unique features can I expect to see on the Petrified Dunes Trail?','The Petrified Dunes Trail offers stunning petrified dunes that are a favorite among photographers due to their striking formations and colors. The trail also leads to a high point that provides fantastic panoramic views of the surrounding landscape.','2025-03-27 22:48:59','2025-03-27 22:48:59'),(10937,'trails',144,'Is it permissible to take Moqui Balls from the trail?','No, visitors are encouraged to practice Leave No Trace principles, which means observing Moqui Balls without collecting them. It\'s important to respect the natural environment and leave these unique features for others to enjoy.','2025-03-27 22:48:59','2025-03-27 22:48:59'),(10938,'trails',144,'What is the difficulty level of the Petrified Dunes Trail?','This trail is classified as intermediate to difficult, making it suitable for those with some hiking experience.','2025-03-27 22:48:59','2025-03-27 22:48:59'),(10939,'trails',144,'What are the elevation details for Petrified Dunes Trail?','The trail has a consistent elevation of 3444 feet throughout, with a total incline of 56 feet and a decline of 227 feet.','2025-03-27 22:48:59','2025-03-27 22:48:59'),(10940,'trails',144,'How long is the Petrified Dunes Trail?','The trail is approximately 0.7 miles long and follows a point-to-point format.','2025-03-27 22:48:59','2025-03-27 22:48:59'),(10941,'trails',144,'What is the average and maximum grade of the trail?','The average grade for the Petrified Dunes Trail is about 0.08%, with a maximum grade reaching up to 0.30%.','2025-03-27 22:48:59','2025-03-27 22:48:59'),(10