ad is a gentle 0.02%, with a maximum grade reaching up to 0.05%, ensuring a comfortable hiking experience.','2025-03-27 22:49:07','2025-03-27 22:49:07'),(10951,'trails',145,'What features can hikers expect to see on this trail?','The trail offers beautiful scenic views, perfect for enjoying the surrounding natural landscapes.','2025-03-27 22:49:07','2025-03-27 22:49:07'),(10952,'trails',145,'Are dogs allowed on West Canyon Road?','Information about whether dogs are allowed on this trail is currently unknown.','2025-03-27 22:49:07','2025-03-27 22:49:07'),(10953,'trails',145,'What are the geographic coordinates of West Canyon Road?','The coordinates for this trail are approximately 37.1949° latitude and -113.648° longitude.','2025-03-27 22:49:07','2025-03-27 22:49:07'),(10954,'trails',146,'What is the Hidden Pinyon Overlook Spur?','The Hidden Pinyon Overlook Spur is a scenic trail located in Snow Canyon State Park, offering stunning views of the surrounding landscapes.','2025-03-27 22:49:13','2025-03-27 22:49:13'),(10955,'trails',146,'Who manages the Hidden Pinyon Overlook Spur?','The trail is managed by Utah State Parks, specifically within the Snow Canyon regional area.','2025-03-27 22:49:13','2025-03-27 22:49:13'),(10956,'trails',146,'What is the difficulty level of the trail?','The trail is rated as intermediate, making it suitable for hikers with some experience.','2025-03-27 22:49:13','2025-03-27 22:49:13'),(10957,'trails',146,'What is the elevation range of the trail?','The trail maintains a consistent elevation, reaching a highest point of 3,433 feet throughout.','2025-03-27 22:49:13','2025-03-27 22:49:13'),(10958,'trails',146,'How long is the Hidden Pinyon Overlook Spur?','This trail is quite short, measuring only 0.1 miles in length.','2025-03-27 22:49:13','2025-03-27 22:49:13'),(10959,'trails',146,'What type of trail is it?','The trail type is currently classified as unknown.','2025-03-27 22:49:13','2025-03-27 22:49:13'),(10960,'trails',146,'What is the incline of the trail?','The trail has an incline of 43 feet, which contributes to its intermediate difficulty.','2025-03-27 22:49:13','2025-03-27 22:49:13'),(10961,'trails',146,'What is the average grade of the Hidden Pinyon Overlook Spur?','The average grade of the trail is approximately 0.09%, indicating a gentle slope throughout.','2025-03-27 22:49:13','2025-03-27 22:49:13'),(10962,'trails',146,'What is the maximum grade experienced on the trail?','Hikers may encounter a maximum grade of 0.22%, which is manageable for those with some hiking experience.','2025-03-27 22:49:13','2025-03-27 22:49:13'),(10963,'trails',146,'What notable features does the Hidden Pinyon Overlook Spur offer?','The trail is known for its panoramic views, providing hikers with breathtaking scenery of the surrounding landscapes.','2025-03-27 22:49:13','2025-03-27 22:49:13'),(10964,'trails',146,'What are the geographic coordinates of the trail?','The Hidden Pinyon Overlook Spur is located at a latitude of 37.2084 and a longitude of -113.647.','2025-03-27 22:49:13','2025-03-27 22:49:13'),(10965,'trails',147,'What is the Johnson Arch Trail like?','The Johnson Arch Trail is a short and accessible hike that leads to a magnificent natural arch, offering breathtaking views along the way.','2025-03-27 22:49:19','2025-03-27 22:49:19'),(10966,'trails',147,'What is the difficulty level of the Johnson Arch Trail?','The trail is categorized as easy to intermediate, making it a suitable option for a wide range of hikers.','2025-03-27 22:49:20','2025-03-27 22:49:20'),(10967,'trails',147,'What is the total length of the Johnson Arch Trail?','This trail spans approximately 0.9 miles, making it a quick adventure for those looking to enjoy some time outdoors.','2025-03-27 22:49:20','2025-03-27 22:49:20'),(10968,'trails',147,'Is the Johnson Arch Trail a loop or point-to-point?','The Johnson Arch Trail is a point-to-point trail, meaning that you\'ll return the same way you came.','2025-03-27 22:49:20','2025-03-27 22:49:20'),(10969,'trails',147,'What is the elevation gain on the Johnson Arch Trail?','The trail features a gentle incline of about 85 feet, with a decline of 75 feet, making it relatively manageable.','2025-03-27 22:49:20','2025-03-27 22:49:20'),(10970,'trails',147,'What are the elevation details of the Johnson Arch Trail?','The trail starts and ends at an elevation of 3,104 feet, ensuring a consistent hiking experience without major altitude changes.','2025-03-27 22:49:20','2025-03-27 22:49:20'),(10971,'trails',147,'What is the average and maximum grade of the Johnson Arch Trail?','The average grade is a mild 0.03%, while the maximum grade reaches up to 0.17%, ensuring an easy walk with minimal strain.','2025-03-27 22:49:20','2025-03-27 22:49:20'),(10972,'trails',147,'Where is the Johnson Arch Trail located?','The trail is situated at a latitude of 37.1781 and a longitude of -113.645, providing picturesque surroundings.','2025-03-27 22:49:20','2025-03-27 22:49:20'),(10973,'trails',148,'What is the Scout Cave Trail?','The Scout Cave Trail connects Snow Canyon to the Paradise Canyon Area and can be traversed in either direction. The trail features diverse terrain and includes a shallow cave situated along the path.','2025-03-27 22:49:29','2025-03-27 22:49:29'),(10974,'trails',148,'How do I access the Scout Cave Trail?','There isn\'t a dedicated trailhead for the Scout Cave Trail. It can be reached from the Johnson\'s Arch Trail in the north, approximately 0.4 miles from its trailhead, or from the Gila Trail in the south, which is a little over a mile from the nearest trailhead on Cascade Canyon Drive.','2025-03-27 22:49:29','2025-03-27 22:49:29'),(10975,'trails',148,'What can I expect on the north section of the trail?','The northern section of the trail runs along the edge of a lava flow above Sand Hollow Wash, crosses the wash, and then ascends to the base of a cliff to reach Scout Cave—though don\'t expect a grand cave experience, it\'s essentially just a hole in the cliff.','2025-03-27 22:49:29','2025-03-27 22:49:29'),(10976,'trails',148,'What does the southern section of the trail offer?','The southern end of the Scout Cave Trail ascends to the top of the red cliffs, where it connects with the Gila Trail. From there, hikers can continue south into the Paradise Canyon section of the state park or north towards the Ledges area.','2025-03-27 22:49:29','2025-03-27 22:49:29'),(10977,'trails',148,'What is the difficulty level of the trail?','The trail is categorized as intermediate to difficult, making it suitable for those with some hiking experience.','2025-03-27 22:49:29','2025-03-27 22:49:29'),(10978,'trails',148,'What are the elevation details for the trail?','The Scout Cave Trail has a maximum elevation of 2,961 feet and a minimum elevation of the same, indicating a relatively flat terrain throughout the hike.','2025-03-27 22:49:29','2025-03-27 22:49:29'),(10979,'trails',148,'What is the length of the Scout Cave Trail?','The total length of the trail is approximately 2.7 miles, providing a manageable hiking distance.','2025-03-27 22:49:29','2025-03-27 22:49:29'),(10980,'trails',148,'Is the Scout Cave Trail a loop or point-to-point?','The trail is a point-to-point route, meaning you will need to return via the same path or arrange for transportation at one end.','2025-03-27 22:49:29','2025-03-27 22:49:29'),(10981,'trails',148,'What is the incline and decline on this trail?','The trail features an incline of 481 feet and a decline of 213 feet, offering some challenging sections to ascend.','2025-03-27 22:49:29','2025-03-27 22:49:29'),(10982,'trails',148,'What is the average and maximum grade of the trail?','The average grade is about 0.05%, with the maximum grade reaching up to 0.23%, indicating generally mild slopes.','2025-03-27 22:49:29','2025-03-27 22:49:29'),(10983,'trails',148,'Are dogs allowed on the Scout Cave Trail?','It is currently unclear whether dogs are permitted on the Scout Cave Trail, so hikers with pets sh