hallenging nature.','2025-03-27 22:54:27','2025-03-27 22:54:27'),(11200,'trails',96,'What is the average and maximum grade of the trail?','The average grade is relatively gentle at 0.03%, but the maximum grade can reach up to 0.09%, indicating some steeper sections.','2025-03-27 22:54:27','2025-03-27 22:54:27'),(11201,'trails',96,'What are the geographical coordinates of the trail?','The Bull Valley Gorge Route is located at a latitude of 37.4732 and a longitude of -112.116.','2025-03-27 22:54:27','2025-03-27 22:54:27'),(11202,'trails',96,'What kind of scenery can hikers expect on the Bull Valley Gorge Route?','Hikers can look forward to stunning geological formations and breathtaking views throughout the journey.','2025-03-27 22:54:27','2025-03-27 22:54:27'),(11203,'trails',99,'What kind of trail is the White Trail?','The White Trail is a mostly flat doubletrack that winds through the heart of Gooseberry Mesa, offering a unique blend of surfaces including hard packed dirt, sand, and slickrock.','2025-03-27 22:54:34','2025-03-27 22:54:34'),(11204,'trails',99,'How does the White Trail connect to other trails?','This trail serves as a convenient connector, making it easier to create loops with various other trails within the Gooseberry network.','2025-03-27 22:54:34','2025-03-27 22:54:34'),(11205,'trails',99,'What is the difficulty level of the White Trail?','The White Trail is rated as intermediate in difficulty.','2025-03-27 22:54:34','2025-03-27 22:54:34'),(11206,'trails',99,'What are the elevation details of the White Trail?','The highest elevation along the trail reaches 5164 feet, while the lowest point also sits at 5164 feet.','2025-03-27 22:54:34','2025-03-27 22:54:34'),(11207,'trails',99,'What is the total length of the White Trail?','The White Trail spans a total distance of 3.2 miles.','2025-03-27 22:54:34','2025-03-27 22:54:34'),(11208,'trails',99,'What is the incline and decline on the White Trail?','The trail features an incline of 273 feet and a decline of 81 feet.','2025-03-27 22:54:34','2025-03-27 22:54:34'),(11209,'trails',99,'What are the average and maximum grades of the White Trail?','The average grade of the White Trail is a gentle 0.02%, with a maximum grade of 0.24%.','2025-03-27 22:54:34','2025-03-27 22:54:34'),(11210,'trails',99,'What kind of views can hikers expect on the White Trail?','Hikers can enjoy scenic views throughout their journey along the White Trail.','2025-03-27 22:54:34','2025-03-27 22:54:34'),(11211,'trails',99,'Are dogs allowed on the White Trail?','The policy regarding dogs on the White Trail remains unclear.','2025-03-27 22:54:34','2025-03-27 22:54:34'),(11212,'trails',99,'What are the geographical coordinates of the White Trail?','The White Trail is located at a latitude of 37.1415 and a longitude of -113.173.','2025-03-27 22:54:34','2025-03-27 22:54:34'),(11213,'trails',102,'What is the Windmill Trail like?','The Windmill Trail is a traditional singletrack that provides a refreshing change from the slickrock terrain, with stunning views to enjoy after spending the day on other Gooseberry trails.','2025-03-27 22:54:39','2025-03-27 22:54:39'),(11214,'trails',102,'What is the difficulty level of the Windmill Trail?','This trail is considered to be of intermediate difficulty.','2025-03-27 22:54:39','2025-03-27 22:54:39'),(11215,'trails',102,'What are the highest and lowest elevations on the trail?','The highest and lowest elevations on the Windmill Trail remain at 5067 feet.','2025-03-27 22:54:39','2025-03-27 22:54:39'),(11216,'trails',102,'How long is the Windmill Trail?','The length of the Windmill Trail is 1.3 miles.','2025-03-27 22:54:39','2025-03-27 22:54:39'),(11217,'trails',102,'What type of trail is the Windmill Trail?','The Windmill Trail is a point-to-point trail.','2025-03-27 22:54:39','2025-03-27 22:54:39'),(11218,'trails',102,'What is the elevation decline on this trail?','The trail experiences a decline of 115 feet.','2025-03-27 22:54:39','2025-03-27 22:54:39'),(11219,'trails',102,'What is the average grade of the Windmill Trail?','The average grade of the trail is quite gentle, at 0.02%.','2025-03-27 22:54:39','2025-03-27 22:54:39'),(11220,'trails',102,'What is the maximum grade on the Windmill Trail?','The maximum grade reaches up to 0.03%.','2025-03-27 22:54:39','2025-03-27 22:54:39'),(11221,'trails',102,'What are the latitude and longitude coordinates of the Windmill Trail?','The trail is located at a latitude of 37.1468 and a longitude of -113.184.','2025-03-27 22:54:39','2025-03-27 22:54:39'),(11222,'trails',104,'What is the Dead Ringer trail?','The Dead Ringer trail is located within the Hurricane Cliffs Trail network and was completed in 2015, thanks to a collaboration between the Dixie Mountain Bike Trails Association and the BLM. It features a fascinating history, having been named after the skeletal remains of a cow found during its scouting, which still had a bell around its neck.','2025-03-27 22:54:48','2025-03-27 22:54:48'),(11223,'trails',104,'What type of climbing and descending experience does Dead Ringer offer?','Hikers can expect an accessible climb to the JEM parking lot, facilitated by a lengthy bench trail built at a gentle 6% grade. This trail also provides an enjoyable descent with smooth paths and stunning views. Two trail splits are available, allowing hikers to choose between easy or more challenging descents.','2025-03-27 22:54:48','2025-03-27 22:54:48'),(11224,'trails',104,'Can Dead Ringer be combined with other trails?','Yes, while Dead Ringer can be enjoyed as a standalone out-and-back trail, it can also be linked with the JEM Trail or the Goulds Rim Trail for extended routes exceeding 20 miles.','2025-03-27 22:54:48','2025-03-27 22:54:48'),(11225,'trails',104,'Are there any cautionary details hikers should consider?','Hikers should be aware that the trail accommodates two-way traffic and features several blind corners, particularly in the narrower sections of the bench. It’s advisable to be cautious about speed and maintain awareness of your surroundings.','2025-03-27 22:54:48','2025-03-27 22:54:48'),(11226,'trails',104,'What is the difficulty level of the Dead Ringer trail?','The trail is rated as easy to intermediate, making it suitable for a wide range of hikers.','2025-03-27 22:54:48','2025-03-27 22:54:48'),(11227,'trails',104,'What is the elevation range of Dead Ringer?','The highest elevation along the trail reaches 3,777 feet, with a minimal decline of 60 feet, keeping the hike relatively mild in terms of elevation changes.','2025-03-27 22:54:48','2025-03-27 22:54:48'),(11228,'trails',104,'How long is the Dead Ringer trail?','The total length of the Dead Ringer trail is approximately 5.2 miles.','2025-03-27 22:54:48','2025-03-27 22:54:48'),(11229,'trails',104,'What features can hikers expect on the Dead Ringer trail?','Hikers will be treated to beautiful vistas throughout their journey, making this a visually rewarding hike.','2025-03-27 22:54:48','2025-03-27 22:54:48'),(11230,'trails',104,'Are dogs allowed on the Dead Ringer trail?','Yes, dogs are permitted on the trail, and they can enjoy some time off-leash.','2025-03-27 22:54:48','2025-03-27 22:54:48'),(11231,'trails',104,'What are the trail coordinates?','The Dead Ringer trail is located at a latitude of 37.1766 and a longitude of -113.239.','2025-03-27 22:54:48','2025-03-27 22:54:48'),(11232,'trails',107,'What is the overall experience of the Cryptobionic Family Friendly trail?','The Cryptobionic Family Friendly trail offers a delightful hiking experience with its smooth, easy-to-navigate pathway, making it perfect for families. It features stunning views and a pleasant ambiance, ideal for combining with other trails.','2025-03-27 22:54:56','2025-03-27 22:54:56'),(11233,'trails',107,'What is the difficulty level of the Cryptobionic trail?','The trail is rated as intermediate, making it manageable for those with some hiking experience.','2025-03-27 22:54:56','2025-03-27 22:54:56'),(11234,'trails',107,'What are the elevation statistics for this trail?','The trail has a consistent elevation, featuring a highest point of 3,667 feet. Its incline is 279 feet and decline is 26 feet.','2025-03-27 22:54:56','2025-03-27 22:54:56'),(11235,'trails',107,'How long is the Cryptobionic Family Friendly trail?','The trail spans 3.3 miles in length, designed as a point-to-point hike.','2025-03-27 22:54:56','2025-03-27 22:54:56'),(11236,'trails',107,'What is the average and maximum grade of the trail?','The trail has an average grade of just 0.02%, with a maximum grade of 0.09%, ensuring a gentle hiking experience.','2025-03-27 22:54:56','2025-03-27 22:54:56'),(11237,'trails',107,'What features can hikers expect on the trail?','Hikers will enjoy breathtaking views throughout the trail, adding to the overall experience.','2025-03-27 22:54:56','2025-03-27 22:54:56'),(11238,'trails',107,'Are dogs allowed on the Cryptobionic trail?','It\'s currently unknown if dogs are permitted on this trail, so be sure to check any specific regulations before your hike.','2025-03-27 22:54:56','2025-03-27 22:54:56'),(11239,'trails',107,'What are the geographical coordinates of the trail?','The Cryptobionic Family Friendly trail is located at a latitude of 37.1961 and a longitude of -113.235.','2025-03-27 22:54:56','2025-03-27 22:54:56'),(11240,'trails',108,'What is the name of the trail?','The trail is known as the Secret Trail.','2025-03-27 22:55:05','2025-03-27 22:55:05'),(11241,'trails',108,'What type of trail is the Secret Trail?','The Secret Trail is a point-to-point hike.','2025-03-27 22:55:05','2025-03-27 22:55:05'),(11242,'trails',108,'What is the total length of the Secret Trail?','The total distance of the Secret Trail is 6.6 miles.','2025-03-27 22:55:05','2025-03-27 22:55:05'),(11243,'trails',108,'What is the difficulty level of the hike?','The hike is classified as difficult.','2025-03-27 22:55:05','2025-03-27 22:55:05'),(11244,'trails',108,'What are the highest and lowest elevations on the trail?','The trail has the same elevation at both its highest and lowest points, which is 5090 feet.','2025-03-27 22:55:05','2025-03-27 22:55:05'),(11245,'trails',108,'What is the total incline and decline of the Secret Trail?','Hikers will experience a total incline of 786 feet and a decline of 907 feet along the trail.','2025-03-27 22:55:05','2025-03-27 22:55:05'),(11246,'trails',108,'What is the average grade of the Secret Trail?','The average grade of the trail is 0.05%.','2025-03-27 22:55:05','2025-03-27 22:55:05'),(11247,'trails',108,'What is the maximum grade encountered on the trail?','The maximum grade on the Secret Trail reaches up to 0.30%.','2025-03-27 22:55:05','2025-03-27 22:55:05'),(11248,'trails',108,'What scenic features can be found along the Secret Trail?','Hikers can enjoy stunning views of the mesa\'s edge while traversing the charming singletrack of slick rock and dirt.','2025-03-27 22:55:05','2025-03-27 22:55:05'),(11249,'trails',108,'What are the geographical coordinates of the trail?','The latitude and longitude of the Secret Trail are approximately 37.1293 and -113.198, respectively.','2025-03-27 22:55:05','2025-03-27 22:55:05'),(11250,'trails',109,'What is the North Point Loop hike like?','The North Point Loop offers a solid lollipop hike featuring enjoyable singletrack trails, some rougher sections, and breathtaking views of Gooseberry Mesa throughout the journey.','2025-03-27 22:55:13','2025-03-27 22:55:13'),(11251,'trails',109,'What level of difficulty can I expect on the North Point Loop?','This trail is considered difficult, with some challenging sections, though most of the hike has a manageable grade.','2025-03-27 22:55:13','2025-03-27 22:55:13'),(11252,'trails',109,'What are the elevations along the North Point Loop?','The elevation on the North Point Loop ranges from 5,369 feet at both its highest and lowest points, making for relatively consistent elevation without significant changes.','2025-03-27 22:55:13','2025-03-27 22:55:13'),(11253,'trails',109,'How long is the North Point Loop trail?','The North Point Loop stretches over a distance of approximately 4.1 miles.','2025-03-27 22:55:13','2025-03-27 22:55:13'),(11254,'trails',109,'What type of trail is the North Point Loop?','The North Point Loop is a point-to-point trail, allowing for a unique hiking experience.','2025-03-27 22:55:13','2025-03-27 22:55:13'),(11255,'trails',109,'Can I bring my dog on the North Point Loop trail?','Yes, dogs are welcome on this trail, and they can roam off-leash.','2025-03-27 22:55:13','2025-03-27 22:55:13'),(11256,'trails',109,'What types of trail surfaces can I expect?','The trail features a diverse array of surfaces, ranging from loose rock to solid sandstone slick rock, adding variety to your hiking experience.','2025-03-27 22:55:13','2025-03-27 22:55:13'),(11257,'trails',109,'Are there any spectacular views on the North Point Loop?','Absolutely! Hikers will be treated to magnificent vistas of Gooseberry Mesa at various points along the trail.','2025-03-27 22:55:13','2025-03-27 22:55:13'),(11258,'trails',109,'What should I keep in mind while hiking in this area?','Since the North Point Loop is popular with mountain bikers, it’s important to stay alert and be respectful of other trail users.','2025-03-27 22:55:13','2025-03-27 22:55:13'),(11259,'trails',109,'What are the incline and decline statistics for the North Point Loop?','The hike has an incline of 484 feet and a decline of 491 feet, contributing to the varied terrain.','2025-03-27 22:55:13','2025-03-27 22:55:13'),(11260,'trails',109,'What is the average and maximum grade of the North Point Loop?','The North Point Loop features an average grade of 0.04% and a maximum grade of 0.34%, making it accessible to many hikers despite its challenging sections.','2025-03-27 22:55:13','2025-03-27 22:55:13'),(11261,'trails',110,'What is the overall experience like on Goosebump trail?','Goosebump trail provides an exhilarating adventure as it meanders along the stunning contours of the mesa, featuring breathtaking vistas. The trail has a dynamic roller coaster feel with frequent short climbs and descents, making it an exciting journey.','2025-03-27 22:55:21','2025-03-27 22:55:21'),(11262,'trails',110,'What can I expect from the terrain on this trail?','The terrain on Goosebump varies, with sections that get rugged (Blue) and others that are smooth and enjoyable (Green). You’ll find a mix of short climbs and quick descents throughout the hike.','2025-03-27 22:55:21','2025-03-27 22:55:21'),(11263,'trails',110,'Where does Goosebump trail end?','The trail concludes at a junction with several jeep and ATV trails, marking the end of a thrilling hike.','2025-03-27 22:55:21','2025-03-27 22:55:21'),(11264,'trails',110,'What is the difficulty level of Goosebump trail?','The trail is rated as intermediate, making it suitable for those with some hiking experience.','2025-03-27 22:55:21','2025-03-27 22:55:21'),(11265,'trails',110,'What are the highest and lowest elevations on Goosebump trail?','The trail reaches a maximum elevation of 3,924 feet, which is also the lowest elevation, providing a generally level experience.','2025-03-27 22:55:21','2025-03-27 22:55:21'),(11266,'trails',110,'What is the total length of Goosebump trail?','Goosebump trail stretches for a total distance of 3.6 miles.','2025-03-27 22:55:21','2025-03-27 22:55:21'),(11267,'trails',110,'Is Goosebump a point-to-point trail?','Yes, Goosebump is classified as a point-to-point trail.','2025-03-27 22:55:21','2025-03-27 22:55:21'),(11268,'trails',110,'What is the elevation gain and drop on the Goosebump trail?','The trail features an elevation gain of 219 feet and a decline of 272 feet.','2025-03-27 22:55:21','2025-03-27 22:55:21'),(11269,'trails',110,'What are the average and maximum grades of the trail?','The average grade of Goosebump trail is approximately 0.03%, with a maximum grade reaching up to 0.14%.','2025-03-27 22:55:21','2025-03-27 22:55:21'),(11270,'trails',110,'What unique features does Goosebump trail offer?','One of the standout features of the Goosebump trail is its spectacular views along the way, enhancing the hiking experience.','2025-03-27 22:55:21','2025-03-27 22:55:21'),(11271,'trails',110,'Are dogs allowed on Goosebump trail?','It is currently unknown whether dogs are permitted on the Goosebump trail.','2025-03-27 22:55:21','2025-03-27 22:55:21'),(11272,'trails',110,'What are the geographical coordinates of Goosebump trail?','The trail is located at latitude 37.1519 and longitude -113.252.','2025-03-27 22:55:21','2025-03-27 22:55:21'),(11273,'trails',112,'What is the Goosebump Connector trail?','The Goosebump Connector is a scenic trail that links the Goosebump and Jems trails, offering stunning views of the beautiful landscapes of Utah and Arizona.','2025-03-27 22:55:26','2025-03-27 22:55:26'),(11274,'trails',112,'What is the difficulty level of the Goosebump Connector?','This trail is classified as intermediate, making it suitable for hikers with some experience.','2025-03-27 22:55:26','2025-03-27 22:55:26'),(11275,'trails',112,'What is the highest elevation on the Goosebump Connector?','The trail reaches a maximum elevation of 3,758 feet.','2025-03-27 22:55:26','2025-03-27 22:55:26'),(11276,'trails',112,'What is the lowest elevation on the Goosebump Connector?','The lowest elevation along the trail is also 3,758 feet, indicating it is a relatively level trek.','2025-03-27 22:55:26','2025-03-27 22:55:26'),(11277,'trails',112,'How long is the Goosebump Connector trail?','The trail spans 1.7 miles in length.','2025-03-27 22:55:26','2025-03-27 22:55:26'),(11278,'trails',112,'What type of trail is the Goosebump Connector?','It is a point-to-point trail, connecting two locations directly.','2025-03-27 22:55:26','2025-03-27 22:55:26'),(11279,'trails',112,'What is the total elevation decline on the Goosebump Connector?','Hikers will experience a descent of 196 feet along the trail.','2025-03-27 22:55:26','20