22:55:34'),(11289,'trails',115,'What is the average and maximum grade of the trail?','On average, the trail has a grade of 0.08%, with a maximum steepness reaching 0.39%.','2025-03-27 22:55:34','2025-03-27 22:55:34'),(11290,'trails',115,'What are the latitude and longitude coordinates for the trail?','The coordinates for the Three Falls Trail are approximately 37.1642° latitude and -113.287° longitude.','2025-03-27 22:55:34','2025-03-27 22:55:34'),(11291,'trails',116,'What is the Wire Mesa Loop trail like?','The Wire Mesa Loop offers a diverse range of terrain, making it stand out from other mesa trails. Hikers can enjoy breathtaking views of southern Utah and northern Arizona.','2025-03-27 22:55:41','2025-03-27 22:55:41'),(11292,'trails',116,'What level of difficulty is the Wire Mesa Loop?','This trail is categorized as intermediate, making it suitable for those who have some hiking experience.','2025-03-27 22:55:41','2025-03-27 22:55:41'),(11293,'trails',116,'What is the highest elevation on the Wire Mesa Loop?','The highest point on the trail reaches an elevation of 4,326 feet.','2025-03-27 22:55:41','2025-03-27 22:55:41'),(11294,'trails',116,'What is the lowest elevation on the Wire Mesa Loop?','Similar to its highest point, the lowest elevation on the Wire Mesa Loop is also 4,326 feet, offering a level trail experience throughout.','2025-03-27 22:55:41','2025-03-27 22:55:41'),(11295,'trails',116,'How long is the Wire Mesa Loop trail?','The total length of the Wire Mesa Loop is approximately 7.4 miles.','2025-03-27 22:55:41','2025-03-27 22:55:41'),(11296,'trails',116,'What type of trail is the Wire Mesa Loop?','The Wire Mesa Loop is a loop trail, allowing hikers to complete the circuit without retracing their steps.','2025-03-27 22:55:41','2025-03-27 22:55:41'),(11297,'trails',116,'What is the total incline and decline on the Wire Mesa Loop?','The trail features a total incline of 428 feet and a decline of 415 feet.','2025-03-27 22:55:41','2025-03-27 22:55:41'),