tures a total incline of 181 feet, which is manageable for most hikers.','2025-03-27 22:59:39','2025-03-27 22:59:39'),(11606,'trails',167,'What is the average grade of the trail?','The average grade of the Brooks Nature Trail is about 0.11%, providing a gentle walking experience.','2025-03-27 22:59:39','2025-03-27 22:59:39'),(11607,'trails',167,'What is the maximum grade on the trail?','The maximum grade on this trail reaches 0.20%, ensuring a comfortable hike.','2025-03-27 22:59:39','2025-03-27 22:59:39'),(11608,'trails',167,'What features can hikers expect on the trail?','Hikers will enjoy scenic views of a lake and the opportunity to observe local wildlife along the trail.','2025-03-27 22:59:39','2025-03-27 22:59:39'),(11609,'trails',167,'Are dogs allowed on the trail?','The policy regarding dogs on the Brooks Nature Trail is currently unknown.','2025-03-27 22:59:39','2025-03-27 22:59:39'),(11610,'trails',167,'What are the geographical coordinates of the trail?','The Brooks Nature Trail is located at a latitude of 37.1159 and a longitude of -113.583.','2025-03-27 22:59:39','2025-03-27 22:59:39'),(11611,'trails',168,'What type of trail is Mustang Pass?','Mustang Pass is a rocky singletrack trail that traverses through charred post-fire desert landscapes, providing hikers with stunning views of the rocky surroundings.','2025-03-27 22:59:50','2025-03-27 22:59:50'),(11612,'trails',168,'What is the difficulty level of the Mustang Pass trail?','The Mustang Pass trail is rated as intermediate to difficult, making it suitable for experienced hikers looking for a challenge.','2025-03-27 22:59:50','2025-03-27 22:59:50'),(11613,'trails',168,'What is the elevation range of Mustang Pass?','The trail reaches a maximum elevation of 3,198 feet, with the lowest elevation also at 3,198 feet, indicating a relatively flat terrain along its length.','2025-03-27 22:59:50','2025-03-27 22:59:50'),(11614,'trails',168,'How long is the Mustang Pass trail?','The total length of the Mustang Pass trail is 2.8 miles, perfect for a short but engaging hike.','2025-03-27 22:59:50','2025-03-27 22:59:50'),(11615,'trails',168,'What is the trail type for Mustang Pass?','Mustang Pass is a point-to-point trail, which means you will start at one endpoint and finish at another, rather than looping back.','2025-03-27 22:59:50','2025-03-27 22:59:50'),(11616,'trails',168,'What are the incline and decline statistics for Mustang Pass?','Hikers can expect an incline of 348 feet and a decline of 305 feet over the course of the trail, adding to the overall hiking experience.','2025-03-27 22:59:50','2025-03-27 22:59:50'),(11617,'trails',168,'What is the average and maximum grade of Mustang Pass?','The trail has an average grade of just 0.04% with the steepest point reaching a maximum grade of 0.09%, making it generally manageable.','2025-03-27 22:59:50','2025-03-27 22:59:50'),(11618,'trails',168,'Can you provide the geographic coordinates of Mustang Pass?','Mustang Pass is located at approximately 37.1665° latitude and -113.526° longitude, placing it in a scenic region ideal for hiking.','2025-03-27 22:59:50','2025-03-27 22:59:50'),(11619,'trails',169,'What is the overall experience of hiking through Church Rocks?','Church Rocks offers a delightful hiking experience characterized by mostly smooth rocky terrain, making for a fun and enjoyable outing.','2025-03-27 22:59:55','2025-03-27 22:59:55'),(11620,'trails',169,'What is the difficulty level of the Church Rocks trail?','The trail is classified as intermediate to difficult, catering to hikers with some experience.','2025-03-27 22:59:55','2025-03-27 22:59:55'),(11621,'trails',169,'What is the highest and lowest elevation on the Church Rocks trail?','The trail starts and finishes at an elevation of 3,212 feet, ensuring a relatively stable altitude throughout the hike.','2025-03-27 22:59:55','2025-03-27 22:59:55'),(11622,'trails',169,'How long is the Church Rocks trail?','The trail stretches for 2.3 miles, making it a manageable distance for a quick hike.','2025-03-27 22:59:55','2025-03-27 22:59:55'),(11623,'trails',169,'What type of trail is Church Rocks?','Church Rocks is a point-to-point trail, meaning you will start at one location and end at another.','2025-03-27 22:59:55','2025-03-27 22:59:55'),(11624,'trails',169,'What is the incline and decline on this trail?','Hikers will experience an incline of 211 feet and a decline of 227 feet while traversing the trail.','2025-03-27 22:59:55','2025-03-27 22:59:55'),(11625,'trails',169,'What is the average grade of the Church Rocks trail?','The average grade is quite gentle, at around 0.04%, making it accessible for most walkers.','2025-03-27 22:59:55','2025-03-27 22:59:55'),(11626,'trails',169,'What is the maximum grade of the trail?','The steepest section of the trail reaches a maximum grade of 0.11%, which is still relatively easy for most hikers.','2025-03-27 22:59:55','2025-03-27 22:59:55'),(11627,'trails',169,'What are the geographic coordinates of the Church Rocks trail?','The trail is located at approximately latitude 37.1614 and longitude -113.471.','2025-03-27 22:59:55','2025-03-27 22:59:55'),(11628,'trails',170,'What is the Bracken Connector trail like?','The Bracken Connector trail offers hikers stunning desert landscapes and remarkable views, showcasing the beauty of southern Utah and northern Arizona.','2025-03-27 23:00:05','2025-03-27 23:00:05'),(11629,'trails',170,'What is the difficulty level of the Bracken Connector trail?','The trail is rated as difficult, making it suitable for experienced hikers looking for a challenge.','2025-03-27 23:00:05','2025-03-27 23:00:05'),(11630,'trails',170,'What is the highest elevation on the Bracken Connector trail?','The highest point on the trail reaches an elevation of 3,215 feet.','2025-03-27 23:00:05','2025-03-27 23:00:05'),(11631,'trails',170,'What is the lowest elevation on the Bracken Connector trail?','The lowest elevation on the Bracken Connector trail also stands at 3,215 feet.','2025-03-27 23:00:05','2025-03-27 23:00:05'),(11632,'trails',170,'How long is the Bracken Connector trail?','The trail spans 0.4 miles, making it a short yet rewarding hike.','2025-03-27 23:00:05','2025-03-27 23:00:05'),(11633,'trails',170,'What type of trail is the Bracken Connector?','The Bracken Connector is a point-to-point trail, meaning hikers start and finish at different points.','2025-03-27 23:00:05','2025-03-27 23:00:05'),(11634,'trails',170,'What is the elevation gain on the Bracken Connector trail?','Hikers will encounter a total incline of 23 feet, along with a decline of 94 feet.','2025-03-27 23:00:05','2025-03-27 23:00:05'),(11635,'trails',170,'What are the average and maximum grades of the Bracken Connector trail?','The trail features an average grade of approximately 0.06% and a maximum grade of up to 0.12%.','2025-03-27 23:00:05','2025-03-27 23:00:05'),(11636,'trails',170,'What are the coordinates for the Bracken Connector trail?','The trail is located at latitude 37.1611 and longitude -113.476.','2025-03-27 23:00:05','2025-03-27 23:00:05'),(11637,'trails',171,'What is the nature of the terrain on the Spanish Wash trail?','Hikers should prepare for a challenging experience as the trail features deep sand, making it an unrunnable slog through an impressive desert landscape.','2025-03-27 23:00:12','2025-03-27 23:00:12'),(11638,'trails',171,'What is the difficulty level of the Spanish Wash trail?','The trail is rated as easy to intermediate, which makes it accessible for a range of hikers with varying levels of experience.','2025-03-27 23:00:12','2025-03-27 23:00:12'),(11639,'trails',171,'What are the elevation details of the Spanish Wash trail?','The trail has a consistent elevation, with both the highest and lowest points reaching 3,216 feet.','2025-03-27 23:00:12','2025-03-27 23:00:12'),(11640,'trails',171,'How long is the Spanish Wash trail?','The trail stretches for a total length of 0.6 miles, offering a manageable distance for hikers.','2025-03-27 23:00:12','2025-03-27 23:00:12'),(11641,'trails',171,'What type of trail is Spanish Wash?','Spanish Wash is a point-to-point trail, allowing hikers to start at one end and finish at the other.','2025-03-27 23:00:12','2025-03-27 23:00:12'),(11642,'trails',171,'What are the incline and decline statistics for this trail?','Hikers will encounter a slight incline of 14 feet and a decline of 76 feet along the way.','2025-03-27 23:00:12','2025-03-27 23:00:12'),(11643,'trails',171,'What is the average and maximum grade of the trail?','The average gradient of the trail is quite gentle at 0.03%, with a maximum grade of 0.11%, making it relatively easy to navigate.','2025-03-27 23:00:12','2025-03-27 23:00:12'),(11644,'trails',171,'What are the geographical coordinates for the Spanish Wash trail?','The trail is located at a latitude of 37.1786 and a longitude of -113.453, perfect for GPS navigation.','2025-03-27 23:00:12','2025-03-27 23:00:12'),(11645,'trails',172,'What is the starting point for the Historic Babylon Trail?','The trailhead for the Historic Babylon Trail is marked by an apparent gap in the cliffs where you can park. This area can accommodate about three to four vehicles.','2025-03-27 23:00:23','2025-03-27 23:00:23'),(11646,'trails',172,'Are there any notable sights near the trailhead?','Yes, just before you exit the gap in the cliffs, look to your left to discover some intriguing petroglyphs.','2025-03-27 23:00:23','2025-03-27 23:00:23'),(11647,'trails',172,'What type of terrain can I expect on the Historic Babylon Trail?','The trail traverses through a diverse terrain; it initially follows a dry wash and then ascends steeply through thick vegetation. Be prepared for sections where the trail might be tricky to follow.','2025-03-27 23:00:23','2025-03-27 23:00:23'),(11648,'trails',172,'How should I navigate the trail?','Keep an eye out for small cairns along the route as they will help guide you through the sections where the trail is not clearly defined.','2025-03-27 23:00:23','2025-03-27 23:00:23'),(11649,'trails',172,'What is the elevation change on the trail?','You will encounter a total incline of 855 feet, and the trail reaches its highest point at an elevation of 2907 feet.','2025-03-27 23:00:23','2025-03-27 23:00:23'),(11650,'trails',172,'What can I expect at the 2.5-mile mark?','At about 2.5 miles into your hike, you\'ll come across a barbed wire fence. Here, you will need to make a sharp left turn as the trail continues to ascend.','2025-03-27 23:00:23','2025-03-27 23:00:23'),(11651,'trails',172,'What follows the Historic Babylon Trail?','The trail transitions into the Little Purgatory Trail after you navigate the barbed wire fence. This open desert trail is characterized by its lack of shade and features more petroglyphs.','2025-03-27 23:00:23','2025-03-27 23:00:23'),(11652,'trails',172,'What is the difficulty level of the Historic Babylon Trail?','The trail is classified as difficult, so be prepared for a challenging hike.','2025-03-27 23:00:23','2025-03-27 23:00:23'),(11653,'trails',172,'What are the total distances and elevations for the trail?','The Historic Babylon Trail spans approximately 3.0 miles, maintaining an elevation range of 2907 feet throughout.','2025-03-27 23:00:23','2025-03-27 23:00:23'),(11654,'trails',172,'Are dogs allowed on the trail?','It is currently unknown whether dogs are permitted on the Historic Babylon Trail.','2025-03-27 23:00:23','2025-03-27 23:00:23'),(11655,'trails',172,'What features can I enjoy while hiking?','As you hike, you\'ll enjoy scenic views along with fascinating petroglyphs, particularly at the beginning of the Little Purgatory Trail.','2025-03-27 23:00:23','2025-03-27 23:00:23'),(11656,'trails',173,'When is the best time to hike the Little Purgatory Trail?','For the best experience, it\'s recommended to hike the Little Purgatory Trail early in the morning to enjoy full sunlight and avoid afternoon heat.','2025-03-27 23:00:35','2025-03-27 23:00:35'),(11657,'trails',173,'What type of views can I expect on the Little Purgatory Trail?','As you hike, you\'ll be treated to stunning views of Sandstone Mountain and the striking Red Cliffs that characterize the open desert landscape.','2025-03-27 23:00:35','2025-03-27 23:00:35'),(11658,'trails',173,'How difficult is the Little Purgatory Trail?','The Little Purgatory Trail is considered difficult, making it suitable for experienced hikers who are prepared for a challenging hike.','2025-03-27 23:00:35','2025-03-27 23:00:35'),(11659,'trails',173,'What is the elevation change on the Little Purgatory Trail?','The trail has a significant incline of 867 feet, with a maximum elevation of 2,963 feet, contributing to its challenging nature.','2025-03-27 23:00:35','2025-03-27 23:00:35'),(11660,'trails',173,'How long is the Little Purgatory Trail?','The trail spans 2.8 miles and follows a point-to-point route.','2025-03-27 23:00:35','2025-03-27 23:00:35'),(11661,'trails',173,'What is the average and maximum grade of the trail?','The average grade of the Little Purgatory Trail is about 0.07%, while the maximum grade reaches up to 0.16%, indicating some steep sections.','2025-03-27 23:00:35','2025-03-27 23:00:35'),(11662,'trails',173,'Are dogs allowed on the Little Purgatory Trail?','It is currently unclear whether dogs are permitted on the Little Purgatory Trail, so checking local regulations before bringing your pet is advisable.','2025-03-27 23:00:35','2025-03-27 23:00:35'),(11663,'trails',173,'What are the geographical coordinates for the Little Purgatory Trail?','The trail is located at approximately latitude 37.2055 and longitude -113.349.','2025-03-27 23:00:35','2025-03-27 23:00:35'),(11664,'trails',173,'What features can I enjoy while hiking the Little Purgatory Trail?','In addition to compelling views along the way, the trail stands out for its dramatic desert landscape, making it an attractive hike for nature enthusiasts.','2025-03-27 23:00:35','2025-03-27 23:00:35'),(11665,'trails',174,'What can I expect to see on The Vortex trail?','Hikers can look forward to breathtaking views of Dammeron Valley and Pine Mountain while traversing through stunning red rock scenery.','2025-03-27 23:00:42','2025-03-27 23:00:42'),(11666,'trails',174,'What is the difficulty level of The Vortex trail?','The Vortex trail is rated as difficult, making it suitable for experienced hikers.','2025-03-27 23:00:42','2025-03-27 23:00:42'),(11667,'trails',174,'What is the length of The Vortex trail?','The trail spans approximately 1.1 miles and follows a point-to-point layout.','2025-03-27 23:00:42','2025-03-27 23:00:42'),(11668,'trails',174,'What elevations can I expect on The Vortex trail?','The trail has a highest elevation of 4018 feet and maintains this elevation throughout, as its lowest elevation is also 4018 feet.','2025-03-27 23:00:42','2025-03-27 23:00:42'),(11669,'trails',174,'What are the incline and decline details for The Vortex trail?','Hikers will experience an incline of 399 feet and a decline of 101 feet along the trail.','2025-03-27 23:00:42','2025-03-27 23:00:42'),(11670,'trails',174,'What is the average and maximum grade of The Vortex trail?','The average grade is about 0.09%, with a maximum grade reaching up to 0.24%.','2025-03-27 23:00:42','2025-03-27 23:00:42'),(11671,'trails',174,'Are dogs allowed on The Vortex trail?','Yes, dogs are welcome on the trail but must be kept on a leash.','2025-03-27 23:00:43','2025-03-27 23:00:43'),(11672,'trails',174,'Is there anything to be cautious about while hiking The Vortex trail?','Hikers should be mindful of muddy sections on the gravel road, especially following rainfall, as these areas can become slippery.','2025-03-27 23:00:43','2025-03-27 23:00:43'),(11673,'trails',174,'What are the coordinates for The Vortex trail?','The trail is located at a latitude of 37.28 and a longitude of -113.739.','2025-03-27 23:00:43','2025-03-27 23:00:43'),(11674,'trails',175,'Where does the Chinle Trail start?','The Chinle Trail begins at the Anasazi Way sub-division.','2025-03-27 23:00:54','2025-03-27 23:00:54'),(11675,'trails',175,'What scenery can I expect on the Chinle Trail?','Hikers can enjoy stunning views of impressive cliffs such as West Temple and Mount Kinesava as they traverse the open desert landscape.','2025-03-27 23:00:54','2025-03-27 23:00:54'),(11676,'trails',175,'What unique geological features will I encounter on the trail?','Along the Chinle Trail, you’ll find areas rich in petrified wood and notable cryptobiotic soil, showcasing the fascinating geology of the region.','2025-03-27 23:00:54','2025-03-27 23:00:54'),(11677,'trails',175,'What is the best time of year to hike the Chinle Trail?','The trail is most enjoyable during the cooler spring and fall months, as it can become very hot in the summer.','2025-03-27 23:00:54','2025-03-27 23:00:54'),(11678,'trails',175,'Is there a well-defined path throughout Coalpits Wash?','While there\'s no officially developed trail in Coalpits Wash, there is a well-trodden path that is easy to follow toward the junction with Scoggins Wash.','2025-03-27 23:00:54','2025-03-27 23:00:54'),(11679,'trails',175,'What should I do at the junction of Scoggins Wash?','At the Scoggins Wash junction, make a left turn to ascend toward the narrows and scenic pools, which are located among large boulders and small waterfalls.','2025-03-27 23:00:54','2025-03-27 23:00:54'),(11680,'trails',175,'What is the overall difficulty level of the Chinle Trail?','The trail is classified as intermediate to difficult, making it suitable for those with some hiking experience.','2025-03-27 23:00:54','2025-03-27 23:00:54'),(11681,'trails',175,'What are the elevation details of the Chinle Trail?','The highest point on the trail reaches 3,810 feet and it starts and ends at the same elevation.','2025-03-27 23:00:55','2025-03-27 23:00:55'),(11682,'trails',175,'How long is the Chinle Trail?','The full length of the Chinle Trail is approximately 8.1 miles and operates as a point-to-point trail.','2025-03-27 23:00:55','2025-03-27 23:00:55'),(11683,'trails',175,'What is the elevation gain and loss on the Chinle Trail?','Hikers will experience an incline of 875 feet and a decline of 576 feet during their trek.','2025-03-27 23:00:55','2025-03-27 23:00:55'),(11684,'trails',175,'What amenities and features should I expect along the trail?','Expect to see several beautiful features, including opportunities for birdwatching, stunning fall colors, and encounters with creek environments, plus a variety of wildlife and wildflowers.','2025-03-27 23:00:55','2025-03-27 23:00:55'),(11685,'trails',175,'Are dogs allowed on the Chinle Trail?','Unfortunately, dogs are not permitted on this trail.','2025-03-27 23:00:55','2025-03-27 23:00:55'),(11686,'trails',175,'What are the geographic coordinates of the Chinle Trail?','The Chinle Trail is located at a latitude of 37.1613 and a longitude of -113.019.','2025-03-27 23:00:55','2025-03-27 23:00:55'),(11687,'trails',176,'What are the highlights of the Eagle Crags Trail?','The Eagle Crags Trail offers spectacular views of Zion National Park and the surrounding canyons, making it perfect for those seeking a short yet breathtaking hiking experience.','2025-03-27 23:01:04','2025-03-27 23:01:04'),(11688,'trails',176,'How accessible is the access road to the trailhead?','The road leading to the trailhead is quite rugged, but vehicles that are not all-wheel drive or four-wheel drive can make it to the top. However, exercise caution if choosing to drive a car without 4WD. It\'s important to note that although there may be signs from homeowners dissuading access, the road is managed by the Bureau of Land Management (BLM) and is fully legal to use.','2025-03-27 23:01:04','2025-03-27 23:01:04'),(11689,'trails',176,'Is camping allowed along the Eagle Crags Trail?','Yes, there are fantastic dispersed camping options available at the top of the trail, providing you with a great opportunity to immerse yourself in the stunning scenery.','2025-03-27 23:01:04','2025-03-27 23:01:04'),(11690,'trails',176,'What is the difficulty level of the Eagle Crags Trail?','The trail is considered to be of intermediate to difficult difficulty, offering a good challenge for more experienced hikers.','2025-03-27 23:01:04','2025-03-27 23:01:04'),(11691,'trails',176,'What is the elevation range on the trail?','The Eagle Crags Trail maintains a constant elevation of 4259 feet, making it a straightforward trek with a total incline of 1046 feet and a decline of 164 feet.','2025-03-27 23:01:04','2025-03-27 23:01:04'),(11692,'trails',176,'How long is the Eagle Crags Trail?','The trail stretches for 2.9 miles, offering a point-to-point hiking experience that can be completed in a reasonable time.','2025-03-27 23:01:04','2025-03-27 23:01:04'),(11693,'trails',176,'What are the grade statistics for the trail?','The average grade of the trail is relatively mild at 0.08%, with a maximum grade reaching up to 0.28%, ensuring a manageable hike for most.','2025-03-27 23:01:04','2025-03-27 23:01:04'),(11694,'trails',176,'Can I bring my dog on the Eagle Crags Trail?','Yes, dogs are allowed on the trail, provided they are kept on a leash to ensure the safety of fellow hikers and the environment.','2025-03-27 23:01:04','2025-03-27 23:01:04'),(11695,'trails',176,'What are the geographical coordinates of the Eagle Crags Trail?','The Eagle Crags Trail is located at a latitude of 37.1474 and a longitude of -113.031, which you can use for navigation.','2025-03-27 23:01:04','2025-03-27 23:01:04'),(11696,'trails',177,'What is the overall experience like on the Barrel Roll trail?','Hikers can expect a pleasant outing on the Barrel Roll trail, featuring rolling hills and breathtaking views of Santa Clara, St. George, and the surrounding mountains, including Red Mountain and the Pine Valley Mountains.','2025-03-27 23:01:11','2025-03-27 23:01:11'),(11697,'trails',177,'What are the highlights of the scenery along the Barrel Roll trail?','Along the Barrel Roll trail, you\'ll enjoy stunning vistas of the Santa Clara River corridor and the striking desert mesas of the Santa Clara River Reserve, making it a visually rewarding hike.','2025-03-27 23:01:11','2025-03-27 23:01:11'),(11698,'trails',177,'How challenging is the Barrel Roll trail?','The Barrel Roll trail is classified as intermediate in difficulty. It features some elevation gain but maintains a manageable grade, making it accessible for many hikers.','2025-03-27 23:01:11','2025-03-27 23:01:11'),(11699,'trails',177,'What is the total distance of the Barrel Roll trail?','The Barrel Roll trail stretches for 5.8 miles, offering a fulfilling experience for hikers looking to explore the area.','2025-03-27 23:01:11','2025-03-27 23:01:11'),(11700,'trails',177,'What is the elevation range of the Barrel Roll trail?','The trail has a steady elevation of 3,156 feet, with an elevation gain of 523 feet and a decline of 506 feet, providing a gentle incline throughout the hike.','2025-03-27 23:01:11','2025-03-27 23:01:11'),(11701,'trails',177,'Can the Barrel Roll trail be hiked in different directions?','Yes, the Barrel Roll trail is a loop that can be traversed in either a clockwise or counter-clockwise direction, giving hikers flexibility in their experience.','2025-03-27 23:01:11','2025-03-27 23:01:11'),(11702,'trails',177,'What types of features can be seen on the Barrel Roll trail?','Hikers can enjoy the scenic views along the trail, which may also feature local wildflowers during the appropriate seasons.','2025-03-27 23:01:11','2025-03-27 23:01:11'),(11703,'trails',177,'Are dogs allowed on the Barrel Roll trail?','The policy regarding dogs on the Barrel Roll trail is currently unknown, so it is advisable to check local regulations before bringing your furry friend.','2025-03-27 23:01:11','2025-03-27 23:01:11'),(11704,'trails',177,'Where is the Barrel Roll trail located?','The Barrel Roll trail is located at a latitude of 37.121 and a longitude of -113.676, conveniently close to the communities of Santa Clara and Ivins.','2025-03-27 23:01:11','2025-03-27 23:01:11'),(11705,'trails',178,'What kind of views can I expect on the Sidewinder trail?','Hiking the Sidewinder trail offers breathtaking views along a narrow mesa, allowing you to soak in stunning vistas as you navigate its winding path.','2025-03-27 23:01:21','2025-03-27 23:01:21'),(11706,'trails',178,'What is the difficulty level of the Sidewinder trail?','The Sidewinder trail is categorized as intermediate, making it suitable for those with some hiking experience.','2025-03-27 23:01:21','2025-03-27 23:01:21'),(11707,'trails',178,'What is the total length of the Sidewinder trail?','The length of the Sidewinder trail is 1.7 miles, providing a concise yet rewarding hiking experience.','2025-03-27 23:01:21','2025-03-27 23:01:21'),(11708,'trails',178,'What are the elevation details for the Sidewinder trail?','On the Sidewinder trail, you will experience a highest elevation of 3,291 feet, while the lowest elevation remains at the same level, making it a relatively flat hike overall.','2025-03-27 23:01:21','2025-03-27 23:01:21'),(11709,'trails',178,'How much elevation gain can I expect on the Sidewinder trail?','Hikers will experience a total incline of 372 feet along the trail, with a small decline of 44 feet.','2025-03-27 23:01:22','2025-03-27 23:01:22'),(11710,'trails',178,'What is the trail type of the Sidewinder trail?','The Sidewinder trail is a point-to-point trail, so plan your transportation accordingly for a one-way hike.','2025-03-27 23:01:22','2025-03-27 23:01:22'),(11711,'trails',178,'What is the average and maximum grade of the Sidewinder trail?','The trail boasts an average grade of 0.05%, with a maximum grade of 0.09%, making it manageable for most hikers.','2025-03-27 23:01:22','2025-03-27 23:01:22'),(11712,'trails',178,'What are the geographical coordinates of the Sidewinder trail?','The geographical coordinates for the Sidewinder trail are approximately 37.1233° latitude and -113.686° longitude.','2025-03-27 23:01:22','2025-03-27 23:01:22'),(11713,'trails',179,'What can I expect to see on the Precipice Trail?','Hikers will enjoy breathtaking views and diverse terrain as the trail navigates through stunning desert landscapes, presenting awe-inspiring vistas and moments of exposure.','2025-03-27 23:01:34','2025-03-27 23:01:34'),(11714,'trails',179,'Where does the Precipice Trail start?','The trail begins approximately 50 feet from the trailhead, branching off from the Barrel Roll Trail to the left.','2025-03-27 23:01:34','2025-03-27 23:01:34'),(11715,'trails',179,'Does the Precipice Trail connect to other trails?','Yes, the Precipice Trail connects to the Sidewinder Trail, offering an alternative route for navigating the lower section of the Barrel Roll Trail.','2025-03-27 23:01:34','2025-03-27 23:01:34'),(11716,'trails',179,'How does the terrain on Precipice Trail differ from Barrel Roll?','Although it runs just below Barrel Roll, the Precipice Trail features distinct terrain, unique plant life, and different viewpoints, making it a unique experience.','2025-03-27 23:01:34','2025-03-27 23:01:34'),(11717,'trails',179,'Why is it called the Precipice Trail?','The name \'Precipice\' comes from a section of the trail where massive rock slabs create a tight squeeze, pinching the path against a lower cliff edge, providing both excitement and exposure.','2025-03-27 23:01:34','2025-03-27 23:01:34'),(11718,'trails',179,'What is the difficulty level of the Precipice Trail?','The trail is categorized as intermediate in difficulty, suitable for those with some hiking experience.','2025-03-27 23:01:34','2025-03-27 23:01:34'),(11719,'trails',179,'What are the elevation details for the Precipice Trail?','The highest point along the trail reaches 3,146 feet, and it starts and ends at the same elevation, making it a relatively flat hike overall.','2025-03-27 23:01:34','2025-03-27 23:01:34'),(11720,'trails',179,'How long is the Precipice Trail?','The trail stretches for a total of 0.9 miles, making it a short yet rewarding hike.','2025-03-27 23:01:34','2025-03-27 23:01:34'),(11721,'trails',179,'What type of trail is the Precipice Trail?','Precipice Trail is a point-to-point trail, providing a direct route from start to finish.','2025-03-27 23:01:34','2025-03-27 23:01:34'),(11722,'trails',179,'What is the incline and decline on the Precipice Trail?','The trail features an incline of 147 feet, with a minimal decline of just 2 feet.','2025-03-27 23:01:34','2025-03-27 23:01:34'),(11723,'trails',179,'What are the grade details for the Precipice Trail?','The average grade is a gentle 0.03%, while the maximum grade reaches up to 0.14%, making it manageable for intermediate hikers.','2025-03-27 23:01:34','2025-03-27 23:01:34'),(11724,'trails',179,'What features should I be aware of on the trail?','Hikers can look forward to remarkable views throughout the trail, which is one of its highlights.','2025-03-27 23:01:34','2025-03-27 23:01:34'),(11725,'trails',179,'Are dogs allowed on the Precipice Trail?','Information regarding dog access on the Precipice Trail is currently unknown.','2025-03-27 23:01:34','2025-03-27 23:01:34'),(11726,'trails',179,'What are the latitude and longitude coordinates for the Precipice Trail?','The trail is located at latitude 37.1211 and longitude -113.675.','2025-03-27 23:01:34','2025-03-27 23:01:34'),(11727,'trails',180,'What is the name of the trail?','The trail is known as the Suicidal Tendencies trail.','2025-03-27 23:01:45','2025-03-27 23:01:45'),(11728,'trails',180,'What type of terrain can I expect on this trail?','Hikers will encounter steep switchbacks and exposed sections, especially during the initial descent from Sidewinder Mesa.','2025-03-27 23:01:45','2025-03-27 23:01:45'),(11729,'trails',180,'How long is the round trip from the Cove Wash Trailhead?','The total distance for the round trip is approximately 13.2 miles.','2025-03-27 23:01:45','2025-03-27 23:01:45'),(11730,'trails',180,'What is the highest and lowest elevation on the trail?','The trail reaches a highest elevation of 3,433 feet, with the lowest point also at 3,433 feet.','2025-03-27 23:01:45','2025-03-27 23:01:45'),(11731,'trails',180,'What is the difficulty level of the Suicidal Tendencies trail?','This trail is rated as difficult due to its steep and technical sections.','2025-03-27 23:01:45','2025-03-27 23:01:45'),(11732,'trails',180,'What features can I expect to see along the trail?','Hikers are rewarded with stunning views of the Beaver Dam Mountains and the unique rock formations like Hangover and Thread the Needle.','2025-03-27 23:01:45','2025-03-27 23:01:45'),(11733,'trails',180,'Are dogs allowed on this trail?','It is currently unclear if dogs are permitted on this trail.','2025-03-27 23:01:45','2025-03-27 23:01:45'),(11734,'trails',180,'What should I be mindful of while hiking?','Be aware of other trail users and keep an eye out for desert wildlife during your hike.','2025-03-27 23:01:45','2025-03-27 23:01:45'),(11735,'trails',180,'How does the trail change as I progress?','After the challenging sections, the trail becomes less technical with gentle switchbacks as you reach the top of the mesa.','2025-03-27 23:01:45','2025-03-27 23:01:45'),(11736,'trails',180,'What important waypoints should I know?','Key landmarks include the steep descent at Sidewinder Mesa, the Hangover rock formation, and the challenging area known as Thread the Needle.','2025-03-27 23:01:45','2025-03-27 23:01:45'),(11737,'trails',180,'What direction does the trail run?','The Suicidal Tendencies trail is a point-to-point trail, requiring a return hike along the same path after reaching the top.','2025-03-27 23:01:45','2025-03-27 23:01:45'),(11738,'trails',180,'What are the incline and decline statistics?','The trail features an incline of 645 feet and a decline of 553 feet.','2025-03-27 23:01:45','2025-03-27 23:01:45'),(11739,'trails',180,'What is the latitude and longitude of the trail?','The trail is located at a latitude of 37.1218 and a longitude of -113.698.','2025-03-27 23:01:45','2025-03-27 23:01:45'),(11740,'trails',181,'What is the Pushing Tin Loop trail like?','The Pushing Tin Loop is a fun and easy multi-use singletrack trail that offers beautiful morning views and is relatively clean with low foot traffic.','2025-03-27 23:01:56','2025-03-27 23:01:56'),(11741,'trails',181,'How long is the Pushing Tin Loop?','The total length of the trail is 2.7 miles, making it a convenient option for a short hike.','2025-03-27 23:01:56','2025-03-27 23:01:56'),(11742,'trails',181,'What is the elevation range of the trail?','The trail maintains a consistent elevation of 2721 feet, with both the highest and lowest points at this altitude.','2025-03-27 23:01:56','2025-03-27 23:01:56'),(11743,'trails',181,'What are the key features along the trail?','Hikers can enjoy scenic views, and there’s the opportunity to spot airplanes above. A notable landmark is Will Gilbert Point, which has a sign and a folding bench-table offering a great resting spot.','2025-03-27 23:01:56','2025-03-27 23:01:56'),(11744,'trails',181,'How does the trail differ at the beginning?','The first quarter-mile is a doubletrack that runs alongside a sandy wash before leading into the singletrack portion of the loop.','2025-03-27 23:01:56','2025-03-27 23:01:56'),(11745,'trails',181,'Are there any tricky parts on the trail?','Yes, there are two potentially confusing areas if you hike counter-clockwise. The first is a small switchback with a misleading turn at 0.6 miles, and the second is a fork at 1.25 miles where you can choose between an alternate technical line or an easier route.','2025-03-27 23:01:56','2025-03-27 23:01:56'),(11746,'trails',181,'What is the difficulty level of the trail?','The Pushing Tin Loop has an intermediate difficulty level, suitable for those looking for a bit of a challenge without being too strenuous.','2025-03-27 23:01:56','2025-03-27 23:01:56'),(11747,'trails',181,'Is this trail dog-friendly?','Yes, dogs are allowed on the trail and can be off-leash, making it a great outing for pet owners.','2025-03-27 23:01:56','2025-03-27 23:01:56'),(11748,'trails',181,'How can I access the trail?','You can access the Pushing Tin Loop from the main parking lot at the trailhead, or via the Meditation Rock Connector or Saddle Trail Connector.','2025-03-27 23:01:56','2025-03-27 23:01:56'),(11749,'trails',181,'What kind of terrain should I expect on the trail?','The trail has a gentle incline and decline of about 165 feet, with an average grade of 0.02% and a maximum grade of 0.07%, making it mainly flat and manageable.','2025-03-27 23:01:56','2025-03-27 23:01:56'),(11750,'trails',181,'What can I do at Will Gilbert Point?','At Will Gilbert Point, you can take a break and enjoy the views while using the folding bench-table, perfect for snacking or resting.','2025-03-27 23:01:56','2025-03-27 23:01:56'),(11751,'trails',182,'What is the overall experience of the Kentucky Lucky Chicken Trail?','The Kentucky Lucky Chicken Trail offers a short but technically challenging loop, highlighted by breathtaking views of the surrounding landscape.','2025-03-27 23:02:03','2025-03-27 23:02:03'),(11752,'trails',182,'What is the difficulty level of the trail?','This trail is rated as intermediate to difficult, making it suitable for hikers with some experience.','2025-03-27 23:02:03','2025-03-27 23:02:03'),(11753,'trails',182,'What are the elevation details of the trail?','The trail has a consistent elevation, with both the highest and lowest points reaching 2790 feet.','2025-03-27 23:02:03','2025-03-27 23:02:03'),(11754,'trails',182,'How long is the Kentucky Lucky Chicken Trail?','The total length of the trail is 3.9 miles, making it a manageable hike for those looking for a quick adventure.','2025-03-27 23:02:03','2025-03-27 23:02:03'),(11755,'trails',182,'Is the trail a loop?','Yes, the Kentucky Lucky Chicken Trail is a loop trail, allowing hikers to complete the circuit and return to the starting point.','2025-03-27 23:02:03','2025-03-27 23:02:03'),(11756,'trails',182,'What are the incline and decline metrics of the trail?','Hikers will experience a total incline of 404 feet and a decline of 411 feet throughout the loop.','2025-03-27 23:02:03','2025-03-27 23:02:03'),(11757,'trails',182,'What is the average grade of the trail?','The average grade of the trail is about 0.04%, providing a relatively gentle hiking experience.','2025-03-27 23:02:03','2025-03-27 23:02:03'),(11758,'trails',182,'What is the maximum grade encountered on the trail?','The maximum grade on the Kentucky Lucky Chicken Trail can reach up to 0.12%, which adds some challenge to the trek.','2025-03-27 23:02:03','2025-03-27 23:02:03'),(11759,'trails',182,'What are the geographical coordinates of the trail?','The trail is situated at approximately 37.0658 latitude and -113.566 longitude, placing it in a beautiful natural setting.','2025-03-27 23:02:03','2025-03-27 23:02:03'),(11760,'trails',183,'What is the name of the trail and its location?','The trail is called Rim Rock Trail, and it starts at the Sand Cove Trailhead.','2025-03-27 23:02:10','2025-03-27 23:02:10'),(11761,'trails',183,'What is the trail type?','The Rim Rock Trail is a point-to-point trail.','2025-03-27 23:02:10','2025-03-27 23:02:10'),(11762,'trails',183,'How long is the Rim Rock Trail?','The trail spans a distance of 3.2 miles.','2025-03-27 23:02:10','2025-03-27 23:02:10'),(11763,'trails',183,'What is the difficulty level of the trail?','This trail is classified as difficult.','2025-03-27 23:02:10','2025-03-27 23:02:10'),(11764,'trails',183,'What are the highest and lowest elevations on the trail?','The trail has a highest elevation of 3044 feet, and the lowest elevation is also 3044 feet.','2025-03-27 23:02:10','2025-03-27 23:02:10'),(11765,'trails',183,'What is the total incline and decline on the trail?','Hikers will experience a total incline of 425 feet and a decline of 217 feet.','2025-03-27 23:02:10','2025-03-27 23:02:10'),(11766,'trails',183,'What are the average and maximum grades of the trail?','The average grade is approximately 0.04%, while the maximum grade reaches up to 0.09%.','2025-03-27 23:02:10','2025-03-27 23:02:10'),(11767,'trails',183,'What geographical coordinates can I use to locate the trail?','The trail is located at a latitude of 37.1207 and a longitude of -113.675.','2025-03-27 23:02:10','2025-03-27 23:02:10'),(11768,'trails',183,'What scenic features can hikers expect to see on the trail?','Hikers can anticipate breathtaking rock formations that add to the appeal of the Rim Rock Trail.','2025-03-27 23:02:10','2025-03-27 23:02:10'),(11769,'trails',184,'What is the additional loop to the Rim Reaper like?','The side loop to Rim Reaper offers an exciting extension, featuring more singletrack that allows hikers to enjoy stunning views of the expansive rim.','2025-03-27 23:02:16','2025-03-27 23:02:16'),(11770,'trails',184,'What is the difficulty level of the side loop?','This side loop is categorized as difficult, so be prepared for a challenging hike!','2025-03-27 23:02:16','2025-03-27 23:02:16'),(11771,'trails',184,'What is the highest and lowest elevation of the side loop?','The side loop maintains a constant elevation of 3245 feet, providing a steady hiking experience.','2025-03-27 23:02:16','2025-03-27 23:02:16'),(11772,'trails',184,'How long is the side loop?','The side loop measures 0.8 miles, making it a great addition to your hike on the Rim Reaper.','2025-03-27 23:02:16','2025-03-27 23:02:16'),(11773,'trails',184,'What type of trail is the side loop?','This side trail is a point-to-point route, allowing for a straightforward hike that can easily be integrated into your current trek.','2025-03-27 23:02:16','2025-03-27 23:02:16'),(11774,'trails',184,'What are the incline and decline stats for the side loop?','Hikers will experience an incline of 82 feet and a decline of 26 feet, allowing for a bit of elevation change as you navigate the loop.','2025-03-27 23:02:16','2025-03-27 23:02:16'),(11775,'trails',184,'What is the average and maximum grade of the side loop?','The average grade is quite gentle at 0.03%, but it can peak at a maximum grade of 0.09%, adding a bit of challenge to the experience.','2025-03-27 23:02:16','2025-03-27 23:02:16'),(11776,'trails',184,'What are the geographic coordinates of the side loop?','You can find this side loop at latitude 37.1173 and longitude -113.679, right off the main Rim Reaper trail.','2025-03-27 23:02:16','2025-03-27 23:02:16'),(11777,'trails',185,'What is the starting point of the Rim Runner Trail?','The Rim Runner Trail begins from the Rim Rock Trail, where hikers will encounter a split after 1.6 miles.','2025-03-27 23:02:25','2025-03-27 23:02:25'),(11778,'trails',185,'What can hikers expect when combining the Rim Runner Trail with the Rim Rock Trail?','By merging these trails, hikers can enjoy additional singletrack paths along with breathtaking views on solid sandy soil adorned with large rounded rocks.','2025-03-27 23:02:25','2025-03-27 23:02:25'),(11779,'trails',185,'Is there a side loop on the Rim Runner Trail?','Yes, there is a charming side loop that offers stunning vistas in every direction.','2025-03-27 23:02:25','2025-03-27 23:02:25'),(11780,'trails',185,'What is the difficulty level of the Rim Runner Trail?','The trail is classified as difficult.','2025-03-27 23:02:25','2025-03-27 23:02:25'),(11781,'trails',185,'What are the elevation details for the Rim Runner Trail?','The highest and lowest elevation along the trail is 3394 feet.','2025-03-27 23:02:25','2025-03-27 23:02:25'),(11782,'trails',185,'How long is the Rim Runner Trail?','The trail measures approximately 0.7 miles in length.','2025-03-27 23:02:25','2025-03-27 23:02:25'),(11783,'trails',185,'What type of trail is the Rim Runner Trail?','The Rim Runner Trail is a loop trail.','2025-03-27 23:02:25','2025-03-27 23:02:25'),(11784,'trails',185,'What is the incline and decline like on the Rim Runner Trail?','The trail features an incline of 54 feet and a decline of 39 feet.','2025-03-27 23:02:25','2025-03-27 23:02:25'),(11785,'trails',185,'What is the average and maximum grade of the Rim Runner Trail?','The average grade is about 0.03%, with a maximum grade reaching 0.07%.','2025-03-27 23:02:25','2025-03-27 23:02:25'),(11786,'trails',185,'What features can hikers expect along the Rim Runner Trail?','Hikers can look forward to impressive views along the trail.','2025-03-27 23:02:25','2025-03-27 23:02:25'),(11787,'trails',185,'Are dogs allowed on the Rim Runner Trail?','The information regarding dogs on the trail is currently unknown.','2025-03-27 23:02:25','2025-03-27 23:02:25'),(11788,'trails',185,'What are the geographic coordinates of the Rim Runner Trail?','The trail is located at a latitude of 37.1138 and a longitude of -113.685.','2025-03-27 23:02:25','2025-03-27 23:02:25'),(11789,'trails',186,'What is the length of the Temple Quarry Trail?','The Temple Quarry Trail stretches for 2.5 miles.','2025-03-27 23:02:34','2025-03-27 23:02:34'),(11790,'trails',186,'Where is the Temple Quarry Trail located?','This trail is conveniently situated in the heart of St. George.','2025-03-27 23:02:34','2025-03-27 23:02:34'),(11791,'trails',186,'What kind of views can hikers expect from the trail?','Hikers will be treated to stunning birds-eye views of St. George along the trail.','2025-03-27 23:02:34','2025-03-27 23:02:34'),(11792,'trails',186,'What is the historical significance of the Temple Quarry Trail?','The trail was historically used by Mormon Pioneers between 1871 and 1874 to access a quarry for rocks needed in building the St. George Temple.','2025-03-27 23:02:34','2025-03-27 23:02:34'),(11793,'trails',186,'What type of rock was quarried from the site?','The site contains a large deposit of lava rocks, which are naturally resistant to the area\'s alkaline soil.','2025-03-27 23:02:34','2025-03-27 23:02:34'),(11794,'trails',186,'Is the trail suitable for families?','Yes, the Temple Quarry Trail is family-friendly and offers opportunities for education and exploration.','2025-03-27 23:02:34','2025-03-27 23:02:34'),(11795,'trails',186,'What can hikers find along the trail?','The trail features benches, historical markers, and a loop where the wagons used to turn around for hauling stones are located.','2025-03-27 23:02:34','2025-03-27 23:02:34'),(11796,'trails',186,'What is the difficulty level of the hike?','The hike is rated as intermediate in difficulty.','2025-03-27 23:02:34','2025-03-27 23:02:34'),(11797,'trails',186,'What are the trail\'s elevation details?','The trail has a highest elevation of 2,934 feet and a lowest elevation of 2,934 feet with a slight incline and decline.','2025-03-27 23:02:34','2025-03-27 23:02:34'),(11798,'trails',186,'What types of activities are allowed on the trail?','Both dogs and mountain bikes are permitted on the trail.','2025-03-27 23:02:34','2025-03-27 23:02:34'),(11799,'trails',186,'What kind of wildlife or natural features might hikers see?','The trail offers beautiful views and opportunities to see local wildlife.','2025-03-27 23:02:34','2025-03-27 23:02:34'),(11800,'trails',186,'What is the latitude and longitude of the trail?','The coordinates for the trail are latitude 37.1028 and longitude -113.596.','2025-03-27 23:02:34','2025-03-27 23:02:34'),(11801,'trails',187,'What is the main feature of the Gates Lane hike?','The Gates Lane hike showcases stunning rock formations and offers breathtaking panoramic views of southern Utah.','2025-03-27 23:02:39','2025-03-27 23:02:39'),(11802,'trails',187,'What is the difficulty level of the Gates Lane trail?','The trail is classified as intermediate, making it suitable for hikers with some experience.','2025-03-27 23:02:39','2025-03-27 23:02:39'),(11803,'trails',187,'What is the highest elevation reached on the trail?','Hikers will reach a maximum elevation of 2,761 feet during the hike.','2025-03-27 23: