yon Loop?','This trail is classified as a point-to-point route.','2025-03-27 23:02:45','2025-03-27 23:02:45'),(11814,'trails',188,'What is the elevation change on the Desert Canyon Loop?','Hikers and bikers will experience a total incline of 233 feet and a descent of 184 feet along the trail.','2025-03-27 23:02:45','2025-03-27 23:02:45'),(11815,'trails',188,'What is the average grade of the Desert Canyon Loop?','The trail features an average grade of 0.03%, indicating a gentle slope throughout the journey.','2025-03-27 23:02:45','2025-03-27 23:02:45'),(11816,'trails',188,'What is the maximum grade of the trail?','The maximum grade on the Desert Canyon Loop reaches 0.07%, ensuring a relatively easy experience.','2025-03-27 23:02:45','2025-03-27 23:02:45'),(11817,'trails',188,'What are the geographical coordinates of the Desert Canyon Loop?','The trail is located at a latitude of 37.0128 and a longitude of -113.516.','2025-03-27 23:02:45','2025-03-27 23:02:45'),(11818,'trails',189,'What is the Black Brush Trail like?','The Black Brush Trail offers an opportunity to experience breathtaking views of the enchanting desert landscape, impressive sandstone cliffs, and various wildlife.','2025-03-27 23:02:53','2025-03-27 23:02:53'),(11819,'trails',189,'What level of difficulty is the Black Brush Trail?','This trail is considered to be of intermediate to difficult level, making it suitable for those with some hiking experience.','2025-03-27 23:02:53','2025-03-27 23:02:53'),(11820,'trails',189,'What is the highest elevation along the Black Brush Trail?','The highest point you will reach on the Black Brush Trail is 2,907 feet.','2025-03-27 23:02:53','2025-03-27 23:02:53'),(11821,'trails',189,'What is the lowest elevation on the Black Brush Trail?','The lowest elevation along the trail is also 2,907 feet.','2025-03-27 23:02:53','2025-03-27 23:02:53'),(11822,'trails',189,'How long is the Black Brush Trail?','The length of the Black Brush Trail is 3.3 miles, offering a rewarding hike for those looking to explore the area.','2025-03-27 23:02:53','2025-03-27 23:02:53'),(11823,'trails',189,'Is the Black Brush Trail a loop or point-to-point?','The trail is a point-to-point hike, meaning you will need to return to your starting point after completing the trail.','2025-03-27 23:02:53','2025-03-27 23:02:53'),(11824,'trails',189,'What is the total incline on the Black Brush Trail?','During your hike, you will encounter a total incline of 428 feet.','2025-03-27 23:02:53','2025-03-27 23:02:53'),(11825,'trails',189,'What is the total decline on the Black Brush Trail?','The overall decline you will experience on the Black Brush Trail is 528 feet.','2025-03-27 23:02:53','2025-03-27 23:02:53'),(11826,'trails',189,'What is the average grade of the Black Brush Trail?','The average grade of the trail is relatively gentle at 0.06%, making it manageable for most hikers.','2025-03-27 23:02:53','2025-03-27 23:02:53'),(11827,'trails',189,'What is the maximum grade of the Black Brush Trail?','At its steepest point, the trail has a maximum grade of 0.19%.','2025-03-27 23:02:53','2025-03-27 23:02:53'),(11828,'trails',189,'What are the geographical coordinates of the Black Brush Trail?','The trail is located at a latitude of 37.121 and a longitude of -113.675.','2025-03-27 23:02:53','2025-03-27 23:02:53'),(11829,'trails',190,'What is the main attraction of the Maverick Trail?','The Maverick Trail offers an opportunity to witness stunning red rock formations, impressive sandstone cliffs, and panoramic views of the beautiful landscapes in southern Utah and northern Arizona.','2025-03-27 23:03:00','2025-03-27 23:03:00'),(11830,'trails',190,'What is the difficulty level of the Maverick Trail?','The trail is considered to be at an intermediate difficulty level, making it suitable for those with some hiking experience.','2025-03-27 23:03:00','2025-03-27 23:03:00'),(11831,'trails',190,'What are the highest and lowest elevations on the Maverick Trail?','The Maverick Trail has a highest elevation of 2807 feet, while the lowest elevation is also 2807 feet.','2025-03-27 23:03:00','2025-03-27 23:03:00'),(11832,'trails',190,'How long is the Maverick Trail?','The Maverick Trail stretches for 1.0 mile, making it a manageable hike for various skill levels.','2025-03-27 23:03:00','2025-03-27 23:03:00'),(11833,'trails',190,'What type of trail is the Maverick Trail?','The trail is a point-to-point route, meaning you will start and finish at different endpoints.','2025-03-27 23:03:00','2025-03-27 23:03:00'),(11834,'trails',190,'What is the elevation gain on the Maverick Trail?','Hikers will encounter an elevation gain of 319 feet along the trail.','2025-03-27 23:03:00','2025-03-27 23:03:00'),(11835,'trails',190,'Is there any decline on the Maverick Trail?','Yes, the trail features a slight decline of 5 feet.','2025-03-27 23:03:00','2025-03-27 23:03:00'),(11836,'trails',190,'What is the average grade of the Maverick Trail?','The average grade of the trail is approximately 0.06%, which indicates a relatively gentle incline.','2025-03-27 23:03:00','2025-03-27 23:03:00'),(11837,'trails',190,'What is the maximum grade found on the Maverick Trail?','The trail has a maximum grade of about 0.17%, which is manageable for most hikers.','2025-03-27 23:03:00','2025-03-27 23:03:00'),(11838,'trails',190,'What are the GPS coordinates of the Maverick Trail?','The trail is located at a latitude of 37.1291 and a longitude of -113.663.','2025-03-27 23:03:00','2025-03-27 23:03:00'),(11839,'trails',191,'What is the Stucki Springs Loop like?','The Stucki Springs Loop offers an impressive experience within the Bearclaw Poppy trail network, showcasing breathtaking views of southern Utah\'s landscape.','2025-03-27 23:03:07','2025-03-27 23:03:07'),(11840,'trails',191,'What is the difficulty level of the Stucki Springs Loop?','This trail is classified as intermediate, making it suitable for those with some hiking experience.','2025-03-27 23:03:07','2025-03-27 23:03:07'),(11841,'trails',191,'What are the elevation details of the trail?','The trail reaches a maximum elevation of 2846 feet, with its lowest point also at 2846 feet.','2025-03-27 23:03:07','2025-03-27 23:03:07'),(11842,'trails',191,'How long is the Stucki Springs Loop?','The total length of the Stucki Springs Loop is 5.7 miles.','2025-03-27 23:03:07','2025-03-27 23:03:07'),(11843,'trails',191,'What type of trail is the Stucki Springs Loop?','The trail is a point-to-point type, providing a unique hiking experience.','2025-03-27 23:03:07','2025-03-27 23:03:07'),(11844,'trails',191,'What is the elevation change on the trail?','Hikers will encounter an incline of 320 feet and a decline of 490 feet along the Stucki Springs Loop.','2025-03-27 23:03:07','2025-03-27 23:03:07'),(11845,'trails',191,'What is the average grade of the trail?','The average grade of the Stucki Springs Loop is about 0.03%, offering a relatively gentle hiking experience.','2025-03-27 23:03:07','2025-03-27 23:03:07'),(11846,'trails',191,'What is the maximum grade on the Stucki Springs Loop?','The maximum grade on this trail can reach up to 0.06%, allowing for a manageable ascent.','2025-03-27 23:03:07','2025-03-27 23:03:07'),(11847,'trails',191,'Can you provide the geographical coordinates of Stucki Springs Loop?','Yes, the trail is located at a latitude of 37.0995 and a longitude of -113.676.','2025-03-27 23:03:07','2025-03-27 23:03:07'),(11848,'trails',192,'What can you tell me about the Bearclaw Poppy Trail?','The Bearclaw Poppy Trail is a captivating scenic route that connects to various other trails, offering breathtaking panoramic views of the landscapes in southern Utah and northern Arizona.','2025-03-27 23:03:16','2025-03-27 23:03:16'),(11849,'trails',192,'What is the difficulty level of the Bearclaw Poppy Trail?','This trail is categorized as intermediate, making it suitable for hikers with some experience.','2025-03-27 23:03:16','2025-03-27 23:03:16'),(11850,'trails',192,'What are the elevation details for the Bearclaw Poppy Trail?','The trail reaches a highest point of 2,575 feet and has its lowest elevation also at 2,575 feet, maintaining a relatively steady elevation throughout.','2025-03-27 23:03:16','2025-03-27 23:03:16'),(11851,'trails',192,'How long is the Bearclaw Poppy Trail?','The trail stretches for 3.9 miles, providing a rewarding hike amid stunning scenery.','2025-03-27 23:03:16','2025-03-27 23:03:16'),(11852,'trails',192,'What type of trail is the Bearclaw Poppy Trail?','The Bearclaw Poppy Trail is a point-to-point trail, meaning it starts at one location and ends at another.','2025-03-27 23:03:16','2025-03-27 23:03:16'),(11853,'trails',192,'What are the incline and decline statistics for the Bearclaw Poppy Trail?','The trail features an incline of 111 feet and a decline of 460 feet, which contributes to its intermediate difficulty level.','2025-03-27 23:03:16','2025-03-27 23:03:16'),(11854,'trails',192,'What is the average and maximum grade of the Bearclaw Poppy Trail?','The average grade of the trail is a gentle 0.03%, with a maximum grade reaching up to 0.05%.','2025-03-27 23:03:16','2025-03-27 23:03:16'),(11855,'trails',192,'What are the geographical coordinates of the Bearclaw Poppy Trail?','The trail is located at a latitude of 37.0888 and a longitude of -113.641, placing it in a beautiful area of southern Utah.','2025-03-27 23:03:16','2025-03-27 23:03:16'),(11856,'trails',193,'What is the Kolob Arch Trail?','The Kolob Arch Trail is a scenic seven-mile hike located in the remote Kolob Canyons District of Zion National Park, leading to the impressive Kolob Arch, which is perched high on a canyon wall.','2025-03-27 23:03:28','2025-03-27 23:03:28'),(11857,'trails',193,'What can I expect to see along the trail?','Hikers will enjoy stunning views of colorful canyon walls, the soothing sounds of La Verkin Creek, and the spectacular Kolob Terrace, enriching your hiking experience with picturesque landscapes.','2025-03-27 23:03:28','2025-03-27 23:03:28'),(11858,'trails',193,'How difficult is the Kolob Arch Trail?','The trail is considered intermediate in difficulty, making it suitable for those who are accustomed to hiking but may still offer a challenge.','2025-03-27 23:03:28','2025-03-27 23:03:28'),(11859,'trails',193,'What are the elevation details of the trail?','The highest and lowest point of the trail is at 5,225 feet, featuring a gentle incline of 122 feet, with both maximum and average grades being quite gradual.','2025-03-27 23:03:28','2025-03-27 23:03:28'),(11860,'trails',193,'What makes Kolob Arch special?','Kolob Arch, with its 287-foot span and 75-foot thickness, is renowned for its beauty and impressive structure, making it a popular destination despite not being the largest arch in the world.','2025-03-27 23:03:28','2025-03-27 23:03:28'),(11861,'trails',193,'Will I see any wildlife on the trail?','Yes, the trail is home to a variety of wildlife including reptiles, birds, and mammals, offering plenty of opportunities for nature observation.','2025-03-27 23:03:28','2025-03-27 23:03:28'),(11862,'trails',193,'Are dogs allowed on the Kolob Arch Trail?','No, dogs are not permitted on the Kolob Arch Trail, so please plan accordingly if you\'re traveling with your pet.','2025-03-27 23:03:28','2025-03-27 23:03:28'),(11863,'trails',193,'What activities can I enjoy at Kolob Arch Trail?','Aside from hiking, visitors can enjoy birdwatching, photography, and experiencing the beautiful fall colors, wildflowers, and the tranquil river and creek scenery.','2025-03-27 23:03:28','2025-03-27 23:03:28'),(11864,'trails',193,'How long is the trail?','The Kolob Arch Trail is approximately 0.5 miles long, allowing for a relatively short yet rewarding hike.','2025-03-27 23:03:28','2025-03-27 23:03:28'),(11865,'trails',193,'Is the trail point-to-point or a loop?','The Kolob Arch Trail is a point-to-point trail, guiding you directly to the arch and back.','2025-03-27 23:03:28','2025-03-27 23:03:28'),(11866,'trails',193,'What are the geographical coordinates of the trail?','The trail is located at latitude 37.4159 and longitude -113.151, placing it in a stunning part of Zion National Park.','2025-03-27 23:03:28','2025-03-27 23:03:28'),(11867,'trails',194,'What is the starting point of the Deertrap Mountain Trail?','The Deertrap Mountain Trail begins where it diverges from the Cable Mountain Trail, heading westward.','2025-03-27 23:03:37','2025-03-27 23:03:37'),(11868,'trails',194,'What can I see along the Deertrap Mountain Trail?','As you traverse the Deertrap Mountain Trail, you\'ll be treated to stunning views of notable landmarks such as the Mountain of the Sun, Emerald Pool, the Twin Brothers, Angels Landing, and the Court of the Patriarchs, among other scenic vistas.','2025-03-27 23:03:37','2025-03-27 23:03:37'),(11869,'trails',194,'How difficult is the Deertrap Mountain Trail?','The trail is considered intermediate in difficulty, offering a manageable yet rewarding experience for hikers.','2025-03-27 23:03:37','2025-03-27 23:03:37'),(11870,'trails',194,'What is the total length of the Deertrap Mountain Trail?','The Deertrap Mountain Trail spans approximately 2.7 miles, making it a relatively short hike with plenty of attractions.','2025-03-27 23:03:37','2025-03-27 23:03:37'),(11871,'trails',194,'What is the highest and lowest elevation on the Deertrap Mountain Trail?','The trail reaches a maximum elevation of 6685 feet, with the lowest elevation also being 6685 feet, indicating a mostly flat route with some undulations.','2025-03-27 23:03:37','2025-03-27 23:03:37'),(11872,'trails',194,'What kind of incline and decline can I expect on this trail?','Hikers can expect an incline of about 334 feet and a decline of approximately 467 feet along the Deertrap Mountain Trail.','2025-03-27 23:03:37','2025-03-27 23:03:37'),(11873,'trails',194,'What are the average and maximum grades of the Deertrap Mountain Trail?','The average grade of the trail is around 0.06%, with a maximum grade of 0.26%, ensuring a gentle ascent and descent.','2025-03-27 23:03:37','2025-03-27 23:03:37'),(11874,'trails',194,'What features can I enjoy while hiking the Deertrap Mountain Trail?','This trail offers a variety of features to enjoy, including opportunities for birdwatching, vibrant fall colors, scenic river and creek views, wildflowers, and chances to spot local wildlife.','2025-03-27 23:03:37','2025-03-27 23:03:37'),(11875,'trails',194,'Are dogs allowed on the Deertrap Mountain Trail?','Unfortunately, dogs are not permitted on the Deertrap Mountain Trail, ensuring a more natural experience for all hikers.','2025-03-27 23:03:37','2025-03-27 23:03:37'),(11876,'trails',194,'What are the geographic coordinates for the Deertrap Mountain Trail?','The trail is located at a latitude of 37.2527 and a longitude of -112.917, which you can use for navigation purposes.','2025-03-27 23:03:37','2025-03-27 23:03:37'),(11877,'trails',195,'What is the Hidden Canyon Trail like?','The Hidden Canyon Trail is a moderately strenuous hike that runs alongside a cliff face, leading to the entrance of a narrow canyon. The trail includes steep gradients and requires the use of chains bolted into the rock for added stability.','2025-03-27 23:03:45','2025-03-27 23:03:45'),(11878,'trails',195,'How challenging is the Hidden Canyon Trail?','The trail is considered difficult due to its steep sections and high exposure, especially along the cliff edges. While the incline becomes less steep as you go, the overall challenge remains significant.','2025-03-27 23:03:45','2025-03-27 23:03:45'),(11879,'trails',195,'What are the key features of the Hidden Canyon Trail?','Hikers will enjoy a variety of features on the trail, including opportunities for birdwatching, views of caves, stunning landscapes, and sightings of local wildlife.','2025-03-27 23:03:45','2025-03-27 23:03:45'),(11880,'trails',195,'What is the total distance of the Hidden Canyon Trail?','The trail spans approximately 1.1 miles from start to finish.','2025-03-27 23:03:45','2025-03-27 23:03:45'),(11881,'trails',195,'What is the elevation range for this trail?','The Hidden Canyon Trail maintains an elevation of 4,746 feet throughout its length.','2025-03-27 23:03:45','2025-03-27 23:03:45'),(11882,'trails',195,'Is the Hidden Canyon Trail suitable for dogs?','Unfortunately, dogs are not permitted on the Hidden Canyon Trail.','2025-03-27 23:03:45','2025-03-27 23:03:45'),(11883,'trails',195,'What is the trail\'s incline and grade?','The incline of the trail is about 520 feet, with a maximum grade reaching up to 0.60% and an average grade of 0.09%.','2025-03-27 23:03:45','2025-03-27 23:03:45'),(11884,'trails',195,'Can I continue past the canyon\'s mouth?','Yes, hikers can choose to scramble further into the hanging canyon beyond the official trail endpoint, although this should only be attempted by those who can manage a significant fear of heights.','2025-03-27 23:03:45','2025-03-27 23:03:45'),(11885,'trails',195,'Where is the Hidden Canyon Trail located?','The trail is situated at latitude 37.2695 and longitude -112.936, offering stunning natural surroundings.','2025-03-27 23:03:45','2025-03-27 23:03:45'),(11886,'trails',196,'What can I expect to see on the Observation Point Trail?','Observation Point Trail offers stunning panoramic vistas of the canyon. You\'ll have unobstructed views of Angel\'s Landing to the southwest and the Great White Throne directly south, making it a must-see for nature enthusiasts.','2025-03-27 23:03:53','2025-03-27 23:03:53'),(11887,'trails',196,'How challenging is the Observation Point Trail?','The trail is categorized as intermediate to difficult, making it suitable for those who are relatively experienced with hiking.','2025-03-27 23:03:53','2025-03-27 23:03:53'),(11888,'trails',196,'What is the elevation range for the Observation Point Trail?','The trail reaches a maximum elevation of 6,495 feet, which is also its starting elevation, offering a consistent height throughout the hike.','2025-03-27 23:03:53','2025-03-27 23:03:53'),(11889,'trails',196,'How long is the Observation Point Trail?','The trail stretches 0.4 miles, providing a short yet rewarding hike.','2025-03-27 23:03:53','2025-03-27 23:03:53'),(11890,'trails',196,'What type of trail is the Observation Point Trail?','This is a point-to-point trail, meaning it leads from a starting point to a designated endpoint, often at an observation vantage.','2025-03-27 23:03:53','2025-03-27 23:03:53'),(11891,'trails',196,'What are the incline and decline statistics for the trail?','You\'ll encounter a slight incline of 28 feet and a minor decline of 5 feet throughout the hike, making it manageable for most hikers.','2025-03-27 23:03:53','2025-03-27 23:03:53'),(11892,'trails',196,'What is the average and maximum grade of the trail?','The average grade is a gentle 0.02%, with a maximum grade of 0.04%, contributing to the trail\'s overall accessibility.','2025-03-27 23:03:53','2025-03-27 23:03:53'),(11893,'trails',196,'What features can I expect on the Observation Point Trail?','In addition to breathtaking views, you\'ll have opportunities for birdwatching and wildlife spotting along the trail.','2025-03-27 23:03:53','2025-03-27 23:03:53'),(11894,'trails',196,'Are dogs allowed on the Observation Point Trail?','Unfortunately, dogs are not permitted on this trail, so please plan accordingly.','2025-03-27 23:03:53','2025-03-27 23:03:53'),(11895,'trails',196,'What are the geographical coordinates for Observation Point Trail?','The trail is located at latitude 37.2811 and longitude -112.937, helping with navigation in the area.','2025-03-27 23:03:53','2025-03-27 23:03:53'),(11896,'trails',197,'Is the Weeping Rock Trail suitable for families?','Yes, the Weeping Rock Trail is designed to be family-friendly, making it accessible for hikers of various ages.','2025-03-27 23:04:01','2025-03-27 23:04:01'),(11897,'trails',197,'What is the difficulty level of the Weeping Rock Trail?','The trail is categorized as easy to intermediate, making it manageable for most hikers.','2025-03-27 23:04:01','2025-03-27 23:04:01'),(11898,'trails',197,'What can I expect to see at the end of the Weeping Rock Trail?','The trail culminates at a stunning rock alcove, which is a remarkable geological feature that many find breathtaking.','2025-03-27 23:04:01','2025-03-27 23:04:01'),(11899,'trails',197,'How long is the Weeping Rock Trail?','The total length of the Weeping Rock Trail is just 0.2 miles, making it a short hike.','2025-03-27 23:04:01','2025-03-27 23:04:01'),(11900,'trails',197,'What is the elevation change on the Weeping Rock Trail?','The trail has a slight incline of 64 feet, with a highest elevation of 4,372 feet.','2025-03-27 23:04:01','2025-03-27 23:04:01'),(11901,'trails',197,'What type of trail is the Weeping Rock Trail?','This is a point-to-point trail, which means it starts and ends at different points.','2025-03-27 23:04:01','2025-03-27 23:04:01'),(11902,'trails',197,'What are the views like on the Weeping Rock Trail?','Hikers can enjoy scenic views while following the trail, enhancing the overall experience of the hike.','2025-03-27 23:04:01','2025-03-27 23:04:01'),(11903,'trails',197,'Are dogs allowed on the Weeping Rock Trail?','No, dogs are not permitted on the Weeping Rock Trail.','2025-03-27 23:04:01','2025-03-27 23:04:01'),(11904,'trails',197,'What are the geographical coordinates of the Weeping Rock Trail?','The coordinates of the trail are approximately 37.2709 latitude and -112.939 longitude.','2025-03-27 23:04:01','2025-03-27 23:04:01'),(11905,'trails',198,'What is the starting point of the Watchman Trail?','The Watchman Trail begins at the Visitor Center.','2025-03-27 23:04:11','2025-03-27 23:04:11'),(11906,'trails',198,'How does the terrain of the Watchman Trail change?','The trail starts off gently but soon becomes quite steep as you approach the mesa.','2025-03-27 23:04:11','2025-03-27 23:04:11'),(11907,'trails',198,'What can hikers expect to see at the top of the Watchman Trail?','Once you reach the Watchman Trail mesa, you\'ll be treated to stunning views of the Towers of the Virgin, the lower Zion Canyon, and the town of Springdale.','2025-03-27 23:04:11','2025-03-27 23:04:11'),(11908,'trails',198,'How difficult is the Watchman Trail?','The trail is classified as intermediate in terms of difficulty.','2025-03-27 23:04:11','2025-03-27 23:04:11'),(11909,'trails',198,'What is the highest elevation point of the Watchman Trail?','The highest elevation you will reach on this trail is 3,931 feet.','2025-03-27 23:04:11','2025-03-27 23:04:11'),(11910,'trails',198,'What is the length of the Watchman Trail?','The total length of the trail is 1.8 miles.','2025-03-27 23:04:11','2025-03-27 23:04:11'),(11911,'trails',198,'Is the Watchman Trail a loop or point to point?','The Watchman Trail is a point-to-point trail.','2025-03-27 23:04:11','2025-03-27 23:04:11'),(11912,'trails',198,'What is the elevation gain on the Watchman Trail?','Hikers will experience an elevation gain of 559 feet.','2025-03-27 23:04:11','2025-03-27 23:04:11'),(11913,'trails',198,'What features can hikers enjoy along the Watchman Trail?','This trail offers features such as birding opportunities, vibrant fall colors, beautiful views, wildflowers, and chances to spot wildlife.','2025-03-27 23:04:11','2025-03-27 23:04:11'),(11914,'trails',198,'Are dogs allowed on the Watchman Trail?','No, dogs are not permitted on the Watchman Trail.','2025-03-27 23:04:12','2025-03-27 23:04:12'),(11915,'trails',198,'What are the geographic coordinates of the Watchman Trail?','The trail is located at a latitude of 37.2013 and a longitude of -112.986.','2025-03-27 23:04:12','2025-03-27 23:04:12'),(11916,'trails',199,'Where does the La Verkin Creek Trail start?','The La Verkin Creek Trail begins at Lee Pass, which is the second to last trailhead on the Kolob Canyons Road.','2025-03-27 23:04:21','2025-03-27 23:04:21'),(11917,'trails',199,'What kind of views can hikers expect on the La Verkin Creek Trail?','Hikers will enjoy stunning views of nearby canyons and cliffs as the trail travels alongside Timber Creek and ascends toward La Verkin Creek.','2025-03-27 23:04:21','2025-03-27 23:04:21'),(11918,'trails',199,'What is the length of the La Verkin Creek Trail and its destination?','The trail stretches for 7 miles and leads to Kolob Arch, renowned as one of the largest natural arches globally.','2025-03-27 23:04:21','2025-03-27 23:04:21'),(11919,'trails',199,'Can I extend my hike beyond Kolob Arch?','Yes! From Kolob Arch, hikers can continue on to Beartrap Canyon and Willis Canyon for both extended trips and day hikes.','2025-03-27 23:04:21','2025-03-27 23:04:21'),(11920,'trails',199,'What are the trailhead facilities at Lee Pass?','At the Lee Pass Trailhead, you\'ll find limited parking. However, there are no water or restroom facilities available, so plan accordingly.','2025-03-27 23:04:21','2025-03-27 23:04:21'),(11921,'trails',199,'What regulations apply to hikers on the La Verkin Creek Trail?','Wilderness rules are in effect, which include limits on group sizes, waste disposal requirements, and a prohibition on pets along the trail.','2025-03-27 23:04:21','2025-03-27 23:04:21'),(11922,'trails',199,'What are the group size limits on the trail?','Groups are limited to a maximum of 12 individuals to minimize environmental impact and preserve the wilderness experience.','2025-03-27 23:04:21','2025-03-27 23:04:21'),(11923,'trails',199,'Are there restroom facilities near the trail?','Restrooms are available at the Kolob Canyons Visitor Center, with pit toilets located at several nearby trailheads. It\'s best to use restrooms before starting your hike.','2025-03-27 23:04:21','2025-03-27 23:04:21'),(11924,'trails',199,'What should I do if I need to use the restroom while on the trail?','If you\'re on the trail, be prepared to carry out any human waste and hygiene products. It\'s recommended to use human waste disposal bags for this purpose.','2025-03-27 23:04:21','2025-03-27 23:04:21'),(11925,'trails',199,'Can I bring my pet on the La Verkin Creek Trail?','No pets are allowed on the La Verkin Creek Trail, with the exception of the Pa\'rus Trail, which is the only pet-friendly trail in Zion National Park.','2025-03-27 23:04:21','2025-03-27 23:04:21'),(11926,'trails',199,'What level of difficulty is the La Verkin Creek Trail?','The trail is classified as intermediate to difficult, due to the incline and rugged terrain.','2025-03-27 23:04:21','2025-03-27 23:04:21'),(11927,'trails',199,'What is the maximum elevation of the La Verkin Creek Trail?','The highest point on the trail reaches an elevation of 5,052 feet.','2025-03-27 23:04:21','2025-03-27 23:04:21'),(11928,'trails',199,'What types of natural features can I expect to see along the trail?','Hikers can enjoy birdwatching, fall colors, rivers and creeks, wildflowers, and potentially see local wildlife throughout the hike.','2025-03-27 23:04:21','2025-03-27 23:04:21'),(11929,'trails',200,'What is the purpose of the Connector Trail?','The Connector Trail serves as a valuable link between the Hop Valley Trail and Wildcat Canyon Trail, enhancing the hiking experience within Zion National Park.','2025-03-27 23:04:29','2025-03-27 23:04:29'),(11930,'trails',200,'What is the difficulty level of the Connector Trail?','This trail is considered intermediate, making it suitable for hikers with some experience.','2025-03-27 23:04:29','2025-03-27 23:04:29'),(11931,'trails',200,'What are the elevation details of the Connector Trail?','The Connector Trail has a consistent elevation of 6,388 feet, providing a unique hiking experience at this height.','2025-03-27 23:04:29','2025-03-27 23:04:29'),(11932,'trails',200,'How long is the Connector Trail?','The total length of the Connector Trail is 4.0 miles, making it a manageable trek for most hikers.','2025-03-27 23:04:29','2025-03-27 23:04:29'),(11933,'trails',200,'What type of trail is the Connector Trail?','The Connector Trail is a point-to-point trail, meaning hikers will start at one end and finish at the other.','2025-03-27 23:04:29','2025-03-27 23:04:29'),(11934,'trails',200,'What is the incline and decline of the Connector Trail?','Over the course of the trail, hikers will experience an overall incline of 144 feet and a decline of 672 feet.','2025-03-27 23:04:29','2025-03-27 23:04:29'),(11935,'trails',200,'What is the average grade of the Connector Trail?','The average grade is very gentle, sitting at 0.04%, which makes for a comfortable hike.','2025-03-27 23:04:29','2025-03-27 23:04:29'),(11936,'trails',200,'What is the maximum grade of the Connector Trail?','The trail features a maximum grade of 0.10%, ensuring a relatively easy ascent and descent.','2025-03-27 23:04:29','2025-03-27 23:04:29'),(11937,'trails',200,'What features can hikers enjoy on the Connector Trail?','Hikers can look forward to a variety of features including birding opportunities, stunning fall colors, views of rivers and creeks, wildflowers, and diverse wildlife.','2025-03-27 23:04:29','2025-03-27 23:04:29'),(11938,'trails',200,'Are dogs allowed on the Connector Trail?','No, dogs are not permitted on this trail, so hikers should plan accordingly.','2025-03-27 23:04:29','2025-03-27 23:04:29'),(11939,'trails',200,'What are the geographical coordinates of the Connector Trail?','The trail is located at a latitude of 37.3396 and a longitude of -113.062.','2025-03-27 23:04:30','2025-03-27 23:04:30'),(11940,'trails',201,'What are the highlights of the Wildcat Canyon Trail?','The Wildcat Canyon Trail offers breathtaking views of the Northgate Peaks, winds through scenic ponderosa pine forests, and provides stunning vistas of the deep Wildcat Canyon.','2025-03-27 23:04:37','2025-03-27 23:04:37'),(11941,'trails',201,'Where does the Wildcat Canyon Trail begin?','This trail starts at the Wildcat Trailhead and intersects with the Northgate Peaks Trail, making it easy to access.','2025-03-27 23:04:37','2025-03-27 23:04:37'),(11942,'trails',201,'What is the length of the Wildcat Canyon Trail?','The total length of the Wildcat Canyon Trail is approximately 5.9 miles.','2025-03-27 23:04:37','2025-03-27 23:04:37'),(11943,'trails',201,'What is the difficulty level of this trail?','The Wildcat Canyon Trail is classified as intermediate, making it suitable for those with some hiking experience.','2025-03-27 23:04:37','2025-03-27 23:04:37'),(11944,'trails',201,'What are the elevation details for the Wildcat Canyon Trail?','The highest elevation along the trail is 6,915 feet, which matches the lowest point, making it a relatively level hike in terms of elevation change.','2025-03-27 23:04:37','2025-03-27 23:04:37'),(11945,'trails',201,'What kind of terrain can hikers expect?','Hikers will experience a rolling backcountry trail as it meanders towards the West Rim Trail, with some slight inclines and declines.','2025-03-27 23:04:37','2025-03-27 23:04:37'),(11946,'trails',201,'Are there any established campsites along this trail?','There are no designated campsites along the Wildcat Canyon Trail, but a permit is required for overnight stays in the area.','2025-03-27 23:04:37','2025-03-27 23:04:37'),(11947,'trails',201,'What should hikers know about bringing pets on the trail?','Dogs are allowed on the Wildcat Canyon Trail, but they must be kept on a leash at all times.','2025-03-27 23:04:37','2025-03-27 23:04:37'),(11948,'trails',201,'What scenic features can hikers expect on this trail?','The trail is known for its rich wildlife, beautiful wildflowers, vibrant fall colors, and excellent birding opportunities, alongside the astonishing views.','2025-03-27 23:04:37','2025-03-27 23:04:37'),(11949,'trails',201,'What are the coordinates of the Wildcat Canyon Trail?','The Wildcat Canyon Trail can be located at latitude 37.3398 and longitude -113.076.','2025-03-27 23:04:37','2025-03-27 23:04:37'),(11950,'trails',202,'What is the Northgate Peaks Trail like?','The Northgate Peaks Trail offers a relatively flat hiking experience, perfect for families, as it meanders through open grasslands and pinyon-juniper before reaching the stunning views between the east and west Northgate Peaks.','2025-03-27 23:04:45','2025-03-27 23:04:45'),(11951,'trails',202,'Where does the Northgate Peaks Trail start?','This trail begins at a junction with the Wildcat Canyon Trail, located about a mile from the main trailhead.','2025-03-27 23:04:45','2025-03-27 23:04:45'),(11952,'trails',202,'What kind of scenery can I expect on this trail?','Hikers will enjoy beautiful landscapes characterized by grassy areas and pinyon-juniper trees, with spectacular views of the North Guardian Angel sandstone formation at the trail\'s end.','2025-03-27 23:04:45','2025-03-27 23:04:45'),(11953,'trails',202,'Is there an option to climb the Northgate Peaks?','Yes, there are several scrambling routes available to ascend either of the Northgate Peaks for an even more breathtaking vantage point, but please adhere to marked paths to protect the fragile desert flora.','2025-03-27 23:04:45','2025-03-27 23:04:45'),(11954,'trails',202,'What is the difficulty level of the Northgate Peaks Trail?','The trail is rated as intermediate, making it accessible for most hikers, especially families looking for a manageable adventure.','2025-03-27 23:04:45','2025-03-27 23:04:45'),(11955,'trails',202,'What are the elevation details for this trail?','The trail has a consistent elevation at 6,903 feet, with a slight incline of 22 feet and a decline of 46 feet.','2025-03-27 23:04:45','2025-03-27 23:04:45'),(11956,'trails',202,'How long is the Northgate Peaks Trail?','The trail stretches for 1.1 miles, following a point-to-point route.','2025-03-27 23:04:45','2025-03-27 23:04:45'),(11957,'trails',202,'What is the average and maximum grade of the trail?','The Northgate Peaks Trail has an average grade of only 0.01% and a maximum grade of 0.07%, making it gentle in nature.','2025-03-27 23:04:45','2025-03-27 23:04:45'),(11958,'trails',202,'Are there any notable features along the trail?','Hikers can expect to witness vibrant fall colors, a variety of wildflowers, and possibly spot some local wildlife during their hike.','2025-03-27 23:04:45','2025-03-27 23:04:45'),(11959,'trails',202,'Are dogs allowed on the Northgate Peaks Trail?','Yes, dogs are permitted but must be kept on a leash throughout the hike.','2025-03-27 23:04:45','2025-03-27 23:04:45'),(11960,'trails',202,'What are the GPS coordinates for the Northgate Peaks Trail?','The coordinates for the trail are approximately 37.34 latitude and -113.06 longitude.','2025-03-27 23:04:45','2025-03-27 23:04:45'),(11961,'trails',203,'What is the East Mesa Trail like?','The East Mesa Trail is a less-traveled path that weaves through a dense forest, offering stunning views of the Pink Cliffs and Brian Head Peak. While it may not be as famous as other hikes in Zion, it provides access to beautiful landscapes, including Bulloch Gulch and a connection to the highly regarded Observation Point Trail.','2025-03-27 23:04:52','2025-03-27 23:04:52'),(11962,'trails',203,'What can I expect in terms of elevation on the East Mesa Trail?','The East Mesa Trail has a highest elevation of 5,627 feet, with a steep ascent at the beginning as it switchbacks up from the East Rim Trail. After the initial climb, the trail levels out, making for easier hiking.','2025-03-27 23:04:52','2025-03-27 23:04:52'),(11963,'trails',203,'How long is the East Mesa Trail?','The total length of the East Mesa Trail is approximately 4.4 miles, making it a manageable hike for those with intermediate skill levels.','2025-03-27 23:04:52','2025-03-27 23:04:52'),(11964,'trails',203,'What is the difficulty level of the East Mesa Trail?','This trail is categorized as intermediate, featuring an elevation gain of 1,177 feet but leveling off after the initial steep section, which helps make the hike more accessible.','2025-03-27 23:04:52','2025-03-27 23:04:52'),(11965,'trails',203,'What is the trail type for the East Mesa Trail?','The East Mesa Trail is a point-to-point trail, meaning it starts at one location and ends at another, specifically connecting the East Rim Trail to the eastern edge of the park.','2025-03-27 23:04:52','2025-03-27 23:04:52'),(11966,'trails',203,'What kind of scenery can I expect while hiking the East Mesa Trail?','Hiking the East Mesa Trail allows you to enjoy vibrant scenery, including dense pinion and juniper forests, stunning fall colors, views of surrounding canyons, and opportunities for birdwatching and observing wildlife.','2025-03-27 23:04:52','2025-03-27 23:04:52'),(11967,'trails',203,'Are dogs allowed on the East Mesa Trail?','No, dogs are not permitted on the East Mesa Trail, so plan accordingly if you\'re traveling with a pet.','2025-03-27 23:04:52','2025-03-27 23:04:52'),(11968,'trails',203,'What trail should I not miss while hiking the East Mesa Trail?','Be sure to check out the Observation Point Trail, which branches off from East Mesa and leads to one of the best viewing spots in Zion National Park. It\'s a brief connector that enhances your hiking experience.','2025-03-27 23:04:53','2025-03-27 23:04:53'),(11969,'trails',203,'What are the coordinates for the East Mesa Trail?','The East Mesa Trail is located at approximately latitude 37.2742 and longitude -112.929.','2025-03-27 23:04:53','2025-03-27 23:04:53'),(11970,'trails',204,'What can I expect to see on the Hop Valley Trail?','The Hop Valley Trail offers stunning views of surrounding rock formations and expansive open fields. As you progress, you\'ll be greeted by the magnificent Hop Valley, characterized by its flat sandy floor and towering vertical walls.','2025-03-27 23:05:01','2025-03-27 23:05:01'),(11971,'trails',204,'Where does the Hop Valley Trail start?','The trailhead is situated off Kolob Terrace Road, providing easy access to the start of your adventure.','2025-03-27 23:05:01','2025-03-27 23:05:01'),(11972,'trails',204,'What is the terrain like on the Hop Valley Trail?','The trail features a sandy, well-worn path that allows for easier navigation through the scenic landscape.','2025-03-27 23:05:01','2025-03-27 23:05:01'),(11973,'trails',204,'Are there camping options along the Hop Valley Trail?','Yes, there are designated camping sites located at the far end of Hop Valley before you begin the descent into La Verkin Creek.','2025-03-27 23:05:01','2025-03-27 23:05:01'),(11974,'trails',204,'Is there a steep descent on the trail?','Indeed, there is a steep descent into La Verkin Creek, which also provides access to the impressive Kolob Arch.','2025-03-27 23:05:01','2025-03-27 23:05:01'),(11975,'trails',204,'What is the difficulty level of the Hop Valley Trail?','The trail is classified as intermediate to difficult, making it suitable for hikers with some experience.','2025-03-27 23:05:01','2025-03-27 23:05:01'),(11976,'trails',204,'What are the length and elevation details of the Hop Valley Trail?','The trail spans 6.6 miles with a highest elevation of 5,342 feet and a notable decline of 1,319 feet.','2025-03-27 23:05:01','2025-03-27 23:05:01'),(11977,'trails',204,'Can I bring my dog on the Hop Valley Trail?','Unfortunately, dogs are not permitted on the Hop Valley Trail.','2025-03-27 23:05:01','2025-03-27 23:05:01'),(11978,'trails',204,'What type of features can I expect to encounter along the trail?','The trail boasts a variety of features including opportunities for birdwatching, stunning fall colors, a river or creek, beautiful views, wildflowers, and a possibility to spot wildlife.','2025-03-27 23:05:01','2025-03-27 23:05:01'),(11979,'trails',204,'What are the coordinates for the Hop Valley Trail?','The geographical coordinates for the trail are approximately latitude 37.3403 and longitude -113.113.','2025-03-27 23:05:01','2025-03-27 23:05:01'),(11980,'trails',205,'Where does the East Rim Trail begin?','The East Rim Trail begins at the East Rim Trailhead, guiding hikers toward the region\'s famous sandstone cliffs.','2025-03-27 23:05:16','2025-03-27 23:05:16'),(11981,'trails',205,'What is a notable landmark along the trail?','One of the key highlights along the trail is Jolly Gulch, a spectacular canyon that appears to drop off dramatically, making it a perfect turnaround point for a shorter hike.','2025-03-27 23:05:16','2025-03-27 23:05:16'),(11982,'trails',205,'What can I expect in the middle section of the East Rim Trail?','In the middle stretch, the trail crosses a high plateau characterized by cooler temperatures and a beautiful ponderosa pine forest, eventually offering breathtaking views of the Echo Canyon Basin.','2025-03-27 23:05:16','2025-03-27 23:05:16'),(11983,'trails',205,'Is there a water source along the trail?','Yes, Stave Springs is approximately five miles from the East Entrance Trailhead. However, it can occasionally run dry, so it\'s wise to check the conditions before your hike.','2025-03-27 23:05:16','2025-03-27 23:05:16'),(11984,'trails',205,'What trails branch off near Stave Springs?','Near Stave Springs, you will find the Cable Mountain Trail that veers left and the Stave Spring Trail that branches to the right, both leading towards additional pathways and a dirt road linked to the Zion Ponderosa Ranch Resort.','2025-03-27 23:05:16','2025-03-27 23:05:16'),(11985,'trails',205,'What is the elevation at Stave Springs?','Stave Springs is located at an elevation of 6,493 feet.','2025-03-27 23:05:16','2025-03-27 23:05:16'),(11986,'trails',205,'How steep is the descent on the trail?','After enjoying the rim views, expect a steep descent of 2,300 feet down to Zion Canyon, navigating through Echo Canyon and ultimately reaching Weeping Rock.','2025-03-27 23:05:16','2025-03-27 23:05:16'),(11987,'trails',205,'When is the best time to hike the East Rim Trail?','Late spring and fall are the ideal times to hike this trail, as it can be snow-covered in winter and very dry during the summer months.','2025-03-27 23:05:16','2025-03-27 23:05:16'),(11988,'trails',205,'Are there any camping facilities along the East Rim Trail?','While there are no designated campsites along the East Rim Trail, a permit is required for any camping, available on a walk-up basis.','2025-03-27 23:05:16','2025-03-27 23:05:16'),(11989,'trails',205,'What is the difficulty level of the East Rim Trail?','The East Rim Trail is rated as intermediate to difficult, making it suitable for those looking for a more challenging hiking experience.','2025-03-27 23:05:16','2025-03-27 23:05:16'),(11990,'trails',205,'What is the total length of the East Rim Trail?','The trail stretches approximately 10.3 miles and follows a point-to-point layout.','2025-03-27 23:05:17','2025-03-27 23:05:17'),(11991,'trails',205,'What are the elevation changes on the East Rim Trail?','The trail features a total incline of about 1,162 feet, with a total decline of approximately 2,509 feet, culminating at its endpoint.','2025-03-27 23:05:17','2025-03-27 23:05:17'),(11992,'trails',205,'What type of features can I expect on the trail?','Hikers can enjoy a variety of features along the East Rim Trail, including birdwatching, stunning fall colors, views of rivers and creeks, wildflowers, and diverse wildlife.','2025-03-27 23:05:17','2025-03-27 23:05:17'),(11993,'trails',205,'Are dogs allowed on the East Rim Trail?','Unfortunately, dogs are not permitted on the East Rim Trail to preserve the natural environment.','2025-03-27 23:05:17','2025-03-27 23:05:17'),(11994,'trails',206,'What is the starting point for the Cable Mountain Trail?','You can begin your hike on the Cable Mountain Trail from the East Rim Trail and Stave Spring.','2025-03-27 23:05:27','2025-03-27 23:05:27'),(11995,'trails',206,'What kind of environment will I experience on the trail?','As you hike, you\'ll traverse through beautiful juniper and pinyon pine forests, immersing yourself in the serene nature of the area.','2025-03-27 23:05:27','2025-03-27 23:05:27'),(11996,'trails',206,'What should I expect after passing Deertrap Mountain Trail?','After Deertrap Mountain Trail, the trail will have a slight rise followed by a gentle descent toward the canyon\'s edge, providing a relaxing hiking experience.','2025-03-27 23:05:27','2025-03-27 23:05:27'),(11997,'trails',206,'What are some of the scenic views along the Cable Mountain Trail?','The trail offers stunning views of Angel\'s Landing, The Great White Throne, and the historic Cable Mountain Draw Works at its endpoint.','2025-03-27 23:05:27','2025-03-27 23:05:27'),(11998,'trails',206,'What is the Cable Mountain Draw Works?','The Cable Mountain Draw Works is a historic aerial tramway built in the early 20th century, once used to transport timber from the mesas to the floor of Zion Canyon. It was listed in the National Register of Historic Places in 1978.','2025-03-27 23:05:27','2025-03-27 23:05:27'),(11999,'trails',206,'Who was responsible for the creation of the Draw Works?','The Draw Works was built by Springdale pioneer David Flanigan, who envisioned it fulfilled a prophecy by Brigham Young about transporting lumber from the canyon rim.','2025-03-27 23:05:27','2025-03-27 23:05:27'),(12000,'trails',206,'What was the operational period of the Cable Mountain Draw Works?','The Draw Works operated from 1901 until 1927, moving immense quantities of lumber and even occasionally ferrying people and a dog down to the canyon floor.','2025-03-27 23:05:27','2025-03-27 23:05:27'),(12001,'trails',206,'What is the difficulty level of the Cable Mountain Trail?','The trail is classified as intermediate, making it suitable for hikers with some experience.','2025-03-27 23:05:27','2025-03-27 23:05:27'),(12002,'trails',206,'What is the total length of the Cable Mountain Trail?','The total length of the Cable Mountain Trail is approximately 3.0 miles.','2025-03-27 23:05:27','2025-03-27 23:05:27'),(12003,'trails',206,'What are the elevation details for this trail?','The trail reaches a highest elevation of 6,453 feet and has a lowest elevation of 6,453 feet, resulting in a slight incline of 444 feet and a decline of 442 feet.','2025-03-27 23:05:27','2025-03-27 23:05:27'),(12004,'trails',206,'What features can I enjoy on the Cable Mountain Trail?','While hiking, look out for opportunities for birdwatching, admire the fall colors, enjoy beautiful views, observe wildflowers, and possibly spot wildlife.','2025-03-27 23:05:27','2025-03-27 23:05:27'),(12005,'trails',206,'Are dogs permitted on the Cable Mountain Trail?','Unfortunately, dogs are not allowed on the Cable Mountain Trail.','2025-03-27 23:05:27','2025-03-27 23:05:27'),(12006,'trails',206,'What are the geographical coordinates of the Cable Mountain Trail?','The trail is located at a latitude of 37.2622 and a longitude of -112.906.','2025-03-27 23:05:27','2025-03-27 23:05:27'),(12007,'trails',207,'What is the Wrangler Trail?','The Wrangler Trail is a scenic path that leads from Zion Lodge to the stunning Court of the Patriarchs, with beautiful views of the Virgin River along the way.','2025-03-27 23:05:38','2025-03-27 23:05:38'),(12008,'trails',207,'How difficult is the Wrangler Trail?','The trail is considered easy, making it accessible for hikers of all skill levels.','2025-03-27 23:05:38','2025-03-27 23:05:38'),(12009,'trails',207,'What is the total length of the trail?','The Wrangler Trail stretches for approximately 1.0 mile.','2025-03-27 23:05:38','2025-03-27 23:05:38'),(12010,'trails',207,'What kind of trail is the Wrangler Trail?','It is a point-to-point trail, which means it starts at one location and ends at another without a loop.','2025-03-27 23:05:38','2025-03-27 23:05:38'),(12011,'trails',207,'What are the elevation levels on the trail?','The trail starts and ends at an elevation of 4242 feet, featuring a minor incline of 3 feet and a gentle decline of 21 feet.','2025-03-27 23:05:38','2025-03-27 23:05:38'),(12012,'trails',207,'What kind of scenery can I expect on the Wrangler Trail?','Hikers will enjoy stunning views including birdwatching opportunities, fall colors, and wildlife sightings, along with beautiful wildflowers and river vistas.','2025-03-27 23:05:38','2025-03-27 23:05:38'),(12013,'trails',207,'Are dogs allowed on the Wrangler Trail?','No, dogs are not permitted on this trail, so please plan accordingly.','2025-03-27 23:05:38','2025-03-27 23:05:38'),(12014,'trails',207,'What is the latitude and longitude of the Wrangler Trail?','The trail is located at approximately 37.2498° N latitude and -112.958° W longitude.','2025-03-27 23:05:38','2025-03-27 23:05:38'),(12015,'trails',208,'What is the Kayenta Trail?','The Kayenta Trail is a short connector path that connects the Grotto Bus Stop to the Emerald Pools in Zion National Park.','2025-03-27 23:05:48','2025-03-27 23:05:48'),(12016,'trails',208,'How long is the Kayenta Trail?','This trail stretches approximately 0.6 miles (2.0 km) in length.','2025-03-27 23:05:48','2025-03-27 23:05:48'),(12017,'trails',208,'What is the difficulty level of the Kayenta Trail?','The trail is rated as easy to intermediate, making it accessible for a wide range of hikers.','2025-03-27 23:05:48','2025-03-27 23:05:48'),(12018,'trails',208,'What type of terrain can I expect on the Kayenta Trail?','The trail is primarily flat and well-maintained, running alongside the beautiful Virgin River.','2025-03-27 23:05:48','2025-03-27 23:05:48'),(12019,'trails',208,'Are there any notable features along the Kayenta Trail?','Yes! Hikers can enjoy stunning views of Zion Canyon, birding opportunities, and vibrant wildflowers, particularly in the fall.','2025-03-27 23:05:48','2025-03-27 23:05:48'),(12020,'trails',208,'Where does the Kayenta Trail start?','The trailhead is found at The Grotto, which is accessible via shuttle stop #6.','2025-03-27 23:05:48','2025-03-27 23:05:48'),(12021,'trails',208,'What should I be aware of while hiking the Kayenta Trail?','Be cautious of long drop-offs along the trail as you hike, preserving safety while enjoying the views.','2025-03-27 23:05:48','2025-03-27 23:05:48'),(12022,'trails',208,'Can I make a loop with the Kayenta Trail?','Absolutely! Hikers can either return on the same trail or create a loop by connecting to one of the Emerald Pools trails.','2025-03-27 23:05:48','2025-03-27 23:05:48'),(12023,'trails',208,'Is there access to amenities near the Kayenta Trail?','Yes, there are restrooms and water available at The Grotto for hikers to use before or after the trail.','2025-03-27 23:05:48','2025-03-27 23:05:48'),(12024,'trails',208,'What are the elevation details for the Kayenta Trail?','The highest and lowest elevations along the trail are both at 4,356 feet, with a gentle incline and decline throughout.','2025-03-27 23:05:48','2025-03-27 23:05:48'),(12025,'trails',208,'Are dogs allowed on the Kayenta Trail?','No, dogs are not permitted on the Kayenta Trail.','2025-03-27 23:05:48','2025-03-27 23:05:48'),(12026,'trails',208,'What are the geographic coordinates for the Kayenta Trail?','The trail is located at the coordinates 37.2602 latitude and -112.952 longitude.','2025-03-27 23:05:48','2025-03-27 23:05:48'),(12027,'trails',209,'Is the Pa\'rus Trail accessible for everyone?','Yes, the Pa\'rus Trail is one of the few ADA accessible trails in Zion National Park, making it suitable for individuals with mobility challenges, families, and those using strollers.','2025-03-27 23:05:59','2025-03-27 23:05:59'),(12028,'trails',209,'What is the overall experience on the Pa\'rus Trail?','The trail offers a serene experience with the soothing sounds of the Virgin River and stunning views of the Watchman. It’s a wonderful option for hikers, bikers, and dog walkers alike.','2025-03-27 23:05:59','2025-03-27 23:05:59'),(12029,'trails',209,'Where can I start the Pa\'rus Trail?','You can begin your journey from either the Zion Canyon Visitor Center (shuttle stop #1) or Canyon Junction (shuttle stop #3). At the Visitor Center, follow the sidewalk to the bridge leading to the trailhead.','2025-03-27 23:05:59','2025-03-27 23:05:59'),(12030,'trails',209,'How long is the Pa\'rus Trail?','The Pa\'rus Trail is approximately 1.7 miles long, providing a pleasant trail experience suitable for a leisurely stroll or a bike ride.','2025-03-27 23:05:59','2025-03-27 23:05:59'),(12031,'trails',209,'What kind of wildlife might I see on the trail?','Hikers often spot wildlife such as deer in the meadows surrounding the trail, adding a delightful aspect to your nature experience.','2025-03-27 23:05:59','2025-03-27 23:05:59'),(12032,'trails',209,'Are there amenities available along the Pa\'rus Trail?','Yes, there are restrooms and water filling stations located at the Visitor Center to ensure you have everything you need during your visit.','2025-03-27 23:05:59','2025-03-27 23:05:59'),(12033,'trails',209,'What are some features of the Pa\'rus Trail?','The trail is known for its birding opportunities, beautiful fall colors, river views, wildflowers, and a chance to observe wildlife, making it a picturesque hike.','2025-03-27 23:05:59','2025-03-27 23:05:59'),(12034,'trails',209,'Is the trail suitable for pets and bicycles?','Absolutely! The Pa\'rus Trail welcomes both pets on leashes and bicycles, making it a friendly environment for all types of outdoor enthusiasts.','2025-03-27 23:05:59','2025-03-27 23:05:59'),(12035,'trails',209,'Can I access the Pa\'rus Trail from other locations?','Yes! You can access the trail from the Museum at Shuttle Stop #2 via a short connector trail, but keep in mind that this segment is not wheelchair accessible and not approved for bikes or pets.','2025-03-27 23:05:59','2025-03-27 23:05:59'),(12036,'trails',209,'What is the elevation change on the Pa\'rus Trail?','The trail has a slight incline of 101 feet and a decline of 13 feet, making it generally flat and easy for all hikers.','2025-03-27 23:05:59','2025-03-27 23:05:59'),(12037,'trails',209,'What makes the Pa\'rus Trail a good place for photography?','The trail offers excellent spots for sunset views, stargazing, and astrophotography, providing an incredible backdrop for capturing nature’s beauty.','2025-03-27 23:05:59','2025-03-27 23:05:59'),(12038,'trails',210,'Where does the West Rim Trail start?','The West Rim Trail begins at the West Rim Trailhead, located near Lava Point.','2025-03-27 23:06:06','2025-03-27 23:06:06'),(12039,'trails',210,'What are the scenic highlights of the West Rim Trail?','Hikers can enjoy striking vistas of Wildcat Canyon, Potato Hollow, and Right Fork Canyon, along with sights of notable landmarks such as Church Mesa, Inclined Temple, Ivins Mountain, and Greatheart Mesa.','2025-03-27 23:06:06','2025-03-27 23:06:06'),(12040,'trails',210,'What is the elevation range of the West Rim Trail?','The highest point on the West Rim Trail reaches an elevation of 4,338 feet, while the lowest elevation is the same, indicating a relatively flat terrain overall.','2025-03-27 23:06:06','2025-03-27 23:06:06'),(12041,'trails',210,'How long is the West Rim Trail?','The total length of the West Rim Trail is approximately 14.7 miles.','2025-03-27 23:06:06','2025-03-27 23:06:06'),(12042,'trails',210,'What is the difficulty level of the West Rim Trail?','The trail is considered difficult, making it best suited for experienced hikers.','2025-03-27 23:06:06','2025-03-27 23:06:06'),(12043,'trails',210,'Is the West Rim Trail a loop or point-to-point?','The West Rim Trail is a point-to-point trail.','2025-03-27 23:06:06','2025-03-27 23:06:06'),(12044,'trails',210,'Are dogs allowed on the West Rim Trail?','No, dogs are not permitted on the West Rim Trail.','2025-03-27 23:06:06','2025-03-27 23:06:06'),(12045,'trails',210,'What type of terrain can hikers expect to encounter?','The trail features an incline of 867 feet and a decline of 3,981 feet, with an average grade of 0.06% and a maximum grade of 0.78%.','2025-03-27 23:06:06','2025-03-27 23:06:06'),(12046,'trails',210,'What natural features can hikers enjoy along the West Rim Trail?','Hikers can experience a range of natural features including birding opportunities, views, waterfalls, wildflowers, and various wildlife.','2025-03-27 23:06:06','2025-03-27 23:06:06'),(12047,'trails',210,'What trail does the West Rim Trail connect with near its southern end?','Towards its southern terminus, the West Rim Trail intersects with the famous Angel\'s Landing hike, which is a must-see attraction in Zion National Park.','2025-03-27 23:06:06','2025-03-27 23:06:06'),(12048,'trails',210,'What geographical coordinates pinpoint the West Rim Trail?','The geographic coordinates for the West Rim Trail are approximately 37.3816 latitude and -113.023 longitude.','2025-03-27 23:06:06','2025-03-27 23:06:06'),(12049,'trails',211,'What is the main purpose of the Telephone Canyon Trail?','The Telephone Canyon Trail serves as a shortcut, connecting Potato Hollow and Cabin Springs while offering stunning views of a burn area.','2025-03-27 23:06:14','2025-03-27 23:06:14'),(12050,'trails',211,'How does the Telephone Canyon Trail compare to other trails in the area?','While it’s labeled as a canyon trail, it\'s more of an open meadow experience, showcasing the scenery of the surrounding burn area rather than any dramatic canyon formations.','2025-03-27 23:06:14','2025-03-27 23:06:14'),(12051,'trails',211,'Is the Telephone Canyon Trail a good option during snow season?','Yes, this trail is a great choice in snowy conditions, as its exposed landscape is likely to clear of snow earlier than trails situated at higher elevations.','2025-03-27 23:06:14','2025-03-27 23:06:14'),(12052,'trails',211,'What are the requirements for camping along the Telephone Canyon Trail?','Camping is permitted only at designated sites along the trail, ensuring minimal impact on the environment.','2025-03-27 23:06:14','2025-03-27 23:06:14'),(12053,'trails',211,'What is the difficulty level of the Telephone Canyon Trail?','The trail ranges from intermediate to difficult, making it a suitable choice for experienced hikers.','2025-03-27 23:06:14','2025-03-27 23:06:14'),(12054,'trails',211,'What is the length and type of the Telephone Canyon Trail?','The trail stretches for 1.9 miles and is categorized as a point-to-point trail.','2025-03-27 23:06:14','2025-03-27 23:06:14'),(12055,'trails',211,'What are the elevation details of the Telephone Canyon Trail?','The trail has a maximum elevation of 6723 feet, while its lowest point is also at 6723 feet, featuring negligible incline and decline.','2025-03-27 23:06:14','2025-03-27 23:06:14'),(12056,'trails',211,'What natural features can hikers expect to see on the Telephone Canyon Trail?','Hikers can enjoy birding, vibrant fall colors, views of rivers and creeks, wildflowers, and opportunities to spot wildlife along the trail.','2025-03-27 23:06:14','2025-03-27 23:06:14'),(12057,'trails',211,'Are dogs allowed on the Telephone Canyon Trail?','No, dogs are not permitted on this trail.','2025-03-27 23:06:14','2025-03-27 23:06:14'),(12058,'trails',211,'What is the geographical location of the Telephone Canyon Trail?','The trail is located at latitude 37.3048 and longitude -112.986.','2025-03-27 23:06:14','2025-03-27 23:06:14'),(12059,'trails',212,'What can I expect on the Angel\'s Landing Trail?','The Angel\'s Landing Trail offers an exhilarating hike with stunning views and scenic landscapes. The trail culminates at the summit, providing an incredible panoramic view that is truly unforgettable.','2025-03-27 23:06:23','2025-03-27 23:06:23'),(12060,'trails',212,'How do I access the Angel\'s Landing Trail?','You can reach the Angel\'s Landing Trail by starting at the West Rim Trail. It\'s a popular route that leads to this breathtaking destination.','2025-03-27 23:06:23','2025-03-27 23:06:23'),(12061,'trails',212,'What should I be aware of while hiking this trail?','Be mindful of exposure to heights and the presence of other hikers, especially past Scout Lookout. During non-summer months, you may encounter icy conditions, so it\'s important to avoid the summit if there\'s wet rock or storms nearby.','2025-03-27 23:06:23','2025-03-27 23:06:23'),(12062,'trails',212,'What are the temperature conditions like on the trail?','Expect significant temperature fluctuations while hiking. You\'ll experience intense heat on sections like Walter\'s Wiggle and cooler temperatures in shaded areas like Refrigerator Canyon.','2025-03-27 23:06:23','2025-03-27 23:06:23'),(12063,'trails',212,'Is there any assistance available on the exposed parts of the trail?','Yes, the trail features chains that are securely anchored to provide additional support in the exposed segments. Feel free to use them for added safety.','2025-03-27 23:06:23','2025-03-27 23:06:23'),(12064,'trails',212,'What is the difficulty level of this trail?','The trail is categorized as difficult, so it\'s best suited for experienced hikers looking for a challenge.','2025-03-27 23:06:23','2025-03-27 23:06:23'),(12065,'trails',212,'What are the elevation details of the Angel\'s Landing Trail?','The highest elevation on the trail reaches 5,338 feet, while the lowest elevation is also 5,338 feet, making it a relatively short but steep ascent of approximately 390 feet.','2025-03-27 23:06:23','2025-03-27 23:06:23'),(12066,'trails',212,'How long is the Angel\'s Landing Trail?','The trail is about 0.5 miles long and is designed as a point-to-point journey.','2025-03-27 23:06:23','2025-03-27 23:06:23'),(12067,'trails',212,'Are dogs allowed on the Angel\'s Landing Trail?','No, dogs are not permitted on this trail.','2025-03-27 23:06:23','2025-03-27 23:06:23'),(12068,'trails',212,'What unique features does the trail offer?','The Angel\'s Landing Trail is renowned for its breathtaking views, particularly at the summit, which is often described as a once-in-a-lifetime experience.','2025-03-27 23:06:23','2025-03-27 23:06:23'),(12069,'trails',212,'What is the latitude and longitude of the Angel\'s Landing Trail?','The coordinates for the Angel\'s Landing Trail are approximately 37.2749° N latitude and -112.951° W longitude.','2025-03-27 23:06:23','2025-03-27 23:06:23'),(12070,'trails',213,'What is The Grotto Trail like?','The Grotto Trail is a family-friendly hike that provides a pleasant walk with opportunities to appreciate the natural beauty and sounds of the Virgin River, making it perfect for a post-picnic stroll.','2025-03-27 23:06:32','2025-03-27 23:06:32'),(12071,'trails',213,'What is the difficulty level of The Grotto Trail?','This trail is classified as easy, making it accessible for hikers of all skill levels, particularly families.','2025-03-27 23:06:32','2025-03-27 23:06:32'),(12072,'trails',213,'What are the elevation details for The Grotto Trail?','The trail maintains a steady elevation of 4,287 feet, with a modest incline and decline of 22 feet and 70 feet respectively.','2025-03-27 23:06:32','2025-03-27 23:06:32'),(12073,'trails',213,'How long is The Grotto Trail?','The Grotto Trail stretches for 0.8 miles and is designed as a point-to-point trail.','2025-03-27 23:06:32','2025-03-27 23:06:32'),(12074,'trails',213,'What are the incline and decline details for the trail?','Hikers will experience a slight incline of 22 feet and a decline of 70 feet during their journey along the trail.','2025-03-27 23:06:32','2025-03-27 23:06:32'),(12075,'trails',213,'What types of features can be enjoyed along The Grotto Trail?','The trail boasts various features, including opportunities for birdwatching, enjoying fall colors, views of the river, and spotting wildflowers.','2025-03-27 23:06:32','2025-03-27 23:06:32'),(12076,'trails',213,'Are dogs allowed on The Grotto Trail?','No, dogs are not permitted on The Grotto Trail.','2025-03-27 23:06:32','2025-03-27 23:06:32'),(12077,'trails',213,'What is the average and maximum grade of The Grotto Trail?','The trail has an average grade of just 0.02%, with a maximum grade of 0.08%, indicating a smooth and easy walking experience.','2025-03-27 23:06:32','2025-03-27 23:06:32'),(12078,'trails',213,'What are the geographic coordinates of The Grotto Trail?','The trail is located at approximately 37.2602° latitude and -112.952° longitude.','2025-03-27 23:06:32','2025-03-27 23:06:32'),(12079,'trails',214,'What is the Upper Emerald Pools Trail like?','The Upper Emerald Pools Trail is a steep and challenging route that ultimately brings hikers to the picturesque Upper Emerald Pool. The trail traverses rocky outcrops and culminates at the base of a stunning sheer cliff.','2025-03-27 23:06:45','2025-03-27 23:06:45'),(12080,'trails',214,'Where can I access the Upper Emerald Pools Trail?','You can start the Upper Emerald Pools Trail from the Emerald Pools Trailhead located at Zion Lodge or from The Grotto. There are also connections to the trail via other paths.','2025-03-27 23:06:45','2025-03-27 23:06:45'),(12081,'trails',214,'What are the options for getting to the Upper Emerald Pools from Zion Lodge?','From Zion Lodge, hikers have the option to take the simpler Lower Emerald Pool Trail or the moderate Middle Emerald Pools Trail before accessing the Upper Emerald Pools Trail.','2025-03-27 23:06:45','2025-03-27 23:06:45'),(12082,'trails',214,'How do I get to the Upper Emerald Pools Trail from The Grotto?','From The Grotto, you can reach the Upper Emerald Pools Trail by first hiking the moderate 2-mile Kayenta Trail, which joins the Emerald Pools Trails.','2025-03-27 23:06:45','2025-03-27 23:06:45'),(12083,'trails',214,'How long is the Upper Emerald Pools Trail?','The trail spans 1 mile and is characterized by its steep incline and sandy terrain, making it an exhilarating experience.','2025-03-27 23:06:45','2025-03-27 23:06:45'),(12084,'trails',214,'What kind of views can I expect on the Upper Emerald Pools Trail?','Hikers will be treated to breathtaking views of majestic waterfalls, ecological landmarks, and the beautiful sandy shore at Upper Emerald Pool.','2025-03-27 23:06:45','2025-03-27 23:06:45'),(12085,'trails',214,'Are there restroom facilities and water filling stations available?','Yes, restrooms and water filling stations are conveniently located at both Zion Lodge and The Grotto.','2025-03-27 23:06:45','2025-03-27 23:06:45'),(12086,'trails',214,'What is the difficulty level of the Upper Emerald Pools Trail?','The trail is considered to be of intermediate difficulty, challenging enough for those looking for a rewarding hike.','2025-03-27 23:06:45','2025-03-27 23:06:45'),(12087,'trails',214,'What is the elevation profile of the Upper Emerald Pools Trail?','The trail has a highest elevation of 4,419 feet and a total incline of 356 feet, providing a great workout and scenic views.','2025-03-27 23:06:45','2025-03-27 23:06:45'),(12088,'trails',214,'Can I bring my dog on the Upper Emerald Pools Trail?','Yes, dogs are allowed on the trail, but they must be leashed at all times to ensure the safety of all hikers and wildlife.','2025-03-27 23:06:45','2025-03-27 23:06:45'),(12089,'trails',214,'What notable features should I look out for while hiking?','While hiking, you can enjoy features such as birding opportunities, seasonal fall colors, views of the creek, and the chance to see various wildlife and wildflowers along the way.','2025-03-27 23:06:45','2025-03-27 23:06:45'),(12090,'trails',215,'Is this trail suitable for families?','Absolutely! This trail is perfect for a quick out-and-back hike with the whole family. It\'s easy to navigate, making it ideal for hikers of all ages.','2025-03-27 23:06:54','2025-03-27 23:06:54'),(12091,'trails',215,'What are the highlights of the trail?','The trail offers stunning views and leads to some of Zion\'s most beautiful sites, including emerald-colored pools and small waterfalls. The surrounding pinyon-juniper woodlands add to the scenic experience.','2025-03-27 23:06:54','2025-03-27 23:06:54'),(12092,'trails',215,'How long is the hike?','The Middle Emerald Pools Trail extends 2.2 miles (3.5 km), making it a moderate hike that can be enjoyed by a variety of skill levels.','2025-03-27 23:06:54','2025-03-27 23:06:54'),(12093,'trails',215,'What type of trail is it?','This is a point-to-point trail with a well-maintained, paved path at its beginning. As you progress, you\'ll encounter unpaved sections that offer more of a challenge.','2025-03-27 23:06:54','2025-03-27 23:06:54'),(12094,'trails',215,'What should I expect in terms of elevation?','The trail starts at an elevation of 4,307 feet, with a slight incline of 128 feet offering expansive views of Zion Canyon.','2025-03-27 23:06:54','2025-03-27 23:06:54'),(12095,'trails',215,'Are there any precautions I should take?','Yes, please stay away from cliff edges and remember that swimming in the pools is not allowed as they are a critical water source for local wildlife.','2025-03-27 23:06:54','2025-03-27 23:06:54'),(12096,'trails',215,'Where can I find restrooms and water?','Restrooms and water filling stations are conveniently available at the nearby Zion Lodge, making it easy to hydrate and refresh during your outing.','2025-03-27 23:06:54','2025-03-27 23:06:54'),(12097,'trails',215,'Can pets accompany me on this trail?','The information regarding pets is currently unknown, so it\'s advisable to check specific regulations before bringing dogs along.','2025-03-27 23:06:54','2025-03-27 23:06:54'),(12098,'trails',215,'What features can I expect along the trail?','This trail is rich with natural features such as birding opportunities, beautiful fall colors, creeks, views, waterfalls, and wildflowers, enriching your hiking experience.','2025-03-27 23:06:54','2025-03-27 23:06:54'),(12099,'trails',215,'How do I access the trailhead?','The Emerald Pools Trailhead is located directly across from the Zion Lodge at shuttle stop #5. Follow the sidewalk across the Lodge Lawn to begin your adventure.','2025-03-27 23:06:54','2025-03-27 23:06:54'),(12100,'trails',216,'What is the route for hiking The Narrows - Wall Street to Big Springs?','The hike starts at Wall Street and takes you through the stunning narrowest part of the canyon, flanked by towering 2000-foot walls. You\'ll pass notable landmarks like Floating Rock and Hiccup Springs, concluding your journey at Big Springs waterfall.','2025-03-27 23:07:09','2025-03-27 23:07:09'),(12101,'trails',216,'What should I consider before hiking The Narrows?','Hiking The Narrows requires thorough planning for safety and requires sound judgment, as conditions can be challenging and occasionally hazardous. Always check in with the Zion park rangers at the visitor center for updates regarding water conditions, flash flood risks, and the weather forecast.','2025-03-27 23:07:09','2025-03-27 23:07:09'),(12102,'trails',216,'What direction should I take when I reach the end of The Narrows - Bottom Up Route?','Upon reaching the end of The Narrows - Bottom Up Route, make sure to go left to continue your adventure. Taking a right leads into the restricted Orderville Canyon, which is not allowed.','2025-03-27 23:07:09','2025-03-27 23:07:09'),(12103,'trails',216,'What is Wall Street in The Narrows?','Wall Street represents the narrowest section of The Narrows, transforming into a slot canyon where the towering walls can come within 20 feet of each other. It\'s a spectacular sight as you traverse through it.','2025-03-27 23:07:09','2025-03-27 23:07:09'),(12104,'trails',216,'What can I expect to see at Floating Rock?','About 0.5 miles from the Orderville fork, Floating Rock is a massive boulder that divides the river. You can easily navigate around it as you enjoy the scenic surroundings.','2025-03-27 23:07:09','2025-03-27 23:07:09'),(12105,'trails',216,'How do I find Hiccup Springs?','As you progress approximately 0.8 miles from the Orderville fork, listen for the gurgling sound of Hiccup Springs. While not prominently visible, you\'ll notice a small crack on the left side of the river.','2025-03-27 23:07:09','2025-03-27 23:07:09'),(12106,'trails',216,'What is the Boulder Pair?','Around 1.5 miles into the canyon, you\'ll encounter the Boulder Pair—two large boulders that block the river and signal the start of the boulder passage. Although the crossing is manageable, exercise caution as it is a lengthy trek back to the parking area.','2025-03-27 23:07:09','2025-03-27 23:07:09'),(12107,'trails',216,'Where is Sipping Turtle located?','Sipping Turtle can be found roughly 1.8 miles from the Orderville fork. It gets its name from the distinct gurgling sounds that you can hear as you approach.','2025-03-27 23:07:09','2025-03-27 23:07:09'),(12108,'trails',216,'What can I expect at Big Springs?','Big Springs is the final destination of your hike and offers a picturesque waterfall and a large boulder. It’s a perfect spot to rest, hydrate, and have a meal before making the return trip, especially if you don\'t have a permit to continue.','2025-03-27 23:07:09','2025-03-27 23:07:09'),(12109,'trails',216,'How difficult is the hike through The Narrows?','This hike is categorized as difficult, with elevation changes totaling about 700 feet up and 620 feet down, concluding at an elevation of 4630 feet.','2025-03-27 23:07:09','2025-03-27 23:07:09'),(12110,'trails',216,'What is the total length and type of the trail?','The trail spans 2.1 miles and is classified as a point-to-point hike, offering a unique experience through one of Zion\'s most remarkable landscapes.','2025-03-27 23:07:09','2025-03-27 23:07:09'),(12111,'trails',216,'Are dogs allowed on The Narrows trail?','No, dogs are not permitted on this trail, so make arrangements for them elsewhere.','2025-03-27 23:07:09','2025-03-27 23:07:09'),(12112,'trails',216,'What are the geographic coordinates of The Narrows?','The trail is located at approximately 37.3081° latitude and -112.947° longitude.','2025-03-27 23:07:09','2025-03-27 23:07:09'),(12113,'trails',217,'What is the Pine Creek Waterfall Trail like?','The Pine Creek Waterfall Trail offers an easy and flat hike alongside a picturesque creek, culminating in a beautiful waterfall perfect for summer swimming.','2025-03-27 23:07:16','2025-03-27 23:07:16'),(12114,'trails',217,'Is the trail suitable for families?','Yes, the trail is family-friendly, making it a great option for hikers of all ages.','2025-03-27 23:07:16','2025-03-27 23:07:16'),(12115,'trails',217,'How long is the Pine Creek Waterfall Trail?','The trail stretches for 0.4 miles, which makes it a short and accessible hike.','2025-03-27 23:07:16','2025-03-27 23:07:16'),(12116,'trails',217,'What can I expect at the waterfall?','Upon reaching the waterfall, you\'ll find an area ideal for swimming, especially enjoyable during the summer months.','2025-03-27 23:07:16','2025-03-27 23:07:16'),(12117,'trails',217,'What is the difficulty level of the trail?','The trail is rated as intermediate in difficulty, providing a manageable challenge for many hikers.','2025-03-27 23:07:16','2025-03-27 23:07:16'),(12118,'trails',217,'What are the elevation details of the trail?','The trail maintains a steady elevation, with both the highest and lowest points at 4,103 feet.','2025-03-27 23:07:16','2025-03-27 23:07:16'),(12119,'trails',217,'What type of trail is Pine Creek Waterfall Trail?','It is a point-to-point trail, leading directly to the waterfall.','2025-03-27 23:07:16','2025-03-27 23:07:16'),(12120,'trails',217,'What is the incline and decline of the trail?','The trail features a modest incline of 78 feet and a slight decline of 9 feet.','2025-03-27 23:07:16','2025-03-27 23:07:16'),(12121,'trails',217,'What is the average and maximum grade of the trail?','The average grade of the trail is approximately 0.05%, with a maximum grade of 0.11%.','2025-03-27 23:07:16','2025-03-27 23:07:16'),(12122,'trails',217,'Are dogs allowed on the trail?','It is currently unclear if dogs are permitted on the trail.','2025-03-27 23:07:16','2025-03-27 23:07:16'),(12123,'trails',217,'What are the geographic coordinates of the trail?','The trail is located at a latitude of 37.2166 and a longitude of -112.965.','2025-03-27 23:07:16','2025-03-27 23:07:16'),(12124,'trails',218,'What is the difficulty level of the hike?','The hike is rated as intermediate, making it suitable for those with some hiking experience.','2025-03-27 23:07:25','2025-03-27 23:07:25'),(12125,'trails',218,'What is the highest elevation reached on the trail?','Hikers will reach a maximum elevation of 5,320 feet.','2025-03-27 23:07:25','2025-03-27 23:07:25'),(12126,'trails',218,'What is the lowest elevation on the trail?','The trail\'s lowest elevation is also 5,320 feet, meaning the hike is relatively flat.','2025-03-27 23:07:25','2025-03-27 23:07:25'),(12127,'trails',218,'How long is the trail?','The total length of the trail is 1.1 miles, providing a compact but rewarding hike.','2025-03-27 23:07:25','2025-03-27 23:07:25'),(12128,'trails',218,'What type of trail is this?','This is a point-to-point trail, leading you from one endpoint to another.','2025-03-27 23:07:25','2025-03-27 23:07:25'),(12129,'trails',218,'What is the incline and decline on this hike?','The trail features an incline of 563 feet, with a minimal decline of just 17 feet.','2025-03-27 23:07:25','2025-03-27 23:07:25'),(12130,'trails',218,'What is the average grade of the trail?','The average grade of the trail is 0.10%, which indicates a gentle slope overall.','2025-03-27 23:07:25','2025-03-27 23:07:25'),(12131,'trails',218,'What is the maximum grade of the trail?','The steepest section of the trail reaches a maximum grade of 0.23%, but it remains manageable.','2025-03-27 23:07:25','2025-03-27 23:07:25'),(12132,'trails',218,'What will I encounter along the trail?','Hikers will find themselves navigating through sandstone rock and sandy washes, accompanied by numerous small pools of water.','2025-03-27 23:07:25','2025-03-27 23:07:25'),(12133,'trails',218,'What are the geographical coordinates of the trail?','The trail is located at a latitude of 37.2219 and a longitude of -112.915.','2025-03-27 23:07:25','2025-03-27 23:07:25'),(12134,'trails',219,'What is the Sand Bench Trail?','The Sand Bench Trail is a 7.6-mile (12.2 km) roundtrip hike that follows the Virgin River and traverses an ancient rockfall area, providing a stunning view of historical geological formations.','2025-03-27 23:07:33','2025-03-27 23:07:33'),(12135,'trails',219,'How did the Virgin River shape this area?','About 8,000 years ago, a landslide dammed the Virgin River, creating a lake that extended toward Angels Landing. This unique history adds to the trail\'s significance.','2025-03-27 23:07:33','2025-03-27 23:07:33'),(12136,'trails',219,'What should I expect in terms of trail conditions?','The trail features deep sand and lacks shade, which can make progress slower. It\'s important to carry enough water and be mentally prepared for the hike.','2025-03-27 23:07:33','2025-03-27 23:07:33'),(12137,'trails',219,'Where can I find facilities like water and restrooms?','Water and restroom facilities are available at The Zion Lodge, making it a convenient stop during your hike.','2025-03-27 23:07:33','2025-03-27 23:07:33'),(12138,'trails',219,'How do I access the Sand Bench Trail?','You can access the trail mainly from the Emerald Pools Trailhead at Zion Lodge (shuttle stop #5). Alternatively, you can start from the Court of the Patriarchs (shuttle stop #4) by crossing the road and following the sandy trail.','2025-03-27 23:07:34','2025-03-27 23:07:34'),(12139,'trails',219,'Can I hike a shorter version of the trail?','Yes! If you choose to hike just the loop portion, the roundtrip distance is closer to 5 miles (8 km). You have the option to hike up-canyon towards Zion Lodge or back towards the Court of the Patriarchs.','2025-03-27 23:07:34','2025-03-27 23:07:34'),(12140,'trails',219,'Is the Sand Bench Trail open during winter?','Yes, winter hiking is an option, but caution is advised due to possible ice patches along the trail.','2025-03-27 23:07:34','2025-03-27 23:07:34'),(12141,'trails',219,'Are there any restrictions on pets on the trail?','Dogs are not permitted on the Sand Bench Trail, so plan your hike accordingly if you have a pet.','2025-03-27 23:07:34','2025-03-27 23:07:34'),(12142,'trails',219,'What is the trail\'s difficulty level?','The Sand Bench Trail is considered intermediate in difficulty, making it suitable for those who are used to hiking.','2025-03-27 23:07:34','2025-03-27 23:07:34'),(12143,'trails',219,'What features should I look out for on this trail?','As you hike, keep an eye out for diverse wildlife, beautiful wildflowers, and captivating views of the surrounding landscape, especially during the fall season.','2025-03-27 23:07:34','2025-03-27 23:07:34'),(12144,'trails',220,'What is the Left Fork (The Subway) trail?','The Left Fork (The Subway) trail is a stunning hiking route featuring a unique bottom-up experience. It allows adventurous hikers to explore its natural beauty through a captivating landscape.','2025-03-27 23:07:46','2025-03-27 23:07:46'),(12145,'trails',220,'Do I need a permit to hike the Left Fork (The Subway) trail?','Yes, permits are required to access the Left Fork (The Subway) from either direction. For more information on obtaining a permit, please visit nps.gov/zion/planyourvisit.','2025-03-27 23:07:46','2025-03-27 23:07:46'),(12146,'trails',220,'What is the difficulty level of the trail?','The trail is rated as difficult, making it suitable for experienced hikers looking for a challenge.','2025-03-27 23:07:46','2025-03-27 23:07:46'),(12147,'trails',220,'What are the highest and lowest elevations on the trail?','The highest and lowest elevations on the trail are both 4665 feet, providing a mostly flat hiking experience.','2025-03-27 23:07:46','2025-03-27 23:07:46'),(12148,'trails',220,'How long is the Left Fork (The Subway) trail?','The trail spans approximately 3.9 miles in a point-to-point format, making it a manageable hike for many.','2025-03-27 23:07:46','2025-03-27 23:07:46'),(12149,'trails',220,'What is the elevation gain and loss on the trail?','Hikers will experience an elevation gain of 1218 feet and a decline of 919 feet throughout the hike.','2025-03-27 23:07:46','2025-03-27 23:07:46'),(12150,'trails',220,'What is the average and maximum grade of the trail?','The average grade of the trail is about 0.10%, while the maximum grade reaches up to 1.66%, indicating a relatively gradual slope.','2025-03-27 23:07:46','2025-03-27 23:07:46'),(12151,'trails',220,'What features can I expect to see on the trail?','This trail offers a variety of features including birding opportunities, river and creek views, swimming spots, beautiful vistas, waterfalls, and diverse wildlife and wildflowers.','2025-03-27 23:07:46','2025-03-27 23:07:46'),(12152,'trails',220,'Are dogs allowed on the Left Fork (The Subway) trail?','No, dogs are not permitted on this trail, so plan accordingly if you\'re traveling with pets.','2025-03-27 23:07:46','2025-03-27 23:07:46'),(12153,'trails',220,'What are the latitude and longitude coordinates of the trail?','The coordinates for the Left Fork (The Subway) trail are approximately 37.2848° latitude and -113.096° longitude.','2025-03-27 23:07:46','2025-03-27 23:07:46'),(12154,'trails',221,'What can I expect to see at the end of the Ariel Point Trail?','The trail culminates at Ariel Point, a rocky outcrop with stunning, unobstructed views, considered one of the finest viewpoints in the area.','2025-03-27 23:07:56','2025-03-27 23:07:56'),(12155,'trails',221,'What is the terrain like on the Ariel Point Trail?','The trail primarily traverses through sparse trees and occasional meadows, following an old logging road that may require some navigation skills due to its fading path.','2025-03-27 23:07:56','2025-03-27 23:07:56'),(12156,'trails',221,'Is navigating the trail easy or difficult?','While the trail is categorized as easy to intermediate, hikers may need to use GPS tools via the Hiking Project mobile app for navigation, especially as the trail becomes less distinct.','2025-03-27 23:07:56','2025-03-27 23:07:56'),(12157,'trails',221,'What should I do if I lose the trail?','If you find the trail hard to follow, maintain your position on the highest point of the ridgeline heading south towards the canyon rim, where you might spot old trail markers, although they may be sparse.','2025-03-27 23:07:56','2025-03-27 23:07:56'),(12158,'trails',221,'How long is the Ariel Point Trail?','The trail stretches for 3.2 miles as an out-and-back route.','2025-03-27 23:07:56','2025-03-27 23:07:56'),(12159,'trails',221,'What is the elevation range of the Ariel Point Trail?','The trail starts and finishes at the same elevation of 7,941 feet, with a slight climb of 33 feet and a descent of 319 feet along the way.','2025-03-27 23:07:56','2025-03-27 23:07:56'),(12160,'trails',221,'What is the average and maximum grade of the trail?','The average grade of the trail is a mild 0.02%, with portions reaching a maximum grade of 0.09%.','2025-03-27 23:07:56','2025-03-27 23:07:56'),(12161,'trails',221,'Are dogs allowed on the Ariel Point Trail?','Unfortunately, dogs are not permitted on this trail.','2025-03-27 23:07:56','2025-03-27 23:07:56'),(12162,'trails',221,'What features can I expect while hiking the trail?','Apart from breathtaking views at the endpoint, hikers will enjoy a relatively peaceful hike through a less-frequented forested area.','2025-03-27 23:07:56','2025-03-27 23:07:56'),(12163,'trails',221,'Where does the Ariel Point Trail start?','You begin your hike at the junction with the Komo Point Trail, heading south on the Ariel Point Trail, making sure to follow the old roadbed.','2025-03-27 23:07:56','2025-03-27 23:07:56'),(12164,'trails',221,'What difficulties might I face on this trail?','While the trail is generally manageable, its fading nature can pose challenges in navigation, so using a GPS app is advisable.','2025-03-27 23:07:56','2025-03-27 23:07:56'),(12165,'trails',222,'What is the best way to access the Beamer Trail?','Begin your hike on the Beamer Trail by walking down to the river, then head up-canyon. The route is primarily clear, with minor obstructions caused by Dox Sandstone in a few spots.','2025-03-27 23:08:07','2025-03-27 23:08:07'),(12166,'trails',222,'What kind of terrain can hikers expect on the Beamer Trail?','Initially, hikers will encounter dense riparian vegetation near the shore, which gradually transitions to rocky slopes as you approach Palisades Canyon. After this point, the terrain becomes challenging, featuring narrow, exposed ledges along high cliffs.','2025-03-27 23:08:07','2025-03-27 23:08:07'),(12167,'trails',222,'What should hikers be cautious about on the Beamer Trail?','This trail segment includes sections that are quite exposed and may pose difficulties for those with a fear of heights. It\'s essential to tread carefully in these narrow areas overlooking steep drops.','2025-03-27 23:08:07','2025-03-27 23:08:07'),(12168,'trails',222,'What is the elevation change like on the trail?','Hikers will ascend approximately 300 vertical feet up the talus to reach the top of the Tapeats Sandstone, which provides access to continue the trail towards the Little Colorado River.','2025-03-27 23:08:07','2025-03-27 23:08:07'),(12169,'trails',222,'How well-marked is the Beamer Trail?','The Beamer Trail is generally well-defined, but you might experience some route finding challenges when crossing drainages. Be prepared to navigate some tricky sections.','2025-03-27 23:08:07','2025-03-27 23:08:07'),(12170,'trails',222,'Are there any scenic views along the Beamer Trail?','Yes, the trail offers breathtaking views of the surrounding landscape, especially as it runs along the Tapeats rim towards the Little Colorado River.','2025-03-27 23:08:07','2025-03-27 23:08:07'),(12171,'trails',222,'What is the total length and difficulty of the Beamer Trail?','The Beamer Trail spans approximately 9.9 miles and is considered difficult due to its demanding nature and the exposed terrain.','2025-03-27 23:08:07','2025-03-27 23:08:07'),(12172,'trails',222,'What are the elevation statistics for the trail?','The highest elevation reached on this trail is 2,685 feet, and the lowest elevation is also at 2,685 feet, with a total incline of 1,692 feet and a decline of 1,650 feet.','2025-03-27 23:08:07','2025-03-27 23:08:07'),(12173,'trails',222,'Are pets allowed on the Beamer Trail?','No, dogs are not permitted on the Beamer Trail.','2025-03-27 23:08:07','2025-03-27 23:08:07'),(12174,'trails',222,'What should hikers do if they encounter historic artifacts on the trail?','If you come across any remnants of mining or historical activities, kindly leave them in place for others to appreciate and for historians to study, as it’s important to preserve these narratives.','2025-03-27 23:08:07','2025-03-27 23:08:07'),(12175,'trails',223,'What is the overall difficulty level of the Bill Hall Trail?','The Bill Hall Trail is categorized as difficult, making it best suited for experienced hikers.','2025-03-27 23:08:19','2025-03-27 23:08:19'),(12176,'trails',223,'How long is the Bill Hall Trail?','The trail stretches for 2.5 miles and offers a direct route compared to other trails.','2025-03-27 23:08:19','2025-03-27 23:08:19'),(12177,'trails',223,'What types of features can hikers expect to see along the trail?','Hikers can enjoy stunning views, birdwatching opportunities, wildflowers, and potential wildlife sightings.','2025-03-27 23:08:19','2025-03-27 23:08:19'),(12178,'trails',223,'What is the starting elevation of the Bill Hall Trail?','The trail begins at an elevation of 5,433 feet.','2025-03-27 23:08:19','2025-03-27 23:08:19'),(12179,'trails',223,'What is the steepest section of the trail like?','The trail includes steep switchbacks that allow you to navigate the Coconino Sandstone as you approach the Esplanade.','2025-03-27 23:08:19','2025-03-27 23:08:19'),(12180,'trails',223,'Is there any scrambling involved on the Bill Hall Trail?','Yes, there is a 15-foot scramble that may require a short rope to assist in lowering packs.','2025-03-27 23:08:19','2025-03-27 23:08:19'),(12181,'trails',223,'Can dogs accompany hikers on the Bill Hall Trail?','No, dogs are not permitted on the Bill Hall Trail.','2025-03-27 23:08:19','2025-03-27 23:08:19'),(12182,'trails',223,'What historical significance does the trail hold?','The trail is named in honor of Bill Hall, a former park ranger who tragically lost his life in the line of duty.','2025-03-27 23:08:19','2025-03-27 23:08:19'),(12183,'trails',223,'What are the trail\'s incline and decline measurements?','The trail features an incline of 174 feet and a decline of 1,785 feet.','2025-03-27 23:08:19','2025-03-27 23:08:19'),(12184,'trails',223,'Are there alternative trails to reach the Esplanade?','Yes, the Thunder River Trail is a gentler, longer alternative that serves as a historical access point but adds about 2.5 miles to the hike.','2025-03-27 23:08:19','2025-03-27 23:08:19'),(12185,'trails',223,'What is the average and maximum grade of the trail?','The trail has an average grade of 0.15% and reaches a maximum grade of 0.56%.','2025-03-27 23:08:19','2025-03-27 23:08:19'),(12186,'trails',223,'What is the orientation of the Bill Hall Trail?','The trail is a point-to-point route leading hikers from the rim to the Esplanade.','2025-03-27 23:08:19','2025-03-27 23:08:19'),(12187,'trails',223,'What are the geographical coordinates of the trail?','The Bill Hall Trail is located at a latitude of 36.4347 and a longitude of -112.43.','2025-03-27 23:08:19','2025-03-27 23:08:19'),(12188,'trails',224,'Where does the Clear Creek Trail begin?','The Clear Creek Trail starts approximately one mile north of Phantom Ranch on the North Kaibab Trail, marked by a wooden sign.','2025-03-27 23:08:31','2025-03-27 23:08:31'),(12189,'trails',224,'What is the elevation gain on the Clear Creek Trail?','The trail features an incline of 2,716 feet, taking hikers up to a maximum elevation of 2,651 feet.','2025-03-27 23:08:31','2025-03-27 23:08:31'),(12190,'trails',224,'What kind of terrain can hikers expect on the Clear Creek Trail?','Hikers will experience a mix of switchbacks, traversing along the Tonto Platform, crossing minor drainages, and hiking through areas with striking geological features like the Great Unconformity and the orange Hakatai Shale.','2025-03-27 23:08:31','2025-03-27 23:08:31'),(12191,'trails',224,'Are there any notable viewpoints on the trail?','Yes, Phantom Overlook provides a spectacular view of Phantom Ranch below and is a great spot for a rest with stone benches available.','2025-03-27 23:08:31','2025-03-27 23:08:31'),(12192,'trails',224,'How long is the Clear Creek Trail?','The Clear Creek Trail spans 8.8 miles from start to finish.','2025-03-27 23:08:31','2025-03-27 23:08:31'),(12193,'trails',224,'What is the difficulty level of the Clear Creek Trail?','This trail is classified as intermediate, making it suitable for those with some hiking experience.','2025-03-27 23:08:31','2025-03-27 23:08:31'),(12194,'trails',224,'Can hikers camp along the Clear Creek Trail?','Yes, many backpackers set up camp at various impacted sites located just downstream from the confluence with Clear Creek.','2025-03-27 23:08:31','2025-03-27 23:08:31'),(12195,'trails',224,'Is it possible to hike to the Colorado River from the trail?','Yes, there is a faint route leading downstream to the east fork of Clear Creek, but it involves scrambling and multiple creek crossings, as well as a challenging fifteen-foot down climb about a quarter mile from the river.','2025-03-27 23:08:31','2025-03-27 23:08:31'),(12196,'trails',224,'Can hikers visit Cheyava Falls from the Clear Creek Trail?','Absolutely! Many hikers take a day hike up Clear Creek toward Cheyava Falls, which is about five miles one way and showcases the tallest seasonal waterfall in the park, but it only flows in the spring after winters with ample snowfall.','2025-03-27 23:08:31','2025-03-27 23:08:31'),(12197,'trails',224,'What wildlife and natural features can hikers expect to see on the trail?','The trail offers opportunities to view wildlife and features such as rivers, creeks, and beautiful vistas along the route.','2025-03-27 23:08:31','2025-03-27 23:08:31'),(12198,'trails',224,'Are dogs allowed on the Clear Creek Trail?','It is unclear if dogs are permitted on the trail.','2025-03-27 23:08:31','2025-03-27 23:08:31'),(12199,'trails',224,'What is the average and maximum grade of the Clear Creek Trail?','The trail has an average grade of 0.10% and a maximum grade of 0.87%.','2025-03-27 23:08:31','2025-03-27 23:08:31'),(12200,'trails',225,'What is Cliff Springs Trail?','Cliff Springs Trail is a scenic forested path that leads to a cliffside spring, located near Cape Royal.','2025-03-27 23:08:39','2025-03-27 23:08:39'),(12201,'trails',225,'Where does the trailhead start?','The trailhead is conveniently located directly across from a small pullout, just 0.3 miles (0.5 km) down the road from Cape Royal.','2025-03-27 23:08:39','2025-03-27 23:08:39'),(12202,'trails',225,'What can I expect while hiking the trail?','As you hike, you\'ll enjoy a meandering path through a wooded ravine, ultimately reaching a chest-high boulder that sits beneath a large overhang where the spring is located.','2025-03-27 23:08:39','2025-03-27 23:08:39'),(12203,'trails',225,'What is the difficulty level of the trail?','The trail is classified as intermediate in difficulty.','2025-03-27 23:08:39','2025-03-27 23:08:39'),(12204,'trails',225,'What are the highest and lowest elevations on the trail?','The trail has a consistent elevation of 7583 feet, with no significant changes in height.','2025-03-27 23:08:39','2025-03-27 23:08:39'),(12205,'trails',225,'How long is the Cliff Springs Trail?','The trail stretches for 0.4 miles in a point-to-point layout.','2025-03-27 23:08:39','2025-03-27 23:08:39'),(12206,'trails',225,'What is the total incline and decline on the trail?','Hikers will experience a total incline of 44 feet and a decline of 179 feet.','2025-03-27 23:08:39','2025-03-27 23:08:39'),(12207,'trails',225,'What is the average and maximum grade of the trail?','The average grade is quite gentle at 0.10%, with a maximum steepness of 0.21%.','2025-03-27 23:08:39','2025-03-27 23:08:39'),(12208,'trails',225,'What features can I see along the trail?','Hiking along the Cliff Springs Trail offers beautiful views, the sights and sounds of a river or creek, and the chance to see wildflowers in bloom.','2025-03-27 23:08:39','2025-03-27 23:08:39'),(12209,'trails',225,'Are pets allowed on the trail?','Unfortunately, dogs are not permitted on the Cliff Springs Trail.','2025-03-27 23:08:39','2025-03-27 23:08:39'),(12210,'trails',225,'What are the geographical coordinates of Cliff Springs?','The trail is located at a latitude of 36.1246 and a longitude of -111.948.','2025-03-27 23:08:39','2025-03-27 23:08:39'),(12211,'trails',226,'What is the Deer Creek trail known for?','Deer Creek trail is famous for its fun slot canyon sections, breathtaking views of a waterfall, and its significance as a site of substantial water flow since prehistoric times.','2025-03-27 23:08:47','2025-03-27 23:08:47'),(12212,'trails',226,'Is the Deer Creek trail suitable for families?','Yes, the trail is family-friendly but is best suited for older kids who can navigate the slot canyon safely with supervision.','2025-03-27 23:08:47','2025-03-27 23:08:47'),(12213,'trails',226,'How accessible is the Deer Creek trail?','The trail is conveniently accessible for those arriving via raft, making it a great choice for water sports enthusiasts.','2025-03-27 23:08:47','2025-03-27 23:08:47'),(12214,'trails',226,'What is the difficulty level of the Deer Creek trail?','The trail is classified as intermediate to difficult, so hikers should be prepared for some challenges.','2025-03-27 23:08:47','2025-03-27 23:08:47'),(12215,'trails',226,'What are the elevation details of Deer Creek trail?','The highest and lowest elevation along the trail is 1964 feet, with a small incline of 81 feet and a significant decline of 1882 feet.','2025-03-27 23:08:47','2025-03-27 23:08:47'),(12216,'trails',226,'How long is the Deer Creek trail?','The trail spans a length of 3.2 miles and follows a point-to-point configuration.','2025-03-27 23:08:47','2025-03-27 23:08:47'),(12217,'trails',226,'What can hikers expect in terms of trail features?','Hikers will enjoy opportunities for bird watching, views of the river and creek, stunning scenery, a waterfall, and encounters with wildflowers and wildlife.','2025-03-27 23:08:47','2025-03-27 23:08:47'),(12218,'trails',226,'Are dogs allowed on the Deer Creek trail?','No, pets are not permitted on the Deer Creek trail.','2025-03-27 23:08:47','2025-03-27 23:08:47'),(12219,'trails',226,'What are the latitude and longitude coordinates of the Deer Creek trail?','The trail is located at a latitude of 36.4011 and a longitude of -112.476.','2025-03-27 23:08:47','2025-03-27 23:08:47'),(12220,'trails',227,'What is the overall difficulty of the Escalante Route from Tanner to Cardenas?','This trail is considered very difficult, demanding both physical endurance and careful navigation.','2025-03-27 23:08:59','2025-03-27 23:08:59'),(12221,'trails',227,'What is the total length of the Escalante Route?','The route stretches for approximately 11.3 miles from Tanner to Cardenas.','2025-03-27 23:08:59','2025-03-27 23:08:59'),(12222,'trails',227,'What is the highest elevation of the trail?','The peak elevation along the trail reaches 2,583 feet.','2025-03-27 23:08:59','2025-03-27 23:08:59'),(12223,'trails',227,'What kind of terrain can I expect while hiking this route?','Hikers will navigate through shallow gullies, dry creek beds, rocky ledges, and a significant climb up Dox Hill.','2025-03-27 23:08:59','2025-03-27 23:08:59'),(12224,'trails',227,'Is there reliable water on the route?','Cardenas Creek is nearly always dry, making it essential to carry enough water until you reach the Colorado River at Escalante Creek.','2025-03-27 23:08:59','2025-03-27 23:08:59'),(12225,'trails',227,'What should I be cautious of during my hike?','Caution is advised in areas where missteps could occur, especially while traversing the ridge north of Escalante Creek and navigating ledges near Papago Creek.','2025-03-27 23:08:59','2025-03-27 23:08:59'),(12226,'trails',227,'Are there any notable scenic views along the trail?','Yes, hikers are rewarded with excellent views from the ridge after climbing Dox Hill and throughout the route.','2025-03-27 23:08:59','2025-03-27 23:08:59'),(12227,'trails',227,'What type of trail surfaces will I encounter?','The trail features a mix of sandy and rocky surfaces, especially along the beach leading to Papago Creek.','2025-03-27 23:08:59','2025-03-27 23:08:59'),(12228,'trails',227,'What options do I have upon reaching Hance Rapids?','You can either continue west via the East Tonto Trail or take the New Hance Trail up to the rim.','2025-03-27 23:08:59','2025-03-27 23:08:59'),(12229,'trails',227,'Are dogs allowed on the Escalante Route?','No, dogs are not permitted on this trail.','2025-03-27 23:08:59','2025-03-27 23:08:59'),(12230,'trails',227,'What wildlife and natural features might I see while hiking?','Expect opportunities for birdwatching, stunning views, wildlife sightings, and a variety of wildflowers along the route.','2025-03-27 23:08:59','2025-03-27 23:08:59'),(12231,'trails',227,'What type of trail is the Escalante Route classified as?','The Escalante Route is categorized as a point-to-point trail.','2025-03-27 23:08:59','2025-03-27 23:08:59'),(12232,'trails',227,'What is the average and maximum grade of the trail?','The average grade is about 0.07%, with steep sections reaching a maximum of 0.62%.','2025-03-27 23:08:59','2025-03-27 23:08:59'),(12233,'trails',228,'What is the Francois Matthes Trail?','The Francois Matthes Trail is an isolated former logging road that offers a unique hiking experience, with views of Zoroaster Temple and Wotans Throne, along with the chance to see Cheyava Falls and the Clear Creek drainage.','2025-03-27 23:09:09','2025-03-27 23:09:09'),(12234,'trails',228,'What type of terrain can I expect on the Francois Matthes Trail?','The trail features a broad ridge that descends steadily through scattered pine trees and areas affected by wildfire, making for a diverse and scenic landscape.','2025-03-27 23:09:09','2025-03-27 23:09:09'),(12235,'trails',228,'How long is the Francois Matthes Trail?','The trail spans 4.8 miles in length and is designed as a point-to-point hike.','2025-03-27 23:09:09','2025-03-27 23:09:09'),(12236,'trails',228,'What is the difficulty level of this trail?','The Francois Matthes Trail is rated as easy, making it accessible for various skill levels of hikers.','2025-03-27 23:09:09','2025-03-27 23:09:09'),(12237,'trails',228,'What elevation changes will I encounter on the hike?','The trail has a highest elevation of 8,013 feet and a lowest elevation of the same height, featuring a gentle incline of just 39 feet and a decline of 442 feet.','2025-03-27 23:09:09','2025-03-27 23:09:09'),(12238,'trails',228,'Are there any significant viewpoints on the trail?','Yes, hikers can enjoy stunning views of Zoroaster Temple and Wotans Throne, though they are partially obstructed by brush. Additionally, Cheyava Falls and the Clear Creek drainage are visible from certain points.','2025-03-27 23:09:09','2025-03-27 23:09:09'),(12239,'trails',228,'Are dogs allowed on the Francois Matthes Trail?','No, dogs are not permitted on this trail.','2025-03-27 23:09:09','2025-03-27 23:09:09'),(12240,'trails',228,'What is the historical significance of the trail\'s name?','The trail is named after Francois E. Matthes, a geologist and skilled topographical mapper whose work contributed significantly to glacial geology theories and aided in the establishment of many protected areas in the U.S. as National Parks.','2025-03-27 23:09:09','2025-03-27 23:09:09'),(12241,'trails',228,'How busy is the Francois Matthes Trail?','This trail is infrequently used, providing hikers with opportunities for solitude during their trek.','2025-03-27 23:09:09','2025-03-27 23:09:09'),(12242,'trails',229,'What is the trail type for the Ken Patrick Trail?','The Ken Patrick Trail is a point-to-point trail, offering a scenic hike from Point Imperial to the North Kaibab Trailhead.','2025-03-27 23:09:19','2025-03-27 23:09:19'),(12243,'trails',229,'What is the total length of the Ken Patrick Trail?','This trail spans approximately 9.9 miles.','2025-03-27 23:09:19','2025-03-27 23:09:19'),(12244,'trails',229,'What level of difficulty does the Ken Patrick Trail have?','The trail is categorized as intermediate, suited for those with moderate hiking experience.','2025-03-27 23:09:19','2025-03-27 23:09:19'),(12245,'trails',229,'What are the elevation details for the Ken Patrick Trail?','The trail maintains a consistent highest and lowest elevation of 8110 feet, with a total elevation gain of 1872 feet and a decline of 1327 feet.','2025-03-27 23:09:19','2025-03-27 23:09:19'),(12246,'trails',229,'Are dogs allowed on the Ken Patrick Trail?','No, dogs are not permitted on this trail.','2025-03-27 23:09:19','2025-03-27 23:09:19'),(12247,'trails',229,'What kind of scenic views can hikers expect on the trail?','Hikers will be treated to stunning views into the canyon, including sights of upper Bright Angel Canyon, Mount Hayden, Marble Canyon, and the Nankoweap Creek basin.','2025-03-27 23:09:19','2025-03-27 23:09:19'),(12248,'trails',229,'What should hikers be aware of concerning trail conditions?','While the trail is mainly easy to follow, especially in its first half, the latter part may require careful navigation due to dense undergrowth and some less defined sections.','2025-03-27 23:09:19','2025-03-27 23:09:19'),(12249,'trails',229,'What should I know about wildlife or trail companions like mules?','This trail is also used by mules, particularly in the first section near the North Kaibab Trailhead, so it\'s important to be courteous and be aware of their droppings.','2025-03-27 23:09:19','2025-03-27 23:09:19'),(12250,'trails',229,'Can you tell me about the historical significance of the Ken Patrick Trail?','The trail is named after Kenneth C. Patrick, a Grand Canyon ranger who served in the 1960s and was tragically killed in the line of duty in 1973.','2025-03-27 23:09:19','2025-03-27 23:09:19'),(12251,'trails',229,'What unique features or highlights can be found along the trail?','Hikers can enjoy features like fall colors, wildflowers, and dramatic views throughout the hike, particularly after crossing the Cape Royal Road.','2025-03-27 23:09:19','2025-03-27 23:09:19'),(12252,'trails',229,'What is the recommended access point for starting the trail?','Hikers should begin the Ken Patrick Trail at the mule stable area located at the far end of the North Kaibab trailhead parking lot.','2025-03-27 23:09:19','2025-03-27 23:09:19'),(12253,'trails',230,'What is the starting point for the Komo Point Trail?','The Komo Point Trail begins at the Cape Royal Road on the North Rim.','2025-03-27 23:09:27','2025-03-27 23:09:27'),(12254,'trails',230,'How steep is the Komo Point Trail?','The trail has a gentle and steady descent, making it suitable for hikers at an easy to intermediate level.','2025-03-27 23:09:27','2025-03-27 23:09:27'),(12255,'trails',230,'What is the total length of the Komo Point Trail?','The trail spans approximately 5.2 miles as a point-to-point hike.','2025-03-27 23:09:27','2025-03-27 23:09:27'),(12256,'trails',230,'What elevations can hikers expect on the Komo Point Trail?','The trail starts and ends at an elevation of 8058 feet.','2025-03-27 23:09:27','2025-03-27 23:09:27'),(12257,'trails',230,'What challenges might hikers face on the trail?','Hikers may encounter downed trees, a faint trail that can be difficult to follow, and numerous burned-out tree remains from a past wildfire.','2025-03-27 23:09:27','2025-03-27 23:09:27'),(12258,'trails',230,'Are there any significant landmarks along the trail?','About two-thirds of the way, a fork appears: the southern path leads to Ariel Point, while the western route continues to the end of the Komo Point Trail. Look for a large faded yellow ball at the rocky rim; it served as a mapping reference in the past.','2025-03-27 23:09:27','2025-03-27 23:09:27'),(12259,'trails',230,'What should hikers do if they are worried about navigation?','If you\'re concerned about staying on the right path, consider using the Hiking Project mobile app to assist with route finding.','2025-03-27 23:09:27','2025-03-27 23:09:27'),(12260,'trails',230,'What are the incline and decline details for this hike?','The hike features a slight incline of 20 feet and a decline of 461 feet.','2025-03-27 23:09:27','2025-03-27 23:09:27'),(12261,'trails',230,'What features can hikers enjoy on the Komo Point Trail?','This trail offers beautiful views, especially at the overlook point.','2025-03-27 23:09:27','2025-03-27 23:09:27'),(12262,'trails',230,'Are dogs allowed on the Komo Point Trail?','No, dogs are not permitted on this trail.','2025-03-27 23:09:28','2025-03-27 23:09:28'),(12263,'trails',230,'What type of trail is the Komo Point Trail considered?','The Komo Point Trail is a point-to-point trail.','2025-03-27 23:09:28','2025-03-27 23:09:28'),(12264,'trails',230,'What are the coordinates for the Komo Point Trail?','The trail is located at latitude 36.2305 and longitude -111.983.','2025-03-27 23:09:28','2025-03-27 23:09:28'),(12265,'trails',230,'How does the average grade of the trail compare to its maximum grade?','The trail has an average grade of 0.02%, while the maximum steepness can reach up to 0.05%.','2025-03-27 23:09:28','2025-03-27 23:09:28'),(12266,'trails',231,'Where is the North Bass Trailhead located?','The North Bass Trailhead is situated at Swamp Point, which can be accessed at the end of Swamp Ridge Road. It\'s also possible to reach it from North Rim Village by navigating through the Point Sublime and Kanabownits Roads, although the westward approach via Forest Service Roads is more straightforward.','2025-03-27 23:09:38','2025-03-27 23:09:38'),(12267,'trails',231,'What is the trail\'s general direction and distance?','The North Bass Trail extends approximately 11.9 miles in a point-to-point format, starting from Swamp Point and leading down to the Colorado River, showcasing a variety of landscapes along the way.','2025-03-27 23:09:38','2025-03-27 23:09:38'),(12268,'trails',231,'What can I expect in terms of elevation changes on the trail?','Hikers will experience significant elevation changes, with the highest point reaching 2,233 feet and a total decline of about 6,300 feet throughout the hike. Prepare for a climb of approximately 700 feet towards the end of the trail.','2025-03-27 23:09:38','2025-03-27 23:09:38'),(12269,'trails',231,'How difficult is the North Bass Trail?','The North Bass Trail is classified as very difficult due to its steep and rocky terrain, challenging conditions, and extensive elevation changes.','2025-03-27 23:09:38','2025-03-27 23:09:38'),(12270,'trails',231,'What are the main features of this trail?','This trail is rich in natural beauty, offering opportunities for birding, fall colors, views of the river, swimming spots, breathtaking waterfalls, vibrant wildflowers, and chances to observe wildlife.','2025-03-27 23:09:38','2025-03-27 23:09:38'),(12271,'trails',231,'Is it necessary to have a map for this hike?','Yes, possessing a North Kaibab National Forest map is highly recommended for navigation, as the trail can be quite remote and less marked.','2025-03-27 23:09:38','2025-03-27 23:09:38'),(12272,'trails',231,'Are dogs allowed on the North Bass Trail?','The policy regarding dogs on the North Bass Trail is currently unknown. It would be prudent to check local regulations before considering taking your pet.','2025-03-27 23:09:38','2025-03-27 23:09:38');
INSERT INTO `openai_prompts` (`id`, `source_table`, `source_id`, `prompt`, `answer`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES (12273,'trails',231,'What path does the trail take from Swamp Point?','Starting at Swamp Point, the trail descends nearly a mile via switchbacks to Muav Saddle. Here, you\'ll find an old patrol cabin before the trail continues contouring around the Coconino Sandstone to Queen Anne Spring.','2025-03-27 23:09:38','2025-03-27 23:09:38'),(12274,'trails',231,'What should I know about descending to White Creek?','From Queen Anne Spring, hikers will follow a restored historic trail for roughly a mile down to a benchmark in White Creek, encountering a waterfall that requires a bypass on the creek\'s right side.','2025-03-27 23:09:38','2025-03-27 23:09:38'),(12275,'trails',231,'What challenges will I face while descending through the Redwall?','The descent through the Redwall to White Creek is steep and rocky but well-marked. After navigating down, there’s a significant pour-off in the Bright Angel Shale that requires a bypass that contours along the Tonto before rejoining White Creek.','2025-03-27 23:09:38','2025-03-27 23:09:38'),(12276,'trails',231,'What experience awaits at the mouth of Redwall Canyon?','At the mouth of Redwall Canyon, a prominent pour-off in the Tapeats Sandstone marks the trail\'s end in this drainage, which has been carefully restored to align with historic paths, providing a safe bypass around the fall.','2025-03-27 23:09:38','2025-03-27 23:09:38'),(12277,'trails',231,'How does the trail conclude?','The trail continues following Shinumo Creek downstream for about a mile and a half and then ascends approximately 700 feet to reach a saddle, culminating in a descent to a beach area above the stunning Colorado River.','2025-03-27 23:09:38','2025-03-27 23:09:38'),(12278,'trails',232,'What is the North Kaibab Trail?','The North Kaibab Trail is part of the Arizona Trail, specifically Passage 38, leading hikers through the breathtaking scenery of the Grand Canyon\'s Inner Gorge. This section features steep descents, unique geological formations, and lush valleys.','2025-03-27 23:09:49','2025-03-27 23:09:49'),(12279,'trails',232,'What can hikers expect at the beginning of the North Kaibab Trail?','Hikers will start with a steep descent via numerous switchbacks, offering stunning views of the lush valley below as they make their way down into the canyon.','2025-03-27 23:09:49','2025-03-27 23:09:49'),(12280,'trails',232,'What amenities can be found at the Supai Tunnel?','At the Supai Tunnel, visitors will discover potable water available from mid-May to mid-October, as well as pit toilets, making it a convenient stop on the trail.','2025-03-27 23:09:49','2025-03-27 23:09:49'),(12281,'trails',232,'What is notable about the Redwall Limestone section of the trail?','The Redwall Limestone section of the trail is remarkable for its dramatic cliffs and breathtaking views, where the trail has been carved into the rock, providing an awe-inspiring hiking experience.','2025-03-27 23:09:49','2025-03-27 23:09:49'),(12282,'trails',232,'What should hikers consider visiting near Roaring Springs?','Roaring Springs is a refreshing side trip where hikers can see water flowing directly from the cliffs, creating a beautiful waterfall that cascades into Bright Angel Creek.','2025-03-27 23:09:49','2025-03-27 23:09:49'),(12283,'trails',232,'What is the significance of Pumphouse Residence?','Pumphouse Residence, also known as the Aiken Residence, is a historic site where artist Bruce Aiken lived and worked. In the past, hikers were often greeted by his children offering homemade lemonade.','2025-03-27 23:09:49','2025-03-27 23:09:49'),(12284,'trails',232,'What can hikers find at Ribbon Falls?','Ribbon Falls is a stunning waterfall located in a grotto near Bright Angel Creek, accessible via a short hike from Cottonwood Campground. It\'s a perfect spot to cool off during the hot midday hours.','2025-03-27 23:09:49','2025-03-27 23:09:49'),(12285,'trails',232,'What should hikers know about the Inner Gorge section of the trail?','As hikers traverse the Inner Gorge, they will pass through a narrow canyon surrounded by ancient Vishnu Schist rock. While the elevation isn\'t particularly challenging, this segment can become extremely hot, especially during the summer months.','2025-03-27 23:09:49','2025-03-27 23:09:49'),(12286,'trails',232,'What are the temperature conditions like in the Inner Gorge?','The Inner Gorge can reach scorching temperatures during the day, akin to walking through a hot parking lot in the summer. It\'s crucial to start early and aim to arrive at Bright Angel Campground before 10 a.m.','2025-03-27 23:09:49','2025-03-27 23:09:49'),(12287,'trails',232,'What is the difficulty level of the North Kaibab Trail?','The trail is classified as difficult, presenting challenges such as steep inclines and declines, making it one of the most strenuous in Grand Canyon National Park.','2025-03-27 23:09:49','2025-03-27 23:09:49'),(12288,'trails',232,'What are the trail specifics of the North Kaibab Trail?','The North Kaibab Trail spans 14.7 miles, with a total decline of 6,384 feet and a slight incline of 616 feet. The highest and lowest elevation along the trail is 2,454 feet.','2025-03-27 23:09:49','2025-03-27 23:09:49'),(12289,'trails',232,'Are pets allowed on the North Kaibab Trail?','No, dogs are not permitted on the North Kaibab Trail.','2025-03-27 23:09:49','2025-03-27 23:09:49'),(12290,'trails',232,'What are some features of the North Kaibab Trail?','Hikers can enjoy a variety of scenic features including fall colors, views of the river and creeks, beautiful waterfalls, wildflowers, and potential wildlife sightings along the trail.','2025-03-27 23:09:49','2025-03-27 23:09:49'),(12291,'trails',233,'What is the Bridle Trail known for?','The Bridle Trail on the North Rim is recognized for its scenic beauty and is unique as it allows both dogs and bikes, making it a great option for diverse outdoor activities.','2025-03-27 23:09:59','2025-03-27 23:09:59'),(12292,'trails',233,'What are the difficulty levels for hiking this trail?','The trail is classified as easy to intermediate, making it accessible to a wide range of hikers.','2025-03-27 23:09:59','2025-03-27 23:09:59'),(12293,'trails',233,'What is the highest elevation on the Bridle Trail?','The highest point along the Bridle Trail reaches an elevation of 8,181 feet.','2025-03-27 23:09:59','2025-03-27 23:09:59'),(12294,'trails',233,'What is the lowest elevation on the Bridle Trail?','The trail\'s lowest elevation also stands at 8,181 feet, highlighting its relatively flat terrain.','2025-03-27 23:09:59','2025-03-27 23:09:59'),(12295,'trails',233,'How long is the Bridle Trail?','The total length of the Bridle Trail is 2.0 miles, making it a manageable hike for most.','2025-03-27 23:09:59','2025-03-27 23:09:59'),(12296,'trails',233,'What type of trail is the Bridle Trail?','It is a point-to-point trail, providing a straightforward hiking experience.','2025-03-27 23:09:59','2025-03-27 23:09:59'),(12297,'trails',233,'What are the elevation changes on the Bridle Trail?','Hikers will encounter a slight incline of 198 feet and a decline of 117 feet along the trail.','2025-03-27 23:09:59','2025-03-27 23:09:59'),(12298,'trails',233,'What is the average grade of the Bridle Trail?','The average grade of the trail is approximately 0.03%, indicating a very gentle slope overall.','2025-03-27 23:09:59','2025-03-27 23:09:59'),(12299,'trails',233,'What is the maximum grade of the Bridle Trail?','The steepest section of the trail has a maximum grade of around 0.13%, which is easy to navigate.','2025-03-27 23:09:59','2025-03-27 23:09:59'),(12300,'trails',233,'What are the geographical coordinates for the Bridle Trail?','The coordinates for the trail are 36.196° latitude and -112.051° longitude.','2025-03-27 23:09:59','2025-03-27 23:09:59'),(12301,'trails',234,'What is the starting point of the Old Bright Angel Trail?','The trail begins at the junction with the Ken Patrick Trail, where it is marked for your convenience.','2025-03-27 23:10:14','2025-03-27 23:10:14'),(12302,'trails',234,'What kind of skills are necessary for hiking the Old Bright Angel Trail?','Strong route-finding skills are essential, particularly for the initial miles, due to the prevalence of faint social trails and dense underbrush.','2025-03-27 23:10:14','2025-03-27 23:10:14'),(12303,'trails',234,'What should hikers be aware of while following Bright Angel Creek?','While hiking along Bright Angel Creek, be cautious of misleading paths that might lead to creek crossings. The actual crossing point is likely further than anticipated, and cairns may help guide you.','2025-03-27 23:10:14','2025-03-27 23:10:14'),(12304,'trails',234,'What can hikers expect to find along the trail?','As you traverse the trail, enjoy stunning views, waterfalls, and potentially spot wildlife. The area is especially beautiful during fall when the colors change.','2025-03-27 23:10:14','2025-03-27 23:10:14'),(12305,'trails',234,'How long is the Old Bright Angel Trail and what difficulties might hikers face?','The trail spans approximately 5.1 miles and is classified as difficult, with a challenging descent and sections that may be hard to navigate.','2025-03-27 23:10:14','2025-03-27 23:10:14'),(12306,'trails',234,'What are the elevation details for the trail?','The trail\'s highest elevation reaches 4,541 feet while the lowest point is the same; it features an incline of 368 feet and a significant decline of 4,333 feet.','2025-03-27 23:10:14','2025-03-27 23:10:14'),(12307,'trails',234,'Is the Old Bright Angel Trail maintained?','No, the trail is unmaintained and has become overgrown over the years since it was originally established in 1902 by F.E. Matthes.','2025-03-27 23:10:14','2025-03-27 23:10:14'),(12308,'trails',234,'What is the best way to approach the Old Bright Angel Trail for a loop?','When using the Old Bright Angel Trail as part of a loop, it\'s often recommended to hike it downhill, as it can be easier to identify the trail in that direction.','2025-03-27 23:10:14','2025-03-27 23:10:14'),(12309,'trails',234,'Are dogs allowed on the Old Bright Angel Trail?','No, dogs are not permitted on this trail.','2025-03-27 23:10:14','2025-03-27 23:10:14'),(12310,'trails',234,'What historical significance does the Old Bright Angel Trail have?','Originally surveyed in 1902 for tourists reaching the North Rim, the trail was improved over time and is notable for having once crossed Bright Angel Creek multiple times.','2025-03-27 23:10:14','2025-03-27 23:10:14'),(12311,'trails',234,'Does the trail feature water sources?','Yes, there is a seasonal water source at the Pumphouse seasonal ranger station located at the intersection with the North Kaibab Trail.','2025-03-27 23:10:14','2025-03-27 23:10:14'),(12312,'trails',234,'What type of terrain can hikers expect on the Old Bright Angel Trail?','Hikers will experience a variety of terrains including dry streambeds, creek banks, and areas of dense vegetation.','2025-03-27 23:10:14','2025-03-27 23:10:14'),(12313,'trails',234,'What are some points of interest along the trail?','Besides stunning views and potential wildlife sightings, hikers will appreciate the scenic waterfalls and vibrant fall colors.','2025-03-27 23:10:14','2025-03-27 23:10:14'),(12314,'trails',235,'What is Point Imperial?','Point Imperial is the highest viewpoint on the North Rim, offering stunning panoramic vistas.','2025-03-27 23:10:25','2025-03-27 23:10:25'),(12315,'trails',235,'What is the trail\'s starting point?','The trail begins on the north side of the Point Imperial overlook parking lot.','2025-03-27 23:10:25','2025-03-27 23:10:25'),(12316,'trails',235,'What can hikers expect from the trail terrain?','The trail is primarily flat at the start, then gradually transitions to hilly terrain as you progress.','2025-03-27 23:10:25','2025-03-27 23:10:25'),(12317,'trails',235,'What type of scenery will hikers experience?','Hikers will walk through open meadows, past a burn area with the remnants of pine and aspen trees from the 2000 Outlook wildfire, and witness the regrowth and colorful wildflowers in the early season.','2025-03-27 23:10:25','2025-03-27 23:10:25'),(12318,'trails',235,'What important historical fact is associated with the 2000 Outlook wildfire?','The wildfire was a prescribed burn that got out of control, which temporarily trapped tourists at Imperial Point.','2025-03-27 23:10:25','2025-03-27 23:10:25'),(12319,'trails',235,'What kind of views can hikers enjoy along the trail?','The trail provides excellent views into Marble Canyon and northward toward Boundary Ridge, including Saddle Mountain, the highest point in the area.','2025-03-27 23:10:25','2025-03-27 23:10:25'),(12320,'trails',235,'What is the total length of the trail?','The trail spans 2.7 miles in total.','2025-03-27 23:10:25','2025-03-27 23:10:25'),(12321,'trails',235,'Is this trail considered easy or difficult?','The trail is categorized as an intermediate level, with some moderate inclines.','2025-03-27 23:10:25','2025-03-27 23:10:25'),(12322,'trails',235,'What is the highest elevation that hikers will reach?','The highest point along the trail is 8,758 feet.','2025-03-27 23:10:25','2025-03-27 23:10:25'),(12323,'trails',235,'Are dogs allowed on this trail?','No, dogs are not permitted on this trail.','2025-03-27 23:10:25','2025-03-27 23:10:25'),(12324,'trails',235,'What features can be enjoyed during the hike?','This trail is ideal for birdwatching, appreciating fall colors, enjoying scenic views, and observing wildflowers.','2025-03-27 23:10:25','2025-03-27 23:10:25'),(12325,'trails',235,'What are the coordinates of the trail?','The trail is located at latitude 36.279 and longitude -111.978.','2025-03-27 23:10:25','2025-03-27 23:10:25'),(12326,'trails',235,'Are there any specific guidebook references for this trail?','Some guidebooks may refer to this trail as a northern extension of the Ken Patrick Trail.','2025-03-27 23:10:25','2025-03-27 23:10:25'),(12327,'trails',236,'What is the starting point of the Powell Plateau Trail?','The hike begins at Swamp Point, where the Powell Plateau Trail diverges from the North Bass Trail.','2025-03-27 23:10:33','2025-03-27 23:10:33'),(12328,'trails',236,'What can I explore at the starting point?','At Swamp Point, you can check out the National Park Service ranger cabin, known as Teddy\'s Cabin, although it\'s a common misconception that Theodore Roosevelt actually stayed there.','2025-03-27 23:10:33','2025-03-27 23:10:33'),(12329,'trails',236,'What should I expect during the initial ascent?','Prepare for a series of switchbacks that lead you up to the plateau, moving away from the Muav Saddle and showcasing evidence of past wildfires from 1989.','2025-03-27 23:10:33','2025-03-27 23:10:33'),(12330,'trails',236,'What kind of terrain will I encounter on the trail?','After a steep beginning, the path levels out as you enter a beautiful forest populated with ponderosa pines and colorful wildflowers once you reach the plateau.','2025-03-27 23:10:33','2025-03-27 23:10:33'),(12331,'trails',236,'Can I explore further than the plateau?','Yes, you can venture to Dutton Point for stunning views of the Colorado River, though reaching this point requires navigating through areas with obscured trails and dense brush.','2025-03-27 23:10:33','2025-03-27 23:10:33'),(12332,'trails',236,'What is Dutton Point notable for?','Dutton Point is significant as it offers the only overlook on the plateau with perspectives of the Colorado River and was featured in the historic painting \'Chasm of the Colorado\' which hung in the US Senate.','2025-03-27 23:10:33','2025-03-27 23:10:33'),(12333,'trails',236,'Is this trail suitable for dogs?','No, dogs are not permitted on the Powell Plateau Trail.','2025-03-27 23:10:33','2025-03-27 23:10:33'),(12334,'trails',236,'What is the overall difficulty level of the trail?','The Powell Plateau Trail is categorized as intermediate in terms of difficulty.','2025-03-27 23:10:33','2025-03-27 23:10:33'),(12335,'trails',236,'What are the trail\'s elevation details?','The trail has a maximum elevation of 6,711 feet and a minimum elevation of 6,711 feet, resulting in a total elevation gain of approximately 1,000 feet.','2025-03-27 23:10:33','2025-03-27 23:10:33'),(12336,'trails',236,'How long is the Powell Plateau Trail?','The trail stretches for 3.3 miles and is a point-to-point hike.','2025-03-27 23:10:33','2025-03-27 23:10:33'),(12337,'trails',236,'What features can I experience along the trek?','Hikers can look forward to breathtaking views, a variety of wildflowers, and the chance to observe local wildlife throughout their journey.','2025-03-27 23:10:33','2025-03-27 23:10:33'),(12338,'trails',236,'Are there any historical significances related to the plateau?','Yes, the plateau was inhabited by the Anasazi people in the 11th and 12th centuries, and explorer John Wesley Powell, after whom the plateau is named, visited in 1870. Notably, Clarence Dutton, a geologist, inspired the names of both Dutton Point and Dutton Canyon.','2025-03-27 23:10:33','2025-03-27 23:10:33'),(12339,'trails',236,'How do I navigate the trail if it becomes faint?','As the trail may become difficult to follow, it\'s advisable to have good navigation skills and be prepared with sufficient water supplies, especially if attempting to reach Dutton Point.','2025-03-27 23:10:33','2025-03-27 23:10:33'),(12340,'trails',237,'What scenic views can I expect from the Saddle Horse Loop?','The Saddle Horse Loop offers breathtaking views of the Colorado River, featuring incredible straight-down perspectives from the canyon\'s edge.','2025-03-27 23:10:39','2025-03-27 23:10:39'),(12341,'trails',237,'How do I access the Saddle Horse Loop?','You can access the trail either along the road between Toroweap Overlook and Tuweep Campground or from a trailhead located near campsite 5 in the Tuweep Campground.','2025-03-27 23:10:39','2025-03-27 23:10:39'),(12342,'trails',237,'What is the difficulty level of the Saddle Horse Loop?','This trail is categorized as easy to intermediate, making it suitable for a wide range of hikers.','2025-03-27 23:10:39','2025-03-27 23:10:39'),(12343,'trails',237,'What is the total length of the Saddle Horse Loop?','The loop is approximately 1.1 miles long, providing a quick yet rewarding hiking experience.','2025-03-27 23:10:39','2025-03-27 23:10:39'),(12344,'trails',237,'What are the elevation details for the Saddle Horse Loop?','The trail reaches a highest elevation of 4473 feet and a lowest elevation of 4473 feet since it\'s relatively flat.','2025-03-27 23:10:39','2025-03-27 23:10:39'),(12345,'trails',237,'What is the trail type for Saddle Horse Loop?','This trail is a point-to-point loop, making it easy to follow and navigate.','2025-03-27 23:10:39','2025-03-27 23:10:39'),(12346,'trails',237,'Is the trail steep or hilly?','The incline is minimal, with only a 100-foot gain and a 109-foot decline, resulting in an average grade of just 0.04%.','2025-03-27 23:10:39','2025-03-27 23:10:39'),(12347,'trails',237,'Are pets allowed on the Saddle Horse Loop?','Unfortunately, dogs are not permitted on this trail.','2025-03-27 23:10:39','2025-03-27 23:10:39'),(12348,'trails',237,'What are the geographical coordinates for the Saddle Horse Loop?','The trail is located at a latitude of 36.2239 and a longitude of -113.061.','2025-03-27 23:10:39','2025-03-27 23:10:39'),(12349,'trails',238,'What is the main destination of the Saddle Mountain Trail?','The trail leads hikers to a deep cut in the north rim, situated just below Saddle Mountain, rather than reaching the summit itself.','2025-03-27 23:10:46','2025-03-27 23:10:46'),(12350,'trails',238,'What are some key features of the Saddle Mountain Trail?','Hikers can enjoy views along the way, traverse through a ridgeline, walk through a burn area, and experience flatter, arid sections of ground before reaching the intersection with the Nankoweap Trail.','2025-03-27 23:10:46','2025-03-27 23:10:46'),(12351,'trails',238,'How difficult is the Saddle Mountain Trail?','The trail is categorized as very difficult, so it\'s best suited for experienced hikers.','2025-03-27 23:10:46','2025-03-27 23:10:46'),(12352,'trails',238,'What is the total length of the Saddle Mountain Trail?','The trail stretches approximately 2.3 miles in length.','2025-03-27 23:10:46','2025-03-27 23:10:46'),(12353,'trails',238,'What is the elevation range of the Saddle Mountain Trail?','The highest and lowest elevations along the trail are both 7,558 feet.','2025-03-27 23:10:46','2025-03-27 23:10:46'),(12354,'trails',238,'What is the incline and decline experienced on the Saddle Mountain Trail?','Hikers will experience an incline of 357 feet and a notable decline of 1,630 feet during the hike.','2025-03-27 23:10:46','2025-03-27 23:10:46'),(12355,'trails',238,'What types of views can hikers expect on this trail?','The trail offers stunning views and the possibility of seeing wildflowers along the route.','2025-03-27 23:10:46','2025-03-27 23:10:46'),(12356,'trails',238,'Are dogs allowed on the Saddle Mountain Trail?','Unfortunately, dogs are not permitted on this trail.','2025-03-27 23:10:46','2025-03-27 23:10:46'),(12357,'trails',238,'Where is the Saddle Mountain Trailhead located?','The trailhead can be found off FR610, though it may be somewhat challenging to access.','2025-03-27 23:10:46','2025-03-27 23:10:46'),(12358,'trails',238,'What is the trail type of the Saddle Mountain Trail?','This trail is classified as point-to-point, leading from the trailhead to the intersection with the Nankoweap Trail.','2025-03-27 23:10:46','2025-03-27 23:10:46'),(12359,'trails',239,'What is the Schmutz Spring Trail known for?','The Schmutz Spring Trail is celebrated for its breathtaking desert oasis, making it a unique hiking experience.','2025-03-27 23:10:53','2025-03-27 23:10:53'),(12360,'trails',239,'What is the difficulty level of the Schmutz Spring Trail?','This trail is classified as intermediate, presenting a moderate challenge for hikers.','2025-03-27 23:10:53','2025-03-27 23:10:53'),(12361,'trails',239,'What are the highest and lowest elevations on the Schmutz Spring Trail?','The trail maintains a consistent elevation of 4474 feet throughout its length.','2025-03-27 23:10:53','2025-03-27 23:10:53'),(12362,'trails',239,'How long is the Schmutz Spring Trail?','The trail stretches for a total of 2.1 miles, offering a manageable distance for hikers.','2025-03-27 23:10:53','2025-03-27 23:10:53'),(12363,'trails',239,'What type of trail is the Schmutz Spring Trail?','The Schmutz Spring Trail is a point-to-point trail, allowing hikers to start at one end and finish at another.','2025-03-27 23:10:53','2025-03-27 23:10:53'),(12364,'trails',239,'What is the elevation change like on the Schmutz Spring Trail?','The trail features a slight incline of 29 feet and a notable decline of 1326 feet, providing diverse terrain.','2025-03-27 23:10:53','2025-03-27 23:10:53'),(12365,'trails',239,'What is the average grade of the Schmutz Spring Trail?','The average grade of this trail is around 0.12%, indicating a relatively gentle slope.','2025-03-27 23:10:53','2025-03-27 23:10:53'),(12366,'trails',239,'What is the maximum grade on the Schmutz Spring Trail?','The steepest incline you will encounter on the trail is 0.36%, which adds to the overall hiking experience.','2025-03-27 23:10:53','2025-03-27 23:10:53'),(12367,'trails',239,'What are the geographical coordinates of the Schmutz Spring Trail?','The trail can be found at a latitude of 36.3393 and a longitude of -112.927.','2025-03-27 23:10:53','2025-03-27 23:10:53'),(12368,'trails',240,'What is the Thunder River Trail known for?','The Thunder River Trail is celebrated for its stunning views, expansive slickrock sections, and the remarkable cascades at Thunder River and Tapeats Creek, making it a popular destination for adventure seekers.','2025-03-27 23:11:11','2025-03-27 23:11:11'),(12369,'trails',240,'How do hikers navigate the Thunder River Trail?','Hikers should be vigilant for cairns that mark the way, especially when crossing slickrock sections. It\'s helpful to spot the next cairn before the previous one disappears from sight.','2025-03-27 23:11:11','2025-03-27 23:11:11'),(12370,'trails',240,'What are the trail conditions like on the Thunder River Trail?','Expect the trail to be reasonably flat for the first 2.5 miles, followed by a challenging descent through steep switchbacks that can be rough, especially due to the area\'s notorious heat.','2025-03-27 23:11:11','2025-03-27 23:11:11'),(12371,'trails',240,'When should hikers avoid hiking in Surprise Valley?','To mitigate the heat, it\'s advisable to avoid hiking in Surprise Valley after 10 a.m. during warmer months.','2025-03-27 23:11:11','2025-03-27 23:11:11'),(12372,'trails',240,'What routes are available at the fork in the trail?','At the fork in the trail, you can go east (left) towards Thunder River and Tapeats Creek or west (right) toward Deer Creek.','2025-03-27 23:11:11','2025-03-27 23:11:11'),(12373,'trails',240,'What can hikers expect upon reaching Thunder River?','Upon reaching Thunder River, hikers are greeted by refreshing cascades that provide an inviting spot for rest and relaxation after a long dry trek.','2025-03-27 23:11:11','2025-03-27 23:11:11'),(12374,'trails',240,'Where is the designated Upper Tapeats campsite located?','The Upper Tapeats campsite (AW7) is approximately 0.1 miles below the confluence of Thunder River and Tapeats Creek, situated on the west side of the creek.','2025-03-27 23:11:11','2025-03-27 23:11:11'),(12375,'trails',240,'What challenges should hikers anticipate when crossing Tapeats Creek?','Creek crossings may be challenging due to snowmelt or heavy rain; during high water, hikers might need to navigate a narrow, exposed trail on the west side of the creek as an alternative.','2025-03-27 23:11:11','2025-03-27 23:11:11'),(12376,'trails',240,'What is the difficulty level of the Thunder River Trail?','The Thunder River Trail is classified as intermediate to difficult, requiring a good level of fitness and experience.','2025-03-27 23:11:11','2025-03-27 23:11:11'),(12377,'trails',240,'What are the elevation and trail length details for the Thunder River Trail?','The trail has a highest elevation of 1,989 feet and a lowest elevation of 1,989 feet, covering a total length of 2.3 miles.','2025-03-27 23:11:11','2025-03-27 23:11:11'),(12378,'trails',240,'What are some features of the Thunder River Trail?','This trail offers a variety of features, including opportunities for bird watching, views of rivers and waterfalls, as well as chances to see wildflowers and wildlife.','2025-03-27 23:11:11','2025-03-27 23:11:11'),(12379,'trails',240,'Are pets allowed on the Thunder River Trail?','No, dogs are not permitted on the Thunder River Trail.','2025-03-27 23:11:11','2025-03-27 23:11:11'),(12380,'trails',240,'What are the coordinates for the Thunder River Trail?','The trail is located at latitude 36.3922 and longitude -112.452.','2025-03-27 23:11:11','2025-03-27 23:11:11'),(12381,'trails',241,'What is the starting point of the Thunder River Trail?','The hike begins at the Thunder River Trailhead, heading south across the Esplanade.','2025-03-27 23:11:23','2025-03-27 23:11:23'),(12382,'trails',241,'Are there any markers along the Thunder River Trail?','Yes, cairns are placed throughout the trail, especially across slickrock sections and small drainages, so hikers should remain vigilant in spotting them.','2025-03-27 23:11:23','2025-03-27 23:11:23'),(12383,'trails',241,'What trail conditions can hikers expect on the Esplanade?','Hikers will encounter approximately 2.5 miles of relatively flat walking on the Esplanade, but should anticipate a steep descent through switchbacks as the trail approaches Surprise Valley.','2025-03-27 23:11:23','2025-03-27 23:11:23'),(12384,'trails',241,'How should hikers prepare for the weather in Surprise Valley?','Given the southern exposure and notorious heat, it\'s advisable to avoid hiking in Surprise Valley after 10 a.m. during warm weather.','2025-03-27 23:11:23','2025-03-27 23:11:23'),(12385,'trails',241,'What routes are available at the fork in the trail near Thunder River?','At the fork, hikers can take the left trail to Thunder River and Tapeats Creek, or the right trail leading to Deer Creek.','2025-03-27 23:11:23','2025-03-27 23:11:23'),(12386,'trails',241,'What can hikers expect along the trail to Thunder River?','After crossing the valley floor with its shallow drainages and low hills for about a mile, the trail leads down steep switchbacks to the refreshing cascades of Thunder River.','2025-03-27 23:11:23','2025-03-27 23:11:23'),(12387,'trails',241,'Is there a designated campsite near Thunder River?','Yes, the designated Upper Tapeats campsite (AW7) is located about a mile below where Thunder River meets Tapeats Creek, on the west side of the creek.','2025-03-27 23:11:23','2025-03-27 23:11:23'),(12388,'trails',241,'What are the creek crossing options for hikers headed to the Colorado River?','Hikers can either cross Tapeats Creek just below the campsite or about half a mile down canyon, continuing for two miles to find another crossing back to the west side.','2025-03-27 23:11:23','2025-03-27 23:11:23'),(12389,'trails',241,'What should hikers be cautious of during creek crossings?','Creek crossings may become impassable due to snowmelt or heavy rains, especially after mid-March when water levels rise.','2025-03-27 23:11:23','2025-03-27 23:11:23'),(12390,'trails',241,'What is the difficulty level of the Thunder River Trail?','The trail is classified as intermediate to difficult, suitable for experienced hikers.','2025-03-27 23:11:23','2025-03-27 23:11:23'),(12391,'trails',241,'What is the highest and lowest elevation along the trail?','The highest and lowest elevation along the trail is 2,490 feet, as it is a point-to-point trail.','2025-03-27 23:11:23','2025-03-27 23:11:23'),(12392,'trails',241,'How long is the Thunder River Trail?','The total length of the Thunder River Trail is approximately 12.6 miles.','2025-03-27 23:11:23','2025-03-27 23:11:23'),(12393,'trails',241,'What is the average grade of the trail?','The average grade of the trail is about 0.08%, with some steep sections reaching up to a maximum of 0.71%.','2025-03-27 23:11:23','2025-03-27 23:11:23'),(12394,'trails',241,'What natural features can hikers enjoy on this trail?','Hikers can look forward to experiencing various features including birding opportunities, caves, rivers, views, waterfalls, wildflowers, and wildlife.','2025-03-27 23:11:23','2025-03-27 23:11:23'),(12395,'trails',241,'Are dogs allowed on the Thunder River Trail?','No, dogs are not permitted on this trail.','2025-03-27 23:11:23','2025-03-27 23:11:23'),(12396,'trails',241,'What unique feature transforms the desert landscape around Thunder River?','The cascades of Thunder River, which emerge from caves, transform the arid environment into a lush oasis.','2025-03-27 23:11:23','2025-03-27 23:11:23'),(12397,'trails',242,'What is the condition of the trail to Tiyo Point?','The trail to Tiyo Point is a former road that is becoming increasingly overgrown. While it is generally straightforward to follow, hikers may need to navigate over or around some fallen trees along the way.','2025-03-27 23:11:32','2025-03-27 23:11:32'),(12398,'trails',242,'What can I expect in terms of wildlife and scenery on the trail?','As you hike along this rarely traveled primitive trail, you will be accompanied mainly by wildflowers, creating a beautiful and serene atmosphere. Keep your eyes peeled for wildlife and enjoy the scenic views along the way.','2025-03-27 23:11:32','2025-03-27 23:11:32'),(12399,'trails',242,'How is the elevation change on this trail?','The hike begins with a brief ascent from Point Subline Road, followed by a gentle downhill stretch over rolling terrain. Overall, there is a total decline of 570 feet with a modest incline of 183 feet.','2025-03-27 23:11:32','2025-03-27 23:11:32'),(12400,'trails',242,'What is the total distance of the Tiyo Point trail?','The total length of the Tiyo Point trail is 6.6 miles, making it a manageable hike for those seeking peaceful solitude in nature.','2025-03-27 23:11:32','2025-03-27 23:11:32'),(12401,'trails',242,'Is there a picnic area along the trail?','Yes, there is a solitary picnic area near the end of the trail, perfect for those looking to relax and take in the tranquil surroundings before or after their hike.','2025-03-27 23:11:32','2025-03-27 23:11:32'),(12402,'trails',242,'What is the difficulty level of the trail?','The trail is rated as easy to intermediate, catering to a wide range of hikers, although some sections may require agility to navigate around downed trees.','2025-03-27 23:11:32','2025-03-27 23:11:32'),(12403,'trails',242,'Are dogs allowed on the Tiyo Point trail?','No, dogs are not permitted on the Tiyo Point trail, ensuring a quiet and undisturbed environment for all hikers.','2025-03-27 23:11:32','2025-03-27 23:11:32'),(12404,'trails',242,'What are the geographical coordinates of the Tiyo Point trail?','The Tiyo Point trail is located at a latitude of 36.2585 and a longitude of -112.103.','2025-03-27 23:11:32','2025-03-27 23:11:32'),(12405,'trails',242,'What types of features can I expect to see on the trail?','Hikers can look forward to picturesque views, vibrant wildflowers, and the possibility of encountering wildlife throughout their journey along this scenic trail.','2025-03-27 23:11:32','2025-03-27 23:11:32'),(12406,'trails',243,'What is the length of the Tuckup Trail?','The Tuckup Trail stretches for 3.1 miles.','2025-03-27 23:11:41','2025-03-27 23:11:41'),(12407,'trails',243,'How many access points are there for the Tuckup Trail?','There are two access points: one is clearly marked before reaching Tuweep Campground, and the other starts at campsite 10 within the campground.','2025-03-27 23:11:41','2025-03-27 23:11:41'),(12408,'trails',243,'What type of trail is the Tuckup Trail?','This trail is categorized as a point-to-point route.','2025-03-27 23:11:41','2025-03-27 23:11:41'),(12409,'trails',243,'What is the difficulty level of the Tuckup Trail?','The trail is considered to have an intermediate level of difficulty.','2025-03-27 23:11:41','2025-03-27 23:11:41'),(12410,'trails',243,'What are the elevation details for the Tuckup Trail?','The trail has a highest elevation of 4,357 feet, with no significant changes in elevation as both the highest and lowest points are the same.','2025-03-27 23:11:41','2025-03-27 23:11:41'),(12411,'trails',243,'What is the incline and decline like on the Tuckup Trail?','Hikers will encounter an incline of 89 feet and a decline of 373 feet along the trail.','2025-03-27 23:11:41','2025-03-27 23:11:41'),(12412,'trails',243,'Are dogs allowed on the Tuckup Trail?','No, dogs are not permitted on this trail.','2025-03-27 23:11:41','2025-03-27 23:11:41'),(12413,'trails',243,'What type of scenery can hikers expect on the Tuckup Trail?','Hikers will be treated to breathtaking views of the Grand Canyon\'s unique geology during their trek.','2025-03-27 23:11:41','2025-03-27 23:11:41'),(12414,'trails',243,'How crowded is the Tuckup Trail?','This trail is one of the least frequented in the Grand Canyon, offering a more solitary and rustic hiking experience.','2025-03-27 23:11:41','2025-03-27 23:11:41'),(12415,'trails',243,'What is the average grade of the Tuckup Trail?','The average grade of the trail is relatively gentle at 0.03%, with a maximum grade of 0.09%.','2025-03-27 23:11:41','2025-03-27 23:11:41'),(12416,'trails',243,'What is significant about the Tuckup Trail in relation to the Grand Canyon?','The Tuckup Trail is part of a larger network that covers approximately 60 miles across the Grand Canyon, providing a unique exploration of one of its more isolated areas.','2025-03-27 23:11:41','2025-03-27 23:11:41'),(12417,'trails',244,'What is the Tuckup to Tuweep Campground Connector trail known for?','The Tuckup to Tuweep Campground Connector trail offers hikers stunning views of the beautiful landscapes found in southern Utah and northern Arizona.','2025-03-27 23:11:47','2025-03-27 23:11:47'),(12418,'trails',244,'What is the difficulty level of the Tuckup to Tuweep Campground Connector trail?','This trail is categorized as easy, making it accessible for hikers of all skill levels.','2025-03-27 23:11:47','2025-03-27 23:11:47'),(12419,'trails',244,'What is the length of the Tuckup to Tuweep Campground Connector trail?','The trail stretches for 1.2 miles, making it a great option for a short hike.','2025-03-27 23:11:47','2025-03-27 23:11:47'),(12420,'trails',244,'What are the elevation statistics for the Tuckup to Tuweep Campground Connector trail?','The trail maintains a consistent elevation at 4,566 feet, with a slight incline of 114 feet and a decline of 120 feet.','2025-03-27 23:11:47','2025-03-27 23:11:47'),(12421,'trails',244,'How is the trail graded in terms of average and maximum incline?','The trail features an average grade of 0.04%, with a maximum incline of 0.12%, making it a gentle hike overall.','2025-03-27 23:11:47','2025-03-27 23:11:47'),(12422,'trails',244,'What are the coordinates of the Tuckup to Tuweep Campground Connector trail?','The trail can be found at a latitude of 36.226 and a longitude of -113.06.','2025-03-27 23:11:47','2025-03-27 23:11:47'),(12423,'trails',244,'Is the Tuckup to Tuweep Campground Connector trail in need of adoption?','Yes, this trail is currently in need of adoption, which means that volunteers or organizations can help maintain and preserve its condition.','2025-03-27 23:11:47','2025-03-27 23:11:47'),(12424,'trails',244,'What type of trail is the Tuckup to Tuweep Campground Connector?','This is a point-to-point trail, meaning hikers will need to plan for transportation at both ends of the hike.','2025-03-27 23:11:47','2025-03-27 23:11:47'),(12425,'trails',245,'What is the length of the Unkar Delta trail?','The Unkar Delta trail measures 0.8 miles in length, forming a loop that provides a scenic and informative hike.','2025-03-27 23:11:56','2025-03-27 23:11:56'),(12426,'trails',245,'How much time should I allocate for hiking the Unkar Delta trail?','To fully enjoy the trail, plan to spend approximately 45 minutes walking the loop.','2025-03-27 23:11:56','2025-03-27 23:11:56'),(12427,'trails',245,'What type of terrain can I expect on the Unkar Delta trail?','The trail traverses over alluvial terraces and drainages, offering a mix of natural landscapes along the way.','2025-03-27 23:11:56','2025-03-27 23:11:56'),(12428,'trails',245,'What historical significance does Unkar Delta hold?','Unkar Delta has been a site of human occupation since around AD 850, featuring ruins that reflect the history of ancestral Puebloan dwellings and their agricultural lifestyle.','2025-03-27 23:11:56','2025-03-27 23:11:56'),(12429,'trails',245,'What can I learn about the Pueblo people while hiking this trail?','While hiking, you\'ll discover insights into the growth and migration patterns of the Pueblo people, particularly their peak population around AD 1100 and eventual migration by AD 1200.','2025-03-27 23:11:56','2025-03-27 23:11:56'),(12430,'trails',245,'What types of features can I see along the Unkar Delta trail?','The trail offers features such as birding opportunities, views of the river and creek, swimming spots, and a chance to observe local wildlife.','2025-03-27 23:11:56','2025-03-27 23:11:56'),(12431,'trails',245,'Is the Unkar Delta trail suitable for all hikers?','Yes, the trail is classified as easy, making it accessible for hikers of various experience levels.','2025-03-27 23:11:56','2025-03-27 23:11:56'),(12432,'trails',245,'Are pets allowed on the Unkar Delta trail?','No, dogs are not permitted on the Unkar Delta trail to help protect the delicate environment and prehistoric remains.','2025-03-27 23:11:56','2025-03-27 23:11:56'),(12433,'trails',245,'What are the highest and lowest elevations along the trail?','The trail maintains a consistent elevation of 2,644 feet throughout its path.','2025-03-27 23:11:56','2025-03-27 23:11:56'),(12434,'trails',245,'What is the average and maximum grade of the trail?','The average grade is a gentle 0.04%, with a maximum incline of 0.15%, making it a comfortable trek.','2025-03-27 23:11:56','2025-03-27 23:11:56'),(12435,'trails',245,'What steps have been taken to protect the environment along the trail?','The trail system is designed to allow visitors to explore while preserving the fragile desert ecosystem and the historic remnants of the Pueblo peoples.','2025-03-27 23:11:56','2025-03-27 23:11:56'),(12436,'trails',246,'What is the overall experience of hiking the Walhalla Glades Trail?','Hiking the Walhalla Glades Trail offers a unique adventure with stunning views, as it\'s surrounded by the Grand Canyon on three sides. You can explore a variety of landscapes, from open fields to wooded sections, and get close to the canyon rim, culminating at Cape Royal and The Angels Window overlook.','2025-03-27 23:12:08','2025-03-27 23:12:08'),(12437,'trails',246,'What type of geography surrounds the Walhalla Glades Trail?','The trail is situated on a peninsula encircled by the Grand Canyon, which contributes to its distinctive climate. Warm updrafts create a more favorable environment compared to other areas on the North Rim, supporting diverse vegetation and wildlife.','2025-03-27 23:12:08','2025-03-27 23:12:08'),(12438,'trails',246,'Can you describe the trail\'s starting point and initial descent?','The hike begins from a pull-off along Cape Royal Road, where the Walhalla Glades Trail descends gently over undulating grassy terrain, initially running parallel to the road before veering into open fields marked by burned tree remnants.','2025-03-27 23:12:08','2025-03-27 23:12:08'),(12439,'trails',246,'What other trails intersect with the Walhalla Glades Trail?','As you progress along the trail, you\'ll encounter the Francois Matthes Trail branching off to the right, heading southwest. Additionally, there’s a junction with the Walhalla Connector along the way.','2025-03-27 23:12:08','2025-03-27 23:12:08'),(12440,'trails',246,'What is the difficulty level of the Walhalla Glades Trail?','The trail is rated as easy, making it accessible for hikers of various skill levels.','2025-03-27 23:12:08','2025-03-27 23:12:08'),(12441,'trails',246,'What is the total length of the Walhalla Glades Trail?','The trail stretches for 7.9 miles, offering plenty of space to explore and enjoy the natural surroundings.','2025-03-27 23:12:08','2025-03-27 23:12:08'),(12442,'trails',246,'What can you tell me about the elevation changes on this trail?','The highest point on the trail reaches 7,914 feet, with a total incline of 69 feet and a decline of 650 feet, resulting in a gentle average grade of 0.02%.','2025-03-27 23:12:08','2025-03-27 23:12:08'),(12443,'trails',246,'Are dogs allowed on the Walhalla Glades Trail?','Unfortunately, dogs are not permitted on the Walhalla Glades Trail, so plan accordingly if you’re hiking with pets.','2025-03-27 23:12:08','2025-03-27 23:12:08'),(12444,'trails',246,'What key features can hikers expect on the Walhalla Glades Trail?','Hikers can look forward to breathtaking views of the Grand Canyon at various points along the trail, particularly as it approaches the rim.','2025-03-27 23:12:08','2025-03-27 23:12:08'),(12445,'trails',246,'What type of trail is the Walhalla Glades?','The Walhalla Glades Trail is a point-to-point primitive trail that may be somewhat isolated and could be challenging to navigate in certain areas.','2025-03-27 23:12:08','2025-03-27 23:12:08'),(12446,'trails',246,'What are the latitude and longitude coordinates for the Walhalla Glades Trail?','The trail is located at approximately 36.2232° latitude and -111.966° longitude.','2025-03-27 23:12:08','2025-03-27 23:12:08'),(12447,'trails',247,'What is the main purpose of the Walhalla Connector trail?','The Walhalla Connector trail serves as an east-west route that connects the Walhalla Glades, Francois Matthes, and Ariel Point trails, offering stunning views of the surrounding landscape.','2025-03-27 23:12:13','2025-03-27 23:12:13'),(12448,'trails',247,'What is the difficulty level of the Walhalla Connector?','The trail is categorized as intermediate, making it suitable for those with some hiking experience.','2025-03-27 23:12:13','2025-03-27 23:12:13'),(12449,'trails',247,'What are the highest and lowest elevations on the Walhalla Connector trail?','The trail has a consistent elevation, with both the highest and lowest points reaching 8,037 feet.','2025-03-27 23:12:13','2025-03-27 23:12:13'),(12450,'trails',247,'How long is the Walhalla Connector trail?','The total length of the Walhalla Connector is 2.9 miles.','2025-03-27 23:12:13','2025-03-27 23:12:13'),(12451,'trails',247,'What type of trail is the Walhalla Connector?','This trail is a point-to-point type, meaning it has distinct starting and ending points.','2025-03-27 23:12:13','2025-03-27 23:12:13'),(12452,'trails',247,'What is the incline and decline of the Walhalla Connector?','Hikers will experience an incline of 342 feet and a decline of 403 feet along the trail.','2025-03-27 23:12:13','2025-03-27 23:12:13'),(12453,'trails',247,'What are the average and maximum grades for the Walhalla Connector trail?','The average grade is quite gentle at 0.05%, while the maximum grade reaches up to 0.17%.','2025-03-27 23:12:13','2025-03-27 23:12:13'),(12454,'trails',247,'What are the geographical coordinates of the Walhalla Connector?','The trail is located at a latitude of 36.177 and a longitude of -111.953.','2025-03-27 23:12:13','2025-03-27 23:12:13'),(12455,'trails',248,'What is the length of the Widforss Point Trail?','The Widforss Point Trail stretches approximately 4.9 miles (about 8 kilometers) one way, making it close to 10 miles for a round trip.','2025-03-27 23:12:20','2025-03-27 23:12:20'),(12456,'trails',248,'How difficult is the Widforss Point Trail?','This trail is classified as intermediate in difficulty, suitable for those with some hiking experience.','2025-03-27 23:12:20','2025-03-27 23:12:20'),(12457,'trails',248,'What are the starting and ending elevations of the trail?','Hikers will start and finish at the same elevation of 7965 feet, providing a unique experience without significant elevation change.','2025-03-27 23:12:20','2025-03-27 23:12:20'),(12458,'trails',248,'What type of trail is Widforss Point Trail?','The trail is a point-to-point route, allowing hikers to enjoy the journey out to Widforss Point and back.','2025-03-27 23:12:20','2025-03-27 23:12:20'),(12459,'trails',248,'Are dogs allowed on the Widforss Point Trail?','Unfortunately, dogs are not permitted on this trail, so it\'s a great option for those looking for a pet-free hike.','2025-03-27 23:12:20','2025-03-27 23:12:20'),(12460,'trails',248,'What kind of views can hikers expect along the trail?','As hikers make their way along the trail, they will be treated to breathtaking views of the Grand Canyon and the North Rim, especially upon reaching Widforss Point after traversing a forest of conifers and aspens.','2025-03-27 23:12:20','2025-03-27 23:12:20'),(12461,'trails',248,'What kind of scenery can I expect on this trail?','The course of the trail features a scenic mix of conifer and aspen forests, particularly vibrant during the fall, as well as dramatic canyon vistas that enhance the hiking experience.','2025-03-27 23:12:20','2025-03-27 23:12:20'),(12462,'trails',248,'What is the average and maximum grade of the trail?','The average grade of the trail is a gentle 0.04%, with a maximum steepness of 0.21%, making for a manageable hike.','2025-03-27 23:12:20','2025-03-27 23:12:20'),(12463,'trails',248,'What are the coordinates for Widforss Point Trail?','The trail is located at latitude 36.2237 and longitude -112.065, positioned within the stunning landscapes of the Grand Canyon.','2025-03-27 23:12:20','2025-03-27 23:12:20'),(12464,'trails',249,'What is the Uncle Jim Trail like?','The Uncle Jim Trail is a family-friendly loop that features pleasant, shaded areas and offers breathtaking views of Bright Angel Canyon.','2025-03-27 23:12:29','2025-03-27 23:12:29'),(12465,'trails',249,'What is the difficulty level of the Uncle Jim Trail?','The trail is categorized as intermediate in difficulty, making it suitable for families with varying skill levels.','2025-03-27 23:12:29','2025-03-27 23:12:29'),(12466,'trails',249,'What are the highest and lowest elevations on the trail?','The trail maintains an elevation of 8,256 feet throughout, meaning you won\'t experience significant elevation changes.','2025-03-27 23:12:29','2025-03-27 23:12:29'),(12467,'trails',249,'How long is the Uncle Jim Trail?','The trail stretches for 2.6 miles, providing a pleasant hike in a beautiful setting.','2025-03-27 23:12:29','2025-03-27 23:12:29'),(12468,'trails',249,'Is the Uncle Jim Trail a loop or a point-to-point trail?','The Uncle Jim Trail is a loop trail, allowing hikers to complete the circuit without retracing their steps.','2025-03-27 23:12:29','2025-03-27 23:12:29'),(12469,'trails',249,'What is the vertical incline and decline of the trail?','Hikers will encounter a gentle incline of 227 feet and a decline of 229 feet, ensuring a manageable walk.','2025-03-27 23:12:29','2025-03-27 23:12:29'),(12470,'trails',249,'What are the average and maximum grades on the trail?','The average grade is a gentle 0.03%, while the maximum grade reaches 0.18%, making it a leisurely hike overall.','2025-03-27 23:12:29','2025-03-27 23:12:29'),(12471,'trails',249,'What natural features can I expect to see on the trail?','Trail-goers can enjoy fall colors, stunning views, wildflowers, and chances to spot local wildlife.','2025-03-27 23:12:29','2025-03-27 23:12:29'),(12472,'trails',249,'Are dogs allowed on the Uncle Jim Trail?','No, dogs are not permitted on this trail, so please make other arrangements for your furry friends.','2025-03-27 23:12:29','2025-03-27 23:12:29'),(12473,'trails',249,'What are the coordinates for locating the Uncle Jim Trail?','The trail can be found at latitude 36.227 and longitude -112.049, helpful for those using GPS devices.','2025-03-27 23:12:29','2025-03-27 23:12:29'),(12474,'trails',250,'What is the overall difficulty level of the Lava Falls trail?','The Lava Falls trail is rated as very difficult due to its challenging terrain.','2025-03-27 23:12:38','2025-03-27 23:12:38'),(12475,'trails',250,'What equipment should hikers bring for Lava Falls?','Hikers should pack ice axes and possess strong route finding skills to navigate the trail safely.','2025-03-27 23:12:38','2025-03-27 23:12:38'),(12476,'trails',250,'What unique features can hikers expect to see on the Lava Falls trail?','Along the trail, you\'ll find sandy beaches and a viewpoint overlooking the famous Lava rapid, where rafters may be seen navigating the waters.','2025-03-27 23:12:38','2025-03-27 23:12:38'),(12477,'trails',250,'Are there any hazards to be aware of on this trail?','Yes, be cautious of loose scree and shifting lava blocks. A misstep can trigger rock slides or result in a fall.','2025-03-27 23:12:38','2025-03-27 23:12:38'),(12478,'trails',250,'Is there water available on the Lava Falls trail?','No, there is no water source on the trail. It\'s crucial to plan ahead and filter river water for drinking.','2025-03-27 23:12:38','2025-03-27 23:12:38'),(12479,'trails',250,'How can hikers navigate effectively on this trail?','Using the Hiking Project mobile app can aid in navigation, but ensure your data is up to date and your device is fully charged.','2025-03-27 23:12:38','2025-03-27 23:12:38'),(12480,'trails',250,'Is the Lava Falls trail maintained?','The park service does not maintain this trail and advises caution due to its steepness and condition.','2025-03-27 23:12:38','2025-03-27 23:12:38'),(12481,'trails',250,'What are the elevation details of the Lava Falls trail?','The trail has a highest elevation of 1,676 feet and maintains this elevation for its 1.3-mile length, with a slight incline and a significant decline.','2025-03-27 23:12:38','2025-03-27 23:12:38'),(12482,'trails',250,'Are pets allowed on the Lava Falls trail?','No, dogs are not permitted on this trail.','2025-03-27 23:12:38','2025-03-27 23:12:38'),(12483,'trails',250,'What should hikers know about the terrain of the Lava Falls trail?','The trail consists predominantly of loose scree and unstable lava blocks, making it quite treacherous.','2025-03-27 23:12:39','2025-03-27 23:12:39'),(12484,'trails',250,'What is the incline and decline like on the Lava Falls trail?','The trail has a minimal incline of approximately 16 feet, but it features a steep decline of about 2,512 feet.','2025-03-27 23:12:39','2025-03-27 23:12:39'),(12485,'trails',251,'What is the difficulty level of Passage 39 on the AZT?','Passage 39 is considered easy, making it suitable for a wide range of hikers.','2025-03-27 23:12:45','2025-03-27 23:12:45'),(12486,'trails',251,'What is the total length of Passage 39?','The trail stretches for 12.5 miles, offering ample opportunity for exploration.','2025-03-27 23:12:45','2025-03-27 23:12:45'),(12487,'trails',251,'What are the elevation details for this trail?','The trail maintains a consistently high elevation of 8062 feet, providing stunning views throughout the hike.','2025-03-27 23:12:45','2025-03-27 23:12:45'),(12488,'trails',251,'What type of trail is Passage 39?','This is a point-to-point trail, which means you will start at one point and finish at another, making transportation arrangements necessary.','2025-03-27 23:12:45','2025-03-27 23:12:45'),(12489,'trails',251,'What is the incline and decline like on this trail?','Hikers will experience an incline of approximately 1515 feet and a decline of about 738 feet, offering a bit of challenge without being too strenuous.','2025-03-27 23:12:45','2025-03-27 23:12:45'),(12490,'trails',251,'What is the average and maximum grade of the trail?','The average grade is a gentle 0.03%, while the maximum grade reaches 0.15%, making for a comfortable hiking experience.','2025-03-27 23:12:45','2025-03-27 23:12:45'),(12491,'trails',251,'What are the geographic coordinates for Passage 39?','The coordinates are approximately 36.217° latitude and -112.057° longitude, placing it on the majestic North Rim of the Grand Canyon.','2025-03-27 23:12:45','2025-03-27 23:12:45'),(12492,'trails',251,'Why does Passage 39 need adoption?','The trail is currently in need of dedicated individuals or groups to help maintain and preserve its natural beauty, ensuring a great experience for future hikers.','2025-03-27 23:12:45','2025-03-27 23:12:45'),(12493,'trails',251,'What can I expect to see along Passage 39?','Hikers can expect breathtaking views of the Grand Canyon\'s incredible landscapes, featuring unique rock formations and diverse flora and fauna.','2025-03-27 23:12:45','2025-03-27 23:12:45'),(12494,'trails',252,'What is the Rainbow Rim Trail #10?','The Rainbow Rim Trail #10 is a remote and picturesque singletrack trail that lines the North Rim of the Grand Canyon. It\'s ideal for those seeking to enjoy nature, offering various camping options and breathtaking views along the journey.','2025-03-27 23:12:53','2025-03-27 23:12:53'),(12495,'trails',252,'How can I camp along the Rainbow Rim Trail?','There are ample primitive camping spots available at five different overlook points along the trail. Many hikers and bikers opt to set up camp at Locust Point, a midway point, to split the trail into two enjoyable out-and-back rides.','2025-03-27 23:12:53','2025-03-27 23:12:53'),(12496,'trails',252,'What should I be aware of regarding trail conditions and services?','The Rainbow Rim Trail is situated in a very remote area, so hikers should come prepared for backcountry conditions. Be sure to bring all necessities, including food and water, as there are no services available nearby.','2025-03-27 23:12:53','2025-03-27 23:12:53'),(12497,'trails',252,'What is the best direction to ride or hike the trail?','While many riders prefer the flow from north to south, you can enjoy the trail in either direction. Camping at Locust Point allows for flexible exploration of the trail in segments.','2025-03-27 23:12:53','2025-03-27 23:12:53'),(12498,'trails',252,'Is the Rainbow Rim Trail suitable for all types of users?','Although it is said that around 90% of users are mountain bikers, the trail is also popular among hikers and horseback riders, making it accessible for various outdoor enthusiasts.','2025-03-27 23:12:53','2025-03-27 23:12:53'),(12499,'trails',252,'What is the overall difficulty and elevation of the trail?','The Rainbow Rim Trail is rated as intermediate in difficulty. It has a highest elevation of 7,493 feet and maintains a slight incline overall, with a total trail length of 17.8 miles.','2025-03-27 23:12:53','2025-03-27 23:12:53'),(12500,'trails',252,'What are the notable features of the Rainbow Rim Trail?','This trail boasts stunning views, abundant wildflowers, and diverse wildlife encounters throughout, enhancing the hiking and biking experience.','2025-03-27 23:12:53','2025-03-27 23:12:53'),(12501,'trails',252,'Are dogs allowed on the Rainbow Rim Trail?','Yes, dogs are welcome on the trail, but they must be leashed to ensure the safety of all trail users and wildlife.','2025-03-27 23:12:53','2025-03-27 23:12:53'),(12502,'trails',252,'What type of vehicles can access the trailhead?','The forest roads leading to the Rainbow Rim are manageable for two-wheel drive vehicles, although they may not be in the best condition.','2025-03-27 23:12:53','2025-03-27 23:12:53'),(12503,'trails',252,'Can you describe the incline and decline of the trail?','The trail features a total incline of 1,517 feet and a decline of 1,491 feet, providing a gentle grade that makes for a pleasant hiking or biking experience.','2025-03-27 23:12:53','2025-03-27 23:12:53'),(12504,'trails',253,'What is the name of the trail I will be hiking on?','You will be hiking on Passage 40 of the Arizona Trail, exploring the beautiful Kaibab Plateau South.','2025-03-27 23:13:03','2025-03-27 23:13:03'),(12505,'trails',253,'What are the main features of this trail?','The trail offers breathtaking views of striking red rock canyons and towering ponderosa pines, making for a picturesque hiking experience.','2025-03-27 23:13:03','2025-03-27 23:13:03'),(12506,'trails',253,'What is the difficulty level of the trail?','The trail is classified as easy, making it accessible for hikers of various skill levels.','2025-03-27 23:13:03','2025-03-27 23:13:03'),(12507,'trails',253,'What is the length of the trail?','The total length of the trail is 21.4 miles, providing ample opportunity for exploration.','2025-03-27 23:13:03','2025-03-27 23:13:03'),(12508,'trails',253,'What is the highest elevation point on the trail?','The highest elevation you will reach on this trail is 8,496 feet.','2025-03-27 23:13:03','2025-03-27 23:13:03'),(12509,'trails',253,'What is the lowest elevation point on the trail?','Interestingly, the lowest elevation on the trail is also 8,496 feet, indicating a relatively flat route.','2025-03-27 23:13:03','2025-03-27 23:13:03'),(12510,'trails',253,'What is the overall incline and decline of the trail?','The trail has an incline of 1,916 feet and a decline of 2,069 feet, providing a gently rolling terrain.','2025-03-27 23:13:03','2025-03-27 23:13:03'),(12511,'trails',253,'What is the average grade of the trail?','The average grade of the trail is 0.04%, which means it\'s quite manageable for hikers.','2025-03-27 23:13:03','2025-03-27 23:13:03'),(12512,'trails',253,'What is the maximum grade on the trail?','The steepest part of the trail features a maximum grade of 0.17%, ensuring a comfortable hike.','2025-03-27 23:13:03','2025-03-27 23:13:03'),(12513,'trails',253,'What are the coordinates of the trail?','The trail is located at a latitude of 36.3377 and a longitude of -112.093.','2025-03-27 23:13:03','2025-03-27 23:13:03'),(12514,'trails',253,'Is this trail in need of any maintenance or adoption?','Yes, the trail currently needs adoption, indicating that it could benefit from the attention of dedicated volunteers.','2025-03-27 23:13:03','2025-03-27 23:13:03'),(12515,'trails',253,'What type of trail is this?','The trail is a point-to-point route, allowing for a linear hiking experience.','2025-03-27 23:13:03','2025-03-27 23:13:03'),(12516,'trails',254,'What is the Granite Narrows Route?','The Granite Narrows Route is an adventurous, well-traveled trail that connects Tapeats and Deer Creek, offering breathtaking views and a unique perspective of the stunning Granite Narrows section of the Colorado River.','2025-03-27 23:13:12','2025-03-27 23:13:12'),(12517,'trails',254,'How long is the Granite Narrows Route?','The route spans approximately 3.0 miles from the confluence of Tapeats Creek and the Colorado River to just above the Deer Creek Narrows.','2025-03-27 23:13:12','2025-03-27 23:13:12'),(12518,'trails',254,'What is the difficulty level of the trail?','The trail is considered difficult, requiring good endurance and some rock-hopping skills, particularly along the Colorado River section.','2025-03-27 23:13:12','2025-03-27 23:13:12'),(12519,'trails',254,'What are the elevation details on the trail?','The route has a highest elevation of 1972 feet and a lowest elevation of 1972 feet, indicating that the trail maintains a relatively consistent elevation throughout.','2025-03-27 23:13:12','2025-03-27 23:13:12'),(12520,'trails',254,'What kind of amenities or features can hikers expect?','Hikers can enjoy fantastic views and access to river and creek scenery along the trail. However, amenities are minimal as the route is unmaintained.','2025-03-27 23:13:12','2025-03-27 23:13:12'),(12521,'trails',254,'Are dogs allowed on the Granite Narrows Route?','It\'s unclear if dogs are permitted on this trail, so hikers should check local regulations before bringing their pets.','2025-03-27 23:13:12','2025-03-27 23:13:12'),(12522,'trails',254,'Is the trail well marked?','Yes, the Granite Narrows Route is generally straightforward to navigate, marked by cairns along the pathway, although some route-finding skills may be needed.','2025-03-27 23:13:12','2025-03-27 23:13:12'),(12523,'trails',254,'What are the challenging sections of the trail?','There are two notable challenging areas: one section just east of Bonita Creek involves steep and loose down-climbing when traveling from east to west; another section, a bit west of Bonita Creek, includes a ledge traverse that has considerable exposure.','2025-03-27 23:13:12','2025-03-27 23:13:12'),(12524,'trails',254,'What is the incline and decline on this trail?','The trail features an incline of about 812 feet and a decline of approximately 476 feet, contributing to its challenging nature.','2025-03-27 23:13:12','2025-03-27 23:13:12'),(12525,'trails',254,'What are the environmental conditions like on the trail?','The trail has a southern exposure, which can lead to hot conditions with minimal shade, so hikers should be prepared for warm weather, especially during the day.','2025-03-27 23:13:12','2025-03-27 23:13:12'),(12526,'trails',254,'Can the Granite Narrows Route be accessed from both ends?','Yes, hikers can access the Granite Narrows Route from either end, starting at the confluence of Tapeats Creek and the Colorado River on the east or just above the Deer Creek Narrows on the west.','2025-03-27 23:13:12','2025-03-27 23:13:12'),(12527,'trails',255,'What is the Granite Narrows High Route?','The Granite Narrows High Route is an alternative hiking trail that offers a higher path through the narrows, providing hikers with stunning panoramic views while avoiding the more exposed sections found on the lower trail.','2025-03-27 23:13:26','2025-03-27 23:13:26'),(12528,'trails',255,'How does the Granite Narrows High Route compare to the lower Granite Narrows Route?','While the Granite Narrows High Route is less direct than the lower route, it ascends higher above the river, which helps hikers sidestep the most exposed areas of the lower trail.','2025-03-27 23:13:26','2025-03-27 23:13:26'),(12529,'trails',255,'What is the difficulty level of the Granite Narrows High Route?','This trail is considered to be of intermediate to difficult level, making it suitable for hikers seeking an engaging challenge.','2025-03-27 23:13:26','2025-03-27 23:13:26'),(12530,'trails',255,'What is the highest elevation along the Granite Narrows High Route?','The route reaches a peak elevation of 2,077 feet.','2025-03-27 23:13:26','2025-03-27 23:13:26'),(12531,'trails',255,'What is the total length of the Granite Narrows High Route?','The trail spans approximately 1.4 miles from start to finish.','2025-03-27 23:13:26','2025-03-27 23:13:26'),(12532,'trails',255,'Is the Granite Narrows High Route a loop or point to point?','The Granite Narrows High Route is a point-to-point trail.','2025-03-27 23:13:26','2025-03-27 23:13:26'),(12533,'trails',255,'What are the total elevation changes on the Granite Narrows High Route?','Hikers will encounter an incline of 454 feet and a decline of 39 feet along the trail.','2025-03-27 23:13:26','2025-03-27 23:13:26'),(12534,'trails',255,'What is the average and maximum grade of the trail?','The average grade of the Granite Narrows High Route is about 0.07%, with a maximum grade reaching up to 0.41%.','2025-03-27 23:13:26','2025-03-27 23:13:26'),(12535,'trails',255,'What features can hikers expect on the Granite Narrows High Route?','This trail is popular for backpacking and offers diverse features, including access to a river or creek and breathtaking views of the surrounding landscape.','2025-03-27 23:13:26','2025-03-27 23:13:26'),(12536,'trails',255,'Are dogs permitted on the Granite Narrows High Route?','Information regarding dog access on this trail is currently unknown.','2025-03-27 23:13:26','2025-03-27 23:13:26'),(12537,'trails',255,'What are the geographical coordinates of the Granite Narrows High Route?','The trail is located at a latitude of 36.3806 and a longitude of -112.488.','2025-03-27 23:13:26','2025-03-27 23:13:26'),(12538,'trails',257,'What is the total length of the Sand Caves trail?','The Sand Caves trail covers a distance of 5.4 miles.','2025-03-27 23:13:34','2025-03-27 23:13:34'),(12539,'trails',257,'When is the best time to hike the Sand Caves?','The Sand Caves can be enjoyed year-round, making it a great option any season.','2025-03-27 23:13:34','2025-03-27 23:13:34'),(12540,'trails',257,'How difficult is the Sand Caves trail?','The trail is considered moderate in difficulty, suitable for those with some hiking experience.','2025-03-27 23:13:35','2025-03-27 23:13:35'),(12541,'trails',257,'What is the elevation of the Sand Caves?','The elevation at the Sand Caves is approximately 5,577 feet.','2025-03-27 23:13:35','2025-03-27 23:13:35'),(12542,'trails',257,'Can I drive to the Sand Caves in a standard car?','Yes, the trailhead is accessible with a 2WD vehicle.','2025-03-27 23:13:35','2025-03-27 23:13:35'),(12543,'trails',257,'Are pets allowed on the Sand Caves trail?','Unfortunately, pets are not permitted on this trail.','2025-03-27 23:13:35','2025-03-27 23:13:35'),(12544,'trails',257,'Do I need a reservation to hike the Sand Caves?','No reservations are necessary to access the Sand Caves.','2025-03-27 23:13:35','2025-03-27 23:13:35'),(12545,'trails',257,'How long does it typically take to hike the Sand Caves?','On average, hikers spend between 1 to 2 hours exploring the trail.','2025-03-27 23:13:35','2025-03-27 23:13:35'),(12546,'trails',257,'What type of vehicle is recommended for accessing the Sand Caves?','A standard car works well for reaching the Sand Caves.','2025-03-27 23:13:35','2025-03-27 23:13:35'),(12547,'trails',257,'How do I get to the Sand Caves from Kanab?','To reach the Sand Caves, drive 5.4 miles north on Highway 69 from Kanab. After passing mile post 69, take a right onto Best Friends Road. The parking area will be on your left where you can find a well-marked trail heading north.','2025-03-27 23:13:35','2025-03-27 23:13:35'),(12548,'trails',257,'Can you describe the Sand Caves?','These unique sand caves are located just 3 miles north of Kanab, formed during a brief mining operation. They offer stunning cave structures, so please respect the site and avoid altering or damaging the formations during your exploration.','2025-03-27 23:13:35','2025-03-27 23:13:35'),(12549,'trails',257,'What other attractions are nearby the Sand Caves?','If you have extra time, consider visiting Moqui Cave further north on Highway 89. You can also explore nearby dinosaur tracks, rock collections, Native American arches, and enjoy shopping in Kanab.','2025-03-27 23:13:35','2025-03-27 23:13:35'),(12550,'trails',258,'What is the distance of the Marble Canyon Loop?','The Marble Canyon Loop spans approximately 190 miles.','2025-03-27 23:13:41','2025-03-27 23:13:41'),(12551,'trails',258,'When is the best time to hike the Marble Canyon Loop?','The trail is best explored during seven months of the year, providing ample opportunities for adventure.','2025-03-27 23:13:41','2025-03-27 23:13:41'),(12552,'trails',258,'What is the difficulty level of the Marble Canyon Loop?','This trail is considered easy, making it suitable for hikers of all experience levels.','2025-03-27 23:13:41','2025-03-27 23:13:41'),(12553,'trails',258,'What are the coordinates of the Marble Canyon Loop?','The trail is located at approximately 37.048° latitude and -112.527° longitude.','2025-03-27 23:13:41','2025-03-27 23:13:41'),(12554,'trails',258,'Is the Marble Canyon Loop accessible for all hikers?','Yes, the trail is accessible, making it a great option for many outdoor enthusiasts.','2025-03-27 23:13:41','2025-03-27 23:13:41'),(12555,'trails',258,'Are pets allowed on the Marble Canyon Loop?','Unfortunately, pets are not permitted on this trail.','2025-03-27 23:13:41','2025-03-27 23:13:41'),(12556,'trails',258,'Do I need a reservation to hike the Marble Canyon Loop?','No reservations are required to hike this trail, allowing for spontaneity in your travel plans.','2025-03-27 23:13:41','2025-03-27 23:13:41'),(12557,'trails',258,'How long does it take to hike the Marble Canyon Loop?','The average time to complete the hike is not specified, but it invites hikers to enjoy at their own pace.','2025-03-27 23:13:41','2025-03-27 23:13:41'),(12558,'trails',258,'What type of vehicle is ideal for reaching the Marble Canyon Loop?','A standard car is sufficient for accessing the trailhead.','2025-03-27 23:13:41','2025-03-27 23:13:41'),(12559,'trails',258,'How do I get to the Marble Canyon Loop?','The trail begins in Kanab, Utah, and follows the scenic Highway 89A.','2025-03-27 23:13:41','2025-03-27 23:13:41'),(12560,'trails',258,'Can you describe the scenery along the Marble Canyon Loop?','The Marble Canyon Loop showcases breathtaking views of sandstone cliffs, sagebrush desert, and pine and juniper ridges, offering wonderful sightseeing opportunities.','2025-03-27 23:13:41','2025-03-27 23:13:41'),(12561,'trails',258,'What additional information can you share about the Marble Canyon Loop?','Kanab, known as the Old West Town, serves as a popular basecamp for exploring the natural wonders of the region. Start planning your adventure at www.VisitSouthernUtah.com.','2025-03-27 23:13:41','2025-03-27 23:13:41'),(12562,'trails',259,'What is the distance of the Inchworm Arch trail?','The total distance for the Inchworm Arch hike is a short 0.25 miles round trip.','2025-03-27 23:13:56','2025-03-27 23:13:56'),(12563,'trails',259,'What is the best season to hike Inchworm Arch?','This trail can be enjoyed year-round, making it a great option regardless of the season.','2025-03-27 23:13:56','2025-03-27 23:13:56'),(12564,'trails',259,'How would you rate the difficulty of the Inchworm Arch hike?','The hike is rated as easy, making it accessible for most hikers.','2025-03-27 23:13:56','2025-03-27 23:13:56'),(12565,'trails',259,'What is the elevation of Inchworm Arch?','The trail reaches an elevation of 5,854 feet.','2025-03-27 23:13:56','2025-03-27 23:13:56'),(12566,'trails',259,'What are the GPS coordinates for Inchworm Arch?','The coordinates for the trail are latitude 37.10037 and longitude 112.33401.','2025-03-27 23:13:56','2025-03-27 23:13:56'),(12567,'trails',259,'What type of vehicle is required to access Inchworm Arch?','To reach Inchworm Arch, you will need an ATV or a 4WD vehicle due to the terrain.','2025-03-27 23:13:56','2025-03-27 23:13:56'),(12568,'trails',259,'Are pets allowed on the Inchworm Arch trail?','Unfortunately, pets are not permitted on this trail.','2025-03-27 23:13:56','2025-03-27 23:13:56'),(12569,'trails',259,'Is a reservation needed to hike Inchworm Arch?','No reservations are required to hike Inchworm Arch.','2025-03-27 23:13:56','2025-03-27 23:13:56'),(12570,'trails',259,'How long does it typically take to hike to Inchworm Arch?','Most hikers spend about half a day enjoying the hike to Inchworm Arch.','2025-03-27 23:13:56','2025-03-27 23:13:56'),(12571,'trails',259,'What is the best way to get to the Inchworm Arch trail?','To get to the trailhead, drive east on HWY 89 from Kanab, turning left at Johnson Canyon. After traveling 9.1 miles, you\'ll find the Nephi Posture Trailhead on your right, where you can unload your ATV. Follow road #556 for about 8 miles, then turn right onto road #558, continuing for a mile before taking the first left and proceeding 1.5 miles. Stay left at the fork and you\'ll eventually reach a brown \'No Vehicles\' sign, where you can hike down the sand hill behind it.','2025-03-27 23:13:56','2025-03-27 23:13:56'),(12572,'trails',259,'Can you describe Inchworm Arch?','Inchworm Arch was named by a group of Kando Boy Scouts during a backpacking trip. It has become a beloved local attraction, known for its unique appearance resembling an inchworm when viewed from a specific angle. To fully appreciate this natural wonder, hikers must descend into the canyon and gaze up at the arch. Getting there requires a 4WD or ATV due to the deep sands, but the journey offers stunning views of the White Cliffs along the way.','2025-03-27 23:13:56','2025-03-27 23:13:56'),(12573,'trails',259,'What additional information should hikers know before visiting Inchworm Arch?','Hikers should consider this disclaimer: the provided map and directions are for general reference only. Always verify local road and weather conditions before heading out. Stick to designated routes, and be aware that dirt roads can be impassable when wet. Respect private property, and prepare for a wilderness adventure by bringing extra water, food, sunscreen, and supplies. Note that cell phone service is typically unavailable in most areas. Keep the park pristine by not removing artifacts or defacing rock art, and practice Leave No Trace principles. For any inquiries, you can contact 435.644.5033.','2025-03-27 23:13:56','2025-03-27 23:13:56'),(12574,'trails',164,'What is the Grapevine Trail like?','The Grapevine Trail offers a scenic hike where you can appreciate the beauty of Church Rocks, along with a short doubletrack connector.','2025-03-28 00:09:36','2025-03-28 00:09:36'),(12575,'trails',164,'What is the difficulty level of the Grapevine Trail?','This trail is rated as easy, making it suitable for hikers of all skill levels.','2025-03-28 00:09:36','2025-03-28 00:09:36'),(12576,'trails',164,'What is the highest elevation on the trail?','The highest point you will reach on the Grapevine Trail is 3,083 feet.','2025-03-28 00:09:36','2025-03-28 00:09:36'),(12577,'trails',164,'What is the lowest elevation on the trail?','The lowest elevation along the Grapevine Trail is also 3,083 feet, indicating a relatively flat route.','2025-03-28 00:09:36','2025-03-28 00:09:36'),(12578,'trails',164,'How long is the Grapevine Trail?','The total length of the Grapevine Trail is 1.0 mile.','2025-03-28 00:09:36','2025-03-28 00:09:36'),(12579,'trails',164,'What type of trail is the Grapevine Trail?','This trail is a point-to-point hike, which means you will start at one point and end at another.','2025-03-28 00:09:36','2025-03-28 00:09:36'),(12580,'trails',164,'What is the total incline on the Grapevine Trail?','During your hike, you will encounter a total incline of 193 feet.','2025-03-28 00:09:36','2025-03-28 00:09:36'),(12581,'trails',164,'What is the average grade of the Grapevine Trail?','The average grade for the Grapevine Trail is about 0.04%, making it a very gentle hike.','2025-03-28 00:09:36','2025-03-28 00:09:36'),(12582,'trails',164,'What is the maximum grade you will encounter on the trail?','The steepest section of the trail reaches a maximum grade of 0.07%.','2025-03-28 00:09:36','2025-03-28 00:09:36'),(12583,'trails',164,'What are the latitude and longitude coordinates for the Grapevine Trail?','The coordinates for the Grapevine Trail are approximately 37.1505° latitude and -113.489° longitude.','2025-03-28 00:09:36','2025-03-28 00:09:36'),(12584,'trails',168,'What is the difficulty level of the Mustang Pass trail?','The Mustang Pass trail is rated as Intermediate to Difficult, making it suitable for experienced hikers.','2025-03-28 00:09:42','2025-03-28 00:09:42'),(12585,'trails',168,'What is the total length of the Mustang Pass trail?','The trail stretches for approximately 2.8 miles, providing a compact yet engaging hiking experience.','2025-03-28 00:09:42','2025-03-28 00:09:42'),(12586,'trails',168,'What type of trail is Mustang Pass?','Mustang Pass is a point-to-point trail, meaning you\'ll start at one location and finish at another.','2025-03-28 00:09:42','2025-03-28 00:09:42'),(12587,'trails',168,'What are the elevation details for Mustang Pass?','The trail reaches a maximum elevation of 3,198 feet, with the lowest point also at 3,198 feet. There is an elevation gain of 348 feet and a decline of 305 feet along the route.','2025-03-28 00:09:42','2025-03-28 00:09:42'),(12588,'trails',168,'What kind of terrain can hikers expect on the Mustang Pass trail?','Hikers will navigate a rocky singletrack trail through an area that has been affected by fire, featuring unique landscapes and stunning views of the surrounding rock formations.','2025-03-28 00:09:42','2025-03-28 00:09:42'),(12589,'trails',168,'What is the average and maximum grade of the Mustang Pass trail?','The trail has an average grade of 0.04% and a maximum grade of 0.09%, indicating a relatively gentle slope overall.','2025-03-28 00:09:42','2025-03-28 00:09:42'),(12590,'trails',168,'Where is Mustang Pass located geographically?','Mustang Pass is situated at a latitude of 37.1665 and a longitude of -113.526, placing it in a remarkable hiking region.','2025-03-28 00:09:42','2025-03-28 00:09:42'),(12591,'trails',169,'What is the length of the Church Rocks hike?','The Church Rocks trail covers a distance of 2.3 miles.','2025-03-28 00:09:51','2025-03-28 00:09:51'),(12592,'trails',169,'What type of trail is Church Rocks?','The Church Rocks hike is a point-to-point trail.','2025-03-28 00:09:51','2025-03-28 00:09:51'),(12593,'trails',169,'What is the difficulty level of the Church Rocks hike?','This hike is considered intermediate to difficult, suitable for hikers with some experience.','2025-03-28 00:09:51','2025-03-28 00:09:51'),(12594,'trails',169,'What is the highest elevation reached on the Church Rocks trail?','The highest elevation on this trail is 3,212 feet.','2025-03-28 00:09:51','2025-03-28 00:09:51'),(12595,'trails',169,'What is the lowest elevation on the Church Rocks trail?','The lowest elevation on the Hiking Church Rocks trail is also 3,212 feet.','2025-03-28 00:09:51','2025-03-28 00:09:51'),(12596,'trails',169,'What is the overall incline of the Church Rocks hike?','The total incline on the trail is 211 feet.','2025-03-28 00:09:51','2025-03-28 00:09:51'),(12597,'trails',169,'What is the overall decline of the Church Rocks hike?','The trail features a total decline of 227 feet.','2025-03-28 00:09:51','2025-03-28 00:09:51'),(12598,'trails',169,'What is the average grade of the Church Rocks trail?','The Church Rocks trail has an average grade of 0.04%.','2025-03-28 00:09:51','2025-03-28 00:09:51'),(12599,'trails',169,'What is the maximum grade on the Church Rocks trail?','The maximum grade encountered on this hike is 0.11%.','2025-03-28 00:09:51','2025-03-28 00:09:51'),(12600,'trails',169,'What can I expect from the surface of the trail?','Hikers will find mostly smooth rocks along the trail, making for an enjoyable hike.','2025-03-28 00:09:51','2025-03-28 00:09:51'),(12601,'trails',169,'What are the geographical coordinates of the Church Rocks trail?','The Church Rocks trail is located at Latitude 37.1614 and Longitude -113.471.','2025-03-28 00:09:51','2025-03-28 00:09:51'),(12602,'trails',170,'What can I expect to see on the Bracken Connector trail?','The Bracken Connector trail offers stunning desert vistas and panoramic views of the beautiful landscapes of southern Utah and northern Arizona.','2025-03-28 00:10:01','2025-03-28 00:10:01'),(12603,'trails',170,'What is the difficulty level of the Bracken Connector trail?','This trail is considered difficult, so be prepared for a challenging hike.','2025-03-28 00:10:01','2025-03-28 00:10:01'),(12604,'trails',170,'What is the highest elevation on the Bracken Connector trail?','The highest point you will reach on this trail is 3,215 feet.','2025-03-28 00:10:02','2025-03-28 00:10:02'),(12605,'trails',170,'What is the lowest elevation on the Bracken Connector trail?','Interestingly, both the highest and lowest elevations on the trail are 3,215 feet, offering a relatively flat hike.','2025-03-28 00:10:02','2025-03-28 00:10:02'),(12606,'trails',170,'How long is the Bracken Connector trail?','The trail stretches for 0.4 miles as a point-to-point route.','2025-03-28 00:10:02','2025-03-28 00:10:02'),(12607,'trails',170,'What is the incline and decline on the Bracken Connector trail?','The trail features a modest incline of 23 feet and a more noticeable decline of 94 feet.','2025-03-28 00:10:02','2025-03-28 00:10:02'),(12608,'trails',170,'What is the average and maximum grade of the Bracken Connector trail?','The average grade is fairly gentle at 0.06%, while the maximum grade can reach up to 0.12%.','2025-03-28 00:10:02','2025-03-28 00:10:02'),(12609,'trails',170,'What are the geographical coordinates of the Bracken Connector trail?','You can find the trail at a latitude of 37.1611 and a longitude of -113.476.','2025-03-28 00:10:02','2025-03-28 00:10:02'),(12610,'trails',171,'What is the experience like on the Spanish Wash trail?','Hikers can expect a challenging trek through deep sand, offering an engaging experience with breathtaking desert vistas.','2025-03-28 00:10:11','2025-03-28 00:10:11'),(12611,'trails',171,'How difficult is the Spanish Wash trail?','The trail is categorized as easy to intermediate, making it accessible for a range of hikers.','2025-03-28 00:10:11','2025-03-28 00:10:11'),(12612,'trails',171,'What is the highest elevation on the trail?','The trail reaches a maximum elevation of 3216 feet.','2025-03-28 00:10:11','2025-03-28 00:10:11'),(12613,'trails',171,'What is the lowest elevation along the Spanish Wash trail?','The trail maintains a consistent elevation of 3216 feet throughout its length.','2025-03-28 00:10:11','2025-03-28 00:10:11'),(12614,'trails',171,'How long is the Spanish Wash trail?','The trail stretches for 0.6 miles, making it a relatively short hike.','2025-03-28 00:10:11','2025-03-28 00:10:11'),(12615,'trails',171,'What type of trail is Spanish Wash?','Spanish Wash is a point-to-point trail, requiring hikers to plan for a return journey.','2025-03-28 00:10:11','2025-03-28 00:10:11'),(12616,'tra