itable for a wide range of skill levels.','2025-03-28 00:11:36','2025-03-28 00:11:36'),(12702,'trails',188,'What is the length of the Desert Canyon Loop?','The trail stretches for 2.5 miles, providing a manageable distance for both hiking and biking.','2025-03-28 00:11:36','2025-03-28 00:11:36'),(12703,'trails',188,'What type of trail is the Desert Canyon Loop?','This trail is a point-to-point route, offering a clear starting and ending point for your outdoor adventure.','2025-03-28 00:11:36','2025-03-28 00:11:36'),(12704,'trails',188,'What is the elevation range of the Desert Canyon Loop?','The highest elevation on the trail is 2,722 feet, and it maintains this elevation throughout, making it relatively flat.','2025-03-28 00:11:36','2025-03-28 00:11:36'),(12705,'trails',188,'What are the incline and decline statistics for the Desert Canyon Loop?','The trail features an incline of 233 feet and a decline of 184 feet, providing a gentle grade for travelers.','2025-03-28 00:11:36','2025-03-28 00:11:36'),(12706,'trails',188,'What is the average grade of the Desert Canyon Loop?','The average grade of the trail is approximately 0.03%, indicating a very gradual slope throughout your hike or ride.','2025-03-28 00:11:36','2025-03-28 00:11:36'),(12707,'trails',188,'What is the maximum grade of the Desert Canyon Loop?','The maximum grade encountered on the trail reaches 0.07%, ensuring a mostly easy experience.','2025-03-28 00:11:36','2025-03-28 00:11:36'),(12708,'trails',188,'What can I expect to see along the Desert Canyon Loop?','Hikers and bikers will enjoy breathtaking views of desert landscapes, making for a visually stunning trip.','2025-03-28 00:11:36','2025-03-28 00:11:36'),(12709,'trails',188,'What are the geographical coordinates for the Desert Canyon Loop?','The trail is located at a latitude of 37.0128 and a longitude of -113.516, so you can easily find it on a map.','2025-03-28 00:11:36','2025-03-28 00:11:36'),(12710,'trails',190,'What is the Maverick trail known for?','The Maverick trail offers a remarkable hiking experience with its stunning red rock formations, majestic sandstone cliffs, and incredible panoramic views of the landscapes in southern Utah and northern Arizona.','2025-03-28 00:11:45','2025-03-28 00:11:45'),(12711,'trails',190,'What is the difficulty level of the Maverick trail?','The Maverick trail is considered to be of intermediate difficulty, making it suitable for hikers with some experience.','2025-03-28 00:11:45','2025-03-28 00:11:45'),(12712,'trails',190,'What is the highest elevation along the Maverick trail?','The highest point on the Maverick trail reaches an elevation of 2807 feet.','2025-03-28 00:11:45','2025-03-28 00:11:45'),(12713,'trails',190,'What is the lowest elevation along the Maverick trail?','The lowest elevation on the Maverick trail is also 2807 feet, indicating a relatively flat hike.','2025-03-28 00:11:45','2025-03-28 00:11:45'),(12714,'trails',190,'How long is the Maverick trail?','The total length of the Maverick trail is 1.0 mile, making it a manageable hike for a day trip.','2025-03-28 00:11:45','2025-03-28 00:11:45'),(12715,'trails',190,'What type of trail is the Maverick trail?','The Maverick trail is a point-to-point trail, meaning hikers will need to start and finish at different points.','2025-03-28 00:11:45','2025-03-28 00:11:45'),(12716,'trails',190,'What are the incline and decline measurements on the Maverick trail?','The trail features an incline of 319 feet and a very minimal decline of just 5 feet.','2025-03-28 00:11:45','2025-03-28 00:11:45'),(12717,'trails',190,'What is the average grade of the Maverick trail?','The average grade of the Maverick trail is 0.06%, which suggests a relatively flat experience overall.','2025-03-28 00:11:45','2025-03-28 00:11:45'),(12718,'trails',190,'What is the maximum grade encountered on the Maverick trail?','The Maverick trail has a maximum grade of 0.17%, making it suitable for various skill levels.','2025-03-28 00:11:45','2025-03-28 00:11:45'),(12719,'trails',190,'What are the geographical coordinates of the Maverick trail?','The Maverick trail is located at approximately 37.1291° latitude and -113.663° longitude.','2025-03-28 00:11:45','2025-03-28 00:11:45'),(12720,'trails',191,'What can I expect from the Stucki Springs loop on the Bearclaw Poppy trail network?','The Stucki Springs loop offers a wonderful opportunity to explore southern Utah\'s stunning landscape, complete with breathtaking views throughout your hike.','2025-03-28 00:11:54','2025-03-28 00:11:54'),(12721,'trails',191,'What is the difficulty level of the Stucki Springs loop?','This trail is considered to have an intermediate difficulty level, making it suitable for those with some hiking experience.','2025-03-28 00:11:54','2025-03-28 00:11:54'),(12722,'trails',191,'What is the highest and lowest elevation on the Stucki Springs loop?','The trail has a highest elevation of 2846 feet and it does not change significantly in elevation as the lowest elevation is also 2846 feet.','2025-03-28 00:11:54','2025-03-28 00:11:54'),(12723,'trails',191,'How long is the Stucki Springs loop?','The total length of the loop is approximately 5.7 miles, offering a satisfying hike in a beautiful setting.','2025-03-28 00:11:54','2025-03-28 00:11:54'),(12724,'trails',191,'Is the Stucki Springs loop a point-to-point trail?','Yes, this trail is classified as a point-to-point trail, which means you will start and finish at different locations.','2025-03-28 00:11:54','2025-03-28 00:11:54'),(12725,'trails',191,'What is the incline and decline when hiking the Stucki Springs loop?','During your hike, you will encounter an incline of 320 feet and a decline of 490 feet, which adds some challenge to the trek.','2025-03-28 00:11:54','2025-03-28 00:11:54'),(12726,'trails',191,'What is the average and maximum grade of the trail?','The average grade of the Stucki Springs loop is a gentle 0.03%, with a maximum grade reaching up to 0.06%.','2025-03-28 00:11:54','2025-03-28 00:11:54'),(12727,'trails',191,'What are the geographical coordinates of the Stucki Springs loop?','The trail is located at a latitude of 37.0995 and a longitude of -113.676, placing it in the beautiful southern Utah scenery.','2025-03-28 00:11:54','2025-03-28 00:11:54'),(12728,'trails',192,'What is the Bearclaw Poppy Trail?','The Bearclaw Poppy Trail is a picturesque route that connects to several other trails, offering breathtaking panoramic views of the landscapes in southern Utah and northern Arizona.','2025-03-28 00:12:00','2025-03-28 00:12:00'),(12729,'trails',192,'What is the difficulty level of the Bearclaw Poppy Trail?','This trail is categorized as intermediate, making it suitable for hikers with some experience.','2025-03-28 00:12:00','2025-03-28 00:12:00'),(12730,'trails',192,'What are the highest and lowest elevations on the trail?','The Bearclaw Poppy Trail features a consistent elevation at 2575 feet, making it a relatively level hike.','2025-03-28 00:12:00','2025-03-28 00:12:00'),(12731,'trails',192,'How long is the Bearclaw Poppy Trail?','The trail stretches for 3.9 miles, providing a decent hike for those looking to explore the area.','2025-03-28 00:12:00','2025-03-28 00:12:00'),(12732,'trails',192,'Is the Bearclaw Poppy Trail a loop or point-to-point?','The Bearclaw Poppy Trail is a point-to-point hike, which means you\'ll start at one end and finish at the other.','2025-03-28 00:12:00','2025-03-28 00:12:00'),(12733,'trails',192,'What is the elevation gain and loss on the trail?','Hikers will experience an incline of 111 feet and a decline of 460 feet along the Bearclaw Poppy Trail.','2025-03-28 00:12:00','2025-03-28 00:12:00'),(12734,'trails',192,'What is the average and maximum grade of the trail?','The average grade of the trail is very mild at 0.03%, with a maximum grade reaching up to 0.05%.','2025-03-28 00:12:00','2025-03-28 00:12:00'),(12735,'trails',192,'What are the geographical coordinates of the Bearclaw Poppy Trail?','The trail is located at a latitude of 37.0888 and a longitude of -113.641.','2025-03-28 00:12:00','2025-03-28 00:12:00'),(12736,'trails',194,'What can I expect to see along the Deertrap Mountain Trail?','While hiking the Deertrap Mountain Trail, you\'ll encounter breathtaking views of several notable landmarks, including the Mountain of the Sun, Emerald Pool, The Twin Brothers, Angels Landing, and The Court of the Patriarchs among others.','2025-03-28 00:12:07','2025-03-28 00:12:07'),(12737,'trails',194,'What is the difficulty level of the Deertrap Mountain Trail?','The trail is classified as intermediate, making it suitable for hikers with a moderate level of experience.','2025-03-28 00:12:07','2025-03-28 00:12:07'),(12738,'trails',194,'What are the elevation details of the Deertrap Mountain Trail?','The trail has a highest elevation of 6,685 feet and varies in elevation but generally remains consistent throughout the hike.','2025-03-28 00:12:07','2025-03-28 00:12:07'),(12739,'trails',194,'How long is the Deertrap Mountain Trail?','The total length of the Deertrap Mountain Trail is approximately 2.7 miles, offering a relatively short hike to a unique viewpoint.','2025-03-28 00:12:07','2025-03-28 00:12:07'),(12740,'trails',194,'What type of trail is the Deertrap Mountain Trail?','The Deertrap Mountain Trail is a point-to-point trail, meaning you\'ll start at one location and finish at another.','2025-03-28 00:12:07','2025-03-28 00:12:07'),(12741,'trails',194,'What is the incline and decline on the Deertrap Mountain Trail?','During your hike, you can expect an incline of 334 feet and a decline of 467 feet as you navigate the terrain.','2025-03-28 00:12:07','2025-03-28 00:12:07'),(12742,'trails',194,'What is the average and maximum grade of the Deertrap Mountain Trail?','The average grade of the trail is about 6%, with some sections reaching a maximum grade of 26%.','2025-03-28 00:12:07','2025-03-28 00:12:07'),(12743,'trails',194,'What features should I look out for on the Deertrap Mountain Trail?','This trail boasts a variety of features, including opportunities for birdwatching, stunning fall colors, views of rivers and creeks, diverse wildflowers, and potential wildlife sightings.','2025-03-28 00:12:07','2025-03-28 00:12:07'),(12744,'trails',194,'Are dogs allowed on the Deertrap Mountain Trail?','Unfortunately, dogs are not permitted on this trail.','2025-03-28 00:12:07','2025-03-28 00:12:07'),(12745,'trails',194,'What are the geographical coordinates of the Deertrap Mountain Trail?','The trail is located at a latitude of 37.2527 and a longitude of -112.917.','2025-03-28 00:12:07','2025-03-28 00:12:07'),(12746,'trails',195,'What is the difficulty level of Hidden Canyon Trail?','The Hidden Canyon Trail is considered difficult due to its moderately strenuous nature and steep grades.','2025-03-28 00:12:16','2025-03-28 00:12:16'),(12747,'trails',195,'What is the total length of the Hidden Canyon Trail?','The trail measures approximately 1.1 miles from start to finish.','2025-03-28 00:12:16','2025-03-28 00:12:16'),(12748,'trails',195,'What type of trail is Hidden Canyon Trail?','It is a point-to-point trail that leads to the mouth of a narrow canyon.','2025-03-28 00:12:16','2025-03-28 00:12:16'),(12749,'trails',195,'What is the highest elevation hikers will reach on this trail?','Hikers will reach a maximum elevation of 4,746 feet along the trail.','2025-03-28 00:12:16','2025-03-28 00:12:16'),(12750,'trails',195,'What is the lowest elevation on Hidden Canyon Trail?','The lowest elevation on the trail is also 4,746 feet, as the trail starts and ends at the same height.','2025-03-28 00:12:16','2025-03-28 00:12:16'),(12751,'trails',195,'What is the total incline you can expect on the Hidden Canyon Trail?','The trail features a total incline of 520 feet.','2025-03-28 00:12:16','2025-03-28 00:12:16'),(12752,'trails',195,'What are the average and maximum grades of the trail?','The average grade of the Hidden Canyon Trail is about 0.09%, with sections reaching a maximum of 0.60% grade.','2025-03-28 00:12:16','2025-03-28 00:12:16'),(12753,'trails',195,'What unique features can hikers expect to find along the Hidden Canyon Trail?','The trail offers beautiful views, opportunities for birding, and encounters with wildlife, as well as the chance to explore a cave.','2025-03-28 00:12:16','2025-03-28 00:12:16'),(12754,'trails',195,'Are dogs allowed on Hidden Canyon Trail?','No, dogs are not permitted on this trail.','2025-03-28 00:12:16','2025-03-28 00:12:16'),(12755,'trails',195,'How should hikers prepare for steep drop-offs along the trail?','Hikers are advised to use the chains bolted to the cliff for stability, especially as the trail features long, steep drop-offs.','2025-03-28 00:12:16','2025-03-28 00:12:16'),(12756,'trails',195,'Can hikers explore beyond the designated trail on Hidden Canyon Trail?','Yes, from the mouth of the canyon, hikers can scramble further into the hanging canyon if they have a manageable fear of heights.','2025-03-28 00:12:16','2025-03-28 00:12:16'),(12757,'trails',196,'What can I expect from the views on Observation Point Trail?','Observation Point Trail offers stunning panoramic views of the canyon, with clear sights of Angel\'s Landing to the southwest and the Great White Throne directly south.','2025-03-28 00:12:29','2025-03-28 00:12:29'),(12758,'trails',196,'What is the difficulty level of the Observation Point Trail?','The trail is classified as intermediate to difficult, making it suitable for those with some hiking experience.','2025-03-28 00:12:29','2025-03-28 00:12:29'),(12759,'trails',196,'What is the elevation of Observation Point?','The highest elevation on this trail reaches 6,495 feet, providing a remarkable vantage point.','2025-03-28 00:12:29','2025-03-28 00:12:29'),(12760,'trails',196,'How long is the Observation Point Trail?','The trail stretches for 0.4 miles, making it a relatively short hike that nonetheless rewards with spectacular views.','2025-03-28 00:12:29','2025-03-28 00:12:29'),(12761,'trails',196,'What type of trail is Observation Point?','Observation Point is a point-to-point trail, meaning you will return via the same route.','2025-03-28 00:12:29','2025-03-28 00:12:29'),(12762,'trails',196,'What is the incline and decline like on the trail?','The trail has a modest incline of 28 feet and a slight decline of 5 feet, resulting in a gentle overall grade.','2025-03-28 00:12:29','2025-03-28 00:12:29'),(12763,'trails',196,'Are dogs permitted on Observation Point Trail?','No, dogs are not allowed on this trail, so please plan accordingly.','2025-03-28 00:12:29','2025-03-28 00:12:29'),(12764,'trails',196,'What features can I expect to see while hiking?','This trail provides excellent opportunities for birdwatching and wildlife spotting, in addition to its breathtaking views.','2025-03-28 00:12:29','2025-03-28 00:12:29'),(12765,'trails',196,'What are the trail\'s latitude and longitude coordinates?','The coordinates for Observation Point Trail are approximately 37.2811° latitude and -112.937° longitude.','2025-03-28 00:12:29','2025-03-28 00:12:29'),(12766,'trails',197,'Is the Weeping Rock Trail suitable for families?','Absolutely! The Weeping Rock Trail is designed to be family-friendly, with a paved path that can be managed by most individuals, making it great for families with children.','2025-03-28 00:12:38','2025-03-28 00:12:38'),(12767,'trails',197,'What can I expect to see at the end of the Weeping Rock Trail?','At the conclusion of the trail, hikers are rewarded with a breathtaking rock alcove, a unique geological feature that is truly a sight to behold.','2025-03-28 00:12:38','2025-03-28 00:12:38'),(12768,'trails',197,'How difficult is the Weeping Rock Trail?','The trail is rated as easy to intermediate. While it is somewhat steep, it is accessible to most hikers, especially given its paved surface.','2025-03-28 00:12:38','2025-03-28 00:12:38'),(12769,'trails',197,'What is the elevation range of the Weeping Rock Trail?','The trail maintains a consistent elevation at 4,372 feet for both its highest and lowest points.','2025-03-28 00:12:38','2025-03-28 00:12:38'),(12770,'trails',197,'What is the length of the Weeping Rock Trail?','The trail stretches approximately 0.2 miles, making it a short but rewarding hike.','2025-03-28 00:12:38','2025-03-28 00:12:38'),(12771,'trails',197,'What type of trail is the Weeping Rock Trail?','This trail is a point-to-point type, meaning it starts and ends at different locations, leading you to a lovely destination.','2025-03-28 00:12:38','2025-03-28 00:12:38'),(12772,'trails',197,'What is the incline of the Weeping Rock Trail?','The trail has an incline of 64 feet, which contributes to its somewhat steep nature.','2025-03-28 00:12:38','2025-03-28 00:12:38'),(12773,'trails',197,'What is the average grade of the Weeping Rock Trail?','The average grade along the Weeping Rock Trail is about 6%, providing a manageable challenge for most hikers.','2025-03-28 00:12:38','2025-03-28 00:12:38'),(12774,'trails',197,'What is the maximum grade along the Weeping Rock Trail?','The maximum grade of the trail can reach up to 14%, so be prepared for some steep sections.','2025-03-28 00:12:38','2025-03-28 00:12:38'),(12775,'trails',197,'Are there any special features along the Weeping Rock Trail?','Yes, the trail offers stunning views, especially as you approach the rock alcove at the end.','2025-03-28 00:12:38','2025-03-28 00:12:38'),(12776,'trails',197,'Are dogs allowed on the Weeping Rock Trail?','Unfortunately, dogs are not permitted on this trail, so plan accordingly if you are hiking with a pet.','2025-03-28 00:12:38','2025-03-28 00:12:38'),(12777,'trails',197,'What are the geographic coordinates for Weeping Rock Trail?','The trail is located at approximately 37.2709° latitude and -112.939° longitude.','2025-03-28 00:12:38','2025-03-28 00:12:38'),(12778,'trails',201,'What can I expect to see on the Wildcat Canyon Trail?','You will be treated to breathtaking views of the Northgate Peaks, traverse a beautiful ponderosa pine forest, and reach stunning overlooks of Wildcat Canyon.','2025-03-28 00:12:58','2025-03-28 00:12:58'),(12779,'trails',201,'Where does the Wildcat Canyon Trail begin?','The trail starts at the Wildcat Trailhead and leads you past the Northgate Peaks Trail junction.','2025-03-28 00:12:58','2025-03-28 00:12:58'),(12780,'trails',201,'Is this trail suitable for beginners?','The trail is considered intermediate in difficulty, making it better suited for those with some hiking experience.','2025-03-28 00:12:58','2025-03-28 00:12:58'),(12781,'trails',201,'What is the total length of the Wildcat Canyon Trail?','The trail spans approximately 5.9 miles, offering a fulfilling hike.','2025-03-28 00:12:58','2025-03-28 00:12:58'),(12782,'trails',201,'What kind of terrain will I encounter?','Expect a rolling backcountry terrain that features slight inclines and declines as you make your way to the West Rim Trail.','2025-03-28 00:12:58','2025-03-28 00:12:58'),(12783,'trails',201,'Are there any notable elevation changes on the trail?','Yes, the trail has a total incline of 796 feet and a decline of 327 feet, with the highest elevation reaching 6,915 feet.','2025-03-28 00:12:58','2025-03-28 00:12:58'),(12784,'trails',201,'Can I camp along the trail?','There are no established campsites along this trail, and hiking or camping requires a permit.','2025-03-28 00:12:58','2025-03-28 00:12:58'),(12785,'trails',201,'What wildlife might I see while hiking?','Hikers can enjoy opportunities for birdwatching and may encounter diverse wildlife as they explore the area.','2025-03-28 00:12:58','2025-03-28 00:12:58'),(12786,'trails',201,'Are dogs allowed on the Wildcat Canyon Trail?','Yes, leashed dogs are welcome on the trail, so you can bring your furry companion along for the adventure.','2025-03-28 00:12:58','2025-03-28 00:12:58'),(12787,'trails',201,'What are some features of the Wildcat Canyon Trail?','The trail is known for its stunning views, vibrant wildflowers, and attractive fall colors, making it beautiful in various seasons.','2025-03-28 00:12:58','2025-03-28 00:12:58'),(12788,'trails',201,'What is the geographic location of the trail?','The Wildcat Canyon Trail is located at approximately latitude 37.3398 and longitude -113.076.','2025-03-28 00:12:58','2025-03-28 00:12:58'),(12789,'trails',203,'What is the East Mesa Trail like?','The East Mesa Trail offers a scenic hike through a dense forest with stunning views of the Pink Cliffs and Brian Head Peak. Although it may not be as popular as some of the other trails in the area, it features beautiful vistas and a connection to the impressive Observation Point Trail.','2025-03-28 00:13:07','2025-03-28 00:13:07'),(12790,'trails',203,'What are the main sights along the East Mesa Trail?','Hikers can enjoy views of the Pink Cliffs, Brian Head Peak, and Bulloch Gulch, along with the surrounding canyon scenery. The trail provides access to Observation Point Trail, known for having some of the best views in Zion National Park.','2025-03-28 00:13:07','2025-03-28 00:13:07'),(12791,'trails',203,'How strenuous is the East Mesa Trail?','This trail is classified as intermediate in difficulty. It begins with a steep ascent, featuring multiple switchbacks before leveling off, making it a manageable hike once you get past the initial climb.','2025-03-28 00:13:08','2025-03-28 00:13:08'),(12792,'trails',203,'What is the elevation range of the East Mesa Trail?','The trail starts and ends at an elevation of 5,627 feet, ensuring a consistent altitude throughout the hike.','2025-03-28 00:13:08','2025-03-28 00:13:08'),(12793,'trails',203,'How long is the East Mesa Trail?','The total length of the East Mesa Trail is approximately 4.4 miles, making it a nice option for a day hike.','2025-03-28 00:13:08','2025-03-28 00:13:08'),(12794,'trails',203,'What type of trail is the East Mesa Trail?','It is a point-to-point trail, beginning at the East Rim Trail and leading through the eastern mesa before connecting to Fir Road.','2025-03-28 00:13:08','2025-03-28 00:13:08'),(12795,'trails',203,'What are the incline and decline statistics for the East Mesa Trail?','The trail has an overall incline of 1,177 feet and a decline of 278 feet, providing a varied hiking experience.','2025-03-28 00:13:08','2025-03-28 00:13:08'),(12796,'trails',203,'What are some features to enjoy on the East Mesa Trail?','Hikers will appreciate opportunities for birding, witnessing fall colors, enjoying beautiful views, and seeing wildflowers and local wildlife along the trail.','2025-03-28 00:13:08','2025-03-28 00:13:08'),(12797,'trails',203,'Are dogs allowed on the East Mesa Trail?','No, dogs are not permitted on this trail.','2025-03-28 00:13:08','2025-03-28 00:13:08'),(12798,'trails',203,'What are the GPS coordinates for the East Mesa Trail?','The trail is located at latitude 37.2742 and longitude -112.929.','2025-03-28 00:13:08','2025-03-28 00:13:08'),(12799,'trails',204,'What is the starting point of the Hop Valley Trail?','The trailhead for the Hop Valley Trail is located off Kolob Terrace Road.','2025-03-28 00:13:15','2025-03-28 00:13:15'),(12800,'trails',204,'What unique scenery can hikers expect on the Hop Valley Trail?','Hikers will enjoy expansive views of surrounding rock formations and picturesque open fields throughout the trail.','2025-03-28 00:13:15','2025-03-28 00:13:15'),(12801,'trails',204,'What makes the valley floor of Hop Valley special?','The valley floor features a stunning flat sandy bottom surrounded by impressive vertical walls, creating a captivating natural landscape.','2025-03-28 00:13:15','2025-03-28 00:13:15'),(12802,'trails',204,'How is the trail\'s terrain described?','The Hop Valley Trail consists of sandy terrain that is well worn, making it easier to navigate despite its ups and downs.','2025-03-28 00:13:15','2025-03-28 00:13:15'),(12803,'trails',204,'Are there camping options available along the trail?','Yes, there are designated camping sites located at the far end of Hop Valley, before the descent into La Verkin Creek.','2025-03-28 00:13:15','2025-03-28 00:13:15'),(12804,'trails',204,'What should hikers know about the descent into La Verkin Creek?','The descent to La Verkin Creek is quite steep, but it provides access to the remarkable Kolob Arch.','2025-03-28 00:13:15','2025-03-28 00:13:15'),(12805,'trails',204,'What is the level of difficulty for hiking the Hop Valley Trail?','The trail is rated as intermediate to difficult, suitable for more experienced hikers.','2025-03-28 00:13:15','2025-03-28 00:13:15'),(12806,'trails',204,'What is the total length of the Hop Valley Trail?','The total length of the trail is approximately 6.6 miles.','2025-03-28 00:13:15','2025-03-28 00:13:15'),(12807,'trails',204,'What is the elevation gain and loss on the trail?','The trail has an elevation gain of about 282 feet and a decline of approximately 1319 feet.','2025-03-28 00:13:15','2025-03-28 00:13:15'),(12808,'trails',204,'What is the maximum elevation reached on the trail?','The highest point along the Hop Valley Trail is 5342 feet.','2025-03-28 00:13:15','2025-03-28 00:13:15'),(12809,'trails',204,'Are dogs allowed on the Hop Valley Trail?','No, dogs are not permitted on this trail.','2025-03-28 00:13:15','2025-03-28 00:13:15'),(12810,'trails',204,'What wildlife and natural features can be observed along the trail?','Hikers may see a variety of wildlife, enjoy birding, and witness seasonal fall colors, as well as wildflowers and vibrant views.','2025-03-28 00:13:15','2025-03-28 00:13:15'),(12811,'trails',204,'What are the coordinates for Hop Valley Trail?','The trail is located at a latitude of 37.3403 and a longitude of -113.113.','2025-03-28 00:13:15','2025-03-28 00:13:15'),(12812,'trails',207,'What is the Wrangler Trail?','The Wrangler Trail is a picturesque hike in Zion National Park that connects Zion Lodge to the Court of the Patriarchs, showcasing stunning views of the Virgin River and impressive rock formations.','2025-03-28 00:13:22','2025-03-28 00:13:22'),(12813,'trails',207,'How difficult is the Wrangler Trail?','The Wrangler Trail is considered easy, making it accessible for hikers of all experience levels.','2025-03-28 00:13:22','2025-03-28 00:13:22'),(12814,'trails',207,'What is the elevation range on the Wrangler Trail?','The trail maintains a constant elevation of 4,242 feet, with very minimal incline and decline throughout.','2025-03-28 00:13:22','2025-03-28 00:13:22'),(12815,'trails',207,'What is the length of the Wrangler Trail?','This trail spans a total distance of 1.0 mile and follows a point-to-point path.','2025-03-28 00:13:22','2025-03-28 00:13:22'),(12816,'trails',207,'What kind of terrain can I expect on the Wrangler Trail?','The Wrangler Trail features a flat, easy terrain, making it perfect for a leisurely walk amidst beautiful surroundings.','2025-03-28 00:13:22','2025-03-28 00:13:22'),(12817,'trails',207,'What are some notable features along the Wrangler Trail?','Hikers can enjoy birdwatching, vibrant fall colors, views of the river, wildflowers, and potential wildlife sightings while on the trail.','2025-03-28 00:13:22','2025-03-28 00:13:22'),(12818,'trails',207,'Are dogs allowed on the Wrangler Trail?','Unfortunately, dogs are not permitted on the Wrangler Trail.','2025-03-28 00:13:22','2025-03-28 00:13:22'),(12819,'trails',207,'Where is the Wrangler Trail located?','The trail is located in Zion National Park, with coordinates of 37.2498° latitude and -112.958° longitude.','2025-03-28 00:13:22','2025-03-28 00:13:22'),(12820,'trails',211,'What is the route of the Telephone Canyon Trail?','The Telephone Canyon Trail connects Potato Hollow and Cabin Springs, offering a scenic route through a burn area and an open meadow.','2025-03-28 00:13:30','2025-03-28 00:13:30'),(12821,'trails',211,'Why might hikers choose the Telephone Canyon Trail when there is snow?','Due to its exposed nature, the trail tends to have less snow compared to other areas, making it a good option for winter hiking.','2025-03-28 00:13:30','2025-03-28 00:13:30'),(12822,'trails',211,'How challenging is the Telephone Canyon Trail?','The trail is rated as intermediate/difficult, suitable for hikers looking for a moderately challenging hike.','2025-03-28 00:13:30','2025-03-28 00:13:30'),(12823,'trails',211,'What are the elevation details of the trail?','Both the highest and lowest elevations on the trail are at 6723 feet, with a slight incline of 6 feet and a decline of 544 feet.','2025-03-28 00:13:31','2025-03-28 00:13:31'),(12824,'trails',211,'What is the total length of the Telephone Canyon Trail?','The trail stretches for 1.9 miles from Potato Hollow to Cabin Springs.','2025-03-28 00:13:31','2025-03-28 00:13:31'),(12825,'trails',211,'What type of trail is the Telephone Canyon Trail?','This is a point-to-point trail, meaning hikers start at one point and end at another without returning to the starting location.','2025-03-28 00:13:31','2025-03-28 00:13:31'),(12826,'trails',211,'What features can hikers expect to see on the trail?','Hikers can enjoy birding, stunning fall colors, views of rivers and creeks, wildflowers, and wildlife along the route.','2025-03-28 00:13:31','2025-03-28 00:13:31'),(12827,'trails',211,'Are dogs allowed on the Telephone Canyon Trail?','No, dogs are not permitted on this trail.','2025-03-28 00:13:31','2025-03-28 00:13:31'),(12828,'trails',211,'What are the geographic coordinates of the Telephone Canyon Trail?','The trail is located at a latitude of 37.3048 and a longitude of -112.986.','2025-03-28 00:13:31','2025-03-28 00:13:31'),(12829,'trails',213,'What is the difficulty level of The Grotto Trail?','The Grotto Trail is classified as easy, making it suitable for families and hikers of all skill levels.','2025-03-28 00:13:39','2025-03-28 00:13:39'),(12830,'trails',213,'What is the total length of The Grotto Trail?','The trail spans 0.8 miles, providing a brief yet enjoyable hiking experience.','2025-03-28 00:13:39','2025-03-28 00:13:39'),(12831,'trails',213,'What are the highest and lowest elevations on The Grotto Trail?','The trail maintains a consistent elevation at 4,287 feet, offering a gentle walking experience.','2025-03-28 00:13:39','2025-03-28 00:13:39'),(12832,'trails',213,'Is The Grotto Trail point-to-point or a loop?','The Grotto Trail is a point-to-point trail, allowing hikers to enjoy a straightforward pathway.','2025-03-28 00:13:39','2025-03-28 00:13:39'),(12833,'trails',213,'What is the incline and decline like on this trail?','The trail features a slight incline of 22 feet and a decline of 70 feet, ensuring an easy walk for all.','2025-03-28 00:13:39','2025-03-28 00:13:39'),(12834,'trails',213,'Are dogs allowed on The Grotto Trail?','Unfortunately, dogs are not permitted on this trail, which is designed for a serene hiking experience.','2025-03-28 00:13:39','2025-03-28 00:13:39'),(12835,'trails',213,'What features can hikers expect to see along The Grotto Trail?','Hikers can enjoy bird watching, beautiful fall colors, views of the Virgin River, and wildflowers along the trail.','2025-03-28 00:13:39','2025-03-28 00:13:39'),(12836,'trails',213,'Is The Grotto Trail suitable for picnics?','Yes, The Grotto Trail is perfect for a leisurely hike after enjoying a picnic, making it an ideal spot for families.','2025-03-28 00:13:39','2025-03-28 00:13:39'),(12837,'trails',213,'What geographical coordinates mark The Grotto Trail?','The trail is located at a latitude of 37.2602 and a longitude of -112.952.','2025-03-28 00:13:39','2025-03-28 00:13:39'),(12838,'trails',213,'What kind of scenery can hikers expect on the trail?','Hikers will be treated to sights and sounds of the Virgin River, making for a scenic and refreshing experience.','2025-03-28 00:13:39','2025-03-28 00:13:39'),(12839,'trails',215,'Is this trail suitable for families?','Absolutely! This trail is ideal for families seeking a quick out-and-back adventure. Everyone can enjoy stunning views and easy hiking along the paved path.','2025-03-28 00:13:53','2025-03-28 00:13:53'),(12840,'trails',215,'What is the trail type and length?','The trail is a point-to-point route with a length of 0.8 miles (1.3 km), making it an accessible choice for casual hikers.','2025-03-28 00:13:53','2025-03-28 00:13:53'),(12841,'trails',215,'What is the difficulty level of the trail?','This hike is considered easy to intermediate, making it suitable for various skill levels, including those who may not have extensive hiking experience.','2025-03-28 00:13:53','2025-03-28 00:13:53'),(12842,'trails',215,'What elevation can I expect while hiking?','The highest elevation reached on this trail is 4,307 feet. The incline is 128 feet with a minimal decline of 4 feet, providing a gentle ascent.','2025-03-28 00:13:53','2025-03-28 00:13:53'),(12843,'trails',215,'What features can I see along the trail?','Hikers will enjoy a variety of natural features, including beautiful views, waterfalls, and opportunities to see wildlife. The trail also boasts diverse flora, especially the pinyon-juniper woodlands.','2025-03-28 00:13:53','2025-03-28 00:13:53'),(12844,'trails',215,'Are dogs allowed on the trail?','The policy on dogs is currently unclear, so it\'s best to check local regulations before bringing your pet along.','2025-03-28 00:13:53','2025-03-28 00:13:53'),(12845,'trails',215,'Where is the trailhead located?','The Emerald Pools Trailhead is conveniently located across from the Zion Lodge, accessible from shuttle stop #5.','2025-03-28 00:13:53','2025-03-28 00:13:53'),(12846,'trails',215,'What precautions should I take while hiking?','Be sure to stay away from cliff edges and refrain from swimming in the delicate emerald pools, as they are crucial water sources for local wildlife.','2025-03-28 00:13:53','2025-03-28 00:13:53'),(12847,'trails',215,'Are there facilities available on the trail?','Yes, hikers will find restrooms and water filling stations conveniently located at the Zion Lodge.','2025-03-28 00:13:53','2025-03-28 00:13:53'),(12848,'trails',215,'What additional trails can I connect to from this hike?','This trail connects to other Emerald Pools trails and the Kayenta Trail, offering an opportunity to further explore the picturesque landscape.','2025-03-28 00:13:53','2025-03-28 00:13:53'),(12849,'trails',218,'What is the difficulty level of the hike?','The hike is categorized as intermediate in difficulty.','2025-03-28 00:14:01','2025-03-28 00:14:01'),(12850,'trails',218,'What is the highest elevation reached on the trail?','The trail reaches a maximum elevation of 5,320 feet.','2025-03-28 00:14:01','2025-03-28 00:14:01'),(12851,'trails',218,'What is the lowest elevation on the hike?','The minimum elevation on this trail is also 5,320 feet.','2025-03-28 00:14:01','2025-03-28 00:14:01'),(12852,'trails',218,'How long is the trail?','The total length of the trail is 1.1 miles.','2025-03-28 00:14:01','2025-03-28 00:14:01'),(12853,'trails',218,'What type of trail is it?','This is a point-to-point trail, meaning you will start and end at different locations.','2025-03-28 00:14:01','2025-03-28 00:14:01'),(12854,'trails',218,'What is the elevation gain for this hike?','Hikers will experience an elevation gain of 563 feet along the route.','2025-03-28 00:14:01','2025-03-28 00:14:01'),(12855,'trails',218,'Is there any elevation loss on the trail?','Yes, there is a slight decline of 17 feet on this hike.','2025-03-28 00:14:01','2025-03-28 00:14:01'),(12856,'trails',218,'What is the average grade of the trail?','The trail has an average grade of about 0.10%.','2025-03-28 00:14:01','2025-03-28 00:14:01'),(12857,'trails',218,'What is the maximum grade encountered on the hike?','The maximum grade on this trail reaches up to 0.23%.','2025-03-28 00:14:01','2025-03-28 00:14:01'),(12858,'trails',218,'Can I expect to see any water features along the hike?','Yes, during the hike, you will come across numerous small pools of water.','2025-03-28 00:14:01','2025-03-28 00:14:01'),(12859,'trails',218,'What type of terrain should I expect on the hike?','The terrain consists primarily of sandstone rock with some sandy wash sections.','2025-03-28 00:14:01','2025-03-28 00:14:01'),(12860,'trails',218,'What are the GPS coordinates for the trail?','The latitude and longitude for this trail are approximately 37.2219 and -112.915, respectively.','2025-03-28 00:14:01','2025-03-28 00:14:01'),(12861,'trails',219,'What is the length of the Sand Bench Trail?','The Sand Bench Trail spans 7.6 miles (or 12.2 kilometers) for a roundtrip hike.','2025-03-28 00:14:09','2025-03-28 00:14:09'),(12862,'trails',219,'What is the significance of the Sand Bench Trail\'s geological features?','This trail is set atop the remnants of an ancient rockfall and traces the path of the Virgin River while ascending a landslide that caused a lake to form 8,000 years ago, extending up to Angels Landing.','2025-03-28 00:14:09','2025-03-28 00:14:09'),(12863,'trails',219,'What should I be aware of regarding trail conditions?','The trail presents deep sand and limited shade, making hydration essential. Expect your pace to be slower due to the sandy terrain, and embrace a positive mindset while hiking.','2025-03-28 00:14:09','2025-03-28 00:14:09'),(12864,'trails',219,'Where can I access the Sand Bench Trail?','You can primarily start the Sand Bench Trail from the Emerald Pools Trailhead at the Zion Lodge (shuttle stop #5). Alternatively, access is available from the Court of the Patriarchs (shuttle stop #4) by crossing the road to reach the sandy trail.','2025-03-28 00:14:09','2025-03-28 00:14:09'),(12865,'trails',219,'Is there a loop option available on this trail?','Yes, hikers can choose to hike the loop portion of the trail, bringing the total distance closer to 5 miles (or 8 kilometers). You can also opt for an out-and-back hike toward the Zion Lodge.','2025-03-28 00:14:09','2025-03-28 00:14:09'),(12866,'trails',219,'Are there facilities available along the Sand Bench Trail?','Yes, the Zion Lodge offers water and restroom facilities, which can be quite handy during your hike.','2025-03-28 00:14:09','2025-03-28 00:14:09'),(12867,'trails',219,'Is it possible to hike the Sand Bench Trail in winter?','Winter hiking is feasible, but be cautious of icy patches along the trail.','2025-03-28 00:14:09','2025-03-28 00:14:09'),(12868,'trails',219,'Does the Sand Bench Trail accommodate pets?','No, dogs are not permitted on the Sand Bench Trail.','2025-03-28 00:14:09','2025-03-28 00:14:09'),(12869,'trails',219,'What other features can I expect on the Sand Bench Trail?','The trail offers opportunities for birdwatching, stunning fall colors, views of nearby rivers and creeks, as well as a chance to see wildflowers and wildlife along the way.','2025-03-28 00:14:09','2025-03-28 00:14:09'),(12870,'trails',220,'What is the Left Fork (The Subway) trail known for?','The Left Fork (The Subway) trail is celebrated for its stunning beauty and adventurous hike, making it a perfect choice for those eager to explore its captivating features.','2025-03-28 00:14:18','2025-03-28 00:14:18'),(12871,'trails',220,'Are permits required to hike the Left Fork (The Subway) trail?','Yes, permits are necessary for access to this area from either direction. For more details, visit nps.gov/zion/planyourvisit.','2025-03-28 00:14:18','2025-03-28 00:14:18'),(12872,'trails',220,'How difficult is the Left Fork (The Subway) trail?','The trail is categorized as difficult, suitable for hikers seeking a challenging experience.','2025-03-28 00:14:18','2025-03-28 00:14:18'),(12873,'trails',220,'What are the highest and lowest elevations on the Left Fork (The Subway) trail?','The trail reaches a highest elevation of 4,665 feet, while the lowest elevation remains the same at 4,665 feet.','2025-03-28 00:14:18','2025-03-28 00:14:18'),(12874,'trails',220,'What is the total length of the Left Fork (The Subway) trail?','The trail spans approximately 3.9 miles, offering a rewarding journey through its scenic landscapes.','2025-03-28 00:14:18','2025-03-28 00:14:18'),(12875,'trails',220,'What type of trail is the Left Fork (The Subway)?','The Left Fork (The Subway) is a point-to-point trail, allowing hikers to start and end at different locations.','2025-03-28 00:14:19','2025-03-28 00:14:19'),(12876,'trails',220,'What are the total incline and decline on the Left Fork (The Subway) trail?','Hikers can expect a total incline of 1,218 feet and a decline of 919 feet throughout the trail.','2025-03-28 00:14:19','2025-03-28 00:14:19'),(12877,'trails',220,'What is the average and maximum grade of the Left Fork (The Subway) trail?','The trail has an average grade of 0.10% and a maximum grade of 1.66%, making for a manageable ascent and descent.','2025-03-28 00:14:19','2025-03-28 00:14:19'),(12878,'trails',220,'What features can be seen along the Left Fork (The Subway) trail?','The trail showcases diverse features including birding opportunities, rivers and creeks, swimming spots, beautiful views, waterfalls, wildflowers, and wildlife.','2025-03-28 00:14:19','2025-03-28 00:14:19'),(12879,'trails',220,'Are dogs allowed on the Left Fork (The Subway) trail?','No, dogs are not permitted on this trail to preserve the natural environment and ensure a better experience for all hikers.','2025-03-28 00:14:19','2025-03-28 00:14:19'),(12880,'trails',220,'Where are the latitude and longitude coordinates for the Left Fork (The Subway) trail?','The trail\'s coordinates are approximately 37.2848° N latitude and -113.096° W longitude.','2025-03-28 00:14:19','2025-03-28 00:14:19'),(12881,'trails',222,'What is the general route of the Beamer Trail?','The Beamer Trail begins at the river and leads up-canyon, presenting a straightforward path between Tanner Canyon and Palisades Creek with some minor obstructions from Dox Sandstone that are easily navigable. The route features dense vegetation near the water\'s edge, gradually transitioning to rocky slopes.','2025-03-28 00:14:30','2025-03-28 00:14:30'),(12882,'trails',222,'How does the trail change at Palisades Canyon?','At Palisades Canyon, the Beamer Trail shifts character from an easy walk on sandy slopes to a challenging trek along narrow and exposed ledges at the edge of steep cliffs.','2025-03-28 00:14:30','2025-03-28 00:14:30'),(12883,'trails',222,'What challenges might hikers face when approaching the Tapeats Sandstone?','As hikers approach the Tapeats Sandstone, they will need to ascend about 300 vertical feet up the talus to reach the trail’s continuation towards the Little Colorado River. This ascent is the only clear break in the sandstone cliff, and the path can be eroded and precarious, demanding caution.','2025-03-28 00:14:30','2025-03-28 00:14:30'),(12884,'trails',222,'Is the trail suitable for hikers with a fear of heights?','Hikers with a fear of heights may find segments of this trail particularly challenging due to its narrow and exposed sections near high cliffs. Caution is advised.','2025-03-28 00:14:30','2025-03-28 00:14:30'),(12885,'trails',222,'How well-defined is the trail, and are there potential navigation challenges?','The trail is generally well-defined, but there may be some navigation difficulties when crossing drainages. It\'s advisable to keep to the main trail along the Tapeats rim for the best views and guidance.','2025-03-28 00:14:30','2025-03-28 00:14:30'),(12886,'trails',222,'Can hikers access the shoreline in any way?','It is possible to scramble down to the shoreline below the confluence for a closer view of the river, but the primary trail remains on the Tapeats rim throughout the hike.','2025-03-28 00:14:30','2025-03-28 00:14:30'),(12887,'trails',222,'What is the overall difficulty level of the Beamer Trail?','The difficulty level of the Beamer Trail is categorized as difficult due to the strenuous sections and exposure along the way.','2025-03-28 00:14:30','2025-03-28 00:14:30'),(12888,'trails',222,'What are the trail\'s elevation statistics?','The Beamer Trail has a highest elevation of 2685 feet and a lowest elevation of 2685 feet, with a total incline of 1692 feet and decline of 1650 feet.','2025-03-28 00:14:30','2025-03-28 00:14:30'),(12889,'trails',222,'What is the total length and type of the Beamer Trail?','The trail stretches for 9.9 miles and is classified as a point-to-point route.','2025-03-28 00:14:30','2025-03-28 00:14:30'),(12890,'trails',222,'Are dogs allowed on the Beamer Trail?','No, dogs are not permitted on the Beamer Trail.','2025-03-28 00:14:30','2025-03-28 00:14:30'),(12891,'trails',222,'What can hikers expect to see along the trail?','Hikers can look forward to stunning views, opportunities for wildlife sightings, and a scenic route alongside the river and canyon landscapes.','2025-03-28 00:14:30','2025-03-28 00:14:30'),(12892,'trails',222,'What should hikers do if they encounter historic artifacts?','If hikers come across remnants of mining or other historic artifacts, it\'s important to leave them in place for the enjoyment of future visitors and to preserve their historical significance.','2025-03-28 00:14:30','2025-03-28 00:14:30'),(12893,'trails',226,'What is the Deer Creek trail like?','The Deer Creek trail offers an adventurous experience with sections of a slot canyon that are suitable for exploration by older kids. It also showcases breathtaking views of a waterfall and highlights the historical significance of this area, which has attracted visitors since prehistoric times.','2025-03-28 00:14:36','2025-03-28 00:14:36'),(12894,'trails',226,'How difficult is the Deer Creek trail?','The trail is categorized as intermediate to difficult, making it a good challenge for those with some hiking experience.','2025-03-28 00:14:36','2025-03-28 00:14:36'),(12895,'trails',226,'What is the elevation range of the Deer Creek trail?','The trail maintains an elevation of 1964 feet throughout, providing relatively steady hiking.','2025-03-28 00:14:36','2025-03-28 00:14:36'),(12896,'trails',226,'What is the length of the Deer Creek trail?','The Deer Creek trail stretches 3.2 miles in a point-to-point configuration.','2025-03-28 00:14:36','2025-03-28 00:14:36'),(12897,'trails',226,'What are the incline and decline features of the trail?','Hikers will encounter a total incline of 81 feet and a decline of 1882 feet along the Deer Creek trail.','2025-03-28 00:14:36','2025-03-28 00:14:36'),(12898,'trails',226,'What is the average and maximum grade of the Deer Creek trail?','The trail has an average grade of 0.12% and a maximum grade of 0.44%, ensuring a manageable hiking experience.','2025-03-28 00:14:36','2025-03-28 00:14:36'),(12899,'trails',226,'What natural features can be found on the Deer Creek trail?','The trail is rich in natural features such as birding opportunities, a river or creek, stunning views, a waterfall, wildflowers, and various wildlife.','2025-03-28 00:14:36','2025-03-28 00:14:36'),(12900,'trails',226,'Are dogs allowed on the Deer Creek trail?','Unfortunately, dogs are not permitted on the Deer Creek trail.','2025-03-28 00:14:36','2025-03-28 00:14:36'),(12901,'trails',226,'What are the geographic coordinates of the Deer Creek trail?','The Deer Creek trail is located at a latitude of 36.4011 and a longitude of -112.476.','2025-03-28 00:14:36','2025-03-28 00:14:36'),(12902,'trails',228,'What is the Francois Matthes Trail?','The Francois Matthes Trail is an old logging road that has been largely reclaimed by nature, offering hikers a unique backdrop featuring Zoroaster Temple and Wotans Throne.','2025-03-28 00:14:49','2025-03-28 00:14:49'),(12903,'trails',228,'What can I see along the Francois Matthes Trail?','Hikers can enjoy distinctive views of Zoroaster Temple and Wotans Throne, along with Cheyava Falls and the Clear Creek drainage, though some views are partially obstructed by brush.','2025-03-28 00:14:49','2025-03-28 00:14:49'),(12904,'trails',228,'How do I navigate the Francois Matthes Trail?','Starting from its junction with the Walhalla Glades Trail, the trail leads southwest over a plateau, steadily descending along a broad ridge adorned with scattered pine trees and a wildfire area.','2025-03-28 00:14:49','2025-03-28 00:14:49'),(12905,'trails',228,'Are there any notable landmarks or intersections on the trail?','You will pass through an intersection with the Walhalla Connector and cross several open meadows, eventually arriving at a viewpoint that provides the scenic overview.','2025-03-28 00:14:49','2025-03-28 00:14:49'),(12906,'trails',228,'What should I know about the trail\'s historical significance?','The trail is named after Francois E. Matthes, a geologist and famed topographical mapper whose work contributed significantly to the understanding of glacial geology and the establishment of many National Parks in the U.S.','2025-03-28 00:14:49','2025-03-28 00:14:49'),(12907,'trails',228,'What is the difficulty level of the Francois Matthes Trail?','The trail is classified as easy, making it suitable for hikers of various skill levels.','2025-03-28 00:14:49','2025-03-28 00:14:49'),(12908,'trails',228,'What are the elevation details for this trail?','The trail offers a highest elevation of 8013 feet and maintains that height throughout, with a slight incline of 39 feet and a descent of 442 feet.','2025-03-28 00:14:49','2025-03-28 00:14:49'),(12909,'trails',228,'How long is the Francois Matthes Trail?','The total length of the Francois Matthes Trail is approximately 4.8 miles, taking hikers on a point-to-point journey.','2025-03-28 00:14:49','2025-03-28 00:14:49'),(12910,'trails',228,'Are dogs allowed on the Francois Matthes Trail?','No, dogs are not permitted on this trail.','2025-03-28 00:14:49','2025-03-28 00:14:49'),(12911,'trails',228,'What kind of surface can I expect on the trail?','The average grade of the trail is very gentle at 0.02%, with a maximum gradient of 0.07%, making it manageable for all hikers.','2025-03-28 00:14:49','2025-03-28 00:14:49'),(12912,'trails',228,'Will I encounter many other hikers on the trail?','Due to its infrequent use, the trail offers a good chance for solitude, making it a great escape for those seeking peace in nature.','2025-03-28 00:14:49','2025-03-28 00:14:49'),(12913,'trails',233,'What is the Bridle Trail?','The Bridle Trail is a scenic trail on the North Rim that offers beautiful surroundings and is unique for allowing dogs and bikes.','2025-03-28 00:15:03','2025-03-28 00:15:03'),(12914,'trails',233,'Can I bring my dog on the Bridle Trail?','Yes, the Bridle Trail is the only one on the North Rim that permits dogs, making it a great option for pet owners.','2025-03-28 00:15:03','2025-03-28 00:15:03'),(12915,'trails',233,'Are bicycles allowed on the Bridle Trail?','Absolutely! The Bridle Trail permits bicycles, making it a versatile trail for both cyclists and hikers.','2025-03-28 00:15:03','2025-03-28 00:15:03'),(12916,'trails',233,'What is the difficulty level of the Bridle Trail?','The trail is categorized as easy to intermediate, suitable for a wide range of skill levels.','2025-03-28 00:15:03','2025-03-28 00:15:03'),(12917,'trails',233,'What is the elevation of the Bridle Trail?','The highest and lowest elevation on the Bridle Trail is 8,181 feet, providing stunning vistas throughout.','2025-03-28 00:15:03','2025-03-28 00:15:03'),(12918,'trails',233,'How long is the Bridle Trail?','The trail stretches for 2.0 miles, making it a manageable option for a leisurely hike or ride.','2025-03-28 00:15:03','2025-03-28 00:15:03'),(12919,'trails',233,'What type of trail is the Bridle Trail?','The Bridle Trail is a point-to-point trail, meaning you start at one point and finish at another.','2025-03-28 00:15:03','2025-03-28 00:15:03'),(12920,'trails',233,'What is the incline and decline of the Bridle Trail?','The trail features an incline of 198 feet and a decline of 117 feet, offering a varied terrain.','2025-03-28 00:15:03','2025-03-28 00:15:03'),(12921,'trails',233,'What is the average grade of the Bridle Trail?','The average grade of the Bridle Trail is quite gentle at 0.03%, making it accessible for all hikers.','2025-03-28 00:15:03','2025-03-28 00:15:03'),(12922,'trails',233,'What is the maximum grade of the Bridle Trail?','The maximum grade reaches 0.13%, ensuring a mild experience while taking in the natural beauty.','2025-03-28 00:15:03','2025-03-28 00:15:03'),(12923,'trails',233,'What are the geographic coordinates of the Bridle Trail?','The geographic coordinates for the Bridle Trail are approximately 36.196° latitude and -112.051° longitude.','2025-03-28 00:15:03','2025-03-28 00:15:03'),(12924,'trails',237,'What is the primary feature of the Saddle Horse Loop trail?','The main highlight of the Saddle Horse Loop is its breathtaking views of the Colorado River.','2025-03-28 00:15:10','2025-03-28 00:15:10'),(12925,'trails',237,'How can I access the Saddle Horse Loop?','You can access the trail from the road located between Toroweap Overlook and Tuweep Campground, or from a trailhead situated near campsite 5 in the Tuweep Campground.','2025-03-28 00:15:10','2025-03-28 00:15:10'),(12926,'trails',237,'What is the difficulty level of this trail?','The trail is categorized as easy to intermediate, making it accessible for a wide range of hikers.','2025-03-28 00:15:10','2025-03-28 00:15:10'),(12927,'trails',237,'What is the elevation range of the Saddle Horse Loop?','The trail has a consistent elevation of 4,473 feet throughout its length.','2025-03-28 00:15:10','2025-03-28 00:15:10'),(12928,'trails',237,'How long is the Saddle Horse Loop?','The total length of the loop is 1.1 miles, making it a short yet rewarding hike.','2025-03-28 00:15:10','2025-03-28 00:15:10'),(12929,'trails',237,'What type of trail is Saddle Horse Loop?','Saddle Horse Loop is a point-to-point trail, offering a straightforward hiking experience.','2025-03-28 00:15:10','2025-03-28 00:15:10'),(12930,'trails',237,'What is the incline and decline of the trail?','The trail features an incline of 100 feet and a decline of 109 feet, resulting in a gentle overall gradient.','2025-03-28 00:15:10','2025-03-28 00:15:10'),(12931,'trails',237,'What is the average and maximum grade of the trail?','The average grade of the trail is 0.04%, while the maximum grade is 0.08%, providing a relatively flat hiking experience.','2025-03-28 00:15:10','2025-03-28 00:15:10'),(12932,'trails',237,'What should I expect in terms of trail features?','Expect stunning views throughout the hike, especially as you approach the canyon edge.','2025-03-28 00:15:10','2025-03-28 00:15:10'),(12933,'trails',237,'Are dogs allowed on the Saddle Horse Loop?','Unfortunately, dogs are not permitted on this trail.','2025-03-28 00:15:10','2025-03-28 00:15:10'),(12934,'trails',237,'What are the geographic coordinates of the trail?','The Saddle Horse Loop is located at latitude 36.2239 and longitude -113.061.','2025-03-28 00:15:10','2025-03-28 00:15:10'),(12935,'trails',238,'What is the trailhead location for the Saddle Mountain Trail?','The Saddle Mountain Trail begins at the Saddle Trailhead, which is sometimes challenging to access off Forest Road 610.','2025-03-28 00:15:17','2025-03-28 00:15:17'),(12936,'trails',238,'What unique features can I expect on the Saddle Mountain Trail?','Hikers will encounter a variety of landscapes, including a ridgeline traverse, a wooded burn area, and expansive flat, parched ground, offering a mix of scenery throughout the hike.','2025-03-28 00:15:17','2025-03-28 00:15:17'),(12937,'trails',238,'Does the Saddle Mountain Trail lead to the summit of Saddle Mountain?','No, the trail does not ascend to the summit of Saddle Mountain. Instead, it takes you to a deep cut on the north rim, positioned just below the summit.','2025-03-28 00:15:17','2025-03-28 00:15:17'),(12938,'trails',238,'What are the views like along the Saddle Mountain Trail?','The trail provides stunning vistas, especially as you traverse the ridgelines and approach the intersection with the Nankoweap Trail.','2025-03-28 00:15:17','2025-03-28 00:15:17'),(12939,'trails',238,'What is the length and elevation of the Saddle Mountain Trail?','The trail stretches 2.3 miles long, with a highest elevation of 7,558 feet and a lowest elevation also at 7,558 feet.','2025-03-28 00:15:17','2025-03-28 00:15:17'),(12940,'trails',238,'What is the trail difficulty rating for Saddle Mountain Trail?','The Saddle Mountain Trail is rated as very difficult, making it suitable for experienced hikers.','2025-03-28 00:15:17','2025-03-28 00:15:17'),(12941,'trails',238,'What is the elevation change on the Saddle Mountain Trail?','The hike features a total incline of 357 feet and a decline of 1,630 feet.','2025-03-28 00:15:17','2025-03-28 00:15:17'),(12942,'trails',238,'Are dogs allowed on the Saddle Mountain Trail?','No, dogs are not permitted on the Saddle Mountain Trail.','2025-03-28 00:15:17','2025-03-28 00:15:17'),(12943,'trails',238,'What are the latitude and longitude coordinates for the Saddle Mountain Trail?','The trail is located at a latitude of 36.3031 and a longitude of -111.995.','2025-03-28 00:15:17','2025-03-28 00:15:17'),(12944,'trails',238,'Is the Saddle Mountain Trail suitable for casual hikers?','Due to its very difficult rating, this trail is better suited for experienced hikers looking for a challenging adventure.','2025-03-28 00:15:17','2025-03-28 00:15:17'),(12945,'trails',239,'What is the Schmutz Spring trail like?','The Schmutz Spring trail offers an opportunity to explore a breathtaking desert oasis, making it a remarkable hike.','2025-03-28 00:15:23','2025-03-28 00:15:23'),(12946,'trails',239,'What is the adoption status of the Schmutz Spring trail?','The Schmutz Spring trail is currently available for adoption, which means you can contribute to its maintenance and preservation.','2025-03-28 00:15:23','2025-03-28 00:15:23'),(12947,'trails',239,'How difficult is the Schmutz Spring trail?','This trail is classified as intermediate, making it suitable for hikers with some experience.','2025-03-28 00:15:23','2025-03-28 00:15:23'),(12948,'trails',239,'What are the elevation details for the Schmutz Spring trail?','The trail has a highest elevation of 4474 feet and a lowest elevation that is the same, providing a unique hiking experience at a consistent altitude.','2025-03-28 00:15:23','2025-03-28 00:15:23'),(12949,'trails',239,'What is the length of the Schmutz Spring trail?','The trail stretches approximately 2.1 miles one way, ideal for a moderate hike.','2025-03-28 00:15:23','2025-03-28 00:15:23'),(12950,'trails',239,'What type of trail is the Schmutz Spring trail?','The Schmutz Spring trail is a point-to-point trail, meaning you start at one point and finish at another.','2025-03-28 00:15:23','2025-03-28 00:15:23'),(12951,'trails',239,'What is the incline and decline on the Schmutz Spring trail?','The trail features a gentle incline of 29 feet and a descent of 1326 feet, which can provide a workout while enjoying the scenery.','2025-03-28 00:15:23','2025-03-28 00:15:23'),(12952,'trails',239,'What are the average and maximum grades of the Schmutz Spring trail?','The average grade of the trail is about 0.12%, while the maximum grade reaches 0.36%, ensuring a mostly gentle hike.','2025-03-28 00:15:23','2025-03-28 00:15:23'),(12953,'trails',239,'What are the geographic coordinates of the Schmutz Spring trail?','You can find the Schmutz Spring trail located at a latitude of 36.3393 and a longitude of -112.927.','2025-03-28 00:15:23','2025-03-28 00:15:23'),(12954,'trails',242,'What is the nature of the trail at Tiyo Point?','The trail follows a gradually overgrown former road that weaves through a forest. Hikers may encounter several downed trees, but the path remains quite navigable.','2025-03-28 00:15:36','2025-03-28 00:15:36'),(12955,'trails',242,'Are there any trail markers to guide me?','While the trail features several old markers affixed to trees, they may be difficult to notice due to the overgrowth.','2025-03-28 00:15:36','2025-03-28 00:15:36'),(12956,'trails',242,'What is the overall terrain like?','You\'ll experience a brief ascent at the beginning from Point Subline Road, followed by a gentle descent across rolling hills. The trail offers a tranquil experience primarily accompanied by wildflowers.','2025-03-28 00:15:36','2025-03-28 00:15:36'),(12957,'trails',242,'What can I expect at the end of the hike?','At the end of the trail, you\'ll find a secluded picnic area that provides a beautiful overlook, perfect for those seeking a quiet and shady escape in nature.','2025-03-28 00:15:36','2025-03-28 00:15:36'),(12958,'trails',242,'How difficult is the hike?','The trail is rated as easy to intermediate, making it accessible for many types of hikers.','2025-03-28 00:15:36','2025-03-28 00:15:36'),(12959,'trails',242,'What are the elevation details of Tiyo Point?','This trail features a highest elevation of 7,777 feet and maintains that same elevation at its lowest point.','2025-03-28 00:15:36','2025-03-28 00:15:36'),(12960,'trails',242,'How long is the Tiyo Point trail?','The total length of the trail is approximately 6.6 miles, following a point-to-point format.','2025-03-28 00:15:36','2025-03-28 00:15:36'),(12961,'trails',242,'What are the incline and decline statistics?','The hike includes a total incline of 183 feet and a decline of 570 feet, contributing to its overall gentle grade.','2025-03-28 00:15:36','2025-03-28 00:15:36'),(12962,'trails',242,'What features and experiences can I expect on this trail?','Hikers can look forward to scenic views, an abundance of wildflowers, and the possibility of spotting wildlife as they traverse this beautiful region.','2025-03-28 00:15:36','2025-03-28 00:15:36'),(12963,'trails',242,'Are dogs permitted on this trail?','Unfortunately, dogs are not allowed on the Tiyo Point trail.','2025-03-28 00:15:36','2025-03-28 00:15:36'),(12964,'trails',242,'What are the geographical coordinates for Tiyo Point?','The trail is located at a latitude of 36.2585 and a longitude of -112.103.','2025-03-28 00:15:36','2025-03-28 00:15:36'),(12965,'trails',244,'What is the Tuckup to Tuweep Campground Connector trail like?','The Tuckup to Tuweep Campground Connector trail offers an easy hike with breathtaking views. It takes you through stunning landscapes in southern Utah and northern Arizona.','2025-03-28 00:15:43','2025-03-28 00:15:43'),(12966,'trails',244,'What level of difficulty is the trail?','This trail is classified as easy, making it suitable for hikers of all skill levels.','2025-03-28 00:15:43','2025-03-28 00:15:43'),(12967,'trails',244,'What is the highest elevation on the trail?','The highest point along the trail reaches an elevation of 4,566 feet.','2025-03-28 00:15:43','2025-03-28 00:15:43'),(12968,'trails',244,'What is the lowest elevation on the trail?','The trail maintains a consistent elevation of 4,566 feet throughout its course, so there is no significant change in elevation.','2025-03-28 00:15:43','2025-03-28 00:15:43'),(12969,'trails',244,'How long is the trail?','The trail spans a distance of 1.2 miles, making it a short yet rewarding hike.','2025-03-28 00:15:43','2025-03-28 00:15:43'),(12970,'trails',244,'What type of trail is this?','This is a point-to-point trail, meaning it starts at one location and ends at another.','2025-03-28 00:15:43','2025-03-28 00:15:43'),(12971,'trails',244,'What is the elevation gain on the trail?','The trail has a slight incline of 114 feet, providing a gentle climb.','2025-03-28 00:15:43','2025-03-28 00:15:43'),(12972,'trails',244,'Is there any decline on the trail?','Yes, the trail features a decline of 120 feet, contributing to the overall ease of the hike.','2025-03-28 00:15:43','2025-03-28 00:15:43'),(12973,'trails',244,'What is the average grade of the trail?','The average grade of the trail is approximately 0.04%, offering a very manageable hiking experience.','2025-03-28 00:15:43','2025-03-28 00:15:43'),(12974,'trails',244,'What is the maximum grade of the trail?','The steepest section of the trail has a maximum grade of 0.12%, which is quite mild.','2025-03-28 00:15:43','2025-03-28 00:15:43'),(12975,'trails',244,'What are the coordinates of the trail?','The trail is located at approximately latitude 36.226 and longitude -113.06.','2025-03-28 00:15:43','2025-03-28 00:15:43'),(12976,'trails',247,'What is the Walhalla Connector Trail?','The Walhalla Connector Trail is an east-west route that links the Walhalla Glades, Francois Matthes, and Ariel Point trails, offering stunning views of the surrounding landscape.','2025-03-28 00:15:50','2025-03-28 00:15:50'),(12977,'trails',247,'What is the difficulty level of the Walhalla Connector Trail?','This trail is classified as intermediate in difficulty, making it suitable for hikers with some experience.','2025-03-28 00:15:50','2025-03-28 00:15:50'),(12978,'trails',247,'What is the length of the Walhalla Connector Trail?','The trail stretches for 2.9 miles, providing a manageable distance for a pleasant hike.','2025-03-28 00:15:50','2025-03-28 00:15:50'),(12979,'trails',247,'What are the elevation details of the Walhalla Connector Trail?','The trail features a highest elevation of 8,037 feet and a lowest elevation of 8,037 feet, indicating a relatively stable elevation throughout.','2025-03-28 00:15:50','2025-03-28 00:15:50'),(12980,'trails',247,'What is the elevation gain and loss on the Walhalla Connector Trail?','Hikers will experience an incline of 342 feet and a decline of 403 feet as they traverse the trail.','2025-03-28 00:15:50','2025-03-28 00:15:50'),(12981,'trails',247,'What is the average and maximum grade of the Walhalla Connector Trail?','The average grade is a mild 0.05%, while the maximum grade reaches up to 0.17%, making for a comfortable hiking experience.','2025-03-28 00:15:50','2025-03-28 00:15:50'),(12982,'trails',247,'What type of trail is the Walhalla Connector?','This is a point-to-point trail, meaning you\'ll start and end at different points rather than in a loop.','2025-03-28 00:15:50','2025-03-28 00:15:50'),(12983,'trails',247,'What are the geographical coordinates of the Walhalla Connector Trail?','The trail is located at a latitude of 36.177 and a longitude of -111.953, in what is likely a scenic region.','2025-03-28 00:15:50','2025-03-28 00:15:50'),(12984,'trails',248,'What is the total distance of the Widforss Point Trail?','The Widforss Point Trail covers a total distance of about 4.9 miles (approximately 8 kilometers) one way, making it nearly 10 miles (16 kilometers) for a round trip.','2025-03-28 00:16:02','2025-03-28 00:16:02'),(12985,'trails',248,'How difficult is the Widforss Point Trail?','The trail is considered to have an intermediate level of difficulty, suitable for those with some hiking experience.','2025-03-28 00:16:02','2025-03-28 00:16:02'),(12986,'trails',248,'What type of terrain can I expect on the Widforss Point Trail?','Hikers will enjoy a well-marked trail that runs along the dramatic canyon rim before leading into a scenic forest populated with conifers and aspens.','2025-03-28 00:16:02','2025-03-28 00:16:02'),(12987,'trails',248,'What notable views can I see along the trail?','As you hike, wonderful views of the Grand Canyon become visible, especially when you reach Widforss Point, where the panorama of the North Rim is truly breathtaking.','2025-03-28 00:16:02','2025-03-28 00:16:02'),(12988,'trails',248,'What is the elevation range of the Widforss Point Trail?','The trail maintains an elevation of approximately 7,965 feet throughout, with a total incline of about 495 feet and a decline of around 628 feet.','2025-03-28 00:16:02','2025-03-28 00:16:02'),(12989,'trails',248,'What are the average and maximum grades of the Widforss Point Trail?','The trail features an average grade of 0.04%, with a maximum inclination of 0.21%, making it generally accessible for hikers.','2025-03-28 00:16:02','2025-03-28 00:16:02'),(12990,'trails',248,'Are dogs allowed on the Widforss Point Trail?','Unfortunately, dogs are not permitted on this trail.','2025-03-28 00:16:02','2025-03-28 00:16:02'),(12991,'trails',248,'What kind of flora can I expect to see during the hike?','You\'ll traverse a lovely forest filled with fir, spruce, and aspen trees, especially vibrant during the fall when colors are at their peak.','2025-03-28 00:16:02','2025-03-28 00:16:02'),(12992,'trails',248,'Where is the Widforss Point Trail located?','The trail is situated at latitude 36.2237 and longitude -112.065, placed precisely within the stunning landscapes of the Grand Canyon area.','2025-03-28 00:16:02','2025-03-28 00:16:02'),(12993,'trails',249,'Is the Uncle Jim Trail suitable for families?','Yes, the Uncle Jim Trail is designed to be family-friendly, making it a great choice for hikers of all ages.','2025-03-28 00:16:09','2025-03-28 00:16:09'),(12994,'trails',249,'What type of trail is the Uncle Jim Trail?','The Uncle Jim Trail is a pleasant and shaded loop trail, which means it allows hikers to enjoy nature while experiencing various scenic views.','2025-03-28 00:16:09','2025-03-28 00:16:09'),(12995,'trails',249,'What can hikers expect to see on the Uncle Jim Trail?','Hikers will be treated to stunning views of Bright Angel Canyon along the trail, as well as opportunities to see fall colors, wildflowers, and possibly some wildlife.','2025-03-28 00:16:09','2025-03-28 00:16:09'),(12996,'trails',249,'What is the difficulty level of the Uncle Jim Trail?','The trail is classified as intermediate, making it accessible for those with some hiking experience.','2025-03-28 00:16:09','2025-03-28 00:16:09'),(12997,'trails',249,'What is the total length of the Uncle Jim Trail?','The Uncle Jim Trail spans approximately 2.6 miles.','2025-03-28 00:16:09','2025-03-28 00:16:09'),(12998,'trails',249,'What is the elevation change on the Uncle Jim Trail?','The trail has a slight incline of 227 feet and a decline of 229 feet from start to finish.','2025-03-28 00:16:10','2025-03-28 00:16:10'),(12999,'trails',249,'What are the elevation details for the Uncle Jim Trail?','The trail maintains its elevation at a high point of 8,256 feet throughout its length.','2025-03-28 00:16:10','2025-03-28 00:16:10'),(13000,'trails',249,'What is the average and maximum grade of the trail?','The average grade of the Uncle Jim Trail is around 0.03%, with a maximum incline of 0.18%. This means it is relatively easy to navigate.','2025-03-28 00:16:10','2025-03-28 00:16:10'),(13001,'trails',249,'Are dogs allowed on the Uncle Jim Trail?','No, unfortunately, dogs are not permitted on the Uncle Jim Trail.','2025-03-28 00:16:10','2025-03-28 00:16:10'),(13002,'trails',249,'What geographic coordinates pinpoint the Uncle Jim Trail?','The trail is located at a latitude of 36.227 and a longitude of -112.049.','2025-03-28 00:16:10','2025-03-28 00:16:10'),(13003,'trails',251,'What is the general overview of Passage 39 on the AZT?','Passage 39 offers hikers a chance to experience the stunning vistas of the North Rim of the Grand Canyon, characterized by its breathtaking landscapes and natural beauty.','2025-03-28 00:16:18','2025-03-28 00:16:18'),(13004,'trails',251,'How difficult is Passage 39?','This section of the trail is considered easy, making it suitable for hikers of all skill levels.','2025-03-28 00:16:18','2025-03-28 00:16:18'),(13005,'trails',251,'What is the highest elevation on Passage 39?','Hikers will reach a maximum elevation of 8,062 feet while traversing this passage.','2025-03-28 00:16:18','2025-03-28 00:16:18'),(13006,'trails',251,'What is the lowest elevation on Passage 39?','Interestingly, the lowest elevation for this trail is also 8,062 feet, indicating a relatively flat route overall.','2025-03-28 00:16:18','2025-03-28 00:16:18'),(13007,'trails',251,'How long is Passage 39?','The total length of this trail segment is 12.5 miles, providing a rewarding hike with ample opportunities for exploration.','2025-03-28 00:16:18','2025-03-28 00:16:18'),(13008,'trails',251,'What type of trail is Passage 39?','Passage 39 is a point-to-point trail, meaning hikers will start at one endpoint and finish at another without a loop.','2025-03-28 00:16:18','2025-03-28 00:16:18'),(13009,'trails',251,'What are the elevation changes like on Passage 39?','Hikers will experience a total incline of 1,515 feet and a decline of 738 feet, offering a gentle yet engaging hiking experience.','2025-03-28 00:16:18','2025-03-28 00:16:18'),(13010,'trails',251,'What is the average grade of the trail?','The average grade for Passage 39 is only 0.03%, making it quite manageable for hikers.','2025-03-28 00:16:18','2025-03-28 00:16:18'),(13011,'trails',251,'What is the maximum grade experienced on the trail?','The steepest section of Passage 39 has a maximum grade of 0.15%, ensuring a comfortable hike for participants.','2025-03-28 00:16:18','2025-03-28 00:16:18'),(13012,'trails',251,'What are the geographical coordinates for this trail segment?','Passage 39 can be located at approximately 36.217° latitude and -112.057° longitude.','2025-03-28 00:16:18','2025-03-28 00:16:18'),(13013,'trails',252,'What is the Rainbow Rim Trail #10?','The Rainbow Rim Trail #10 is a captivating singletrack trail that runs along the North Rim of the Grand Canyon. It offers remarkable views and the chance to immerse yourself in a remote wilderness setting.','2025-03-28 00:16:29','2025-03-28 00:16:29'),(13014,'trails',252,'Are there camping options along the trail?','Yes, there are primitive camping sites available at five different overlook points along the trail, making it a great location for multi-day trips.','2025-03-28 00:16:29','2025-03-28 00:16:29'),(13015,'trails',252,'What should I bring with me when hiking the trail?','Since the nearest services are quite far, it\'s essential to bring all necessary supplies, including food and plenty of water, as there are no facilities available.','2025-03-28 00:16:29','2025-03-28 00:16:29'),(13016,'trails',252,'How is the access to the Rainbow Rim Trail?','The forest roads leading to the Rainbow Rim are suitable for two-wheel drive vehicles, although the conditions might not be ideal.','2025-03-28 00:16:29','2025-03-28 00:16:29'),(13017,'trails',252,'What is a recommended way to experience the trail?','Many hikers and bikers enjoy traversing the trail from north to south. Setting up camp at Locust Point allows for two unique out-and-back excursions: one heading south to Timp Point and another north to Parissawampitts Point.','2025-03-28 00:16:29','2025-03-28 00:16:29'),(13018,'trails',252,'Who else uses the Rainbow Rim Trail besides mountain bikers?','While up to 90% of the trail\'s use is by mountain bikers, both hikers and horseback riders also frequent this scenic route.','2025-03-28 00:16:29','2025-03-28 00:16:29'),(13019,'trails',252,'What is the difficulty level of the Rainbow Rim Trail?','The trail is classified as intermediate, making it suitable for those with some hiking or biking experience.','2025-03-28 00:16:29','2025-03-28 00:16:29'),(13020,'trails',252,'What are the elevation details of the trail?','The highest and lowest elevations are both at 7493 feet, with an overall incline of 1517 feet and a decline of 1491 feet.','2025-03-28 00:16:29','2025-03-28 00:16:29'),(13021,'trails',252,'What is the length and type of the trail?','The Rainbow Rim Trail spans 17.8 miles and is a point-to-point trail.','2025-03-28 00:16:29','2025-03-28 00:16:29'),(13022,'trails',252,'What features can I expect to see on the trail?','Hikers can look forward to stunning views, vibrant wildflowers, and the potential to spot various wildlife.','2025-03-28 00:16:29','2025-03-28 00:16:29'),(13023,'trails',252,'Are dogs allowed on the trail?','Yes, dogs are permitted on the trail, but they must be kept on a leash.','2025-03-28 00:16:29','2025-03-28 00:16:29'),(13024,'trails',252,'What are the geographical coordinates of the trail?','The Rainbow Rim Trail is located at a latitude of 36.4187 and a longitude of -112.367.','2025-03-28 00:16:29','2025-03-28 00:16:29'),(13025,'trails',260,'What is the difficulty level of the trail?','The trail is classified as difficult, suggesting that hikers should be prepared for challenging conditions and possibly steep or rugged terrain.','2025-03-28 01:28:24','2025-03-28 01:28:24'),(13026,'trails',261,'What is the distance of the Alstrom Point trail?','The Alstrom Point trail covers a distance of 56 miles.','2025-03-28 01:28:34','2025-03-28 01:28:34'),(13027,'trails',261,'When is the best time to hike Alstrom Point?','This trail can be enjoyed year-round, allowing for hiking at any time.','2025-03-28 01:28:34','2025-03-28 01:28:34'),(13028,'trails',261,'How difficult is the Alstrom Point trail?','The hike is classified as moderate to difficult, making it suitable for experienced hikers.','2025-03-28 01:28:34','2025-03-28 01:28:34'),(13029,'trails',261,'What is the elevation gain for Alstrom Point?','The trail has an elevation change of 330 feet.','2025-03-28 01:28:34','2025-03-28 01:28:34'),(13030,'trails',261,'What are the coordinates for Alstrom Point?','The trail is located at a latitude of 37.059 and a longitude of -111.364.','2025-03-28 01:28:34','2025-03-28 01:28:34'),(13031,'trails',261,'Is a special vehicle required to access Alstrom Point?','Yes, a 4WD vehicle is necessary to navigate the trail effectively.','2025-03-28 01:28:34','2025-03-28 01:28:34'),(13032,'trails',261,'Are pets allowed on the Alstrom Point trail?','Unfortunately, pets are not permitted on this trail.','2025-03-28 01:28:34','2025-03-28 01:28:34'),(13033,'trails',261,'Do I need to make a reservation to hike Alstrom Point?','No reservations are required to hike this trail.','2025-03-28 01:28:34','2025-03-28 01:28:34'),(13034,'trails',261,'How long does it take to hike Alstrom Point?','Plan to spend a full day hiking to fully enjoy the experience.','2025-03-28 01:28:34','2025-03-28 01:28:34'),(13035,'trails',261,'What vehicle should I use to get to the trailhead?','You will want to use a high-clearance vehicle, specifically a model like the K8150.','2025-03-28 01:28:34','2025-03-28 01:28:34'),(13036,'trails',261,'What are the directions to reach Alstrom Point?','From Kanab, drive 56 miles east on HWY 89, then turn left onto Ethan Allen Road, continue for 0.3 miles, turn right on K8000/300 for 14 miles, then right on K8200/340 and drive 4.23 miles, finally turn right on K8180 and proceed 6.88 miles to Alstrom Point. The route can be tricky, with slick rock areas and rock cairns marking the way.','2025-03-28 01:28:34','2025-03-28 01:28:34'),(13037,'trails',261,'What can I expect to see at Alstrom Point?','Alstrom Point offers stunning panoramas of Lake Powell, ideal for photography, especially during sunrise and sunset. The majestic Navajo Mountain can also be observed in the distance, representing significant cultural heritage for Native Americans.','2025-03-28 01:28:34','2025-03-28 01:28:34'),(13038,'trails',261,'Is it safe to drive to Alstrom Point at night?','Driving to Alstrom Point at night is not advisable due to the challenging terrain and lack of visibility.','2025-03-28 01:28:34','2025-03-28 01:28:34'),(13039,'trails',261,'What should I know before visiting Alstrom Point?','Ensure your 4WD vehicle is in excellent condition as the area is very remote with limited to no cell service. Carry ample food, water, fuel, and a shovel. Always check the weather and road conditions beforehand, and respect private property by leaving no trace of your visit.','2025-03-28 01:28:34','2025-03-28 01:28:34'),(13040,'trails',262,'What is the length of the Belly of the Dragon trail?','The Belly of the Dragon hike is approximately half a mile long.','2025-03-28 01:28:43','2025-03-28 01:28:43'),(13041,'trails',262,'When is the best time to hike the Belly of the Dragon?','This trail is accessible year-round, making it a great option no matter the season.','2025-03-28 01:28:43','2025-03-28 01:28:43'),(13042,'trails',262,'How difficult is the Belly of the Dragon hike?','The trail is rated as easy, making it suitable for hikers of all skill levels.','2025-03-28 01:28:43','2025-03-28 01:28:43'),(13043,'trails',262,'What is the elevation of the Belly of the Dragon trail?','The trail sits at an elevation of 6,000 feet.','2025-03-28 01:28:43','2025-03-28 01:28:43'),(13044,'trails',262,'Are pets allowed on the Belly of the Dragon trail?','Unfortunately, pets are not permitted on this trail.','2025-03-28 01:28:43','2025-03-28 01:28:43'),(13045,'trails',262,'Is a reservation needed to hike the Belly of the Dragon?','No reservations are required to access this trail.','2025-03-28 01:28:43','2025-03-28 01:28:43'),(13046,'trails',262,'How long does it typically take to complete the trail?','You can expect to spend about 1 to 2 hours hiking the Belly of the Dragon.','2025-03-28 01:28:43','2025-03-28 01:28:43'),(13047,'trails',262,'What type of vehicle is suitable for accessing the trailhead?','A standard car with 2WD can easily reach the trailhead.','2025-03-28 01:28:43','2025-03-28 01:28:43'),(13048,'trails',262,'What are the directions to get to the Belly of the Dragon?','To get there from Kanab, drive about 16 miles north on HWY 89. After passing mile post 80, look for the Zion National Park sign, turn left onto the dirt road, and follow it until you veer left at a fork. Park at the top of the hill, walk up, and you\'ll see the tunnel entrance.','2025-03-28 01:28:43','2025-03-28 01:28:43'),(13049,'trails',262,'Can you describe the Belly of the Dragon hike?','The Belly of the Dragon is a fun and picturesque hike that features a carved tunnel beneath Highway 89, serving as a drainage for nearby upper canyons flowing into the North Fork River. Be sure to avoid entering the tunnel during rain, as it can be unsafe. The hike includes some rock scrambling, and you\'ll find interesting carvings at the tunnel entrance, which should be respected. You can also continue further up the wash for about 4 miles to discover a stunning narrow slot canyon with spectacular views.','2025-03-28 01:28:43','2025-03-28 01:28:43'),(13050,'trails',262,'What additional information should I keep in mind while hiking?','Use this map and directions mainly for reference. It\'s important to check local road and weather conditions prior to your hike. Stick to designated roads, as dirt paths can become impassable if wet. Respect private property and be adequately prepared with food, water, sunscreen, and necessary supplies. Note that cell service is often unavailable. Finally, please do not remove artifacts or deface rock art, and remember to leave no trace to preserve the experience for others.','2025-03-28 01:28:43','2025-03-28 01:28:43'),(13051,'trails',263,'What is the distance of the Aspen Mirror Lake trail?','The Aspen Mirror Lake trail spans approximately 11.1 miles.','2025-03-28 01:28:54','2025-03-28 01:28:54'),(13052,'trails',263,'When is the best time to hike the Aspen Mirror Lake trail?','You can enjoy the Aspen Mirror Lake trail year-round, as it offers unique beauty in every season.','2025-03-28 01:28:54','2025-03-28 01:28:54'),(13053,'trails',263,'How difficult is the Aspen Mirror Lake trail?','The trail is considered easy, making it accessible for hikers of various skill levels.','2025-03-28 01:28:54','2025-03-28 01:28:54'),(13054,'trails',263,'What is the elevation of Aspen Mirror Lake?','The trail reaches an elevation of about 8500 feet.','2025-03-28 01:28:54','2025-03-28 01:28:54'),(13055,'trails',263,'What are the coordinates of Aspen Mirror Lake?','Aspen Mirror Lake is located at a latitude of 37.517 and a longitude of 112.682.','2025-03-28 01:28:54','2025-03-28 01:28:54'),(13056,'trails',263,'Is the Aspen Mirror Lake trail accessible by all vehicles?','Yes, the trail can be accessed by 2WD vehicles.','2025-03-28 01:28:54','2025-03-28 01:28:54'),(13057,'trails',263,'Are pets allowed on the Aspen Mirror Lake trail?','Unfortunately, pets are not permitted on this trail.','2025-03-28 01:28:54','2025-03-28 01:28:54'),(13058,'trails',263,'Do I need a reservation to hike the Aspen Mirror Lake trail?','No reservations are required to hike this trail.','2025-03-28 01:28:54','2025-03-28 01:28:54'),(13059,'trails',263,'How long does it typically take to hike the Aspen Mirror Lake trail?','Hiking the trail can take anywhere from 3 hours to a full day, depending on your pace and enjoyment of the surroundings.','2025-03-28 01:28:54','2025-03-28 01:28:54'),(13060,'trails',263,'How do I get to Aspen Mirror Lake?','To reach Aspen Mirror Lake, drive 40 miles north from Kanab on HWY 89, turn left onto HWY 14, drive about 11.1 miles, then turn right onto FR057. After a short distance, take another right onto the Markagunt Plateau OHV Trail and fork there.','2025-03-28 01:28:55','2025-03-28 01:28:55'),(13061,'trails',263,'Can you describe the Aspen Mirror Lake trail?','Nestled away from main roads, Aspen Mirror Lake is a picturesque spot surrounded by pines and aspen trees, particularly beautiful in fall and offering cool retreats in summer. The lake, which reflects the stunning aspens, is a paradise for photographers. It is also stocked with rainbow trout, making it a great fishing destination. Wildlife enthusiasts will enjoy sightings of deer, chipmunks, squirrels, foxes, frogs, and snakes. Additionally, several hiking, biking, and OHV trails are nearby. Don\'t forget to explore Duck Creek Village for dining options. For more details, reach out to the Dixie National Forest Visitor Center at 435-865-3730.','2025-03-28 01:28:55','2025-03-28 01:28:55'),(13062,'trails',263,'Is there any important additional information for hikers of Aspen Mirror Lake?','Please note that the provided map and directions are for general reference. Always verify local road and weather conditions, stay on designated paths, and prepare for wilderness experiences by bringing extra food, water, and supplies. Be aware that cell phone service is often unreliable in the area. Respect private property and natural resources, and remember to practice Leave No Trace principles so that others can appreciate the trail.','2025-03-28 01:28:55','2025-03-28 01:28:55'),(13063,'trails',265,'What is the length of the Coral Pink Sand Dunes State Park trail?','The trail spans approximately 5 miles, providing plenty of space for exploration.','2025-03-28 01:29:11','2025-03-28 01:29:11'),(13064,'trails',265,'When is the best time to visit the Coral Pink Sand Dunes State Park?','This park is ideal for visits throughout the year, offering diverse experiences in every season.','2025-03-28 01:29:11','2025-03-28 01:29:11'),(13065,'trails',265,'How challenging is the trail at Coral Pink Sand Dunes State Park?','The trail is categorized as easy, making it accessible for hikers of all skill levels.','2025-03-28 01:29:11','2025-03-28 01:29:11'),(13066,'trails',265,'What is the elevation of Coral Pink Sand Dunes State Park?','The park\'s elevation is around 6,000 feet, providing stunning views of the surrounding landscape.','2025-03-28 01:29:11','2025-03-28 01:29:11'),(13067,'trails',265,'What are the GPS coordinates for Coral Pink Sand Dunes State Park?','You can find the park at latitude 37.040398 and longitude -112.732130.','2025-03-28 01:29:11','2025-03-28 01:29:11'),(13068,'trails',265,'Is the Coral Pink Sand Dunes State Park accessible for everyone?','Yes, the park is designed to be accessible, making it easier for all visitors to enjoy.','2025-03-28 01:29:11','2025-03-28 01:29:11'),(13069,'trails',265,'Are pets allowed on the trail?','Unfortunately, pets are not permitted within the park.','2025-03-28 01:29:11','2025-03-28 01:29:11'),(13070,'trails',265,'Do I need a reservation to visit Coral Pink Sand Dunes State Park?','No reservations are necessary for entrance to this beautiful park.','2025-03-28 01:29:11','2025-03-28 01:29:11'),(13071,'trails',265,'How long does it typically take to hike the trail?','Depending on your pace, you can spend anywhere from 1 to 8 hours enjoying the hike.','2025-03-28 01:29:11','2025-03-28 01:29:11'),(13072,'trails',265,'Can I use an off-road vehicle at Coral Pink Sand Dunes State Park?','Yes, off-road vehicles are welcome, and the park offers ample space for thrilling adventures.','2025-03-28 01:29:11','2025-03-28 01:29:11'),(13073,'trails',265,'What is the best way to get to Coral Pink Sand Dunes State Park?','To reach the park, drive 8 miles north from Kanab on HWY 89, take a left after mile post 71 onto Hancock Road, travel 9.5 miles, then turn left at the stop sign. The park entrance will be about 5 miles down the road on your left.','2025-03-28 01:29:11','2025-03-28 01:29:11'),(13074,'trails',265,'Can you describe what Coral Pink Sand Dunes State Park has to offer?','Coral Pink Sand Dunes State Park is a popular destination where your imagination can run free. You can explore the stunning pink sands on foot, bike, board, or off-road vehicle. There\'s 1,200 acres of open riding areas for OHV enthusiasts, and nearby, you\'ll find additional trails on BLM land. The park also features fascinating attractions like the South Fork Indian Canyon Pictographs and dinosaur tracks. Don’t forget to bring a picnic to enjoy at the facilities provided while taking in the view from the Observation Deck.','2025-03-28 01:29:11','2025-03-28 01:29:11'),(13075,'trails',265,'What additional activities can I enjoy after visiting the park?','After an exhilarating day at the dunes, head back to Kanab for dining options. Be sure to reserve a table at one of the popular local restaurants for a delightful dining experience in Southern Utah. For more adventure, visit the Kane County Visitor Center to find maps and additional activities in the area.','2025-03-28 01:29:11','2025-03-28 01:29:11'),(13076,'trails',266,'What is the distance of the Dinosaur Tracks Hike?','The hike spans a total of 3.4 miles.','2025-03-28 01:29:24','2025-03-28 01:29:24'),(13077,'trails',266,'When is the best season to hike the Dinosaur Tracks Trail?','This trail can be enjoyed year-round, making it accessible in any season.','2025-03-28 01:29:24','2025-03-28 01:29:24'),(13078,'trails',266,'What is the difficulty level of the Dinosaur Tracks Hike?','The trail is categorized as steep and rocky, presenting an intermediate challenge to hikers.','2025-03-28 01:29:24','2025-03-28 01:29:24'),(13079,'trails',266,'What is the elevation of the Dinosaur Tracks Hike?','The hike reaches an elevation of approximately 5,700 feet.','2025-03-28 01:29:24','2025-03-28 01:29:24'),(13080,'trails',266,'Where is the Dinosaur Tracks Hike located?','The hike is located near the coordinates 37.190355 latitude and -112.645567 longitude.','2025-03-28 01:29:24','2025-03-28 01:29:24'),(13081,'trails',266,'How can I access the Dinosaur Tracks Hike?','You can reach the trailhead by car. From Kanab, take Hwy 89 north for about 3 miles and turn right at the Port of Entry between mileposts 67 and 68.','2025-03-28 01:29:25','2025-03-28 01:29:25'),(13082,'trails',266,'Are pets allowed on the Dinosaur Tracks Hike?','Unfortunately, pets are not permitted on this trail.','2025-03-28 01:29:25','2025-03-28 01:29:25'),(13083,'trails',266,'Do I need a reservation to hike the Dinosaur Tracks?','No reservation is required for this trail, making it easy to plan your visit.','2025-03-28 01:29:25','2025-03-28 01:29:25'),(13084,'trails',266,'How long does it typically take to complete the Dinosaur Tracks Hike?','On average, hikers can expect to spend about 2 hours on this trail.','2025-03-28 01:29:25','2025-03-28 01:29:25'),(13085,'trails',266,'What should I know about getting to the Dinosaur Tracks Hike?','After parking at the south end near the porta-potty, walk through the sagebrush to find an old dirt road heading east. Follow it until you locate the opening in the rocks that leads you upward.','2025-03-28 01:29:25','2025-03-28 01:29:25'),(13086,'trails',266,'What can I expect to see on the Dinosaur Tracks hike?','This hike leads you to a fascinating area where over 20 species of dinosaurs have been found, showcasing well-preserved tracks from various ancient creatures, including a six-foot-long carnivorous dinosaur.','2025-03-28 01:29:25','2025-03-28 01:29:25'),(13087,'trails',266,'Are there any safety concerns for hikers on this trail?','Hikers should be cautious as the trail is steep and rocky, and there have been reports of rattlesnakes in the area.','2025-03-28 01:29:25','2025-03-28 01:29:25'),(13088,'trails',266,'What additional information should I consider for my hike?','Keep in mind that road and weather conditions may vary. Stick to designated paths, avoid wet dirt roads, and respect local private properties. It is advisable to carry extra water, food, sunscreen, and other essentials as cell service is limited. Enjoy your hike responsibly!','2025-03-28 01:29:25','2025-03-28 01:29:25'),(13089,'trails',267,'What is the distance of the Eagle Sink trail?','The Eagle Sink trail covers a total distance of 20.75 miles.','2025-03-28 01:29:37','2025-03-28 01:29:37'),(13090,'trails',267,'When is the best time to hike the Eagle Sink trail?','This trail can be enjoyed year-round, making it a versatile option for hikers.','2025-03-28 01:29:37','2025-03-28 01:29:37'),(13091,'trails',267,'What is the difficulty level of the Eagle Sink trail?','Hikers will find the Eagle Sink trail to be of moderate difficulty.','2025-03-28 01:29:37','2025-03-28 01:29:37'),(13092,'trails',267,'What is the elevation of the Eagle Sink trail?','The trail reaches an elevation of 5,800 feet, offering stunning views from the top.','2025-03-28 01:29:37','2025-03-28 01:29:37'),(13093,'trails',267,'What are the GPS coordinates for Eagle Sink?','The coordinates for Eagle Sink are approximately 37.0442° latitude and -112.1508° longitude.','2025-03-28 01:29:37','2025-03-28 01:29:37'),(13094,'trails',267,'What type of vehicle is recommended for accessing the Eagle Sink trail?','A 4WD vehicle is recommended to navigate the access road to the trail.','2025-03-28 01:29:37','2025-03-28 01:29:37'),(13095,'trails',267,'Are pets allowed on the Eagle Sink trail?','Yes, pets are welcome on the Eagle Sink trail.','2025-03-28 01:29:37','2025-03-28 01:29:37'),(13096,'trails',267,'Is a reservation required to hike the Eagle Sink trail?','No reservations are necessary to access this trail.','2025-03-28 01:29:37','2025-03-28 01:29:37'),(13097,'trails',267,'How long does it typically take to hike the Eagle Sink trail?','On average, hikers should plan for about 3 hours to complete the hike.','2025-03-28 01:29:37','2025-03-28 01:29:37'),(13098,'trails',267,'What are the directions to get to the Eagle Sink trail?','From Kanab, drive 20.75 miles east on HWY 89. After mile post 43, turn right, cross the cattle guard, and follow the road which will Y into another road heading west. Keep an eye out for a T road on the left (road #730) and take that. Watch for another Y directing you to Eagle Sink on the right.','2025-03-28 01:29:37','2025-03-28 01:29:37'),(13099,'trails',267,'Can you describe Eagle Sink?','Eagle Sink is a remarkable limestone sinkhole visible from the highway, plunging approximately 160 feet deep, and surrounded by breathtaking 360-degree views. A portion is fenced for safety, so be cautious near the edge due to loose rocks and wind. The sinkhole is home to various bird species, adding to its charm. Located around 21 miles east of Kanab, the access road can turn slick when wet, requiring 4WD. Adventurers may also explore other nearby sinkholes in the Grand Staircase-Escalante National Monument.','2025-03-28 01:29:37','2025-03-28 01:29:37'),(13100,'trails',267,'What additional information should I know before hiking at Eagle Sink?','Always check local road and weather conditions, stay on marked paths, and be aware that dirt roads can become impassable in wet conditions. Respect private property, and come prepared for a wilderness outing: bring extra water, snacks, sunscreen, and supplies. Note that cell service is limited in the area. Finally, practice leave-no-trace principles to preserve the site for future visitors.','2025-03-28 01:29:37','2025-03-28 01:29:37'),(13101,'trails',269,'How long is the Lower Hackberry Canyon trail?','The Lower Hackberry Canyon trail covers a distance of 4.5 miles.','2025-03-28 01:29:46','2025-03-28 01:29:46'),(13102,'trails',269,'What is the best season to hike Lower Hackberry Canyon?','The trail is best enjoyed in the Spring, Summer, and Fall due to the pleasant weather conditions.','2025-03-28 01:29:46','2025-03-28 01:29:46'),(13103,'trails',269,'What is the difficulty level of the hike?','This hike is classified as Easy, making it suitable for hikers of all skill levels.','2025-03-28 01:29:46','2025-03-28 01:29:46'),(13104,'trails',269,'What is the elevation of the Lower Hackberry Canyon?','The trail reaches an elevation of 4,770 feet.','2025-03-28 01:29:46','2025-03-28 01:29:46'),(13105,'trails',269,'Is the trail accessible by car?','Yes, the trailhead is accessible by vehicle, specifically by car.','2025-03-28 01:29:46','2025-03-28 01:29:46'),(13106,'trails',269,'Are pets allowed on the Lower Hackberry Canyon trail?','The policy regarding pets is currently unknown, so it\'s best to check local guidelines before bringing your pet.','2025-03-28 01:29:46','2025-03-28 01:29:46'),(13107,'trails',269,'Do I need a reservation to hike Lower Hackberry Canyon?','No reservations are required to hike this trail.','2025-03-28 01:29:46','2025-03-28 01:29:46'),(13108,'trails',269,'How many hours should I allocate for this hike?','Most hikers will complete the trail in about half a day.','2025-03-28 01:29:46','2025-03-28 01:29:46'),(13109,'trails',269,'How do I get to Lower Hackberry Canyon?','To reach Lower Hackberry Canyon from Kanab, drive 46.2 miles east on Highway 89. After passing mile marker 18, take a left onto road #200 (Cottonwood Road). Continue for approximately 14.7 miles, then turn left at the sign for Lower Hackberry Canyon. Park in the designated area, put on your water shoes, and head west into the wash. Follow the willows on the main hiking path to enter Hackberry Canyon.','2025-03-28 01:29:46','2025-03-28 01:29:46'),(13110,'trails',269,'What can I expect to see on the hike?','The Lower Hackberry Canyon offers a picturesque narrow slot canyon with clear, shallow water flowing through a sandy stream bed. During the hike, you\'ll reach dinosaur tracks located on the left bank at about 2.1 miles in. This area is perfect for families and provides a remarkable wilderness experience.','2025-03-28 01:29:46','2025-03-28 01:29:46'),(13111,'trails',269,'What should I remember about hiking Lower Hackberry Canyon?','Always ensure you\'re prepared for a wilderness experience by bringing extra water, food, sunscreen, and necessary supplies. Be mindful of possible flash floods during the monsoon season, and it\'s advisable to check local weather and road conditions before your visit. Remember to respect the environment and practice Leave No Trace principles.','2025-03-28 01:29:46','2025-03-28 01:29:46'),(13112,'trails',270,'What is the length of the Cottonwood Canyon Trail?','The Cottonwood Canyon Trail spans 10.6 miles.','2025-03-28 01:29:58','2025-03-28 01:29:58'),(13113,'trails',270,'When is the best time of year to hike the Cottonwood Canyon Trail?','This trail can be enjoyed throughout the year, although it\'s particularly pleasant during the cooler months.','2025-03-28 01:29:58','2025-03-28 01:29:58'),(13114,'trails',270,'What is the difficulty level of the trail?','The trail is rated as moderate in difficulty, making it suitable for those with some hiking experience.','2025-03-28 01:29:58','2025-03-28 01:29:58'),(13115,'trails',270,'What is the elevation of the Cottonwood Canyon Trail?','The trail reaches an elevation of 5,040 feet.','2025-03-28 01:29:58','2025-03-28 01:29:58'),(13116,'trails',270,'What are the coordinates of the trail?','The trail is located at approximately 37.0368° N latitude and 112.4580° W longitude.','2025-03-28 01:29:58','2025-03-28 01:29:58'),(13117,'trails',270,'Is the trail accessible?','Yes, the Cottonwood Canyon Trail is accessible.','2025-03-28 01:29:58','2025-03-28 01:29:58'),(13118,'trails',270,'Are pets allowed on the trail?','Unfortunately, pets are not permitted on this trail.','2025-03-28 01:29:58','2025-03-28 01:29:58'),(13119,'trails',270,'Do I need a reservation to hike the Cottonwood Canyon Trail?','No reservation is required to hike this trail.','2025-03-28 01:29:58','2025-03-28 01:29:58'),(13120,'trails',270,'How long does it typically take to complete the hike?','On average, hikers can complete the trail in about half a day.','2025-03-28 01:29:58','2025-03-28 01:29:58'),(13121,'trails',270,'What type of vehicle is recommended to access the trail?','A car is the best option to reach the trailhead.','2025-03-28 01:29:58','2025-03-28 01:29:58'),(13122,'trails',270,'How do I get to the Cottonwood Canyon Trail?','To reach the trail, start from the center of Kanab, head south on HWY 89A for about 1.2 miles, then turn right onto Kench Creek Drive. After driving 2 miles, turn right onto Stanfield Drive at the top of the hill. The parking area for the Bunting Trail will be the first on your right; for Cottonwood Canyon, continue up the hill.','2025-03-28 01:29:58','2025-03-28 01:29:58'),(13123,'trails',270,'Can you describe the trail experience?','The Cottonwood Canyon Trail offers breathtaking views of the Vermilion Cliffs and traverses through rugged canyons in southern Utah and northern Arizona. It\'s a moderately challenging hike that features various desert landscapes and ravines, ideal for those looking for scenic beauty. Keep in mind that cell phone reception in the area is limited.','2025-03-28 01:29:58','2025-03-28 01:29:58'),(13124,'trails',270,'What additional information should I know before hiking?','The directions and map are provided for general guidance, so be sure to check road and weather conditions prior to your visit, as dirt roads may become impassable after rain. Respect private property and practice Leave No Trace principles. Always come prepared with extra water, food, sunscreen, and proper hiking gear. For more information, you can contact 435.644.5033.','2025-03-28 01:29:58','2025-03-28 01:29:58'),(13125,'trails',271,'What is the length of the Bunting Trail?','The Bunting Trail stretches for a distance of 2.3 miles.','2025-03-28 01:30:10','2025-03-28 01:30:10'),(13126,'trails',271,'When is the best time to hike the Bunting Trail?','You can enjoy the Bunting Trail throughout the year, as it\'s accessible in all seasons.','2025-03-28 01:30:10','2025-03-28 01:30:10'),(13127,'trails',271,'What level of difficulty can I expect on the Bunting Trail?','This trail is considered hard and steep, making it suitable for experienced hikers.','2025-03-28 01:30:10','2025-03-28 01:30:10'),(13128,'trails',271,'What is the elevation range of the Bunting Trail?','Hikers will experience elevations ranging from 5040 to 5860 feet.','2025-03-28 01:30:10','2025-03-28 01:30:10'),(13129,'trails',271,'Is the Bunting Trail accessible for all hikers?','Yes, the trail is designed to be accessible for hikers.','2025-03-28 01:30:10','2025-03-28 01:30:10'),(13130,'trails',271,'Can I bring my pets on the Bunting Trail?','Unfortunately, pets are not allowed on the Bunting Trail.','2025-03-28 01:30:10','2025-03-28 01:30:10'),(13131,'trails',271,'Do I need a reservation to hike the Bunting Trail?','No, there is no reservation needed to access this trail.','2025-03-28 01:30:10','2025-03-28 01:30:10'),(13132,'trails',271,'How long does it typically take to hike the Bunting Trail?','Most hikers can complete the trail in about half a day.','2025-03-28 01:30:10','2025-03-28 01:30:10'),(13133,'trails',271,'What type of vehicle do I need to access the parking area for the Bunting Trail?','A standard 2WD vehicle is sufficient to reach the parking area.','2025-03-28 01:30:10','2025-03-28 01:30:10'),(13134,'trails',271,'What are the directions to get to the Bunting Trail?','To reach the trailhead, head south on HWY 89A from Main Street for about 1.2 miles. Turn right onto Kanab Creek Drive, continue for 2 miles, then make a right onto Stanfield Drive at the top of the hill. The parking area for the Bunting Trail will be the first on your right. Proceed north to find the trailhead.','2025-03-28 01:30:10','2025-03-28 01:30:10'),(13135,'trails',271,'What can I expect to see on the Bunting Trail?','As you hike the Bunting Trail, you\'ll be treated to stunning views of Kanab and the surrounding landscape. At the summit, you\'ll discover fascinating petroglyphs and a magnificent overlook of the Grand Staircase and Bryce Canyon National Park.','2025-03-28 01:30:11','2025-03-28 01:30:11'),(13136,'trails',271,'What should I keep in mind while hiking the Bunting Trail?','As you near the top, be on the lookout for petroglyphs. For the adventurous, there\'s a Spur Trail offering additional scenic views. Make sure to bring extra water, snacks, sunscreen, and other essentials since cell phone service is limited in the area. Always respect private property and practice leave-no-trace principles.','2025-03-28 01:30:11','2025-03-28 01:30:11'),(13137,'trails',271,'Who can I contact for more information about the Bunting Trail?','For further information, you can reach out to the Kanab Visitor\'s Center at 435.644.5033.','2025-03-28 01:30:11','2025-03-28 01:30:11'),(13138,'trails',272,'What is the distance of the Cascade Falls trail?','The Cascade Falls trail stretches for 1.6 miles, making it an accessible option for various hikers.','2025-03-28 01:30:21','2025-03-28 01:30:21'),(13139,'trails',272,'What is the best time of year to hike Cascade Falls?','The optimal time to explore the Cascade Falls trail is from June through October, when conditions are most favorable.','2025-03-28 01:30:21','2025-03-28 01:30:21'),(13140,'trails',272,'How difficult is the Cascade Falls hike?','The hike is categorized as easy, making it suitable for families and beginner hikers.','2025-03-28 01:30:21','2025-03-28 01:30:21'),(13141,'trails',272,'What is the elevation of the Cascade Falls trail?','The trail reaches an elevation of 9,500 feet, offering some breathtaking views.','2025-03-28 01:30:21','2025-03-28 01:30:21'),(13142,'trails',272,'Can I bring my pet on the Cascade Falls trail?','Yes, pets are allowed on the trail, provided they are kept on a leash.','2025-03-28 01:30:21','2025-03-28 01:30:21'),(13143,'trails',272,'Is a reservation needed to hike Cascade Falls?','No reservations are required to access the trail, allowing for spontaneous adventures.','2025-03-28 01:30:21','2025-03-28 01:30:21'),(13144,'trails',272,'How long does it take to hike Cascade Falls?','On average, the hike typically takes around 2 hours to complete.','2025-03-28 01:30:21','2025-03-28 01:30:21'),(13145,'trails',272,'What type of vehicle is recommended for accessing the trail?','A 2WD vehicle is sufficient to reach the parking area for the trail.','2025-03-28 01:30:21','2025-03-28 01:30:21'),(13146,'trails',272,'Can you explain how to get to Cascade Falls?','To reach Cascade Falls, start from Kanab and head north for 40 miles on HWY 89. After mile marker 25, take a left onto HWY 14. Drive approximately 15 miles, then turn left onto Navajo Lake Road. Continue for 32 miles and make a left on FR054. Drive 1.1 miles and stay to the right on FR054 until you arrive at the trailhead parking area.','2025-03-28 01:30:21','2025-03-28 01:30:21'),(13147,'trails',272,'What can I expect to see on the Cascade Falls trail?','The Cascade Falls hike offers remarkable canyon views and features a well-marked, mostly flat trail. Benches are available along the route to provide spots for resting and enjoying the scenery, culminating in a lovely waterfall that flows from the cliff rocks at the trail\'s end, sourced from Navajo Lake.','2025-03-28 01:30:21','2025-03-28 01:30:21'),(13148,'trails',272,'Are there any additional tips for hiking Cascade Falls?','Be sure to check local road and weather conditions before your hike. It\'s essential to stay on marked paths, as dirt roads can be challenging during wet weather. Remember to respect private property, bring extra water, snacks, sunscreen, and other necessary supplies, as cell phone service may be limited. Please leave no trace to preserve the area for others.','2025-03-28 01:30:21','2025-03-28 01:30:21'),(13149,'trails',273,'What is the distance of Catstair trail?','The Catstair trail stretches for 0.50 miles.','2025-03-28 01:30:33','2025-03-28 01:30:33'),(13150,'trails',273,'When is the best time to hike Catstair?','You can enjoy hiking the Catstair trail year-round, regardless of the season.','2025-03-28 01:30:33','2025-03-28 01:30:33'),(13151,'trails',273,'How challenging is the Catstair trail?','This trail is categorized as easy, making it suitable for hikers of all experience levels.','2025-03-28 01:30:33','2025-03-28 01:30:33'),(13152,'trails',273,'What is the elevation of the Catstair trail?','The trail reaches an elevation of 4,709 feet.','2025-03-28 01:30:33','2025-03-28 01:30:33'),(13153,'trails',273,'Where is the Catstair trail located?','The coordinates for the Catstair trail are 37.04376 latitude and -112.49916 longitude.','2025-03-28 01:30:34','2025-03-28 01:30:34'),(13154,'trails',273,'Is the Catstair trail accessible with full sun?','Yes, the trail offers full sun exposure, so be prepared for bright conditions.','2025-03-28 01:30:34','2025-03-28 01:30:34'),(13155,'trails',273,'Are pets allowed on the Catstair trail?','Unfortunately, pets are not permitted on the trail.','2025-03-28 01:30:34','2025-03-28 01:30:34'),(13156,'trails',273,'Do I need a reservation to hike Catstair?','No reservation is necessary to hike the Catstair trail.','2025-03-28 01:30:34','2025-03-28 01:30:34'),(13157,'trails',273,'How long does it typically take to hike the Catstair trail?','On average, you can expect to spend about 1.5 hours on this hike.','2025-03-28 01:30:34','2025-03-28 01:30:34'),(13158,'trails',273,'What type of vehicle is suitable for reaching the Catstair trail?','The trail can be accessed by passenger vehicles.','2025-03-28 01:30:34','2025-03-28 01:30:34'),(13159,'trails',273,'How do I get to the Catstair trail?','To reach the trail, drive 39 miles east from Kanab on HWY 89. After milepost 25, look for a gap in the guardrail on the south side of the road. Turn carefully into the trailhead and park at the end of the road. The trailhead is located just down a short hill on the south side, and you’ll enter the narrow slot canyon by heading downstream in the wash.','2025-03-28 01:30:34','2025-03-28 01:30:34'),(13160,'trails',273,'Can you describe what I’ll see on the Catstair trail?','As you hike, you\'ll encounter a stunning water pocket fold in the earth and the picturesque Cotshmir slot canyon, famed for its dramatic scenery and film history. About a quarter-mile in, you\'ll come across the Detroit Rip-Rap, and don\'t miss the nearby Carstair Writings, which showcase ancient petroglyphs and pictographs.','2025-03-28 01:30:34','2025-03-28 01:30:34'),(13161,'trails',273,'Is there any additional information I should know before hiking Catstair?','Make sure to check local road and weather conditions before your visit, as this map and directions are meant for general reference. It\'s essential to respect private property, prepare for a wilderness experience by bringing sufficient water, food, sunscreen, and supplies, and note that cell phone service may be unreliable. Please ensure to leave no trace and preserve the area for future visitors.','2025-03-28 01:30:34','2025-03-28 01:30:34'),(13162,'trails',274,'What is the length of the Catstair Writings trail?','The Catstair Writings trail covers a total distance of 1.5 miles for a round trip.','2025-03-28 01:30:45','2025-03-28 01:30:45'),(13163,'trails',274,'What is the best time of year to hike Catstair Writings?','You can enjoy the Catstair Writings trail in any season, making it accessible year-round.','2025-03-28 01:30:45','2025-03-28 01:30:45'),(13164,'trails',274,'How difficult is the Catstair Writings trail?','This trail is considered easy, making it suitable for hikers of all experience levels.','2025-03-28 01:30:45','2025-03-28 01:30:45'),(13165,'trails',274,'What is the elevation of the Catstair Writings trail?','The trail reaches an elevation of 4,573 feet.','2025-03-28 01:30:45','2025-03-28 01:30:45'),(13166,'trails',274,'Can I access Catstair Writings by vehicle?','The trail is accessible by hiking only; you will need to park and begin your hike from the designated point.','2025-03-28 01:30:45','2025-03-28 01:30:45'),(13167,'trails',274,'Are pets allowed on the Catstair Writings trail?','No, pets are not permitted on this hiking trail.','2025-03-28 01:30:45','2025-03-28 01:30:45'),(13168,'trails',274,'Do I need a reservation to hike Catstair Writings?','There is no reservation needed to hike the Catstair Writings trail.','2025-03-28 01:30:45','2025-03-28 01:30:45'),(13169,'trails',274,'How long does it typically take to hike Catstair Writings?','Most hikers complete the trail in a few hours, allowing plenty of time to take in the sights.','2025-03-28 01:30:45','2025-03-28 01:30:45'),(13170,'trails',274,'What are the directions to reach Catstair Writings?','From Kanab, travel 39.8 miles east on Highway 89. Just after House Rock Valley Road, look for a gate on the south side of the road, between mileposts 25 and 24. Turn here, open the gate, and drive through.','2025-03-28 01:30:45','2025-03-28 01:30:45'),(13171,'trails',274,'What can I expect to see while hiking Catstair Writings?','As you hike, you will encounter fascinating petroglyphs, pictographs, and unique \'Cowboy glyphs\' from early ranchers, all while enjoying the stunning views of the box canyon.','2025-03-28 01:30:46','2025-03-28 01:30:46'),(13172,'trails',274,'What should I know before hiking Catstair Writings?','Be mindful of private property and prepare for an outdoor experience. Always carry extra water, food, sunscreen, and necessary supplies. Note that cell phone service is limited in many areas, and remember to leave no trace to preserve the site for future visitors.','2025-03-28 01:30:46','2025-03-28 01:30:46'),(13173,'trails',275,'What is the distance of the Cliffs Trail?','The Cliffs Trail spans approximately 500 miles.','2025-03-28 01:30:59','2025-03-28 01:30:59'),(13174,'trails',275,'When is the best time to hike the Cliffs Trail?','You can hike the Cliffs Trail year-round, making it a versatile option for outdoor enthusiasts at any time.','2025-03-28 01:30:59','2025-03-28 01:30:59'),(13175,'trails',275,'How difficult is the Cliffs Trail?','The trail is categorized as difficult, so it\'s best suited for experienced hikers.','2025-03-28 01:30:59','2025-03-28 01:30:59'),(13176,'trails',275,'What is the elevation you will reach on the Cliffs Trail?','Hikers will ascend to an elevation of around 6000 feet on this trail.','2025-03-28 01:30:59','2025-03-28 01:30:59'),(13177,'trails',275,'Where is the Cliffs Trail located?','The Cliffs Trail is located at a latitude of 37.0464 and a longitude of -112.5244.','2025-03-28 01:30:59','2025-03-28 01:30:59'),(13178,'trails',275,'Is the trail accessible by 2WD vehicles?','Yes, the trail can be accessed by a 2WD vehicle.','2025-03-28 01:30:59','2025-03-28 01:30:59'),(13179,'trails',275,'Are pets allowed on the Cliffs Trail?','Unfortunately, pets are not permitted on this trail.','2025-03-28 01:30:59','2025-03-28 01:30:59'),(13180,'trails',275,'Do I need a reservation to hike the Cliffs Trail?','No reservations are required to hike the Cliffs Trail.','2025-03-28 01:30:59','2025-03-28 01:30:59'),(13181,'trails',275,'How long does it typically take to hike the Cliffs Trail?','Most hikers complete the Cliffs Trail in about 3 hours.','2025-03-28 01:30:59','2025-03-28 01:30:59'),(13182,'trails',275,'How do I get to the Cliffs Trail?','To reach the trailhead, start from the town center at the intersection of Center and Main Streets. Head north on Main Street, make a right on 300 North, go 4 blocks into the La Estancia subdivision, turn right at the waterwheel, and park at the street curve. Walk up the hill to find the trailhead kiosk.','2025-03-28 01:30:59','2025-03-28 01:30:59'),(13183,'trails',275,'What can I expect while hiking the Cliffs Trail?','This trail offers a rugged hike that leads you through scenic canyons and up to stunning cliff-top vistas. Keep an eye out for the Cliffs Connector Trail on your left, which provides access to several other trails, including Cliffs 2 and Squaw Trail. The climb can be steep and rocky, but the views from the top are worth the effort.','2025-03-28 01:30:59','2025-03-28 01:30:59'),(13184,'trails',275,'Is there any additional information I should know before hiking?','Please note that the map and directions are for general use. Always verify current road and weather conditions, stick to designated paths, and respect private property. Be prepared with adequate water, food, sunscreen, and other essentials, as cell service is limited. Remember to practice Leave No Trace principles and enjoy your wilderness experience responsibly.','2025-03-28 01:30:59','2025-03-28 01:30:59'),(13185,'trails',276,'What is the length of the Crosby Canyon trail?','The Crosby Canyon trail spans approximately 7 miles.','2025-03-28 01:31:11','2025-03-28 01:31:11'),(13186,'trails',276,'When is the best time to hike Crosby Canyon?','This trail is accessible and enjoyable throughout the year.','2025-03-28 01:31:11','2025-03-28 01:31:11'),(13187,'trails',276,'What is the difficulty level of the Crosby Canyon hike?','The hike is rated as moderate, making it suitable for hikers with some experience.','2025-03-28 01:31:11','2025-03-28 01:31:11'),(13188,'trails',276,'What is the elevation of Crosby Canyon?','Crosby Canyon reaches an elevation of 3,717 feet.','2025-03-28 01:31:11','2025-03-28 01:31:11'),(13189,'trails',276,'Are pets allowed on the Crosby Canyon trail?','Yes, pets are welcome to join you on the trail.','2025-03-28 01:31:11','2025-03-28 01:31:11'),(13190,'trails',276,'Do I need a reservation to hike in Crosby Canyon?','No reservations are needed; you can hike the trail freely.','2025-03-28 01:31:11','2025-03-28 01:31:11'),(13191,'trails',276,'How long will the hike take?','Expect to spend a full day exploring the trail.','2025-03-28 01:31:11','2025-03-28 01:31:11'),(13192,'trails',276,'What type of vehicle is recommended to access the trail?','An off-road vehicle is recommended for accessing the trail.','2025-03-28 01:31:11','2025-03-28 01:31:11'),(13193,'trails',276,'How do I get to Crosby Canyon?','To reach Crosby Canyon, drive east on HWY 89 from Kanab for 57 miles to Big Water. Turn left past mile post 7 onto Ethan Allen Road and head north. Follow road #300, the Smoky Mountain Road, for 9.3 miles, then look for the Crosby Canyon road #231 sign and turn right. Continue for about 3.95 miles until you reach the Warm Creek Canyon overlook.','2025-03-28 01:31:11','2025-03-28 01:31:11'),(13194,'trails',276,'Can you describe the experience on the Crosby Canyon trail?','Crosby Canyon offers an exhilarating off-road adventure filled with opportunities for jeeping, swimming, fishing, camping, and ATVs. The route winds through a picturesque gorge with narrow curves, hinting at its underwater past. As you approach the end of the canyon, breathtaking views of Lake Powell unfold, revealing various small beaches and peninsulas ideal for camping and fishing. Do note, the area is especially renowned for great fishing. However, avoid traveling when the roads are wet, as conditions can become impassable.','2025-03-28 01:31:11','2025-03-28 01:31:11'),(13195,'trails',276,'Is there any additional information I should know before hiking?','It\'s important to use these maps and directions for general reference only, as road and weather conditions can vary. Always stay on marked trails, respect private property, and be prepared for a wilderness experience by bringing ample water, food, sunscreen, and supplies. Keep in mind that cell phone service may be limited in many areas. Please refrain from disturbing rock art and practice leave-no-trace principles to preserve the experience for future visitors.','2025-03-28 01:31:11','2025-03-28 01:31:11'),(13196,'trails',278,'What is the distance of the Greenhalgh trail?','The Greenhalgh trail covers a total distance of 4 miles for a round trip.','2025-03-28 01:31:24','2025-03-28 01:31:24'),(13197,'trails',278,'What is the best season to hike the Greenhalgh trail?','You can enjoy hiking the Greenhalgh trail year-round, making it accessible in all seasons.','2025-03-28 01:31:24','2025-03-28 01:31:24'),(13198,'trails',278,'How difficult is the Greenhalgh trail?','The trail is categorized as moderate in difficulty, suitable for hikers with some experience.','2025-03-28 01:31:24','2025-03-28 01:31:24'),(13199,'trails',278,'What is the elevation gain on the Greenhalgh trail?','Hikers will reach an elevation of 5850 feet along the Greenhalgh trail.','2025-03-28 01:31:24','2025-03-28 01:31:24'),(13200,'trails',278,'What are the GPS coordinates for the Greenhalgh trail?','The Greenhalgh trail is located at approximately 37.1088° latitude and -112.5450° longitude.','2025-03-28 01:31:24','2025-03-28 01:31:24'),(13201,'trails',278,'Is the Greenhalgh trail accessible by regular vehicles?','Yes, the trail can be accessed by 2WD vehicles.','2025-03-28 01:31:24','2025-03-28 01:31:24'),(13202,'trails',278,'Are pets allowed on the Greenhalgh trail?','Unfortunately, pets are not permitted on this trail.','2025-03-28 01:31:24','2025-03-28 01:31:24'),(13203,'trails',278,'Do I need a reservation to hike the Greenhalgh trail?','No reservations are required to hike the Greenhalgh trail.','2025-03-28 01:31:24','2025-03-28 01:31:24'),(13204,'trails',278,'How long does it generally take to hike the Greenhalgh trail?','Most hikers take about 3 hours to complete the hike.','2025-03-28 01:31:24','2025-03-28 01:31:24'),(13205,'trails',278,'How can I get to the Greenhalgh trailhead?','To reach the trailhead, head north on HWY 89 from the town center. After passing mile post 66, take a left onto the dirt road. Stay left at the fork, and you’ll find the Greenhalgh trailhead on your right after 5 miles. Park at the ATV bridge, cross it, and head left along the dirt road to start your hike.','2025-03-28 01:31:24','2025-03-28 01:31:24'),(13206,'trails',278,'Can you tell me more about the Greenhalgh trail\'s history?','The trail is named after the Greenhalgh brothers, Harry and Willard, who were local ranchers during the 1900s. They used this path to manage cattle west of Trail Canyon. This trail also served as an original mail route between Kanab and Springdale, where mail was lowered down cliffs using a rope system. The views from the trail, particularly from the Vermilion Cliffs, are truly remarkable!','2025-03-28 01:31:24','2025-03-28 01:31:24'),(13207,'trails',278,'What additional information should I keep in mind while hiking the Greenhalgh trail?','Always refer to local road and weather conditions; dirt roads can become impractical when wet. Respect private properties and maintain the integrity of the area by following Leave No Trace principles. Be sure to bring extra water, food, sunscreen, and other supplies, as cell phone reception is unreliable in most areas.','2025-03-28 01:31:24','2025-03-28 01:31:24'),(13208,'trails',278,'Who can I contact for more information about the Greenhalgh trail?','For further inquiries, you can contact the local information center at 435.644.5033.','2025-03-28 01:31:24','2025-03-28 01:31:24'),(13209,'trails',279,'What is the name of the trail?','The trail is called Hell Dive Pictographs.','2025-03-28 01:31:39','2025-03-28 01:31:39'),(13210,'trails',279,'How long is the Hell Dive Pictographs trail?','The trail stretches for approximately 3.44 miles.','2025-03-28 01:31:39','2025-03-28 01:31:39'),(13211,'trails',279,'When is the best time to hike Hell Dive?','The ideal seasons for hiking this trail are Spring, Summer, and Fall.','2025-03-28 01:31:39','2025-03-28 01:31:39'),(13212,'trails',279,'What is the difficulty level of the Hell Dive trail?','The trail is classified as very difficult, presenting numerous challenges along the way.','2025-03-28 01:31:39','2025-03-28 01:31:39'),(13213,'trails',279,'What is the elevation of Hell Dive Pictographs?','The trail reaches an elevation of 5,525 feet.','2025-03-28 01:31:39','2025-03-28 01:31:39'),(13214,'trails',279,'What are the GPS coordinates for the trail?','The latitude is 37.044167 and the longitude is -112.640617.','2025-03-28 01:31:39','2025-03-28 01:31:39'),(13215,'trails',279,'What type of vehicle is required to access the trail?','A high clearance 4WD vehicle or ATV is necessary to access the trail.','2025-03-28 01:31:39','2025-03-28 01:31:39'),(13216,'trails',279,'Are pets allowed on the Hell Dive trail?','Yes, pets are permitted on the trail.','2025-03-28 01:31:39','2025-03-28 01:31:39'),(13217,'trails',279,'Do I need a reservation to hike Hell Dive?','No reservations are required to hike this trail.','2025-03-28 01:31:39','2025-03-28 01:31:39'),(13218,'trails',279,'How long does it typically take to hike Hell Dive?','On average, the hike takes around 4 hours to complete.','2025-03-28 01:31:40','2025-03-28 01:31:40'),(13219,'trails',279,'How do I get to Hell Dive Pictographs?','To reach the trailhead, drive 8 miles north of Kanab, past Milepost 71, then turn west onto Hancock Road. After that, make a left onto Road 50. A high clearance 4WD is needed from that point. At the next intersection, turn right onto Road 51. When the road forks, keep left until you reach the end; park there and hike along the wall to find the alcove and trail.','2025-03-28 01:31:40','2025-03-28 01:31:40'),(13220,'trails',279,'What can I expect on the Hell Dive hike?','The hike is quite demanding as it leads to ancient rock art pictographs in an alcove. The trail involves extreme rock crawling, and while portions are very tough, it rewards hikers with stunning views of Zion National Park in the distance. It\'s essential to respect the rock art and leave no trace behind.','2025-03-28 01:31:40','2025-03-28 01:31:40'),(13221,'trails',279,'Is there any additional information I should know before hiking Hell Dive?','This map and the directions are for general reference. Always check local weather and road conditions, as dirt roads can be impassable when wet. Stick to designated routes, be mindful of private property, and prepare for a wilderness experience with ample water, food, sunscreen, and necessary supplies. Note that cell phone signals are mostly nonexistent here. Avoid removing artifacts or damaging the rock art, and ensure to leave no trace for others to enjoy later. For further details, consider visiting the Kanab Visitor\'s Center.','2025-03-28 01:31:40','2025-03-28 01:31:40'),(13222,'trails',280,'What is the Kanab Heritage Walking Tour?','The Kanab Heritage Walking Tour offers a fascinating opportunity to delve into the historical significance of Kanab, Utah, showcasing various historical homes and buildings throughout the city.','2025-03-28 01:31:49','2025-03-28 01:31:49'),(13223,'trails',280,'How do I access the Kanab Heritage Walking Tour?','You can easily reach the Kanab Heritage Walking Tour by car via U.S. Highway 89, starting right in the city of Kanab.','2025-03-28 01:31:49','2025-03-28 01:31:49'),(13224,'trails',280,'What are some highlights of the tour?','The tour features notable sites such as the Heritage House, Johnson/Hicks Hotel and Restaurant, and the IDS Church and Family History Visitors Center, among other historic buildings.','2025-03-28 01:31:49','2025-03-28 01:31:49'),(13225,'trails',280,'Is there an entry fee for the Kanab Heritage Walking Tour?','No entry fee is required; the tour is accessible for everyone without the need for reservations.','2025-03-28 01:31:49','2025-03-28 01:31:49'),(13226,'trails',280,'Is the Kanab Heritage Walking Tour suitable for pets?','Unfortunately, pets are not allowed on the Kanab Heritage Walking Tour, so plan accordingly.','2025-03-28 01:31:49','2025-03-28 01:31:49'),(13227,'trails',280,'What is the difficulty level of the walking tour?','The tour is considered easy, making it accessible for walkers of all skill levels.','2025-03-28 01:31:49','2025-03-28 01:31:49'),(13228,'trails',280,'What should I know about the privacy of residents during the tour?','Please be respectful of the residents\' privacy, as some homes along the tour are private and not open to the public.','2025-03-28 01:31:49','2025-03-28 01:31:49'),(13229,'trails',280,'What is the best time of year to enjoy the Kanab Heritage Walking Tour?','The tour is enjoyable during the summer months when the weather is typically more pleasant for walking.','2025-03-28 01:31:49','2025-03-28 01:31:49'),(13230,'trails',280,'Where can I find more information about the tour?','For further details, you can visit the Kane County Visitors Center located at 78 S 100 E, Kanab, Utah, or call 435.644.5033.','2025-03-28 01:31:49','2025-03-28 01:31:49'),(13231,'trails',281,'What is the trail name?','The trail is known as the Horseshoe Bend Overlook Hike.','2025-03-28 01:32:00','2025-03-28 01:32:00'),(13232,'trails',281,'How long is the hike?','The total distance of the hike is 1.5 miles round trip.','2025-03-28 01:32:00','2025-03-28 01:32:00'),(13233,'trails',281,'When is the best time to hike this trail?','This trail is accessible year-round, making it a great option at any time.','2025-03-28 01:32:00','2025-03-28 01:32:00'),(13234,'trails',281,'What is the difficulty level of the hike?','The hike is rated as easy, suitable for hikers of all skill levels.','2025-03-28 01:32:00','2025-03-28 01:32:00'),(13235,'trails',281,'What is the elevation of the trail?','The hike reaches an elevation of 4,327 feet.','2025-03-28 01:32:01','2025-03-28 01:32:01'),(13236,'trails',281,'What are the GPS coordinates for this trail?','The coordinates are 36.8796 latitude and -111.5110 longitude.','2025-03-28 01:32:01','2025-03-28 01:32:01'),(13237,'trails',281,'Is the trail accessible by vehicle?','Yes, you can access the trail with a 2WD vehicle.','2025-03-28 01:32:01','2025-03-28 01:32:01'),(13238,'trails',281,'Are pets allowed on this trail?','Unfortunately, pets are not allowed on the Horseshoe Bend trail.','2025-03-28 01:32:01','2025-03-28 01:32:01'),(13239,'trails',281,'Do I need a reservation to hike this trail?','No reservation is required to enjoy this hike.','2025-03-28 01:32:01','2025-03-28 01:32:01'),(13240,'trails',281,'How long does it typically take to complete the hike?','On average, hikers spend about 3 hours on this trail.','2025-03-28 01:32:01','2025-03-28 01:32:01'),(13241,'trails',281,'How do I get to the Horseshoe Bend Overlook?','To reach the trailhead, drive east from Kanab on HWY 89 for 72.6 miles to Page, Arizona. From there, proceed 5 miles and look for the Horseshoe Bend sign just past milepost 544. Park in the designated area and pay the entrance fee to start your hike.','2025-03-28 01:32:01','2025-03-28 01:32:01'),(13242,'trails',281,'Can you describe the hike to Horseshoe Bend?','The hike leads you to one of the most photographed spots along the Colorado River, located just 5 miles south of Page, Arizona. You\'ll be captivated by the changing colors of the rocks, the moving shadows, and the sparkling hues of the river below as you embark on an easy 1.5-mile round trip to the stunning overlook.','2025-03-28 01:32:02','2025-03-28 01:32:02'),(13243,'trails',281,'What additional information should I know before hiking?','It\'s important to check local road and weather conditions before your hike. Always stay on designated paths, as dirt roads can become impassable when wet. Be respectful of private property and come prepared with extra water, food, sunscreen, and supplies since cell service is limited in the area. Remember to leave no trace to preserve the beauty for future visitors.','2025-03-28 01:32:02','2025-03-28 01:32:02'),(13244,'trails',281,'Where can I find the nearest visitor\'s center?','The nearest visitor\'s center is located at 785 100 E in Kanab, and you can contact them at 435.644.5033 for more information.','2025-03-28 01:32:02','2025-03-28 01:32:02'),(13245,'trails',282,'What is the total distance of the Huntress Slot Canyon hike?','The hike covers a total distance of 1.3 miles.','2025-03-28 01:32:15','2025-03-28 01:32:15'),(13246,'trails',282,'What is the best season to hike the Huntress Slot Canyon?','This trail can be enjoyed year-round, making it a great option in any season.','2025-03-28 01:32:15','2025-03-28 01:32:15'),(13247,'trails',282,'How difficult is the Huntress Slot Canyon hike?','The hike is classified as easy, making it suitable for hikers of all experience levels.','2025-03-28 01:32:15','2025-03-28 01:32:15'),(13248,'trails',282,'What is the elevation of the Huntress Slot Canyon?','The trail reaches an elevation of 8,173 feet.','2025-03-28 01:32:15','2025-03-28 01:32:15'),(13249,'trails',282,'What type of vehicle is recommended to access the trail?','A 4WD vehicle is required to reach the trailhead.','2025-03-28 01:32:16','2025-03-28 01:32:16'),(13250,'trails',282,'Are pets allowed on the Huntress Slot Canyon hike?','Yes, pets are welcome on this hiking trail.','2025-03-28 01:32:16','2025-03-28 01:32:16'),(13251,'trails',282,'Do I need a reservation to hike the Huntress Slot Canyon?','No reservations are necessary; you can enjoy the hike at your convenience.','2025-03-28 01:32:16','2025-03-28 01:32:16'),(13252,'trails',282,'How many hours should I expect to hike the Huntress Slot Canyon?','On average, the hike takes about 3 hours to complete.','2025-03-28 01:32:16','2025-03-28 01:32:16'),(13253,'trails',282,'What are the directions to get to the Huntress Slot Canyon trailhead?','From Kanab, take Hwy 89 north for 11.4 miles. After passing mile post 76, turn right onto Road 106 and drive for 1.1 miles. At the fork, keep left, and then at the next fork, stay right until you reach the turnout for Road 106T. Hike down the steep dirt hill to the northeast in the wash until you find stunning water pockets. You can also visit Diana\'s Throne for fantastic views.','2025-03-28 01:32:16','2025-03-28 01:32:16'),(13254,'trails',282,'Can you describe the Huntress Slot Canyon hike?','The hike through Huntress Slot Canyon offers a vibrant and picturesque environment with unique toadstool formations. It\'s a beautiful destination for families and pet owners, particularly during sunset. The canyon culminates in a box canyon featuring intriguing water pockets. Should you have the time, the hike to Diana’s Throne presents breathtaking views of Zion National Park. There are also numerous self-guided hikes and ATV trails in the surrounding areas.','2025-03-28 01:32:16','2025-03-28 01:32:16'),(13255,'trails',282,'What additional information should I know before hiking?','Please keep in mind that the directions provided are for general reference. It’s important to verify local road and weather conditions before your visit. Stay on marked paths, as dirt roads can become impassable when wet. Also, respect private property and prepare for a wilderness adventure by bringing extra water, snacks, sunscreen, and supplies, as cell service is limited in the area. Practice Leave No Trace principles and avoid removing artifacts or altering rock art.','2025-03-28 01:32:16','2025-03-28 01:32:16'),(13256,'trails',282,'Where can I contact for more information about the hike?','For additional information, you can contact the Kanab Visitor\'s Center at 435.644.5033, located at 78 5 100 E.','2025-03-28 01:32:16','2025-03-28 01:32:16'),(13257,'trails',283,'What is the length of the Sherry Belle Trail?','The Sherry Belle Trail spans approximately 2.82 miles.','2025-03-28 01:32:27','2025-03-28 01:32:27'),(13258,'trails',283,'When is the best time to hike the Sherry Belle Trail?','You can enjoy the Sherry Belle Trail all year round, making it a versatile hiking option.','2025-03-28 01:32:27','2025-03-28 01:32:27'),(13259,'trails',283,'How difficult is the Sherry Belle Trail?','This trail is categorized as easy, making it suitable for hikers of all skill levels.','2025-03-28 01:32:27','2025-03-28 01:32:27'),(13260,'trails',283,'What is the elevation of the Sherry Belle Trail?','The trail is set at an elevation of 5,771 feet.','2025-03-28 01:32:28','2025-03-28 01:32:28'),(13261,'trails',283,'Is the Sherry Belle Trail accessible for everyone?','Yes, the trail is accessible, ensuring that many can enjoy it.','2025-03-28 01:32:28','2025-03-28 01:32:28'),(13262,'trails',283,'Are pets allowed on the trail?','Absolutely! Pets are welcome on Sherry Belle Trail, but please keep them leashed.','2025-03-28 01:32:28','2025-03-28 01:32:28'),(13263,'trails',283,'Do I need a reservation to hike the trail?','No reservations are required to access the Sherry Belle Trail.','2025-03-28 01:32:28','2025-03-28 01:32:28'),(13264,'trails',283,'What is the recommended vehicle type to get to the trail?','A car is recommended for traveling to the Sherry Belle Trail.','2025-03-28 01:32:28','2025-03-28 01:32:28'),(13265,'trails',283,'How do I get to the Sherry Belle Trail?','To reach the trail, drive 2.8 miles south on HWY 89A from Kanab, then take a left onto Kaneplex Drive and make your first left, keeping right thereafter.','2025-03-28 01:32:28','2025-03-28 01:32:28'),(13266,'trails',283,'Can you provide a brief description of the Sherry Belle Trail?','The Sherry Belle Trail offers a delightful 3.2-mile loop around Jackson Flat Reservoir with lookout points, perfect for hiking and biking. It\'s a great spot for outdoor fun, including disc golf, fishing, and various water activities.','2025-03-28 01:32:28','2025-03-28 01:32:28'),(13267,'trails',283,'What wildlife might I see while on the Sherry Belle Trail?','The area is home to diverse wildlife, including ducks, geese, eagles, and various bird species, as well as frogs, lizards, and snakes.','2025-03-28 01:32:28','2025-03-28 01:32:28'),(13268,'trails',283,'What types of fish can be found in the reservoir?','The reservoir is populated with trout, bass, and sunfish, attracting fishing enthusiasts.','2025-03-28 01:32:28','2025-03-28 01:32:28'),(13269,'trails',283,'What should I bring for my hike on the Sherry Belle Trail?','Be sure to pack extra water, food, sunscreen, and necessary supplies, as cell phone service is limited and it\'s important to respect the environment.','2025-03-28 01:32:28','2025-03-28 01:32:28'),(13270,'trails',283,'Are there any fishing licenses required?','If you plan to fish, you can purchase a fishing license at Claziers Market.','2025-03-28 01:32:29','2025-03-28 01:32:29'),(13271,'trails',283,'What guidelines should I follow while visiting?','Remember to leave no trace, respect private property, and do not disturb any artifacts or rock art.','2025-03-28 01:32:29','2025-03-28 01:32:29'),(13272,'trails',284,'What is the length of the Johnson Canyon Driving Tour?','The Johnson Canyon Driving Tour spans approximately 2.6 miles.','2025-03-28 01:32:38','2025-03-28 01:32:38'),(13273,'trails',284,'What makes Johnson Canyon a special destination?','Johnson Canyon is renowned for its stunning scenery, which has attracted filmmakers and serves as a beautiful backdrop for several movies. It offers a refreshing drive that will uplift your spirits.','2025-03-28 01:32:38','2025-03-28 01:32:38'),(13274,'trails',284,'Are there any notable landmarks along the route?','Yes, during your drive along Johnson Canyon Road, you can view various points of interest, including private areas with Indian and cowboy glyphs, best appreciated with binoculars.','2025-03-28 01:32:38','2025-03-28 01:32:38'),(13275,'trails',284,'Is there an endpoint for the driving tour?','The tour concludes at the point where the pavement transitions to a dirt road. It\'s a great opportunity to turn around and take in the sights again.','2025-03-28 01:32:38','2025-03-28 01:32:38'),(13276,'trails',284,'What historical significance does this area hold?','The area of Dairy Canyon is historically significant with various Indian artifacts discovered, which can be viewed at the Kanab Heritage Museum. A calling ahead is recommended to check museum hours.','2025-03-28 01:32:39','2025-03-28 01:32:39'),(13277,'trails',284,'Can you tell me about the ATV and OHV trails nearby?','Yes, there are ATV/OHV trailheads accessible from this route that open the door to exciting off-road adventures in the area.','2025-03-28 01:32:39','2025-03-28 01:32:39'),(13278,'trails',284,'Is there an interesting legend associated with Johnson Canyon?','Absolutely! In 1914, a man named Freddie Crystal rode into the area with a treasure map claiming that Montezuma had hidden his riches in a cave within the canyon. While no gold was found, the legend continues to intrigue locals and visitors alike.','2025-03-28 01:32:39','2025-03-28 01:32:39'),(13279,'trails',284,'What larger natural area does Johnson Canyon belong to?','Johnson Canyon is located at the southern edge of the Grand Staircase-Escalante National Monument, the largest national monument in the U.S., encompassing nearly 2 million acres of diverse landscapes, including slot canyons and opportunities for solitude.','2025-03-28 01:32:39','2025-03-28 01:32:39'),(13280,'trails',285,'What is the distance of the Kanab Creek trail?','The Kanab Creek trail covers a distance of approximately 2.8 miles.','2025-03-28 01:32:51','2025-03-28 01:32:51'),(13281,'trails',285,'When is the best time to hike the Kanab Creek trail?','The ideal seasons for hiking Kanab Creek are Spring, Summer, and Fall.','2025-03-28 01:32:51','2025-03-28 01:32:51'),(13282,'trails',285,'How difficult is the Kanab Creek trail?','The trail is rated as easy, making it accessible for hikers of all skill levels.','2025-03-28 01:32:51','2025-03-28 01:32:51'),(13283,'trails',285,'What is the elevation of the Kanab Creek trail?','The trail sits at an elevation of 4,970 feet.','2025-03-28 01:32:51','2025-03-28 01:32:51'),(13284,'trails',285,'Can I bring my pet on the Kanab Creek trail?','Unfortunately, pets are not permitted on this trail.','2025-03-28 01:32:51','2025-03-28 01:32:51'),(13285,'trails',285,'Is a reservation required to hike the Kanab Creek trail?','No reservations are needed to hike the Kanab Creek trail.','2025-03-28 01:32:51','2025-03-28 01:32:51'),(13286,'trails',285,'How long does it typically take to complete the hike?','Hikers usually spend a few hours completing the Kanab Creek hike.','2025-03-28 01:32:51','2025-03-28 01:32:51'),(13287,'trails',285,'What type of vehicle is needed to access the trail?','A 2WD vehicle is sufficient for accessing the trailhead.','2025-03-28 01:32:51','2025-03-28 01:32:51'),(13288,'trails',285,'How do I get to the Kanab Creek trailhead?','To reach the trailhead, drive 5 miles north from Kanab on HWY 89 and make a right turn after milepost 69.','2025-03-28 01:32:51','2025-03-28 01:32:51'),(13289,'trails',285,'What can I expect to see while hiking the Kanab Creek trail?','The trail features Kanab Creek, a persistent water source, and a fascinating slot canyon near Best Friends. As you hike, you\'ll have the opportunity to see varied water levels ranging from ankle-deep to waist-high. There\'s also Hidden Lake, an underground lake within a cave formed by water seeping through red sandstone.','2025-03-28 01:32:51','2025-03-28 01:32:51'),(13290,'trails',285,'What unique historical use does Hidden Lake have?','Locals used the cave at Hidden Lake as a natural cooler by placing dairy products in a boat tied to a rope and then lowering it into the cave\'s depths to keep them cool.','2025-03-28 01:32:51','2025-03-28 01:32:51'),(13291,'trails',285,'What precautions should I take while hiking?','Always check local road and weather conditions before heading out. Stay on designated roads, particularly since dirt roads can be impassable when wet. Be prepared for a wilderness experience by bringing extra water, food, sunscreen, and other supplies; and remember that cell phone service is limited in most areas. Respect the environment by not removing artifacts or damaging rock art, and practice Leave No Trace principles.','2025-03-28 01:32:51','2025-03-28 01:32:51'),(13292,'trails',285,'Where can I find more information about the area?','For additional information, you can visit the Kanab Visitor\'s Center located at 78 5 100 E, or call them at 435.644.5033.','2025-03-28 01:32:51','2025-03-28 01:32:51'),(13293,'trails',288,'What is the name of the trail?','The trail is called Lick Wash Slot Canyon.','2025-03-28 01:33:03','2025-03-28 01:33:03'),(13294,'trails',288,'How long is the Lick Wash Slot Canyon trail?','The trail covers a distance of 16.2 miles.','2025-03-28 01:33:03','2025-03-28 01:33:03'),(13295,'trails',288,'When is the best time to hike this trail?','The ideal seasons to hike are Spring, Summer, and Fall.','2025-03-28 01:33:03','2025-03-28 01:33:03'),(13296,'trails',288,'What is the difficulty level of the trail?','The Lick Wash Slot Canyon trail is rated as moderate in difficulty.','2025-03-28 01:33:03','2025-03-28 01:33:03'),(13297,'trails',288,'What is the elevation of this trail?','The trail reaches an elevation of 8,000 feet.','2025-03-28 01:33:03','2025-03-28 01:33:03'),(13298,'trails',288,'What are the latitude and longitude coordinates of Lick Wash?','The trail is located at latitude 37.364617 and longitude -112.188517.','2025-03-28 01:33:04','2025-03-28 01:33:04'),(13299,'trails',288,'Is the trail accessible?','Yes, the trail is accessible.','2025-03-28 01:33:04','2025-03-28 01:33:04'),(13300,'trails',288,'Are pets allowed on this trail?','No, pets are not permitted on the trail.','2025-03-28 01:33:04','2025-03-28 01:33:04'),(13301,'trails',288,'Do I need a reservation to hike this trail?','No, you do not need a reservation to hike the Lick Wash Slot Canyon.','2025-03-28 01:33:04','2025-03-28 01:33:04'),(13302,'trails',288,'How long does it typically take to hike the trail?','On average, it takes about half a day to complete the hike.','2025-03-28 01:33:04','2025-03-28 01:33:04'),(13303,'trails',288,'What type of vehicle is recommended to reach the trailhead?','A vehicle with A5 capability is recommended.','2025-03-28 01:33:04','2025-03-28 01:33:04'),(13304,'trails',288,'How do I get to Lick Wash Slot Canyon?','From Kanab, head east on HWY 89 for 9.5 miles, then take a left onto Johnson Canyon Road. Continue for 16.2 miles until the pavement ends, and turn right onto Skutumpah Road #500.','2025-03-28 01:33:04','2025-03-28 01:33:04'),(13305,'trails',288,'Can you describe the trail?','Lick Wash is a delightful half-day hike through a scenic narrow canyon adorned with ponderosa pines, Douglas firs, and expansive Navajo sandstone. The shaded narrows offer a cool respite, while the broader areas have less cover. The canyon showcases stunning autumn foliage. It\'s an easy, four-mile one-way hike along a gravel wash. You can choose your distance — just turn back whenever you\'re ready. This path also provides access to Furk Wash and No Mans Mesa.','2025-03-28 01:33:04','2025-03-28 01:33:04'),(13306,'trails',288,'What additional information should I know before hiking?','This map and directions are for general reference. Always check local road and weather conditions beforehand. Stick to designated roads, as dirt paths can become impassable when wet. Respect private property and prepare for a true wilderness experience by bringing extra water, food, sunscreen, and necessary supplies. Note that cell service is often unavailable. Please do not disturb any artifacts or rock art and practice Leave No Trace principles.','2025-03-28 01:33:05','2025-03-28 01:33:05'),(13307,'trails',289,'What is the name of the trail?','The trail is called Mail Drop ATV/Hike.','2025-03-28 01:33:18','2025-03-28 01:33:18'),(13308,'trails',289,'How long is the Mail Drop trail?','The trail spans approximately 1 mile.','2025-03-28 01:33:18','2025-03-28 01:33:18'),(13309,'trails',289,'When is the best time to hike this trail?','You can enjoy this trail year-round, making it accessible in all seasons.','2025-03-28 01:33:18','2025-03-28 01:33:18'),(13310,'trails',289,'What is the difficulty level of the hike?','The trail is rated as moderate, so it\'s suitable for those with some hiking experience.','2025-03-28 01:33:18','2025-03-28 01:33:18'),(13311,'trails',289,'What is the elevation of the trail?','The hike takes you up to an elevation of 5600 feet.','2025-03-28 01:33:18','2025-03-28 01:33:18'),(13312,'trails',289,'What are the geographic coordinates of the trail?','The trail is located at latitude 37.0461° N and longitude 113.1584° W.','2025-03-28 01:33:18','2025-03-28 01:33:18'),(13313,'trails',289,'Is the trail accessible for individuals with mobility challenges?','Yes, the trail is accessible.','2025-03-28 01:33:18','2025-03-28 01:33:18'),(13314,'trails',289,'Are pets allowed on this trail?','Yes, you can bring your pets along while hiking.','2025-03-28 01:33:19','2025-03-28 01:33:19'),(13315,'trails',289,'Do I need a reservation to hike this trail?','No reservations are required to enjoy this hike.','2025-03-28 01:33:19','2025-03-28 01:33:19'),(13316,'trails',289,'How long does it typically take to complete the hike?','On average, the hike will take about half a day.','2025-03-28 01:33:19','2025-03-28 01:33:19'),(13317,'trails',289,'What type of vehicle is recommended to access the trail?','A 4WD vehicle is recommended for access to the trailhead.','2025-03-28 01:33:19','2025-03-28 01:33:19'),(13318,'trails',289,'How do I get to the trailhead?','To reach the trailhead from Kanab, take HWY 39 north for 7.8 miles, then turn left onto Hancock Road. Continue for 9.3 miles and turn left at the stop sign. After 9.1 miles, turn right onto road K1250 (3200 West). Drive for 2.2 miles to a road map sign to park and unload ATVs. The trail begins on your left, continuing 1 mile to the overlook.','2025-03-28 01:33:19','2025-03-28 01:33:19'),(13319,'trails',289,'Can you describe the trail?','This trail is a beloved route for ATVs and jeeps. Starting 4 miles southwest of the Coral Pink Sand Dunes State Park, it winds past Elephant Butte and through deep sand, sandstone formations, sagebrush, and juniper trees, offering stunning views of Zion National Park. The hike itself is about 2 miles round trip, primarily in a sandy wash.','2025-03-28 01:33:19','2025-03-28 01:33:19'),(13320,'trails',289,'Is there any historical significance to this trail?','This area has a rich history tied to mail delivery from Kanab to the settlers in Shunes Creek, which used to be perilous. A cable system was later established to lower mail down a 300-foot cliff, bypassing surrounding towns like Rockville and Springdale.','2025-03-28 01:33:20','2025-03-28 01:33:20'),(13321,'trails',289,'What should I know before hiking this trail?','This hike is situated within the Canaan Mountain Wilderness, so please adhere to Leave No Trace principles to protect the environment.','2025-03-28 01:33:20','2025-03-28 01:33:20'),(13322,'trails',289,'What is the contact number for more information about the trail?','For more information, you can reach the Kanab Visitor\'s Center at 435-644-5033.','2025-03-28 01:33:20','2025-03-28 01:33:20'),(13323,'trails',289,'Where is the Kanab Visitor\'s Center located?','The center is located at 78 5 100 E, Kanab.','2025-03-28 01:33:20','2025-03-28 01:33:20'),(13324,'trails',290,'What is the distance of the Mammoth Cave trail?','The total length of the Mammoth Cave trail is 5.4 miles.','2025-03-28 01:33:30','2025-03-28 01:33:30'),(13325,'trails',290,'When is the best time to hike at Mammoth Cave?','The ideal season for hiking Mammoth Cave is from May to September.','2025-03-28 01:33:30','2025-03-28 01:33:30'),(13326,'trails',290,'What is the difficulty level of the trail?','The trail offers an Easy to Moderate level of difficulty.','2025-03-28 01:33:30','2025-03-28 01:33:30'),(13327,'trails',290,'What is the elevation of Mammoth Cave?','The trail has an elevation of 8,060 feet.','2025-03-28 01:33:30','2025-03-28 01:33:30'),(13328,'trails',290,'What are the GPS coordinates for Mammoth Cave?','Mammoth Cave can be found at latitude 37.56941 and longitude -112.5876.','2025-03-28 01:33:30','2025-03-28 01:33:30'),(13329,'trails',290,'When is the trail accessible for hiking?','The trail is accessible for exploring from May to September.','2025-03-28 01:33:30','2025-03-28 01:33:30'),(13330,'trails',290,'Are pets allowed on the Mammoth Cave trail?','Yes, pets are permitted on the trail.','2025-03-28 01:33:30','2025-03-28 01:33:30'),(13331,'trails',290,'Are reservations needed to hike at Mammoth Cave?','No reservations are required to hike this trail.','2025-03-28 01:33:31','2025-03-28 01:33:31'),(13332,'trails',290,'How much time should I plan for hiking this trail?','You can expect to spend about half a day hiking at Mammoth Cave.','2025-03-28 01:33:31','2025-03-28 01:33:31'),(13333,'trails',290,'What types of vehicles can access the Mammoth Cave?','The trail is accessible by all types of vehicles.','2025-03-28 01:33:31','2025-03-28 01:33:31'),(13334,'trails',290,'What are the directions to reach the Mammoth Cave trailhead?','To get there from Kanab, drive 40 miles north on HWY 89, turn left onto HWY 14, travel 9.4 miles, then take a right onto FH50/Mammoth Road for 5.4 miles. After that, turn right onto road 1609 and continue straight on road 950 for 45 miles until you reach the trailhead.','2025-03-28 01:33:31','2025-03-28 01:33:31'),(13335,'trails',290,'Can you describe what to expect at Mammoth Cave?','Mammoth Cave is one of the largest lava tubes in Utah, featuring over 2,100 feet of passages and five entrances. Exploring the cave, which looks like a large hole in the ground, can be thrilling. It is very dark inside, so bringing a good flashlight is essential. The cave comprises four chambers, with the largest located to the west. At the end of the longest tunnel, there is a narrow passage that serves as an exit, approximately a quarter-mile in length. For comfort, wearing long pants and long-sleeve shirts is advisable, and a jacket may be necessary due to the cool temperatures inside.','2025-03-28 01:33:31','2025-03-28 01:33:31'),(13336,'trails',290,'What additional information should I know before hiking Mammoth Cave?','The directions and map provided are for general use only; always check local road and weather conditions before heading out. Respect private property and stay on designated paths. Be prepared for a wilderness experience by bringing extra water, food, sunscreen, and supplies, as cell service is often unavailable. Remember to leave no trace and avoid removing any artifacts or damaging rock art, allowing others to enjoy the area as well.','2025-03-28 01:33:31','2025-03-28 01:33:31'),(13337,'trails',292,'What is the distance of the Mansard trail?','The Mansard trail stretches for 6.5 miles as a round trip.','2025-03-28 01:33:42','2025-03-28 01:33:42'),(13338,'trails',292,'When is the best time to hike the Mansard trail?','You can enjoy hiking the Mansard trail year-round.','2025-03-28 01:33:42','2025-03-28 01:33:42'),(13339,'trails',292,'How difficult is the Mansard trail?','The trail is considered steep and strenuous, ideal for experienced hikers.','2025-03-28 01:33:42','2025-03-28 01:33:42'),(13340,'trails',292,'What is the elevation of the Mansard trail?','The trail reaches an elevation of 5940 feet.','2025-03-28 01:33:42','2025-03-28 01:33:42'),(13341,'trails',292,'Do I need a special vehicle to access the Mansard trail?','Any type of vehicle can access the trailhead.','2025-03-28 01:33:42','2025-03-28 01:33:42'),(13342,'trails',292,'Are pets allowed on the Mansard trail?','Unfortunately, pets are not permitted on this trail.','2025-03-28 01:33:42','2025-03-28 01:33:42'),(13343,'trails',292,'Is a reservation required to hike the Mansard trail?','No reservation is necessary to enjoy the Mansard trail.','2025-03-28 01:33:43','2025-03-28 01:33:43'),(13344,'trails',292,'How long does it typically take to hike the Mansard trail?','Expect to spend about half a day completing the hike.','2025-03-28 01:33:43','2025-03-28 01:33:43'),(13345,'trails',292,'Can you provide directions to the Mansard trailhead?','To reach the trailhead, drive 6.5 miles east of Kanab, just past milepost 59. Turn left onto Vista Drive Road, take a right on Grand Vermilion Avenue, then a left on Coyote Canyon. Continue left onto Rocky Ledge Lane, go through the gate onto road #1051, and stay right at the fork onto #1054. When the road ends, you can park, and the trail begins there.','2025-03-28 01:33:43','2025-03-28 01:33:43'),(13346,'trails',292,'What can I expect to see while hiking the Mansard trail?','Expect stunning rock formations and remarkable views of the Yaron Chifa, Kanab Plateau, and al Kanals, along with unique ancient petroglyphs in a secluded alcove.','2025-03-28 01:33:43','2025-03-28 01:33:43'),(13347,'trails',292,'What should I be aware of while hiking Mansard?','Be prepared for warm weather and make sure to bring plenty of water. It\'s important to stay on designated paths and avoid touching or walking on the petroglyphs to protect this historic area. Keep in mind that cell service is limited in many parts of the trail.','2025-03-28 01:33:43','2025-03-28 01:33:43'),(13348,'trails',292,'What else should I know before hiking the Mansard trail?','Prepare for a wilderness experience by packing extra water, snacks, sunscreen, and necessary supplies. Always check local conditions before your hike, as dirt roads can become impassable when wet.','2025-03-28 01:33:43','2025-03-28 01:33:43'),(13349,'trails',294,'What is the length of the Navajo Loop Trail?','The Navajo Loop Trail covers a distance of 11.2 miles.','2025-03-28 01:33:56','2025-03-28 01:33:56'),(13350,'trails',294,'What is the best time of year to hike the Navajo Loop Trail?','The ideal seasons for hiking the Navajo Loop Trail are Spring, Summer, and Fall.','2025-03-28 01:33:56','2025-03-28 01:33:56'),(13351,'trails',294,'How difficult is the Navajo Loop Trail?','The trail is considered to be of moderate difficulty.','2025-03-28 01:33:56','2025-03-28 01:33:56'),(13352,'trails',294,'What is the elevation of the Navajo Loop Trail?','The trail reaches an elevation of 9,035 feet.','2025-03-28 01:33:56','2025-03-28 01:33:56'),(13353,'trails',294,'What are the trail\'s coordinates?','The Navajo Loop Trail is located at latitude 37.519 and longitude 112.795.','2025-03-28 01:33:56','2025-03-28 01:33:56'),(13354,'trails',294,'Is the trail accessible by standard vehicles?','Yes, the trail is accessible with a 2WD vehicle.','2025-03-28 01:33:56','2025-03-28 01:33:56'),(13355,'trails',294,'Are pets allowed on the Navajo Loop Trail?','Unfortunately, pets are not permitted on this trail.','2025-03-28 01:33:56','2025-03-28 01:33:56'),(13356,'trails',294,'Do I need a reservation to hike the trail?','No reservations are required to access the Navajo Loop Trail.','2025-03-28 01:33:56','2025-03-28 01:33:56'),(13357,'trails',294,'How long does it typically take to hike the trail?','On average, it takes around 3 hours to complete the hike.','2025-03-28 01:33:57','2025-03-28 01:33:57'),(13358,'trails',294,'Where should I park for the trail?','You can park at the Navajo Lake Campground.','2025-03-28 01:33:57','2025-03-28 01:33:57'),(13359,'trails',294,'What are the directions to get to the Navajo Loop Trail?','From Kanab, head north on HWY 89 for 40 miles. Turn left onto HWY 14, continue for about 15 miles, then turn left onto Navajo Lake Road. After 2.9 miles, take a slight right onto FR 4222 and proceed for another 0.3 miles to arrive at the campground.','2025-03-28 01:33:57','2025-03-28 01:33:57'),(13360,'trails',294,'Can you describe the Navajo Loop Trail?','The Navajo Loop Trail is a scenic 11.2-mile loop suitable for hikers, equestrians, and bikers, located just east of Navajo Lake Campground. The circumference of Navajo Lake is 6 miles.','2025-03-28 01:33:57','2025-03-28 01:33:57'),(13361,'trails',294,'What facilities are available at the nearby Navajo Lake Campground?','The campground features 15 single sites, one double site, and 11 hike-in sites, along with amenities such as fire pits/grills and picnic tables.','2025-03-28 01:33:57','2025-03-28 01:33:57'),(13362,'trails',294,'What activities can I enjoy at Navajo Lake?','At Navajo Lake, you can engage in various activities including boating, kayaking, canoeing, camping, fishing, hiking, biking, and photography.','2025-03-28 01:33:57','2025-03-28 01:33:57'),(13363,'trails',294,'What other hikes are nearby?','Some nearby hikes include the Navajo Sky Loop, Virgin Rim Trail, and Cascade Falls.','2025-03-28 01:33:57','2025-03-28 01:33:57'),(13364,'trails',295,'What is the distance of the Paria River trail?','The trail stretches 22 miles in a one-way direction, making it a substantial trek for adventurous hikers.','2025-03-28 01:34:09','2025-03-28 01:34:09'),(13365,'trails',295,'When is the best time of year to hike the Paria River?','This trail can be explored year-round, offering unique experiences in every season.','2025-03-28 01:34:09','2025-03-28 01:34:09'),(13366,'trails',295,'What is the difficulty level of the Paria River hike?','The hike is considered difficult, suitable for those with experience and good physical fitness.','2025-03-28 01:34:09','2025-03-28 01:34:09'),(13367,'trails',295,'What is the elevation of the Paria River trail?','Hikers will find themselves at an elevation of 5,040 feet while navigating this adventurous path.','2025-03-28 01:34:09','2025-03-28 01:34:09'),(13368,'trails',295,'What are the geographical coordinates of the Paria River trail?','The trail is located at a latitude of 37.25218 and a longitude of -111.93495.','2025-03-28 01:34:09','2025-03-28 01:34:09'),(13369,'trails',295,'Is the Paria River trail easily accessible?','This trail is off the beaten path, offering a more secluded hiking experience.','2025-03-28 01:34:09','2025-03-28 01:34:09'),(13370,'trails',295,'Are pets allowed on the Paria River trail?','Yes, you are welcome to bring your pets with you on this trail.','2025-03-28 01:34:09','2025-03-28 01:34:09'),(13371,'trails',295,'Do I need a reservation to hike the Paria River?','No reservations are required to hike this trail, offering flexibility for spontaneous adventurers.','2025-03-28 01:34:10','2025-03-28 01:34:10'),(13372,'trails',295,'How long does it typically take to hike the Paria River?','Most hikers will spend a full day exploring this extensive trail, so plan accordingly.','2025-03-28 01:34:10','2025-03-28 01:34:10'),(13373,'trails',295,'What type of vehicle is recommended for accessing the Paria River trail?','A 4WD vehicle is recommended to navigate the dirt roads leading to the trailhead.','2025-03-28 01:34:10','2025-03-28 01:34:10'),(13374,'trails',295,'How do I get to the Paria River trailhead?','From Kanab, drive 33.5 miles south on Hwy 89, turn left at mile post 31 by the Old Paria Townsite marker, and follow the dirt road for about 5.6 miles to the canyon base. Continue past the cemetery to find parking.','2025-03-28 01:34:10','2025-03-28 01:34:10'),(13375,'trails',295,'Can you describe the Paria River hike?','The hike along the Paria River is a remarkable 22-mile journey accessible by trekking upstream in the river. Hikers can choose how far to go before turning back. The scenery is stunning, with opportunities to view rock art—though it\'s crucial not to touch it. Caution is advised for quicksand and flash floods, particularly during the monsoon.','2025-03-28 01:34:10','2025-03-28 01:34:10'),(13376,'trails',295,'What additional information should I know before hiking the Paria River?','It\'s important to note that map and instructions are for reference only. Always check local conditions and stay respectful of private property and wilderness regulations. Bring ample water, food, sunscreen, and necessary supplies, as cell service may be unreliable. Avoid disturbing any artifacts or rock art to preserve it for future visitors, and feel free to contact the BLM Visitor Center for more information.','2025-03-28 01:34:10','2025-03-28 01:34:10'),(13377,'trails',296,'What is the distance of the Paria Townsite trail?','The Paria Townsite trail spans an impressive 22 miles.','2025-03-28 01:34:20','2025-03-28 01:34:20'),(13378,'trails',296,'When is the best time to hike the Paria Townsite?','This trail can be enjoyed year-round, offering options no matter the season.','2025-03-28 01:34:20','2025-03-28 01:34:20'),(13379,'trails',296,'How challenging is the Paria Townsite hike?','The trail is considered easy, making it suitable for hikers of all skill levels.','2025-03-28 01:34:20','2025-03-28 01:34:20'),(13380,'trails',296,'What is the elevation range of the trail?','Hikers will experience elevations ranging from 6040 to 6800 feet.','2025-03-28 01:34:20','2025-03-28 01:34:20'),(13381,'trails',296,'Can I bring my pets on the Paria Townsite trail?','Pets are not allowed on this trail, so plan accordingly.','2025-03-28 01:34:20','2025-03-28 01:34:20'),(13382,'trails',296,'Do I need a reservation to hike the Paria Townsite?','No reservations are required for this trail, making it easy to access.','2025-03-28 01:34:20','2025-03-28 01:34:20'),(13383,'trails',296,'How long does it take to hike the trail?','You can complete this hike in half a day to a full day, depending on your pace and exploration.','2025-03-28 01:34:21','2025-03-28 01:34:21'),(13384,'trails',296,'What type of vehicle is suitable for accessing the trail?','A standard car can be used, but be cautious of rough dirt roads.','2025-03-28 01:34:21','2025-03-28 01:34:21'),(13385,'trails',296,'How do I get to the Paria Townsite trailhead?','To reach the trailhead, drive 33.5 miles east on HWY 89 from Kanab, turn left after mile 31 at the Old Town Paria Rock marker, and continue on the dirt road for about 5.6 miles into the canyon. Note that dirt roads may become impassable in wet conditions.','2025-03-28 01:34:21','2025-03-28 01:34:21'),(13386,'trails',296,'What is the historical significance of Paria Townsite?','Paria Townsite was once a thriving community, now mostly ruins due to floods and resource loss. Visitors can still see remnants like old foundations, wooden fences, and a historical cemetery with around 20 graves. The site was also the backdrop for several western films in the 1930s.','2025-03-28 01:34:21','2025-03-28 01:34:21'),(13387,'trails',296,'What should I know before hiking the Paria Townsite trail?','Always check the local road and weather conditions before heading out. Stay on designated roads, respect private property, and prepare for a wilderness experience. Bring extra water, food, sunscreen, and necessary supplies as cell phone service is often unavailable. Remember to leave no trace of your visit.','2025-03-28 01:34:21','2025-03-28 01:34:21'),(13388,'trails',297,'What is the distance of the Peekaboo Slot Canyon trail?','The trail stretches for approximately 9 miles, offering a rewarding hike through stunning landscapes.','2025-03-28 01:34:30','2025-03-28 01:34:30'),(13389,'trails',297,'When is the best time to hike the Peekaboo Slot Canyon?','You can enjoy the Peekaboo Slot Canyon year-round, making it a versatile choice for hikers any season.','2025-03-28 01:34:31','2025-03-28 01:34:31'),(13390,'trails',297,'How difficult is the hike through Peekaboo Slot Canyon?','The hike is considered moderate, so it\'s suitable for those with some hiking experience.','2025-03-28 01:34:31','2025-03-28 01:34:31'),(13391,'trails',297,'What is the elevation of Peekaboo Slot Canyon?','The trail has an elevation of 5,525 feet, providing breathtaking views from higher vantage points.','2025-03-28 01:34:31','2025-03-28 01:34:31'),(13392,'trails',297,'What are the coordinates for Peekaboo Slot Canyon?','The trail\'s coordinates are approximately 37.176° latitude and -112.564° longitude, guiding you to this remarkable spot.','2025-03-28 01:34:31','2025-03-28 01:34:31'),(13393,'trails',297,'What type of vehicle is needed to access the trail?','A high clearance vehicle is necessary to navigate the sandy road leading to the trailhead.','2025-03-28 01:34:31','2025-03-28 01:34:31'),(13394,'trails',297,'Are pets allowed on the Peekaboo Slot Canyon trail?','Unfortunately, pets are not permitted on this trail.','2025-03-28 01:34:31','2025-03-28 01:34:31'),(13395,'trails',297,'Is a reservation needed to hike Peekaboo Slot Canyon?','No reservations are required; you can hike the canyon on your own schedule.','2025-03-28 01:34:31','2025-03-28 01:34:31'),(13396,'trails',297,'How long does it typically take to hike the Peekaboo Slot Canyon?','Most hikers complete the trail in about half a day, allowing ample time to savor the scenery.','2025-03-28 01:34:31','2025-03-28 01:34:31'),(13397,'trails',297,'How do I get to the Peekaboo Slot Canyon trailhead?','To reach the trailhead, drive about 9 miles north of Kanab on HWY 89, where you\'ll find the turn-off on the east side at milepost 72 and 73. The sandy track into the canyon may require you to lower your tire pressure for better traction.','2025-03-28 01:34:31','2025-03-28 01:34:31'),(13398,'trails',297,'What should I know about the hiking experience at Peekaboo Slot Canyon?','Peekaboo Slot Canyon, also known as Red Canyon, is less crowded than famous alternatives like Antelope Canyon. The geological formations are shaped by centuries of rushing water through sandstone, and you\'ll find fascinating water level markings on the walls. Be sure to hike to the end to fully appreciate the canyon\'s beauty.','2025-03-28 01:34:31','2025-03-28 01:34:31'),(13399,'trails',297,'What additional information should hikers consider when visiting Peekaboo Slot Canyon?','Always check local road and weather conditions before heading out. It\'s vital to stay on designated paths, especially since dirt roads can be challenging when wet. Carry plenty of water, food, and supplies since cell phone service is limited. Respect the area by not removing artifacts or damaging rock art, and practice leave no trace principles to protect this beautiful location.','2025-03-28 01:34:31','2025-03-28 01:34:31'),(13400,'trails',299,'What is the distance of the Raven/Roadrunner trail?','The trail spans approximately 1.21 miles.','2025-03-28 01:34:42','2025-03-28 01:34:42'),(13401,'trails',299,'When is the best season to hike the Raven/Roadrunner trail?','You can enjoy this trail throughout the year.','2025-03-28 01:34:42','2025-03-28 01:34:42'),(13402,'trails',299,'How difficult is the Raven/Roadrunner trail?','The trail is considered easy, making it suitable for a variety of hikers.','2025-03-28 01:34:42','2025-03-28 01:34:42'),(13403,'trails',299,'What is the elevation range of the trail?','The elevation varies between 5040 to 5800 feet.','2025-03-28 01:34:42','2025-03-28 01:34:42'),(13404,'trails',299,'Is the Raven/Roadrunner trail accessible?','Yes, access to the trail is DIY (Do It Yourself).','2025-03-28 01:34:43','2025-03-28 01:34:43'),(13405,'trails',299,'Are pets allowed on the Raven/Roadrunner trail?','Yes, pets are welcome but must be kept on a leash.','2025-03-28 01:34:43','2025-03-28 01:34:43'),(13406,'trails',299,'Do I need to make a reservation to hike this trail?','No reservations are required to hike the Raven/Roadrunner trail.','2025-03-28 01:34:43','2025-03-28 01:34:43'),(13407,'trails',299,'How long does it typically take to hike the trail?','Expect to spend a few hours enjoying the hike.','2025-03-28 01:34:43','2025-03-28 01:34:43'),(13408,'trails',299,'What type of vehicle access is available for the Raven/Roadrunner trail?','You can access the trail by bike or on foot.','2025-03-28 01:34:43','2025-03-28 01:34:43'),(13409,'trails',299,'How do I get to the Raven/Roadrunner trail?','To reach the trailhead, start from downtown, head north on 100 East, stay right at the bend by Farry Lodge, look for the Squaw Trailhead behind the ball fields, and follow it until you see the Roadrunner trail sign. There is extra parking available off to the west behind the ball fields.','2025-03-28 01:34:43','2025-03-28 01:34:43'),(13410,'trails',299,'What can I expect from the Raven/Roadrunner trail experience?','The Raven/Roadrunner trail offers a short but exhilarating ride or hike through stunning red rock landscapes. It\'s ideal for families and is best tackled in a clockwise direction. It\'s the initial section of a larger mountain biking trail system and is suitable for both bikers and hikers alike.','2025-03-28 01:34:43','2025-03-28 01:34:43'),(13411,'trails',299,'Are there any important safety notes for the trail?','Yes! It\'s crucial to stay on designated paths, have extra water, food, sunscreen, and supplies. Cell service might be limited, and avoid removing any artifacts or disturbing rock art. Always aim to leave no trace during your visit.','2025-03-28 01:34:43','2025-03-28 01:34:43'),(13412,'trails',299,'Where is the nearest visitor center?','The visitor center is located at 78 5 100 E, and you can call them at 435.644.5033 for more information.','2025-03-28 01:34:43','2025-03-28 01:34:43'),(13413,'trails',300,'What is the distance of the Sand Dune Arch trail?','The trail spans a distance of 8 miles.','2025-03-28 01:34:54','2025-03-28 01:34:54'),(13414,'trails',300,'When is the best time to hike the Sand Dune Arch trail?','This trail can be enjoyed year-round, making it a versatile option for hikers.','2025-03-28 01:34:54','2025-03-28 01:34:54'),(13415,'trails',300,'How difficult is the Sand Dune Arch hike?','The hike is rated as easy, making it suitable for hikers of all skill levels.','2025-03-28 01:34:54','2025-03-28 01:34:54'),(13416,'trails',300,'What is the elevation of Sand Dune Arch?','The trail is situated at an elevation of 6000 feet.','2025-03-28 01:34:54','2025-03-28 01:34:54'),(13417,'trails',300,'What are the GPS coordinates for Sand Dune Arch?','The coordinates are latitude 37.146567 and longitude -112.585867.','2025-03-28 01:34:54','2025-03-28 01:34:54'),(13418,'trails',300,'Is 4WD necessary to access Sand Dune Arch?','Yes, a 4WD vehicle is required for access to the trail.','2025-03-28 01:34:54','2025-03-28 01:34:54'),(13419,'trails',300,'Are pets allowed on the Sand Dune Arch trail?','Yes, pets are welcome on the trail.','2025-03-28 01:34:54','2025-03-28 01:34:54'),(13420,'trails',300,'Do I need a reservation to hike Sand Dune Arch?','No reservation is required; you can hike the trail freely.','2025-03-28 01:34:54','2025-03-28 01:34:54'),(13421,'trails',300,'How long does it typically take to hike the Sand Dune Arch?','On average, hikers spend about 2 hours on the trail.','2025-03-28 01:34:54','2025-03-28 01:34:54'),(13422,'trails',300,'Which direction should I drive to get to Sand Dune Arch?','You should head north to reach the trailhead.','2025-03-28 01:34:54','2025-03-28 01:34:54'),(13423,'trails',300,'What are the directions to get to Sand Dune Arch?','From Kanab, travel 8 miles north on HWY 89. Turn left onto Hancock Road just past milepost 71, continue for about 8 miles, then turn right onto Road #648. 4WD is necessary from this point. Drive towards a prominent hoodoo and park there to start your hike.','2025-03-28 01:34:54','2025-03-28 01:34:54'),(13424,'trails',300,'Can you describe Sand Dune Arch?','The arch is a remarkable natural formation located off Hancock Road, surrounded by stunning rock formations, as well as pinion and juniper trees. It’s a great spot if you’re visiting Coral Pink Sand Dunes State Park or just have a little time to explore.','2025-03-28 01:34:54','2025-03-28 01:34:54'),(13425,'trails',300,'What additional attractions can I expect near Sand Dune Arch?','While hiking, you\'ll be treated to breathtaking views of the White Cliffs, part of the Grand Staircase-Escalante National Monument.','2025-03-28 01:34:54','2025-03-28 01:34:54'),(13426,'trails',300,'What should I prepare for when visiting Sand Dune Arch?','It\'s essential to be ready for a wilderness experience. Bring extra water, food, sunscreen, and other supplies, as cell service can be limited. Ensure you check road and weather conditions, stick to designated roads, and respect private property.','2025-03-28 01:34:55','2025-03-28 01:34:55'),(13427,'trails',300,'What are some important hiking ethics to follow?','Please do not remove artifacts or vandalize rock art. Always leave no trace to preserve the beauty of the area for future visitors.','2025-03-28 01:34:55','2025-03-28 01:34:55'),(13428,'trails',301,'What is the name of the trail?','The trail is known as the Smoky Mountains.','2025-03-28 01:35:10','2025-03-28 01:35:10'),(13429,'trails',301,'How long is the Smoky Mountains trail?','The Smoky Mountains trail spans an impressive distance of 327 miles.','2025-03-28 01:35:10','2025-03-28 01:35:10'),(13430,'trails',301,'What is the best season to hike on this trail?','You can explore this trail throughout the year, as it is suitable in all seasons.','2025-03-28 01:35:10','2025-03-28 01:35:10'),(13431,'trails',301,'What is the difficulty level of the Smoky Mountains trail?','This trail presents a challenging hike and is classified as difficult.','2025-03-28 01:35:10','2025-03-28 01:35:10'),(13432,'trails',301,'What is the elevation range for the Smoky Mountains trail?','You\'ll experience elevations between 4,500 to 6,500 feet along the trail.','2025-03-28 01:35:10','2025-03-28 01:35:10'),(13433,'trails',301,'What are the geographic coordinates of the trail?','The trail is located at approximately 37.227 latitude and -111.429 longitude.','2025-03-28 01:35:10','2025-03-28 01:35:10'),(13434,'trails',301,'What type of vehicle is recommended for accessing the trail?','For access, a high clearance 4WD vehicle is strongly recommended.','2025-03-28 01:35:11','2025-03-28 01:35:11'),(13435,'trails',301,'Are pets allowed on the Smoky Mountains trail?','Yes, you are welcome to bring pets along on the trail.','2025-03-28 01:35:11','2025-03-28 01:35:11'),(13436,'trails',301,'Is a reservation needed to hike this trail?','No reservations are required to hike the Smoky Mountains trail.','2025-03-28 01:35:11','2025-03-28 01:35:11'),(13437,'trails',301,'How long does it typically take to complete the hike?','Most hikers should plan for a full day to complete their hike on this trail.','2025-03-28 01:35:11','2025-03-28 01:35:11'),(13438,'trails',301,'How do I reach the Smoky Mountains trail?','To get to the trailhead, drive 57 miles east from Kanab on HWY 89. After passing mile post 7, make a left onto road #300 (Smoky Mountain Road). Continue for 9.3 miles, then take a left at Crosby Canyon. Proceed for 3.7 miles until road #332, and then drive 9.9 miles before turning right. The smoke holes are less than a mile away.','2025-03-28 01:35:11','2025-03-28 01:35:11'),(13439,'trails',301,'Can you describe the trail?','The Smoky Mountain Road is a backcountry byway that winds through the Grand Staircase-Escalante National Monument. Its name comes from an actual mountain that has been smoking for millions of years due to an underground fire. The area features vibrant rolling mud hills and stunning views of Lake Powell, set against a stark and colorful landscape with limited vegetation.','2025-03-28 01:35:11','2025-03-28 01:35:11'),(13440,'trails',301,'What additional information should hikers know?','The trail includes sections like the steep Kelly Grade, which can be adventurous due to its narrow switchbacks. A high-clearance 4WD is necessary for many areas. This region is quite remote, with limited cell phone service, so ensure your vehicle is well-maintained and carry ample food, water, gas, and a shovel.','2025-03-28 01:35:11','2025-03-28 01:35:11'),(13441,'trails',305,'What is the distance of the Squaw Trail?','The Squaw Trail covers a total distance of 3 miles for a round trip.','2025-03-28 01:35:20','2025-03-28 01:35:20'),(13442,'trails',305,'What is the best season to hike Squaw Trail?','You can enjoy the Squaw Trail in any season throughout the year.','2025-03-28 01:35:20','2025-03-28 01:35:20'),(13443,'trails',305,'How difficult is the Squaw Trail?','The trail is classified as moderate, making it suitable for hikers with a bit of experience.','2025-03-28 01:35:21','2025-03-28 01:35:21'),(13444,'trails',305,'What are the elevation ranges on this trail?','The Squaw Trail ascends from an elevation of 5040 feet to 5802 feet.','2025-03-28 01:35:21','2025-03-28 01:35:21'),(13445,'trails',305,'Are pets allowed on the Squaw Trail?','The pet policy on the Squaw Trail is currently unspecified.','2025-03-28 01:35:21','2025-03-28 01:35:21'),(13446,'trails',305,'Is a reservation required to hike the Squaw Trail?','No reservations are needed to access the Squaw Trail.','2025-03-28 01:35:21','2025-03-28 01:35:21'),(13447,'trails',305,'How long does it typically take to hike Squaw Trail?','Most hikers complete the trail in about 2 to 3 hours.','2025-03-28 01:35:21','2025-03-28 01:35:21'),(13448,'trails',305,'What type of vehicles can access the trailhead?','You can reach the trailhead using any type of vehicle.','2025-03-28 01:35:21','2025-03-28 01:35:21'),(13449,'trails',305,'How do I get to the Squaw Trail trailhead?','To reach the trailhead, turn right onto Main Street at the coplight of Cemer and Ivain, then right on 300 North. After one block, turn left on 100 E, pass Jacob Hamblin Park, and continue straight until you find the trailhead marked by the Squaw Trail sign. For additional navigation, consult the Kane County Visitor Center or download the Kanab Trails App.','2025-03-28 01:35:21','2025-03-28 01:35:21'),(13450,'trails',305,'Can you describe the Squaw Trail?','The Squaw Trail is a well-loved hiking route in Kanab, easily accessible from town. It\'s ideal if you\'re looking to do just one hike in the area. The trail features a moderately steep ascent of 780 feet, leading to breathtaking views of Kanab, Arizona, and the surrounding landscapes. You\'ll encounter fantastic rock formations along the way, and at the summit, you can connect to an extensive network of other trails.','2025-03-28 01:35:21','2025-03-28 01:35:21'),(13451,'trails',305,'What should I keep in mind before hiking the Squaw Trail?','Please be aware that the provided map and directions are for general reference only. Always check the local road and weather conditions prior to your visit. Stay on designated trails, as dirt paths may become impassable in wet conditions. Respect private property and prepare for an outdoor experience by bringing water, food, sunscreen, and necessary supplies. Note that cell phone service can be unreliable in many areas, and it\'s important to leave no trace and not remove any natural artifacts.','2025-03-28 01:35:21','2025-03-28 01:35:21'),(13452,'trails',306,'What is the name of the trail?','The trail is known as Lottery Location.','2025-03-28 01:35:32','2025-03-28 01:35:32'),(13453,'trails',306,'What distance is involved in this trail?','The distance specifics for this trail are currently not provided.','2025-03-28 01:35:32','2025-03-28 01:35:32'),(13454,'trails',306,'When is the best season to hike this trail?','Information regarding the optimal season for hiking this trail has not been specified.','2025-03-28 01:35:32','2025-03-28 01:35:32'),(13455,'trails',306,'What is the difficulty level of this trail?','The difficulty level for this trail hasn\'t been indicated.','2025-03-28 01:35:32','2025-03-28 01:35:32'),(13456,'trails',306,'What is the elevation of this trail?','Details regarding the elevation of this trail are currently unavailable.','2025-03-28 01:35:32','2025-03-28 01:35:32'),(13457,'trails',306,'What are the coordinates for the trail?','The latitude and longitude for the trail have not been provided.','2025-03-28 01:35:32','2025-03-28 01:35:32'),(13458,'trails',306,'Is this trail accessible for everyone?','Accessibility information has not been shared.','2025-03-28 01:35:32','2025-03-28 01:35:32'),(13459,'trails',306,'Are pets allowed on the trail?','Details about pet allowance are not included.','2025-03-28 01:35:33','2025-03-28 01:35:33'),(13460,'trails',306,'Is a reservation required to hike this trail?','Yes, hikers need to secure a permit due to the sensitive environment of this area, specifically for North and South Coyote Buttes.','2025-03-28 01:35:33','2025-03-28 01:35:33'),(13461,'trails',306,'How long does it typically take to hike this trail?','The average time required to hike the trail isn\'t specified.','2025-03-28 01:35:33','2025-03-28 01:35:33'),(13462,'trails',306,'What kind of vehicle is needed to access the trail?','Vehicle requirements for accessing the trail have not been detailed.','2025-03-28 01:35:33','2025-03-28 01:35:33'),(13463,'trails',306,'How do I get to the trail?','The trail is accessed from Kanab, where permits can be obtained; specific instructions for reaching the trailhead have not been given.','2025-03-28 01:35:33','2025-03-28 01:35:33'),(13464,'trails',306,'Can you provide a description of the trail?','Lottery Location is part of the breathtaking North and South Coyote Buttes area, noted for its stunning landscapes and unique geological formations.','2025-03-28 01:35:33','2025-03-28 01:35:33'),(13465,'trails',306,'What additional information should I know about this trail?','This area is known for requiring a lottery system for permits due to its fragile ecosystem. The only legal lottery in Utah operates with limited daily permits for the waves - 10 for South Coyote Buttes and 16 for North Coyote Buttes. Applicants should apply at Rec.gov and follow the established permit process, which includes safety briefings.','2025-03-28 01:35:33','2025-03-28 01:35:33'),(13466,'trails',307,'What is the distance of the Toadstools Hike?','The Toadstools Hike is a 2-mile round trip adventure.','2025-03-28 01:35:43','2025-03-28 01:35:43'),(13467,'trails',307,'When is the best time to hike the Toadstools?','You can hike the Toadstools year-round!','2025-03-28 01:35:43','2025-03-28 01:35:43'),(13468,'trails',307,'What is the difficulty level of the Toadstools Hike?','This trail is easy and suitable for families.','2025-03-28 01:35:43','2025-03-28 01:35:43'),(13469,'trails',307,'What is the elevation gain on the Toadstools Hike?','The hike involves an elevation change of 600 feet.','2025-03-28 01:35:43','2025-03-28 01:35:43'),(13470,'trails',307,'What are the GPS coordinates for the Toadstools Hike?','The trail is located at a latitude of 37.6494 and a longitude of -112.8709.','2025-03-28 01:35:44','2025-03-28 01:35:44'),(13471,'trails',307,'Is the Toadstools Hike shaded?','The trail is fully exposed to the sun.','2025-03-28 01:35:44','2025-03-28 01:35:44'),(13472,'trails',307,'Are pets allowed on the Toadstools Hike?','Unfortunately, pets are not permitted on this trail.','2025-03-28 01:35:44','2025-03-28 01:35:44'),(13473,'trails',307,'Do I need a reservation for the Toadstools Hike?','No reservations are required to hike this trail.','2025-03-28 01:35:44','2025-03-28 01:35:44'),(13474,'trails',307,'How long does it typically take to hike the Toadstools?','Most hikers complete this trail in about half a day.','2025-03-28 01:35:44','2025-03-28 01:35:44'),(13475,'trails',307,'What type of vehicle is recommended to reach the Toadstools?','You can easily access the trail by car.','2025-03-28 01:35:44','2025-03-28 01:35:44'),(13476,'trails',307,'How do I get to the Toadstools Hike?','From Kanab, travel 45 miles east along HWY 89. The parking area and trailhead are located just past milepost 20 on your left. The trail starts behind the information sign, where you should follow the wash and the well-marked trail to the hoodoos.','2025-03-28 01:35:44','2025-03-28 01:35:44'),(13477,'trails',307,'What can I expect to see on the Toadstools Hike?','Prepare to be amazed by the striking natural features, including balancing rocks and hoodoos in various colors and shapes. The hike culminates in the unique toadstool formations that resemble mushrooms.','2025-03-28 01:35:44','2025-03-28 01:35:44'),(13478,'trails',307,'What should I know before hiking the Toadstools?','Be mindful of the hot desert environment, especially in summer; bring plenty of water and sunscreen. It\'s also wise to check road and weather conditions ahead of your visit. Respect private property and avoid removing any artifacts or defacing rock art. Always follow Leave No Trace principles to preserve the beauty for future visitors.','2025-03-28 01:35:45','2025-03-28 01:35:45'),(13479,'trails',308,'What is the length of the Scenic Kanab trail?','The Scenic Kanab trail spans over 60 miles, making it a great option for those looking for an adventurous outing.','2025-03-28 01:35:57','2025-03-28 01:35:57'),(13480,'trails',308,'When is the best time to hike the Scenic Kanab trail?','The ideal months to experience the Scenic Kanab trail are from May to September, when weather conditions are most favorable.','2025-03-28 01:35:57','2025-03-28 01:35:57'),(13481,'trails',308,'How difficult is the Scenic Kanab trail?','The trail is classified as easy, making it accessible for hikers of all skill levels.','2025-03-28 01:35:57','2025-03-28 01:35:57'),(13482,'trails',308,'What is the elevation of the Scenic Kanab trail?','The trail reaches an elevation of 7,835 feet, offering stunning views of the surrounding landscape.','2025-03-28 01:35:57','2025-03-28 01:35:57'),(13483,'trails',308,'Are there any accessibility features on the Scenic Kanab trail?','Unfortunately, the trail does not have accessibility features, so be prepared for a rustic experience.','2025-03-28 01:35:57','2025-03-28 01:35:57'),(13484,'trails',308,'Can you bring pets on the Scenic Kanab trail?','Pet policies are not specified; check local guidelines before bringing your furry friends along.','2025-03-28 01:35:57','2025-03-28 01:35:57'),(13485,'trails',308,'Is a reservation required to hike the Scenic Kanab trail?','There is no reservation necessary for accessing the trail.','2025-03-28 01:35:58','2025-03-28 01:35:58'),(13486,'trails',308,'How many hours should I allocate to hike the Scenic Kanab trail?','The average time to complete the hike is not specified, so plan accordingly based on your pace and experience.','2025-03-28 01:35:58','2025-03-28 01:35:58'),(13487,'trails',308,'What type of vehicle is suitable for getting to the Scenic Kanab trail?','An ATV is the recommended vehicle for accessing the area around the trail.','2025-03-28 01:35:58','2025-03-28 01:35:58'),(13488,'trails',308,'How do I get to the Scenic Kanab trail?','To reach the trailhead, drive 60 miles north from Kanab on Scenic Highway 89, then turn right onto Scenic Byway 12. After about 13.5 miles, beyond mile post 10, make a right onto road #87. Travel 7 miles to Tropic Reservoir and Kings Creek Campground, then head half a mile around the reservoir to the parking area for the trailhead. If you have some extra time, consider taking the 3-mile ATV trail to Ruby\'s Inn for a meal.','2025-03-28 01:35:58','2025-03-28 01:35:58'),(13489,'trails',308,'What can I expect to see along the Scenic Kanab trail?','The trail features the charming Tropic Reservoir in Dixie National Forest, popular for activities such as fishing, boating, ATV riding, mountain biking, and hiking. The Panguitch Trail offers panoramic views of the stunning Pink Cliffs within the Grand Staircase National Forest. You\'ll also find great fishing opportunities at Kings Creek Campground and access to scenic routes leading to Bryce Canyon\'s iconic hoodoos.','2025-03-28 01:35:58','2025-03-28 01:35:58'),(13490,'trails',308,'What should I know before hiking the Scenic Kanab trail?','Before your hike, always check local road and weather conditions. Stay on designated paths, as dirt roads can be challenging after rainfall. Be prepared for a wilderness journey and bring extra supplies like water, food, and sunscreen, since cell service may be unreliable. Please respect the natural environment and leave no trace behind. For inquiries, you can reach the local ranger at 435.644.5033.','2025-03-28 01:35:58','2025-03-28 01:35:58'),(13491,'trails',309,'How long is the Wahweap Hoodoos trail?','The Wahweap Hoodoos trail spans a total distance of 9 miles for a round trip.','2025-03-28 01:36:10','2025-03-28 01:36:10'),(13492,'trails',309,'What is the best time of year to hike the Wahweap Hoodoos?','The ideal seasons for hiking the Wahweap Hoodoos are spring and fall, when temperatures are more pleasant.','2025-03-28 01:36:10','2025-03-28 01:36:10'),(13493,'trails',309,'What is the difficulty level of the trail?','The difficulty of the Wahweap Hoodoos trail can vary based on weather conditions, ranging from easy to hard.','2025-03-28 01:36:10','2025-03-28 01:36:10'),(13494,'trails',309,'What is the elevation of the Wahweap Hoodoos?','The hike reaches an elevation of 4042 feet.','2025-03-28 01:36:10','2025-03-28 01:36:10'),(13495,'trails',309,'Where is the Wahweap Hoodoos located?','The trail is located near Big Water, Utah, with coordinates of latitude 37.162485 and longitude -111.711799.','2025-03-28 01:36:10','2025-03-28 01:36:10'),(13496,'trails',309,'Is the Wahweap Hoodoos trail accessible?','Yes, the trail is accessible.','2025-03-28 01:36:11','2025-03-28 01:36:11'),(13497,'trails',309,'Can I bring my pet on the Wahweap Hoodoos trail?','Unfortunately, pets are not allowed on this trail.','2025-03-28 01:36:11','2025-03-28 01:36:11'),(13498,'trails',309,'Do I need a reservation to hike at Wahweap Hoodoos?','No reservations are required for hiking the Wahweap Hoodoos.','2025-03-28 01:36:11','2025-03-28 01:36:11'),(13499,'trails',309,'How long does it typically take to hike the Wahweap Hoodoos?','Most hikers complete the trail in about a day.','2025-03-28 01:36:11','2025-03-28 01:36:11'),(13500,'trails',309,'What type of vehicles can access the trailhead?','Vehicles with 2-wheel drive can park on the right side of the road before the creek, while high clearance 4-wheel drive vehicles may continue past the corral and park at the designated 4WD area near the trailhead.','2025-03-28 01:36:11','2025-03-28 01:36:11'),(13501,'trails',309,'How do I get to the Wahweap Hoodoos trailhead?','To reach the trailhead from Kanab, take HWY 89 east for about 55 miles to Big Water. Turn left onto Ethan Allen Road, which is located between mile markers 6 and 7, directly across from the Grand Staircase-Escalante Visitor Center. Follow this road until you hit a T-junction, then turn left and continue for 3 miles past the corral. 2WD vehicles should park along the right side of the road before the creek. The hiking begins by ascending Wahweap Creek.','2025-03-28 01:36:11','2025-03-28 01:36:11'),(13502,'trails',309,'What can I expect to see on the Wahweap Hoodoos trail?','The Wahweap Hoodoos trail offers stunning views of exclusive geological features such as hoodoos and balancing rocks, as well as the scenic beauty of Wahweap Creek.','2025-03-28 01:36:12','2025-03-28 01:36:12'),(13503,'trails',309,'What should I bring when hiking the Wahweap Hoodoos?','It\'s advisable to carry extra water, food, sunscreen, and other essentials to ensure a comfortable wilderness experience.','2025-03-28 01:36:12','2025-03-28 01:36:12'),(13504,'trails',309,'Are there any important tips for hiking the Wahweap Hoodoos?','Before embarking on your hike, it\'s essential to check local road and weather conditions. Stay on established paths and avoid dirt roads when wet. Be respectful of private property and refrain from removing artifacts or damaging rock art. Remember to leave no trace by taking all trash with you, and note that cell phone service can be limited in this region.','2025-03-28 01:36:12','2025-03-28 01:36:12'),(13505,'trails',310,'What is the distance of the Warriors Walk trail?','The Warriors Walk trail spans approximately 19 miles.','2025-03-28 01:36:24','2025-03-28 01:36:24'),(13506,'trails',310,'When is the best time to hike Warriors Walk?','This trail can be enjoyed year-round, making it a versatile option for hikers in any season.','2025-03-28 01:36:24','2025-03-28 01:36:24'),(13507,'trails',310,'How difficult is the Warriors Walk trail?','The trail is categorized as moderate in difficulty, making it suitable for many hikers who are reasonably fit.','2025-03-28 01:36:24','2025-03-28 01:36:24'),(13508,'trails',310,'What is the elevation gain of Warriors Walk?','Hikers will encounter an elevation of about 5,771 feet along this trail.','2025-03-28 01:36:24','2025-03-28 01:36:24'),(13509,'trails',310,'Where is Warriors Walk located?','Warriors Walk is situated at latitude 37.3289 and longitude -112.7177.','2025-03-28 01:36:24','2025-03-28 01:36:24'),(13510,'trails',310,'Is the Warriors Walk trail accessible?','Yes, the trail is accessible, providing opportunities for a variety of outdoor enthusiasts.','2025-03-28 01:36:24','2025-03-28 01:36:24'),(13511,'trails',310,'Are pets allowed on the Warriors Walk?','Yes, you can bring your pets along on this trail.','2025-03-28 01:36:24','2025-03-28 01:36:24'),(13512,'trails',310,'Do I need a reservation to hike Warriors Walk?','No reservations are required to enjoy this trail.','2025-03-28 01:36:24','2025-03-28 01:36:24'),(13513,'trails',310,'How long does it typically take to hike Warriors Walk?','The average time to complete the hike is about 5 hours.','2025-03-28 01:36:24','2025-03-28 01:36:24'),(13514,'trails',310,'What type of vehicle is suitable for getting to Warriors Walk?','An ATV or jeep is recommended to reach the starting point of the trail.','2025-03-28 01:36:24','2025-03-28 01:36:24'),(13515,'trails',310,'How do I get to Warriors Walk?','To reach the trail, start from Kanab and drive north on HWY 89 for 7.8 miles. After passing mile marker 71, turn left onto Hancock Road. Continue for 9.3 miles to a stop sign and turn left, then drive 9.1 miles before turning right on road K1250, also noted as 13200 West. Proceed 2.2 miles to a sign with a road map; you can park here and unload ATVs. The trailhead is to your left. For those driving further, after turning left on road 17 and following right on road 19, turn left on road 19A where the road ends for more parking near stunning views of Zion.','2025-03-28 01:36:25','2025-03-28 01:36:25'),(13516,'trails',310,'Can you describe the scenery along Warriors Walk?','Warriors Walk offers stunning views, featuring sandy trails surrounded by sagebrush and juniper trees, interspersed with sandstone sections. The backdrop includes breathtaking views of Zion National Park.','2025-03-28 01:36:25','2025-03-28 01:36:25'),(13517,'trails',310,'What historical significance does the trail have?','The origins of the pathway are a mystery, with speculation that it may have been utilized by Native Americans, as indicated by the rock-lined trail across the sandstone.','2025-03-28 01:36:25','2025-03-28 01:36:25'),(13518,'trails',310,'What should I bring for my hike?','Be sure to bring plenty of water, snacks, sunscreen, and other necessary supplies for a wilderness experience, as cell service is mostly unavailable in the area.','2025-03-28 01:36:25','2025-03-28 01:36:25'),(13519,'trails',310,'Are there any additional points of interest near Warriors Walk?','If time permits, visitors can explore nearby areas such as the Mail Drop or other local trails for additional adventure.','2025-03-28 01:36:25','2025-03-28 01:36:25'),(13520,'trails',310,'What are the important guidelines to follow while hiking?','Always check local road and weather conditions. Stay on designated paths, respect private property, and ensure you leave no trace behind. It\'s vital to avoid removing artifacts or damaging rock art.','2025-03-28 01:36:25','2025-03-28 01:36:25'),(13521,'trails',310,'How can I get more information about Warriors Walk?','For further inquiries, you can contact the local office at 435.644.5033.','2025-03-28 01:36:25','2025-03-28 01:36:25'),(13522,'trails',311,'What is the name of the trail?','The trail is known as White Pocket.','2025-03-28 01:36:37','2025-03-28 01:36:37'),(13523,'trails',311,'How long is the trail?','The distance of the trail is not specified.','2025-03-28 01:36:37','2025-03-28 01:36:37'),(13524,'trails',311,'What is the best season to hike White Pocket?','White Pocket can be enjoyed year-round.','2025-03-28 01:36:37','2025-03-28 01:36:37'),(13525,'trails',311,'What is the difficulty level of this hike?','The hike is classified as easy but involves navigating deep sand.','2025-03-28 01:36:37','2025-03-28 01:36:37'),(13526,'trails',311,'What is the elevation of White Pocket?','The elevation here is 5,673 feet.','2025-03-28 01:36:37','2025-03-28 01:36:37'),(13527,'trails',311,'What are the latitude and longitude coordinates for White Pocket?','The coordinates are 36.93734 latitude and -111.957692 longitude.','2025-03-28 01:36:37','2025-03-28 01:36:37'),(13528,'trails',311,'How accessible is the trail?','Access to the trail requires a high clearance 4WD vehicle.','2025-03-28 01:36:37','2025-03-28 01:36:37'),(13529,'trails',311,'Are pets allowed on the trail?','Yes, pets are permitted on the trail.','2025-03-28 01:36:37','2025-03-28 01:36:37'),(13530,'trails',311,'Is a reservation required to hike White Pocket?','No, you do not need a reservation to hike this trail.','2025-03-28 01:36:37','2025-03-28 01:36:37'),(13531,'trails',311,'How many hours does it typically take to hike the trail?','Expect the hike to take a full day.','2025-03-28 01:36:37','2025-03-28 01:36:37'),(13532,'trails',311,'What type of vehicle is needed to reach the trailhead?','A 4WD or an ATV is needed to navigate the terrain.','2025-03-28 01:36:37','2025-03-28 01:36:37'),(13533,'trails',311,'How do I get to White Pocket?','From Kanab, drive 38.6 miles east on HWY 89. Look for House Rock Valley Road between mileposts 26 and 25. After that, follow the detailed road instructions which require high clearance, 4WD for about 20 miles to reach the trailhead.','2025-03-28 01:36:38','2025-03-28 01:36:38'),(13534,'trails',311,'What can I expect to see at White Pocket?','White Pocket features unique, swirling, multi-colored formations resembling a moonscape, offering striking natural artwork and scenery.','2025-03-28 01:36:38','2025-03-28 01:36:38'),(13535,'trails',311,'Is there any additional information I should know?','Be mindful that much of White Pocket is privately ranched; please respect their property and animals. Also, plan for outdoor conditions by bringing sufficient water, food, sunscreen, and supplies. Cell service is limited in the area, and it\'s important to leave no trace.','2025-03-28 01:36:38','2025-03-28 01:36:38'),(13536,'trails',311,'Where can I find more information or assistance?','For more assistance, you can contact the Kanab Visitor\'s Center at 785 100 E, or by phone at 435.544.5033.','2025-03-28 01:36:38','2025-03-28 01:36:38'),(13537,'trails',312,'What is the length of the White Wave trail?','The White Wave trail stretches for 2.6 miles.','2025-03-28 01:36:49','2025-03-28 01:36:49'),(13538,'trails',312,'When is the best time to hike the White Wave trail?','You can hike the White Wave trail throughout the year.','2025-03-28 01:36:50','2025-03-28 01:36:50'),(13539,'trails',312,'How challenging is the White Wave trail?','The trail is considered difficult, making it suitable for experienced hikers.','2025-03-28 01:36:50','2025-03-28 01:36:50'),(13540,'trails',312,'What is the elevation at the highest point of the trail?','The trail reaches an elevation of 6,018 feet.','2025-03-28 01:36:50','2025-03-28 01:36:50'),(13541,'trails',312,'What are the coordinates for the White Wave trail?','The trail is located at latitude 37.193183 and longitude -112.579600.','2025-03-28 01:36:50','2025-03-28 01:36:50'),(13542,'trails',312,'What type of vehicle is needed to access the trail?','A high clearance 4WD vehicle is required to access the trailhead.','2025-03-28 01:36:50','2025-03-28 01:36:50'),(13543,'trails',312,'Are pets allowed on the White Wave trail?','Yes, you can bring pets with you on the trail.','2025-03-28 01:36:50','2025-03-28 01:36:50'),(13544,'trails',312,'Do I need a reservation to hike the White Wave trail?','No reservations are necessary to hike this trail.','2025-03-28 01:36:50','2025-03-28 01:36:50'),(13545,'trails',312,'How long does it typically take to hike the White Wave trail?','On average, the hike takes about 4 hours to complete.','2025-03-28 01:36:50','2025-03-28 01:36:50'),(13546,'trails',312,'How do I get to the White Wave trail?','To reach the trail, from Kanab, drive 8.8 miles north on HWY 89. After passing milepost 8, turn right into the Peekaboo parking area. The trailhead is located northeast of the parking area along road 102. Follow this road until you enter the wash, then switch to road 107H for 6 miles. After that, turn left onto road 102H for 2.6 miles until the road ends. Park here and walk up the wash to continue your hike to the White Wave.','2025-03-28 01:36:50','2025-03-28 01:36:50'),(13547,'trails',312,'What can I expect to see on the White Wave trail?','The trail offers an exciting ride through deep sand and a diverse desert landscape, showcasing cacti, sagebrush, junipers, yuccas, and pinion pines. You can also explore the nearby Peekaboo Slot Canyon and admire the fascinating rock formations of the White Wave.','2025-03-28 01:36:50','2025-03-28 01:36:50'),(13548,'trails',312,'Is there anything else to consider before hiking the trail?','Be sure to explore the area for petroglyphs but tread carefully. Check local road and weather conditions beforehand, as dirt roads can become impassable when wet. Always respect private property and prepare for a wilderness experience by bringing extra water, food, sunscreen, and supplies. Note that cell phone service is largely unavailable in this area. Please do not remove artifacts or damage rock art, and remember to practice Leave No Trace principles to preserve the trail for future visitors. For further information, you can reach the Kanab Visitor\'s Center at 435.644.5033.','2025-03-28 01:36:51','2025-03-28 01:36:51'),(13549,'trails',316,'What is the elevation change on the Peekaboo Loop?','The Peekaboo Loop features a descent of 670 feet (204 meters) from Bryce Point down to the loop trail before ascending back up to the starting point.','2025-03-28 01:37:02','2025-03-28 01:37:02'),(13550,'trails',316,'What is the total distance of the Peekaboo Loop hike?','The total distance for the Peekaboo Loop hike is approximately 5.5 miles (8.9 km).','2025-03-28 01:37:02','2025-03-28 01:37:02'),(13551,'trails',316,'How long does it typically take to complete the Peekaboo Loop?','Most hikers can expect to finish the Peekaboo Loop in about 3 to 4 hours, depending on pace and stops along the way.','2025-03-28 01:37:02','2025-03-28 01:37:02'),(13552,'trails',316,'How much elevation gain will hikers experience on this trail?','This trail has a total elevation gain of around 1560 feet (474 meters), making it a challenging hike.','2025-03-28 01:37:02','2025-03-28 01:37:02'),(13553,'trails',316,'What is the difficulty level of the Peekaboo Loop?','The Peekaboo Loop is categorized as strenuous due to its significant elevation gain and longer distance.','2025-03-28 01:37:02','2025-03-28 01:37:02'),(13554,'trails',316,'Are there restroom facilities available on the trail?','Yes, there are pit toilets located on the west side of the Peekaboo Loop, but they are only available during the summer months.','2025-03-28 01:37:02','2025-03-28 01:37:02'),(13555,'trails',316,'Is there a recommended direction for hiking the Peekaboo Loop?','It is recommended to hike the Peekaboo Loop in a clockwise direction for the best experience.','2025-03-28 01:37:02','2025-03-28 01:37:02'),(13556,'trails',316,'Can I bring my pet on the Peekaboo Loop trail?','No, pets are not allowed on this trail; however, service animals are permitted within national parks.','2025-03-28 01:37:03','2025-03-28 01:37:03'),(13557,'trails',316,'What should hikers know about encountering horses or mules on the trail?','Hikers may come across horses and mules along the trail and should yield the right-of-way to these riders.','2025-03-28 01:37:03','2025-03-28 01:37:03'),(13558,'trails',316,'Is the Peekaboo Loop accessible for individuals with mobility challenges?','Due to the trail\'s natural terrain, it is not considered accessible for those with mobility challenges.','2025-03-28 01:37:03','2025-03-28 01:37:03'),(13559,'trails',316,'What is the surface type of the trail?','The trail consists of firm native sediment, providing a stable walking surface.','2025-03-28 01:37:03','2025-03-28 01:37:03'),(13560,'trails',316,'What are the typical and maximum grades of the Peekaboo Loop?','The typical grade is about 6.0%, while the maximum grade reaches up to 27.0%.','2025-03-28 01:37:03','2025-03-28 01:37:03'),(13561,'trails',316,'What are the width specifications of the trail?','The trail typically measures 76 inches (193 cm) in width, with a minimum width of 48 inches (122 cm).','2025-03-28 01:37:03','2025-03-28 01:37:03'),(13562,'trails',316,'Where is the trailhead for the Peekaboo Loop located?','The trailhead for the Peekaboo Loop is located at Bryce Point, where parking is available.','2025-03-28 01:37:03','2025-03-28 01:37:03'),(13563,'trails',316,'Is there a shuttle service available for the Peekaboo Loop?','Yes, shuttle service is available, but during mid-winter, snow can make the trail inaccessible, with depths ranging from 2 to 15 feet (0.7 to 5 m).','2025-03-28 01:37:03','2025-03-28 01:37:03'),(13564,'trails',316,'What are the GPS coordinates for the Peekaboo Loop trailhead?','The GPS coordinates for the trailhead are latitude 37.6043 and longitude -112.157.','2025-03-28 01:37:04','2025-03-28 01:37:04'),(13565,'trails',317,'Where does the Navajo Loop Trail start and end?','The Navajo Loop Trail begins and concludes at Sunset Point.','2025-03-28 01:37:16','2025-03-28 01:37:16'),(13566,'trails',317,'What can I expect to see along the Navajo Loop Trail?','As you traverse the Navajo Loop, you\'ll experience stunning switchbacks amid colorful limestone walls, accompanied by impressive views of tall Douglas-fir trees and the renowned Thor\'s hammer hoodoo.','2025-03-28 01:37:16','2025-03-28 01:37:16'),(13567,'trails',317,'What are the two sections of the Navajo Loop Trail?','The trail features two distinct sections: Two Bridges and Wall Street. The Two Bridges section is accessible year-round, while Wall Street is closed in winter.','2025-03-28 01:37:16','2025-03-28 01:37:16'),(13568,'trails',317,'Is the Two Bridges section of the trail open year-round?','Yes, the Two Bridges side is open all year long, allowing for out-and-back hiking or combination with other trails during winter.','2025-03-28 01:37:16','2025-03-28 01:37:16'),(13569,'trails',317,'What is the total distance of the Navajo Loop Trail?','The complete loop measures approximately 1.3 miles (2.1 kilometers) round trip.','2025-03-28 01:37:16','2025-03-28 01:37:16'),(13570,'trails',317,'How long does it typically take to hike the Navajo Loop Trail?','Hikers usually take about 1 to 2 hours to complete the trail.','2025-03-28 01:37:16','2025-03-28 01:37:16'),(13571,'trails',317,'What is the elevation gain on the Navajo Loop Trail?','The trail includes an elevation gain of 515 feet (157 meters).','2025-03-28 01:37:16','2025-03-28 01:37:16'),(13572,'trails',317,'How difficult is the Navajo Loop Trail?','This trail is rated as moderate, with less than 1000 feet of elevation gain and a moderate distance.','2025-03-28 01:37:16','2025-03-28 01:37:16'),(13573,'trails',317,'What facilities are available at Sunset Point?','At Sunset Point, you\'ll find accessible restrooms year-round, as well as seasonal water-fill stations.','2025-03-28 01:37:17','2025-03-28 01:37:17'),(13574,'trails',317,'Is there shuttle service available for the Navajo Loop Trail?','Yes, there is shuttle service in the summer, and the recommended hiking direction is counter-clockwise during that time. In winter, you can hike Two Bridges as an out-and-back.','2025-03-28 01:37:17','2025-03-28 01:37:17'),(13575,'trails',317,'Are pets allowed on the Navajo Loop Trail?','Pets are not permitted on this trail, but service animals are allowed in national parks.','2025-03-28 01:37:17','2025-03-28 01:37:17'),(13576,'trails',317,'Can the Navajo Loop be combined with other trails?','Many hikers combine the Navajo Loop with Queen\'s Garden for a total round trip of 2.9 miles, utilizing the descent of Queen\'s Garden at Sunrise Point and ascending back via the Navajo Loop.','2025-03-28 01:37:17','2025-03-28 01:37:17'),(13577,'trails',317,'Is the Navajo Loop Trail accessible?','Due to its natural terrain, the Navajo Loop Trail is not considered accessible.','2025-03-28 01:37:17','2025-03-28 01:37:17'),(13578,'trails',317,'What is the surface type of the Navajo Loop Trail?','The trail has a firm native sediment surface.','2025-03-28 01:37:17','2025-03-28 01:37:17'),(13579,'trails',317,'What are the dimensions and grades of the trail?','The trail typically has a grade of 14%, with a maximum grade of 30%, and varies in width from 25 inches to 77 inches.','2025-03-28 01:37:17','2025-03-28 01:37:17'),(13580,'trails',317,'Can I bring my dog on this trail?','While dogs are not allowed on the Navajo Loop Trail, one/service animal is permitted.','2025-03-28 01:37:17','2025-03-28 01:37:17'),(13581,'trails',317,'What are the geographic coordinates of the Navajo Loop Trail?','The trail is located at a latitude of 37.6227 and a longitude of -112.166.','2025-03-28 01:37:18','2025-03-28 01:37:18'),(13582,'trails',318,'What is the hiking distance from Sunset Point to Sunrise Point on the Rim Trail?','The hike from Sunset Point to Sunrise Point covers a distance of 1 mile (1.6 km), making it a half-mile one-way trip.','2025-03-28 01:37:30','2025-03-28 01:37:30'),(13583,'trails',318,'Is the Rim Trail from Sunset Point to Sunrise Point paved?','Yes, this section of the Rim Trail is the only paved part, offering an easy walking experience.','2025-03-28 01:37:30','2025-03-28 01:37:30'),(13584,'trails',318,'What kind of views can I expect on the Rim Trail?','Hikers will be treated to stunning views of the Bryce Canyon Amphitheater and the unique hoodoo formations below.','2025-03-28 01:37:30','2025-03-28 01:37:30'),(13585,'trails',318,'Can I access the Rim Trail from both Sunset Point and Sunrise Point?','Absolutely! The trail can be accessed from either Sunset Point or Sunrise Point.','2025-03-28 01:37:30','2025-03-28 01:37:30'),(13586,'trails',318,'Is there a shuttle service available for the trail?','Yes, for those who prefer to hike one way, you can take a shuttle back to your starting point.','2025-03-28 01:37:31','2025-03-28 01:37:31'),(13587,'trails',318,'How long will it take to hike the Rim Trail between Sunset Point and Sunrise Point?','The hike typically takes about 1 hour to complete.','2025-03-28 01:37:31','2025-03-28 01:37:31'),(13588,'trails',318,'What is the elevation gain on this portion of the Rim Trail?','This trail features a modest elevation gain of 40 feet (12 meters), contributing to its easy rating.','2025-03-28 01:37:31','2025-03-28 01:37:31'),(13589,'trails',318,'What is the difficulty level of this hike?','The hike is classified as easy due to its short distance and minimal elevation gain.','2025-03-28 01:37:31','2025-03-28 01:37:31'),(13590,'trails',318,'Are there restroom facilities available along the trail?','Yes, accessible restrooms can be found at Sunset Point year-round and at the General Store near Sunrise Point seasonally.','2025-03-28 01:37:31','2025-03-28 01:37:31'),(13591,'trails',318,'Where can I fill up on water during the hike?','Water refill stations are available at Sunset Point (seasonally) and the restroom at Sunset Point (year-round), as well as the General Store (seasonally).','2025-03-28 01:37:31','2025-03-28 01:37:31'),(13592,'trails',318,'Are pets allowed on the Rim Trail?','Yes, pets are permitted on paved surfaces along the Rim Trail.','2025-03-28 01:37:31','2025-03-28 01:37:31'),(13593,'trails',318,'How accessible is this section of the Rim Trail?','This segment is fully paved, providing accessibility for all hikers.','2025-03-28 01:37:31','2025-03-28 01:37:31'),(13594,'trails',318,'What are the typical and maximum slopes along the trail?','The typical grade is around 3.3%, while the maximum grade can reach 16.5% at certain points.','2025-03-28 01:37:32','2025-03-28 01:37:32'),(13595,'trails',318,'What are the width regulations on this trail?','The typical width of the path is 97 inches (246.2 cm), with a minimum width of 72 inches (182.9 cm) ensuring ample space for hikers.','2025-03-28 01:37:32','2025-03-28 01:37:32'),(13596,'trails',318,'Are service animals allowed on this trail?','Yes, service animals are permitted in national parks, including this section of the Rim Trail.','2025-03-28 01:37:32','2025-03-28 01:37:32'),(13597,'trails',318,'What are the geographic coordinates of the Rim Trail?','The latitude and longitude coordinates for the area are 37.6226 and -112.166, respectively.','2025-03-28 01:37:32','2025-03-28 01:37:32'),(13598,'trails',319,'What is the Bryce Amphitheater and why is it notable?','The Bryce Amphitheater is the park\'s most famous area, recognized for having the world\'s highest density of unique rock formations called \'hoodoos.\' This stunning bowl-shaped landscape has been formed by seasonal rainfall and snowmelt.','2025-03-28 01:37:36','2025-03-28 01:37:36'),(13599,'trails',319,'Which viewpoints should I prioritize in the Bryce Amphitheater?','If your time is limited, make sure to visit Bryce Point, Inspiration Point, Sunset Point, and Sunrise Point. These viewpoints offer breathtaking panoramic views and serve as starting points for hiking trails around the rim of the Paunsaugunt plateau.','2025-03-28 01:37:37','2025-03-28 01:37:37'),(13600,'trails',319,'Are the viewpoints in the Bryce Amphitheater accessible?','Yes, all viewpoints are paved and provide easy access, making it convenient for visitors. For more detailed accessibility information, check our Accessibility page.','2025-03-28 01:37:37','2025-03-28 01:37:37'),(13601,'trails',319,'Does the park provide any guided services for the Bryce Amphitheater?','Absolutely! You can utilize the Park App’s \'Tours\' section for a guided tour that highlights this must-see area in the park.','2025-03-28 01:37:37','2025-03-28 01:37:37'),(13602,'trails',319,'Can I bring my dog to the Bryce Amphitheater?','Yes, dogs are allowed in the Bryce Amphitheater, but be sure to check the specific regulations and guidelines regarding pet access.','2025-03-28 01:37:37','2025-03-28 01:37:37'),(13603,'trails',320,'Where is the Mossy Cave Trail located?','The Mossy Cave Trail can be found off Highway 12 in the northern section of the park, making it easily accessible for visitors traveling through.','2025-03-28 01:37:45','2025-03-28 01:37:45'),(13604,'trails',320,'Do I need a park pass to hike the Mossy Cave Trail?','Yes, Mossy Cave is a fee area like the rest of the park. Ensure you have your park pass or a proof of admission in your vehicle for any ranger inspections.','2025-03-28 01:37:45','2025-03-28 01:37:45'),(13605,'trails',320,'Is there parking available at the Mossy Cave Trail?','Parking is available at the trailhead, but be aware that the lot may fill up quickly. If it\'s full, it\'s best to return later. Note that parking along SR 12 is prohibited and unsafe.','2025-03-28 01:37:46','2025-03-28 01:37:46'),(13606,'trails',320,'What are the best times to visit the Mossy Cave Trail to avoid crowds?','To steer clear of heavy foot traffic, it’s advisable to visit in the early morning or later in the evening, especially during peak hours from 10 AM to 6 PM.','2025-03-28 01:37:46','2025-03-28 01:37:46'),(13607,'trails',320,'What is the distance and time estimate for hiking the Mossy Cave Trail?','The Mossy Cave Trail is a short hike of 0.8 miles (1.3 km) round trip and is usually completed in about an hour.','2025-03-28 01:37:46','2025-03-28 01:37:46'),(13608,'trails',320,'What is the elevation gain for the Mossy Cave Trail?','The trail features a modest elevation gain of 150 feet (46 meters), making it a relatively easy hike.','2025-03-28 01:37:46','2025-03-28 01:37:46'),(13609,'trails',320,'Are there any facilities available at the trailhead?','Yes, there are accessible restrooms available at the trailhead for your convenience.','2025-03-28 01:37:46','2025-03-28 01:37:46'),(13610,'trails',320,'Can I bring my dog on the Mossy Cave Trail?','Unfortunately, pets are not allowed on this trail. However, service animals are permitted in national parks.','2025-03-28 01:37:46','2025-03-28 01:37:46'),(13611,'trails',320,'What kind of terrain can I expect on the Mossy Cave Trail?','The trail has firm native sediment as its surface type. Keep in mind that due to the natural terrain, it is not considered an accessible trail.','2025-03-28 01:37:46','2025-03-28 01:37:46'),(13612,'trails',320,'What precautions should I take regarding the trail\'s environment?','This area contains delicate rocks and sensitive plants. Please stay on the designated main trail and follow all posted signs to protect the ecosystem.','2025-03-28 01:37:46','2025-03-28 01:37:46'),(13613,'trails',320,'What are the latitude and longitude coordinates for Mossy Cave Trail?','The coordinates for the Mossy Cave Trail are approximately 37.6658 latitude and -112.11 longitude.','2025-03-28 01:37:46','2025-03-28 01:37:46'),(13614,'trails',321,'What is the Rim Trail?','The Rim Trail is a scenic pathway in Bryce Canyon National Park that offers stunning views of the Bryce Amphitheater. It connects several viewpoints and can be accessed from multiple locations.','2025-03-28 01:37:58','2025-03-28 01:37:58'),(13615,'trails',321,'How long is the Rim Trail?','The Rim Trail extends approximately 5.5 miles (8.9 km) from Bryce Point in the south to Fairyland Point in the north, with various sections ranging in distance.','2025-03-28 01:37:58','2025-03-28 01:37:58'),(13616,'trails',321,'What is the difficulty level of the Rim Trail?','The Rim Trail is generally classified as easy to moderate, depending on the section you choose to hike.','2025-03-28 01:37:58','2025-03-28 01:37:58'),(13617,'trails',321,'Can pets walk on the Rim Trail?','Yes, pets are permitted on the paved section of the Rim Trail between Sunrise and Sunset Points, making it a pet-friendly option for hikers.','2025-03-28 01:37:58','2025-03-28 01:37:58'),(13618,'trails',321,'What trailheads can I use to access the Rim Trail?','You can start your hike from several trailheads including Bryce, Inspiration, Sunset, Sunrise, or Fairyland Point.','2025-03-28 01:37:58','2025-03-28 01:37:58'),(13619,'trails',321,'Are there parking facilities available along the Rim Trail?','Yes, parking is available at each of the aforementioned trailheads, but be mindful of peak times for larger crowds.','2025-03-28 01:37:58','2025-03-28 01:37:58'),(13620,'trails',321,'How long does it take to hike the Rim Trail?','Depending on the distance you choose to cover, it can take anywhere from about 1 hour to 7.5 hours to complete your hike.','2025-03-28 01:37:58','2025-03-28 01:37:58'),(13621,'trails',321,'What are the elevation changes on the Rim Trail?','The total elevation gain can reach up to 719 feet (219 meters) along the trail, with specific sections being more gradual.','2025-03-28 01:37:58','2025-03-28 01:37:58'),(13622,'trails',321,'Where can I find restrooms and water on the Rim Trail?','Restrooms are available at Sunset Point year-round, and seasonally near Sunrise Point, along with water-fill stations at strategic locations.','2025-03-28 01:37:58','2025-03-28 01:37:58'),(13623,'trails',321,'Is there a shuttle service for the Rim Trail?','Yes, a shuttle service operates at Bryce, Inspiration, Sunset, and Sunrise Points, though it does not serve Fairyland Point.','2025-03-28 01:37:58','2025-03-28 01:37:58'),(13624,'trails',321,'Is the Rim Trail accessible for all hikers?','While the trail offers some accessible portions, due to the park\'s natural terrain, only certain areas are suitable for those needing accessibility accommodations.','2025-03-28 01:37:58','2025-03-28 01:37:58'),(13625,'trails',321,'What is the easiest hike on the Rim Trail?','The simplest hike is the 0.5-mile (0.8 km) segment that connects Sunset and Sunrise Points, ideal for those looking for an easy walk with minimal elevation gain.','2025-03-28 01:37:59','2025-03-28 01:37:59'),(13626,'trails',321,'What conditions are there for service animals?','Service animals are welcome in national parks, allowing individuals with disabilities to access the trail.','2025-03-28 01:37:59','2025-03-28 01:37:59'),(13627,'trails',322,'What is the Bristlecone Loop Trail?','The Bristlecone Loop Trail is a scenic path that winds through the forest at the highest point of the park, with elevations surpassing 9,100 feet. It features ancient bristlecone pines and offers stunning views of the Four Corners region.','2025-03-28 01:38:07','2025-03-28 01:38:07'),(13628,'trails',322,'How do I access the Bristlecone Loop Trail?','You can start exploring the Bristlecone Loop Trail from either Rainbow Point or Yovimpa Point, both located at the southern end of the park.','2025-03-28 01:38:07','2025-03-28 01:38:07'),(13629,'trails',322,'What is the distance and estimated time for hiking the Bristlecone Loop Trail?','The trail is approximately 1.0 mile (1.6 km) in length and typically takes about 1 hour to complete.','2025-03-28 01:38:07','2025-03-28 01:38:07'),(13630,'trails',322,'What is the difficulty level of the Bristlecone Loop Trail?','This trail is classified as easy, with an elevation gain of only 200 feet (61 meters) and a shorter distance.','2025-03-28 01:38:07','2025-03-28 01:38:07'),(13631,'trails',322,'Are there any parking facilities available for the Bristlecone Loop Trail?','Yes, parking is available at the trailhead. It\'s best to check when the parking lots are busiest, and oversized vehicles are permitted.','2025-03-28 01:38:07','2025-03-28 01:38:07'),(13632,'trails',322,'What amenities are available along the Bristlecone Loop Trail?','There are accessible restrooms available seasonally near the trail. However, shuttle services are not provided for this trail.','2025-03-28 01:38:07','2025-03-28 01:38:07'),(13633,'trails',322,'Is the Bristlecone Loop Trail open year-round?','The trail can be closed in mid-winter due to snow accumulation, which can range from 2 to 15 feet (0.7 to 5 meters).','2025-03-28 01:38:07','2025-03-28 01:38:07'),(13634,'trails',322,'Are pets allowed on the Bristlecone Loop Trail?','No, pets are not allowed on this trail, but service animals are permitted in national parks.','2025-03-28 01:38:07','2025-03-28 01:38:07'),(13635,'trails',322,'What wildlife can I expect to see along the Bristlecone Loop Trail?','Hikers may spot a variety of wildlife, including grouse, woodpeckers, owls, squirrels, chipmunks, Ravens, and Steller\'s Jays in the area.','2025-03-28 01:38:08','2025-03-28 01:38:08'),(13636,'trails',322,'What type of terrain can I expect on the Bristlecone Loop Trail?','The trail features a firm native sediment surface, with varying grades and slopes, making it a moderately easy hike.','2025-03-28 01:38:08','2025-03-28 01:38:08'),(13637,'trails',322,'Is the Bristlecone Loop Trail accessible for everyone?','Due to the natural terrain of the park, the Bristlecone Loop Trail is not considered fully accessible.','2025-03-28 01:38:08','2025-03-28 01:38:08'),(13638,'trails',322,'What are the geographical coordinates for the Bristlecone Loop Trail?','The trail is located at a latitude of 37.4753 and a longitude of -112.24.','2025-03-28 01:38:08','2025-03-28 01:38:08'),(13639,'trails',323,'What is the Queen\'s Garden Trail?','The Queen\'s Garden Trail is an easy trail that takes you down from the rim into the Bryce Canyon Amphitheater, showcasing stunning hoodoos along the way. It wraps up at the beautiful Queen Victoria hoodoo, accessible via a short spur off the main trail.','2025-03-28 01:38:20','2025-03-28 01:38:20'),(13640,'trails',323,'Where does the Queen\'s Garden Trail begin?','The trailhead for the Queen\'s Garden Trail is conveniently located at Sunrise Point.','2025-03-28 01:38:20','2025-03-28 01:38:20'),(13641,'trails',323,'Is parking available near the Queen\'s Garden Trail?','Yes, there is parking available at Sunrise Point. Keep in mind that parking can get busy, so plan accordingly. Additionally, oversized vehicles cannot park in this area when the shuttle service is operational.','2025-03-28 01:38:20','2025-03-28 01:38:20'),(13642,'trails',323,'What is the length and roundtrip distance of the Queen\'s Garden Trail?','The Queen\'s Garden Trail spans 1.8 miles (2.9 km) roundtrip.','2025-03-28 01:38:20','2025-03-28 01:38:20'),(13643,'trails',323,'How long does it typically take to hike the Queen\'s Garden Trail?','Most hikers will take about 1 to 2 hours to complete the trail.','2025-03-28 01:38:20','2025-03-28 01:38:20'),(13644,'trails',323,'What is the elevation gain for the Queen\'s Garden Trail?','Hikers will experience an elevation gain of approximately 450 feet (137 meters) while on the Queen\'s Garden Trail.','2025-03-28 01:38:20','2025-03-28 01:38:20'),(13645,'trails',323,'What is the difficulty level of the Queen\'s Garden Trail?','The trail is rated as moderate due to its elevation gain, but it is one of the easier options for descending into the amphitheater.','2025-03-28 01:38:20','2025-03-28 01:38:20'),(13646,'trails',323,'Are there facilities available along the Queen\'s Garden Trail?','Yes, there are restrooms and a seasonal water-fill station available at the General Store located near Sunrise Point.','2025-03-28 01:38:20','2025-03-28 01:38:20'),(13647,'trails',323,'Is there a shuttle service for accessing the Queen\'s Garden Trail?','Yes, shuttle service is available. However, please note that pets are not allowed on this trail; only service animals are permitted in national parks.','2025-03-28 01:38:20','2025-03-28 01:38:20'),(13648,'trails',323,'Can I combine the Queen\'s Garden Trail with other trails?','Absolutely! The Queen\'s Garden Trail is often combined with the Navajo Loop, creating a scenic 2.9-mile loop where you can enjoy both descending the Queen\'s Garden and ascending via the Navajo Loop to Sunset Point, before returning along the Rim Trail.','2025-03-28 01:38:20','2025-03-28 01:38:20'),(13649,'trails',323,'Is the Queen\'s Garden Trail accessible for everyone?','Due to the natural terrain of the park, this trail is not considered accessible for all visitors.','2025-03-28 01:38:20','2025-03-28 01:38:20'),(13650,'trails',323,'What is the surface type of the Queen\'s Garden Trail?','The trail features a firm native sediment surface, ensuring a stable walking path.','2025-03-28 01:38:21','2025-03-28 01:38:21'),(13651,'trails',323,'What are the gradient characteristics of the Queen\'s Garden Trail?','The trail has a typical gradient of 11.0%, reaching a maximum grade of 25.0%. The typical cross slope is about 5.0%, with a maximum of 17.0%.','2025-03-28 01:38:21','2025-03-28 01:38:21'),(13652,'trails',323,'What is the width of the Queen\'s Garden Trail?','The trail varies in width, with an average width of 81 inches (206 cm) and a minimum width of 33 inches (84 cm).','2025-03-28 01:38:21','2025-03-28 01:38:21'),(13653,'trails',323,'What are the geographic coordinates of the Queen\'s Garden Trail?','The latitude and longitude coordinates for the trail are 37.6284° N and 112.163° W.','2025-03-28 01:38:21','2025-03-28 01:38:21'),(13654,'trails',324,'What is the Queen\'s/Navajo Combination Loop?','The Queen\'s/Navajo Combination Loop is a scenic hiking trail that takes you into the amphitheater at Sunrise Point via the Queen\'s Garden Trail, connecting with either the Two Bridges or Wall Street section of the Navajo Loop before ascending to Sunset Point. You then complete your journey back to Sunrise Point through the Rim Trail, featuring spectacular views, unique hoodoos, and impressive canyon walls.','2025-03-28 01:38:34','2025-03-28 01:38:34'),(13655,'trails',324,'Which trailhead should I start from?','You can begin your hike from either Sunrise Point or Sunset Point, both offering convenient access to the trail.','2025-03-28 01:38:34','2025-03-28 01:38:34'),(13656,'trails',324,'What is the total distance of the loop?','The loop covers a distance of 2.9 miles (4.6 km) roundtrip.','2025-03-28 01:38:34','2025-03-28 01:38:34'),(13657,'trails',324,'How long will the hike typically take?','Expect to spend approximately 2 to 3 hours completing the hike.','2025-03-28 01:38:34','2025-03-28 01:38:34'),(13658,'trails',324,'What is the elevation gain for the hike?','Hikers will experience an elevation gain of about 625 feet (191 meters).','2025-03-28 01:38:34','2025-03-28 01:38:34'),(13659,'trails',324,'What is the difficulty level of the trail?','The trail is classified as moderate, as it features less than 1000 feet of elevation gain and is of moderate length.','2025-03-28 01:38:34','2025-03-28 01:38:34'),(13660,'trails',324,'Are there parking facilities available?','Yes, parking is provided at both Sunrise and Sunset Points. Be mindful of busy times when planning your visit, and note that oversized vehicles are prohibited when the shuttle is in operation.','2025-03-28 01:38:34','2025-03-28 01:38:34'),(13661,'trails',324,'What amenities are available along the trail?','Accessible restrooms can be found year-round at Sunset Point and seasonally at the General Store near Sunrise Point. Water fill stations are also available at Sunset Point and the General Store on a seasonal basis.','2025-03-28 01:38:35','2025-03-28 01:38:35'),(13662,'trails',324,'Is there shuttle service available?','Yes, a shuttle service is offered. In winter, it\'s recommended to use the Two Bridges section of the Navajo Loop, as Wall Street may be closed.','2025-03-28 01:38:35','2025-03-28 01:38:35'),(13663,'trails',324,'Can I bring my pet on the trail?','Pets are not permitted on this trail. However, service animals are allowed throughout national parks.','2025-03-28 01:38:35','2025-03-28 01:38:35'),(13664,'trails',324,'Is the trail accessible for everyone?','Due to the park\'s natural terrain, this trail is not classified as accessible.','2025-03-28 01:38:35','2025-03-28 01:38:35'),(13665,'trails',324,'What is the typical and maximum grade of the trails?','The typical grade for Queen\'s Garden is 11.0% and for Navajo Loop is 14.0%. The maximum grade reaches 25.0% for Queen\'s Garden and 30.0% for Navajo.','2025-03-28 01:38:35','2025-03-28 01:38:35'),(13666,'trails',324,'What are the surface conditions like on the trail?','The trail is composed of firm native sediment, making it manageable for hikers.','2025-03-28 01:38:35','2025-03-28 01:38:35'),(13667,'trails',324,'What are the location coordinates of the trail?','The latitude and longitude coordinates for the trail are 37.6284 and -112.163, respectively.','2025-03-28 01:38:35','2025-03-28 01:38:35'),(13668,'trails',325,'What is the length of the Tower Bridge hike?','The Tower Bridge hike covers a distance of 3.0 miles (or 4.8 kilometers) for a round trip.','2025-03-28 01:38:42','2025-03-28 01:38:42'),(13669,'trails',325,'How long does it typically take to complete the Tower Bridge hike?','You can expect to complete the hike in approximately 2 to 3 hours.','2025-03-28 01:38:42','2025-03-28 01:38:42'),(13670,'trails',325,'What is the difficulty level of the Tower Bridge trail?','This trail is rated as moderate, featuring an elevation gain of 760 feet (232 meters) over the hike.','2025-03-28 01:38:42','2025-03-28 01:38:42'),(13671,'trails',325,'Where can I park for the Tower Bridge trail?','Parking is available at Sunrise Point, but keep in mind that it can get busy, especially during peak hours.','2025-03-28 01:38:42','2025-03-28 01:38:42'),(13672,'trails',325,'Are oversized vehicles allowed in the parking area?','No, oversized vehicles cannot park in the area when the shuttle service is in operation.','2025-03-28 01:38:43','2025-03-28 01:38:43'),(13673,'trails',325,'Is the Tower Bridge trail suitable for pets?','Pets are not permitted on this trail, although service animals are allowed in national parks.','2025-03-28 01:38:43','2025-03-28 01:38:43'),(13674,'trails',325,'What amenities are available at the starting point of the hike?','You can find accessible restrooms and a water-fill station at the General Store near Sunrise Point, though these services are seasonal.','2025-03-28 01:38:43','2025-03-28 01:38:43'),(13675,'trails',325,'What is the trailhead location for the Tower Bridge hike?','The trailhead for the Tower Bridge hike is located north of Sunrise Point on the rim trail.','2025-03-28 01:38:43','2025-03-28 01:38:43'),(13676,'trails',325,'What type of surface can I expect on the Tower Bridge trail?','The trail features a firm native sediment surface, typical for backcountry trails.','2025-03-28 01:38:43','2025-03-28 01:38:43'),(13677,'trails',325,'Is the Tower Bridge trail accessible for people with mobility challenges?','This trail is not considered accessible due to its natural terrain and backcountry characteristics.','2025-03-28 01:38:43','2025-03-28 01:38:43'),(13678,'trails',325,'Is shuttle service available for the Tower Bridge trail?','Yes, shuttle service is available for visitors hiking in the area.','2025-03-28 01:38:43','2025-03-28 01:38:43'),(13679,'trails',326,'What is the Swamp Canyon Loop trail known for?','The Swamp Canyon Loop offers a more intimate experience with nature, showcasing the sheltered Swamp Canyon view, and takes hikers through a rugged, forested backcountry.','2025-03-28 01:38:56','2025-03-28 01:38:56'),(13680,'trails',326,'Where does the Swamp Canyon Loop trail begin?','The trailhead is located at the Swamp Canyon Viewpoint, which can be found at Mile 6 on the Southern Scenic Drive.','2025-03-28 01:38:56','2025-03-28 01:38:56'),(13681,'trails',326,'Is there parking available at the Swamp Canyon Viewpoint?','Yes, parking is available at the Swamp Canyon Viewpoint, but it\'s advisable to check peak times for busyness. Oversized vehicles are permitted.','2025-03-28 01:38:56','2025-03-28 01:38:56'),(13682,'trails',326,'What is the length of the Swamp Canyon Loop trail?','The total distance of the Swamp Canyon Loop is 4.0 miles (6.4 km) round trip.','2025-03-28 01:38:56','2025-03-28 01:38:56'),(13683,'trails',326,'How long does it typically take to hike the Swamp Canyon Loop?','Hikers can expect to spend approximately 3 to 4 hours on this trail.','2025-03-28 01:38:56','2025-03-28 01:38:56'),(13684,'trails',326,'What is the elevation gain of the Swamp Canyon Loop?','The trail has an elevation gain of about 800 feet (244 meters).','2025-03-28 01:38:56','2025-03-28 01:38:56'),(13685,'trails',326,'What is the difficulty level of the Swamp Canyon Loop?','The hike is rated as moderate, as it has an elevation gain of less than 1000 feet and a moderate distance.','2025-03-28 01:38:56','2025-03-28 01:38:56'),(13686,'trails',326,'Are there any services available on the Swamp Canyon Loop trail?','No services are available along the trail, and there is no shuttle service provided. Private options might be available.','2025-03-28 01:38:56','2025-03-28 01:38:56'),(13687,'trails',326,'Can the Swamp Canyon Loop trail be accessed in winter?','The trail may be inaccessible during mid-winter due to snow depths that can range from 2 to 15 feet (0.7 to 5 meters).','2025-03-28 01:38:57','2025-03-28 01:38:57'),(13688,'trails',326,'Are pets allowed on the Swamp Canyon Loop?','Pets are not permitted on this trail, but service animals are allowed in national parks.','2025-03-28 01:38:57','2025-03-28 01:38:57'),(13689,'trails',326,'What about accessibility on the Swamp Canyon Loop trail?','This trail is a backcountry path with natural terrain and is not considered accessible.','2025-03-28 01:38:57','2025-03-28 01:38:57'),(13690,'trails',326,'What is the surface type of the Swamp Canyon Loop trail?','The trail features a firm native sediment surface.','2025-03-28 01:38:57','2025-03-28 01:38:57'),(13691,'trails',326,'What are the coordinates of the Swamp Canyon Loop trail?','The trail\'s latitude is 37.5874 and the longitude is -112.214.','2025-03-28 01:38:57','2025-03-28 01:38:57'),(13692,'trails',327,'What is the Fairyland Loop hike like?','The Fairyland Loop is a serene 8-mile trail in southern Utah that showcases stunning views of the Bryce Amphitheater and its iconic hoodoos, combining scenic walking along the plateau rim and into the canyon.','2025-03-28 01:39:07','2025-03-28 01:39:07'),(13693,'trails',327,'Where can I start the Fairyland Loop hike?','You can begin the Fairyland Loop at either Fairyland Point or the Tower Bridge trailhead, which is located north of Sunrise Point.','2025-03-28 01:39:07','2025-03-28 01:39:07'),(13694,'trails',327,'What direction should I hike the Fairyland Loop?','It\'s recommended to hike in a counter-clockwise direction for a better experience of the views and terrain.','2025-03-28 01:39:07','2025-03-28 01:39:07'),(13695,'trails',327,'Is there a shuttle service available for the Fairyland Loop?','There is no shuttle service at Fairyland Point, so you\'ll need to walk to your starting point to complete the loop. However, shuttle service is available at Sunrise Point.','2025-03-28 01:39:07','2025-03-28 01:39:07'),(13696,'trails',327,'What are the parking options for the hike?','You can park at Fairyland Point (which accommodates oversized vehicles) or at Sunrise Point, but keep in mind that oversized vehicles are not allowed at Sunrise Point when the shuttle is in operation.','2025-03-28 01:39:07','2025-03-28 01:39:07'),(13697,'trails',327,'How long will it take to hike the Fairyland Loop?','The hike typically takes around 4 to 5 hours to complete, depending on your pace and the time spent enjoying the views.','2025-03-28 01:39:07','2025-03-28 01:39:07'),(13698,'trails',327,'What is the elevation gain for this trail?','The trail features an elevation gain of approximately 1,900 feet (579 meters), making it a strenuous hike due to its rapid ascent and length.','2025-03-28 01:39:08','2025-03-28 01:39:08'),(13699,'trails',327,'Are there any facilities available along the hike?','There are accessible restrooms and water fill stations available at the General Store near Sunrise Point, but no services are provided at Fairyland Point.','2025-03-28 01:39:08','2025-03-28 01:39:08'),(13700,'trails',327,'Can I bring my pets on the Fairyland Loop hike?','Pets are not permitted on the trail, but service animals are allowed in national parks.','2025-03-28 01:39:08','2025-03-28 01:39:08'),(13701,'trails',327,'What should I know about trail accessibility?','The Fairyland Loop is a backcountry trail with natural terrain and is not designated as accessible. Hikers should be prepared for varying trail conditions.','2025-03-28 01:39:08','2025-03-28 01:39:08'),(13702,'trails',327,'Could the trail be closed during winter?','Yes, the trail may be inaccessible during mid-winter due to snow accumulation, which can range from 2 to 15 feet.','2025-03-28 01:39:08','2025-03-28 01:39:08'),(13703,'trails',327,'What is the trail\'s surface type?','The trail consists of firm native sediment, providing a stable surface for hiking.','2025-03-28 01:39:08','2025-03-28 01:39:08'),(13704,'trails',327,'What are the dimensions of the trail?','The trail has a typical width of 49 inches (124 cm) with a minimum width of 16 inches (41 cm), and features various grades and slopes along its route.','2025-03-28 01:39:08','2025-03-28 01:39:08'),(13705,'trails',327,'What are the GPS coordinates for the Fairyland Loop?','The latitude for the Fairyland Loop is 37.6493 and the longitude is -112.147.','2025-03-28 01:39:09','2025-03-28 01:39:09'),(13706,'trails',328,'What is the total distance of the Navajo/Peekaboo Combination Loop?','The hike spans a total distance of 4.9 miles (7.9 km).','2025-03-28 01:39:20','2025-03-28 01:39:20'),(13707,'trails',328,'What is the elevation gain on this trail?','Hikers can expect an elevation gain of 1475 feet (450 meters), which makes it quite challenging.','2025-03-28 01:39:20','2025-03-28 01:39:20'),(13708,'trails',328,'How long will it take to complete the hike?','It typically takes between 3 to 4 hours to finish this strenuous hike.','2025-03-28 01:39:20','2025-03-28 01:39:20'),(13709,'trails',328,'What is the difficulty level of the trail?','This trail is classified as strenuous due to its rapid elevation gain and longer distance.','2025-03-28 01:39:20','2025-03-28 01:39:20'),(13710,'trails',328,'Where does the hike begin?','The trail begins at Sunset Point, where parking is also available.','2025-03-28 01:39:20','2025-03-28 01:39:20'),(13711,'trails',328,'Are there facilities available at the trailhead?','Yes, there are accessible restrooms at Sunset Point year-round, as well as pit toilets on the Peekaboo Loop during the summer.','2025-03-28 01:39:20','2025-03-28 01:39:20'),(13712,'trails',328,'Is there water available along the trail?','Water-fill stations are available seasonally at Sunset Point and year-round at the Sunset Point restroom.','2025-03-28 01:39:20','2025-03-28 01:39:20'),(13713,'trails',328,'Is shuttle service provided for hikers?','Yes, there is a shuttle service available, but it’s important to check if it\'s operating as it may vary seasonally.','2025-03-28 01:39:20','2025-03-28 01:39:20'),(13714,'trails',328,'Can I bring my pet on this trail?','No, pets are not allowed on the Navajo/Peekaboo Combination Loop, but service animals are permitted in national parks.','2025-03-28 01:39:21','2025-03-28 01:39:21'),(13715,'trails',328,'What should hikers do if they encounter horses or mules on the trail?','Hikers should give the right-of-way to horses and mules, which may be encountered on the Peekaboo Loop.','2025-03-28 01:39:21','2025-03-28 01:39:21'),(13716,'trails',328,'Is this trail accessible for those with mobility challenges?','Due to the natural terrain, this trail is not considered accessible for individuals with mobility challenges.','2025-03-28 01:39:21','2025-03-28 01:39:21'),(13717,'trails',328,'What is the typical grade of the trail?','The typical grade is 14.0% on the Navajo Loop and 6.0% on the Peekaboo Loop.','2025-03-28 01:39:21','2025-03-28 01:39:21'),(13718,'trails',328,'What is the maximum grade hikers can expect?','Hikers may encounter a maximum grade of 30.0% on the Navajo Loop and 27.0% on the Peekaboo Loop.','2025-03-28 01:39:21','2025-03-28 01:39:21'),(13719,'trails',328,'What kind of surface can hikers expect on this trail?','The trail features a firm native sediment surface, which provides good footing for hikers.','2025-03-28 01:39:21','2025-03-28 01:39:21'),(13720,'trails',328,'What is the starting latitude and longitude of the trail?','The starting coordinates of the trail are approximately 37.6227 latitude and -112.166 longitude.','2025-03-28 01:39:21','2025-03-28 01:39:21'),(13721,'trails',328,'Can hikers complete the trails separately?','Yes, hikers have the option to hike the Navajo Loop and Peekaboo Loop individually if they choose.','2025-03-28 01:39:21','2025-03-28 01:39:21'),(13722,'trails',329,'What is the Bryce Amphitheater Traverse?','The Bryce Amphitheater Traverse is a scenic one-way hike that links the Peekaboo Loop and the Queen\'s Garden trail. It starts at Bryce Point, where hikers descend, turn left onto the Peekaboo Loop, and then connect to the Queen\'s Garden trail, culminating at Sunrise Point.','2025-03-28 01:39:36','2025-03-28 01:39:36'),(13723,'trails',329,'Where can I find the trailhead for this hike?','The trailhead is located at Bryce Point, where you can also find parking facilities.','2025-03-28 01:39:36','2025-03-28 01:39:36'),(13724,'trails',329,'Is parking available at the trailhead?','Yes, there is parking at the trailhead. However, it\'s a good idea to check when the lot is busiest, especially if you are in an oversized vehicle, as they are not allowed during shuttle operation times.','2025-03-28 01:39:36','2025-03-28 01:39:36'),(13725,'trails',329,'What is the distance of the Bryce Amphitheater Traverse?','The total distance of the hike is approximately 4.7 miles (7.6 kilometers).','2025-03-28 01:39:36','2025-03-28 01:39:36'),(13726,'trails',329,'How long is the hike expected to take?','On average, hikers can expect to complete the traverse in about 3 to 4 hours.','2025-03-28 01:39:36','2025-03-28 01:39:36'),(13727,'trails',329,'What is the elevation gain on this trail?','The hike features an elevation gain of around 1145 feet (349 meters), making it a strenuous ascent.','2025-03-28 01:39:36','2025-03-28 01:39:36'),(13728,'trails',329,'How difficult is the hike?','This trail is considered strenuous, primarily due to its rapid elevation gain and length.','2025-03-28 01:39:36','2025-03-28 01:39:36'),(13729,'trails',329,'Are there any facilities along the trail?','Yes, you can find pit toilets on the west side of the Peekaboo Loop, but these are only available during the summer months.','2025-03-28 01:39:36','2025-03-28 01:39:36'),(13730,'trails',329,'Is there a shuttle service for this trail?','Yes, shuttle services are available, but please note that the trail may be impassable during mid-winter due to significant snow depths ranging from 2 to 15 feet.','2025-03-28 01:39:36','2025-03-28 01:39:36'),(13731,'trails',329,'Can I bring my pet on this trail?','Pets are not permitted on this trail; however, service animals are allowed in national parks.','2025-03-28 01:39:36','2025-03-28 01:39:36'),(13732,'trails',329,'What should I know about encountering horses and mules on the trail?','Hikers may come across horses and mules along the Peekaboo Loop. It is important to yield the right-of-way to these riders.','2025-03-28 01:39:36','2025-03-28 01:39:36'),(13733,'trails',329,'Is the trail accessible for everyone?','Due to the natural terrain of the park, this trail is not considered accessible.','2025-03-28 01:39:36','2025-03-28 01:39:36'),(13734,'trails',329,'What type of surface can I expect on the trail?','The trail consists of firm native sediment, providing a stable walking surface.','2025-03-28 01:39:36','2025-03-28 01:39:36'),(13735,'trails',329,'What are the average and maximum grades on the trail?','The typical grade is around 11.0% on the Queen\'s Garden trail and 6.0% on the Peekaboo Loop, with maximum grades reaching 25.0% and 27.0%, respectively.','2025-03-28 01:39:36','2025-03-28 01:39:36'),(13736,'trails',329,'What is the typical and minimum width of the trails?','The trails typically range from 76 inches (193 cm) on the Peekaboo Loop to 81 inches (206 cm) on the Queen\'s Garden trail; the minimum width is 48 inches (122 cm) for Peekaboo and 33 inches (84 cm) for Queen\'s.','2025-03-28 01:39:36','2025-03-28 01:39:36'),(13737,'trails',329,'What is the geographical location of the trail?','The latitude and longitude coordinates for the trail are approximately 37.6057° N and 112.158° W.','2025-03-28 01:39:36','2025-03-28 01:39:36'),(13738,'trails',330,'What is the Figure-8 Combination trail?','The Figure-8 Combination trail is an iconic hiking experience that merges three stunning hikes: Queen\'s Garden, Navajo Loop, and Peekaboo Loop. This route showcases breathtaking rock formations and allows hikers to explore the beautiful amphitheater area.','2025-03-28 01:39:47','2025-03-28 01:39:47'),(13739,'trails',330,'What is the recommended direction to hike the Figure-8 Combination?','It is suggested to start the hike in a clockwise direction, descending into Queen\'s Garden, then connecting to the Peekaboo Loop also clockwise, and finally ascending the Navajo Loop. In winter, you can use the Two Bridges route.','2025-03-28 01:39:47','2025-03-28 01:39:47'),(13740,'trails',330,'Where does the Figure-8 Combination trail start?','You can begin your hike from either Sunrise Point or Sunset Point, both of which have parking available.','2025-03-28 01:39:48','2025-03-28 01:39:48'),(13741,'trails',330,'How long is the Figure-8 Combination trail?','The total distance for the Figure-8 Combination trail is approximately 6.4 miles (10.3 kilometers).','2025-03-28 01:39:48','2025-03-28 01:39:48'),(13742,'trails',330,'What is the estimated time to complete the hike?','Most hikers can expect to complete the Figure-8 Combination in about 4 to 5 hours.','2025-03-28 01:39:48','2025-03-28 01:39:48'),(13743,'trails',330,'What is the elevation gain on this trail?','The trail features an elevation gain of around 1,575 feet (480 meters), making it a challenging hike.','2025-03-28 01:39:48','2025-03-28 01:39:48'),(13744,'trails',330,'How difficult is the Figure-8 Combination hike?','This trail is classified as strenuous due to its significant elevation gain and its overall length.','2025-03-28 01:39:48','2025-03-28 01:39:48'),(13745,'trails',330,'What services are available on this trail?','Accessible restrooms are located at Sunset Point year-round and seasonally near Sunrise Point. Water refill stations are also available at various points, including Sunset Point and the General Store.','2025-03-28 01:39:48','2025-03-28 01:39:48'),(13746,'trails',330,'Is there a shuttle service for this trail?','Yes, there is a shuttle service available; however, this trail may be inaccessible in mid-winter due to deep snow.','2025-03-28 01:39:48','2025-03-28 01:39:48'),(13747,'trails',330,'Are pets allowed on the Figure-8 Combination trail?','No, pets are not allowed on this trail, but service animals are permitted in national parks.','2025-03-28 01:39:48','2025-03-28 01:39:48'),(13748,'trails',330,'What should I do if I encounter horses or mules on the trail?','Hikers are encouraged to yield the right-of-way to horseback riders and mule trains encountered on the Peekaboo Loop.','2025-03-28 01:39:48','2025-03-28 01:39:48'),(13749,'trails',330,'Is the Figure-8 Combination trail accessible for everyone?','Due to the natural terrain of the park, this trail is not considered accessible.','2025-03-28 01:39:49','2025-03-28 01:39:49'),(13750,'trails',330,'What type of surface can I expect on this trail?','The trail surface is primarily firm native sediment, providing a solid footing for hikers.','2025-03-28 01:39:49','2025-03-28 01:39:49'),(13751,'trails',330,'Can I hike the individual trails separately?','Yes, you can hike the Queen\'s Garden, Navajo Loop, and Peekaboo Loop as standalone trails if you prefer shorter hikes.','2025-03-28 01:39:49','2025-03-28 01:39:49'),(13752,'trails',331,'What is the Riggs Spring Loop trail like?','The Riggs Spring Loop is a challenging 8.6-mile backcountry trail that navigates through beautiful spruce, fir, and bristlecone forests, providing stunning views of distant cliffs along the way.','2025-03-28 01:40:02','2025-03-28 01:40:02'),(13753,'trails',331,'Where does the Riggs Spring Loop start and end?','The trail begins and concludes at Yovimpa Point, which also offers accessible restrooms year-round.','2025-03-28 01:40:02','2025-03-28 01:40:02'),(13754,'trails',331,'Are permits required for hiking the Riggs Spring Loop?','No permits are needed for day hikes on this trail. However, if you plan to stay overnight at designated backcountry campsites, a permit is essential.','2025-03-28 01:40:02','2025-03-28 01:40:02'),(13755,'trails',331,'What is the difficulty level of the Riggs Spring Loop?','This trail is classified as strenuous due to its challenging elevation gain and rugged terrain.','2025-03-28 01:40:02','2025-03-28 01:40:02'),(13756,'trails',331,'What is the elevation gain for the Riggs Spring Loop?','The trail features an elevation gain of approximately 2200 feet (671 meters).','2025-03-28 01:40:02','2025-03-28 01:40:02'),(13757,'trails',331,'How long does it take to complete the Riggs Spring Loop?','On average, hikers can expect to complete the trail in about 5 hours.','2025-03-28 01:40:02','2025-03-28 01:40:02'),(13758,'trails',331,'Are there facilities available at Yovimpa Point?','Yes, Yovimpa Point has accessible restrooms available, but there are no water-fill stations.','2025-03-28 01:40:03','2025-03-28 01:40:03'),(13759,'trails',331,'Is this trail suitable for pets?','Pets are not allowed on the Riggs Spring Loop, although service animals are permitted in national parks.','2025-03-28 01:40:03','2025-03-28 01:40:03'),(13760,'trails',331,'What should hikers know about winter conditions on this trail?','During mid-winter, the trail may be inaccessible due to snow depths that can range from 2 to 15 feet (0.7 to 5 meters).','2025-03-28 01:40:03','2025-03-28 01:40:03'),(13761,'trails',331,'Can hikers camp along the Riggs Spring Loop?','Backcountry camping is allowed, but only in designated campsites, and an overnight permit is required.','2025-03-28 01:40:03','2025-03-28 01:40:03'),(13762,'trails',331,'What is the best way to hike the Riggs Spring Loop?','Most hikers prefer to tackle the loop in a counter-clockwise direction, often combining it with additional nights on the Under-the-Rim Trail.','2025-03-28 01:40:03','2025-03-28 01:40:03'),(13763,'trails',331,'What kind of terrain can hikers expect on this trail?','The trail features natural terrain with firm native sediment, but it is not classified as accessible for those with mobility challenges.','2025-03-28 01:40:03','2025-03-28 01:40:03'),(13764,'trails',331,'Is shuttle service available for the Riggs Spring Loop?','There is no official shuttle service for this trail, but private options may be arranged.','2025-03-28 01:40:03','2025-03-28 01:40:03'),(13765,'trails',331,'What are the coordinates of the Riggs Spring Loop?','The latitude and longitude for the Riggs Spring Loop are approximately 37.4733 and -112.24, respectively.','2025-03-28 01:40:03','2025-03-28 01:40:03'),(13766,'trails',332,'What is the best way to explore Bryce Canyon by bike?','The ideal way to explore Bryce Canyon by bike is by using the Shared-Use Path, which spans 5 miles of vehicle-free, two-lane path connecting key locations such as the Shuttle Station, Visitor Center, and Inspiration Point.','2025-03-28 01:40:15','2025-03-28 01:40:15'),(13767,'trails',332,'How far is the ride from the Park Shuttle Station to Inspiration Point?','The route from the Park Shuttle Station to Inspiration Point is 4.0 miles, covering various elevations with a total climb of around 343 feet.','2025-03-28 01:40:15','2025-03-28 01:40:15'),(13768,'trails',332,'What biking opportunities are available for different skill levels?','Bryce Canyon offers biking opportunities suitable for all skill levels, from leisurely rides on the Shared-Use Path to more challenging rides along the main park road.','2025-03-28 01:40:15','2025-03-28 01:40:15'),(13769,'trails',332,'Are there bike rentals available?','Yes, you can rent a standard bike or an E-bike at the Historic Service Station if you didn\'t bring your own.','2025-03-28 01:40:15','2025-03-28 01:40:15'),(13770,'trails',332,'What regulations should cyclists be aware of?','Cyclists should stay on paved surfaces, pass on the left while announcing their presence, and ride single file on park roads. E-bikes are permitted if they have operable pedals and a motor under 750 watts.','2025-03-28 01:40:15','2025-03-28 01:40:15'),(13771,'trails',332,'What types of vehicles are allowed on the Shared-Use Path?','The Shared-Use Path is designated for non-motorized vehicles, allowing cyclists, pedestrians, rollerbladers, and leashed pets, but no off-pavement or motorized vehicles are permitted.','2025-03-28 01:40:15','2025-03-28 01:40:15'),(13772,'trails',332,'Is it safe to ride on the main park road?','Riding on the main park road can be challenging due to traffic and narrow shoulders. Safety precautions, such as riding single file and using lights during low visibility, are essential.','2025-03-28 01:40:15','2025-03-28 01:40:15'),(13773,'trails',332,'What are the main elevation changes on the Shared-Use Path?','Along the Shared-Use Path, cyclists experience a total elevation gain of 746 feet while riding from the Shuttle Station to Inspiration Point and a descent of 266 feet.','2025-03-28 01:40:16','2025-03-28 01:40:16'),(13774,'trails',332,'Can cyclists ride anywhere in the park?','Cyclists must stick to paved surfaces within the park; riding on unpaved trails is not allowed.','2025-03-28 01:40:16','2025-03-28 01:40:16'),(13775,'trails',332,'What should I consider for visibility and safety while biking?','Ensure to have front and rear lights or reflectors that meet visibility requirements. Wearing a helmet and bright clothing is also highly recommended to enhance visibility.','2025-03-28 01:40:16','2025-03-28 01:40:16'),(13776,'trails',332,'What is the maximum steepness for the Shared-Use Path?','The Shared-Use Path features a maximum grade of 5% to ensure accessibility for a range of users.','2025-03-28 01:40:16','2025-03-28 01:40:16'),(13777,'trails',332,'Are pets allowed on the Shared-Use Path?','Yes, pets are allowed on the Shared-Use Path, but they must be kept on a leash.','2025-03-28 01:40:16','2025-03-28 01:40:16'),(13778,'trails',332,'What facilities are available at key points along the biking route?','Bike racks are available at scenic viewpoints such as Inspiration, Sunset, and Sunrise Points, as well as at the Visitor Center and Shuttle Station.','2025-03-28 01:40:16','2025-03-28 01:40:16'),(13779,'trails',333,'What is the Night Sky Telescope Program?','The Night Sky Telescope Program offers visitors a chance to explore the stunning dark skies of Bryce Canyon, complete with guided tours and telescope observations. It focuses on the science and cultural significance of this designated International Dark Sky Park.','2025-03-28 01:40:22','2025-03-28 01:40:22'),(13780,'trails',333,'When is the Night Sky Telescope Program available?','The program runs until August 4, 2023, starting nightly at 9:30 p.m.','2025-03-28 01:40:22','2025-03-28 01:40:22'),(13781,'trails',333,'How do I reserve a spot for the Night Sky Telescope Program?','Reservations are necessary to participate in the program and can be made at the Visitor Center on the day of the event, starting at 8:15 a.m.','2025-03-28 01:40:22','2025-03-28 01:40:22'),(13782,'trails',333,'What can participants expect from the Night Sky Telescope Program?','Participants will experience the enchanting views of the night sky through telescopes, guided by park rangers, while learning about the astronomy and cultural stories linked to the park\'s unique environment.','2025-03-28 01:40:23','2025-03-28 01:40:23'),(13783,'trails',333,'Is there an option for stargazing independently?','Yes, if you weren\'t able to make a reservation, there are still plenty of opportunities to enjoy the night sky at Bryce Canyon independently. Check out our Stargazing page for more details.','2025-03-28 01:40:23','2025-03-28 01:40:23'),(13784,'trails',333,'Is the Night Sky Telescope Program accessible for everyone?','Absolutely! The program is ADA accessible, ensuring that everyone can enjoy the marvels of the night sky.','2025-03-28 01:40:23','2025-03-28 01:40:23'),(13785,'trails',333,'Can I bring my dog to the Night Sky Telescope Program?','Yes, dogs are allowed to accompany you during the Night Sky Telescope Program, making it a fun experience for pet owners as well.','2025-03-28 01:40:23','2025-03-28 01:40:23'),(13786,'trails',333,'What are the geographical coordinates of Bryce Canyon?','Bryce Canyon is located at a latitude of 37.6404 and a longitude of -112.17.','2025-03-28 01:40:23','2025-03-28 01:40:23'),(13787,'trails',334,'What is special about stargazing at Bryce Canyon?','Bryce Canyon is renowned for its exceptionally dark skies, making it one of the best locations for stargazing in the country. With its high elevation, clean air, and remote setting, visitors can witness thousands of stars and the stunning Milky Way on clear nights.','2025-03-28 01:40:30','2025-03-28 01:40:30'),(13788,'trails',334,'Which areas are recommended for the best stargazing views?','Some of the prime spots for stargazing in Bryce Canyon include Sunset Point, Sunrise Point, Inspiration Point, and Paria View. Each of these locations offers breathtaking perspectives of the night sky.','2025-03-28 01:40:30','2025-03-28 01:40:30'),(13789,'trails',334,'Are there specific trails for night photography?','For those interested in night photography, the Queen\'s Garden and Navajo Trails are highly recommended due to their unique foregrounds featuring hoodoos that can enhance your night shots.','2025-03-28 01:40:30','2025-03-28 01:40:30'),(13790,'trails',334,'How can I find out about stargazing programs?','To discover available programs during your visit, be sure to check the Calendar or stop by the Visitor Center for the latest information on ranger-led astronomy activities.','2025-03-28 01:40:30','2025-03-28 01:40:30'),(13791,'trails',334,'What is the significance of the International Dark Sky status?','Bryce Canyon received the International Dark Sky designation in 2019, underscoring its commitment to preserving its dark skies. This status allows visitors to experience the grandeur of the night sky, especially during phases of the new moon on clear nights.','2025-03-28 01:40:30','2025-03-28 01:40:30'),(13792,'trails',334,'Can I participate in ranger-led telescope programs?','Ranger-led telescope programs may be offered during your visit depending on the timing and day of the week. Regardless, visitors are welcome to enjoy the spectacular night sky independently at any time.','2025-03-28 01:40:31','2025-03-28 01:40:31'),(13793,'trails',334,'Is the stargazing area accessible?','The accessibility of stargazing locations may vary. However, all the recommended viewpoints for stargazing are paved and accessible. Check the specific location links for more detailed accessibility information.','2025-03-28 01:40:31','2025-03-28 01:40:31'),(13794,'trails',334,'Are dogs allowed in the stargazing areas?','Yes, dogs are permitted in the stargazing areas, so you can enjoy the night sky with your furry friend.','2025-03-28 01:40:31','2025-03-28 01:40:31'),(13795,'trails',334,'What are the geographical coordinates for Bryce Canyon?','Bryce Canyon is located at a latitude of 37.5952 and a longitude of -112.171.','2025-03-28 01:40:31','2025-03-28 01:40:31'),(13796,'trails',335,'What is the Under-the-Rim Trail?','The Under-the-Rim Trail is a scenic hiking route that connects Rainbow Point and Bryce Point, offering captivating views of distant cliffs, lush forests, and peaceful meadows.','2025-03-28 01:40:46','2025-03-28 01:40:46'),(13797,'trails',335,'What is the typical hiking direction for the Under-the-Rim Trail?','Most hikers choose to traverse the trail from south to north, starting at Rainbow Point and finishing at Bryce Point.','2025-03-28 01:40:46','2025-03-28 01:40:46'),(13798,'trails',335,'How long is the Under-the-Rim Trail?','The trail spans approximately 22.9 miles (36.9 kilometers).','2025-03-28 01:40:46','2025-03-28 01:40:46'),(13799,'trails',335,'What is the recommended duration for hiking the Under-the-Rim Trail?','It is generally recommended to complete this hike in 2 to 3 days, allowing time to enjoy the surroundings and set up camp.','2025-03-28 01:40:46','2025-03-28 01:40:46'),(13800,'trails',335,'What is the elevation gain on this trail?','Hikers can expect a total elevation gain of about 5500 feet (1676 meters), which contributes to its strenuous rating.','2025-03-28 01:40:46','2025-03-28 01:40:46'),(13801,'trails',335,'Is a permit required for hiking the Under-the-Rim Trail?','While no permits are needed for day hiking, all overnight stays in the backcountry require a permit.','2025-03-28 01:40:46','2025-03-28 01:40:46'),(13802,'trails',335,'What facilities are available at the trailheads?','Parking is available at both Rainbow Point and Bryce Point; however, oversized vehicles are only permitted at Rainbow Point.','2025-03-28 01:40:46','2025-03-28 01:40:46'),(13803,'trails',335,'Are there restroom facilities along the Under-the-Rim Trail?','There are accessible restrooms located at Rainbow Point, but there are no services along the trail itself.','2025-03-28 01:40:46','2025-03-28 01:40:46'),(13804,'trails',335,'Can I bring my pet on the Under-the-Rim Trail?','Pets are not allowed on this trail, but service animals are permitted within national parks.','2025-03-28 01:40:46','2025-03-28 01:40:46'),(13805,'trails',335,'What is the hiking difficulty level of the Under-the-Rim Trail?','This trail is considered strenuous due to its elevation gain and challenging terrain.','2025-03-28 01:40:47','2025-03-28 01:40:47'),(13806,'trails',335,'Are there campsites available along the Under-the-Rim Trail?','Yes, there are six designated campsites and one group site, providing opportunities for backcountry camping along the route.','2025-03-28 01:40:47','2025-03-28 01:40:47'),(13807,'trails',335,'What season might the Under-the-Rim Trail be inaccessible?','The trail may be difficult to access in mid-winter, as snow can accumulate to depths between 2 and 15 feet (0.7 to 5 meters).','2025-03-28 01:40:47','2025-03-28 01:40:47'),(13808,'trails',335,'What nearby trails intersect with the Under-the-Rim Trail?','The Under-the-Rim Trail intersects with three connecting trails at Agua Canyon, Whiteman Bench, and Swamp Canyon trailheads.','2025-03-28 01:40:47','2025-03-28 01:40:47'),(13809,'trails',335,'Is shuttle service available for this trail?','Shuttle service is available to Bryce Point, but there is no shuttle to Rainbow Point. However, private shuttle options may be accessible.','2025-03-28 01:40:47','2025-03-28 01:40:47'),(13810,'trails',335,'What should hikers know about the accessibility of the Under-the-Rim Trail?','This trail consists of natural and rugged terrain, making it unsuitable for those requiring accessible paths.','2025-03-28 01:40:47','2025-03-28 01:40:47'),(13811,'trails',335,'Can I combine the Under-the-Rim Trail hike with other trails?','Some hikers opt to extend their adventure by combining the Under-the-Rim Trail with an additional night along the Riggs Spring Loop.','2025-03-28 01:40:47','2025-03-28 01:40:47'),(13812,'trails',336,'What is the duration and distance of the ranger-led Rim Walk?','The ranger-led Rim Walk lasts approximately one hour and covers a distance of about 1/2 mile on a paved path.','2025-03-28 01:40:58','2025-03-28 01:40:58'),(13813,'trails',336,'Is the Rim Walk suitable for all ages?','Yes, the Rim Walk is designed to be suitable for participants of all ages.','2025-03-28 01:40:58','2025-03-28 01:40:58'),(13814,'trails',336,'When does the Rim Walk typically take place?','The Rim Walk is usually offered daily from Memorial Day through Labor Day at 2:00 p.m.','2025-03-28 01:40:58','2025-03-28 01:40:58'),(13815,'trails',336,'Where can I meet for the Rim Walk?','You can meet for the Rim Walk at Sunset Point, near the observation platform.','2025-03-28 01:40:58','2025-03-28 01:40:58'),(13816,'trails',336,'Is the Rim Walk accessible for those with mobility challenges?','Absolutely, the path is wheelchair accessible, making it easier for everyone to enjoy.','2025-03-28 01:40:58','2025-03-28 01:40:58'),(13817,'trails',336,'What should I do if the weather is poor?','Please note that inclement weather may result in the cancellation of the Rim Walk.','2025-03-28 01:40:58','2025-03-28 01:40:58'),(13818,'trails',336,'Can I bring my dog on the Rim Walk?','Yes, dogs are allowed on the Rim Walk, making it a pet-friendly activity.','2025-03-28 01:40:58','2025-03-28 01:40:58'),(13819,'trails',336,'What can I expect to learn during the Rim Walk?','During the walk, you will learn about the enchanting hoodoos, the historical significance of the area, and the unique adaptations of the local wildlife and plant life in Bryce Canyon National Park.','2025-03-28 01:40:59','2025-03-28 01:40:59'),(13820,'trails',336,'Where can I check for the latest information on daily programs?','For updated program information, it\'s a good idea to check the Calendar or visit the Visitor Center when you arrive.','2025-03-28 01:40:59','2025-03-28 01:40:59'),(13821,'trails',337,'What time do I need to arrive at the Visitor Center for the Full Moon Hike lottery?','Participants should arrive at the Visitor Center a few minutes before 4 p.m. (Mountain Time) to enter the Full Moon Hike lottery.','2025-03-28 01:41:07','2025-03-28 01:41:07'),(13822,'trails',337,'What is the duration and type of hike during the Full Moon event?','The Full Moon Hike typically lasts between 1 to 2 miles, with the route being a \'ranger\'s choice.\' It may involve an easy walk along the plateau\'s rim or a more challenging descent into the canyon on steep, rocky trails.','2025-03-28 01:41:07','2025-03-28 01:41:07'),(13823,'trails',337,'How can I obtain a ticket for the Full Moon Hike?','Tickets for the Full Moon Hike are obtained through a same-day in-person lottery held at the Visitor Center at 4 p.m. You must be present to participate.','2025-03-28 01:41:07','2025-03-28 01:41:07'),(13824,'trails',337,'Are there any restrictions on participants?','Children aged 7 and younger cannot join the hike. Each group must have their hiking shoes or boots inspected before receiving a lottery ticket.','2025-03-28 01:41:07','2025-03-28 01:41:07'),(13825,'trails',337,'What should I bring with me for the hike?','It\'s important to bring water and a jacket, as nighttime temperatures can get quite chilly. Additionally, make sure you have appropriate hiking footwear.','2025-03-28 01:41:07','2025-03-28 01:41:07'),(13826,'trails',337,'What are the guidelines for lighting during the hike?','Participants are not allowed to use white light flashlights or headlamps during the hike; however, red light flashlights are permitted if needed, and flash photography has specific restrictions.','2025-03-28 01:41:07','2025-03-28 01:41:07'),(13827,'trails',337,'Is the Full Moon Hike accessible for everyone?','Unfortunately, the Full Moon Hike is not wheelchair accessible due to the steep and rocky nature of the trails.','2025-03-28 01:41:08','2025-03-28 01:41:08'),(13828,'trails',337,'What happens if the weather is not suitable for the hike?','The Full Moon Hikes are canceled if weather conditions include cloudy skies or temperatures falling below 10 degrees Fahrenheit (-12°C).','2025-03-28 01:41:08','2025-03-28 01:41:08'),(13829,'trails',337,'When are the scheduled Full Moon Hikes for 2023?','Full Moon Hikes are scheduled for January 4, February 4, March 7, May 5, June 3, July 3, August 1, September 29, November 27, and December 26 in 2023, with no hikes scheduled in April and October.','2025-03-28 01:41:08','2025-03-28 01:41:08'),(13830,'trails',337,'How can I get more information about the Full Moon Hike?','For more details about the Full Moon Hike lottery and other inquiries, you can contact us at brca_information@nps.gov.','2025-03-28 01:41:08','2025-03-28 01:41:08'),(13831,'trails',338,'What time do the evening programs at Bryce Canyon National Park start?','Evening programs at Bryce Canyon National Park begin at 8:30 p.m.','2025-03-28 01:41:14','2025-03-28 01:41:14'),(13832,'trails',338,'Where do the evening programs take place?','These programs are held in the historic Bryce Canyon Lodge auditorium.','2025-03-28 01:41:14','2025-03-28 01:41:14'),(13833,'trails',338,'What topics are covered in the evening ranger programs?','Ranger programs explore a variety of themes, including navigation, the impact of nature on health, moonlight, thunderstorms, geology, adaptations, and captivating stories about the park.','2025-03-28 01:41:14','2025-03-28 01:41:14'),(13834,'trails',338,'When are the evening programs typically offered?','Evening programs are usually available from Memorial Day through Labor Day.','2025-03-28 01:41:14','2025-03-28 01:41:14'),(13835,'trails',338,'How can I find out about the specific programs available during my visit?','You can check the Calendar or visit the Visitor Center for information on the programs being offered during your stay.','2025-03-28 01:41:15','2025-03-28 01:41:15'),(13836,'trails',338,'Are dogs allowed at the evening programs?','Yes, dogs are permitted at the evening programs, but please limit it to one per visitor.','2025-03-28 01:41:15','2025-03-28 01:41:15'),(13837,'trails',338,'Is the evening program accessible?','The program is seated and fully accessible for all attendees.','2025-03-28 01:41:15','2025-03-28 01:41:15'),(13838,'trails',338,'What are some examples of topics from previous evening programs?','Some past offerings include \'Finding Your Way – Introduction to Navigation,\' \'Flower Power and the Effects of Nature on your Health and Wellbeing,\' \'The Lighter Side of the Moon,\' and \'Scary Stories to Tell in the Dark: Fire in Bryce Canyon.\'','2025-03-28 01:41:15','2025-03-28 01:41:15'),(13839,'trails',338,'Where can I find the daily topics for the evening programs?','A schedule of daily topics can be found at the Visitor Center.','2025-03-28 01:41:15','2025-03-28 01:41:15'),(13840,'trails',339,'What is the Hoodoo Geology Talk?','The Hoodoo Geology Talk is a ranger-led discussion held at Sunset Point, focusing on the formation and history of the unique hoodoo formations in Bryce Canyon and the various people who have traversed this stunning landscape.','2025-03-28 01:41:21','2025-03-28 01:41:21'),(13841,'trails',339,'Where and when does the talk take place?','This informative session occurs at Sunset Point, typically offered year-round at 11 a.m. Be sure to check the park\'s Calendar or visit the Visitor Center for the latest program details during your stay.','2025-03-28 01:41:21','2025-03-28 01:41:21'),(13842,'trails',339,'Is walking required for attending the talk?','No walking is needed to attend the Hoodoo Geology Talk, as it is held on a paved area along the rim of the Bryce Canyon Amphitheater.','2025-03-28 01:41:21','2025-03-28 01:41:21'),(13843,'trails',339,'What should I bring to the talk?','Since the talk is standing room only and does not provide seating, feel free to bring your own chair or cushion for your comfort.','2025-03-28 01:41:21','2025-03-28 01:41:21'),(13844,'trails',339,'Is the Hoodoo Geology Talk accessible to everyone?','Yes, the talk is accessible to all, as it takes place along a paved surface that does not require walking.','2025-03-28 01:41:21','2025-03-28 01:41:21'),(13845,'trails',339,'Are dogs allowed during the talk?','Yes, dogs are permitted at the Hoodoo Geology Talk, allowing you to enjoy this experience with your furry friend.','2025-03-28 01:41:21','2025-03-28 01:41:21'),(13846,'trails',339,'What makes Sunset Point a special location?','Sunset Point is renowned for its breathtaking views, offering an exceptional perspective of the amphitheaters filled with fascinating hoodoos, making it a memorable experience for visitors.','2025-03-28 01:41:21','2025-03-28 01:41:21'),(13847,'trails',339,'What geological information can I expect to learn?','Attendees will gain insights into the unique geological processes that shaped Bryce Canyon and the formation of its distinct hoodoos, as well as the history of the people who have visited this magical area.','2025-03-28 01:41:21','2025-03-28 01:41:21'),(13848,'trails',340,'What is a ranger-led snowshoe hike?','A ranger-led snowshoe hike is an organized outdoor activity where participants explore the winter landscapes of Bryce Canyon under the guidance of a park ranger, who shares insights about the environment and local wildlife.','2025-03-28 01:41:30','2025-03-28 01:41:30'),(13849,'trails',340,'What can I expect to see on this hike?','On this hike, you will encounter stunning contrasts of freshly fallen white snow, striking red rocks, expansive blue skies, and lush evergreen trees, all of which contribute to the breathtaking beauty of Bryce Canyon in winter.','2025-03-28 01:41:30','2025-03-28 01:41:30'),(13850,'trails',340,'How long is the hike?','The hike spans approximately 1 mile (1.6 km), making it accessible for participants of various fitness levels.','2025-03-28 01:41:30','2025-03-28 01:41:30'),(13851,'trails',340,'What equipment do I need?','Snowshoes and poles are provided at no cost for all participants, though it is essential to bring winter clothing, water, and waterproof boots, as tennis shoes are not allowed on the trail.','2025-03-28 01:41:30','2025-03-28 01:41:30'),(13852,'trails',340,'When and where do I sign up for the hike?','Sign-ups for the hike take place at the Visitor Center starting at 8 a.m. on the day of the program, and registration continues until the hike is fully booked. Advance reservations are not available.','2025-03-28 01:41:30','2025-03-28 01:41:30'),(13853,'trails',340,'Is this hike suitable for everyone?','The snowshoe hike is designed for hikers of all experience levels, from beginners to experts, ensuring that everyone can enjoy the winter scenery.','2025-03-28 01:41:30','2025-03-28 01:41:30'),(13854,'trails',340,'Is the hike ADA accessible?','Unfortunately, due to the nature of the snowshoe hike, it is not ADA accessible.','2025-03-28 01:41:30','2025-03-28 01:41:30'),(13855,'trails',340,'Can I bring my dog on the hike?','Yes, dogs are permitted on this hike, but it\'s advisable to check specific regulations before bringing your pet.','2025-03-28 01:41:30','2025-03-28 01:41:30'),(13856,'trails',340,'What should I check before my visit?','It\'s a good idea to check the Calendar or visit the Visitor Center for information about available programs during your stay, as offerings may vary.','2025-03-28 01:41:30','2025-03-28 01:41:30'),(13857,'trails',340,'What elevation is Bryce Canyon at?','Bryce Canyon is situated at an elevation of 8,000 feet (2,438 meters), where the winter scenery transforms beautifully compared to other seasons.','2025-03-28 01:41:31','2025-03-28 01:41:31'),(13858,'trails',341,'Where can I have a picnic along the Southern Scenic Drive?','The CCC Picnic Area, located at mile 4.75 of the Southern Scenic Drive, is a great spot to enjoy your picnic surrounded by breathtaking views.','2025-03-28 01:41:36','2025-03-28 01:41:36'),(13859,'trails',341,'What are the picnic areas available in Bryce Canyon?','You can find several picnic areas in Bryce Canyon, including the Amphitheater Area (Miles 1-3), North Campground Picnic Area, General Store, Sunset Point, CCC Picnic Area, Whiteman Bench Picnic Area, and Rainbow Point.','2025-03-28 01:41:36','2025-03-28 01:41:36'),(13860,'trails',341,'Are there any restrictions on wildlife at picnic areas?','Yes, it\'s essential to follow federal regulations, which prohibit feeding wildlife in the park. Also, be cautious around these animals, as they can be dangerous if approached.','2025-03-28 01:41:36','2025-03-28 01:41:36'),(13861,'trails',341,'What is the accessibility of the picnic areas?','All picnic areas consist of unpaved surfaces made of compact native sediment. Although generally hard packed, these areas might become muddy and challenging to traverse after rain or snow. They are conveniently located next to paved sidewalks and parking areas.','2025-03-28 01:41:36','2025-03-28 01:41:36'),(13862,'trails',341,'Are dogs allowed in the picnic areas?','Yes, you are permitted to bring dogs to the picnic areas, but remember to keep them leashed and supervise them closely.','2025-03-28 01:41:36','2025-03-28 01:41:36'),(13863,'trails',341,'What are the coordinates for the CCC Picnic Area?','The CCC Picnic Area can be found at the geographical coordinates of 37.6067 latitude and -112.2 longitude.','2025-03-28 01:41:36','2025-03-28 01:41:36'),(13864,'trails',342,'What trails can I access from Bryce Point?','Bryce Point serves as a starting point for several trails, including the Hat Shop Peekaboo Loop, the Hat Shop trail itself, and the Under-the-Rim trail.','2025-03-28 01:41:46','2025-03-28 01:41:46'),(13865,'trails',342,'What is the difficulty level of the Hat Shop trail?','The Hat Shop trail is categorized as strenuous due to its significant elevation gain and the longer hike duration.','2025-03-28 01:41:46','2025-03-28 01:41:46'),(13866,'trails',342,'What are the total distance and elevation gain for the Hat Shop trail?','The trail is approximately 4.0 miles (6.4 km) roundtrip and involves a considerable elevation drop of 1,380 feet (421 meters).','2025-03-28 01:41:46','2025-03-28 01:41:46'),(13867,'trails',342,'How long does it typically take to hike the Hat Shop trail?','Hikers can expect to spend around 3 to 4 hours completing the hike.','2025-03-28 01:41:46','2025-03-28 01:41:46'),(13868,'trails',342,'What type of scenery can I expect on the Hat Shop trail?','As you hike down the trail, you\'ll be treated to breathtaking views of the vibrant cliffs of the Grand Staircase and unique hoodoos topped with large gray boulders.','2025-03-28 01:41:46','2025-03-28 01:41:46'),(13869,'trails',342,'Are there any amenities along the Hat Shop trail?','There are no services available on this trail, so it\'s essential to come prepared with everything you need.','2025-03-28 01:41:46','2025-03-28 01:41:46'),(13870,'trails',342,'Is there a shuttle service available for this trail?','Yes, a shuttle service operates during specific times, but it is worth noting that oversized vehicles are not allowed in the parking area when the shuttle is in service.','2025-03-28 01:41:47','2025-03-28 01:41:47'),(13871,'trails',342,'Can I hike the Hat Shop trail during winter?','Winter hiking on the Hat Shop trail is not recommended unless you are exceptionally well-prepared for challenging winter conditions, including ice and deep snow.','2025-03-28 01:41:47','2025-03-28 01:41:47'),(13872,'trails',342,'Are pets allowed on the Hat Shop trail?','Pets are not permitted on this trail; however, service animals are allowed in national parks.','2025-03-28 01:41:47','2025-03-28 01:41:47'),(13873,'trails',342,'Is the Hat Shop trail accessible for individuals with mobility challenges?','Due to the natural ruggedness of the terrain, this trail is not considered accessible for individuals with mobility constraints.','2025-03-28 01:41:47','2025-03-28 01:41:47'),(13874,'trails',342,'What should I know about the terrain of the Hat Shop trail?','The surface of the trail consists of firm native sediment, featuring varying slopes and grades throughout your hike.','2025-03-28 01:41:47','2025-03-28 01:41:47'),(13875,'trails',342,'What are the coordinates for Bryce Point?','The geographical coordinates for Bryce Point are approximately 37.6043 latitude and -112.157 longitude.','2025-03-28 01:41:47','2025-03-28 01:41:47'),(13876,'trails',343,'What is the Southern Scenic Drive?','The Southern Scenic Drive is an 18-mile stretch of the main park road in Bryce Canyon that offers breathtaking views from 9 unique viewpoints, showcasing the stunning geologic features and vast landscapes of the Paria Valley and the Grand Staircase.','2025-03-28 01:41:57','2025-03-28 01:41:57'),(13877,'trails',343,'How long does it take to drive the Southern Scenic Drive?','Driving the entire Southern Scenic Drive from the Visitor Center typically takes about 40 minutes. It’s advisable to start at Rainbow and Yovimpa Points and then explore the viewpoints on the way back, making for a smoother and safer experience.','2025-03-28 01:41:57','2025-03-28 01:41:57'),(13878,'trails',343,'What are some must-see viewpoints along the drive?','Rainbow Point, Yovimpa Point, Agua Canyon, and Natural Bridge are highly recommended overlooks that you shouldn’t miss while driving along the Southern Scenic Drive.','2025-03-28 01:41:57','2025-03-28 01:41:57'),(13879,'trails',343,'What elevation changes can be expected on the Southern Scenic Drive?','The elevation increases significantly as you travel south on the drive. The Visitor Center is at 7,894 feet (2,406 m), while Rainbow and Yovimpa Points surpass 9,000 feet (2,743 m), showcasing dramatic views due to this elevation change.','2025-03-28 01:41:58','2025-03-28 01:41:58'),(13880,'trails',343,'Are there any winter closures to consider?','Yes, the high elevations can lead to temporary winter closures at Mile 3, so it is essential to check the Conditions page for the latest information regarding road access during the winter months.','2025-03-28 01:41:58','2025-03-28 01:41:58'),(13881,'trails',343,'How long should I plan for a trip along the Southern Scenic Drive?','A full trip primarily focused on driving and enjoying the viewpoints typically takes around 2 to 3 hours, ensuring ample time to relish the views without rushing.','2025-03-28 01:41:58','2025-03-28 01:41:58'),(13882,'trails',343,'What wildlife might I see along the Southern Scenic Drive?','The area provides opportunities for wildlife viewing, with sightings of species such as elk, black bears, mule deer, and various birds like Clark\'s nutcrackers and peregrine falcons as you explore the different viewpoints.','2025-03-28 01:41:59','2025-03-28 01:41:59'),(13883,'trails',343,'Is any hiking required to enjoy the viewpoints?','No significant hiking is necessary, as all viewpoints are within a short walk from the parking areas. However, to appreciate the spectacular views, visitors are encouraged to walk the brief distances to the overlook railings.','2025-03-28 01:41:59','2025-03-28 01:41:59'),(13884,'trails',343,'Are there hiking trails available near the Southern Scenic Drive?','Yes, there are two popular hiking options: the easy Bristlecone Loop at Rainbow and Yovimpa Points, which typically takes about an hour, and the Swamp Canyon Loop at Swamp Canyon overlook, which usually takes 3 to 4 hours. Additionally, the Under-the-Rim Trail offers more extensive backcountry hiking opportunities.','2025-03-28 01:41:59','2025-03-28 01:41:59'),(13885,'trails',343,'Are the viewpoints accessible for everyone?','All viewpoints along the Southern Scenic Drive have paved paths that ensure relatively flat access, except for Piracy Point, which involves a flat, unpaved 1,000-foot (39m) path that is reasonable to navigate when dry.','2025-03-28 01:41:59','2025-03-28 01:41:59'),(13886,'trails',343,'Are dogs allowed along the Southern Scenic Drive?','Yes, dogs are allowed on the Southern Scenic Drive, making it a great outing for pet owners.','2025-03-28 01:41:59','2025-03-28 01:41:59'),(13887,'trails',344,'How can I become a Junior Ranger at Bryce Canyon National Park?','To become a Junior Ranger at Bryce Canyon, you need to complete two main tasks: First, learn about the park by visiting the park museum, attending a ranger-led presentation or hike, or watching the informative park movie. Second, utilize an activity booklet tailored to your age, completing a number of activities that corresponds to your age (complete as many activities as you are years old). After fulfilling these requirements, return to the Visitor Center for your official induction as a Junior Ranger, where you will receive a free badge. There are also unique souvenirs available for purchase in the park bookstore.','2025-03-28 01:42:10','2025-03-28 01:42:10'),(13888,'trails',344,'Where can I obtain the Junior Ranger booklet?','You can obtain your Junior Ranger booklet at the Visitor Center front desk, where the rangers will provide it to you along with your badge once you complete the requirements. Alternatively, you can download the Bryce Canyon Junior Ranger booklet [PDF 6.4 MB] to start your activities as soon as you arrive at the park. Printed copies are also available at the Visitor Center.','2025-03-28 01:42:10','2025-03-28 01:42:10'),(13889,'trails',344,'What should I do if I get stuck on an activity in the booklet?','If you\'re having trouble with any activity in the Junior Ranger booklet, you can find hints and helpful suggestions on our dedicated Junior Ranger webpage. Additionally, feel free to reach out to a ranger via email for further assistance.','2025-03-28 01:42:10','2025-03-28 01:42:10'),(13890,'trails',344,'Can I complete the Junior Ranger booklet from home?','Yes, you can complete the Junior Ranger booklet from home! Once finished, take a photo of your favorite page or activity with an adult\'s signature verifying your completion. Email this photo to brca_information@nps.gov, and include your mailing address. We’d also love to hear what you enjoyed about the activity! Please note that you should not mail your booklet; mailed books will not be returned.','2025-03-28 01:42:11','2025-03-28 01:42:11'),(13891,'trails',344,'What will I receive after completing the Junior Ranger booklet from home?','After your submission, you will receive an official Junior Ranger sticker badge by mail. Due to shipping costs, we only provide the gold foil sticker badge; however, if you wish for a wooden badge, you will need to send a pre-paid bubble envelope with first-class postage to the park.','2025-03-28 01:42:11','2025-03-28 01:42:11'),(13892,'trails',344,'What is the mailing address for sending the pre-paid envelope for a wooden badge?','You can mail your pre-paid envelope to: Bryce Canyon National Park, PO Box 640201, Bryce, UT 84764. Make sure to use a padded bubble envelope, as regular envelopes will not be accepted by USPS.','2025-03-28 01:42:11','2025-03-28 01:42:11'),(13893,'trails',344,'Are there any accessibility options for the Junior Ranger booklet?','Yes, a 508-compliant version of the Junior Ranger booklet is available online, ensuring accessibility for all visitors.','2025-03-28 01:42:11','2025-03-28 01:42:11'),(13894,'trails',344,'Are dogs allowed on the Junior Ranger activities?','Yes, you are allowed to bring one dog with you while participating in the Junior Ranger activities at Bryce Canyon.','2025-03-28 01:42:11','2025-03-28 01:42:11'),(13895,'trails',344,'Where can I find more information about Junior Ranger programs at other national parks?','For information on other Junior Ranger programs throughout the national park system, check our website which provides additional resources about similar programs in different parks.','2025-03-28 01:42:11','2025-03-28 01:42:11'),(13896,'trails',345,'What is the total distance of the Under-the-Rim Trail?','The Under-the-Rim Trail spans a total distance of 22.9 miles (36.9 km).','2025-03-28 01:42:25','2025-03-28 01:42:25'),(13897,'trails',345,'What distinguishes the scenery along the Under-the-Rim Trail?','This trail features beautiful views of vibrant, rainbow-colored cliffs and passes through scenic forests and meadows.','2025-03-28 01:42:27','2025-03-28 01:42:27'),(13898,'trails',345,'What type of camping is allowed on the Under-the-Rim Trail?','Backcountry camping is permitted, but only in designated campsites to minimize impact on the environment.','2025-03-28 01:42:27','2025-03-28 01:42:27'),(13899,'trails',345,'How can I obtain a backcountry camping permit for the Under-the-Rim Trail?','You can obtain a backcountry permit at the Visitor Center prior to any overnight trips.','2025-03-28 01:42:27','2025-03-28 01:42:27'),(13900,'trails',345,'How many campsites are there on the Under-the-Rim Trail?','There are a total of 7 designated campsites along the Under-the-Rim Trail, although Sheep Creek campsite is currently closed.','2025-03-28 01:42:27','2025-03-28 01:42:27'),(13901,'trails',345,'What is the difficulty level of the Under-the-Rim Trail?','The Under-the-Rim Trail is classified as strenuous, featuring significant elevation changes and rugged terrain.','2025-03-28 01:42:27','2025-03-28 01:42:27'),(13902,'trails',345,'What is the elevation range on the Under-the-Rim Trail?','The elevation on the trail varies from 6,800 feet (2,073 meters) to 9,115 feet (2,778 meters).','2025-03-28 01:42:27','2025-03-28 01:42:27'),(13903,'trails',345,'How long does it typically take to hike the Under-the-Rim Trail?','Most hikers complete the Under-the-Rim Trail in an average of 2-3 days.','2025-03-28 01:42:27','2025-03-28 01:42:27'),(13904,'trails',345,'Is the Under-the-Rim Trail accessible in winter?','The trail may not be accessible during mid-winter due to snow depths that can range from 2 to 15 feet (0.7 to 5 meters).','2025-03-28 01:42:28','2025-03-28 01:42:28'),(13905,'trails',345,'What are the average hiking times for the Riggs Spring Loop Trail?','The Riggs Spring Loop Trail is approximately 8.8 miles (14.2 km) long and typically takes between 4-6 hours to complete.','2025-03-28 01:42:28','2025-03-28 01:42:28'),(13906,'trails',345,'Are there any fireplace restrictions on the Under-the-Rim Trail?','Open fires are not allowed anywhere in the park except in the established fire rings at North and Sunset Campgrounds, but you can use gas-powered cooking stoves.','2025-03-28 01:42:28','2025-03-28 01:42:28'),(13907,'trails',345,'What wildlife might I encounter along the Under-the-Rim Trail?','In addition to small animals like squirrels and snakes, hikers may encounter larger wildlife such as mountain lions, coyotes, and black bears.','2025-03-28 01:42:28','2025-03-28 01:42:28'),(13908,'trails',345,'How can I ensure my food is safe from bears while camping?','It\'s highly recommended to use bear-resistant food canisters when hiking overnight, which are available for free loan at the Visitor Center.','2025-03-28 01:42:28','2025-03-28 01:42:28'),(13909,'trails',345,'Is there a transportation option available for accessing the trailhead?','Yes, when available, hikers can reserve seats on the Rainbow Point Tour bus to access Rainbow and Yovimpa Points, but this service operates seasonally.','2025-03-28 01:42:28','2025-03-28 01:42:28'),(13910,'trails',345,'Are dogs allowed on the Under-the-Rim Trail?','Yes, dogs are allowed on the Under-the-Rim Trail, but they must be kept on a leash.','2025-03-28 01:42:28','2025-03-28 01:42:28'),(13911,'trails',345,'Is the Under-the-Rim Trail accessible for those with mobility challenges?','No, the park\'s backcountry trails are very rugged and are not considered accessible.','2025-03-28 01:42:28','2025-03-28 01:42:28'),(13912,'trails',346,'What is the film \'A Song of Seasons\' about?','The film \'A Song of Seasons\' features stunning visuals and engaging narration that highlights the natural beauty of the area.','2025-03-28 01:42:35','2025-03-28 01:42:35'),(13913,'trails',346,'When can I watch \'A Song of Seasons\'?','\'A Song of Seasons\' is shown in the Visitor Center theater every half hour during operating hours.','2025-03-28 01:42:36','2025-03-28 01:42:36'),(13914,'trails',346,'Is there an online option to view the film?','Yes, you can also watch \'A Song of Seasons\' online.','2025-03-28 01:42:36','2025-03-28 01:42:36'),(13915,'trails',346,'Are there accessibility features for the film?','The film includes captions and assisted listening devices are available upon request. Additionally, the theater is fully accessible.','2025-03-28 01:42:36','2025-03-28 01:42:36'),(13916,'trails',346,'Are dogs allowed in the Visitor Center theater?','Yes, one dog is permitted in the Visitor Center theater.','2025-03-28 01:42:36','2025-03-28 01:42:36'),(13917,'trails',346,'What are the geographical coordinates of the trail?','The trail is located at approximately 37.6401° latitude and -112.17° longitude.','2025-03-28 01:42:36','2025-03-28 01:42:36'),(13918,'trails',347,'What are some easy hikes available in the park?','The park features several easy trails including the Mossy Cave, which is 0.8 miles (1.3 km), the scenic Sunset to Sunrise along the Rim Trail at 1.0 mile (1.6 km), and the unique Bristlecone Loop, also at 1.0 mile (1.6 km).','2025-03-28 01:42:51','2025-03-28 01:42:51'),(13919,'trails',347,'What is the elevation like in this park?','Most of the park sits at an elevation of 8,000 feet (2,438 m) or higher, which significantly affects the available oxygen, providing only about 70% of what you would find at sea level. This means you might feel the effects if you push your limits.','2025-03-28 01:42:51','2025-03-28 01:42:51'),(13920,'trails',347,'What precautions should hikers take due to the high elevation?','It\'s important to choose hikes within your comfort zone and take it slow since even short trails can be incredibly rewarding. Be aware that at this elevation, altitude-related health issues can occur, so listen to your body.','2025-03-28 01:42:51','2025-03-28 01:42:51'),(13921,'trails',347,'What are the UV radiation concerns in this park?','At higher elevations, UV radiation is more intense, so it\'s crucial to protect your skin and eyes. Wear sunscreen, sunglasses, and protective clothing to minimize exposure.','2025-03-28 01:42:51','2025-03-28 01:42:51'),(13922,'trails',347,'What should I do if a storm approaches while hiking?','Storms can develop rapidly in this area, so if you hear thunder, it\'s best to seek shelter immediately. Avoid tall structures like trees, and instead, look for lower spots or vehicle shelter when lightning is a threat.','2025-03-28 01:42:52','2025-03-28 01:42:52'),(13923,'trails',347,'How much water should I bring on a hike?','Given the altitude, your body will need more hydration as you\'ll dehydrate quicker. It\'s advisable to carry about one liter of water for every 1-2 hours of hiking, as there are no water sources on the trails.','2025-03-28 01:42:52','2025-03-28 01:42:52'),(13924,'trails',347,'What type of footwear is recommended for hiking in the park?','Proper footwear is essential to navigate the trails safely, as many have loose rocks that can cause slips and injuries. Opt for shoes with good tread and ankle support, especially since icy conditions in winter can further increase hazards.','2025-03-28 01:42:52','2025-03-28 01:42:52'),(13925,'trails',347,'Are there accessible trails in the park?','Yes, the park offers an accessible section of the Rim Trail, specifically the 0.5-mile (0.8 km) Sunset to Sunrise trail. Other trails may have varying accessibility standards.','2025-03-28 01:42:52','2025-03-28 01:42:52'),(13926,'trails',347,'Are dogs allowed on the trails?','Yes, you are welcome to bring your dog along on the trails in the park!','2025-03-28 01:42:52','2025-03-28 01:42:52'),(13927,'trails',348,'Where can I collect a cancellation stamp for my passport at Bryce Canyon?','You can obtain your cancellation stamp at the passport counter situated in the back right corner of the Visitor Center.','2025-03-28 01:42:57','2025-03-28 01:42:57'),(13928,'trails',348,'What is the purpose of the cancellation stamp at Bryce Canyon?','The cancellation stamp serves as a unique keepsake to commemorate your visit to Bryce Canyon, allowing you to mark it in your passport book.','2025-03-28 01:42:58','2025-03-28 01:42:58'),(13929,'trails',348,'Is the Bryce Canyon Visitor Center accessible?','Yes, the Visitor Center at Bryce Canyon is fully accessible for all visitors.','2025-03-28 01:42:58','2025-03-28 01:42:58'),(13930,'trails',348,'Are dogs allowed in Bryce Canyon?','Yes, you can bring one dog with you in certain areas of Bryce Canyon.','2025-03-28 01:42:58','2025-03-28 01:42:58'),(13931,'trails',348,'What are the geographical coordinates of Bryce Canyon?','Bryce Canyon is located at a latitude of 37.6404 and a longitude of -112.17.','2025-03-28 01:42:58','2025-03-28 01:42:58'),(13932,'trails',349,'What is the \'Hike the Hoodoos!\' program?','The \'Hike the Hoodoos!\' program is an engaging activity in Bryce Canyon National Park that combines hiking with a scavenger hunt. Participants must hike at least 3 miles on designated trails and locate benchmark survey markers to earn a special reward.','2025-03-28 01:43:07','2025-03-28 01:43:07'),(13933,'trails',349,'What do I need to do to earn a reward?','To earn a reward, you need to hike a minimum of 3 miles and find at least one of the \'Hike the Hoodoos\' benchmark markers. You can demonstrate your achievement by collecting rubbings or taking photos with the markers and presenting them to a ranger at the Visitor Center.','2025-03-28 01:43:07','2025-03-28 01:43:07'),(13934,'trails',349,'How many benchmarks are there and where can I find them?','There are nine \'Hike the Hoodoos!\' benchmarks located along eight different hiking trails in the park. While only 3 miles of hiking is required for a reward, many hikers enjoy collecting photos or rubbings from all nine benchmarks, totaling 18.4 miles.','2025-03-28 01:43:07','2025-03-28 01:43:07'),(13935,'trails',349,'What are the trails featured in the program?','The program’s benchmarks can be found on the following trails: Mossy Cave (0.8 mi), Bristlecone Loop (1.0 mi), Queen\'s Garden (1.8 mi), Navajo Loop (1.3 mi), Tower Bridge (3.0 mi), Swamp Canyon Loop (4.0 mi), Peekaboo Loop (5.5 mi), and Fairyland Loop (8.0 mi).','2025-03-28 01:43:07','2025-03-28 01:43:07'),(13936,'trails',349,'Can I combine hikes to earn more benchmarks?','Yes! Hikers often combine the Queen\'s Garden and Navajo Loop trails into a single hike of approximately 3 miles to collect two benchmarks and claim the reward.','2025-03-28 01:43:07','2025-03-28 01:43:07'),(13937,'trails',349,'Are the trails accessible for everyone?','The trails are not wheelchair accessible as they include uneven surfaces, steep grades, and loose rocks. However, service animals are allowed on all included trails.','2025-03-28 01:43:07','2025-03-28 01:43:07'),(13938,'trails',349,'Are dogs allowed on the trails?','Yes, dogs are allowed on the trails, but it\'s important to keep them on a leash and under control.','2025-03-28 01:43:07','2025-03-28 01:43:07'),(13939,'trails',349,'Who sponsored the \'Hike the Hoodoos!\' program?','The \'Hike the Hoodoos!\' program received support from the National Park Foundation, thanks to the generous backing of the Coca-Cola Foundation.','2025-03-28 01:43:08','2025-03-28 01:43:08'),(13940,'trails',350,'What wildlife can I expect to see in Bryce Canyon National Park?','Hikers in Bryce Canyon National Park can observe various wildlife, including migratory hummingbirds, nesting Peregrine Falcons, Rocky Mountain Elk, and Pronghorn, all of which traverse the park\'s canyons, plateaus, and forested regions.','2025-03-28 01:43:17','2025-03-28 01:43:17'),(13941,'trails',350,'What should I know about wildlife safety in the park?','It\'s important to treat wildlife with respect as you are in their habitat. Avoid feeding any wild animals, as this can lead to harmful behaviors and can be dangerous for you. Maintain a safe distance and use binoculars or telephoto lenses for closer views. When exploring areas where venomous snakes may be present, wear protective clothing and be cautious of your surroundings.','2025-03-28 01:43:17','2025-03-28 01:43:17'),(13942,'trails',350,'How should I handle food and attractants while hiking?','To avoid attracting wildlife, hang food and any scented items, like toiletries, at least 10 feet off the ground and 6 feet from tree trunks, or use bear-proof containers. Never store food inside your tent.','2025-03-28 01:43:17','2025-03-28 01:43:17'),(13943,'trails',350,'What should I do if I encounter a bear or mountain lion?','If you encounter a bear, back away slowly without making direct eye contact, but maintain eye contact with a mountain lion. Do not run. Raise your arms to appear larger, make noise, and throw rocks or sticks if necessary.','2025-03-28 01:43:17','2025-03-28 01:43:17'),(13944,'trails',350,'When is the best time to see wildlife in the park?','Spring is a transition time as snow typically lingers into April at higher elevations. While some animals, like Mule Deer, can be seen year-round, others like Pronghorn are absent in winter and return with the melting snow. Utah Prairie Dogs come out of hibernation in late winter, while many wildlife sightings increase during the warmer months.','2025-03-28 01:43:17','2025-03-28 01:43:17'),(13945,'trails',350,'Where can I find Utah Prairie Dog colonies in the park?','You can find Utah Prairie Dog colonies near their burrows in the meadows south of the Visitor Center, as well as on the right side of the road around Mile 2. Another colony is on the route to Sunrise Point after the second left turn past the Visitor Center. Observe these colonies from a distance to avoid potential dangers.','2025-03-28 01:43:18','2025-03-28 01:43:18'),(13946,'trails',350,'What areas are known for wildlife viewing in the park?','Wildlife can frequently be seen along the Southern Scenic Drive, particularly in meadows around Mile 4, and at Bryce Amphitheater, where you\'ll find chipmunks, ground squirrels, and mule deer. Stargazing at Sunset Point may also reward you with a glimpse of a ringtail.','2025-03-28 01:43:18','2025-03-28 01:43:18'),(13947,'trails',350,'Are there accessible viewpoints for viewing wildlife?','Yes, the viewpoints in the park offer paved, flat surfaces that are accessible to all visitors. However, trail accessibility may vary, so check the park\'s Accessibility page for more detailed information.','2025-03-28 01:43:18','2025-03-28 01:43:18'),(13948,'trails',350,'Are dogs allowed in Bryce Canyon National Park?','Yes, dogs are permitted in the park, but be sure to follow all guidelines and leash regulations to ensure a safe and enjoyable visit for everyone.','2025-03-28 01:43:18','2025-03-28 01:43:18'),(13949,'trails',351,'What types of birds can I expect to see in Bryce Canyon National Park?','Bryce Canyon National Park is home to over 175 bird species, including western bluebirds, American robins, hummingbirds, and Townsend\'s solitaires. Some birds are seasonal visitors, while others stay year-round, offering a delightful sight for birdwatchers.','2025-03-28 01:43:27','2025-03-28 01:43:27'),(13950,'trails',351,'When is the best time to view birds at Bryce Canyon?','Spring brings the return of migratory birds like western bluebirds and American robins starting in late February and March. Warblers and hummingbirds follow in late spring, making May to July the peak breeding season. Year-round residents can be seen throughout winter.','2025-03-28 01:43:27','2025-03-28 01:43:27'),(13951,'trails',351,'Where are the best spots for birdwatching within the park?','Key birdwatching locations include the Southern Scenic Drive, Bryce Amphitheater, Mossy Cave, and the Tropic Trail. Each area has unique habitats, attracting various bird species throughout the year.','2025-03-28 01:43:27','2025-03-28 01:43:27'),(13952,'trails',351,'What bird species can I spot along the Southern Scenic Drive?','While traveling along the Southern Scenic Drive, you might encounter species like dusky grouse, peregrine falcons, and Clark\'s nutcracker, especially in the high-elevation conifer woodlands.','2025-03-28 01:43:27','2025-03-28 01:43:27'),(13953,'trails',351,'What makes the Bryce Amphitheater a good birdwatching location?','The Bryce Amphitheater\'s ponderosa forests host a variety of birds such as pygmy nuthatches and violet-green swallows. Keep an ear out for songbirds, and you might spot owls or other interesting species along the rim trails.','2025-03-28 01:43:27','2025-03-28 01:43:27'),(13954,'trails',351,'What wildlife can I find at Mossy Cave?','Mossy Cave is one of the few places in the park with consistent water, attracting a variety of birds. Look for flycatchers and warblers in the nearby Gambel oak and Nootka rose areas.','2025-03-28 01:43:27','2025-03-28 01:43:27'),(13955,'trails',351,'What is special about the Tropic Trail?','The Tropic Trail is a hidden gem in the park, featuring lush vegetation. It’s an ideal spot for observing towhees, jays, and other birds, including occasional visitors from lower elevations.','2025-03-28 01:43:28','2025-03-28 01:43:28'),(13956,'trails',351,'Are there birdwatching opportunities outside of the park?','Yes, just north of the park in Bryce Canyon City, you can explore open fields and waterpond areas that attract a variety of birds, including larks and raptors.','2025-03-28 01:43:28','2025-03-28 01:43:28'),(13957,'trails',351,'Is the park accessible for everyone?','Yes, many viewpoints in the park are designed with accessible, paved pathways. However, trail accessibility can vary. For more details, please visit the park’s Accessibility page.','2025-03-28 01:43:28','2025-03-28 01:43:28'),(13958,'trails',351,'Are dogs allowed on the trails?','Dogs are allowed on a limited basis in certain areas of the park, so check local guidelines for specifics about where they can accompany you.','2025-03-28 01:43:28','2025-03-28 01:43:28'),(13959,'trails',352,'What trails can I snowshoe on in Bryce Canyon National Park?','You can snowshoe on all trails throughout the park, but popular choices include the Rim Trail, Bristlecone Loop, Fairyland Road, and Paria Road.','2025-03-28 01:43:38','2025-03-28 01:43:38'),(13960,'trails',352,'What are the snow conditions needed for snowshoeing in the park?','Snowshoeing in Bryce Canyon is ideal when there is at least 12 inches of snow on the ground.','2025-03-28 01:43:38','2025-03-28 01:43:38'),(13961,'trails',352,'Is there an organized snowshoeing activity I can join?','Yes! You can participate in free ranger-led snowshoe hikes, which are suitable for all experience levels, provided there is sufficient snow.','2025-03-28 01:43:38','2025-03-28 01:43:38'),(13962,'trails',352,'What is the duration and distance of the ranger-led snowshoe hikes?','These hikes typically last around 2 hours and cover approximately 1 mile (1.6 km).','2025-03-28 01:43:38','2025-03-28 01:43:38'),(13963,'trails',352,'Is there a fee to join the ranger-led snowshoe hikes?','No, there is no fee to participate in the ranger-led snowshoe hikes; they are offered for free.','2025-03-28 01:43:38','2025-03-28 01:43:38'),(13964,'trails',352,'What is the minimum age requirement for the ranger-led snowshoe hikes?','Participants must be at least 8 years old to join the ranger-led snowshoe hikes.','2025-03-28 01:43:38','2025-03-28 01:43:38'),(13965,'trails',352,'What equipment do I need to bring for snowshoeing?','You should wear winter clothing, bring enough water, and wear waterproof boots. The park provides snowshoes and poles for free during ranger-led programs.','2025-03-28 01:43:38','2025-03-28 01:43:38'),(13966,'trails',352,'How do I sign up for the ranger-led snowshoe hikes?','Registration is required for these hikes due to limited group sizes. You can sign up at the Visitor Center starting at 8 a.m. on the day of the hike, while spots remain available. Advance reservations are not accepted.','2025-03-28 01:43:38','2025-03-28 01:43:38'),(13967,'trails',352,'Where can I rent snowshoes or cross-country skis?','You can rent snowshoes and cross-country skis from Ruby\'s Inn, located in Bryce Canyon City outside the park.','2025-03-28 01:43:39','2025-03-28 01:43:39'),(13968,'trails',352,'What is a full moon snowshoe hike?','A full moon snowshoe hike is a unique ranger-led program that takes place during full moon nights, depending on weather conditions. Check the full moon hike calendar for availability.','2025-03-28 01:43:39','2025-03-28 01:43:39'),(13969,'trails',352,'Is snowshoeing accessible for everyone?','While snowshoeing is not inherently accessible, the park strives to make accommodations wherever possible.','2025-03-28 01:43:39','2025-03-28 01:43:39'),(13970,'trails',352,'Are dogs allowed on the snowshoeing trails?','Yes, dogs are permitted on the snowshoeing trails, but you should bring only one dog per participant.','2025-03-28 01:43:39','2025-03-28 01:43:39'),(13971,'trails',353,'What can I learn from the Native Perspectives video at the Visitor Center?','The Native Perspectives video, which runs for 24 minutes, provides valuable insights into the area\'s history and significance from the viewpoint of Native communities.','2025-03-28 01:43:47','2025-03-28 01:43:47'),(13972,'trails',353,'What exhibits can I find in the park museum at the Visitor Center?','The park museum features a variety of exhibits that explore geological, ecological, and human timelines, along with special displays focusing on the Night Sky and Air Quality.','2025-03-28 01:43:47','2025-03-28 01:43:47'),(13973,'trails',353,'Is the museum helpful for Jr. Ranger activities?','Absolutely! The museum is an excellent resource for those working on their Jr. Ranger book, as it contains answers to many activities, including the Prairie Dog crossword puzzle.','2025-03-28 01:43:47','2025-03-28 01:43:47'),(13974,'trails',353,'How accessible is the Visitor Center for individuals with mobility challenges?','The Visitor Center is designed to be accessible, featuring two ramps with moderate slopes leading from the parking lot, a lowered information desk, and a fully accessible auditorium where a captioned 24-minute film is shown.','2025-03-28 01:43:47','2025-03-28 01:43:47'),(13975,'trails',353,'Are there any assistive devices available in the Visitor Center?','Yes, assistive listening devices and audio description devices can be requested at the front desk to enhance your experience.','2025-03-28 01:43:47','2025-03-28 01:43:47'),(13976,'trails',353,'What facilities are available for visitors with disabilities?','The restrooms at the Visitor Center are equipped with fully-accessible stalls to accommodate visitors\' needs.','2025-03-28 01:43:47','2025-03-28 01:43:47'),(13977,'trails',353,'Are dogs allowed at the Visitor Center?','Yes, dogs are permitted at the Visitor Center, but please remember to keep them leashed.','2025-03-28 01:43:47','2025-03-28 01:43:47'),(13978,'trails',353,'What are the geographical coordinates of the Visitor Center?','The Visitor Center is located at a latitude of 37.6401 and a longitude of -112.17.','2025-03-28 01:43:47','2025-03-28 01:43:47'),(13979,'trails',354,'What is the Rim Trail at Bryce Canyon National Park?','The Rim Trail offers stunning views as it connects key viewpoints like Bryce Point, Inspiration Point, Sunset Point, Sunrise Point, and Fairyland Point. It provides a gradual hike through some of the park\'s most scenic areas.','2025-03-28 01:43:56','2025-03-28 01:43:56'),(13980,'trails',354,'How long is the Rim Trail?','The Rim Trail spans 5.5 miles (8.9 km) starting from Bryce Point in the south to Fairyland Point in the north.','2025-03-28 01:43:56','2025-03-28 01:43:56'),(13981,'trails',354,'What is the easiest hike on the Rim Trail?','The easiest hike is the 0.5-mile (0.8 km) stretch between Sunset and Sunrise Points, with minimal elevation gain, making it ideal for a short and pleasant walk.','2025-03-28 01:43:56','2025-03-28 01:43:56'),(13982,'trails',354,'What is the elevation gain for the hike between Sunset and Sunrise Points?','The elevation gain for the section between Sunset and Sunrise Points is just 34 feet (10 meters).','2025-03-28 01:43:57','2025-03-28 01:43:57'),(13983,'trails',354,'What is the total elevation change when hiking the entire Rim Trail?','Hiking the entire Rim Trail involves an elevation ascent of 1,330 feet (405 m) and a descent of 1,825 feet (556 m).','2025-03-28 01:43:57','2025-03-28 01:43:57'),(13984,'trails',354,'How long does it typically take to hike the Rim Trail?','Plan for approximately 3 to 4 hours to complete the Rim Trail, depending on your hiking speed and how many viewpoints you stop to enjoy.','2025-03-28 01:43:57','2025-03-28 01:43:57'),(13985,'trails',354,'Are there any sections of the trail that are closed during winter?','Yes, the 1.5-mile (2.4 km) segment from Bryce Point to Inspiration Point is regularly closed during winter months.','2025-03-28 01:43:57','2025-03-28 01:43:57'),(13986,'trails',354,'Can I complete a one-way hike using the shuttle service?','During the shuttle season, you can take advantage of shuttle stops at Bryce, Inspiration, Sunset, and Sunrise Points to facilitate one-way hikes. Note that Fairyland Point does not have shuttle service.','2025-03-28 01:43:57','2025-03-28 01:43:57'),(13987,'trails',354,'Is the Rim Trail accessible for wheelchair users?','Due to the natural terrain of the park, only the 0.5-mile (0.8 km) section between Sunset and Sunrise Points is wheelchair accessible.','2025-03-28 01:43:57','2025-03-28 01:43:57'),(13988,'trails',354,'Are dogs allowed on the Rim Trail?','Yes, dogs are permitted on the Rim Trail, but be sure to keep them on a leash and follow park regulations.','2025-03-28 01:43:57','2025-03-28 01:43:57'),(13989,'trails',354,'What are the coordinates for the Rim Trail?','The geographic coordinates for the Rim Trail are approximately 37.6226° N latitude and -112.166° W longitude.','2025-03-28 01:43:57','2025-03-28 01:43:57'),(13990,'trails',355,'What can I expect to see while hiking the South Rim Trail?','Hiking the South Rim Trail offers stunning views of hoodoos, arches, waterfalls, and other fascinating geological formations as the trail meanders along the edge of Cedar Breaks Amphitheater.','2025-03-28 01:44:02','2025-03-28 01:44:02'),(13991,'trails',355,'Where does the South Rim Trail begin?','The South Rim Trail starts at the Point Supreme parking lot, making it easily accessible for hikers looking to explore this beautiful area.','2025-03-28 01:44:02','2025-03-28 01:44:02'),(13992,'trails',355,'What is the overall experience of the South Rim Trail?','The South Rim Trail is renowned for providing one of the most memorable hiking experiences at Cedar Breaks, as it leads you along the rim while showcasing breathtaking scenic viewpoints.','2025-03-28 01:44:02','2025-03-28 01:44:02'),(13993,'trails',355,'What is the trail\'s terrain and accessibility like?','The trail consists of a narrow dirt path with varying elevations, featuring some steep sections, and includes water-breaks or small stairs designed to minimize erosion.','2025-03-28 01:44:02','2025-03-28 01:44:02'),(13994,'trails',355,'Are dogs allowed on the South Rim Trail?','Yes, dogs are permitted on the South Rim Trail, allowing you to bring your furry friends along for the adventure.','2025-03-28 01:44:02','2025-03-28 01:44:02'),(13995,'trails',357,'What is Alstrom Point?','Alstrom Point is a scenic overlook located in the southwest part of Glen Canyon National Recreation Area, offering breathtaking views of Lake Powell and the surrounding canyons, along with fascinating geological features.','2025-03-28 01:44:15','2025-03-28 01:44:15'),(13996,'trails',357,'How long is the drive to Alstrom Point?','The journey to Alstrom Point spans approximately 46 miles through the stunning landscapes of Glen Canyon National Recreation Area, providing an exciting experience for adventurous travelers.','2025-03-28 01:44:16','2025-03-28 01:44:16'),(13997,'trails',357,'What notable geological features can be seen along the drive?','Along the route, you can admire Tropic Shale, Romana Sandstone, and various canyons of Lake Powell, as well as potential hoodoo formations.','2025-03-28 01:44:16','2025-03-28 01:44:16'),(13998,'trails',357,'Are there any side hikes available on the way to Alstrom Point?','Yes, there are several side hikes available, including options at Wiregrass Canyon and Resurrection Canyon. Both offer unique hiking experiences amid beautiful landscapes.','2025-03-28 01:44:16','2025-03-28 01:44:16'),(13999,'trails',357,'What type of vehicle is recommended for this drive?','A high clearance 4WD vehicle is necessary for the last stretch to Alstrom Point. A high clearance 2WD vehicle is advisable for the entire drive, especially given some road conditions.','2025-03-28 01:44:16','2025-03-28 01:44:16'),(14000,'trails',357,'How should I prepare for my trip to Alstrom Point?','It\'s essential to be well-prepared with plenty of water, an emergency kit, proper footwear, sunscreen, and a hat, as there is no shade throughout the area.','2025-03-28 01:44:16','2025-03-28 01:44:16'),(14001,'trails',357,'Is there cell service available along the drive?','Cellular coverage is limited along the entire route, so it\'s advisable to leave your travel itinerary with someone back home in case of emergencies.','2025-03-28 01:44:16','2025-03-28 01:44:16'),(14002,'trails',357,'What safety precautions should I take?','Avoid traveling during wet weather as roads can become impassable. Always check weather conditions before setting out, and never attempt to cross washes during storms.','2025-03-28 01:44:16','2025-03-28 01:44:16'),(14003,'trails',357,'What should I do if I encounter running water at creek crossings?','If you approach Wahweap Creek and the water is running too high or fast, turn back. It\'s crucial to prioritize safety and avoid attempts that could jeopardize your vehicle or life.','2025-03-28 01:44:17','2025-03-28 01:44:17'),(14004,'trails',357,'Are there any facilities at Alstrom Point?','Alstrom Point is unimproved and lacks facilities. Visitors should bring their own water, gear, and be prepared to pack out all trash and human waste.','2025-03-28 01:44:17','2025-03-28 01:44:17'),(14005,'trails',357,'What should I do about waste disposal?','You must pack out everything you bring in, including all trash and human waste, as burying waste is not feasible in this rocky desert environment.','2025-03-28 01:44:17','2025-03-28 01:44:17'),(14006,'trails',357,'What are the best times to photograph Alstrom Point?','Sunrise and sunset are the prime times for photography at Alstrom Point, but interesting weather conditions can also enhance photos throughout the day.','2025-03-28 01:44:17','2025-03-28 01:44:17'),(14007,'trails',357,'Is it safe to drive to Alstrom Point at night?','Driving to Alstrom Point at night is unsafe due to limited visibility and challenging road conditions, so plan your visit during daylight hours.','2025-03-28 01:44:17','2025-03-28 01:44:17'),(14008,'trails',357,'How long does it take to drive to Alstrom Point?','The driving time to Alstrom Point is at least two hours each way, so ensure adequate daylight and time for your round trip.','2025-03-28 01:44:17','2025-03-28 01:44:17'),(14009,'trails',357,'Can I bring my dog to Alstrom Point?','Yes, dogs are allowed at Alstrom Point, but be sure to keep them leashed and clean up after them to preserve the environment.','2025-03-28 01:44:17','2025-03-28 01:44:17'),(14010,'trails',358,'What is Coyote Gulch?','Coyote Gulch is a picturesque tributary of the Escalante River in Utah, celebrated for its stunning arches, natural bridge, waterfalls, and a perennial stream.','2025-03-28 01:44:29','2025-03-28 01:44:29'),(14011,'trails',358,'How can I access Coyote Gulch?','You can reach Coyote Gulch via several entry points along Hole-in-the-Rock Road. Depending on your chosen trailhead, such as Red Well or Hurricane Wash, your hiking experience will vary.','2025-03-28 01:44:30','2025-03-28 01:44:30'),(14012,'trails',358,'What are the entry points to Coyote Gulch?','Entry points include Red Well, Hurricane Wash, and Fortymile Ridge, each with unique access roads and challenges, from easy walks to more strenuous climbs.','2025-03-28 01:44:30','2025-03-28 01:44:30'),(14013,'trails',358,'Is Coyote Gulch suitable for a day trip or an overnight hike?','Coyote Gulch can be enjoyed either as a long day hike or as an overnight backpacking adventure, with trip lengths depending on your starting point.','2025-03-28 01:44:30','2025-03-28 01:44:30'),(14014,'trails',358,'What should I know about water along the trail?','You\'ll find several seeps, springs, and a constant stream throughout Coyote Gulch. Most of the hike involves stream crossings, so expect to get your feet wet.','2025-03-28 01:44:30','2025-03-28 01:44:30'),(14015,'trails',358,'Are there any weather hazards to consider?','Yes, always be aware of the risk of flash floods in canyon areas. Even if the weather looks clear, storms miles away can cause sudden floods.','2025-03-28 01:44:30','2025-03-28 01:44:30'),(14016,'trails',358,'What is the maximum group size allowed?','To minimize impact on the environment, Coyote Gulch allows only groups of 12 people or fewer. Larger groups must split up and keep at least a half-mile distance apart.','2025-03-28 01:44:30','2025-03-28 01:44:30'),(14017,'trails',358,'What are the Leave No Trace principles?','Practice Leave No Trace by leaving the natural environment as you found it. This includes taking all trash with you, not removing natural features, and being respectful to wildlife.','2025-03-28 01:44:31','2025-03-28 01:44:31'),(14018,'trails',358,'How should I handle human waste while hiking?','All human waste must be removed from Coyote Gulch. Use a specialized portable toilet or engineered waste containment bag, and never leave any waste behind.','2025-03-28 01:44:31','2025-03-28 01:44:31'),(14019,'trails',358,'Are campfires allowed in Coyote Gulch?','No, fires are not permitted in Coyote Gulch to help preserve the area’s natural beauty.','2025-03-28 01:44:31','2025-03-28 01:44:31'),(14020,'trails',358,'What should I know about building rock cairns?','Building rock cairns is discouraged, as they can mislead other hikers. Stick to your map and compass for navigation instead.','2025-03-28 01:44:31','2025-03-28 01:44:31'),(14021,'trails',358,'Is Coyote Gulch accessible for people with mobility issues?','Coyote Gulch is not ideal for those with low mobility. The access roads are rough, and the trails can be challenging with deep sand and slickrock.','2025-03-28 01:44:31','2025-03-28 01:44:31'),(14022,'trails',358,'Are dogs allowed on the trail?','Yes, dogs are permitted in Coyote Gulch, but remember to keep them leashed and follow pet waste disposal guidelines.','2025-03-28 01:44:31','2025-03-28 01:44:31'),(14023,'trails',358,'When is the best time to visit Coyote Gulch?','The ideal seasons to hike in Coyote Gulch are spring and fall when temperatures are milder and the scenery is at its best.','2025-03-28 01:44:31','2025-03-28 01:44:31'),(14024,'trails',360,'What is the main destination of the hike?','The hike leads to the awe-inspiring Rainbow Bridge, a natural marvel reaching 290 feet high and spanning 275 feet wide, cherished by the Navajo as a symbol of hope and resilience.','2025-03-28 01:44:44','2025-03-28 01:44:44'),(14025,'trails',360,'Is camping allowed at Rainbow Bridge?','Overnight camping near Rainbow Bridge is not permitted. Hikers must return to their boats by sundown unless they possess a permit to continue hiking across the Navajo Nation.','2025-03-28 01:44:45','2025-03-28 01:44:45'),(14026,'trails',360,'What is the distance of the hike?','Hikers can expect to travel between 0.5 to 1.5 miles (0.8 to 2.4 km) each way, depending on the water levels. The distance may vary throughout the year.','2025-03-28 01:44:45','2025-03-28 01:44:45'),(14027,'trails',360,'What should I prepare for in terms of trail conditions?','The trail includes some elevation gain and can be rocky in parts. Follow the courtesy dock to reach the trailhead, and proceed carefully. The section of the trail beyond the second viewing area may be steep and narrow.','2025-03-28 01:44:45','2025-03-28 01:44:45'),(14028,'trails',360,'Is there any specific weather-related advice for hikers?','Hikers should be cautious in extreme heat as summer temperatures can exceed 100°F (37°C). It\'s essential to carry sufficient water, as shade is scarce along the trail.','2025-03-28 01:44:45','2025-03-28 01:44:45'),(14029,'trails',360,'Are pets allowed on the trail?','No, pets are not allowed on the trail, and drones are also prohibited. It\'s important to respect the natural environment and the sacred nature of the site.','2025-03-28 01:44:45','2025-03-28 01:44:45'),(14030,'trails',360,'What amenities are available on the trail?','There are no restroom facilities after leaving the docks, so it\'s crucial to take care of your needs before starting the hike.','2025-03-28 01:44:45','2025-03-28 01:44:45'),(14031,'trails',360,'Can I walk under Rainbow Bridge?','Visitors are asked to respect the sacredness of Rainbow Bridge by not approaching or walking underneath it, in line with the traditions of the Native American tribes.','2025-03-28 01:44:45','2025-03-28 01:44:45'),(14032,'trails',360,'What is the \'Hanging Garden\'?','The Hanging Garden is a unique ecosystem found along the trail, where spring-fed plants thrive on the cliffs, providing a striking contrast to the surrounding desert landscape.','2025-03-28 01:44:45','2025-03-28 01:44:45'),(14033,'trails',360,'What can I see at the Lower Viewing Area?','At the Lower Viewing Area, you can catch glimpses of Navajo Mountain, a historic shelter for the Navajo people, symbolizing resilience following their forced removal from their homeland.','2025-03-28 01:44:46','2025-03-28 01:44:46'),(14034,'trails',360,'Describe the experience at the Upper Viewing Area.','The Upper Viewing Area offers stunning vistas of Rainbow Bridge, one of the largest natural bridges worldwide, inspiring awe among visitors while reminding them to treat the site with respect.','2025-03-28 01:44:46','2025-03-28 01:44:46'),(14035,'trails',360,'What geological features shape the bridge?','Water flowing around the rocks gradually erodes them to form a natural bridge, with the surrounding landscape lending insight into how natural forces work.','2025-03-28 01:44:46','2025-03-28 01:44:46'),(14036,'trails',360,'Why is Nasja Begay and Jim Mike\'s contribution significant?','Nasja Begay and Jim Mike played a crucial role in the discovery of Rainbow Bridge in 1909. Commemorative plaques honor their efforts to share this landmark with the world.','2025-03-28 01:44:46','2025-03-28 01:44:46'),(14037,'trails',360,'Is the trail accessible for everyone?','The trail has varying conditions and is not suitable for those with limited mobility. It is made up of different surface types, including rocky areas and steep sections.','2025-03-28 01:44:46','2025-03-28 01:44:46'),(14038,'trails',360,'What should I expect regarding water levels during the hike?','Trail accessibility is dependent on water levels, which can fluctuate throughout the year. If the water is low, hikers may need to navigate sandy or muddy areas to reach the main trail.','2025-03-28 01:44:46','2025-03-28 01:44:46'),(14039,'trails',361,'What is the Cathedral Wash Trail like?','The Cathedral Wash Trail offers an exciting scramble through towering canyon walls, allowing you to explore stunning formations of Kaibab Limestone and Toroweap as you approach the Colorado River.','2025-03-28 01:44:54','2025-03-28 01:44:54'),(14040,'trails',361,'How do I get to the trailhead?','To reach the trailhead, start from Page, Arizona, and travel 42 miles south on Highway 89, then west on Highway 89A. If you\'re coming from the North Rim of the Grand Canyon, it\'s approximately 85 miles via Highway 89A and Highway 67. The trailhead is located about 1.3 miles down the Lees Ferry access road after turning off Highway 89A.','2025-03-28 01:44:56','2025-03-28 01:44:56'),(14041,'trails',361,'What kind of terrain can I expect on this trail?','The trail features a combination of dry washes, soft sand, and rocky surfaces, which require careful navigation over ledges and drops. It\'s generally not technical, but users should be prepared for some scrambling.','2025-03-28 01:44:57','2025-03-28 01:44:57'),(14042,'trails',361,'What are the key features of the trail?','Key highlights of the trail include the breathtaking Cathedral Rock at the beginning and the impressive Cathedral Wash Rapid created by the debris, all while surrounded by striking geological formations.','2025-03-28 01:44:57','2025-03-28 01:44:57'),(14043,'trails',361,'Is the trail accessible for everyone?','The trail is steep and involves descents onto uneven surfaces, including scrambles and narrow ledges. Therefore, it may not be suitable for those with mobility issues.','2025-03-28 01:44:57','2025-03-28 01:44:57'),(14044,'trails',361,'Can I bring my dog on the trail?','Yes, dogs are permitted on the Cathedral Wash Trail, but it\'s advisable to keep them on a leash for safety.','2025-03-28 01:44:57','2025-03-28 01:44:57'),(14045,'trails',361,'What are the GPS coordinates for the trailhead?','The latitude and longitude for the Cathedral Wash Trailhead are 36.8342 and -111.64, respectively.','2025-03-28 01:44:57','2025-03-28 01:44:57'),(14046,'trails',362,'How do I get to Lonely Dell Ranch?','You can reach Lonely Dell Ranch by taking Hwy 89 south and Hwy 89A west from Page, which is about 42 miles away, or from the North Rim of the Grand Canyon via Hwy 89A and Hwy 67, a distance of approximately 85 miles.','2025-03-28 01:45:05','2025-03-28 01:45:05'),(14047,'trails',362,'What can I expect to see during the walking tour?','The self-guided walking tour is a 1 mile (1.6 km) round trip that takes you through an orchard, log cabins, a stone ranch house, and a pioneer cemetery, offering a glimpse into the unique history of this isolated settlement.','2025-03-28 01:45:05','2025-03-28 01:45:05'),(14048,'trails',362,'What type of terrain will I encounter on the trail?','You\'ll navigate mixed terrain that includes gravel, sandy patches, and rocky surfaces, all with varying elevation changes, so be prepared for uneven paths.','2025-03-28 01:45:05','2025-03-28 01:45:05'),(14049,'trails',362,'Is fruit collection allowed in the orchard?','Yes, you can collect fruit from the orchard for personal consumption. However, there\'s a limit of 5 gallons per person per day.','2025-03-28 01:45:05','2025-03-28 01:45:05'),(14050,'trails',362,'What is the accessibility of the ranch and trails?','The road to Lonely Dell Ranch is an improved dirt road, but be aware that two uneven dirt trails lead into the orchard and main ranch areas, which require cautious walking due to their uneven surfaces.','2025-03-28 01:45:06','2025-03-28 01:45:06'),(14051,'trails',362,'Are dogs allowed at Lonely Dell Ranch?','You can bring one dog with you to Lonely Dell Ranch, making it more fun for everyone!','2025-03-28 01:45:06','2025-03-28 01:45:06'),(14052,'trails',362,'What historical significance does Lonely Dell Ranch hold?','This ranch was a vital settlement for families during the Great Mormon Migration, serving as a foundation for daily life in a challenging desert environment, where individuals worked hard to make a living.','2025-03-28 01:45:06','2025-03-28 01:45:06'),(14053,'trails',362,'What should I know about the orchard\'s irrigation system?','The orchard features a hand-dug irrigation system, and while you\'re encouraged to explore, please pay close attention to where you step as the terrain can be uneven.','2025-03-28 01:45:06','2025-03-28 01:45:06'),(14054,'trails',362,'How far is Lees Ferry Junction from the nearby landmarks?','Lees Ferry Junction and Park Entrance is located in Marble Canyon, just west of the Navajo Bridge Interpretive Center.','2025-03-28 01:45:06','2025-03-28 01:45:06'),(14055,'trails',362,'What facilities are available at Lonely Dell Ranch?','Lonely Dell Ranch serves as a restful spot for travelers, providing natural beauty and shaded areas to relax amidst the historic site.','2025-03-28 01:45:06','2025-03-28 01:45:06'),(14056,'trails',362,'What should I keep in mind while visiting?','Be aware that the trails to the pioneer cemetery and the Paria Canyon Wilderness trailhead are uneven and exposed to direct sunlight, so prepare accordingly.','2025-03-28 01:45:06','2025-03-28 01:45:06'),(14057,'trails',363,'What is the big relief map at the Glen Canyon Conservancy?','The big relief map is an intricately detailed model that showcases the topography of the Glen Canyon National Recreation Area and its surroundings, including 12 hidden natural bridges and arches. It serves as a tool for navigation and exploration in the area\'s landscape.','2025-03-28 01:45:17','2025-03-28 01:45:17'),(14058,'trails',363,'Where can I find the relief map?','You can find the relief map at the flagship store of Glen Canyon Conservancy, located at 12 Lake Powell Blvd in the City of Page.','2025-03-28 01:45:17','2025-03-28 01:45:17'),(14059,'trails',363,'How was the relief map created?','The map was crafted by Bob Miller, who used topographic maps and aerial imagery for precision. Constructed over a year in his basement, it was designed to reflect the actual terrain accurately and was cut into seven pieces for transport to the Glen Canyon Visitor Center.','2025-03-28 01:45:17','2025-03-28 01:45:17'),(14060,'trails',363,'Can the map help with navigation?','Absolutely! The relief map is oriented to match real-life geography, making it a helpful resource for finding your way around the Glen Canyon area.','2025-03-28 01:45:17','2025-03-28 01:45:17'),(14061,'trails',363,'Are there any unique features on the map?','Yes! The model includes 12 natural bridges and arches that have been integrated into its design. A fun challenge is to see how many of these you can spot on the map.','2025-03-28 01:45:17','2025-03-28 01:45:17'),(14062,'trails',363,'Is the relief map accessible for everyone?','The relief map is designed with accessibility in mind. It stands about three feet high and is 12 feet long, with a surrounding railing that allows wheelchair access. Service animals are welcome in the building.','2025-03-28 01:45:17','2025-03-28 01:45:17'),(14063,'trails',363,'What is the historical significance of the relief map?','Installed in the Glen Canyon Visitor Center, the relief map has been a remarkable representation of the area for nearly 55 years. It accurately reflects most of the landscape, aside from some new roads, since its original creation.','2025-03-28 01:45:17','2025-03-28 01:45:17'),(14064,'trails',363,'What should I know before my visit?','Don\'t forget to allow yourself some time to explore and contemplate your place in this stunning desert canyon landscape. The map provides a unique visual experience that enhances your understanding of the environment.','2025-03-28 01:45:18','2025-03-28 01:45:18'),(14065,'trails',363,'What are the geographical coordinates of the relief map?','The relief map is located at latitude 36.9196 and longitude -111.461.','2025-03-28 01:45:18','2025-03-28 01:45:18'),(14066,'trails',363,'Are dogs allowed at the Glen Canyon Conservancy?','Yes, dogs are permitted in the area, but please note there are specific regulations regarding their presence.','2025-03-28 01:45:18','2025-03-28 01:45:18'),(14067,'trails',364,'Where can I camp on Lake Powell?','You can set up camp along the undeveloped shoreline of Lake Powell, which offers nearly 2000 miles of beach where you can also beach your boat for day trips or camping.','2025-03-28 01:45:35','2025-03-28 01:45:35'),(14068,'trails',364,'What types of camping are available on Lake Powell?','Camping options on Lake Powell range from adventurous experiences like winter kayaking in the desert to luxurious stays on multimillion-dollar houseboats, with various levels of camping or glamping available in between.','2025-03-28 01:45:35','2025-03-28 01:45:35'),(14069,'trails',364,'What should I know about boating regulations on Lake Powell?','It\'s essential to familiarize yourself with boating regulations and safety tips before you go; you can find more information on the National Park Service\'s boating webpage.','2025-03-28 01:45:35','2025-03-28 01:45:35'),(14070,'trails',364,'How popular is boating at Glen Canyon National Recreation Area?','Boating is the most popular activity in the Glen Canyon National Recreation Area, attracting nearly two million visitors who enjoy the beautiful turquoise waters of Lake Powell each year.','2025-03-28 01:45:35','2025-03-28 01:45:35'),(14071,'trails',364,'Do I need a map for camping on Lake Powell?','Yes, purchasing a map beforehand is advisable. It will help you locate side canyons, hiking spots, points of interest, and marinas, as well as explain the navigation system and fishing information.','2025-03-28 01:45:35','2025-03-28 01:45:35'),(14072,'trails',364,'What should I do in case of an emergency?','In case of an emergency, it will be crucial to know your exact location; the main channel of the lake varies in depth from 100 to 600 feet.','2025-03-28 01:45:35','2025-03-28 01:45:35'),(14073,'trails',364,'Can I camp anywhere on Lake Powell\'s shoreline?','Yes, you can camp along the shorelines, but ensure you anchor your boat on a beach for safety, as high winds can cause instability.','2025-03-28 01:45:36','2025-03-28 01:45:36'),(14074,'trails',364,'Are vehicles allowed in the backcountry areas of Glen Canyon?','No, motor vehicles, off-road vehicles, and bicycles are not permitted in the roadless backcountry areas of Glen Canyon.','2025-03-28 01:45:36','2025-03-28 01:45:36'),(14075,'trails',364,'What are the waste disposal requirements for campers?','All campsites require a portable toilet unless toilets are available within a certain distance. Waste must be disposed of properly; burying waste is prohibited.','2025-03-28 01:45:36','2025-03-28 01:45:36'),(14076,'trails',364,'Is it allowed to have campfires on Lake Powell?','Ground fires are permitted below the high-water mark, except in developed areas. However, check for any fire restrictions due to fire danger conditions.','2025-03-28 01:45:36','2025-03-28 01:45:36'),(14077,'trails',364,'What are the quiet hours for camping?','Quiet hours are observed from 10 PM to 6 AM, unless otherwise indicated.','2025-03-28 01:45:36','2025-03-28 01:45:36'),(14078,'trails',364,'Where is camping prohibited on Lake Powell?','Camping is not allowed in the Rainbow Bridge National Monument or on archaeological sites.','2025-03-28 01:45:36','2025-03-28 01:45:36'),(14079,'trails',364,'Is there any accessibility assistance for getting to beach campsites?','Boat owners or renters must be responsible for reaching the beach themselves, as there is no transportation service available to beach campsites.','2025-03-28 01:45:36','2025-03-28 01:45:36'),(14080,'trails',364,'What facilities should I expect at the beaches on Lake Powell?','The beaches are primitive with no running water or facilities. You\'ll need to bring your own toilets and supplies.','2025-03-28 01:45:36','2025-03-28 01:45:36'),(14081,'trails',364,'Are pets allowed at Lake Powell campsites?','Yes, pets and service animals are welcome as long as they are leashed, and you must clean up after them.','2025-03-28 01:45:36','2025-03-28 01:45:36'),(14082,'trails',364,'How many dogs are allowed per camping group?','You may bring one dog per camping group.','2025-03-28 01:45:36','2025-03-28 01:45:36'),(14083,'trails',365,'What is Horseshoe Bend and where is it located?','Horseshoe Bend is a stunning natural landmark that showcases a dramatic meander of the Colorado River. It lies within the Glen Canyon National Recreation Area, close to the Grand Canyon National Park, and is situated near the towns of Page, AZ, Kanab, UT, and St. George, UT, as well as the Navajo Nation.','2025-03-28 01:45:48','2025-03-28 01:45:48'),(14084,'trails',365,'How long is the hike to Horseshoe Bend?','The hike to the Horseshoe Bend overlook is a 1.5-mile (approximately 2.4 km) round-trip journey along a firm path.','2025-03-28 01:45:48','2025-03-28 01:45:48'),(14085,'trails',365,'Is the Horseshoe Bend trail accessible for those with disabilities?','Yes, the trail is accessible in accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, featuring a hardened surface suited for low mobility hikers, although it does not have railings along its length.','2025-03-28 01:45:48','2025-03-28 01:45:48'),(14086,'trails',365,'What kind of environment can hikers expect on the trail?','Hikers should anticipate a desert landscape with limited shade. There are two designated shade structures along the trail, but none at the overlook itself.','2025-03-28 01:45:48','2025-03-28 01:45:48'),(14087,'trails',365,'What precautions should hikers take before starting the hike?','It\'s essential to come prepared with plenty of water, sturdy footwear, sunscreen, and other basic hiking gear. Be aware that it’s wise to avoid hiking during the hottest parts of the day to ensure a safe experience.','2025-03-28 01:45:49','2025-03-28 01:45:49'),(14088,'trails',365,'Is there a parking fee for visiting Horseshoe Bend?','Yes, the City of Page charges for parking at the Horseshoe Bend trailhead. Note that National Park Service passes are not valid for this parking lot. It\'s advisable to check with the City of Page for current parking fees and any updates.','2025-03-28 01:45:49','2025-03-28 01:45:49'),(14089,'trails',365,'Are there any transportation alternatives during busy times?','During holidays and peak weekends, the City of Page may require visitors to use a shuttle service once the parking lot is full. It’s recommended to verify their policies if planning a visit during crowded periods.','2025-03-28 01:45:49','2025-03-28 01:45:49'),(14090,'trails',365,'Can dogs accompany hikers on this trail?','Yes, dogs are allowed on the Horseshoe Bend trail. Just make sure to keep them under control and clean up after them.','2025-03-28 01:45:49','2025-03-28 01:45:49'),(14091,'trails',365,'What should hikers know about the overlook?','At the end of the trail, hikers will find a flat viewing deck with railings for safety. However, beyond this deck, the edge becomes rocky and lacks railings, so caution is advised.','2025-03-28 01:45:49','2025-03-28 01:45:49'),(14092,'trails',365,'What are the GPS coordinates for Horseshoe Bend?','The GPS coordinates for Horseshoe Bend are latitude 36.8769 and longitude -111.507.','2025-03-28 01:45:49','2025-03-28 01:45:49'),(14093,'trails',365,'How far is the parking lot from the main attractions?','The parking area for Horseshoe Bend is conveniently located off US Highway 89, about 5 miles (8 km) south of the Carl Hayden Visitor Center, making it easily accessible for visitors.','2025-03-28 01:45:49','2025-03-28 01:45:49'),(14094,'trails',367,'What is Hermit Road?','Hermit Road is a picturesque 7-mile (11 km) route along the west side of Grand Canyon Village on the South Rim, known for its breathtaking views of the Grand Canyon, including sights of the Colorado River at Hopi Point and the sounds of Granite Rapid from Pima Point.','2025-03-28 01:45:59','2025-03-28 01:45:59'),(14095,'trails',367,'How can I access Hermit Road?','Hermit Road can be accessed via shuttle bus, on foot, by bicycle, or through commercial bus tours. During the winter months of December to February, private vehicles are permitted.','2025-03-28 01:45:59','2025-03-28 01:45:59'),(14096,'trails',367,'What are the main highlights of Hermit Road?','The road offers nine designated viewpoints that provide spectacular views, as well as the opportunity for both short and long walks along the Canyon Rim Trail, which runs alongside the road.','2025-03-28 01:45:59','2025-03-28 01:45:59'),(14097,'trails',367,'How frequent are the shuttle buses on Hermit Road?','Shuttle buses operate every 15 minutes during most of the day, making it easy to hop on and off at various viewpoints.','2025-03-28 01:45:59','2025-03-28 01:45:59'),(14098,'trails',367,'What should I know about biking on Hermit Road?','Bicyclists are welcome on Hermit Road, and shuttle buses are equipped with bike racks that can hold two to three bicycles with wheels 16 inches (41 cm) or larger. Riders are responsible for loading and unloading their bikes.','2025-03-28 01:45:59','2025-03-28 01:45:59'),(14099,'trails',367,'Are there facilities along Hermit Road?','Yes, there are vault toilets available at Hopi Point and Hermits Rest, as well as water and a snackbar at Hermits Rest.','2025-03-28 01:45:59','2025-03-28 01:45:59'),(14100,'trails',367,'Is Hermit Road accessible for individuals with mobility issues?','The shuttle buses are wheelchair accessible, and many paths between shuttle stops and scenic overlooks meet accessibility standards. However, larger wheelchairs and most motorized scooters may not fit on the shuttles.','2025-03-28 01:45:59','2025-03-28 01:45:59'),(14101,'trails',367,'Can I bring my dog on Hermit Road?','Yes, dogs are allowed on Hermit Road, but they must be leashed at all times.','2025-03-28 01:46:00','2025-03-28 01:46:00'),(14102,'trails',367,'What are the months when private vehicles can drive on Hermit Road?','Private vehicles are allowed on Hermit Road only during December, January, and February. It is closed to personal cars from March 1 through November 30.','2025-03-28 01:46:00','2025-03-28 01:46:00'),(14103,'trails',367,'Where does Hermit Road start?','Hermit Road begins at the interchange on the west side of the Village Historic District, near Bright Angel Lodge.','2025-03-28 01:46:00','2025-03-28 01:46:00'),(14104,'trails',368,'Where is the Weeping Rock Trailhead located?','The Weeping Rock Trailhead can be found at Shuttle Stop 7.','2025-03-28 01:46:06','2025-03-28 01:46:06'),(14105,'trails',368,'What can I expect to see on the Weeping Rock Trail?','Along the trail, you\'ll encounter small exhibits, beautiful rock alcoves, and the impressive sight of dripping springs at the end.','2025-03-28 01:46:06','2025-03-28 01:46:06'),(14106,'trails',368,'How challenging is the Weeping Rock Trail?','The trail is short but steep, gaining 98 feet (30 meters) over a distance of 0.4 miles (0.6 kilometers).','2025-03-28 01:46:06','2025-03-28 01:46:06'),(14107,'trails',368,'What type of trail surface should I expect?','The majority of the Weeping Rock Trail is paved, making it easier to navigate.','2025-03-28 01:46:06','2025-03-28 01:46:06'),(14108,'trails',368,'Are there any safety considerations on the trail?','Be mindful of minor drop-offs along the trail, and note that there are several stairs to manage.','2025-03-28 01:46:06','2025-03-28 01:46:06'),(14109,'trails',368,'What facilities are available at the parking area?','At the parking area, you will find pit toilets for visitor convenience.','2025-03-28 01:46:06','2025-03-28 01:46:06'),(14110,'trails',368,'Are dogs allowed on the Weeping Rock Trail?','Yes, dogs are permitted on the Weeping Rock Trail.','2025-03-28 01:46:06','2025-03-28 01:46:06'),(14111,'trails',368,'What kind of exhibits can I find on the trail?','There are small trailside exhibits that provide interesting insights about the environment as you hike.','2025-03-28 01:46:07','2025-03-28 01:46:07'),(14112,'trails',369,'What types of activities can I participate in at Zion National Park?','You can join a variety of ranger-led activities that explore the unique features of Zion National Park, including topics such as geology, wildlife, human history, and art. These programs offer a great opportunity to learn more about the park\'s diverse aspects.','2025-03-28 01:46:18','2025-03-28 01:46:18'),(14113,'trails',369,'Where can I find the schedule for ranger-led activities?','The schedule for ranger-led activities is available on the Events Calendar on the official Zion National Park website, where you can check the upcoming programs throughout the year.','2025-03-28 01:46:18','2025-03-28 01:46:18'),(14114,'trails',369,'Are there any costs associated with ranger-led programs?','No, all ranger-led programs are completely free to attend, making it easy to enjoy learning more about the park without any fees.','2025-03-28 01:46:18','2025-03-28 01:46:18'),(14115,'trails',369,'What accessibility options are available for ranger-led programs?','Accessibility features include assistive listening devices available at the Zion Canyon Visitor Center, and all talks currently take place outdoors. The Visitor Center also has a shaded area with sandstone benches and room for mobility devices and wheelchairs.','2025-03-28 01:46:18','2025-03-28 01:46:18'),(14116,'trails',369,'Can I bring my dog to ranger-led activities?','Yes, dogs are allowed in certain areas of Zion National Park, so you can bring your furry friend along while you participate in ranger-led activities.','2025-03-28 01:46:18','2025-03-28 01:46:18'),(14117,'trails',369,'Are the ranger-led walks accessible for people with mobility challenges?','Ranger walks on the Pa\'rus Trail are wheelchair accessible, but please note that hikes on the Watchman Trail are not suitable for those requiring mobility assistance.','2025-03-28 01:46:18','2025-03-28 01:46:18'),(14118,'trails',369,'How do I access the Ride with A Ranger program?','The Ride with A Ranger program takes place on Zion Canyon shuttle buses, which are equipped to accommodate wheelchairs, making it easy for everyone to join.','2025-03-28 01:46:18','2025-03-28 01:46:18'),(14119,'trails',369,'What is the geographical location of shuttle stop #1 at Zion National Park?','Shuttle stop #1 is located at latitude 37.2004 and longitude -112.987, right at the heart of the park\'s activities.','2025-03-28 01:46:19','2025-03-28 01:46:19'),(14120,'trails',370,'What is the length and difficulty level of the Upper Emerald Pools Trail?','The Upper Emerald Pools Trail is approximately 1 mile (1.6 km) long and is considered a moderate hike.','2025-03-28 01:46:27','2025-03-28 01:46:27'),(14121,'trails',370,'How can I access the Upper Emerald Pools Trail?','You can access the Upper Emerald Pools Trail from either the Emerald Pools Trailhead located at Zion Lodge (shuttle stop #5) or from The Grotto (shuttle stop #6).','2025-03-28 01:46:27','2025-03-28 01:46:27'),(14122,'trails',370,'What landmarks can I see along the trail?','While hiking, you\'ll be treated to stunning views of canyon landmarks including Lady Mountain and The Great White Throne, as well as seasonal waterfalls.','2025-03-28 01:46:27','2025-03-28 01:46:27'),(14123,'trails',370,'What is the trail\'s terrain like?','The trail features a combination of stone steps and a sandy path that winds through pinyon-juniper woodlands, leading to the base of dramatic canyon walls.','2025-03-28 01:46:27','2025-03-28 01:46:27'),(14124,'trails',370,'What is the ending point of the trail?','The trail concludes at the tranquil sandy shore of Upper Emerald Pool, which is an important water source for local wildlife.','2025-03-28 01:46:27','2025-03-28 01:46:27'),(14125,'trails',370,'Are there any restrictions on accessing the water at Upper Emerald Pool?','It is important to stay out of the water at Upper Emerald Pool, as the area is sensitive and vital for wildlife.','2025-03-28 01:46:27','2025-03-28 01:46:27'),(14126,'trails',370,'Are restrooms or water stations available near the trail?','Yes, restrooms and water filling stations are available at both Zion Lodge and The Grotto for your convenience.','2025-03-28 01:46:27','2025-03-28 01:46:27'),(14127,'trails',370,'What is the trail’s elevation change?','The Upper Emerald Pools Trail involves an elevation gain of about 200 feet (61 m).','2025-03-28 01:46:27','2025-03-28 01:46:27'),(14128,'trails',370,'Is the trail suitable for dogs?','Yes, dogs are permitted on the Upper Emerald Pools Trail.','2025-03-28 01:46:27','2025-03-28 01:46:27'),(14129,'trails',370,'Can I combine this trail with other trails?','The Upper Emerald Pools Trail connects to the Lower Emerald Pools Trail, Middle Emerald Pools Trail, and the Kayenta Trail, providing opportunities for longer hikes.','2025-03-28 01:46:28','2025-03-28 01:46:28'),(14130,'trails',370,'What is the accessibility of the trail?','The trail is wide but unpaved and sandy, featuring several sections with sandstone steps and some drop-offs.','2025-03-28 01:46:28','2025-03-28 01:46:28'),(14131,'trails',371,'What is the total distance of the Sand Bench Trail?','The Sand Bench Trail offers a roundtrip hike of 7.6 miles (12.2 km).','2025-03-28 01:46:41','2025-03-28 01:46:41'),(14132,'trails',371,'What unique geological features can I expect to see on the Sand Bench Trail?','Hikers will explore the remnants of an ancient rockfall, follow the scenic Virgin River, and ascend a historical landslide that formed a dam approximately 8,000 years ago, which created a lake stretching towards Angels Landing.','2025-03-28 01:46:41','2025-03-28 01:46:41'),(14133,'trails',371,'Where can I access the Sand Bench Trail?','You can access the Sand Bench Trail from the Emerald Pools Trailhead at the Zion Lodge (shuttle stop #5) or from the Court of the Patriarchs (shuttle stop #4).','2025-03-28 01:46:42','2025-03-28 01:46:42'),(14134,'trails',371,'How do I get to the Sand Bench Trail from Zion Lodge?','From the Zion Lodge, follow the sidewalk past the lodge lawn to the crosswalk, cross the road, and continue over the bridge. Then make a left to begin the Sand Bench Trail.','2025-03-28 01:46:42','2025-03-28 01:46:42'),(14135,'trails',371,'What additional options do I have at the Court of the Patriarchs shuttle stop?','From the Court of the Patriarchs, you can cross the road to the wooden steps leading down to a sandy trail. You can either head up-canyon towards Zion Lodge or proceed to ascend the longer loop portion of the trail back towards the Court of the Patriarchs.','2025-03-28 01:46:42','2025-03-28 01:46:42'),(14136,'trails',371,'How long is the loop portion of the Sand Bench Trail?','If you choose to hike only the loop portion of the Sand Bench Trail, the roundtrip distance is approximately 5 miles (8 km).','2025-03-28 01:46:42','2025-03-28 01:46:42'),(14137,'trails',371,'What is the elevation gain for the Sand Bench Trail?','The Sand Bench Trail features an elevation gain of about 466 feet (142 meters).','2025-03-28 01:46:42','2025-03-28 01:46:42'),(14138,'trails',371,'Are there any amenities available along the Sand Bench Trail?','Yes, you can find water and restrooms available at The Zion Lodge.','2025-03-28 01:46:42','2025-03-28 01:46:42'),(14139,'trails',371,'What should I be aware of when hiking in winter?','During winter hikes, be cautious of possible ice patches along the trail.','2025-03-28 01:46:42','2025-03-28 01:46:42'),(14140,'trails',371,'Is the Sand Bench Trail suitable for pets?','Yes, dogs are allowed on the Sand Bench Trail.','2025-03-28 01:46:42','2025-03-28 01:46:42'),(14141,'trails',371,'What is the terrain like on the Sand Bench Trail?','The trail consists of sandy paths, wooden and sandstone stairs, along with sections that have steep drop-offs.','2025-03-28 01:46:42','2025-03-28 01:46:42'),(14142,'trails',371,'What is the best time of year to hike the Sand Bench Trail?','The trail is a commercial horse trail from March to October, but it can be hiked year-round with proper precautions.','2025-03-28 01:46:42','2025-03-28 01:46:42'),(14143,'trails',371,'What are the GPS coordinates for the Sand Bench Trail?','The Sand Bench Trail is located at latitude 37.251 and longitude -112.959.','2025-03-28 01:46:43','2025-03-28 01:46:43'),(14144,'trails',371,'Does the Sand Bench Trail offer shade during the hike?','The Sand Bench Trail provides very little shade, especially during the hot summer months.','2025-03-28 01:46:43','2025-03-28 01:46:43'),(14145,'trails',372,'What can I expect to see on the Lower Emerald Pool Trail?','On the Lower Emerald Pool Trail, you can enjoy stunning views of the Lower Emerald Pool and seasonal waterfalls, all within a beautiful pinyon-juniper woodland.','2025-03-28 01:46:51','2025-03-28 01:46:51'),(14146,'trails',372,'Where does the Lower Emerald Pool Trail begin?','The trailhead for Lower Emerald Pool is conveniently located across from Zion Lodge at shuttle stop #5. From there, you can easily follow the sidewalk and cross the road to access the trail.','2025-03-28 01:46:51','2025-03-28 01:46:51'),(14147,'trails',372,'Is the Lower Emerald Pool Trail suitable for all hikers?','The trail is narrow and paved but features several steps and minor drop-offs. It\'s important to be cautious, particularly near the edges of cliffs. A metal handrail is available towards the end for added support.','2025-03-28 01:46:52','2025-03-28 01:46:52'),(14148,'trails',372,'Are there amenities available near the Lower Emerald Pool Trail?','Yes! There are restrooms and water filling stations located at the nearby Zion Lodge, making it convenient for hikers.','2025-03-28 01:46:52','2025-03-28 01:46:52'),(14149,'trails',372,'Can I swim in the Lower Emerald Pool?','Swimming is not allowed in the Lower Emerald Pool to protect its delicate ecosystem, which serves as a crucial water source for local wildlife.','2025-03-28 01:46:52','2025-03-28 01:46:52'),(14150,'trails',372,'Does the Lower Emerald Pool Trail connect to other trails?','Absolutely! The Lower Emerald Pool Trail connects with the other Emerald Pools trails and the Kayenta Trail, providing more options for exploration.','2025-03-28 01:46:52','2025-03-28 01:46:52'),(14151,'trails',372,'Are dogs allowed on the Lower Emerald Pool Trail?','Yes, dogs are permitted on the Lower Emerald Pool Trail, but please be sure to keep them leashed and under control.','2025-03-28 01:46:52','2025-03-28 01:46:52'),(14152,'trails',372,'What are the coordinates for the Lower Emerald Pool Trail?','The coordinates for the Lower Emerald Pool Trail are approximately latitude 37.251 and longitude -112.959.','2025-03-28 01:46:52','2025-03-28 01:46:52'),(14153,'trails',373,'What is the length of the Middle Emerald Pools Trail?','The Middle Emerald Pools Trail stretches for 2.2 miles (3.5 km).','2025-03-28 01:47:00','2025-03-28 01:47:00'),(14154,'trails',373,'What is the difficulty level of the Middle Emerald Pools Trail?','This trail is considered moderate, featuring a combination of steep sections and more gradual terrain.','2025-03-28 01:47:00','2025-03-28 01:47:00'),(14155,'trails',373,'Where can I find the trailhead for the Middle Emerald Pools Trail?','The trailhead is conveniently located across from the Zion Lodge, at shuttle stop #5.','2025-03-28 01:47:00','2025-03-28 01:47:00'),(14156,'trails',373,'What kind of scenery can I expect on the Middle Emerald Pools Trail?','Hikers will be treated to breathtaking views of Zion Canyon, shaded woodlands filled with pinyon and juniper trees, and beautiful emerald-colored pools set against the backdrop of sandstone cliffs.','2025-03-28 01:47:00','2025-03-28 01:47:00'),(14157,'trails',373,'Are pets allowed on the Middle Emerald Pools Trail?','Yes, dogs are allowed on the trail, but it\'s important to keep them under control and clean up after them.','2025-03-28 01:47:00','2025-03-28 01:47:00'),(14158,'trails',373,'What are the main highlights of the Middle Emerald Pools Trail?','Highlights include steep climbs to stunning canyon views, shaded areas with diverse flora, and the delicate pools formed above small waterfalls.','2025-03-28 01:47:01','2025-03-28 01:47:01'),(14159,'trails',373,'Is swimming permitted in the pools along the Middle Emerald Pools Trail?','Swimming is not allowed in the pools as they are fragile and serve as vital water sources for local wildlife.','2025-03-28 01:47:01','2025-03-28 01:47:01'),(14160,'trails',373,'What facilities are available at the Middle Emerald Pools Trail?','Restrooms and water filling stations can be found at the nearby Zion Lodge for your convenience.','2025-03-28 01:47:01','2025-03-28 01:47:01'),(14161,'trails',373,'What should I be cautious of while hiking the Middle Emerald Pools Trail?','Hikers should be aware of the steep drop-offs and cliff edges, particularly near the trail\'s borders. It\'s advisable to stay away from these areas for safety.','2025-03-28 01:47:01','2025-03-28 01:47:01'),(14162,'trails',373,'What is the terrain like on the Middle Emerald Pools Trail?','The trail consists of rocky, unpaved terrain that ascends approximately 150 feet (46 m), and it features some uneven sections with wooden stairs leading to the pools at the end.','2025-03-28 01:47:01','2025-03-28 01:47:01'),(14163,'trails',374,'Where does the hike to Angels Landing start?','The hike to Angels Landing begins at The Grotto, which is located at shuttle stop #6.','2025-03-28 01:47:10','2025-03-28 01:47:10'),(14164,'trails',374,'What trail do I take after The Grotto?','After The Grotto, you will cross the road and bridge to join the sandy West Rim Trail.','2025-03-28 01:47:10','2025-03-28 01:47:10'),(14165,'trails',374,'What is the terrain like on the Angels Landing hike?','The trail is steep and challenging, featuring uneven steps and sections with chains for support. It includes narrow paths with sheer drop-offs, so it\'s essential to stay cautious.','2025-03-28 01:47:10','2025-03-28 01:47:10'),(14166,'trails',374,'Are permits required for the Angels Landing hike?','Yes, as of April 1, 2022, hikers need a permit to continue from Scout Lookout to Angels Landing. You can obtain this permit at recreation.gov.','2025-03-28 01:47:10','2025-03-28 01:47:10'),(14167,'trails',374,'How exhilarating is the view from Angels Landing?','The view at the end of the hike is breathtaking, offering spectacular sights of Zion Canyon, which makes the strenuous journey well worth it.','2025-03-28 01:47:10','2025-03-28 01:47:10'),(14168,'trails',374,'What facilities are available along the hike?','Restrooms can be found at both Scout Lookout and The Grotto, and water filling stations are available at The Grotto.','2025-03-28 01:47:10','2025-03-28 01:47:10'),(14169,'trails',374,'Is the trail accessible for all hikers?','The trail is unpaved and rocky, with many sections less than 3 feet wide. It has chains acting as handrails and features significant drop-offs, making it less accessible for those with mobility difficulties.','2025-03-28 01:47:11','2025-03-28 01:47:11'),(14170,'trails',374,'Are dogs permitted on the Angels Landing trail?','Yes, dogs are allowed on the Angels Landing hike, but be sure to keep them on a leash.','2025-03-28 01:47:11','2025-03-28 01:47:11'),(14171,'trails',374,'What should I be mindful of regarding other hikers?','The trail often has limited space, so be prepared to yield to oncoming hikers, especially in narrow sections where passing may be challenging.','2025-03-28 01:47:11','2025-03-28 01:47:11'),(14172,'trails',375,'What is the difficulty level of the West Rim Trail?','The West Rim Trail is considered strenuous, featuring significant elevation gain and steep sections, making it suitable for experienced hikers.','2025-03-28 01:47:20','2025-03-28 01:47:20'),(14173,'trails',375,'How much elevation do hikers ascend on the West Rim Trail?','Hikers will climb 1,488 feet (454 meters) to reach Scout Lookout, providing stunning views of the surrounding canyon.','2025-03-28 01:47:20','2025-03-28 01:47:20'),(14174,'trails',375,'Where does the West Rim Trail start?','The trailhead is located at The Grotto, specifically at shuttle stop #6. Hikers will need to cross the road and a bridge to begin their adventure.','2025-03-28 01:47:20','2025-03-28 01:47:20'),(14175,'trails',375,'What can hikers expect along the trail?','The trail initially crosses the Virgin River and includes a series of steep switchbacks. Once in Refrigerator Canyon, there is a brief flat section, followed by a challenging ascent known as Walter\'s Wiggles, featuring 21 switchbacks that lead up to Scout Lookout.','2025-03-28 01:47:21','2025-03-28 01:47:21'),(14176,'trails',375,'What amenities are available for hikers on the West Rim Trail?','Water and restroom facilities are available at The Grotto, and there are restrooms at Scout Lookout as well.','2025-03-28 01:47:21','2025-03-28 01:47:21'),(14177,'trails',375,'What sights can hikers see at Scout Lookout?','Scout Lookout offers a scenic vantage point of Zion Canyon and is a great spot for spotting endangered California condors that inhabit the area.','2025-03-28 01:47:21','2025-03-28 01:47:21'),(14178,'trails',375,'Is a permit required to continue to Angels Landing?','Yes, a permit is necessary to proceed to Angels Landing, which can be obtained through recreation.gov starting from April 1, 2022.','2025-03-28 01:47:21','2025-03-28 01:47:21'),(14179,'trails',375,'What are the accessibility features of the West Rim Trail?','Sections of the trail are paved but can be steep and narrow, lacking handrails or fences. The ascent is challenging, and parts of Refrigerator Canyon may have low visibility, particularly in early morning or late evening.','2025-03-28 01:47:21','2025-03-28 01:47:21'),(14180,'trails',375,'Are dogs allowed on the West Rim Trail?','Yes, dogs are permitted on the West Rim Trail, but keep in mind the challenging terrain.','2025-03-28 01:47:21','2025-03-28 01:47:21'),(14181,'trails',375,'What are the geographic coordinates of the West Rim Trail?','The trail is located at a latitude of 37.2592 and a longitude of -112.951.','2025-03-28 01:47:21','2025-03-28 01:47:21'),(14182,'trails',376,'What can I expect to see on the Kayenta Trail?','The Kayenta Trail offers stunning panoramic views of Zion Canyon as you hike alongside the Virgin River, leading up to the Lower and Upper Emerald Pools.','2025-03-28 01:47:30','2025-03-28 01:47:30'),(14183,'trails',376,'How long is the Kayenta Trail?','The trail spans approximately 2.0 miles (3.2 km) and is rated as moderate, making it a manageable hike for many.','2025-03-28 01:47:30','2025-03-28 01:47:30'),(14184,'trails',376,'Where does the Kayenta Trailhead start?','You can find the Kayenta Trailhead at The Grotto, which is noted as shuttle stop #6. From there, use the crosswalk to cross the Virgin River and ascend the sandstone steps to commence your hike.','2025-03-28 01:47:30','2025-03-28 01:47:30'),(14185,'trails',376,'Can I loop back after hiking the Kayenta Trail?','Yes, you have the option to either retrace your steps back along the Kayenta Trail or complete a loop by utilizing one of the Emerald Pool trails.','2025-03-28 01:47:30','2025-03-28 01:47:30'),(14186,'trails',376,'Are there any amenities along the Kayenta Trail?','Yes, water and restroom facilities are available at The Grotto for your convenience.','2025-03-28 01:47:30','2025-03-28 01:47:30'),(14187,'trails',376,'What is the terrain like on the Kayenta Trail?','The trail consists of unpaved paths covering sandy, rocky, and uneven ground. Be prepared for sandstone steps at various points, and take caution as there are long drop-offs in certain areas.','2025-03-28 01:47:30','2025-03-28 01:47:30'),(14188,'trails',376,'What is the overall elevation gain on the Kayenta Trail?','The trail has a total elevation gain of 150 feet (46 meters), providing a gentle ascent as you hike.','2025-03-28 01:47:30','2025-03-28 01:47:30'),(14189,'trails',376,'Are dogs allowed on the Kayenta Trail?','Yes, dogs are permitted on the Kayenta Trail, but please ensure they are well-behaved and kept on a leash.','2025-03-28 01:47:30','2025-03-28 01:47:30'),(14190,'trails',376,'What are the coordinates for the Kayenta Trail?','The latitude and longitude for the Kayenta Trail are 37.2592 and -112.951, respectively.','2025-03-28 01:47:30','2025-03-28 01:47:30'),(14191,'trails',377,'What is the length of the Canyon Overlook Trail?','The Canyon Overlook Trail spans approximately 1 mile (1.6 km).','2025-03-28 01:47:38','2025-03-28 01:47:38'),(14192,'trails',377,'What is the difficulty level of the Canyon Overlook Trail?','This trail is considered moderate, making it suitable for a variety of hikers.','2025-03-28 01:47:38','2025-03-28 01:47:38'),(14193,'trails',377,'What type of terrain can hikers expect on the trail?','Hikers will encounter a series of sandstone steps and rocky paths as they navigate the trail, along with a metal handrail for safety.','2025-03-28 01:47:38','2025-03-28 01:47:38'),(14194,'trails',377,'What kind of views will I see from the trail?','The trail offers stunning vistas of red and cream-colored slickrock, as well as impressive views of the Towers of the Virgin at the overlook.','2025-03-28 01:47:38','2025-03-28 01:47:38'),(14195,'trails',377,'Is it possible to see wildlife on the Canyon Overlook Trail?','Yes, hikers may spot bighorn sheep along the trail, adding to the experience.','2025-03-28 01:47:39','2025-03-28 01:47:39'),(14196,'trails',377,'How do I access the Canyon Overlook Trailhead?','To reach the Canyon Overlook Trailhead, follow State Route 9 through the Zion-Mount Carmel Tunnel.','2025-03-28 01:47:39','2025-03-28 01:47:39'),(14197,'trails',377,'What is the parking situation at the Canyon Overlook Trailhead?','Parking is very limited, so be prepared to try several times to find a spot.','2025-03-28 01:47:39','2025-03-28 01:47:39'),(14198,'trails',377,'Are there any restroom facilities available near the trailhead?','Yes, pit toilets are available at the parking area for visitor convenience.','2025-03-28 01:47:39','2025-03-28 01:47:39'),(14199,'trails',377,'Are there any safety considerations for the Canyon Overlook Trail?','Yes, the trail has long drop-offs and is mostly fenced, but it is rocky and uneven with a climb of 163 ft (50 m), so caution is advised.','2025-03-28 01:47:39','2025-03-28 01:47:39'),(14200,'trails',377,'Are dogs allowed on the Canyon Overlook Trail?','Yes, dogs are permitted on the trail, but make sure to keep them leashed.','2025-03-28 01:47:39','2025-03-28 01:47:39'),(14201,'trails',377,'What are the coordinates for the Canyon Overlook Trail?','The coordinates for the Canyon Overlook Trail are 37.2131° latitude and -112.941° longitude.','2025-03-28 01:47:39','2025-03-28 01:47:39'),(14202,'trails',378,'What can I expect to see on The Narrows hike?','On The Narrows hike, you\'ll encounter the stunning Virgin River as it carves through a narrow slot canyon, creating a breathtaking landscape perfect for photography and nature appreciation.','2025-03-28 01:47:49','2025-03-28 01:47:49'),(14203,'trails',378,'How do I access The Narrows trailhead?','To start The Narrows hike, first walk along the easy, paved Riverside Walk from the Temple of Sinawava, which is designated as shuttle stop #9. The Narrows begins at the end of this walk.','2025-03-28 01:47:49','2025-03-28 01:47:49'),(14204,'trails',378,'What is the difficulty level of The Narrows?','The Narrows is considered a strenuous hike due to its unique conditions, as you will be wading through the Virgin River on rocky and often unstable terrain.','2025-03-28 01:47:49','2025-03-28 01:47:49'),(14205,'trails',378,'Are there any safety concerns I should be aware of?','Yes, hikers should be cautious of potential flash flooding and the risk of hypothermia. Proper planning, gear, and sound judgment are essential for a safe hiking experience.','2025-03-28 01:47:50','2025-03-28 01:47:50'),(14206,'trails',378,'How does the hike progress after the Riverside Walk?','After completing the one-mile Riverside Walk, you’ll descend a set of stairs into the Virgin River, where you will continue your hike, navigating through the river\'s varying depths and rocky floors.','2025-03-28 01:47:50','2025-03-28 01:47:50'),(14207,'trails',378,'Is there a specific endpoint for The Narrows hike?','There isn\'t a formal destination for The Narrows hike. It\'s vital to judge your energy levels and turn back before you feel fatigued to ensure a safe return trip.','2025-03-28 01:47:50','2025-03-28 01:47:50'),(14208,'trails',378,'Do I need a permit to hike The Narrows?','No permit is necessary for this day hike; however, venturing beyond Big Spring or up Orderville Canyon does require a Wilderness permit.','2025-03-28 01:47:50','2025-03-28 01:47:50'),(14209,'trails',378,'Where can I find facilities during my hike?','Water and restroom facilities are available at the Temple of Sinawava, the starting point for The Narrows.','2025-03-28 01:47:50','2025-03-28 01:47:50'),(14210,'trails',378,'How accessible is The Narrows trail?','The trail is essentially the river itself, with slippery and uneven rocks. Water depths can vary significantly, ranging from just ankle-deep to as deep as chest-high.','2025-03-28 01:47:50','2025-03-28 01:47:50'),(14211,'trails',378,'Are dogs allowed on The Narrows hike?','Yes, you are welcome to bring one dog with you on The Narrows hike.','2025-03-28 01:47:50','2025-03-28 01:47:50'),(14212,'trails',378,'What is the geographical location of The Narrows trail?','The Narrows is located at a latitude of 37.2852 and a longitude of -112.948.','2025-03-28 01:47:50','2025-03-28 01:47:50'),(14213,'trails',379,'What is the Riverside Walk trail like?','The Riverside Walk is an easy, flat, and paved trail that spans 2.2 miles (3.5 km) round-trip in the northern section of Zion Canyon. Hikers will enjoy stunning views as they follow the Virgin River and walk between towering sandstone walls.','2025-03-28 01:47:59','2025-03-28 01:47:59'),(14214,'trails',379,'How long is the Riverside Walk trail?','The trail is a 2.2-mile (3.5 km) round-trip journey, making it a great option for both casual hikers and families.','2025-03-28 01:47:59','2025-03-28 01:47:59'),(14215,'trails',379,'Is the Riverside Walk suitable for everyone?','The initial 0.4 miles (0.6 km) of the trail is wheelchair accessible. However, after that point, the trail becomes steeper and may be challenging for those with mobility issues.','2025-03-28 01:47:59','2025-03-28 01:47:59'),(14216,'trails',379,'What will I see along the Riverside Walk?','As you walk along the trail, you will encounter informative exhibits that explain the processes of canyon carving, erosion, and the area\'s diverse ecosystem, adding an educational aspect to your hike.','2025-03-28 01:47:59','2025-03-28 01:47:59'),(14217,'trails',379,'Can I continue to The Narrows from the Riverside Walk?','Yes, the Riverside Walk provides access to The Narrows. If you prefer to stay dry, you can turn back at the end of the paved section.','2025-03-28 01:47:59','2025-03-28 01:47:59'),(14218,'trails',379,'Where does the Riverside Walk trail start?','The trail begins at the Temple of Sinawava, which is the last stop on the Zion Canyon Scenic Drive. Follow the sidewalk past the shuttle stop and restrooms to initiate your hike.','2025-03-28 01:47:59','2025-03-28 01:47:59'),(14219,'trails',379,'Are there facilities available on the Riverside Walk?','Yes, there are water sources and restrooms available at the Temple of Sinawava, ensuring convenience for hikers.','2025-03-28 01:47:59','2025-03-28 01:47:59'),(14220,'trails',379,'What elevation change can I expect on the trail?','The Riverside Walk features a modest elevation change of 57 feet (17 meters), making it a gentle hike.','2025-03-28 01:47:59','2025-03-28 01:47:59'),(14221,'trails',379,'Can I bring my dog on the Riverside Walk?','Yes, dogs are allowed on the Riverside Walk, making it a pet-friendly option for hiking.','2025-03-28 01:47:59','2025-03-28 01:47:59'),(14222,'trails',380,'What is the La Verkin Creek Trail to Kolob Arch?','The La Verkin Creek Trail is a hiking path that leads to Kolob Arch, recognized as one of the world’s largest natural arches. This trail begins at the Lee Pass Trailhead along Kolob Canyons Road and features breathtaking views of Kolob Canyons, culminating in a seven-mile descent toward La Verkin Creek.','2025-03-28 01:48:10','2025-03-28 01:48:10'),(14223,'trails',380,'Where is the Lee Pass Trailhead located?','The Lee Pass Trailhead is situated near the end of Kolob Canyons Road and is the second-to-last trailhead on this scenic route.','2025-03-28 01:48:10','2025-03-28 01:48:10'),(14224,'trails',380,'What are the parking facilities like at Lee Pass Trailhead?','Parking at the Lee Pass Trailhead is limited, so hikers should arrive early to ensure a spot.','2025-03-28 01:48:10','2025-03-28 01:48:10'),(14225,'trails',380,'Are there restroom facilities near the trailhead?','No, there are no restrooms at the Lee Pass Trailhead. However, restroom facilities are available at the Kolob Canyons Visitor Center.','2025-03-28 01:48:10','2025-03-28 01:48:10'),(14226,'trails',380,'What are the regulations regarding group sizes on the trail?','To protect the delicate wilderness environment, group sizes are limited to a maximum of 12 individuals who share a common affiliation, such as friends, family, or recreational groups. Those exceeding this limit must separate into different areas rather than splitting up on the same trail.','2025-03-28 01:48:10','2025-03-28 01:48:10'),(14227,'trails',380,'What should I do regarding restroom needs while hiking?','Before setting out, ensure you visit the restroom at the Kolob Canyons Visitor Center. If you are on the trail, be prepared to pack out any human waste, including toilet paper and hygiene products. It’s advisable to use human waste disposal bags.','2025-03-28 01:48:10','2025-03-28 01:48:10'),(14228,'trails',380,'Can I bring my pet on the La Verkin Creek Trail?','Unfortunately, pets are not allowed on the La Verkin Creek Trail or any other trails in Zion National Park, with the sole exception being the Pa\'rus Trail.','2025-03-28 01:48:11','2025-03-28 01:48:11'),(14229,'trails',380,'What kind of terrain can I expect on this trail?','The trail is considered strenuous, featuring rocky, sandy, and uneven terrain, as well as water crossings. It involves an elevation change of 1,037 feet over a distance of 14 miles.','2025-03-28 01:48:11','2025-03-28 01:48:11'),(14230,'trails',380,'What can I expect to see at the Kolob Arch viewpoint?','After a seven-mile hike, a spur trail leads you to a viewpoint of the Kolob Arch. This impressive natural formation features a span of 287 feet and a thickness of 75 feet, showcasing the grandeur of nature.','2025-03-28 01:48:11','2025-03-28 01:48:11'),(14231,'trails',381,'What activities can be enjoyed on the Pa\'rus Trail?','The Pa\'rus Trail is perfect for hiking, biking, and walking dogs. It\'s a versatile path that caters to various outdoor activities.','2025-03-28 01:48:20','2025-03-28 01:48:20'),(14232,'trails',381,'What kind of wildlife can I see along the trail?','While exploring the Pa\'rus Trail, keep an eye out for wildlife, including deer that are often spotted in the meadows adjacent to the trail.','2025-03-28 01:48:20','2025-03-28 01:48:20'),(14233,'trails',381,'Where are the access points to the Virgin River along the trail?','The trail offers multiple convenient access points to the Virgin River, allowing visitors to enjoy the water.','2025-03-28 01:48:20','2025-03-28 01:48:20'),(14234,'trails',381,'What unique features are available along the Pa\'rus Trail?','You can find trailside exhibits that provide insights into the local plant and animal life, geology, and historical context of the area.','2025-03-28 01:48:20','2025-03-28 01:48:20'),(14235,'trails',381,'What does the name \'Pa\'rus\' mean?','\'Pa’rus\' translates to \'bubbling water\' in the Paiute language, reflecting the trail’s scenic route along the Virgin River.','2025-03-28 01:48:20','2025-03-28 01:48:20'),(14236,'trails',381,'How do I access the Pa\'rus Trail from Zion Canyon Visitor Center?','Start at the Zion Canyon Visitor Center by walking through the plaza, past the shuttle stop, and crossing the bridge to reach the trailhead near South Campground.','2025-03-28 01:48:20','2025-03-28 01:48:20'),(14237,'trails',381,'Can I access the trail from Canyon Junction?','Yes, from Canyon Junction, follow the sidewalk southward, towards the Watchman, and proceed under the roadway bridge to reach the trail.','2025-03-28 01:48:20','2025-03-28 01:48:20'),(14238,'trails',381,'Is the Pa\'rus Trail wheelchair accessible?','Yes, the Pa\'rus Trail is a wide, cement-paved path that is accessible for wheelchairs, as well as for leashed pets and bicycles.','2025-03-28 01:48:21','2025-03-28 01:48:21'),(14239,'trails',381,'Are there any facilities available nearby?','Restrooms and water filling stations are conveniently located at the Zion Canyon Visitor Center for visitor use.','2025-03-28 01:48:21','2025-03-28 01:48:21'),(14240,'trails',381,'What is the elevation change on the Pa\'rus Trail?','The trail has a gentle elevation change of about 50 feet (15 meters), making it an easier hike for all skill levels.','2025-03-28 01:48:21','2025-03-28 01:48:21'),(14241,'trails',381,'What time of day is best for visiting the Pa\'rus Trail?','The Pa\'rus Trail is an excellent spot for sunset viewing, stargazing, and astrophotography, providing breathtaking views at twilight.','2025-03-28 01:48:21','2025-03-28 01:48:21'),(14242,'trails',382,'What can I expect to see on the Timber Creek Overlook Trail?','Hikers will be treated to breathtaking views of Shuntavi Butte, Timber Creek, Kolob Terrace, and the Pine Valley Mountains. On clear days, it\'s possible to spot Mount Trumbull, located 100 miles away at the north rim of the Grand Canyon. Additionally, in the spring and early summer, the trail is adorned with beautiful desert wildflowers.','2025-03-28 01:48:30','2025-03-28 01:48:30'),(14243,'trails',382,'How do I get to the Timber Creek Overlook Trailhead?','To reach the Timber Creek Overlook Trailhead, start at the Kolob Canyons Visitor Center and follow Kolob Canyons Road to its end where you will find the trailhead and parking area.','2025-03-28 01:48:30','2025-03-28 01:48:30'),(14244,'trails',382,'Are there any amenities available at the trailhead?','Yes, there are restrooms available at the trailhead, and you can find water facilities at the Kolob Canyons Visitor Center.','2025-03-28 01:48:30','2025-03-28 01:48:30'),(14245,'trails',382,'Is Timber Creek Overlook Trail suitable for beginners?','Absolutely! The Timber Creek Overlook Trail is a short and relatively easy hike that follows a rocky ridge with minimal elevation gain, making it an excellent choice for those new to hiking.','2025-03-28 01:48:30','2025-03-28 01:48:30'),(14246,'trails',382,'What is the length and elevation gain of the Timber Creek Overlook Trail?','This trail features a total elevation gain of approximately 100 feet (30 meters) and is designed for quick hikes, leaving you ample time to enjoy the stunning overlook.','2025-03-28 01:48:30','2025-03-28 01:48:30'),(14247,'trails',382,'What should I be aware of regarding trail conditions?','The dirt trail can become muddy when wet, so be prepared for potentially slippery conditions. Also, keep in mind that the trail is unpaved and traverses uneven, rocky terrain, with a narrow path leading to steep drop-offs at the overlook.','2025-03-28 01:48:30','2025-03-28 01:48:30'),(14248,'trails',382,'Are dogs allowed on the Timber Creek Overlook Trail?','Yes, dogs are allowed on the Timber Creek Overlook Trail, so feel free to bring your furry companions along for the hike!','2025-03-28 01:48:31','2025-03-28 01:48:31'),(14249,'trails',382,'Is there a place to have a picnic near the trail?','Yes, there is a small picnic area located just a short distance from the trailhead, perfect for relaxing after your hike.','2025-03-28 01:48:31','2025-03-28 01:48:31'),(14250,'trails',382,'What are the coordinates of the Timber Creek Overlook Trail?','The geographical coordinates for the Timber Creek Overlook Trail are approximately Latitude 37.4355 and Longitude -113.202.','2025-03-28 01:48:31','2025-03-28 01:48:31'),(14251,'trails',383,'What makes Zion National Park a popular climbing destination?','Zion National Park is famous for its stunning 2,000-foot sandstone cliffs, offering some of the most adventurous big wall climbs in the world. The unique rock formation provides a challenging experience, although the routes are generally not suitable for novice climbers due to their difficulty and the soft nature of the rock.','2025-03-28 01:48:43','2025-03-28 01:48:43'),(14252,'trails',383,'Are permits required for overnight climbing in Zion?','Yes, permits are mandatory for all overnight bivouacs in Zion National Park, whereas day climbs do not require a permit. You can reserve bivy spots in advance for popular climbs. Be sure to pick up your permits at the Zion Canyon Visitor Center either the day before or the day of your climbing adventure.','2025-03-28 01:48:44','2025-03-28 01:48:44'),(14253,'trails',383,'What should I know about human waste disposal while climbing?','It is essential to properly manage human waste by using a tube or bag to carry it out with you. Leaving waste behind is not permitted, so make sure to follow Leave No Trace principles.','2025-03-28 01:48:44','2025-03-28 01:48:44'),(14254,'trails',383,'Is commercial guiding allowed in Zion\'s climbing areas?','No, commercial guiding is prohibited in the Zion Wilderness, which encompasses all climbing routes in the park.','2025-03-28 01:48:44','2025-03-28 01:48:44'),(14255,'trails',383,'What is the policy on bolting and route development?','The National Park Service does not inspect or maintain climbing bolts and equipment within the park. Climbers are responsible for their own safety and should visually evaluate any existing bolts or fixed pins. The park discourages over-reliance on bolts, encouraging climbers to use traditional climbing techniques instead.','2025-03-28 01:48:44','2025-03-28 01:48:44'),(14256,'trails',383,'Can I leave equipment unattended while climbing?','Do not leave climbing equipment, including fixed ropes, unattended for more than 24 hours as it will be deemed abandoned property and may be removed by the National Park Service.','2025-03-28 01:48:44','2025-03-28 01:48:44'),(14257,'trails',383,'How do I establish a new climbing route in Zion?','If you plan to set up a new climbing route, visit the Wilderness Desk at the Zion Canyon Visitor Center to discuss your plans with a ranger. They can assist you with determining if your route lies within the designated Wilderness area and provide important information.','2025-03-28 01:48:44','2025-03-28 01:48:44'),(14258,'trails',383,'What are the best climbing conditions in Zion?','The ideal climbing seasons in Zion are from March to May and September to early November. Remember that summer temperatures can exceed 100 degrees, and monsoon rains can weaken the sandstone rock, making it unsafe to climb soon after rain.','2025-03-28 01:48:44','2025-03-28 01:48:44'),(14259,'trails',383,'Where can I find bouldering opportunities in the park?','Zion offers two bouldering locations: The Globe, a large boulder situated just west of the south entrance, and the Drilled Pocket Boulder, located half a mile north of the south entrance with distinct slab features.','2025-03-28 01:48:44','2025-03-28 01:48:44'),(14260,'trails',383,'Can I bring my dog while climbing in Zion?','Yes, dogs are allowed in Zion National Park, but be sure to check specific regulations regarding pet access in certain areas.','2025-03-28 01:48:44','2025-03-28 01:48:44'),(14261,'trails',384,'What is the Taylor Creek Trail known for?','The Taylor Creek Trail is famous for its breathtaking natural formations, including the Double Arch Alcove, and its scenic journey through a narrow box canyon featuring the delightful Taylor Creek and the unique Kanarraville Fold.','2025-03-28 01:48:58','2025-03-28 01:48:58'),(14262,'trails',384,'Where do I start my hike on the Taylor Creek Trail?','You can begin your hike at the Taylor Creek Trailhead, which is accessible after driving along the Kolob Canyons Road from the Kolob Canyons Visitor Center in New Harmony, Utah.','2025-03-28 01:48:58','2025-03-28 01:48:58'),(14263,'trails',384,'Are there restrooms available on the trail?','Yes, restrooms are situated at the Kolob Canyons Visitor Center and pit toilets can be found at the Taylor Creek Trailhead and other nearby locations. It\'s advisable to use restrooms before heading out on the trail.','2025-03-28 01:48:58','2025-03-28 01:48:58'),(14264,'trails',384,'Is there a water source available along the trail?','Water can be obtained at the Kolob Canyons Visitor Center, so make sure to fill your bottles before starting your hike as you won\'t find additional water sources along the trail.','2025-03-28 01:48:58','2025-03-28 01:48:58'),(14265,'trails',384,'How far is Taylor Creek Trail from the Zion Canyon area?','The Kolob Canyons section, which includes the Taylor Creek Trail, is approximately an hour\'s drive from the Zion Canyon area.','2025-03-28 01:48:58','2025-03-28 01:48:58'),(14266,'trails',384,'Are there any restrictions on group sizes for hiking?','Yes, to safeguard the wilderness, group sizes are capped at 12 individuals. Groups that exceed this limit must disperse and visit different areas, without splitting up to hike the same trail on the same day.','2025-03-28 01:48:58','2025-03-28 01:48:58'),(14267,'trails',384,'What should I know about restroom usage while on the trail?','While there are limited restroom facilities, if you need to go while hiking, you must carry out any human waste and hygiene products. It is highly recommended to use human waste disposal bags to transport solid waste.','2025-03-28 01:48:58','2025-03-28 01:48:58'),(14268,'trails',384,'Can I bring my pet on the Taylor Creek Trail?','Pets are not allowed on the Taylor Creek Trail or any other trails in this section of Zion National Park, with the exception of the Pa\'rus Trail, which is pet-friendly.','2025-03-28 01:48:58','2025-03-28 01:48:58'),(14269,'trails',384,'What conditions should I expect on the trail?','The trail features unpaved and uneven terrain, which includes rocky and sandy sections along with multiple water crossings. Be aware that it climbs an elevation of 450 feet (137 meters).','2025-03-28 01:48:58','2025-03-28 01:48:58'),(14270,'trails',384,'How can I prepare for winter hiking conditions?','In winter, be ready for icy conditions on the trail, and expect water crossings during the spring that might leave your feet wet. Ensure you have appropriate footwear and gear for these conditions.','2025-03-28 01:48:58','2025-03-28 01:48:58'),(14271,'trails',384,'What historical features can I see on the Taylor Creek Trail?','While hiking the trail, you will encounter two historic homestead cabins built in the early 1930s, adding a touch of history to your scenic hike.','2025-03-28 01:48:58','2025-03-28 01:48:58'),(14272,'trails',385,'What is the length of the Grotto Trail?','The Grotto Trail is a leisurely hike that spans 1.0 mile (1.6 km) round trip.','2025-03-28 01:49:05','2025-03-28 01:49:05'),(14273,'trails',385,'Where does the Grotto Trail start and end?','The trail connects shuttle stop #5 at the Zion Lodge to shuttle stop #6 at The Grotto.','2025-03-28 01:49:05','2025-03-28 01:49:05'),(14274,'trails',385,'What can I expect in terms of terrain on the Grotto Trail?','This trail is mostly flat and shaded, making it suitable for a relaxing walk while also being slightly elevated, climbing around 35 feet (11 m).','2025-03-28 01:49:05','2025-03-28 01:49:05'),(14275,'trails',385,'Is the Grotto Trail accessible for everyone?','While the trail is generally wide and flat, it does feature a rocky and narrow section. Therefore, it may pose some challenges for those with mobility difficulties.','2025-03-28 01:49:05','2025-03-28 01:49:05'),(14276,'trails',385,'What kind of wildlife might I see along the Grotto Trail?','Hikers may encounter various wildlife, including birds, turkeys, and deer, enhancing the natural experience.','2025-03-28 01:49:05','2025-03-28 01:49:05'),(14277,'trails',385,'Are there restroom facilities available on the trail?','Yes, restrooms are conveniently located at both the Zion Lodge and The Grotto.','2025-03-28 01:49:06','2025-03-28 01:49:06'),(14278,'trails',385,'Can I bring my dog on the Grotto Trail?','Yes, dogs are permitted on the Grotto Trail.','2025-03-28 01:49:06','2025-03-28 01:49:06'),(14279,'trails',385,'Can the Grotto Trail be combined with other hikes?','Yes, hikers can connect the Grotto Trail with the Emerald Pools and Kayenta Trails to create a delightful loop.','2025-03-28 01:49:06','2025-03-28 01:49:06'),(14280,'trails',386,'Where does the Watchman Trail start?','The Watchman Trail begins at the Zion Canyon Visitor Center.','2025-03-28 01:49:14','2025-03-28 01:49:14'),(14281,'trails',386,'What is the difficulty level of the Watchman Trail?','The Watchman Trail is categorized as a moderate hike.','2025-03-28 01:49:14','2025-03-28 01:49:14'),(14282,'trails',386,'How long is the Watchman Trail?','The Watchman Trail is an out-and-back hike with a vertical gain of 368 feet (112 meters).','2025-03-28 01:49:14','2025-03-28 01:49:14'),(14283,'trails',386,'What kind of views can hikers expect from the trail?','Hikers will enjoy stunning views of the Watchman, Temples and Towers, lower Zion Canyon, and the Town of Springdale from the trail\'s endpoint.','2025-03-28 01:49:14','2025-03-28 01:49:14'),(14284,'trails',386,'What type of terrain can hikers expect on the Watchman Trail?','The trail features sandy, rocky, and uneven terrain, with a moderate uphill climb and some drop-offs.','2025-03-28 01:49:14','2025-03-28 01:49:14'),(14285,'trails',386,'Are there any facilities available at the trailhead?','Yes, restrooms and water filling stations are available at the Zion Canyon Visitor Center.','2025-03-28 01:49:14','2025-03-28 01:49:14'),(14286,'trails',386,'Can I ride my bike on the Watchman Trail?','No, bicycles are not allowed on the Watchman Trail.','2025-03-28 01:49:14','2025-03-28 01:49:14'),(14287,'trails',386,'How do I reach the trailhead from the Visitor Center?','To get to the trailhead, follow the sidewalk through the Visitor Center plaza, go past the shuttle stop, and cross at the crosswalk, then stay along the river to begin the hike.','2025-03-28 01:49:14','2025-03-28 01:49:14'),(14288,'trails',386,'Is the Watchman Trail dog-friendly?','Yes, dogs are permitted on the Watchman Trail.','2025-03-28 01:49:15','2025-03-28 01:49:15'),(14289,'trails',386,'What should I know about the trail\'s accessibility?','The trail is unpaved and consists of sandy, rocky, and uneven sections with moderate elevation changes and some cliffside overlooks.','2025-03-28 01:49:15','2025-03-28 01:49:15'),(14290,'trails',387,'What is the trail like on the Spencer Trail?','The Spencer Trail presents a challenging hike that requires navigating tricky rock and scree, traversing exposed cliffs, moving through boulders, and climbing sandy stone steps to reach a beautiful plateau.','2025-03-28 01:49:23','2025-03-28 01:49:23'),(14291,'trails',387,'What kind of views can I expect from the top of the Spencer Trail?','At the summit, hikers are rewarded with breathtaking vistas including Page, the Paria River, Lake Powell, Glen Canyon, Echo Peaks, the Vermilion Cliffs, Navajo Mountain, and Lee\'s Ferry, along with interesting historical mining relics and a sunken paddle boat.','2025-03-28 01:49:23','2025-03-28 01:49:23'),(14292,'trails',387,'How strenuous is the hike on the Spencer Trail?','Despite the short distance of 1.9 miles, the elevation gain is steep and quick, making this trail more strenuous than it may seem at first glance.','2025-03-28 01:49:23','2025-03-28 01:49:23'),(14293,'trails',387,'What are the notable historical features along the Spencer Trail?','Hikers will encounter historical sites such as the remnants of Lees Fort and nearby mining debris, as well as the sunken wreck of a paddle boat that add a sense of history to the trail.','2025-03-28 01:49:23','2025-03-28 01:49:23'),(14294,'trails',387,'What type of terrain can I expect on the Spencer Trail?','The terrain features a variety of challenges, including wide dirt roads over flat areas, exposed cliffs, boulders, and steep switchbacks as you ascend the hills.','2025-03-28 01:49:23','2025-03-28 01:49:23'),(14295,'trails',387,'What is the maximum elevation on the Spencer Trail?','The highest elevation you will reach on the Spencer Trail is 3,134 feet.','2025-03-28 01:49:24','2025-03-28 01:49:24'),(14296,'trails',387,'What is the trail’s elevation gain?','The trail features an elevation gain of 1,586 feet, contributing to its difficulty.','2025-03-28 01:49:24','2025-03-28 01:49:24'),(14297,'trails',387,'Is this trail suitable for dogs?','No, dogs are not permitted on the Spencer Trail.','2025-03-28 01:49:24','2025-03-28 01:49:24'),(14298,'trails',387,'What is the trail type of the Spencer Trail?','The Spencer Trail is a point-to-point trail.','2025-03-28 01:49:24','2025-03-28 01:49:24'),(14299,'trails',387,'What is the average and maximum grade of the trail?','The average grade of the Spencer Trail is about 0.16%, with a maximum grade reaching up to 0.36%.','2025-03-28 01:49:24','2025-03-28 01:49:24'),(14300,'trails',387,'Who is the Spencer Trail named after?','The trail is named after Charles Spencer, who was in charge of gold mining operations and originally constructed the trail to transport coal from Utah to the mine.','2025-03-28 01:49:24','2025-03-28 01:49:24'),(14301,'trails',388,'What is the difficulty level of the Horseshoe Bend Trail?','The Horseshoe Bend Trail is considered easy to intermediate, making it accessible for a wide range of hikers.','2025-03-28 01:49:32','2025-03-28 01:49:32'),(14302,'trails',388,'What are the highest and lowest elevations on the trail?','The trail has a consistent elevation, staying at 3,914 feet throughout its length.','2025-03-28 01:49:33','2025-03-28 01:49:33'),(14303,'trails',388,'How long is the Horseshoe Bend Trail?','The trail stretches for 0.7 miles, offering a short yet rewarding hike.','2025-03-28 01:49:33','2025-03-28 01:49:33'),(14304,'trails',388,'What type of trail is the Horseshoe Bend Trail?','This trail is a point-to-point path, meaning you will hike to a viewpoint and then return along the same route.','2025-03-28 01:49:33','2025-03-28 01:49:33'),(14305,'trails',388,'What is the elevation change along the trail?','Hikers will experience a total incline of 110 feet and a decline of 531 feet as they navigate the trail.','2025-03-28 01:49:33','2025-03-28 01:49:33'),(14306,'trails',388,'What is the average and maximum grade of the trail?','The average grade is quite gentle at 0.16%, with a maximum grade that reaches up to 2.73%.','2025-03-28 01:49:33','2025-03-28 01:49:33'),(14307,'trails',388,'What can I expect to see while hiking the Horseshoe Bend Trail?','The main attraction of this trail is the breathtaking views of the stunning natural wonder at Horseshoe Bend.','2025-03-28 01:49:33','2025-03-28 01:49:33'),(14308,'trails',388,'Are dogs allowed on the trail?','Yes, dogs are permitted as long as they are kept on a leash.','2025-03-28 01:49:33','2025-03-28 01:49:33'),(14309,'trails',388,'Where is Horseshoe Bend Trail located?','The trail is located at latitude 36.8767 and longitude -111.503.','2025-03-28 01:49:33','2025-03-28 01:49:33'),(14310,'trails',388,'Is the Horseshoe Bend Trail suitable for families?','Definitely! The easy terrain and short distance make it a family-friendly hike.','2025-03-28 01:49:33','2025-03-28 01:49:33'),(14311,'trails',260,'What is the overall difficulty of the trail?','The trail is classified as difficult, which may pose challenges for less experienced hikers.','2025-03-28 01:52:38','2025-03-28 01:52:38'),(14312,'trails',280,'What is the Kanab Heritage Walking Tour?','The Kanab Heritage Walking Tour is a scenic exploration of Kanab\'s historical significance, featuring a variety of historic buildings and homes throughout the city.','2025-03-28 01:52:48','2025-03-28 01:52:48'),(14313,'trails',280,'How difficult is the Kanab Heritage Walking Tour?','The tour is classified as easy, making it accessible for people of all ages and abilities.','2025-03-28 01:52:48','2025-03-28 01:52:48'),(14314,'trails',280,'Is a reservation required to join the Kanab Heritage Walking Tour?','No reservations are needed to enjoy the Kanab Heritage Walking Tour; you can embark on it at your convenience.','2025-03-28 01:52:49','2025-03-28 01:52:49'),(14315,'trails',280,'Can I bring my pet on the Kanab Heritage Walking Tour?','Pets are not permitted on the tour, so it\'s best to plan accordingly.','2025-03-28 01:52:49','2025-03-28 01:52:49'),(14316,'trails',280,'What is the best season to visit the Kanab Heritage Walking Tour?','While there\'s no specific season mentioned, the tour is particularly enjoyable during the summer months when the weather is pleasant.','2025-03-28 01:52:49','2025-03-28 01:52:49'),(14317,'trails',280,'How do I get to the Kanab Heritage Walking Tour?','The tour starts in Kanab, Utah, which is accessible by car via U.S. Highway 89.','2025-03-28 01:52:49','2025-03-28 01:52:49'),(14318,'trails',280,'What historic sites can I see on the Kanab Heritage Walking Tour?','The tour features numerous historic sites, including the Heritage House, several notable hotels, and the Monument to Major John Wesley Powell, among others.','2025-03-28 01:52:49','2025-03-28 01:52:49'),(14319,'trails',280,'Are there any additional guidelines for the Kanab Heritage Walking Tour?','It’s important to respect residents\' privacy during the tour, as some homes are private and not open to the public.','2025-03-28 01:52:49','2025-03-28 01:52:49'),(14320,'trails',280,'Where can I find more information about the Kanab Heritage Walking Tour?','For additional details, you can visit the Kane County Visitors Center located at 78 S 100 E, Kanab, Utah, or call them at 435.644.5033.','2025-03-28 01:52:49','2025-03-28 01:52:49'),(14321,'trails',280,'How long does the Kanab Heritage Walking Tour take?','The average time for the walk is not specified, allowing visitors to take their time exploring at their own pace.','2025-03-28 01:52:49','2025-03-28 01:52:49'),(14322,'trails',284,'What is the length of the Johnson Canyon Driving Tour?','The Johnson Canyon Driving Tour stretches for 2.6 miles, providing a pleasant drive through stunning scenery.','2025-03-28 01:52:57','2025-03-28 01:52:57'),(14323,'trails',284,'When is the best time to visit Johnson Canyon?','The trail does not specify a best season, but visiting during temperate weather can enhance your experience of the beautiful landscape.','2025-03-28 01:52:57','2025-03-28 01:52:57'),(14324,'trails',284,'What level of difficulty is the Johnson Canyon Driving Tour?','This driving tour is suitable for all skill levels, making it an accessible adventure for everyone.','2025-03-28 01:52:57','2025-03-28 01:52:57'),(14325,'trails',284,'What is the elevation of the Johnson Canyon area?','The elevation information is not provided, but the drive showcases varied landscapes that are enjoyable from the road.','2025-03-28 01:52:58','2025-03-28 01:52:58'),(14326,'trails',284,'Can I bring my pets on the Johnson Canyon Driving Tour?','Pet policy details are not specified; it is recommended to check local regulations before bringing pets along.','2025-03-28 01:52:58','2025-03-28 01:52:58'),(14327,'trails',284,'Is a reservation needed to experience the Johnson Canyon Driving Tour?','No reservations are required to take this scenic drive; you can enjoy it at your convenience.','2025-03-28 01:52:58','2025-03-28 01:52:58'),(14328,'trails',284,'How long should I expect to take on the Johnson Canyon Driving Tour?','There is no specified time to complete the tour, allowing you to take as long as you wish to enjoy the sights.','2025-03-28 01:52:58','2025-03-28 01:52:58'),(14329,'trails',284,'What kind of vehicle is recommended for the tour?','Most vehicles should handle the drive well; however, keep in mind that the tour ends where the pavement gives way to dirt.','2025-03-28 01:52:58','2025-03-28 01:52:58'),(14330,'trails',284,'How do I get to Johnson Canyon?','You can start your journey by turning onto Johnson Canyon Road and resetting your car\'s trip meter to begin your scenic drive.','2025-03-28 01:52:58','2025-03-28 01:52:58'),(14331,'trails',284,'What can I expect to see while driving through Johnson Canyon?','The tour showcases breathtaking scenery and interesting historic sites. Bring binoculars to spot ancient Indian and cowboy glyphs along the way.','2025-03-28 01:52:58','2025-03-28 01:52:58'),(14332,'trails',284,'What is a notable feature at Dairy Canyon?','Dairy Canyon holds significant historical value as several important Indian artifacts have been discovered here, some of which are displayed at the Kanab Heritage Museum.','2025-03-28 01:52:58','2025-03-28 01:52:58'),(14333,'trails',284,'What to know about the legend of Montezuma\'s treasure?','A fascinating local legend tells of Freddie Crystal, who arrived in the canyon with a treasure map in 1914. Though locals found multiple chambers and artifacts, the gold remains elusive!','2025-03-28 01:52:58','2025-03-28 01:52:58'),(14334,'trails',284,'What is the Grand Staircase-Escalante National Monument?','Johnson Canyon marks the entrance to the southern boundary of this expansive National Monument, which boasts nearly 2 million acres of stunning landscapes and endless outdoor adventures.','2025-03-28 01:52:59','2025-03-28 01:52:59'),(14335,'trails',319,'What is the Bryce Amphitheater known for?','The Bryce Amphitheater is famous for having the highest concentration of irregular rock formations, called \'hoodoos\', anywhere in the world.','2025-03-28 01:53:07','2025-03-28 01:53:07'),(14336,'trails',319,'Which viewpoints should I prioritize when visiting Bryce Amphitheater?','If you\'re short on time, make sure to visit Bryce Point, Inspiration Point, Sunset Point, and Sunrise Point, as these offer breathtaking views and serve as starting points for various hikes along the plateau.','2025-03-28 01:53:08','2025-03-28 01:53:08'),(14337,'trails',319,'What is the significance of the term \'amphitheater\' in relation to Bryce?','The term \'amphitheater\' refers to the bowl-shaped landscape formed by the drainage of seasonal rains and melting snow, rather than a canyon which is shaped by flowing rivers.','2025-03-28 01:53:08','2025-03-28 01:53:08'),(14338,'trails',319,'Are the viewpoints in the Bryce Amphitheater accessible?','Yes, all viewpoints in the Bryce Amphitheater are paved and designed for easy access, providing a relatively flat path to enjoy the stunning scenery. For detailed accessibility options, check the park\'s Accessibility page.','2025-03-28 01:53:08','2025-03-28 01:53:08'),(14339,'trails',319,'Can I bring my dog to the Bryce Amphitheater?','Yes, dogs are allowed in the Bryce Amphitheater area with some restrictions. Be sure to check the specific park regulations regarding pets.','2025-03-28 01:53:08','2025-03-28 01:53:08'),(14340,'trails',319,'What resources are available for learning more about the Bryce Amphitheater?','You can explore the Park App\'s \'Tours\' section for an informative guide that covers the must-see highlights of the Bryce Amphitheater.','2025-03-28 01:53:08','2025-03-28 01:53:08'),(14341,'trails',333,'What is the Night Sky Telescope Program at Bryce Canyon?','The Night Sky Telescope Program offers visitors a chance to explore the stunning dark skies of Bryce Canyon with guided tours and telescopes. Participants will learn about the science and cultural heritage of this recognized International Dark Sky Park.','2025-03-28 01:53:15','2025-03-28 01:53:15'),(14342,'trails',333,'When is the Night Sky Telescope Program available?','The program is available nightly through August 4, 2023, starting at 9:30 p.m.','2025-03-28 01:53:15','2025-03-28 01:53:15'),(14343,'trails',333,'How can I make a reservation for the program?','Reservations for the Night Sky Telescope Program are required and can be made at the Visitor Center starting at 8:15 a.m. on the day of the event.','2025-03-28 01:53:15','2025-03-28 01:53:15'),(14344,'trails',333,'Can I participate in the program if I don\'t make a reservation?','If you\'re unable to secure a reservation, there are several ways to enjoy the Bryce Canyon night sky independently. You can visit the Stargazing page for more details on enjoying the night sky on your own.','2025-03-28 01:53:16','2025-03-28 01:53:16'),(14345,'trails',333,'Is the Night Sky Telescope Program accessible?','Yes, the program is ADA accessible, ensuring everyone can participate in this celestial experience.','2025-03-28 01:53:16','2025-03-28 01:53:16'),(14346,'trails',333,'Are dogs allowed at the Night Sky Telescope Program?','Yes, dogs are permitted to join you at the Night Sky Telescope Program, but please limit it to one dog per visitor.','2025-03-28 01:53:16','2025-03-28 01:53:16'),(14347,'trails',333,'What are the geographical coordinates of Bryce Canyon?','The latitude of Bryce Canyon is 37.6404, and the longitude is -112.17.','2025-03-28 01:53:16','2025-03-28 01:53:16'),(14348,'trails',333,'Where can I find more information about programs during my visit?','For updates on available programs during your visit, be sure to check the park\'s Calendar or stop by the Visitor Center for current information.','2025-03-28 01:53:16','2025-03-28 01:53:16'),(14349,'trails',334,'What makes Bryce Canyon a great spot for stargazing?','Bryce Canyon\'s high elevation, pristine air quality, and remote setting contribute to its status as one of the best places for stargazing in the country. With International Dark Sky status since 2019, visitors can experience breathtaking views of thousands of stars and the Milky Way on clear nights, especially during the new moon.','2025-03-28 01:53:24','2025-03-28 01:53:24'),(14350,'trails',334,'What are the best viewpoints for stargazing at Bryce Canyon?','Some of the top viewpoints for an unforgettable stargazing experience include Sunset Point, Sunrise Point, Inspiration Point, and Paria View. These locations provide excellent vantage points to take in the night sky.','2025-03-28 01:53:24','2025-03-28 01:53:24'),(14351,'trails',334,'Are there special trails for night photography?','Yes! If you\'re interested in capturing night photography with the stunning hoodoos as your foreground, the Queen\'s Garden and Navajo Trails are highly recommended for their scenic views.','2025-03-28 01:53:24','2025-03-28 01:53:24'),(14352,'trails',334,'Can I participate in ranger-led programs for stargazing?','Ranger-led telescope programs may be available depending on the season and day of the week during your visit. Check the calendar or visit the Visitor Center for the latest information on available programs.','2025-03-28 01:53:24','2025-03-28 01:53:24'),(14353,'trails',334,'Is stargazing accessible for all visitors?','Yes, all recommended stargazing viewpoints are paved and accessible, although it’s a good idea to review the specific accessibility information for each location to ensure they meet your needs.','2025-03-28 01:53:24','2025-03-28 01:53:24'),(14354,'trails',334,'Are dogs allowed on the trails and viewpoints?','Yes, dogs are permitted on the trails and viewpoints, making it easier for pet owners to enjoy the stunning night sky together with their furry companions.','2025-03-28 01:53:24','2025-03-28 01:53:24'),(14355,'trails',334,'What should I check before visiting for stargazing?','Before heading out for some stargazing, be sure to check the park\'s calendar or stop by the Visitor Center to find out about any scheduled programs during your visit.','2025-03-28 01:53:25','2025-03-28 01:53:25'),(14356,'trails',334,'What is the geographic location of Bryce Canyon?','Bryce Canyon is located at a latitude of 37.5952 and a longitude of -112.171, placing it in a remote area that contributes to its exceptional night sky visibility.','2025-03-28 01:53:25','2025-03-28 01:53:25'),(14357,'trails',336,'What is the Rim Walk at Bryce Canyon National Park?','The Rim Walk is a guided one-hour experience led by a ranger, where visitors can explore the hoodoos, learn about the cultural history of the area, and discover the unique ecosystems of Bryce Canyon. It starts at Sunset Point and covers approximately 1/2 mile on a paved path.','2025-03-28 01:53:37','2025-03-28 01:53:37'),(14358,'trails',336,'Where does the Rim Walk take place?','The Rim Walk begins at Sunset Point, conveniently near the observation platform in Bryce Canyon National Park.','2025-03-28 01:53:37','2025-03-28 01:53:37'),(14359,'trails',336,'When is the Rim Walk typically offered?','This walk is usually available from Memorial Day through Labor Day, with the sessions starting at 2:00 p.m.','2025-03-28 01:53:37','2025-03-28 01:53:37'),(14360,'trails',336,'Is the Rim Walk suitable for all ages?','Yes, the Rim Walk is designed to be accessible for people of all ages, making it a family-friendly activity.','2025-03-28 01:53:37','2025-03-28 01:53:37'),(14361,'trails',336,'Is the Rim Walk accessible for individuals with mobility challenges?','Absolutely! The walk is wheelchair accessible, allowing everyone to enjoy this beautiful experience in nature.','2025-03-28 01:53:38','2025-03-28 01:53:38'),(14362,'trails',336,'What if it rains or there is bad weather?','In the event of inclement weather, the Rim Walk may be canceled, so it\'s good to check beforehand.','2025-03-28 01:53:38','2025-03-28 01:53:38'),(14363,'trails',336,'How long does the Rim Walk last?','The Rim Walk lasts about one hour, but it can vary from 45 minutes to an hour, depending on the pace of the group.','2025-03-28 01:53:38','2025-03-28 01:53:38'),(14364,'trails',336,'How far does the Rim Walk cover?','Participants will cover roughly 1/2 mile along a paved path during the walk.','2025-03-28 01:53:38','2025-03-28 01:53:38'),(14365,'trails',336,'Where can I find more information about the Rim Walk schedule?','For the latest information on available programs, it\'s a good idea to check the Calendar or visit the Visitor Center during your trip.','2025-03-28 01:53:38','2025-03-28 01:53:38'),(14366,'trails',336,'Are pets allowed on the Rim Walk?','Yes, dogs are permitted on the Rim Walk, but they must be kept under control.','2025-03-28 01:53:38','2025-03-28 01:53:38'),(14367,'trails',336,'What are the geographical coordinates of Sunset Point?','Sunset Point is located at latitude 37.6226 and longitude -112.166.','2025-03-28 01:53:38','2025-03-28 01:53:38'),(14368,'trails',337,'What time should participants arrive for the Full Moon Hike lottery?','Participants need to arrive at the Visitor Center a few minutes before 4 p.m. to enter the Full Moon Hike lottery.','2025-03-28 01:53:50','2025-03-28 01:53:50'),(14369,'trails',337,'What type of hike can participants expect during the Full Moon Hike?','During the Full Moon Hike, guests can expect a 1 to 2-mile ranger\'s choice hike, which may either be an easy stroll along the plateau\'s rim or a more challenging trek down steep, rocky trails into the canyon.','2025-03-28 01:53:50','2025-03-28 01:53:50'),(14370,'trails',337,'How can one secure a ticket for the Full Moon Hike?','Tickets for the Full Moon Hike are available through a same-day in-person lottery at the Visitor Center, which occurs at 4:00 p.m.','2025-03-28 01:53:50','2025-03-28 01:53:50'),(14371,'trails',337,'Is it necessary for the entire group to be present for the lottery?','Yes, every member of your group must be at the lottery with appropriate hiking footwear to receive a ticket. Late arrivals will not be included.','2025-03-28 01:53:50','2025-03-28 01:53:50'),(14372,'trails',337,'What should participants know about footwear for the hike?','Hiking boots or shoes with lug soles in good condition are mandatory for safety reasons, and must pass inspection at the lottery.','2025-03-28 01:53:50','2025-03-28 01:53:50'),(14373,'trails',337,'What happens if my group\'s lottery ticket is drawn?','If your ticket is drawn, only the number of participants noted on the back of the ticket will be issued hiker tickets, with a maximum of six individuals.','2025-03-28 01:53:51','2025-03-28 01:53:51'),(14374,'trails',337,'What weather conditions could lead to a cancellation of the hike?','The hike may be canceled due to cloudy skies or if the temperature drops below 10 degrees Fahrenheit (-12 degrees Celsius).','2025-03-28 01:53:51','2025-03-28 01:53:51'),(14375,'trails',337,'Are there any restrictions for children on the hike?','Unfortunately, children aged 7 and younger cannot participate in the Full Moon Hike.','2025-03-28 01:53:51','2025-03-28 01:53:51'),(14376,'trails',337,'What type of lighting is allowed during the hike?','Participants can use red light flashlights or headlamps as needed, but white light is prohibited during the hike. You may carry them for use later.','2025-03-28 01:53:51','2025-03-28 01:53:51'),(14377,'trails',337,'What should participants bring to the hike?','It is advisable to bring drinking water and a jacket, as temperatures can drop at night.','2025-03-28 01:53:51','2025-03-28 01:53:51'),(14378,'trails',337,'Is the Full Moon Hike accessible for individuals using wheelchairs?','No, due to the steep and rocky nature of the trails, the Full Moon Hike is not wheelchair accessible.','2025-03-28 01:53:51','2025-03-28 01:53:51'),(14379,'trails',337,'Are pets allowed on the Full Moon Hike?','Yes, one dog is allowed to accompany participants on the hike.','2025-03-28 01:53:51','2025-03-28 01:53:51'),(14380,'trails',337,'How can I get more information about the Full Moon Hike lottery?','For more details about the lottery, feel free to reach out via email at brca_information@nps.gov.','2025-03-28 01:53:52','2025-03-28 01:53:52'),(14381,'trails',337,'When are the scheduled dates for the Full Moon Hike in 2023?','The scheduled Full Moon Hikes for 2023 are on January 4, February 4, March 7, May 5, June 3, July 3, August 1, September 29, November 27, and December 26.','2025-03-28 01:53:52','2025-03-28 01:53:52'),(14382,'trails',337,'Is flash photography allowed during the hike?','Flash photography may be allowed under specific restrictions.','2025-03-28 01:53:52','2025-03-28 01:53:52'),(14383,'trails',338,'What time do the evening programs at Bryce Canyon National Park start?','The evening programs at Bryce Canyon National Park commence at 8:30 p.m.','2025-03-28 01:54:00','2025-03-28 01:54:00'),(14384,'trails',338,'Where do the evening programs take place?','These engaging programs are held in the historic Bryce Canyon Lodge auditorium.','2025-03-28 01:54:00','2025-03-28 01:54:00'),(14385,'trails',338,'What topics might be covered in the evening ranger programs?','The ranger-led sessions cover a variety of fascinating topics including navigation, the health benefits of nature, the beauty of moonlight, thunderstorms, geological features, thrilling stories, and adaptive strategies of wildlife, among others.','2025-03-28 01:54:00','2025-03-28 01:54:00'),(14386,'trails',338,'When are the evening programs offered?','Evening programs are typically available from Memorial Day to Labor Day, showcasing the captivating stories and unique features of Bryce Canyon National Park.','2025-03-28 01:54:00','2025-03-28 01:54:00'),(14387,'trails',338,'Where can I find the schedule of programs during my visit?','You can check the daily program schedule at the Visitor Center or on the Calendar for updated information about available programs during your stay.','2025-03-28 01:54:01','2025-03-28 01:54:01'),(14388,'trails',338,'What are some of the specific programs offered in 2023?','In 2023, some featured programs include \'Finding Your Way – Introduction to Navigation,\' \'Flower Power and the Effects of Nature on Your Health and Wellbeing,\' \'The Lighter Side of the Moon,\' and \'Scary Stories to Tell in the Dark: Fire in Bryce Canyon,\' among others.','2025-03-28 01:54:01','2025-03-28 01:54:01'),(14389,'trails',338,'Is the evening program accessible for all visitors?','Yes, the evening program is a seated event and is accessible to attendees.','2025-03-28 01:54:01','2025-03-28 01:54:01'),(14390,'trails',338,'Are dogs allowed at the evening programs?','Yes, dogs are permitted at the evening programs, with a limit of one per guest.','2025-03-28 01:54:01','2025-03-28 01:54:01'),(14391,'trails',338,'What are the geographic coordinates of Bryce Canyon?','The geographic coordinates of Bryce Canyon are approximately latitude 37.627 and longitude -112.168.','2025-03-28 01:54:01','2025-03-28 01:54:01'),(14392,'trails',339,'What is the Hoodoo Geology Talk?','The Hoodoo Geology Talk is an informative ranger-led session at Sunset Point where you can learn about the unique evolution of the hoodoos and the different groups of people who have historically visited Bryce Canyon\'s stunning amphitheaters.','2025-03-28 01:54:11','2025-03-28 01:54:11'),(14393,'trails',339,'Is any walking required to attend the Hoodoo Geology Talk?','No walking is required to attend this event as it takes place on a paved surface along the rim of the Bryce Canyon Amphitheater.','2025-03-28 01:54:11','2025-03-28 01:54:11'),(14394,'trails',339,'When is the Hoodoo Geology Talk scheduled?','The talk is typically held year-round at 11 a.m. at Sunset Point, but it\'s a good idea to check the Calendar or visit the Visitor Center for exact times and available programs during your visit.','2025-03-28 01:54:11','2025-03-28 01:54:11'),(14395,'trails',339,'What can I expect to see at Sunset Point during the talk?','You can expect to be wowed by the breathtaking views of the amphitheater filled with magical hoodoos that may leave you with many questions about their formation and history.','2025-03-28 01:54:11','2025-03-28 01:54:11'),(14396,'trails',339,'Is the Hoodoo Geology Talk accessible for everyone?','Yes, the talk is accessible as it does not involve walking and is held along the rim where participants stand. However, no seating is provided, so you may want to bring your own portable seating if needed.','2025-03-28 01:54:11','2025-03-28 01:54:11'),(14397,'trails',339,'Are dogs allowed at the Hoodoo Geology Talk?','Yes, dogs are permitted at this event, allowing you to bring your furry friend to enjoy the talk with you.','2025-03-28 01:54:11','2025-03-28 01:54:11'),(14398,'trails',339,'What geographic coordinates define Sunset Point?','Sunset Point is located at a latitude of 37.6226 and a longitude of -112.166.','2025-03-28 01:54:11','2025-03-28 01:54:11'),(14399,'trails',340,'What is a ranger-led snowshoe hike?','A ranger-led snowshoe hike is an organized outdoor activity where participants can explore the winter landscape of Bryce Canyon under the guidance of a park ranger.','2025-03-28 01:54:22','2025-03-28 01:54:22'),(14400,'trails',340,'What can I expect to see on this hike?','Hikers will enjoy the stunning contrast of freshly fallen white snow against red rocks, clear blue skies, and evergreen trees, creating a breathtaking winter scenery.','2025-03-28 01:54:22','2025-03-28 01:54:22'),(14401,'trails',340,'What is the distance of the hike?','The snowshoe hike covers approximately 1 mile (1.6 km), making it accessible for most participants.','2025-03-28 01:54:22','2025-03-28 01:54:22'),(14402,'trails',340,'Where can I sign up for the hike?','Sign-up is available at the Visitor Center starting at 8 a.m. on the day of the hike and continues until the spots are filled, but there are no advance reservations.','2025-03-28 01:54:22','2025-03-28 01:54:22'),(14403,'trails',340,'What equipment is provided for the snowshoe hike?','Snowshoes and poles will be provided at no cost to participants, as long as the snow conditions and staffing allow.','2025-03-28 01:54:22','2025-03-28 01:54:22'),(14404,'trails',340,'What should I wear for the snowshoe hike?','It is essential to wear winter clothing, bring water, and have waterproof boots. Note that tennis shoes are not allowed for safety and comfort.','2025-03-28 01:54:23','2025-03-28 01:54:23'),(14405,'trails',340,'Is the hike suitable for beginners?','Yes, the snowshoe hike is designed for all levels of experience, from beginners to seasoned hikers.','2025-03-28 01:54:23','2025-03-28 01:54:23'),(14406,'trails',340,'Is this hike accessible for individuals with disabilities?','Unfortunately, this particular snowshoe hike is not ADA accessible due to the nature of the activity.','2025-03-28 01:54:23','2025-03-28 01:54:23'),(14407,'trails',340,'Can I bring my dog on the hike?','Yes, dogs are allowed on the snowshoe hike, but it’s best to confirm any specific regulations ahead of time.','2025-03-28 01:54:23','2025-03-28 01:54:23'),(14408,'trails',340,'What is the elevation of Bryce Canyon where the hike takes place?','The snowshoe hike occurs at an elevation of 8,000 feet (2,438 meters), where the winter scenery transforms dramatically.','2025-03-28 01:54:23','2025-03-28 01:54:23'),(14409,'trails',341,'What is the location of the CCC Picnic Area?','The CCC Picnic Area can be found at mile 4.75 along the beautiful 18-mile Southern Scenic Drive.','2025-03-28 01:54:31','2025-03-28 01:54:31'),(14410,'trails',341,'Is the CCC Picnic Area a good spot for a picnic?','Absolutely! The CCC Picnic Area offers breathtaking views of the surrounding landscapes, making it a perfect place for a relaxing picnic.','2025-03-28 01:54:31','2025-03-28 01:54:31'),(14411,'trails',341,'Are there other picnic areas in Bryce Canyon?','Yes, besides the CCC Picnic Area, you can find several picnic spots in Bryce Canyon, including the Amphitheater Area, North Campground Picnic Area, General Store, Sunset Point, Whiteman Bench Picnic Area, Rainbow Point, and one outside the park at the Bryce Canyon Shuttle Station.','2025-03-28 01:54:31','2025-03-28 01:54:31'),(14412,'trails',341,'What should I know about wildlife while picnicking?','It\'s important to remember that federal law prohibits feeding any wildlife in the park. Be cautious, as some animals may be near the trails and roads, and should not be approached because they can be dangerous.','2025-03-28 01:54:31','2025-03-28 01:54:31'),(14413,'trails',341,'How accessible are the picnic areas?','All picnic areas utilize unpaved surfaces made of firm native sediment. Although these surfaces are typically hard-packed, they might become muddy and harder to walk on after rain or snow. Each picnic area is conveniently located near paved sidewalks or parking areas.','2025-03-28 01:54:31','2025-03-28 01:54:31'),(14414,'trails',341,'Are dogs allowed in the picnic areas?','Yes, you are permitted to bring dogs in the picnic areas, but please keep in mind that there is a limit to one dog per group.','2025-03-28 01:54:31','2025-03-28 01:54:31'),(14415,'trails',341,'What are the latitude and longitude coordinates of the CCC Picnic Area?','The coordinates for the CCC Picnic Area are 37.6067° N latitude and -112.2° W longitude.','2025-03-28 01:54:31','2025-03-28 01:54:31'),(14416,'trails',344,'How can I become a Junior Ranger at Bryce Canyon National Park?','To become a Junior Ranger at Bryce Canyon, you will need to complete two main tasks: first, learn about the park by visiting the park museum, attending a ranger-led presentation or hike, or watching the park movie. Second, work through the activity booklet that corresponds to your age by completing a number of activities equal to your age. After finishing these tasks, return to the Visitor Center for your induction as a Junior Ranger, and you\'ll receive a free badge along with other unique souvenirs.','2025-03-28 01:54:46','2025-03-28 01:54:46'),(14417,'trails',344,'Where can I get my Junior Ranger booklet?','You can obtain your Junior Ranger booklet from the rangers at the front desk of the Visitor Center, where they\'ll also reward you with your badge. If you prefer, you can also download the Bryce Canyon Junior Ranger book from the park\'s website and print it before your visit.','2025-03-28 01:54:46','2025-03-28 01:54:46'),(14418,'trails',344,'What should I do if I get stuck on an activity in the Junior Ranger booklet?','If you\'re having trouble with an activity in the booklet, you can find hints and helpful tips on our Junior Ranger webpage. Additionally, park rangers are available for assistance if you need further help.','2025-03-28 01:54:47','2025-03-28 01:54:47'),(14419,'trails',344,'Can I complete the Junior Ranger booklet from home?','Absolutely! If you finish your booklet at home, simply take a picture of your favorite page along with an adult\'s signature on it to verify your completion, and email it to brca_information@nps.gov. Don\'t forget to include your mailing address, and share what you enjoyed about that activity. Once your email is received, we\'ll send you a Junior Ranger sticker badge!','2025-03-28 01:54:47','2025-03-28 01:54:47'),(14420,'trails',344,'Will I receive a physical badge by mail?','While we cannot send physical badges due to shipping costs, you\'ll receive a gold foil Junior Ranger sticker badge instead. If you prefer a wooden badge, you will need to send a pre-paid bubble envelope to cover the shipping costs.','2025-03-28 01:54:47','2025-03-28 01:54:47'),(14421,'trails',344,'What address should I use to send my pre-paid envelope for a wooden badge?','You can mail your pre-paid envelope to the following address: Bryce Canyon National Park, PO Box 640201, Bryce, UT 84764. Ensure your envelope is a padded bubble type and has First Class package postage.','2025-03-28 01:54:47','2025-03-28 01:54:47'),(14422,'trails',344,'Is there an accessible version of the Junior Ranger book?','Yes, a 508-compliant version of the Junior Ranger booklet is available online for those who need accessible formats.','2025-03-28 01:54:47','2025-03-28 01:54:47'),(14423,'trails',344,'Are dogs allowed at Bryce Canyon National Park?','Yes, dogs are permitted in certain areas of Bryce Canyon National Park, but it\'s essential to check the park regulations for specific restrictions.','2025-03-28 01:54:47','2025-03-28 01:54:47'),(14424,'trails',346,'What film is featured in the Visitor Center theater?','The film \'A Song of Seasons\' is showcased in the Visitor Center theater, providing a visual and narrative experience of the region\'s natural beauty.','2025-03-28 01:54:54','2025-03-28 01:54:54'),(14425,'trails',346,'When does \'A Song of Seasons\' play?','\'A Song of Seasons\' is shown every half hour during the open hours of the Visitor Center.','2025-03-28 01:54:54','2025-03-28 01:54:54'),(14426,'trails',346,'Can I watch \'A Song of Seasons\' online?','Yes, the film is available for online viewing.','2025-03-28 01:54:54','2025-03-28 01:54:54'),(14427,'trails',346,'Is the film accessible for those with hearing impairments?','Absolutely! The film comes with captions and, upon request, assisted listening devices are available.','2025-03-28 01:54:54','2025-03-28 01:54:54'),(14428,'trails',346,'Is the Visitor Center theater accessible for all?','Yes, the theater is fully accessible to accommodate all visitors.','2025-03-28 01:54:54','2025-03-28 01:54:54'),(14429,'trails',346,'Are dogs allowed in the Visitor Center?','Yes, dogs are permitted, with specific guidelines applying.','2025-03-28 01:54:54','2025-03-28 01:54:54'),(14430,'trails',346,'What are the geographical coordinates of the Visitor Center?','The Visitor Center is located at a latitude of 37.6401 and a longitude of -112.17.','2025-03-28 01:54:55','2025-03-28 01:54:55'),(14431,'trails',347,'What are some easy hikes available in the park?','In the park, you\'ll find several easy hikes, including Mossy Cave at 0.8 miles (1.3 km), the beautiful Sunset to Sunrise along the Rim Trail at 1.0 mile (1.6 km), and the unique Bristlecone Loop, also at 1.0 mile (1.6 km).','2025-03-28 01:55:04','2025-03-28 01:55:04'),(14432,'trails',347,'What is the elevation at the park and how does it affect hiking?','The park sits primarily above 8,000 feet (2,438 m), where oxygen levels are about 70% of what you\'d find at sea level. This can make hiking feel more strenuous, so it\'s advisable to choose hikes that match your abilities and to take it easy.','2025-03-28 01:55:04','2025-03-28 01:55:04'),(14433,'trails',347,'What precautions should hikers take regarding UV exposure?','At high elevations, UV radiation is significantly stronger, so it\'s important to protect your skin and eyes. Wear sunscreen, clothing that covers your skin, and sunglasses to help shield yourself from the sun\'s rays.','2025-03-28 01:55:04','2025-03-28 01:55:04'),(14434,'trails',347,'What should I know about the weather and potential storms?','Storms can develop rapidly in this park, particularly during the summer. If you hear thunder, it\'s essential to seek shelter immediately, as lightning poses a serious danger. Seek refuge in a building, vehicle, or find a sheltered depression if you\'re on a trail.','2025-03-28 01:55:04','2025-03-28 01:55:04'),(14435,'trails',347,'How much water should I bring while hiking?','Due to the lower oxygen levels, you\'ll dehydrate more quickly while hiking. It\'s recommended to bring about one liter of water for every 1 to 2 hours of your hike, as there are no water sources available on the trails.','2025-03-28 01:55:04','2025-03-28 01:55:04'),(14436,'trails',347,'What footwear is best for hiking in the park?','Proper footwear is crucial, as loose rocks on the trails can easily cause slips and injuries. It\'s best to wear shoes with good tread and ankle support. In winter, using footwear traction devices is highly recommended to navigate icy conditions safely.','2025-03-28 01:55:04','2025-03-28 01:55:04'),(14437,'trails',347,'Are there any accessible trails in the park?','The only fully accessible trail in the park is a 0.5-mile (0.8 km) segment of the Sunset to Sunrise section along the Rim Trail. Other trails may have varying degrees of accessibility.','2025-03-28 01:55:04','2025-03-28 01:55:04'),(14438,'trails',347,'Are dogs allowed on the trails?','Yes, dogs are permitted on the trails within the park, so you can bring your furry friends along for your hiking adventures.','2025-03-28 01:55:05','2025-03-28 01:55:05'),(14439,'trails',348,'Where can I collect the cancellation stamp for Bryce Canyon?','You can find the cancellation stamp at the passport counter in the back right corner of the Visitor Center. It\'s a great way to commemorate your visit!','2025-03-28 01:55:08','2025-03-28 01:55:08'),(14440,'trails',348,'Is the Bryce Canyon Visitor Center accessible for all visitors?','Yes, the Visitor Center at Bryce Canyon is fully accessible, ensuring that everyone can enjoy the facilities.','2025-03-28 01:55:08','2025-03-28 01:55:08'),(14441,'trails',348,'Are dogs allowed in Bryce Canyon National Park?','Yes, dogs are permitted in Bryce Canyon with a limit of one dog per visitor.','2025-03-28 01:55:08','2025-03-28 01:55:08'),(14442,'trails',348,'What are the latitude and longitude coordinates for Bryce Canyon?','The coordinates for Bryce Canyon are approximately 37.6404° N latitude and 112.17° W longitude.','2025-03-28 01:55:08','2025-03-28 01:55:08'),(14443,'trails',349,'What is the \'Hike the Hoodoos!\' program?','The \'Hike the Hoodoos!\' program encourages visitors to stay active while enjoying the beauty of Bryce Canyon National Park. Participants hike at least 3 miles along designated trails and locate benchmark survey markers, earning a special reward upon completion.','2025-03-28 01:55:19','2025-03-28 01:55:19'),(14444,'trails',349,'How can hikers participate in the program?','Visitors can join by hiking a minimum of 3 miles on marked trails and finding benchmark markers. They can either take rubbings of the benchmarks or snap photographs with them to verify their hike before claiming a reward at the Visitor Center.','2025-03-28 01:55:20','2025-03-28 01:55:20'),(14445,'trails',349,'How many benchmarks are there and where are they located?','There are nine \'Hike the Hoodoos!\' benchmarks spread across eight different hiking trails in Bryce Canyon National Park.','2025-03-28 01:55:20','2025-03-28 01:55:20'),(14446,'trails',349,'What is the total distance if someone wants to collect all the benchmarks?','Although only 3 miles are needed for the reward, if hikers wish to collect rubbings or photos from all nine benchmarks, they\'ll complete a total of 18.4 miles of hiking!','2025-03-28 01:55:20','2025-03-28 01:55:20'),(14447,'trails',349,'What are the available trails and distances for the benchmarks?','Here are the trails and the corresponding distances: Mossy Cave (0.8 mi), Bristlecone Loop (1.0 mi), Queen\'s Garden (1.8 mi), Navajo Loop (1.3 mi), Tower Bridge (3.0 mi), Swamp Canyon Loop (4.0 mi), Peekaboo Loop (5.5 mi with 2 benchmarks), and Fairyland Loop (8.0 mi with 2 benchmarks).','2025-03-28 01:55:20','2025-03-28 01:55:20'),(14448,'trails',349,'Can I combine trails to fulfill the program\'s hiking requirement?','Yes! Many hikers combine the Queen\'s Garden and Navajo Loop trails to complete a 3-mile loop known as the Queen\'s/Navajo Loop, enabling them to collect two benchmarks.','2025-03-28 01:55:20','2025-03-28 01:55:20'),(14449,'trails',349,'Are there any accessibility considerations for these trails?','Service animals are allowed on all trails, but please note that the trails are not wheelchair accessible due to uneven surfaces, steep grades, and loose rocks.','2025-03-28 01:55:20','2025-03-28 01:55:20'),(14450,'trails',349,'Are pets allowed on the hiking trails?','Yes, dogs are permitted on the trails, but they must be well-behaved and kept under control at all times.','2025-03-28 01:55:20','2025-03-28 01:55:20'),(14451,'trails',349,'Was \'Hike the Hoodoos!\' program funded by any grants?','The program was supported by a grant from the National Park Foundation, thanks to the generous contribution from the Coca-Cola Foundation.','2025-03-28 01:55:20','2025-03-28 01:55:20'),(14452,'trails',350,'What types of wildlife can I expect to see in Bryce Canyon National Park?','Bryce Canyon National Park is rich in wildlife, including migratory hummingbirds, nesting Peregrine Falcons, Rocky Mountain Elk, and Pronghorn. These animals traverse the canyons, plateaus, and forests of the park as they search for food and water.','2025-03-28 01:55:33','2025-03-28 01:55:33'),(14453,'trails',350,'How should I interact with wildlife while hiking?','It\'s important to treat wildlife with respect, as they are in their natural habitat. Avoid feeding animals, as it can lead to harmful behaviors or health issues. Maintain a safe distance by using binoculars or a telephoto lens for photography, and always stay on designated trails.','2025-03-28 01:55:33','2025-03-28 01:55:33'),(14454,'trails',350,'Are there any safety precautions to consider regarding wildlife?','When hiking in areas where venomous snakes might be present, wear boots and loose-fitting pants. Ensure that food and scented items are properly secured at least 10 feet above ground, using bear-proof containers whenever possible.','2025-03-28 01:55:33','2025-03-28 01:55:33'),(14455,'trails',350,'What should I do if I encounter a bear or mountain lion?','If you come across a bear, back away slowly while avoiding direct eye contact. For mountain lions, maintain eye contact and do not run. Make yourself appear larger by raising your arms and make noise to encourage them to leave.','2025-03-28 01:55:33','2025-03-28 01:55:33'),(14456,'trails',350,'What wildlife can I expect to see in different seasons?','Spring arrives late at these high elevations, affecting wildlife visibility. While some animals like Mule Deer can be seen year-round, others like Pronghorn are typically absent until spring, and creatures such as black bears hibernate and are rarely seen until summer.','2025-03-28 01:55:33','2025-03-28 01:55:33'),(14457,'trails',350,'Where can I find Utah Prairie Dogs in the park?','You can spot Utah Prairie Dog colonies at several locations: near the main road south of the Visitor Center, around Mile 2 on the park road, and on the way to Sunrise Point. It\'s wise to observe them from designated pull-offs to stay safe.','2025-03-28 01:55:33','2025-03-28 01:55:33'),(14458,'trails',350,'What kinds of wildlife can I find around the Southern Scenic Drive?','The Southern Scenic Drive leads to higher elevations where diverse wildlife is often spotted in meadows, particularly near Mile 4 of the park road. Keep an eye out for larger mammals crossing the road in these areas.','2025-03-28 01:55:33','2025-03-28 01:55:33'),(14459,'trails',350,'What wildlife might I see around Bryce Amphitheater?','At Bryce Amphitheater, you can often see chipmunks, ground squirrels, and families of mule deer foraging in the forests. For those interested in nighttime wildlife, ringtails may be spotted near the Sunset Point parking lot.','2025-03-28 01:55:33','2025-03-28 01:55:33'),(14460,'trails',350,'Is the park accessible for individuals with disabilities?','Yes, many viewpoints in Bryce Canyon have paved, flat surfaces making them accessible. However, trail accessibility can vary, so it\'s advisable to check the park\'s Accessibility page for detailed information.','2025-03-28 01:55:33','2025-03-28 01:55:33'),(14461,'trails',350,'Are dogs allowed in Bryce Canyon National Park?','Yes, dogs are allowed in certain areas of Bryce Canyon National Park, but there are restrictions on where they can go, so it\'s important to check the guidelines before your visit.','2025-03-28 01:55:33','2025-03-28 01:55:33'),(14462,'trails',351,'How many bird species can I see in Bryce Canyon National Park?','Bryce Canyon National Park is home to over 175 different bird species. Some are migratory, while others can be found year-round or during specific seasons.','2025-03-28 01:55:48','2025-03-28 01:55:48'),(14463,'trails',351,'What types of birds can I expect to see while birdwatching?','You can observe a variety of birds including western bluebirds, American robins, various hummingbirds, hermit thrushes, and Townsend\'s solitaires, among many others.','2025-03-28 01:55:48','2025-03-28 01:55:48'),(14464,'trails',351,'When is the best time to see certain bird species?','The best time to see birds varies by season. For instance, western bluebirds and American robins return around late February to March, while warblers appear later, usually by late April or May. The busy breeding season extends from May to July.','2025-03-28 01:55:49','2025-03-28 01:55:49'),(14465,'trails',351,'Where are the best locations for birdwatching in the park?','Some prime birdwatching spots include the Southern Scenic Drive, Bryce Amphitheater, Mossy Cave, and Tropic Trail. Each area offers unique habitats that attract different species.','2025-03-28 01:55:49','2025-03-28 01:55:49'),(14466,'trails',351,'Can I participate in birdwatching events?','Yes! If you visit in December, consider joining the annual Christmas Bird Count, a fun event for bird enthusiasts.','2025-03-28 01:55:49','2025-03-28 01:55:49'),(14467,'trails',351,'What kinds of birds can I find along the Southern Scenic Drive?','At elevated areas along the Southern Scenic Drive, look for species like dusky grouse, peregrine falcons, and Clark\'s nutcracker among the mixed conifer woodlands.','2025-03-28 01:55:49','2025-03-28 01:55:49'),(14468,'trails',351,'What birds can I see in the Bryce Amphitheater area?','In the Bryce Amphitheater, keep an eye out for pygmy nuthatches and, in winter, mixed flocks of chickadees and juncos. You may also spot summer swallows and various owls.','2025-03-28 01:55:49','2025-03-28 01:55:49'),(14469,'trails',351,'What makes Mossy Cave a notable birdwatching spot?','Mossy Cave is one of the few consistent water sources in the park, which draws various bird species. Look for flycatchers and warblers near the vegetation around the water.','2025-03-28 01:55:49','2025-03-28 01:55:49'),(14470,'trails',351,'What can I expect when hiking the Tropic Trail?','The Tropic Trail is less crowded and features lush vegetation, making it an ideal spot for spotting towhees, jays, and nuthatches, and occasionally, unexpected species like acorn woodpeckers.','2025-03-28 01:55:49','2025-03-28 01:55:49'),(14471,'trails',351,'Are there good birdwatching opportunities outside the park?','Absolutely! Near Bryce Canyon City, you can explore open fields and water ponds that attract a multitude of birds, including larks and raptors.','2025-03-28 01:55:50','2025-03-28 01:55:50'),(14472,'trails',351,'Are the viewpoints and trails accessible for everyone?','Yes, the viewpoints feature paved and flat surfaces accessible to all. However, the trail accessibility may vary, so check the park\'s Accessibility page for more details.','2025-03-28 01:55:50','2025-03-28 01:55:50'),(14473,'trails',351,'Are dogs allowed on the trails?','Yes, dogs are permitted, but be sure to follow the park’s guidelines and regulations regarding pets.','2025-03-28 01:55:50','2025-03-28 01:55:50'),(14474,'trails',353,'What can I learn from the Native Perspectives video?','The Native Perspectives video offers valuable insights into the area\'s history and significance from Native viewpoints. It\'s a 24-minute film available in the Human History section of the museum.','2025-03-28 01:55:57','2025-03-28 01:55:57'),(14475,'trails',353,'Where can I find the park museum?','The park museum is located inside the Visitor Center and features a variety of exhibits that explore geological, ecological, and human timelines, along with unique displays about the Night Sky and Air Quality.','2025-03-28 01:55:57','2025-03-28 01:55:57'),(14476,'trails',353,'Is the museum recommended for Jr. Rangers?','Absolutely! If you\'re working on your Jr. Ranger book, visiting the museum is highly encouraged. You\'ll find answers to many activities, particularly for the Prairie Dog crossword puzzle!','2025-03-28 01:55:57','2025-03-28 01:55:57'),(14477,'trails',353,'What are the accessibility features of the Visitor Center?','The Visitor Center includes two gently sloping ramps for easy access from the parking lot. It has a lowered information desk, a fully accessible auditorium that shows a captioned 24-minute film, and assisted listening and audio description devices available on request. The restrooms also feature fully accessible stalls.','2025-03-28 01:55:57','2025-03-28 01:55:57'),(14478,'trails',353,'Are dogs allowed in the Visitor Center?','Yes, you are allowed to bring one dog into the Visitor Center.','2025-03-28 01:55:57','2025-03-28 01:55:57'),(14479,'trails',353,'What are the GPS coordinates of the Visitor Center?','The GPS coordinates for the Visitor Center are Latitude 37.6401 and Longitude -112.17.','2025-03-28 01:55:57','2025-03-28 01:55:57'),(14480,'trails',355,'Where does the South Rim Trail start?','The South Rim Trail begins at the Point Supreme parking lot.','2025-03-28 01:56:05','2025-03-28 01:56:05'),(14481,'trails',355,'What can I expect to see on the South Rim Trail?','Hikers can enjoy stunning views of hoodoos, arches, waterfalls, and more as the trail meanders along the edge of the amphitheater at Cedar Breaks National Monument.','2025-03-28 01:56:05','2025-03-28 01:56:05'),(14482,'trails',355,'What makes the South Rim Trail a great hiking experience?','The South Rim Trail provides one of the premier hiking experiences within Cedar Breaks, featuring dramatic vistas and unique formations along the rim of the Cedar Breaks Amphitheater.','2025-03-28 01:56:05','2025-03-28 01:56:05'),(14483,'trails',355,'How long is the South Rim Trail?','The trail runs from Point Supreme to the Bartizan, allowing hikers to explore various scenic viewpoints along its course.','2025-03-28 01:56:05','2025-03-28 01:56:05'),(14484,'trails',355,'Is the South Rim Trail accessible for everyone?','This trail is a narrow dirt path that has varying elevations, including some steep sections with water-breaks or small stairs installed to help prevent erosion.','2025-03-28 01:56:05','2025-03-28 01:56:05'),(14485,'trails',355,'Are dogs allowed on the South Rim Trail?','Yes, dogs are permitted on the South Rim Trail.','2025-03-28 01:56:05','2025-03-28 01:56:05'),(14486,'trails',361,'What can I expect to see on the Cathedral Wash Trail?','On the Cathedral Wash Trail, hikers are treated to stunning canyon walls that soar upward as you venture deeper into the landscape. You\'ll encounter fascinating geological formations, including Kaibab Limestone and Toroweap, culminating in a breathtaking view of the Colorado River at Cathedral Wash Rapid.','2025-03-28 01:56:13','2025-03-28 01:56:13'),(14487,'trails',361,'How do I get to the trailhead for Cathedral Wash?','To reach the trailhead, start by traveling to Lees Ferry, which is accessible 42 miles from Page via Hwy 89 south and Hwy 89A west. If you\'re coming from the North Rim of the Grand Canyon, it’s about 85 miles via Hwy 89A and Hwy 67. Once you arrive, follow the Lees Ferry access road for 1.3 miles after turning off Hwy 89A, and you’ll find the trailhead pull-out on your left.','2025-03-28 01:56:13','2025-03-28 01:56:13'),(14488,'trails',361,'What kind of trail conditions can I expect?','The trail follows a predominantly dry wash with some uneven terrain. While there are no significant technical challenges, you will need to scramble over rocks and make thoughtful choices to navigate around ledges and drop-offs. The trail features steep descents, narrow paths, soft sand, and some puddles leading down to the sandy riverbank.','2025-03-28 01:56:13','2025-03-28 01:56:13'),(14489,'trails',361,'Can I bring my dog on the Cathedral Wash Trail?','Yes, dogs are allowed on the Cathedral Wash Trail, but make sure to keep them safe and on a leash as you explore.','2025-03-28 01:56:13','2025-03-28 01:56:13'),(14490,'trails',361,'What is the geographical location of Cathedral Wash?','The coordinates for Cathedral Wash are approximately latitude 36.8342 and longitude -111.64, placing it within a stunning area of Arizona\'s natural scenery.','2025-03-28 01:56:14','2025-03-28 01:56:14'),(14491,'trails',361,'Is there any specific naming significance for the Cathedral Wash?','Yes, the trail is named after the impressive Cathedral Rock which overlooks the canyon\'s head. This rock formation gives the canyon its unique character, reminiscent of a grand cathedral.','2025-03-28 01:56:14','2025-03-28 01:56:14'),(14492,'trails',363,'Where can I find the big relief map of Glen Canyon?','You can explore the big relief map at the Glen Canyon Conservancy\'s flagship store, located at 12 Lake Powell Blvd in the City of Page.','2025-03-28 01:56:23','2025-03-28 01:56:23'),(14493,'trails',363,'What is special about the relief map?','The relief map is an incredibly accurate representation of the Glen Canyon National Recreation Area and its surroundings, showcasing the area\'s topography based on actual topographic maps and aerial photographs.','2025-03-28 01:56:23','2025-03-28 01:56:23'),(14494,'trails',363,'How was the relief map created?','Bob Miller, the map builder, constructed the model over a year using topographic maps and overflights, carefully crafting it in his basement before it was transported in seven pieces to the Glen Canyon Visitor Center.','2025-03-28 01:56:24','2025-03-28 01:56:24'),(14495,'trails',363,'Can I use the map for navigation?','Absolutely! The map is oriented to match the real landscape, making it an excellent tool for wayfinding and appreciating the natural wonders of the area.','2025-03-28 01:56:24','2025-03-28 01:56:24'),(14496,'trails',363,'What unique features are included in the map?','The map features 12 natural bridges and arches embedded in its topography. See if you can spot all of them!','2025-03-28 01:56:24','2025-03-28 01:56:24'),(14497,'trails',363,'What happened to the relief map over the years?','The relief map was removed during updates at the Carl Hayden Visitor Center in 2017, but in 2019, it was retrieved and reassembled by the Glen Canyon Conservancy in their flagship store for public enjoyment.','2025-03-28 01:56:24','2025-03-28 01:56:24'),(14498,'trails',363,'Is the relief map accessible to everyone?','Yes, the map is around three feet high and twelve feet long, surrounded by a railing to allow wheelchair access, and service animals are welcome.','2025-03-28 01:56:24','2025-03-28 01:56:24'),(14499,'trails',363,'Are dogs allowed in the flagship store?','Yes, you can bring your dog along, as the store permits dogs.','2025-03-28 01:56:24','2025-03-28 01:56:24'),(14500,'trails',363,'What is the geographic location of the store?','The Glen Canyon Conservancy flagship store is located at latitude 36.9196 and longitude -111.461.','2025-03-28 01:56:24','2025-03-28 01:56:24'),(14501,'trails',363,'How accurate is the relief map today?','Even after nearly 55 years, the relief map continues to depict the landscape around the Glen Canyon National Recreation Area accurately, apart from a few new roads.','2025-03-28 01:56:25','2025-03-28 01:56:25'),(14502,'trails',367,'What is Hermit Road?','Hermit Road is a picturesque 7-mile (11 km) route that runs along the western portion of the Grand Canyon Village on the South Rim, offering stunning views of the Grand Canyon and the Colorado River.','2025-03-28 01:56:36','2025-03-28 01:56:36'),(14503,'trails',367,'How can I access Hermit Road?','You can access Hermit Road by shuttle bus, on foot, by bicycle, or via commercial bus tours. Note that private vehicles are only permitted during the winter months of December to February.','2025-03-28 01:56:36','2025-03-28 01:56:36'),(14504,'trails',367,'What viewpoints are available along Hermit Road?','There are nine designated viewpoints along Hermit Road where you can stop and enjoy the breathtaking scenery, including locations that allow you to hear the Colorado River at Granite Rapid.','2025-03-28 01:56:36','2025-03-28 01:56:36'),(14505,'trails',367,'What is the Canyon Rim Trail?','The Canyon Rim Trail runs alongside Hermit Road for 7.8 miles (12.6 km) and offers options for both short and long scenic walks among paved and dirt paths.','2025-03-28 01:56:36','2025-03-28 01:56:36'),(14506,'trails',367,'How often do the shuttle buses run?','During most of the day, the shuttle buses operate every 15 minutes, providing easy access to various scenic overlooks.','2025-03-28 01:56:36','2025-03-28 01:56:36'),(14507,'trails',367,'Are bicycles allowed on the shuttle buses?','Yes, the shuttle buses can accommodate two or three bicycles, but ensure your bike has wheels larger than 16 inches (41 cm). Riders must load and unload their own bicycles.','2025-03-28 01:56:36','2025-03-28 01:56:36'),(14508,'trails',367,'What accessibility options are available on Hermit Road?','Shuttle buses are equipped with ramps and have space for wheelchairs, although larger wheelchairs exceeding 30 inches by 48 inches (76 cm x 122 cm) cannot be accommodated. Many paths meet accessibility guidelines.','2025-03-28 01:56:37','2025-03-28 01:56:37'),(14509,'trails',367,'What amenities are available at Hermits Rest?','At Hermits Rest, you\'ll find a water station and a snackbar, as well as vault toilets available at both Hopi Point and Hermits Rest.','2025-03-28 01:56:37','2025-03-28 01:56:37'),(14510,'trails',367,'What should I know about dogs on Hermit Road?','One dog is allowed on Hermit Road, but be sure to check any regulations regarding leashing and clean-up.','2025-03-28 01:56:37','2025-03-28 01:56:37'),(14511,'trails',367,'When is Hermit Road open to private vehicles?','Hermit Road allows private vehicles only from December to February. During the rest of the year, it\'s closed to private traffic, requiring visitors to use the shuttle service.','2025-03-28 01:56:37','2025-03-28 01:56:37'),(14512,'trails',367,'Is there a permit for accessibility on Hermit Road?','Yes, the park offers a Scenic Drive Accessibility Permit for visitors with mobility challenges, allowing access to specific areas that are otherwise closed to public traffic.','2025-03-28 01:56:37','2025-03-28 01:56:37'),(14513,'trails',367,'Where is Hermit Road located?','Hermit Road begins at the interchange near the Bright Angel Lodge in the Village Historic District of the South Rim.','2025-03-28 01:56:37','2025-03-28 01:56:37'),(14514,'trails',368,'Where does the Weeping Rock Trailhead start?','The Weeping Rock Trailhead begins at Shuttle Stop 7.','2025-03-28 01:56:43','2025-03-28 01:56:43'),(14515,'trails',368,'What can I expect to see along the Weeping Rock Trail?','As you hike, enjoy small trailside exhibits and be mindful of minor drop-offs.','2025-03-28 01:56:43','2025-03-28 01:56:43'),(14516,'trails',368,'What is at the end of the Weeping Rock Trail?','The trail culminates at a rock alcove featuring beautiful dripping springs.','2025-03-28 01:56:43','2025-03-28 01:56:43'),(14517,'trails',368,'Are there any facilities at the Weeping Rock Trailhead?','Yes, you can find pit toilets available at the parking area.','2025-03-28 01:56:43','2025-03-28 01:56:43'),(14518,'trails',368,'How steep is the Weeping Rock Trail?','The trail is short but steep, gaining an elevation of 98 feet (30 meters) over a distance of 0.4 miles (0.6 kilometers).','2025-03-28 01:56:43','2025-03-28 01:56:43'),(14519,'trails',368,'Is the Weeping Rock Trail accessible for everyone?','While the trail includes paved sections, it does have several stairs and minor drop-offs, making it more suitable for those with some hiking experience.','2025-03-28 01:56:44','2025-03-28 01:56:44'),(14520,'trails',368,'Are dogs allowed on the Weeping Rock Trail?','Yes, dogs are permitted on this trail.','2025-03-28 01:56:44','2025-03-28 01:56:44'),(14521,'trails',369,'What activities can I join at Zion National Park?','Explore the unique features of Zion National Park through various ranger-led activities that cover subjects like geology, wildlife, art, and human history. Check the Events Calendar for the latest schedule, as all ranger programs are offered at no cost.','2025-03-28 01:56:51','2025-03-28 01:56:51'),(14522,'trails',369,'Where can I find ranger-led activities in the park?','You can participate in ranger-led programs at shuttle stop #1 and throughout the park. Make sure to review the Events Calendar for information on specific topics and times.','2025-03-28 01:56:51','2025-03-28 01:56:51'),(14523,'trails',369,'What topics are covered in ranger-led talks?','Ranger-led talks delve into a variety of topics, including the park\'s geology, wildlife, artistic heritage, and human history. Each program provides a chance to learn something new about the natural world.','2025-03-28 01:56:52','2025-03-28 01:56:52'),(14524,'trails',369,'Are the ranger-led programs accessible?','Yes, all ranger-led talks and evening programs are conducted outdoors, with facilities designed for accessibility. The Zion Canyon Visitor Center offers assistive listening devices and shaded seating for comfort.','2025-03-28 01:56:52','2025-03-28 01:56:52'),(14525,'trails',369,'Can I bring my dog to ranger-led activities?','Yes, dogs are permitted at some locations within the park, but it\'s best to check specific program guidelines regarding pet policies.','2025-03-28 01:56:52','2025-03-28 01:56:52'),(14526,'trails',369,'Are ranger programs wheelchair accessible?','The Ride with A Ranger program on the shuttle buses is wheelchair accessible, and ranger walks on the Pa\'rus Trail are also designed for accessibility. However, the Watchman Trail is not wheelchair friendly.','2025-03-28 01:56:52','2025-03-28 01:56:52'),(14527,'trails',369,'What amenities are available for participants in ranger-led programs?','For those attending ranger-led talks, the Zion Canyon Visitor Center provides shaded areas with sandstone benches for seating, and space for mobility devices and wheelchairs is available to ensure comfort.','2025-03-28 01:56:52','2025-03-28 01:56:52'),(14528,'trails',372,'Where is the Lower Emerald Pool Trailhead located?','The Lower Emerald Pool Trailhead can be found directly across from the Zion Lodge at shuttle stop #5.','2025-03-28 01:57:00','2025-03-28 01:57:00'),(14529,'trails',372,'What is the trail like for Lower Emerald Pool?','The trail is a rugged, paved path that winds through pinyon-juniper woodland, ultimately leading to the picturesque Lower Emerald Pool and seasonal waterfalls.','2025-03-28 01:57:00','2025-03-28 01:57:00'),(14530,'trails',372,'Can I swim in the Lower Emerald Pool?','Swimming is strictly prohibited in the Lower Emerald Pool as the pools are delicate and a vital source of water for local wildlife.','2025-03-28 01:57:00','2025-03-28 01:57:00'),(14531,'trails',372,'What other trails can I access from the Lower Emerald Pool Trail?','This trail provides connectivity to the other Emerald Pools trails and the Kayenta Trail.','2025-03-28 01:57:00','2025-03-28 01:57:00'),(14532,'trails',372,'What amenities are available near the Lower Emerald Pool Trail?','Amenities such as restrooms and water filling stations are conveniently located at the nearby Zion Lodge.','2025-03-28 01:57:00','2025-03-28 01:57:00'),(14533,'trails',372,'How do I begin my hike on the Lower Emerald Pool Trail?','To start your hike, follow the sidewalk from the shuttle stop across the Lodge Lawn, cross the street at the crosswalk, and continue across the bridge. The trail begins on your right.','2025-03-28 01:57:00','2025-03-28 01:57:00'),(14534,'trails',372,'Is the Lower Emerald Pool Trail accessible for all hikers?','The trail is narrow and somewhat rugged, with several steps and minor drop-offs. A metal handrail is available at the end to assist with navigation.','2025-03-28 01:57:01','2025-03-28 01:57:01'),(14535,'trails',372,'Are dogs allowed on the Lower Emerald Pool Trail?','Yes, you are allowed to bring dogs on the Lower Emerald Pool Trail, but please keep them on a leash.','2025-03-28 01:57:01','2025-03-28 01:57:01'),(14536,'trails',372,'What are the geographical coordinates of the Lower Emerald Pool Trail?','The coordinates for the Lower Emerald Pool Trail are latitude 37.251 and longitude -112.959.','2025-03-28 01:57:01','2025-03-28 01:57:01'),(14537,'trails',373,'What is the length of the Middle Emerald Pools Trail?','The trail spans approximately 2.2 miles (3.5 km).','2025-03-28 01:57:11','2025-03-28 01:57:11'),(14538,'trails',373,'What type of terrain can I expect on this trail?','The Middle Emerald Pools Trail features unpaved and rocky terrain, requiring caution due to its uneven surfaces.','2025-03-28 01:57:11','2025-03-28 01:57:11'),(14539,'trails',373,'What are some highlights of the Middle Emerald Pools Trail?','Hikers can enjoy breathtaking views of Zion Canyon, experience shaded pinyon-juniper woodlands, and discover beautiful emerald pools and small waterfalls.','2025-03-28 01:57:12','2025-03-28 01:57:12'),(14540,'trails',373,'Where can I find the trailhead for the Middle Emerald Pools Trail?','The trailhead is conveniently located across from the Zion Lodge at shuttle stop #5. From the shuttle stop, cross the sidewalk, street, and bridge to find the trail.','2025-03-28 01:57:12','2025-03-28 01:57:12'),(14541,'trails',373,'Is the trail suitable for all hikers?','This trail is rated as moderate and includes a notably steep initial ascent, along with some areas that may have drop-offs and cliff edges, which may not be ideal for all hikers.','2025-03-28 01:57:12','2025-03-28 01:57:12'),(14542,'trails',373,'Are there any restrictions regarding the emerald pools?','Visitors are discouraged from entering the water as the pools are delicate and serve as a vital water source for local wildlife.','2025-03-28 01:57:12','2025-03-28 01:57:12'),(14543,'trails',373,'What facilities are available along the trail?','Restrooms and water filling stations can be found at the nearby Zion Lodge, providing necessary amenities for hikers.','2025-03-28 01:57:12','2025-03-28 01:57:12'),(14544,'trails',373,'Can I bring my dog on this trail?','Yes, dogs are permitted on the Middle Emerald Pools Trail, but remember to keep them leashed.','2025-03-28 01:57:12','2025-03-28 01:57:12'),(14545,'trails',373,'What should I be cautious of while hiking this trail?','It\'s important to avoid the edges of cliffs, as they can be hazardous. Additionally, ensure to stay on designated paths to protect the natural environment.','2025-03-28 01:57:12','2025-03-28 01:57:12'),(14546,'trails',373,'Does the trail connect with any other trails?','Yes, the Middle Emerald Pools Trail links to other Emerald Pools trails and the Kayenta Trail, offering more hiking options.','2025-03-28 01:57:12','2025-03-28 01:57:12'),(14547,'trails',374,'Where do I start the hike to Angels Landing?','You can begin your hike to Angels Landing from The Grotto, which is located at shuttle stop #6. Simply cross the road and bridge to access the sandy West Rim Trail.','2025-03-28 01:57:26','2025-03-28 01:57:26'),(14548,'trails',374,'Is there a permit required to hike to Angels Landing?','Yes, starting April 1, 2022, hikers continuing to Angels Landing from Scout Lookout must have a permit. You can obtain this permit from recreation.gov.','2025-03-28 01:57:26','2025-03-28 01:57:26'),(14549,'trails',374,'What is the trail like to Angels Landing?','The trail is strenuous and follows a steep, narrow ridge with uneven steps and occasional chains for support. There are sections that are only a few feet wide, with significant drop-offs, so caution is essential.','2025-03-28 01:57:26','2025-03-28 01:57:26'),(14550,'trails',374,'How dangerous is the Angels Landing trail?','The trail can be quite challenging and features sheer drop-offs of up to 1,000 feet on both sides. It\'s crucial to watch your footing and be mindful of your surroundings at all times.','2025-03-28 01:57:26','2025-03-28 01:57:26'),(14551,'trails',374,'What should I do if I meet other hikers on the trail?','In certain narrow sections, you\'ll need to yield to other hikers, as the trail is often only wide enough for one person. Always be courteous and allow others to pass safely.','2025-03-28 01:57:26','2025-03-28 01:57:26'),(14552,'trails',374,'Are there places to rest along the trail?','Yes, at the end of the hike, the trail widens and provides spots to rest, enjoy some snacks, and take in the breathtaking views of Zion Canyon.','2025-03-28 01:57:26','2025-03-28 01:57:26'),(14553,'trails',374,'Are restroom facilities available on the trail?','Restrooms can be found at both Scout Lookout and The Grotto, making it convenient for hikers.','2025-03-28 01:57:26','2025-03-28 01:57:26'),(14554,'trails',374,'Is there water available on the trail?','You can refill your water bottles at the water filling stations located at The Grotto.','2025-03-28 01:57:26','2025-03-28 01:57:26'),(14555,'trails',374,'How accessible is the Angels Landing trail?','The trail is unpaved and rocky, measuring less than 3 feet wide in many areas. It features chains that serve as handrails, but be prepared for steep drop-offs and limited space for traffic in both directions.','2025-03-28 01:57:27','2025-03-28 01:57:27'),(14556,'trails',374,'Are dogs allowed on the Angels Landing trail?','Yes, dogs are permitted on the trail, but it\'s important to keep them on a leash and prepared for the challenging terrain.','2025-03-28 01:57:27','2025-03-28 01:57:27'),(14557,'trails',374,'What are the coordinates for Angels Landing?','The geographical coordinates for Angels Landing are approximately 37.2592° latitude and -112.951° longitude.','2025-03-28 01:57:27','2025-03-28 01:57:27'),(14558,'trails',375,'What type of trail is the West Rim Trail?','The West Rim Trail is a challenging and strenuous hike, featuring an elevation gain of 1,488 feet (454 meters) to Scout Lookout.','2025-03-28 01:57:36','2025-03-28 01:57:36'),(14559,'trails',375,'What can hikers expect to see from Scout Lookout?','From Scout Lookout, hikers can enjoy stunning views of Zion Canyon and may even catch a glimpse of the endangered California condors that inhabit the cliffs.','2025-03-28 01:57:36','2025-03-28 01:57:36'),(14560,'trails',375,'Where can I access the West Rim Trail?','The trailhead for the West Rim Trail is located at The Grotto, which is accessible via shuttle stop #6. Hikers can begin by crossing the road and the bridge.','2025-03-28 01:57:36','2025-03-28 01:57:36'),(14561,'trails',375,'What is the terrain like on the West Rim Trail?','The trail features steep switchbacks along the canyon wall, especially after crossing the Virgin River. After climbing, there\'s a flatter segment as you pass through Refrigerator Canyon before the climb resumes at Walter’s Wiggles, consisting of 21 switchbacks.','2025-03-28 01:57:36','2025-03-28 01:57:36'),(14562,'trails',375,'Is there a permit required to hike to Angels Landing?','Yes, a permit is required to continue hiking to Angels Landing starting April 1, 2022. Permits can be obtained from recreation.gov.','2025-03-28 01:57:36','2025-03-28 01:57:36'),(14563,'trails',375,'Are there facilities available for hikers?','Yes, there are water and restrooms available at The Grotto, and additional restroom facilities can be found at Scout Lookout.','2025-03-28 01:57:36','2025-03-28 01:57:36'),(14564,'trails',375,'What are the accessibility features of the West Rim Trail?','The trail is paved but sections can be steep and narrow, with an overall elevation gain of 1,488 feet (454 meters). It does not have hand railings or fences. Be cautious as Refrigerator Canyon may have low visibility, especially early in the morning or late in the evening.','2025-03-28 01:57:36','2025-03-28 01:57:36'),(14565,'trails',375,'Are dogs allowed on the West Rim Trail?','Yes, dogs are allowed on the trail, but be sure to check specific regulations regarding pets before your hike.','2025-03-28 01:57:36','2025-03-28 01:57:36'),(14566,'trails',375,'What are the geographical coordinates of the West Rim Trail?','The geographical coordinates for the West Rim Trail are approximately 37.2592 latitude and -112.951 longitude.','2025-03-28 01:57:36','2025-03-28 01:57:36'),(14567,'trails',376,'What kind of views can I expect on the Kayenta Trail?','Hikers will be treated to stunning panoramic views of Zion Canyon as they navigate along the Virgin River and ascend towards the Emerald Pools.','2025-03-28 01:57:47','2025-03-28 01:57:47'),(14568,'trails',376,'How long is the Kayenta Trail?','The trail is moderately challenging, covering a distance of 2.0 miles (3.2 kilometers).','2025-03-28 01:57:47','2025-03-28 01:57:47'),(14569,'trails',376,'Is the trail safe for inexperienced hikers?','While the Kayenta Trail is considered moderate, it includes long drop-offs and uneven terrain. Hikers should be cautious, especially near edges.','2025-03-28 01:57:47','2025-03-28 01:57:47'),(14570,'trails',376,'Where does the Kayenta Trail start?','You can begin your hike at The Grotto, which is shuttle stop #6. Look for the crosswalk that leads to the bridge over the Virgin River, then ascend the sandstone steps.','2025-03-28 01:57:47','2025-03-28 01:57:47'),(14571,'trails',376,'Can I make a loop during my hike?','Yes! Hikers have the option to return on the same trail or create a loop using one of the Emerald Pools trails.','2025-03-28 01:57:47','2025-03-28 01:57:47'),(14572,'trails',376,'What facilities are available at The Grotto?','At The Grotto, you\'ll find essential amenities including water and restrooms for your convenience.','2025-03-28 01:57:47','2025-03-28 01:57:47'),(14573,'trails',376,'What is the elevation gain on the trail?','The Kayenta Trail features a total elevation gain of 150 feet (46 meters) during the hike.','2025-03-28 01:57:47','2025-03-28 01:57:47'),(14574,'trails',376,'What is the terrain like on the Kayenta Trail?','The trail is unpaved and consists of sandy, rocky, and uneven surfaces, along with multiple sandstone steps and areas with long drop-offs.','2025-03-28 01:57:47','2025-03-28 01:57:47'),(14575,'trails',376,'Are dogs allowed on the Kayenta Trail?','Yes, dogs are permitted on the Kayenta Trail, making it a pet-friendly option for hikers.','2025-03-28 01:57:47','2025-03-28 01:57:47'),(14576,'trails',376,'What are the GPS coordinates for the Kayenta Trail?','The trailhead is located at the latitude 37.2592 and longitude -112.951.','2025-03-28 01:57:48','2025-03-28 01:57:48'),(14577,'trails',379,'What is the length and difficulty of the Riverside Walk trail?','The Riverside Walk trail spans 2.2 miles round-trip and offers an easy hiking experience, making it suitable for all skill levels.','2025-03-28 01:57:59','2025-03-28 01:57:59'),(14578,'trails',379,'What is the trail\'s terrain like?','The trail is mostly flat and paved, though some sections have irregular paving and minor drop-offs. The initial half-mile is easier to navigate.','2025-03-28 01:57:59','2025-03-28 01:57:59'),(14579,'trails',379,'Is the Riverside Walk trail wheelchair accessible?','The trail is wheelchair accessible for the first 0.4 miles. Beyond that, steeper gradients make it challenging for those using wheelchairs.','2025-03-28 01:57:59','2025-03-28 01:57:59'),(14580,'trails',379,'What can I see along the Riverside Walk?','As you hike, you\'ll follow the Virgin River and witness stunning sandstone walls that gradually narrow. You\'ll also encounter educational exhibits about canyon formation, erosion, and local ecology.','2025-03-28 01:58:00','2025-03-28 01:58:00'),(14581,'trails',379,'Can I continue my hike beyond Riverside Walk?','Yes, the Riverside Walk also provides access to The Narrows. If you\'d like to keep your feet dry, you can turn back at the end of the paved section.','2025-03-28 01:58:00','2025-03-28 01:58:00'),(14582,'trails',379,'Where can I find facilities along the trail?','Restrooms and water are available at the Temple of Sinawava, which is where the Riverside Walk begins.','2025-03-28 01:58:00','2025-03-28 01:58:00'),(14583,'trails',379,'What is the elevation change on this trail?','The Riverside Walk features a modest elevation change of 57 feet (17 meters), making it a gentle hike.','2025-03-28 01:58:00','2025-03-28 01:58:00'),(14584,'trails',379,'Are dogs allowed on the Riverside Walk?','Yes, dogs are permitted on this trail, allowing you to enjoy the scenery with your furry friend.','2025-03-28 01:58:00','2025-03-28 01:58:00'),(14585,'trails',379,'Where is the starting point for Riverside Walk?','The trail begins at the Temple of Sinawava, which is the last stop on the Zion Canyon Scenic Drive. Just follow the sidewalk past the shuttle stop and restrooms to start your hike.','2025-03-28 01:58:00','2025-03-28 01:58:00'),(14586,'trails',380,'What can I expect to see on the La Verkin Creek Trail to Kolob Arch?','On the La Verkin Creek Trail, hikers will encounter breathtaking views of the Kolob Canyons and unique landscapes leading to Kolob Arch, one of the largest natural arches in the world.','2025-03-28 01:58:11','2025-03-28 01:58:11'),(14587,'trails',380,'Where does the trail to Kolob Arch start?','The hike begins at the Lee Pass Trailhead, located on the Kolob Canyons Road. This is the second to last trailhead in the area.','2025-03-28 01:58:11','2025-03-28 01:58:11'),(14588,'trails',380,'Is there parking available at Lee Pass Trailhead?','Parking at Lee Pass Trailhead is limited, so it\'s advisable to arrive early if you plan to hike.','2025-03-28 01:58:12','2025-03-28 01:58:12'),(14589,'trails',380,'Are there any facilities at the Lee Pass Trailhead?','There are no water sources or restrooms available directly at the Lee Pass Trailhead.','2025-03-28 01:58:12','2025-03-28 01:58:12'),(14590,'trails',380,'What regulations should I be aware of for groups hiking in the Zion Wilderness?','The Zion Wilderness enforces a group size limit of 12 people to minimize impact on the environment. Larger groups must split up and go to different areas on the same day.','2025-03-28 01:58:12','2025-03-28 01:58:12'),(14591,'trails',380,'Where can I find restrooms and fill my water before my hike?','You can fill your water bottle and find restroom facilities at the Kolob Canyons Visitor Center. Additional pit toilets are available at select trailheads nearby.','2025-03-28 01:58:12','2025-03-28 01:58:12'),(14592,'trails',380,'What should I do if I need to go to the restroom while on the trail?','If nature calls while you\'re on the trail, be prepared to pack out your waste using recommended human waste disposal bags. Following Leave No Trace principles is essential.','2025-03-28 01:58:12','2025-03-28 01:58:12'),(14593,'trails',380,'Can I bring my pet on this hiking trail?','Pets are not allowed on the La Verkin Creek Trail or any Zion trails except for the designated Pa\'rus Trail.','2025-03-28 01:58:12','2025-03-28 01:58:12'),(14594,'trails',380,'What is the level of difficulty for the La Verkin Creek Trail?','This trail is considered strenuous, featuring a total elevation change of 1,037 feet (316 meters) over a distance of 14 miles (22.5 kilometers), with rocky and uneven terrain including water crossings.','2025-03-28 01:58:12','2025-03-28 01:58:12'),(14595,'trails',380,'How long is the hike to Kolob Arch?','The hike spans about 14 miles (22.5 kilometers) and takes you on a scenic descent towards La Verkin Creek before reaching the viewpoint for Kolob Arch.','2025-03-28 01:58:12','2025-03-28 01:58:12'),(14596,'trails',380,'What are the geographic coordinates for the La Verkin Creek Trail?','The trail is located at a latitude of 37.4522 and a longitude of -113.191.','2025-03-28 01:58:13','2025-03-28 01:58:13'),(14597,'trails',382,'What type of trail is the Timber Creek Overlook Trail?','The Timber Creek Overlook Trail is a short, easy hike that follows a rocky ridge with minimal elevation gain, making it an excellent choice for a leisurely stroll to a breathtaking viewpoint.','2025-03-28 01:58:23','2025-03-28 01:58:23'),(14598,'trails',382,'What kind of views can I expect from the overlook?','At the overlook, hikers can enjoy stunning views of Shuntavi Butte, Timber Creek, Kolob Terrace, and the Pine Valley Mountains. On a clear day, you might even catch a glimpse of Mount Trumbull, located 100 miles away at the north rim of the Grand Canyon.','2025-03-28 01:58:23','2025-03-28 01:58:23'),(14599,'trails',382,'When is the best time to hike Timber Creek Overlook Trail?','The best time to hike this trail is during the spring and early summer months when the area is adorned with a vibrant display of desert wildflowers.','2025-03-28 01:58:23','2025-03-28 01:58:23'),(14600,'trails',382,'How do I access the Timber Creek Overlook Trailhead?','To reach the Timber Creek Overlook Trailhead, drive to the very end of Kolob Canyons Road, where you\'ll find the trailhead and a parking area.','2025-03-28 01:58:23','2025-03-28 01:58:23'),(14601,'trails',382,'Are there any facilities near the trailhead?','Yes, there are restrooms available at the trailhead, and water can be obtained at the nearby Kolob Canyons Visitor Center.','2025-03-28 01:58:23','2025-03-28 01:58:23'),(14602,'trails',382,'Is the trail suitable for dogs?','Yes, dogs are allowed on the Timber Creek Overlook Trail.','2025-03-28 01:58:24','2025-03-28 01:58:24'),(14603,'trails',382,'What should I know about the trail\'s terrain?','The trail is unpaved and features uneven rocky terrain, so it\'s important to tread carefully. Additionally, the overlook has steep drop-offs, so stay cautious near the edges.','2025-03-28 01:58:24','2025-03-28 01:58:24'),(14604,'trails',382,'What is the total elevation gain of the Timber Creek Overlook Trail?','The trail includes a total elevation gain of about 100 feet (30 meters).','2025-03-28 01:58:24','2025-03-28 01:58:24'),(14605,'trails',382,'Are there any picnic areas nearby?','Yes, there is a small picnic area located a short distance from the trailhead, perfect for a break or a snack after your hike.','2025-03-28 01:58:24','2025-03-28 01:58:24'),(14606,'trails',382,'What should I expect regarding trail conditions?','The trail can often be muddy when wet, so be prepared for varying conditions, especially during or after rain.','2025-03-28 01:58:24','2025-03-28 01:58:24'),(14607,'trails',383,'What type of climbing can I expect in Zion National Park?','Zion National Park is famous for its monumental sandstone cliffs, providing exceptional opportunities for big wall and traditional climbing. Most routes are challenging and not suitable for novice climbers, given the unique qualities of the rock.','2025-03-28 01:58:39','2025-03-28 01:58:39'),(14608,'trails',383,'Are permits needed for climbing in Zion National Park?','Yes, you need permits for all overnight bivouacs, but day climbs do not require permits. It’s advisable to reserve your bivy in advance for popular routes and pick up permits at the Zion Canyon Visitor Center.','2025-03-28 01:58:39','2025-03-28 01:58:39'),(14609,'trails',383,'Can I camp at the base of climbing routes?','Camping at the base of climbing walls or inside vehicles in the park is prohibited unless you are in a designated campground with a reservation. Always check for the right camping guidelines.','2025-03-28 01:58:39','2025-03-28 01:58:39'),(14610,'trails',383,'What should I do with human waste while climbing?','All climbers are required to pack out their human waste. It’s essential to use bags or tubes to properly dispose of waste and avoid leaving it behind in nature.','2025-03-28 01:58:39','2025-03-28 01:58:39'),(14611,'trails',383,'Is commercial guiding available for climbing in Zion?','Commercial guiding is not allowed in the wilderness areas of Zion, including all climbing routes. Solo or group climbing requires individual planning and safety.','2025-03-28 01:58:39','2025-03-28 01:58:39'),(14612,'trails',383,'How are climbing protections like bolts maintained in Zion?','The National Park Service does not inspect or maintain climbing bolts or equipment within the park. Climbers must thoroughly inspect any existing gear for safety and ensure their own climbing protection.','2025-03-28 01:58:39','2025-03-28 01:58:39'),(14613,'trails',383,'What guidelines are there for bolting routes in Zion?','Bolting is highly regulated in Zion. The park prohibits the establishment of bolt-heavy face climbs to preserve wilderness character. Fixed anchors should only be used as a last resort and made with hand drills only.','2025-03-28 01:58:40','2025-03-28 01:58:40'),(14614,'trails',383,'Can I leave equipment unattended while climbing?','Equipment must not be left unattended for more than 24 hours or it may be treated as abandoned property. The park may remove any abandoned gear according to regulations.','2025-03-28 01:58:40','2025-03-28 01:58:40'),(14615,'trails',383,'Who should I contact if I want to establish a new climbing route in Zion?','If you plan to create a new route, visit the Wilderness Desk at the Zion Canyon Visitor Center to discuss your plans with a ranger. They can provide guidance on wilderness regulations and route considerations.','2025-03-28 01:58:40','2025-03-28 01:58:40'),(14616,'trails',383,'When is the best time to climb in Zion?','The ideal times for climbing in Zion are from March to May and September to early November. Summer temperatures can exceed 100 degrees, which, combined with monsoonal rains, can compromise rock conditions.','2025-03-28 01:58:40','2025-03-28 01:58:40'),(14617,'trails',383,'What precautions should I take regarding weather conditions while climbing?','Avoid climbing after rainstorms as the desert sandstone is vulnerable when wet. It may take days for the rock to dry properly, which can affect the integrity of holds and safety of climbs.','2025-03-28 01:58:40','2025-03-28 01:58:40'),(14618,'trails',383,'Where can I find bouldering opportunities in Zion?','Zion offers two main bouldering areas: The Globe, located 40 yards west of the south entrance, and Drilled Pocket Boulder, which is half a mile north of the entrance. Both areas present a variety of challenges.','2025-03-28 01:58:40','2025-03-28 01:58:40'),(14619,'trails',383,'Are dogs allowed on the climbing routes in Zion?','Yes, dogs are allowed in certain areas, but it’s important to check specific guidelines regarding pets on trails and climbing routes.','2025-03-28 01:58:40','2025-03-28 01:58:40'),(14620,'trails',385,'What is the distance of the Grotto Trail?','The Grotto Trail spans an easy 1.0 mile (1.6 km) round trip.','2025-03-28 01:58:51','2025-03-28 01:58:51'),(14621,'trails',385,'Where does the Grotto Trail start and end?','This trail begins at shuttle stop #5 near the Zion Lodge and ends at shuttle stop #6 at The Grotto.','2025-03-28 01:58:51','2025-03-28 01:58:51'),(14622,'trails',385,'Is the Grotto Trail suitable for all hikers?','Yes, the Grotto Trail is categorized as easy and is suitable for a leisurely hike.','2025-03-28 01:58:51','2025-03-28 01:58:51'),(14623,'trails',385,'What type of terrain can I expect on the Grotto Trail?','You\'ll enjoy a mostly flat and shaded trail, making it ideal for a relaxing walk.','2025-03-28 01:58:51','2025-03-28 01:58:51'),(14624,'trails',385,'Are there any chances of spotting wildlife on the Grotto Trail?','Absolutely! Keep an eye out for various wildlife such as birds, turkeys, and deer during your hike.','2025-03-28 01:58:51','2025-03-28 01:58:51'),(14625,'trails',385,'Are there restrooms available along the Grotto Trail?','Yes, restrooms can be found at both the Zion Lodge and The Grotto.','2025-03-28 01:58:51','2025-03-28 01:58:51'),(14626,'trails',385,'How can I access the Grotto Trail?','You can access the trail from behind the shuttle stop at Zion Lodge or from behind the restrooms at The Grotto.','2025-03-28 01:58:51','2025-03-28 01:58:51'),(14627,'trails',385,'What is the elevation change on the Grotto Trail?','The trail features a modest elevation gain of 35 feet (11 meters).','2025-03-28 01:58:52','2025-03-28 01:58:52'),(14628,'trails',385,'Is the Grotto Trail paved?','No, the trail is unpaved and sandy, with a section that is narrower and rocky.','2025-03-28 01:58:52','2025-03-28 01:58:52'),(14629,'trails',385,'Can I bring my dog on the Grotto Trail?','Yes, dogs are allowed on the Grotto Trail.','2025-03-28 01:58:52','2025-03-28 01:58:52'),(14630,'trails',385,'Can I combine the Grotto Trail with other trails?','Yes, you can combine it with the Emerald Pools and Kayenta Trails to create a loop.','2025-03-28 01:58:52','2025-03-28 01:58:52'),(14631,'trails',386,'What is the difficulty level of the Watchman Trail?','The Watchman Trail is classified as a moderate hike, suitable for those with a reasonable fitness level.','2025-03-28 01:59:01','2025-03-28 01:59:01'),(14632,'trails',386,'Where can I access the Watchman Trail?','You can access the Watchman Trail from the Zion Canyon Visitor Center.','2025-03-28 01:59:01','2025-03-28 01:59:01'),(14633,'trails',386,'What are some key features of the Watchman Trail?','The trail offers stunning views of the Watchman, Temples and Towers, lower Zion Canyon, and the Town of Springdale as it ascends 368 feet (112 meters).','2025-03-28 01:59:02','2025-03-28 01:59:02'),(14634,'trails',386,'What type of terrain can I expect on the Watchman Trail?','The trail features a mix of sandy, rocky, and uneven surfaces, including moderate drop-offs in certain sections.','2025-03-28 01:59:02','2025-03-28 01:59:02'),(14635,'trails',386,'Is there any facility at the trailhead?','Yes, there are restrooms and water filling stations available at the Visitor Center.','2025-03-28 01:59:02','2025-03-28 01:59:02'),(14636,'trails',386,'Are bicycles allowed on the Watchman Trail?','No, bicycles are not permitted on the Watchman Trail.','2025-03-28 01:59:02','2025-03-28 01:59:02'),(14637,'trails',386,'How do I reach the trailhead from the Zion Canyon Visitor Center?','To reach the trailhead, walk through the Visitor Center plaza, past the shuttle stop, and use the crosswalk to begin along the river.','2025-03-28 01:59:02','2025-03-28 01:59:02'),(14638,'trails',386,'Can I bring my dog on the Watchman Trail?','Yes, dogs are allowed on the Watchman Trail.','2025-03-28 01:59:02','2025-03-28 01:59:02'),(14639,'trails',386,'What safety considerations should I keep in mind while hiking the Watchman Trail?','Be cautious of moderate drop-offs and the uneven terrain, especially near the cliffside overlooks at the trail\'s end.','2025-03-28 01:59:02','2025-03-28 01:59:02'),(14640,'trails',386,'What is the elevation gain on the Watchman Trail?','The trail has an elevation gain of approximately 368 feet (112 meters).','2025-03-28 01:59:02','2025-03-28 01:59:02'),(14641,'trails',388,'What type of trail is the Horseshoe Bend Trail?','The Horseshoe Bend Trail is a sandy path that offers an easy hiking experience, making it suitable for families and casual hikers.','2025-03-28 01:59:11','2025-03-28 01:59:11'),(14642,'trails',388,'What notable feature can I expect to see on the trail?','Hikers are treated to breathtaking views of the stunning natural wonder known as Horseshoe Bend.','2025-03-28 01:59:11','2025-03-28 01:59:11'),(14643,'trails',388,'How difficult is the Horseshoe Bend Trail?','The trail is rated as easy to intermediate, making it accessible for most hikers.','2025-03-28 01:59:11','2025-03-28 01:59:11'),(14644,'trails',388,'What is the length of the Horseshoe Bend Trail?','The trail stretches for 0.7 miles, perfect for a quick hike.','2025-03-28 01:59:11','2025-03-28 01:59:11'),(14645,'trails',388,'What is the elevation change on the trail?','The trail features an incline of 110 feet and a decline of 531 feet, with a maximum elevation of 3,914 feet.','2025-03-28 01:59:12','2025-03-28 01:59:12'),(14646,'trails',388,'Is the Horseshoe Bend Trail family-friendly?','Absolutely! The easy terrain makes it a great choice for families to enjoy the outdoors together.','2025-03-28 01:59:12','2025-03-28 01:59:12'),(14647,'trails',388,'Are dogs allowed on the Horseshoe Bend Trail?','Yes, dogs are permitted on the trail, but they must be kept on a leash.','2025-03-28 01:59:12','2025-03-28 01:59:12'),(14648,'trails',388,'What is the trail type of Horseshoe Bend?','Horseshoe Bend Trail is a point-to-point trail.','2025-03-28 01:59:12','2025-03-28 01:59:12'),(14649,'trails',388,'What kind of views can I expect on the trail?','Hikers can enjoy spectacular views throughout the hike, especially at the end point where the scenic overlook is situated.','2025-03-28 01:59:12','2025-03-28 01:59:12'),(14650,'trails',388,'What is the average and maximum grade of the trail?','The trail features an average grade of 0.16% and peaks at a maximum grade of 2.73%, making it fairly easy to navigate.','2025-03-28 01:59:12','2025-03-28 01:59:12'),(14651,'trails',389,'What can I expect to see on the Antelope Canyon Trail?','Hikers will be treated to breathtaking views of stunning rock formations and the captivating beauty of a unique slot canyon.','2025-03-28 01:59:18','2025-03-28 01:59:18'),(14652,'trails',389,'How difficult is the Antelope Canyon Trail?','The trail is classified as easy to intermediate, making it accessible for a range of hikers.','2025-03-28 01:59:18','2025-03-28 01:59:18'),(14653,'trails',389,'What is the elevation range of the Antelope Canyon Trail?','The trail maintains a constant elevation at 3967 feet, providing a level hiking experience.','2025-03-28 01:59:18','2025-03-28 01:59:18'),(14654,'trails',389,'What is the total length of the Antelope Canyon Trail?','The trail spans 0.6 miles and is structured as a loop.','2025-03-28 01:59:18','2025-03-28 01:59:18'),(14655,'trails',389,'What\'s the incline and decline on the Antelope Canyon Trail?','The trail features a slight incline of 135 feet and a decline of 138 feet.','2025-03-28 01:59:18','2025-03-28 01:59:18'),(14656,'trails',389,'What is the average grade of the Antelope Canyon Trail?','The average grade is an easy 0.09%, providing a pleasant hiking experience.','2025-03-28 01:59:18','2025-03-28 01:59:18'),(14657,'trails',389,'What is the maximum grade on the Antelope Canyon Trail?','The maximum grade on this trail is 0.22%, ensuring a manageable ascent and descent.','2025-03-28 01:59:18','2025-03-28 01:59:18'),(14658,'trails',389,'What are the geographical coordinates of the Antelope Canyon Trail?','The trail is located at a latitude of 36.9025 and a longitude of -111.411.','2025-03-28 01:59:19','2025-03-28 01:59:19');
